IBA_DATA("vocab",{"iba":["IBA BBA 05-06","IBA BBA 06-07","IBA BBA 07-08","IBA BBA 08-09","IBA BBA 09-10","IBA BBA 10-11","IBA BBA 11-12","IBA BBA 12-13","IBA BBA 13-14","IBA BBA 14-15","IBA BBA 15-16","IBA BBA 16-17","IBA BBA 17-18","IBA BBA 19-20","IBA MBA 07-08","IBA MBA 08-09","IBA MBA 09-10","IBA MBA 10-11","IBA MBA 2011 (December)","IBA MBA 2011 (June)","IBA MBA 2012 (December)","IBA MBA 2012 (June)","IBA MBA 2013 (June)","IBA MBA 2014","IBA MBA 2015 (December)","IBA MBA 2015 (June)","IBA MBA 2016 (December)","IBA MBA 2016 (June)","IBA MBA 2017 (December)","IBA MBA 2017 (June)","IBA MBA 2018"],"words":[{"w":"abandon","p":"verb","d":"To leave someone or something completely, or to give up a plan or activity before finishing it.","lb":"leave, give up","s":["desert","forsake","leave","quit","discard","ditch"],"k":["desolate","give up","relinquish","renounce"],"a":["keep","stay","retain","support"],"ex":["The driver abandoned his broken-down car on the highway and walked to a petrol station.","Many pets are abandoned on the street when their owners move to a new city.","We had to abandon the picnic when it began to pour with rain."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"abase","p":"verb","d":"To lower someone's dignity, rank or self-respect, or to behave in a way that humbles yourself.","lb":"humble, degrade","s":["humble","degrade","demean","humiliate","lower","debase"],"k":["bow down","bruise","crawl","dishonour"],"a":["exalt","elevate","honor","raise"],"ex":["He refused to abase himself by begging his rival for a favor.","Some employees abase themselves before the boss, laughing at every joke to keep their jobs.","The cruel remarks were meant to abase her in front of her classmates."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"abash","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel embarrassed, ashamed or uncomfortable.","lb":"embarrass, shame","s":["embarrass","shame","humiliate","disconcert","mortify","discomfit"],"k":["confuse","disgrace","perturb","unsettle"],"a":["embolden","encourage","reassure","comfort"],"ex":["Nothing seemed to abash the child, who sang loudly in front of the whole school.","Rafi was abashed when the teacher read his poor answer aloud to the class.","She was not abashed by the interviewer's tough questions and answered every one calmly."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"abate","p":"verb","d":"To become less strong, intense or widespread over time.","lb":"reduce, lessen","s":["subside","lessen","diminish","ease","die down","wane"],"k":["curtail","decline","die away","fall"],"a":["intensify","increase","escalate","strengthen"],"ex":["After two hours, the heavy monsoon rain finally began to abate, and we walked home.","The pain in my knee did not abate until the doctor changed my medicine.","Public anger over the sudden price rise has not abated, even after the apology."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"abdicate","p":"verb","d":"To give up a position of power, such as a throne, or to fail to accept a duty.","lb":"step down, renounce","s":["step down","resign","renounce","relinquish","give up","quit"],"k":["abandon","bow out","cede","forgo"],"a":["retain","assume","claim","seize"],"ex":["The old king abdicated in favor of his daughter after a long illness.","Parents who let children do whatever they like have abdicated their responsibility.","The club president abdicated his role after losing the members' trust."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"aberrant","p":"adjective","d":"Different from what is normal, expected or accepted, often in a worrying way.","lb":"abnormal, deviant","s":["abnormal","deviant","atypical","irregular","anomalous","odd"],"k":["bizarre","eccentric","erratic","freakish"],"a":["normal","typical","regular","standard"],"ex":["The bank's software flagged an aberrant transaction and blocked the card until the owner called.","The doctor was concerned by the aberrant results in the blood test and ordered a second one.","Teachers noticed aberrant behavior in the usually cheerful boy and spoke gently to his parents."],"b":67,"y":1},{"w":"aberration","p":"noun","d":"Something that is unusual and different from what is normal or expected.","lb":"anomaly, deviation","s":["anomaly","oddity","irregularity","deviation","abnormality","exception"],"k":["blip","deviance","distortion","fluke"],"a":["norm","rule","standard","regularity"],"ex":["Her low score was an aberration, since she normally tops the class.","A cold day in the middle of summer is a weather aberration.","The sudden jump in sales proved to be an aberration, not a lasting trend."],"b":536,"y":0},{"w":"abet","p":"verb","d":"To help or encourage someone to do something wrong, especially to commit a crime.","lb":"assist, encourage","s":["aid","assist","help","encourage","support","back"],"k":["back up","collude","connive","conspire"],"a":["hinder","thwart","discourage","obstruct"],"ex":["The police said the driver had abetted the thieves by waiting outside with the engine running.","A student who helps a classmate cheat in an exam is abetting dishonesty.","The man was charged with aiding and abetting a fraud against elderly customers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"abeyance","p":"noun","d":"A state of temporary inactivity, when something is paused and not being used or decided.","lb":"suspension, dormancy","s":["suspension","inactivity","pause","lull","postponement","limbo"],"k":["freeze","hiatus","inaction","intermission"],"a":["activity","continuation","operation","use"],"ex":["Construction of the footbridge has been in abeyance since the city ran out of funds.","Our family rule about phones at dinner fell into abeyance during the holidays.","The company held the new hiring policy in abeyance until the board could meet next month."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"abhor","p":"verb","d":"To hate something very strongly, usually for moral reasons or because it disgusts you.","lb":"detest, loathe","s":["detest","loathe","hate","despise","abominate","dislike"],"k":["deplore","disdain","find repugnant","recoil from"],"a":["love","adore","admire","cherish"],"ex":["I abhor cruelty to animals, so I could not watch that film.","Nadia abhors waste and always saves leftover rice for the next meal.","Most teachers abhor cheating because it makes honest students feel cheated."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"abhorrence","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of very strong hatred and disgust towards something.","lb":"hatred, loathing","s":["hatred","loathing","disgust","revulsion","horror","aversion"],"k":["animosity","antipathy","contempt","distaste"],"a":["love","admiration","liking","fondness"],"ex":["She has a deep abhorrence of cruelty to animals.","He looked at the dirty river with abhorrence.","Many people regard cheating in exams with abhorrence."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"abject","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely bad, hopeless and humiliating, as in very great poverty or failure.","lb":"wretched, hopeless","s":["wretched","miserable","hopeless","pitiful","desperate","degrading"],"k":["deplorable","despairing","despondent","execrable"],"a":["dignified","proud","prosperous","comfortable"],"ex":["Millions of people around the world still live in abject poverty.","The team's abject failure in the final left the fans in silence.","He gave an abject apology, begging his neighbor to forgive him."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"abjure","p":"verb","d":"To formally promise to give up a belief, habit or claim, often in public or under oath.","lb":"renounce, give up","s":["renounce","forswear","relinquish","reject","recant","disavow"],"k":["abdicate","backpedal","cast off","deny"],"a":["embrace","adopt","affirm","espouse"],"ex":["After his illness, he abjured smoking and promised his family he would never touch a cigarette again.","The new member abjured all her old loyalties and swore to follow only the club's rules.","She publicly abjured her earlier statements and apologized to the committee."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"abnegate","p":"verb","d":"To give up or deny yourself something, such as a pleasure, a right or a belief.","lb":"renounce, give up","s":["renounce","relinquish","forgo","surrender","deny oneself","abstain from"],"k":["abandon","abdicate","cede","deny"],"a":["indulge","claim","assert","embrace"],"ex":["Monks abnegate worldly comforts to live a simple life of study and quiet work.","A leader cannot abnegate responsibility when a project fails; he must answer for it.","During exam season, Rafi abnegated video games and parties to focus on his books."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"abnormal","p":"adjective","d":"Different from what is usual, expected or healthy, often in a worrying way.","lb":"unusual, irregular","s":["unusual","irregular","atypical","odd","peculiar","deviant"],"k":["aberrant","bizarre","defective","exceptional"],"a":["normal","usual","regular","typical"],"ex":["The doctor ordered more tests because my blood pressure was abnormal.","It is abnormal for the river to rise this early in the season.","The security system detected abnormal activity on my account and blocked the payment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"abomination","p":"noun","d":"Something that is hated or considered shockingly bad, wicked or disgusting.","lb":"outrage, horror","s":["outrage","atrocity","horror","disgrace","monstrosity","abhorrence"],"k":["affront","aversion","blight","eyesore"],"a":["delight","pleasure","blessing","gem"],"ex":["The new office building, covered in orange panels, was considered an abomination by the neighbors.","To a chef, putting ketchup on a fine steak is an abomination.","He called the dirty public toilet an abomination and demanded that the council fix it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aboriginal","p":"adjective","d":"Existing in a place from the earliest times, or belonging to the first people who lived there.","lb":"native, indigenous","s":["native","indigenous","original","first","primeval","earliest"],"k":["domestic","early","endemic","homegrown"],"a":["foreign","alien","imported","introduced"],"ex":["Aboriginal communities in the hills have lived there for hundreds of years.","The museum displays aboriginal tools made from stone and wood.","Scientists are studying the aboriginal plants of the island to protect them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aborigine","p":"noun","d":"A member of the earliest known people of a region; now often replaced by \"Indigenous person\".","lb":"native, original inhabitant","s":["native","indigenous person"],"k":["ancestral people","first nation","first people","individual"],"a":["settler","colonist","immigrant","newcomer"],"ex":["The museum has an exhibition about the traditional art of the region's aborigines.","Anthropologists studied how the aborigines of the island had lived for thousands of years.","The documentary showed how an aborigine elder passed old stories to younger generations."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"abortive","p":"adjective","d":"Failing to reach the intended result, so that the attempt has to be stopped or given up.","lb":"failed, unsuccessful","s":["failed","unsuccessful","fruitless","futile","vain","ineffectual"],"k":["bootless","botched","bungled","derailed"],"a":["successful","fruitful","productive","effective"],"ex":["After two abortive attempts to start the old generator, we gave up and waited for the electrician.","The company's abortive launch of its new app cost it thousands of users.","Her abortive plan to surprise her sister with a trip ended when the tickets sold out."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"abound","p":"verb","d":"To exist in large numbers or amounts; to be plentiful.","lb":"teem, be plentiful","s":["teem","thrive","flourish","overflow","proliferate","swarm"],"k":["be","be rampant","be rife","be widespread"],"a":["lack","be scarce","be rare","dwindle"],"ex":["Wildflowers abound along the hiking trail in early spring.","Bargains abound in the city's markets in the weeks before Eid.","Rumors abound whenever the school announces a surprise holiday."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"abridge","p":"verb","d":"To make a book, text or speech shorter by cutting parts while keeping the main ideas.","lb":"shorten, condense","s":["shorten","condense","cut","trim","compress","summarize"],"k":["boil down","decrease","edit","edit out"],"a":["expand","lengthen","extend","enlarge"],"ex":["The publisher abridged the thick novel so that younger readers could finish it quickly.","Can you abridge your speech to five minutes? We are short of time.","The film abridges the long book by leaving out several minor characters."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"abrogate","p":"verb","d":"To officially cancel or end a law, agreement or right.","lb":"repeal, cancel","s":["repeal","revoke","cancel","annul","rescind","nullify"],"k":["call off","countermand","dismantle","get rid of"],"a":["enact","establish","ratify","uphold"],"ex":["The council voted to abrogate the old rule that banned street vendors from the main road.","The company abrogated the contract after the supplier missed three deadlines.","A new law abrogated the earlier regulation about school uniforms."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"abscond","p":"verb","d":"To leave a place suddenly and secretly, usually to avoid arrest or to take something that is not yours.","lb":"flee, escape","s":["run away","flee","bolt","escape","disappear","make off"],"k":["do a runner","elope","fly","go off"],"a":["stay","remain","surrender","return"],"ex":["The cashier absconded with the shop's weekly earnings and has not been seen since.","The accused man absconded while out on bail, so the police are searching for him.","A tenant absconded in the night without paying three months' rent."],"b":69,"y":1},{"w":"absolute","p":"adjective","d":"Complete and total, with no limits, conditions or exceptions.","lb":"total, complete","s":["total","complete","utter","outright","sheer","perfect"],"k":["arbitrary","arrant","categorical","consummate"],"a":["partial","limited","qualified","conditional"],"ex":["The exam hall was in absolute silence except for the sound of pens moving on paper.","I have absolute trust in my sister, so I told her everything.","Getting the scholarship was an absolute joy for the whole family."],"b":272,"y":0},{"w":"absolve","p":"verb","d":"To declare officially that someone is free from blame, guilt or a duty.","lb":"acquit, exonerate","s":["acquit","exonerate","clear","pardon","forgive","excuse"],"k":["cleanse","discharge","exculpate","let off"],"a":["blame","condemn","accuse","convict"],"ex":["The investigation absolved the driver of any blame for the accident.","The new rule does not absolve parents of responsibility for their children's safety.","A written apology cannot absolve you of the duty to repay what you borrowed."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"abstemious","p":"adjective","d":"Careful to eat and drink only small amounts and to avoid indulging yourself.","lb":"moderate, sparing","s":["temperate","moderate","sober","restrained","frugal","austere"],"k":["ascetic","cautious","clement","conservative"],"a":["gluttonous","greedy","intemperate","immoderate"],"ex":["My grandfather is abstemious: he eats one small meal at night and never touches sweets.","Training for the marathon made her far more abstemious about food and late nights.","Though he was wealthy, the old judge led an abstemious life and drank only water."],"b":9,"y":0},{"w":"abstinent","p":"adjective","d":"Deliberately avoiding something enjoyable, such as alcohol or sweets, usually for health or moral reasons.","lb":"self-denying, temperate","s":["abstemious","temperate","sober","restrained","ascetic","moderate"],"k":["celibate","chaste","clean","clement"],"a":["indulgent","intemperate","greedy","gluttonous"],"ex":["He has been abstinent from sugary drinks since his doctor warned him about diabetes.","Many athletes stay abstinent from alcohol during the training season.","After his heart attack, my uncle became abstinent and no longer touches fried food."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"abstract","p":"adjective","d":"Existing as an idea or quality rather than as a physical object, or too general to relate to real situations.","lb":"theoretical, conceptual","s":["theoretical","conceptual","intangible","general","nonspecific","academic"],"k":["cerebral","hypothetical","ideological","metaphysical"],"a":["concrete","tangible","real","specific"],"ex":["Words like freedom and justice are abstract, so children need examples to understand them.","The lesson was too abstract for the class until the teacher showed a real bridge model.","She prefers practical tasks to abstract discussions about what might happen."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"abstruse","p":"adjective","d":"Difficult to understand because it is deep, complex or very specialized.","lb":"obscure, complex","s":["obscure","complex","esoteric","cryptic","recondite","profound"],"k":["ambiguous","convoluted","dense","enigmatic"],"a":["clear","simple","plain","obvious"],"ex":["The professor's abstruse explanation of the theory left most of us confused.","Without a dictionary, the abstruse legal language was impossible to follow.","Quantum physics can seem abstruse until you see it explained with simple pictures."],"b":88,"y":1},{"w":"abundance","p":"noun","d":"A very large quantity of something; more than enough.","lb":"plenty, profusion","s":["plenty","profusion","wealth","bounty","lots","richness"],"k":["bonanza","excess","heaps","loads"],"a":["scarcity","shortage","lack","dearth"],"ex":["The market had an abundance of fresh vegetables after the harvest.","Bangladesh has an abundance of rivers, which makes the land rich and green.","Flowers grew in abundance along the roadside after the first monsoon rains."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"abysmal","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely bad or poor in quality; terrible, wretched and hopeless.","lb":"terrible, dreadful","s":["terrible","dreadful","awful","appalling","atrocious","dire"],"k":["abominable","deep","deplorable","dreaded"],"a":["excellent","outstanding","superb","splendid"],"ex":["The team's abysmal performance in the final match disappointed all its supporters.","The hostel food was abysmal, so students began cooking in their rooms.","The road is in abysmal condition, full of holes that damage every vehicle."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"abyss","p":"noun","d":"A very deep hole or space that seems to have no bottom, or a huge gap or depth of feeling.","lb":"chasm, bottomless pit","s":["chasm","gulf","void","pit","depths","gorge"],"k":["cavern","gap","maw","precipice"],"a":["peak","summit","height","pinnacle"],"ex":["The climbers looked down into a dark abyss beside the narrow mountain path.","After losing his job and savings, he felt he was falling into an abyss of despair.","A huge abyss separates the rich and the poor in many big cities."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"accede","p":"verb","d":"To agree to a request, demand or proposal, often after first resisting.","lb":"agree, consent","s":["agree","consent","comply","yield","assent","concur"],"k":["accord","approve","back down","bow"],"a":["refuse","decline","reject","resist"],"ex":["After days of pressure from the students, the principal acceded to their request for a longer break.","The shop owner acceded to the customer's demand and refunded the faulty phone.","My father finally acceded to my wish to study abroad."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"accentuate","p":"verb","d":"To make something more noticeable or stronger by drawing attention to it.","lb":"emphasize, highlight","s":["emphasize","highlight","stress","underline","underscore","accent"],"k":["bring out","enhance","evince","express"],"a":["downplay","minimize","play down","understate"],"ex":["A dark blue scarf accentuates the color of her eyes.","The lawyer accentuated the strongest points of the case in her closing speech.","The bright spotlights accentuate the shape of the old building at night."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"access","p":"noun","d":"The right or ability to enter a place, use something or get information.","lb":"entry, admission","s":["entry","admission","entrance","admittance","availability","approach"],"k":["backdoor","clearance","connection","door"],"a":["denial","exclusion","barrier"],"ex":["Many rural students still do not have access to reliable internet.","Only staff have access to the server room.","The new ramp gives wheelchair users easy access to the library."],"b":416,"y":0},{"w":"acclaim","p":"verb","d":"To praise someone or something publicly and with great enthusiasm.","lb":"praise, applaud","s":["praise","applaud","hail","celebrate","laud","commend"],"k":["clap","compliment","congratulate","eulogize"],"a":["criticize","condemn","denounce","disparage"],"ex":["Critics acclaimed the film for its honest story and its beautiful photography.","The newly built bridge was widely acclaimed by engineers as a model for future projects.","Fans acclaimed the young bowler as the hero of the match."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"acclimatize","p":"verb","d":"To become used to a new climate, place or situation, or to help someone do so.","lb":"adapt, adjust","s":["adapt","adjust","accustom","get used to","habituate","settle in"],"k":["alter","bed in","conform","find one's feet"],"a":[],"ex":["Our cousin from Sylhet took a week to acclimatize to the dry heat of Dubai.","Climbers spend several days at base camp to acclimatize to the thin air.","The kitten needed a few days to acclimatize to its new home."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"accolade","p":"noun","d":"An award, praise or honor given to someone for an achievement.","lb":"honor, praise","s":["honor","award","tribute","praise","commendation","recognition"],"k":["bouquet","citation","distinction","gong"],"a":["criticism","condemnation","disapproval","blame"],"ex":["The young author received many accolades for her first novel.","The film won international accolades, including three awards for acting.","Nothing pleased the teacher more than the accolades from her former students."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"accord","p":"verb","d":"To be in agreement or harmony with something, or to give someone something such as respect or a welcome.","lb":"agree, grant","s":["agree","harmonize","match","grant","give","confer"],"k":["afford","allot","approve","assent"],"a":["disagree","conflict","differ","withhold"],"ex":["His story did not accord with what the security camera showed.","The class accorded the new teacher a warm welcome on her first day.","Their opinions accord on most issues, so they rarely argue."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"accost","p":"verb","d":"To approach and speak to someone boldly or aggressively, often when they do not want to talk.","lb":"confront, approach","s":["approach","confront","waylay","buttonhole","stop","address"],"k":["badger","collar","come","come up"],"a":["avoid","ignore","shun","evade"],"ex":["A salesman accosted us outside the mall and tried to sell us a membership.","Reporters accosted the coach as he left the stadium and demanded answers.","A stranger accosted her at the bus stop, asking for money in a rude voice."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"accouterments","p":"noun","d":"The extra clothing, equipment or items that go with a particular activity or role.","lb":"gear, trappings","s":["gear","equipment","trappings","accessories","kit","paraphernalia"],"k":["finery","garb","machinery","props"],"a":[],"ex":["The hikers carried all their accouterments, including tents, ropes and cooking pots, up the hill.","A cricket bag full of accouterments, from helmets to gloves, stood by the door.","The photographer arrived with the usual accouterments: cameras, lenses and a heavy tripod."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"accrete","p":"verb","d":"To grow or increase gradually by adding layers or small amounts over time.","lb":"accumulate, build up","s":["accumulate","amass","gather","collect","build up","increase"],"k":["agglomerate","aggregate","assemble","calcify"],"a":["erode","dwindle","diminish","wear away"],"ex":["Silt slowly accretes along the riverbank, forming new land over many years.","Dust accreted on the old books because no one had opened the room for years.","Small savings accrete into a large sum if you add money every month."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"accrue","p":"verb","d":"To gather or increase gradually over time, especially money, interest or benefits.","lb":"accumulate, build up","s":["accumulate","build up","gather","mount","grow","amass"],"k":["assemble","come to","compound","congregate"],"a":["dwindle","diminish","decrease","shrink"],"ex":["Interest accrues on your savings account every month, even when you do nothing.","Late fees will accrue daily if the electricity bill is not paid on time.","Over the years, many benefits accrue to employees who stay with the company."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"accumulate","p":"verb","d":"To gather or build up a large quantity of something gradually over time.","lb":"gather, collect","s":["gather","collect","amass","build up","pile up","stockpile"],"k":["assemble","compile","conglomerate","congregate"],"a":["scatter","disperse","dissipate","squander"],"ex":["Dust accumulates quickly on the shelves during the dry season.","She accumulated enough savings to open her own shop.","Debt can accumulate fast when you only pay the minimum each month."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"accuse","p":"verb","d":"To say that someone has done something wrong, illegal or dishonest.","lb":"blame, charge","s":["blame","charge","indict","denounce","incriminate","point the finger at"],"k":["arraign","call out","finger","frame"],"a":["defend","absolve","exonerate","acquit"],"ex":["The teacher accused the boy of copying from his neighbour's paper.","Nobody should accuse a person of stealing without clear proof.","She accused the shop of cheating her by charging twice for one item."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"acerbic","p":"adjective","d":"Sharp, harsh and bitter, especially in tone, humor or the way someone speaks.","lb":"harsh, biting","s":["harsh","sharp","biting","caustic","sarcastic","bitter"],"k":["acidic","astringent","barbed","blistering"],"a":["gentle","kind","mild","sweet"],"ex":["The critic is famous for her acerbic wit, and writers fear her reviews.","He answered the question in an acerbic tone that made everybody uneasy.","Her acerbic comments about the group project hurt her teammates."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"acquaint","p":"verb","d":"To make someone know about something or someone, or to get to know it yourself.","lb":"familiarize, introduce","s":["familiarize","inform","introduce","brief","accustom","advise"],"k":["apprise","clue in","educate","fill in"],"a":[],"ex":["Orientation week helps acquaint new students with the library and the labs.","Let me acquaint you with the facts before you make a decision.","I took a walk around the village to acquaint myself with the area."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"acquiesce","p":"verb","d":"To accept or agree to something without arguing, even if you do not really want to.","lb":"comply, consent","s":["comply","consent","agree","submit","yield","assent"],"k":["accept","bow to","buckle","cave in"],"a":["refuse","resist","object","protest"],"ex":["After a long argument, Rafi acquiesced and agreed to go to the family wedding.","The workers acquiesced to the new schedule because they feared losing their jobs.","She did not agree with the plan, but she acquiesced rather than start another quarrel."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"acquiescence","p":"noun","d":"Quiet acceptance of something, or agreement without protest, even if you do not really like it.","lb":"consent, compliance","s":["compliance","consent","assent","agreement","submission","acceptance"],"k":["conformation","deference","docility","meekness"],"a":["resistance","opposition","protest","refusal"],"ex":["His silence at the meeting was taken as acquiescence to the new rules.","The workers' quiet acquiescence to longer hours surprised the union leader.","She nodded in acquiescence, although she secretly disliked the plan."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"acquiescent","p":"adjective","d":"Willing to accept or agree to something without arguing, even if you do not really like it.","lb":"compliant, yielding","s":["compliant","submissive","docile","yielding","passive","obedient"],"k":["agreeable","biddable","cooperative","dutiful"],"a":["defiant","resistant","rebellious","stubborn"],"ex":["The acquiescent committee approved every proposal without asking a single question.","He was too acquiescent at home, so his brothers always chose the movie.","The new employee was acquiescent and accepted the extra work without complaint."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"acquisitive","p":"adjective","d":"Eager to get more money, possessions or knowledge, sometimes too eager.","lb":"greedy, grasping","s":["greedy","avaricious","grasping","covetous","materialistic","possessive"],"k":["accumulative","avid","consumerist","hoarding"],"a":["generous","giving","unselfish","charitable"],"ex":["He is so acquisitive that his room is crowded with gadgets he never uses.","The company has an acquisitive streak and keeps buying smaller rivals.","A child's acquisitive phase starts when she wants every toy in the shop."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"acquit","p":"verb","d":"To decide in a court of law that someone is not guilty of the crime they were accused of.","lb":"clear, free","s":["clear","exonerate","absolve","free","discharge","vindicate"],"k":["bear","behave","conduct oneself","deport"],"a":["convict","condemn","sentence","find guilty"],"ex":["The court acquitted the shopkeeper because there was no proof that he had cheated his customers.","After a two-week trial, the jury acquitted the young driver of all charges.","He was relieved when the judge acquitted him and he could finally go home to his family."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"acrid","p":"adjective","d":"Having a sharp, bitter, unpleasant smell or taste that irritates the nose or throat.","lb":"pungent, bitter","s":["pungent","bitter","sharp","harsh","caustic","biting"],"k":["acerbic","blistering","piquant","pointed"],"a":["sweet","fragrant","mild","pleasant"],"ex":["Acrid smoke from the burning rubbish made everyone on the street cover their noses.","The acrid smell of burnt toast filled the kitchen.","Chemistry students coughed in the lab because of the acrid fumes."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"acrimonious","p":"adjective","d":"Full of angry, bitter feelings, especially in a quarrel or dispute.","lb":"bitter, hostile","s":["bitter","hostile","spiteful","caustic","resentful","nasty"],"k":["bad-tempered","fractious","heated","ill-tempered"],"a":["amicable","friendly","cordial","civil"],"ex":["The two brothers had an acrimonious argument over who should inherit the family land.","After an acrimonious meeting, the committee members left without speaking to one another.","Their business partnership ended in an acrimonious split, and they still avoid each other."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"acronym","p":"noun","d":"A word made from the first letters of a name or phrase, such as radar or laser.","lb":"initials, abbreviation","s":["abbreviation","initials"],"k":["abridged name","alphabet soup","clipping","code name"],"a":[],"ex":["The word laser is an acronym for light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation.","Our teacher asked us to make an acronym to remember the steps of the experiment.","Text messages are full of acronyms that older relatives may not understand."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"acumen","p":"noun","d":"The ability to understand a situation quickly and make sharp, accurate judgments.","lb":"shrewdness, insight","s":["insight","sharpness","judgment","perception","cleverness","wisdom"],"k":["acuity","canniness","discernment","intuition"],"a":["foolishness","stupidity","ignorance","dullness"],"ex":["Her business acumen helped the small shop grow into three branches in five years.","The coach showed great tactical acumen by changing the formation at halftime.","Investors admire the young founder's financial acumen."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"acute","p":"adjective","d":"Sharp and keen; quick to notice and understand small details.","lb":"sharp, keen","s":["keen","sharp","sensitive","perceptive","astute","shrewd"],"k":["ardent","clever","critical","discriminating"],"a":["dull","blunt","insensitive","obtuse"],"ex":["Dogs have an acute sense of smell and can find things people cannot.","She has an acute mind for numbers and spots errors in a spreadsheet at once.","The old fisherman's acute hearing warned him of the storm before anyone else noticed."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"ad hoc","p":"adjective","d":"Created or done for one particular purpose or situation, rather than as part of a regular plan.","lb":"improvised, temporary","s":["improvised","impromptu","makeshift","provisional","temporary","unplanned"],"k":["case-by-case","emergency","interim","jury-rigged"],"a":["permanent","standing","planned","systematic"],"ex":["The school formed an ad hoc committee to organize a farewell party for the retiring principal.","Our team has no fixed schedule, so we hold ad hoc meetings whenever a problem comes up.","After the road flooded, neighbors built an ad hoc bridge from bamboo poles and wooden planks."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"ad-lib","p":"verb","d":"To say or do something without preparing it beforehand, making it up as you go.","lb":"improvise, extemporize","s":["improvise","wing it","make up","speak off the cuff","play it by ear","invent"],"k":["busk","chance it","devise","do"],"a":["rehearse","prepare","script","plan"],"ex":["The host forgot his script and had to ad-lib for five minutes.","The actor ad-libbed a funny line that wasn't in the play.","She ad-libbed her speech when the projector stopped working."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"adamant","p":"adjective","d":"Refusing to change your mind, however much people try to persuade you.","lb":"unyielding, firm","s":["firm","resolute","stubborn","unyielding","determined","insistent"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","dogged","dour"],"a":["flexible","yielding","wavering","hesitant"],"ex":["Rafi was adamant that he would walk to school, even in the heavy rain.","The manager remained adamant about the deadline, despite the team's complaints.","My grandmother is adamant that fresh fish tastes better than frozen fish."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"adapt","p":"verb","d":"To change something, or yourself, to suit a new situation or purpose.","lb":"adjust, modify","s":["adjust","modify","alter","acclimatize","convert","tailor"],"k":["amend","change","conform","mold"],"a":[],"ex":["It took me a few weeks to adapt to the cold weather abroad.","The teacher had to adapt her lesson for students learning online.","Animals in the desert adapt to the heat in remarkable ways."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"address","p":"verb","d":"To speak to a person or group formally, or to begin dealing with a problem.","lb":"speak, tackle","s":["speak to","tackle","deal with","handle","confront","approach"],"k":["accost","broach","call","come up to"],"a":["ignore","avoid","neglect","overlook"],"ex":["The principal will address the students about the new rules at Monday's assembly.","The city council must address the problem of flooded streets before the monsoon.","She addressed the crowd calmly, even though her hands were shaking."],"b":272,"y":0},{"w":"adduce","p":"verb","d":"To mention something as evidence or as an example to support an argument.","lb":"cite, present","s":["cite","present","offer","quote","mention","advance"],"k":["bear witness","prove","refer to","show"],"a":["withhold","conceal","suppress"],"ex":["In her essay she adduced several studies to prove that sleep improves memory.","The lawyer adduced bank records as evidence that the payment had been made.","To defend his plan, the engineer adduced the success of similar bridges in other countries."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"adept","p":"adjective","d":"Very good at doing something that needs skill or practice.","lb":"skilled, proficient","s":["skilled","proficient","expert","adroit","deft","accomplished"],"k":["competent","dexterous","experienced","good"],"a":["unskilled","inept","clumsy","incompetent"],"ex":["My sister is adept at fixing computer problems.","The rickshaw puller was adept at weaving through the crowded lanes.","She became adept in three languages before she was twenty."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"adequately","p":"adverb","d":"In a way that is good enough or enough for a particular purpose.","lb":"sufficiently, well enough","s":["sufficiently","satisfactorily","decently","reasonably","enough"],"k":["fairly","moderately","properly","respectably"],"a":["inadequately","poorly","badly"],"ex":["She felt adequately prepared for the test after two weeks of revision.","Make sure the room is adequately lit before you start reading.","The hospital cannot adequately care for all patients with so few nurses."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"adherent","p":"noun","d":"A person who supports and follows a particular leader, idea, belief or group.","lb":"follower, supporter","s":["follower","supporter","disciple","believer","devotee","advocate"],"k":["acolyte","ally","apostle","faithful"],"a":["opponent","critic","adversary"],"ex":["He is a firm adherent of the idea that students should learn by doing.","The new diet has many adherents who swear that it changed their lives.","Adherents of the club's training method wake up at five and run before breakfast."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"adjourn","p":"verb","d":"To stop a meeting, trial or discussion for a period, planning to continue it later.","lb":"suspend, postpone","s":["suspend","postpone","break off","defer","put off","recess"],"k":["break up","call a halt","cease","discontinue"],"a":["continue","resume","reconvene","proceed"],"ex":["The judge adjourned the hearing until Monday.","The committee adjourned the meeting for lunch.","The principal adjourned the assembly because of the heavy rain."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"adjunct","p":"noun","d":"Something added to a main thing that is useful but not an essential part of it.","lb":"addition, supplement","s":["addition","supplement","complement","accessory","appendage","extra"],"k":["accompaniment","appurtenance","assistant","attachment"],"a":[],"ex":["The mobile app is a useful adjunct to classroom lessons, not a replacement for them.","Physiotherapy is often used as an adjunct to medicine in treating back pain.","A fingerprint scanner is a handy adjunct to the usual password system."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"admonish","p":"verb","d":"To tell someone firmly but kindly that they have done something wrong or should behave better.","lb":"scold, warn","s":["reprimand","rebuke","scold","chide","reprove","caution"],"k":["advise","bawl out","berate","call down"],"a":["praise","commend","applaud","compliment"],"ex":["The teacher gently admonished the class for talking while the guest speaker was presenting.","My mother admonished me not to stay up too late before the exam.","The referee admonished the player for arguing but did not show a card."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"adopt","p":"verb","d":"To start using a new idea, method, plan or habit as your own.","lb":"take up, embrace","s":["embrace","take up","accept","assume","choose","espouse"],"k":["abide by","acquire","borrow","comply"],"a":["reject","abandon","discard","renounce"],"ex":["The school has adopted a new method for teaching English.","Many companies adopted online meetings after the lockdown.","My brother adopted a strict study routine before the admission test."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"adroit","p":"adjective","d":"Quick, clever and skillful in the way one acts or thinks, especially in difficult situations.","lb":"skillful, clever","s":["skillful","deft","dexterous","adept","nimble","clever"],"k":["agile","artful","clean","coordinated"],"a":["clumsy","inept","awkward","bungling"],"ex":["The adroit waiter carried six plates through the crowded restaurant without spilling anything.","She gave an adroit answer to the tricky interview question and kept the panel smiling.","Rafi is adroit at fixing phones, so his friends always bring their broken screens to him."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"adulation","p":"noun","d":"Excessive praise and admiration, often insincere or given to win favor.","lb":"flattery, hero-worship","s":["flattery","worship","praise","devotion","fawning","adoration"],"k":["applause","blandishment","compliment","gushing"],"a":["criticism","contempt","scorn","ridicule"],"ex":["The young singer enjoyed the adulation of thousands of fans after her first hit.","Too much adulation can make a young athlete forget to keep training.","He accepted the crowd's adulation with a polite smile."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"adulterate","p":"verb","d":"To make food, drink or another product worse by secretly adding something cheap or harmful to it.","lb":"contaminate, debase","s":["contaminate","debase","taint","dilute","pollute","corrupt"],"k":["bastardize","bulk out","cut","extend"],"a":["purify","refine","clean","cleanse"],"ex":["Some dishonest sellers adulterate milk with water and starch to increase their profit.","The inspectors found that the spice powder had been adulterated with colored sawdust.","Police arrested the shopkeeper for adulterating cooking oil with a cheaper, unsafe substance."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"advent","p":"noun","d":"The arrival of an important person, event, invention or period of time.","lb":"arrival, coming","s":["arrival","coming","appearance","emergence","onset","dawn"],"k":["approach","approaching","debut","genesis"],"a":["departure","end","disappearance","decline"],"ex":["The advent of smartphones changed the way students look for information.","With the advent of winter, vendors begin selling pitha on street corners.","The advent of cheap flights made foreign travel possible for ordinary families."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"adventitious","p":"adjective","d":"Happening by chance or coming from outside, rather than being a natural or planned part of something.","lb":"accidental, chance","s":["accidental","chance","incidental","fortuitous","casual","external"],"k":["coincidental","extraneous","foreign","inadvertent"],"a":["inherent","intrinsic","planned","essential"],"ex":["The botanist pointed out the adventitious roots growing from the stem of the plant.","The discovery of the new medicine was adventitious; the scientists were actually looking for something else.","His success was largely adventitious, the result of being in the right place at the right time."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"adversarial","p":"adjective","d":"Involving two sides that oppose each other and compete or fight.","lb":"opposing, hostile","s":["hostile","antagonistic","opposing","confrontational","combative","competitive"],"k":["aggressive","bellicose","contrary","factional"],"a":["cooperative","friendly","collaborative","amicable"],"ex":["The two companies had an adversarial relationship and rarely spoke to each other.","A court trial is an adversarial process in which each side presents its case.","The coach wanted a friendly game, not an adversarial one."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"adversary","p":"noun","d":"A person, team or group that you compete or fight against.","lb":"opponent, enemy","s":["opponent","enemy","rival","foe","antagonist","competitor"],"k":["aggressor","belligerent","bugbear","combatant"],"a":["ally","friend","supporter","partner"],"ex":["In the final, our team faced its old adversary from the neighboring school.","The chess champion treated every adversary with respect.","The two shopkeepers became adversaries after a dispute over customers."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"adverse","p":"adjective","d":"Harmful or unfavorable to someone or something, working against their success or health.","lb":"harmful, unfavorable","s":["harmful","unfavorable","negative","hostile","detrimental","unfortunate"],"k":["antagonistic","contrary","critical","hazardous"],"a":["favorable","beneficial","helpful","advantageous"],"ex":["The medicine can have adverse effects, such as headaches and an upset stomach.","Adverse weather forced the ferry to stay in the port overnight.","The movie received adverse reviews, and few people went to see it."],"b":82,"y":2},{"w":"advocate","p":"verb","d":"To publicly support or recommend a particular plan, idea or way of doing something.","lb":"support, recommend","s":["support","promote","champion","recommend","endorse","back"],"k":["advise","assist","defend","encourage"],"a":["oppose","criticize","discourage","reject"],"ex":["Doctors advocate drinking plenty of water during the hot summer months.","Our teacher advocates reading a short passage aloud every day to improve fluency.","The group advocates cleaner public transport in the city."],"b":226,"y":1},{"w":"aesthetic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to beauty and the appreciation of it, especially in art, design or nature.","lb":"artistic, beautiful","s":["artistic","tasteful","stylish","beautiful","decorative","visual"],"k":["cosmetic","exquisite","eye-catching","fashionable"],"a":["ugly","tasteless","unattractive"],"ex":["The architect chose white walls and wooden floors for their aesthetic appeal as much as their cost.","Many people buy that phone for its aesthetic design, not just its camera.","The village pond has great aesthetic value, with lotus flowers floating on its still water."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"affable","p":"adjective","d":"Friendly, pleasant and easy to talk to.","lb":"friendly, approachable","s":["friendly","amiable","genial","approachable","cordial","warm"],"k":["congenial","gregarious","jovial","outgoing"],"a":["unfriendly","cold","aloof","surly"],"ex":["The affable shopkeeper chatted with every customer and always offered them tea.","Our new neighbor is so affable that he knew everyone on the street within a week.","The doctor's affable manner helped nervous patients relax."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"affectation","p":"noun","d":"Behavior, speech or style that is put on to impress other people and is not natural.","lb":"pretense, artificiality","s":["pretense","pretension","show","posturing","artificiality","airs"],"k":["artifice","facade","feigning","phoniness"],"a":["sincerity","simplicity","honesty"],"ex":["His foreign accent was an affectation; he had never lived abroad.","She wore dark glasses indoors as an affectation, hoping to look mysterious.","The restaurant's fancy French menu felt like an affectation to most customers."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"affected","p":"adjective","d":"Behaving or speaking in an artificial way in order to impress other people.","lb":"artificial, pretentious","s":["artificial","pretentious","mannered","unnatural","pompous","insincere"],"k":["constrained","contrived","forced","grandiose"],"a":["natural","genuine","sincere","unaffected"],"ex":["He spoke in an affected accent that nobody believed was his real one.","Her affected laugh made the whole room feel uncomfortable at the dinner.","The actor's affected manner on stage made the sad scene seem false."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"affidavit","p":"noun","d":"A written statement that you swear is true, signed in front of an official, for use in a court.","lb":"sworn statement","s":["sworn statement","deposition","testimony","written oath","declaration","statement under oath"],"k":["affirmation","attested statement","certification","instrument"],"a":[],"ex":["The witness signed an affidavit swearing that she had seen the accident.","To change your name, you may need to submit an affidavit to the court.","The lawyer asked each neighbor to sign an affidavit about the boundary of the land."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"affiliate","p":"verb","d":"To join or connect a person or smaller organization closely to a larger group.","lb":"join, associate","s":["associate","join","connect","ally","link","unite"],"k":["absorb","consort","enlist","federate"],"a":["separate","disconnect","detach","disassociate"],"ex":["The small clinic decided to affiliate with a large hospital to share equipment and doctors.","Our college is affiliated with the national university, so degrees are awarded in its name.","She does not want to affiliate with any club, so she prefers to stay independent."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"affinity","p":"noun","d":"A natural liking for something or someone, or a close similarity between two things.","lb":"attraction, similarity","s":["liking","fondness","attraction","rapport","kinship","similarity"],"k":["attractive force","chemical attraction","chemistry","closeness"],"a":["aversion","dislike","antipathy","hostility"],"ex":["Even as a child, Nadia had a natural affinity for numbers and loved solving puzzles.","The two cousins felt a strong affinity because they shared the same sense of humor.","Linguists noticed an affinity between the two village dialects, even though they sound quite different."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"affliction","p":"noun","d":"Something that causes pain or suffering, such as an illness or a hardship.","lb":"suffering, ailment","s":["suffering","ailment","illness","trouble","hardship","misery"],"k":["adversity","agony","anguish","curse"],"a":["blessing","relief","comfort","health"],"ex":["Asthma has been an affliction of hers since childhood, but she still plays sports.","The old man bore his affliction patiently and never complained about the pain.","Poverty is a constant affliction for families who live along the railway line."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"affluent","p":"adjective","d":"Having a lot of money and a comfortable standard of living.","lb":"wealthy, prosperous","s":["wealthy","rich","prosperous","comfortable","opulent","flush"],"k":["easy","high-income","loaded","luxurious"],"a":["poor","impoverished","needy","destitute"],"ex":["The school draws students from affluent families as well as from poor ones.","She grew up in an affluent neighborhood with big houses and tree-lined streets.","Affluent shoppers filled the mall before Eid, buying expensive clothes."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"afford","p":"verb","d":"To give or provide something, such as a view, an opportunity, protection or pleasure.","lb":"provide, give","s":["provide","give","offer","supply","grant","yield"],"k":["bring","deliver","donate","equip"],"a":["withhold","deny","refuse","deprive"],"ex":["The balcony affords a wide view of the river and the sunset.","A university degree affords graduates more choices when they look for work.","The thick walls afford protection from the summer heat."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"affront","p":"noun","d":"A deliberate act or remark that shows disrespect and makes someone feel insulted.","lb":"insult, slight","s":["insult","slight","offence","snub","indignity","slur"],"k":["aspersion","barb","dig","discourtesy"],"a":["compliment","tribute","flattery","praise"],"ex":["Leaving the meeting without a word was an affront to everyone who had waited for him.","The villagers saw the new rule as an affront to their traditions.","She took his joke about her accent as a personal affront."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aficionado","p":"noun","d":"A person who is very interested in and knows a lot about a particular activity or subject.","lb":"devoted fan, enthusiast","s":["enthusiast","fan","devotee","buff","connoisseur","admirer"],"k":["addict","groupie","junkie","maven"],"a":[],"ex":["My uncle is a cricket aficionado who remembers the score of every match since the nineties.","Coffee aficionados line up early to taste the new roast at the small café.","As an aficionado of old Bangla films, she owns hundreds of rare posters."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"aftermath","p":"noun","d":"The period of time or the situation that follows an important, usually unpleasant, event.","lb":"consequences, fallout","s":["consequences","result","wake","outcome","repercussions","fallout"],"k":["backwash","consequence","effect","event"],"a":["cause","origin","beginning","prelude"],"ex":["In the aftermath of the cyclone, volunteers brought food and clean water.","In the aftermath of the exam, students gathered to compare their answers.","The company struggled in the aftermath of the scandal."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"agenda","p":"noun","d":"A list of things to be discussed at a meeting, or a plan of things to be done.","lb":"plan, schedule","s":["schedule","program","plan","list of items","timetable","order of business"],"k":["course","itinerary","lineup","programme"],"a":[],"ex":["The first item on the agenda was the school's new rules about mobile phones.","Please send me the agenda before the meeting so I can prepare my points.","My agenda for the weekend is simple: sleep late, clean my room and call my grandparents."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"aggrandize","p":"verb","d":"To make someone or something seem more powerful, important or impressive than it really is.","lb":"exaggerate, inflate","s":["exaggerate","inflate","magnify","glorify","embellish","enlarge"],"k":["amplify","blow up","build up","dignify"],"a":["belittle","diminish","downplay","humble"],"ex":["He tried to aggrandize his role in the project by claiming he had done most of the work.","Some job seekers aggrandize their skills on their resumes and then cannot do the tasks.","The company's advertisement aggrandizes a very ordinary product with bold promises."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"aggravate","p":"verb","d":"To make a bad situation, illness or problem worse.","lb":"worsen, intensify","s":["worsen","exacerbate","intensify","compound","inflame","magnify"],"k":["add to","alter","amplify","change"],"a":["improve","relieve","ease","alleviate"],"ex":["Walking on a sprained ankle will only aggravate the injury.","Cold air can aggravate asthma, so cover your face in winter.","Shouting at the driver will only aggravate the situation."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"aggravated","p":"adjective","d":"Made worse or more serious, especially an injury, problem or crime.","lb":"made worse","s":["worsened","exacerbated","intensified","heightened","inflamed","compounded"],"k":["angry","egregious","flagrant","grave"],"a":["eased","relieved","soothed","improved"],"ex":["The court gave a longer sentence for aggravated assault than for a simple fight.","His aggravated knee injury kept him out of the cricket team for two months.","The aggravated rash became so painful that she went back to the clinic."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"aggregate","p":"verb","d":"To gather separate things into one group, or to add up to a total amount.","lb":"gather, accumulate","s":["gather","collect","amass","accumulate","combine","assemble"],"k":["build up","come","congregate","convene"],"a":["disperse","scatter","separate","divide"],"ex":["The website aggregates news from dozens of sources so readers can see everything in one place.","Small donations from hundreds of students aggregated to more than fifty thousand taka.","In still water, tiny particles of clay aggregate into larger clumps and sink to the bottom."],"b":147,"y":0},{"w":"aggrieve","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone unfairly so that they feel hurt, angry or wronged.","lb":"wrong, upset","s":["wrong","offend","injure","mistreat","oppress","distress"],"k":["abuse","exploit","grieve","hurt"],"a":["please","satisfy","appease","compensate"],"ex":["The tenants felt aggrieved when the landlord raised the rent without any warning.","Being passed over for promotion aggrieved him for months.","The unfair decision aggrieved the whole team, and they asked the referee for an explanation."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aghast","p":"adjective","d":"Filled with shock and horror at something you have seen or heard.","lb":"horrified, shocked","s":["horrified","appalled","shocked","stunned","dismayed","astounded"],"k":["afraid","agog","amazed","astonished"],"a":["unconcerned","delighted","calm","indifferent"],"ex":["She was aghast when she saw the size of the electricity bill.","Parents were aghast to learn that the canteen had served spoiled food.","Nadia was aghast to find her phone missing from her bag on the crowded bus."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"agile","p":"adjective","d":"Able to move quickly and easily, or to think and adapt fast.","lb":"nimble, quick","s":["nimble","spry","quick","sprightly","limber","lively"],"k":["active","brisk","deft","fast"],"a":["clumsy","awkward","stiff","slow"],"ex":["The agile goalkeeper dived to his left and saved the penalty.","Monkeys are so agile that they leap between branches without ever slipping.","She is mentally agile and can switch from one problem to another in seconds."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"agitate","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel worried, upset or nervous.","lb":"disturb, upset","s":["disturb","upset","unsettle","trouble","fluster","ruffle"],"k":["bother","budge","charge up","crusade"],"a":["calm","soothe","comfort","pacify"],"ex":["The loud argument next door agitated the baby and woke her up.","News of the layoffs agitated the staff throughout the morning.","Don't agitate your grandfather by talking about the missing wallet."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"agnostic","p":"noun","d":"A person who believes it is impossible to know whether God exists or not.","lb":"doubter, skeptic","s":["skeptic","unbeliever"],"k":["humanist","individual","mortal","nonbeliever"],"a":["believer"],"ex":["My roommate calls himself an agnostic because he says nobody can truly know whether God exists.","As an agnostic, she attends her friends’ festivals out of respect and curiosity rather than belief.","In the survey, a few students described themselves as agnostics who were unsure about life after death."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"agonize","p":"verb","d":"To worry or think painfully for a long time before making a decision.","lb":"worry painfully","s":["worry","fret","brood","struggle","suffer","wrestle"],"k":["dither","mull over","ruminate","second-guess"],"a":[],"ex":["She agonized for days over whether to accept the job abroad.","Rafi agonized over every answer on the multiple-choice paper.","Parents often agonize over which school is best for their children."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"agrarian","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to farming or to the ownership and use of farmland.","lb":"agricultural, farming","s":["agricultural","rural","farming","rustic","pastoral","country"],"k":["agronomic","bucolic","feudal","land-based"],"a":["urban","industrial","metropolitan","city"],"ex":["Bangladesh was largely an agrarian society for centuries, with most families living off the land.","In an agrarian economy, a poor harvest can affect almost everyone.","The history lesson explained how agrarian reforms changed who could own farmland."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"al fresco","p":"adjective","d":"Taking place outdoors, in the open air, especially when talking about a meal.","lb":"outdoor, open-air","s":["outdoor","outdoors","outside","in the open","out of doors"],"k":["alfresco","en plein air","exterior","external"],"a":["indoor","indoors","inside","enclosed"],"ex":["On sunny weekends the cafe by the lake offers al fresco dining under colorful umbrellas.","The school hosted an al fresco concert on the lawn, and parents brought their own blankets.","Nadia loves al fresco breakfasts on the rooftop terrace before the city gets hot."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"alacrity","p":"noun","d":"Quick and cheerful readiness to do something.","lb":"eagerness, promptness","s":["eagerness","readiness","willingness","enthusiasm","promptness","zeal"],"k":["alertness","celerity","dispatch","fervor"],"a":["reluctance","hesitation","unwillingness","apathy"],"ex":["When Mom asked for help carrying the shopping, my brother agreed with alacrity.","The staff responded to the customer's complaint with alacrity and fixed the problem within the hour.","Nadia took up the offer of a free ticket to the science fair with alacrity."],"b":91,"y":1},{"w":"alchemy","p":"noun","d":"A process that changes something into something better in a way that seems almost magical.","lb":"transformation, magic","s":["transformation","magic","conversion","metamorphosis","sorcery"],"k":["chemistry","enchantment","interpersonal chemistry","legerdemain"],"a":[],"ex":["It was pure alchemy: she turned a pile of scrap cloth into a stunning dress.","The alchemy of spices and slow cooking turned simple lentils into a rich dish.","Medieval alchemy tried, without success, to turn lead into gold."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"alienate","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel unfriendly, distant or unwelcome, so that they no longer like or support you.","lb":"estrange, antagonize","s":["estrange","antagonize","isolate","distance","drive away","turn off"],"k":["alter","annoy","change","disaffect"],"a":["win over","attract","unite","befriend"],"ex":["Constant bragging can alienate even your closest friends.","The shop alienated loyal customers by suddenly doubling its prices.","Her harsh criticism alienated the new team members, and several of them quit."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"allay","p":"verb","d":"To reduce or calm a feeling such as fear, worry or doubt.","lb":"calm, relieve","s":["calm","soothe","ease","relieve","alleviate","quiet"],"k":["appease","console","lessen","mitigate"],"a":["intensify","heighten","aggravate","arouse"],"ex":["The doctor spoke gently to allay the patient's fear before the operation.","The bank issued a statement to allay customers' worries about their savings.","A quick call home allayed my mother's concern that I had missed my bus."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"allege","p":"verb","d":"To state that someone did something wrong, without giving proof.","lb":"claim, assert","s":["claim","assert","maintain","charge","accuse","contend"],"k":["argue","aver","avow","hint"],"a":["deny","disprove","refute","retract"],"ex":["The report alleges that the company dumped waste into the river at night.","Police allege that the man used a fake name to open several accounts.","She alleged that her neighbor had been playing loud music after midnight, but she had no recording."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"alleged","p":"adjective","d":"Said to be true or to have happened, but not yet proved.","lb":"claimed, supposed","s":["claimed","supposed","purported","reported","so-called","ostensible"],"k":["declared","presumed","putative","questionable"],"a":["proven","confirmed","established","verified"],"ex":["The police are investigating the alleged theft of three motorbikes from the market.","The alleged cheating in the exam hall led the school to hold an inquiry.","The company denied the alleged pollution of the river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"allegiance","p":"noun","d":"Loyalty and support that you give to a person, group, country or cause.","lb":"loyalty, devotion","s":["loyalty","fidelity","devotion","faithfulness","commitment","obedience"],"k":["attachment","cooperation","dedication","esprit de corps"],"a":["disloyalty","betrayal","treachery","infidelity"],"ex":["Fans show their allegiance to the team by wearing its colors on match days.","Citizens pledge allegiance to the constitution when they take their oath.","His allegiance to his friends was so strong that he never gossiped about them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"allegory","p":"noun","d":"A story, poem or picture in which characters and events stand for deeper ideas, often about morals or society.","lb":"symbolic story, parable","s":["parable","fable","symbolic tale","metaphor","symbolism","analogy"],"k":["apologue","cautionary tale","conceit","dream vision"],"a":[],"ex":["The story of the tortoise and the hare is a simple allegory about steady effort.","In the play, the broken bridge is an allegory for the broken friendship between the two families.","Our literature teacher asked us to explain the allegory hidden in the children's story."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"alleviate","p":"verb","d":"To make pain, difficulty or a problem less severe.","lb":"relieve, ease","s":["relieve","ease","lessen","soothe","reduce","mitigate"],"k":["ameliorate","amend","assuage","decrease"],"a":["aggravate","worsen","intensify","exacerbate"],"ex":["A warm cup of ginger tea can alleviate a sore throat.","The new bus route should alleviate traffic congestion near the university gate.","Regular exercise helped alleviate his stress during the final exam period."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"allocate","p":"verb","d":"To officially give a share of money, time or resources for a particular purpose.","lb":"assign, allot","s":["assign","allot","distribute","apportion","designate","earmark"],"k":["appoint","appropriate","deal out","delegate"],"a":["withhold","retain","hoard","keep back"],"ex":["The school will allocate extra funds to repair the science laboratory.","I allocate two hours every evening for English practice.","The manager allocated each team member a different task for the project."],"b":152,"y":0},{"w":"allot","p":"verb","d":"To give out a share or amount of something, such as time, money, land or work, to people.","lb":"assign, allocate","s":["allocate","assign","distribute","apportion","give out","share out"],"k":["accord","administer","appropriate","deal out"],"a":["withhold","keep","retain","hoard"],"ex":["The teacher allotted twenty minutes to each question in the practice test.","The council allotted a small plot of land to each flood-affected family.","Each student was allotted a locker at the start of the term."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"alloy","p":"noun","d":"A metal made by mixing two or more metals, or a metal and another element.","lb":"metal mixture","s":["blend","mixture","compound","amalgam","composite","fusion"],"k":["brass","bronze","metal","pewter"],"a":[],"ex":["Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc, and it is often used for door handles.","Steel is stronger than pure iron because it is an alloy containing a little carbon.","Bike makers use a light aluminum alloy to keep the frame strong but easy to carry."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"allude","p":"verb","d":"To mention something in an indirect way, without naming it directly.","lb":"hint, refer","s":["refer","hint","suggest","imply","mention","touch on"],"k":["bear on","call to mind","cite","come to"],"a":["state","declare","spell out","name"],"ex":["In his speech, the principal alluded to some problems but did not name anyone.","When my aunt talks about the wedding, she often alludes to how expensive it was.","The poem alludes to an old folk tale about a river and a boatman."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"allusion","p":"noun","d":"A brief, indirect reference to a person, event or work of literature, without naming it fully.","lb":"reference, hint","s":["reference","mention","hint","suggestion","citation","nod"],"k":["comment","cross-reference","echo","evocation"],"a":[],"ex":["The poem contains an allusion to a famous love story that every student knows.","His joke about meeting his Waterloo was an allusion to Napoleon's famous defeat.","She made an allusion to last year's trip, and we all started laughing."],"b":88,"y":1},{"w":"ally","p":"noun","d":"A person, group or country that helps and supports another, especially in a difficult situation.","lb":"partner, supporter","s":["partner","friend","supporter","associate","collaborator","confederate"],"k":["bedfellow","cohort","companion","confidant"],"a":["enemy","opponent","rival","adversary"],"ex":["In the dispute with the landlord, our neighbors were strong allies.","The two countries have been close allies for many decades.","A good mentor can be your best ally in a new job."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"aloof","p":"adjective","d":"Distant and unfriendly, or choosing not to get involved with other people or their activities.","lb":"distant, detached","s":["distant","detached","remote","reserved","standoffish","cool"],"k":["chilly","cold","haughty","isolated"],"a":["friendly","warm","sociable","approachable"],"ex":["New students often feel that the older classmates are aloof and unwelcoming.","He stayed aloof from the office gossip and focused on his work.","The aloof manager rarely spoke to staff or joined them at lunch."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"altercation","p":"noun","d":"A noisy, angry argument, often in public.","lb":"quarrel, row","s":["quarrel","argument","row","dispute","squabble","clash"],"k":["bicker","brawl","conflict","difference"],"a":["agreement","harmony","peace","accord"],"ex":["The two drivers got into an altercation over a small dent in a car.","An altercation between two shopkeepers over parking space drew a crowd.","A heated altercation broke out in the queue when someone tried to push in."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"altruism","p":"noun","d":"Unselfish concern for the welfare of others, shown through helpful actions.","lb":"selflessness, charity","s":["selflessness","generosity","charity","kindness","benevolence","philanthropy"],"k":["beneficence","compassion","largesse","magnanimity"],"a":["selfishness","greed","egotism"],"ex":["Donating blood to strangers is an act of pure altruism.","The students' altruism shone when they gave up their holiday to teach street children.","Some scientists study whether animals show altruism by sharing food with others."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"amalgamate","p":"verb","d":"To combine two or more organizations, groups or things into one.","lb":"merge, combine","s":["merge","combine","unite","fuse","blend","integrate"],"k":["alter","change","flux","link"],"a":["separate","divide","split","disperse"],"ex":["The two small banks decided to amalgamate so they could compete with the larger lenders.","Several local schools were amalgamated into one large school with better facilities.","The chef amalgamates Bengali and Italian flavors in her fusion menu."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"amalgamation","p":"noun","d":"The joining together of two or more organisations, companies or things to form one larger whole.","lb":"merger, union","s":["merger","union","fusion","combination","consolidation","blend"],"k":["alliance","coalescence","conflation","incorporation"],"a":["separation","split","division","breakup"],"ex":["The amalgamation of the two small banks created a stronger company with more branches.","After the amalgamation of the schools, students from both campuses shared one large building.","Workers feared job losses when they heard news of the amalgamation of the two factories."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"amass","p":"verb","d":"To gather together a large amount of something over time.","lb":"accumulate, collect","s":["accumulate","collect","gather","hoard","stockpile","pile up"],"k":["accrue","bank","compile","conglomerate"],"a":["scatter","squander","spend","waste"],"ex":["Over twenty years, my grandfather amassed a collection of more than two thousand old coins.","She amassed a fortune by selling spices to restaurants across the country.","Investigators amassed enough evidence to prove that the invoices were fake."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"amateur","p":"noun","d":"A person who does an activity for pleasure rather than as a paid job.","lb":"hobbyist, nonprofessional","s":["hobbyist","enthusiast","layman","novice","dilettante"],"k":["bungler","greenhorn","layperson","learner"],"a":["professional","expert","pro","specialist"],"ex":["My uncle is an amateur photographer who takes pictures of birds every weekend.","The amateur team beat the professionals in a surprising match.","As an amateur cook, she experiments with new recipes on Fridays."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"ambidextrous","p":"adjective","d":"Able to use the right hand and the left hand equally well.","lb":"two-handed, dexterous","s":["dexterous","adroit","deft","handy","skillful"],"k":["adept","agile","clever","deceitful"],"a":[],"ex":["My cousin is ambidextrous and can write neatly with either hand.","An ambidextrous bowler can surprise the batsman by switching arms in the same over.","She is ambidextrous, so she paints with her left hand when her right hand gets tired."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ambience","p":"noun","d":"The character and mood of a place, and the feeling it gives you.","lb":"atmosphere, mood","s":["atmosphere","mood","feel","air","setting","aura"],"k":["ambiance","climate","condition","disposition"],"a":[],"ex":["The little tea stall has a warm ambience, with soft music and the smell of ginger tea.","We chose the restaurant for its quiet ambience, which made conversation easy.","Fairy lights and flowers gave the wedding hall a cheerful ambience."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adjective","d":"Having more than one possible meaning, so that it is not clear what is intended.","lb":"unclear, vague","s":["unclear","vague","equivocal","uncertain","indefinite","cryptic"],"k":["dubious","enigmatic","evasive","forked"],"a":["clear","unambiguous","explicit","definite"],"ex":["The sign was ambiguous, so half the drivers turned left and the rest turned right.","His ambiguous reply left me unsure whether he was coming to the party or not.","Exam questions should never be ambiguous; students must know exactly what is being asked."],"b":211,"y":2},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adjective","d":"Having a strong desire to succeed, or needing a lot of effort and skill to achieve.","lb":"determined, aspiring","s":["aspiring","driven","determined","enterprising","motivated","striving"],"k":["challenging","compulsive","daring","difficult"],"a":["unambitious","lazy","modest","content"],"ex":["Nadia is an ambitious student who hopes to win a scholarship abroad.","The company has an ambitious plan to open fifty new shops this year.","He set an ambitious goal of reading one book every week."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ambivalence","p":"noun","d":"A state of having mixed or opposite feelings about something, so that you cannot decide.","lb":"uncertainty, mixed feelings","s":["uncertainty","indecision","hesitation","doubt","equivocation","wavering"],"k":["ambiguity","conflicted feelings","feeling","misgivings"],"a":["certainty","conviction","resolve","determination"],"ex":["She felt ambivalence about moving abroad, excited by the job but sad to leave her family.","Many students feel some ambivalence about the admission test: they want the seat but dread the pressure.","His ambivalence towards the new phone plan showed when he kept changing his mind."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"ambivalent","p":"adjective","d":"Having mixed or opposite feelings about something, so that you cannot make up your mind.","lb":"uncertain, conflicted","s":["uncertain","undecided","conflicted","torn","unsure","hesitant"],"k":["doubtful","half-hearted","lukewarm","noncommittal"],"a":["certain","decided","sure","decisive"],"ex":["I feel ambivalent about moving abroad: I want the opportunity but dread leaving my family.","Many students are ambivalent about online classes, enjoying the comfort but missing their friends.","She was ambivalent about the job offer because the pay was good but the hours were long."],"b":82,"y":3},{"w":"ameliorate","p":"verb","d":"To make a bad or unsatisfactory situation better.","lb":"improve, better","s":["improve","better","enhance","relieve","mitigate","upgrade"],"k":["alleviate","alter","amend","boost"],"a":["worsen","aggravate","exacerbate","damage"],"ex":["New drainage channels should ameliorate the flooding that hits the neighborhood every monsoon.","The school hopes extra tutoring will ameliorate the poor exam results in math.","Fresh paint and better lighting ameliorated the gloomy atmosphere of the waiting room."],"b":597,"y":2},{"w":"amenable","p":"adjective","d":"Willing to accept advice, suggestions or requests, and easy to persuade.","lb":"agreeable, willing","s":["agreeable","willing","receptive","open","responsive","compliant"],"k":["accommodating","adaptable","biddable","conformable"],"a":["stubborn","obstinate","uncooperative","resistant"],"ex":["The landlord was amenable to lowering the rent if we signed for another year.","Our new boss is amenable to suggestions, so the team feels free to speak up.","Children are usually more amenable to advice when it is given kindly rather than angrily."],"b":80,"y":3},{"w":"amenity","p":"noun","d":"A useful or pleasant feature of a place or building that makes life more comfortable.","lb":"facility, comfort","s":["facility","comfort","convenience","service","feature","advantage"],"k":["asset","attraction","extra","luxury"],"a":[],"ex":["The new apartment block has amenities such as a gym, a rooftop garden and a small playground.","Basic amenities like clean water and electricity are still missing in some remote villages.","The hostel’s best amenity is its fast Wi-Fi, which students use late at night."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"amiable","p":"adjective","d":"Friendly, pleasant and easy to like or get along with.","lb":"friendly, pleasant","s":["friendly","pleasant","affable","genial","agreeable","cordial"],"k":["companionable","easygoing","enjoyable","gentle"],"a":["unfriendly","hostile","surly","cold"],"ex":["Our amiable neighbor always greets everyone on the stairs with a warm smile.","The interviewers found him amiable and easy to talk to.","She is an amiable colleague who never loses her temper, even on busy days."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"amid","p":"preposition","d":"In the middle of or surrounded by something, especially during a situation.","lb":"among, surrounded by","s":["among","amidst","in the middle of","surrounded by","in the midst of","during"],"k":["engulfed by","enveloped by","in the heart of","in the thick of"],"a":[],"ex":["She found a quiet corner amid the noise of the busy market.","Amid all the excitement of the wedding, someone forgot to bring the cake.","He stayed calm amid the confusion at the airport and found the right gate."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"amity","p":"noun","d":"A friendly relationship between people, groups or countries, with no anger or conflict.","lb":"friendship, goodwill","s":["friendship","goodwill","harmony","friendliness","peace","concord"],"k":["accord","camaraderie","comity","companionship"],"a":["hostility","enmity","animosity","discord"],"ex":["The two neighbouring families have lived in amity for more than fifty years.","The treaty was signed to promote amity between the two countries.","In a spirit of amity, the rival teams shook hands after the match."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"amnesty","p":"noun","d":"An official pardon given by a government or authority to a group of people who have broken a rule or law.","lb":"pardon, forgiveness","s":["pardon","reprieve","absolution","clemency","immunity","forgiveness"],"k":["dispensation","free pardon","grace","indemnity"],"a":["punishment","penalty","sentence","conviction"],"ex":["The library announced a one-week amnesty, so overdue books could be returned without any fine.","The government granted an amnesty to workers who had stayed in the country after their visas expired.","During the weapons amnesty, people could hand in illegal guns without being punished."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"amoeba","p":"noun","d":"A tiny single-celled organism with no fixed shape that moves by pushing out parts of its body.","lb":"single-celled organism","s":["microbe"],"k":["cell","microorganism","protist","rhizopod"],"a":[],"ex":["An amoeba changes shape constantly as it moves and surrounds its food.","The teacher drew an amoeba on the board and labelled its nucleus.","Drinking dirty water can lead to illness caused by a harmful amoeba."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"amoral","p":"adjective","d":"Having no sense of right and wrong, and not caring about moral rules.","lb":"without morals","s":["unprincipled","unscrupulous","unethical","cynical"],"k":["cold-blooded","detached","dispassionate","ethically neutral"],"a":["moral","ethical","principled","virtuous"],"ex":["The villain in the story is amoral, feeling no guilt about lying or stealing.","A small child is amoral in the sense that he does not yet understand right and wrong.","The film's amoral hero cares only about winning, whoever gets hurt."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"amorous","p":"adjective","d":"Showing or feeling romantic love or desire for someone.","lb":"loving, romantic","s":["loving","romantic","passionate","affectionate","tender","fond"],"k":["adoring","amatory","fiery","flirtatious"],"a":["cold","indifferent","hostile","aloof"],"ex":["The old poems are full of amorous words that young lovers once copied into letters.","He sent his fiancée an amorous letter on their anniversary.","The film's amorous scenes were gentle and romantic, with no bad language."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"amorphous","p":"adjective","d":"Having no clear shape, form or structure.","lb":"shapeless, formless","s":["shapeless","formless","vague","nebulous","indistinct","unformed"],"k":["ambiguous","fuzzy","hazy","indefinite"],"a":["defined","distinct","shaped","structured"],"ex":["The clay was an amorphous lump until the potter began shaping it into a bowl.","Through the fog, we saw an amorphous shape moving slowly along the road.","The committee's plan was so amorphous that nobody knew what to do next."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"amputation","p":"noun","d":"The surgical removal of a part of the body, such as an arm, a leg or a finger.","lb":"limb removal","s":["removal","severing","cutting off","dismemberment","excision"],"k":["ablation","abscission","deletion","disability"],"a":[],"ex":["The surgeon explained that an amputation was the only way to stop the infection.","After the amputation of his leg, Rafi learned to walk with an artificial limb.","Untreated diabetes can sometimes lead to the amputation of a toe or foot."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"anachronism","p":"noun","d":"Something that seems out of place because it belongs to a different period of history.","lb":"outdated, relic","s":["throwback","relic","holdover","fossil","dinosaur","survival"],"k":["antique","hangover","has-been","museum piece"],"a":[],"ex":["A wristwatch in a film set in the Middle Ages would be an obvious anachronism.","In today's world of online banking, the paper passbook is almost an anachronism.","The old typewriter on her desk looks like an anachronism next to the sleek computers."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"analogous","p":"adjective","d":"Similar to something else in a way that makes a useful comparison possible.","lb":"similar, comparable","s":["comparable","similar","parallel","corresponding","equivalent","alike"],"k":["cognate","correspondent","kindred","matching"],"a":["dissimilar","different","unlike","unrelated"],"ex":["The heart works in a way analogous to a pump, pushing blood around the body.","Learning to ride a bicycle is analogous to learning a language: you improve only by practicing.","The two cases are analogous, so the court applied the same rule to both."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"analogy","p":"noun","d":"A comparison between two things that shows how they are alike, used to explain an idea.","lb":"comparison, parallel","s":["comparison","parallel","similarity","correspondence","resemblance","likeness"],"k":["allegory","comparing","doctrine of analogy","example"],"a":["difference","contrast","disparity"],"ex":["The teacher used an analogy between the heart and a pump to explain blood flow.","Comparing the internet to a library is a helpful analogy for new users.","She drew an analogy between learning a language and learning to ride a bicycle."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"anarchy","p":"noun","d":"A situation of disorder in which nobody obeys rules because no one is in charge.","lb":"chaos, lawlessness","s":["lawlessness","chaos","disorder","mayhem","turmoil","confusion"],"k":["bedlam","free-for-all","mob rule","nihilism"],"a":["order","law","government","control"],"ex":["When the lights went out in the stadium, the crowd fell into anarchy and rushed for the exits.","Without a referee, the match descended into anarchy within minutes.","The substitute teacher left the room, and the class dissolved into anarchy."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"anathema","p":"noun","d":"Something or someone that you strongly dislike or that goes completely against your beliefs.","lb":"abomination, detested thing","s":["abomination","bane","pet hate","taboo","curse","horror"],"k":["abhorrence","blight","condemnation","disgust"],"a":["blessing","delight","favourite","boon"],"ex":["Cheating is anathema to our teacher, and she never forgives it.","Waste is anathema to my grandmother, who saves every grain of rice.","Loud music is anathema to anyone trying to study for tomorrow's exam."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ancillary","p":"adjective","d":"Giving support or extra help to something more important; secondary.","lb":"supporting, additional","s":["auxiliary","supplementary","secondary","subsidiary","supporting","additional"],"k":["incidental","lesser","minor","spare"],"a":["primary","main","principal","essential"],"ex":["The hospital employs ancillary staff such as cleaners, porters and cooks.","Besides the room rent, there are ancillary costs such as electricity and internet.","The school's ancillary services include a library and a small counselling room."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"anecdote","p":"noun","d":"A short, interesting or amusing story about a real person or event.","lb":"short story, tale","s":["story","tale","yarn","account","narrative","sketch"],"k":["aside","digression","fib","narration"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandfather opened his speech with an anecdote about his first day at school.","The teacher shared a funny anecdote about her own failed exam to relax the students.","He told an amusing anecdote about getting lost in Dhaka on his first visit, and everybody laughed."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"angst","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of worry or anxiety, often about life, the future or one's place in the world.","lb":"anxiety, dread","s":["anxiety","dread","unease","worry","apprehension","anguish"],"k":["fear","malaise","nervousness","stress"],"a":["calm","serenity","contentment","peace"],"ex":["Many teenagers go through a phase of angst about their looks and their future.","Rafi felt a quiet angst every night before the admission test results were announced.","The novel captures the angst of young workers who fear they will never afford a home."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"anguish","p":"noun","d":"Severe mental or physical suffering, especially deep distress caused by loss or worry.","lb":"agony, torment","s":["agony","torment","distress","suffering","misery","grief"],"k":["angst","desolation","despair","heartbreak"],"a":["joy","delight","comfort","happiness"],"ex":["The family waited in anguish for news about the fishing boat that had not returned after the storm.","She cried out in anguish when she realized she had lost her late mother’s necklace.","The long wait for his exam results caused him weeks of anguish."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"animosity","p":"noun","d":"Strong dislike or ill will toward someone that often leads to open hostility.","lb":"hostility, ill will","s":["hostility","hatred","enmity","antagonism","resentment","ill will"],"k":["acrimony","antipathy","bile","malice"],"a":["friendship","goodwill","friendliness","affection"],"ex":["There was no animosity between the two rivals, who shook hands after the match.","Years of arguments over land created deep animosity between the two families.","She felt no animosity toward the classmate who had beaten her for first place."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"annex","p":"verb","d":"To add something to a larger thing, especially to take control of land and make it part of a bigger area.","lb":"take over, add","s":["take over","seize","appropriate","add","attach","incorporate"],"k":["arrogate","assume","claim","commandeer"],"a":["release","relinquish","detach","give up"],"ex":["The city plans to annex several nearby villages to expand its boundaries.","The neighbouring country annexed the island in the nineteenth century.","The university annexed the old hospital building to create more classrooms."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"annihilate","p":"verb","d":"To destroy something or someone completely, so that nothing is left.","lb":"destroy, wipe out","s":["destroy","obliterate","wipe out","exterminate","eradicate","demolish"],"k":["carry off","decimate","eliminate","extinguish"],"a":["create","preserve","save","protect"],"ex":["Our team annihilated the opposition and won the school final by six goals.","A strong pesticide can annihilate the insects that attack the rice crop.","A faulty update annihilated every file on my old computer."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"annotate","p":"verb","d":"To add short notes or comments to a text or diagram to explain it.","lb":"comment on, mark up","s":["comment on","gloss","footnote","mark up","explain","interpret"],"k":["caption","edit","flag","highlight"],"a":[],"ex":["Our teacher asked us to annotate the poem with notes on its main ideas.","I annotate my textbooks with colored pens so I can find key points quickly.","The editor annotated the draft with questions in the margin."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"annuity","p":"noun","d":"A fixed sum of money paid to someone each year, often after retirement, from an insurance plan or investment.","lb":"yearly income, pension","s":["pension","yearly income","allowance","annual payment","stipend","retirement income"],"k":["bonus","endowment","income stream","nest egg"],"a":[],"ex":["After retiring, he bought an annuity that pays him a fixed amount every year.","Her grandmother lives on a small annuity from her late husband's insurance plan.","An annuity can protect retired people from running out of money."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"annul","p":"verb","d":"To officially declare that a law, contract, marriage or result is no longer valid.","lb":"cancel, invalidate","s":["cancel","void","nullify","invalidate","revoke","repeal"],"k":["avoid","countermand","lift","negate"],"a":["validate","enforce","uphold","ratify"],"ex":["The court annulled the contract because one side had hidden important facts.","The exam board annulled the results after finding that the questions had leaked.","The couple asked a judge to annul their marriage after only one month."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"anoint","p":"verb","d":"To rub oil or ointment on someone, especially in a ceremony, or to choose them for an important role.","lb":"rub with oil, consecrate","s":["consecrate","sanctify","bless","ordain","hallow","oil"],"k":["appoint","crown","enthrone","install"],"a":["desecrate","defile","dishonor"],"ex":["The therapist anointed her tired shoulders with warm herbal oil.","The grandmother anointed the baby's head with a little coconut oil before the bath.","In the old tradition, a ruler was anointed with oil during the coronation ceremony."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"anomalous","p":"adjective","d":"Different from what is normal or expected, so that it is hard to explain.","lb":"abnormal, irregular","s":["abnormal","irregular","atypical","aberrant","peculiar","odd"],"k":["baffling","incongruous","inexplicable","mysterious"],"a":["normal","typical","regular","standard"],"ex":["The scientist rechecked the anomalous reading, which was far higher than all the other measurements.","It is anomalous for the river to be this low in the middle of the monsoon.","The auditor noticed several anomalous entries in the shop's accounts."],"b":65,"y":1},{"w":"anomaly","p":"noun","d":"Something that is different from what is normal or expected and cannot easily be explained.","lb":"irregularity, oddity","s":["irregularity","oddity","deviation","exception","aberration","abnormality"],"k":["curiosity","departure","divergence","enigma"],"a":["norm","rule","standard","regularity"],"ex":["One strange result in the experiment was an anomaly that the students could not explain.","A snowfall in this warm region would be a real anomaly.","The accountant noticed an anomaly in the bank statement and called the branch."],"b":90,"y":1},{"w":"antagonize","p":"verb","d":"To make someone angry or hostile towards you by what you say or do.","lb":"provoke, offend","s":["provoke","annoy","alienate","irritate","offend","aggravate"],"k":["bait","bother","chafe","counteract"],"a":["appease","placate","pacify","befriend"],"ex":["Don't antagonize the security guard; he is only following the rules.","The new rule antagonized the staff, who had not been asked for their opinion.","She did not want to antagonize her landlord by complaining about small problems."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"antecedent","p":"noun","d":"Something or someone that came before, and from which a later thing or person developed.","lb":"forerunner, precursor","s":["precursor","forerunner","predecessor","ancestor","forebear","origin"],"k":["earlier model","harbinger","herald","prelude"],"a":["descendant","successor","consequence","offspring"],"ex":["The bicycle was an early antecedent of the modern motorbike.","Historians look for the antecedents of the war in the unfair treaties that came before it.","Her antecedents were farmers, so she understands how hard rural life can be."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"antedate","p":"verb","d":"To come earlier in time than something else.","lb":"precede, predate","s":["precede","come before","go before","anticipate","forego"],"k":["antecede","be earlier than","be older than","be prior to"],"a":["follow","succeed","come after"],"ex":["The old fort antedates the nearby town by several centuries.","Fossils show that some insects antedate the dinosaurs.","Her interest in music antedates her school days, since she sang before she could talk."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"anterior","p":"adjective","d":"Situated at or near the front of something, especially a body or an organ.","lb":"front, forward","s":["front","forward","frontal","fore","foremost","leading"],"k":["bow","cephalic","forward-facing","front-facing"],"a":["posterior","rear","back","hind"],"ex":["The anterior part of the brain helps with planning and decision-making.","The dentist checked the anterior teeth, which are the ones at the front of the mouth.","The doctor examined the anterior surface of his knee, where the swelling was visible."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"anthology","p":"noun","d":"A published collection of poems, stories or songs by different writers, or chosen from one writer's work.","lb":"collection, compilation","s":["collection","compilation","selection","treasury","digest","omnibus"],"k":["assortment","florilegium","medley","potpourri"],"a":[],"ex":["Our English teacher gave us an anthology of short stories to read over the holidays.","She bought an anthology of Bangla poems at the Ekushey Book Fair.","The magazine published an anthology of its best articles from the past ten years."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"anticipated","p":"adjective","d":"Expected or looked forward to, usually with hope or excitement.","lb":"expected, awaited","s":["expected","awaited","eagerly awaited","predicted","foreseen"],"k":["forecast","forthcoming","impending","likely"],"a":["unexpected","unforeseen","surprising","unanticipated"],"ex":["The most anticipated film of the year opens in cinemas this Friday.","The long-anticipated bridge will finally open to traffic next month.","The anticipated rise in rice prices did not happen after the good harvest."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"antipathy","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of dislike or opposition towards someone or something.","lb":"dislike, hostility","s":["dislike","aversion","hostility","hatred","animosity","loathing"],"k":["abhorrence","antagonism","bitterness","disgust"],"a":["affinity","liking","sympathy","fondness"],"ex":["He felt a strong antipathy towards early mornings and avoided any class before ten.","There was open antipathy between the two managers, and meetings were often tense.","Her antipathy to crowded places explains why she never goes to the Eid market on the last night."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"antipodal","p":"adjective","d":"On the opposite side of the Earth, or completely opposite in nature or opinion.","lb":"opposite, polar","s":["opposite","contrary","polar","reverse","contradictory","counter"],"k":["at odds","clashing","conflicting","contrasting"],"a":["identical","similar","same","parallel"],"ex":["Spain and New Zealand lie at almost antipodal points on the globe.","The antipodal point of Dhaka lies deep in the Pacific Ocean.","Our views were antipodal: he loved big cities, and I loved quiet villages."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"antique","p":"adjective","d":"Made in an earlier period and valued because it is old and rare.","lb":"old, collectible","s":["vintage","old","ancient","classic","heirloom","collectible"],"k":["aged","archaic","bygone","ex"],"a":["modern","new","contemporary"],"ex":["My grandmother keeps an antique wooden chest in her bedroom.","The shop sells antique clocks that are more than a hundred years old.","He wore an antique silver ring that once belonged to his great-grandfather."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"antiquity","p":"noun","d":"Ancient times, especially before the Middle Ages, or the great age of something very old.","lb":"ancient times, oldness","s":["ancient times","the distant past","old age","olden days","great age"],"k":["age","bygone days","classical era","history"],"a":["modernity","newness","novelty","the present"],"ex":["Historians believe the city was a trading center in antiquity, thousands of years ago.","The temple’s antiquity is clear from its worn stones and faded carvings.","The museum displays tools and jewelry from antiquity found near the river."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"antiseptic","p":"adjective","d":"Preventing infection by killing germs, as in a cream or liquid used to clean wounds.","lb":"germ-killing, disinfectant","s":["disinfectant","sterilizing","cleansing","aseptic","hygienic","purifying"],"k":["clean","germfree","healthful","sanitary"],"a":["unsanitary","infectious","contaminating","septic"],"ex":["She put antiseptic cream on the cut on her knee before bandaging it.","The nurse cleaned the wound with an antiseptic solution.","Keep antiseptic wipes in your bag for emergencies while traveling."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"antithesis","p":"noun","d":"The exact opposite of something, in meaning, character or quality.","lb":"direct opposite","s":["opposite","reverse","contrary","converse","inverse","contrast"],"k":["foil","inversion","mirror image","negation"],"a":["likeness","equivalent","counterpart","twin"],"ex":["Rafi, who loves rest and quiet, is the antithesis of his noisy, energetic sister.","Fast food is the antithesis of a balanced diet.","The calm, orderly library was the antithesis of the loud canteen next door."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"apartheid","p":"noun","d":"The former South African system of laws that separated people by race and denied most rights to the Black majority.","lb":"racial segregation","s":["segregation","racial segregation","discrimination","racial discrimination","separation","racism"],"k":["bigotry","color bar","exclusion","ghettoization"],"a":["integration","equality","inclusion","racial equality"],"ex":["Under apartheid, people in South Africa were forced to live in separate areas based on race.","Our history teacher explained how protests and international pressure helped bring apartheid to an end.","The museum in Johannesburg tells the story of the long struggle against apartheid."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"apathetic","p":"adjective","d":"Showing little interest, enthusiasm or concern about anything.","lb":"indifferent, uninterested","s":["indifferent","uninterested","unconcerned","listless","passive","uncaring"],"k":["blase","bored","casual","detached"],"a":["enthusiastic","interested","concerned","passionate"],"ex":["The apathetic students stared at the board and never raised their hands.","Residents were apathetic about cleaning the lane, so the rubbish piled up.","After the long illness, he became apathetic and lost interest in his hobbies."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"apathy","p":"noun","d":"A lack of interest, enthusiasm or concern about things that should matter.","lb":"indifference","s":["indifference","lethargy","detachment","passivity","torpor","disinterest"],"k":["complacency","drowsiness","ennui","inertia"],"a":["enthusiasm","concern","interest","passion"],"ex":["Student apathy was obvious when only ten people came to the important club meeting.","Low turnout at the local election was blamed on public apathy.","After months of failure, he sank into apathy and stopped looking for work."],"b":83,"y":4},{"w":"aperture","p":"noun","d":"A small opening or hole in something, especially one that lets light or air pass through.","lb":"opening, gap","s":["opening","hole","gap","slit","crack","vent"],"k":["breach","crevice","lens opening","port"],"a":["closure","blockage","seal"],"ex":["Sunlight streamed through a narrow aperture in the wall of the old storeroom.","The mouse squeezed through a tiny aperture beneath the kitchen door.","Photographers widen the aperture of the lens when they shoot in dim light."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apex","p":"noun","d":"The highest point of something, or the point where it is at its most successful.","lb":"peak, summit","s":["peak","summit","top","pinnacle","zenith","crest"],"k":["culmination","cusp","extreme point","extremity"],"a":["base","bottom","foot","nadir"],"ex":["The apex of the triangle points directly toward the top of the page.","Winning the national prize was the apex of her writing career.","The climbers reached the apex of the hill just before sunrise."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"aphorism","p":"noun","d":"A short, clever saying that expresses a general truth.","lb":"saying, maxim","s":["saying","maxim","adage","proverb","saw","axiom"],"k":["bon mot","expression","gnome","precept"],"a":[],"ex":["My father often repeats the aphorism that slow and steady wins the race.","The poet is famous for short aphorisms that fit easily on a postcard.","An old aphorism says that time and tide wait for no one."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"apocalypse","p":"noun","d":"The total destruction of the world, or any disaster so terrible that it feels like the end of everything.","lb":"doomsday, catastrophe","s":["doomsday","cataclysm","catastrophe","calamity","devastation","end of the world"],"k":["crack of doom","day of judgement","day of judgment","day of reckoning"],"a":[],"ex":["The film is set in a world after a nuclear apocalypse, where survivors search for clean water.","After three days of flooding and load-shedding, the neighbors joked that the apocalypse had arrived.","Scientists warn that ignoring climate change could bring an environmental apocalypse to coastal cities."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"apocryphal","p":"adjective","d":"Widely told as if it were true, but probably not true and never proven to be real.","lb":"doubtful, fictitious","s":["doubtful","dubious","spurious","fictitious","unverified","legendary"],"k":["anecdotal","fabricated","false","folkloric"],"a":["authentic","genuine","true","verified"],"ex":["The story that he walked ten miles to school every day is probably apocryphal.","Many apocryphal quotes spread online are wrongly credited to famous scientists.","It is an apocryphal tale, but the whole village still tells it to visitors."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"apogee","p":"noun","d":"The highest or most successful point of something; also the point in an orbit farthest from Earth.","lb":"peak, high point","s":["peak","summit","zenith","climax","height","pinnacle"],"k":["apex","crest","heyday","high-water mark"],"a":["perigee","nadir","low point","bottom"],"ex":["The satellite is farthest from Earth at its apogee, then slowly falls closer again.","When the moon is at apogee, it looks slightly smaller in the sky.","His career reached its apogee when he became head of the hospital."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"apoplexy","p":"noun","d":"An old-fashioned word for a stroke, a sudden loss of movement and awareness caused by a problem with blood supply to the brain.","lb":"stroke","s":["stroke","cerebral haemorrhage","brain attack","seizure","fit"],"k":["brain bleed","cerebrovascular accident","cva","episode"],"a":[],"ex":["In the old novel, the wealthy merchant dies suddenly of apoplexy at the dinner table.","Doctors once called a stroke apoplexy, because it struck without any warning.","Apoplexy can leave a patient paralysed on one side of the body."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apostasy","p":"noun","d":"The abandonment of a belief, faith, party or cause that you once strongly supported.","lb":"defection, desertion","s":["defection","desertion","renunciation","betrayal","disloyalty","treason"],"k":["defiance","disaffection","dissent","forsaking"],"a":["loyalty","faithfulness","allegiance","devotion"],"ex":["Fans called it apostasy when the captain left his boyhood club to join its fiercest rival.","In his memoir, he describes his apostasy from the party he had supported for decades.","Some scientists saw her move away from the old theory as apostasy, but others praised her courage."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apotheosis","p":"noun","d":"The perfect example or highest point of something; originally, the raising of a person to the status of a god.","lb":"ideal, peak","s":["epitome","quintessence","culmination","pinnacle","peak","height"],"k":["apex","apogee","archetype","climax"],"a":["nadir","low point","depths","rock bottom"],"ex":["For many football fans, that final goal was the apotheosis of the whole tournament.","The kacchi biryani at that old Dhaka restaurant is, for many locals, the apotheosis of the dish.","Her graduation speech was the apotheosis of four years of hard work and late-night study."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"appalling","p":"adjective","d":"Shocking and very bad, causing horror or strong disapproval.","lb":"dreadful, shocking","s":["dreadful","horrifying","shocking","terrible","awful","atrocious"],"k":["abominable","alarming","dire","dreaded"],"a":["wonderful","excellent","pleasing","admirable"],"ex":["The appalling smell from the broken drain made it hard to eat lunch.","Living conditions in the old hostel were appalling, with leaking roofs and no clean water.","It was appalling to see so much food thrown away after the party."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"apparatchik","p":"noun","d":"A loyal official in a large organization or party who follows orders without question.","lb":"loyal official","s":["bureaucrat","official","administrator","company man","minion","lackey"],"k":["cadre","hack","party man","pen pusher"],"a":["maverick","rebel","dissident","nonconformist"],"ex":["The new director was a loyal apparatchik who never questioned a single order from the head office.","Nobody expected the old apparatchik to propose any bold ideas for the company.","Reporters described him as a cautious apparatchik who had never given an interview without approval."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"apparent","p":"adjective","d":"Easy to see or understand; clear to everyone.","lb":"obvious, evident","s":["obvious","evident","clear","plain","visible","noticeable"],"k":["blatant","conspicuous","distinct","lucid"],"a":["hidden","unclear","obscure","concealed"],"ex":["It soon became apparent that the old bus would not reach the town.","The tiredness on his face was apparent to everyone in the room.","Her disappointment was apparent when she read the results."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"apparently","p":"adverb","d":"Used to say that something seems to be true, although you are not completely sure.","lb":"seemingly","s":["seemingly","evidently","ostensibly","supposedly","reportedly","outwardly"],"k":["by all accounts","it appears","it would seem","obviously"],"a":["actually","really","truly","in fact"],"ex":["Apparently, the match has been postponed because of the rain.","He apparently forgot the meeting, since he never turned up.","The shop is apparently closed today; there is no one inside."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"apparition","p":"noun","d":"A ghost, or a strange image of a person or thing that suddenly appears.","lb":"ghost, phantom","s":["ghost","specter","phantom","spirit","spook","vision"],"k":["banshee","disembodied spirit","doppelganger","hallucination"],"a":[],"ex":["In the old story, an apparition in white walks along the river bank at midnight.","Through the thick fog, the lone rickshaw looked like an apparition.","She screamed when a pale apparition appeared at the window, but it was only a curtain."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"appeal","p":"noun","d":"A strong, urgent request for help, money or support, often made to the public.","lb":"request, plea","s":["plea","request","petition","call","cry","campaign"],"k":["asking","charm","collection","prayer"],"a":[],"ex":["The charity launched an appeal for blankets to help families during the cold winter.","The police made a public appeal for anyone who had seen the missing boy.","Her tearful appeal for help brought dozens of volunteers to the flood shelter."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"appease","p":"verb","d":"To calm an angry or demanding person by giving them what they want.","lb":"pacify, placate","s":["pacify","placate","calm","soothe","mollify","satisfy"],"k":["assuage","calm down","lull","quell"],"a":["provoke","anger","enrage","incite"],"ex":["The airline offered free meals to appease passengers angry about the long delay.","To appease her crying baby brother, Nadia gave him her last biscuit.","Teachers know that giving in to a bully's demands may appease him briefly but never stops him."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"appellation","p":"noun","d":"A name or title by which a person or thing is known.","lb":"name, title","s":["name","title","designation","label","tag","moniker"],"k":["christening","dub","pseudonym","sobriquet"],"a":[],"ex":["The professor preferred the appellation Doctor, since he had worked hard for the degree.","The town earned the appellation “City of Lakes” because of its many ponds.","Nobody used his formal appellation; everyone just called him Uncle Jamal."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"appendage","p":"noun","d":"Something attached to a larger or more important thing, such as a limb or an extra part.","lb":"attachment, limb","s":["attachment","addition","extension","limb","accessory","adjunct"],"k":["external body part","extremity","member","process"],"a":[],"ex":["A tail is a useful appendage that helps a monkey keep its balance.","The small shed behind the house was an appendage built many years after the main building.","Octopuses use their eight arms as flexible appendages for catching food."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"applaud","p":"verb","d":"To clap your hands to show that you enjoyed something, or to praise it.","lb":"clap, praise","s":["clap","cheer","praise","acclaim","commend","salute"],"k":["bravo","compliment","extol","gesticulate"],"a":["boo","criticize","condemn","jeer"],"ex":["The audience stood up to applaud the young singer.","Parents applauded loudly when their children finished the school play.","I applaud your decision to apologise to your friend."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"apportion","p":"verb","d":"To divide something and share it out among people according to a plan, need or fairness.","lb":"allocate, distribute","s":["allocate","distribute","share out","divide","allot","assign"],"k":["administer","carve up","deal out","designate"],"a":["withhold","hoard","keep","retain"],"ex":["The teacher apportioned the work equally among the four members of the group.","The will apportioned the family land among the three children.","Insurance companies apportion blame after an accident to decide who pays."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apposite","p":"adjective","d":"Very suitable and relevant to the situation or subject being discussed.","lb":"appropriate, relevant","s":["appropriate","relevant","apt","fitting","pertinent","suitable"],"k":["apropos","on point","on the money","opportune"],"a":["inappropriate","irrelevant","unsuitable","out of place"],"ex":["The teacher gave an apposite example that made the difficult rule easy to understand.","Her apposite comment on the poem helped the class see its real meaning.","A proverb about patience was apposite, since we had been waiting for hours."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"appraise","p":"verb","d":"To judge the value, quality or importance of something carefully, usually as an expert.","lb":"evaluate, assess","s":["assess","evaluate","value","estimate","judge","gauge"],"k":["analyze","critique","examine","look over"],"a":["ignore","overlook","disregard"],"ex":["An expert came to appraise the antique clock before the family sold it.","The bank sent a surveyor to appraise the house before approving the loan.","Teachers appraise each student's progress at the end of the term."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"appreciate","p":"verb","d":"To increase in value over time.","lb":"increase in value","s":["increase","rise","grow","gain","climb","go up"],"k":["ascend","expand","firm up","inflate"],"a":["depreciate","decrease","fall","decline"],"ex":["Land near the new highway has appreciated sharply since the project was announced.","Antique furniture usually appreciates in value, while a new phone loses value every month.","The taka appreciated slightly against the dollar this week, making imports a little cheaper."],"b":464,"y":1},{"w":"apprehension","p":"noun","d":"A worried feeling that something unpleasant may happen in the future.","lb":"anxiety, worry","s":["anxiety","unease","worry","dread","foreboding","nervousness"],"k":["collar","fright","malaise","savvy"],"a":["confidence","calm","assurance","composure"],"ex":["She felt a growing apprehension as she waited outside the interview room.","Many parents voiced apprehension about the new exam system.","He opened the medical report with some apprehension."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"apprehensive","p":"adjective","d":"Worried or fearful that something bad may happen.","lb":"anxious, uneasy","s":["anxious","uneasy","worried","nervous","fearful","concerned"],"k":["discerning","edgy","foreboding","fretful"],"a":["confident","calm","relaxed","unafraid"],"ex":["Nadia felt apprehensive before her first day at the new school.","Passengers grew apprehensive as the plane shook in the storm.","He was apprehensive about the test results and could not eat breakfast."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"apprise","p":"verb","d":"To tell someone about something, especially recent news or changes.","lb":"inform, notify","s":["inform","notify","tell","advise","brief","update"],"k":["alert","clue in","fill in","forewarn"],"a":["keep in the dark","mislead","deceive"],"ex":["Please apprise me of any changes to the exam schedule as soon as you hear.","The doctor apprised the family of the risks before the operation.","The team leader kept the clients apprised of progress through a weekly email."],"b":101,"y":1},{"w":"approbate","p":"verb","d":"To approve of something officially or formally.","lb":"approve, sanction","s":["approve","sanction","endorse","authorize","ratify","validate"],"k":["accept","accredit","allow","bless"],"a":["disapprove","reject","veto","refuse"],"ex":["The board will approbate the new budget at its monthly meeting on Sunday.","The ministry must approbate the textbook before schools are allowed to use it.","Only after the committee approbated the proposal could the engineers begin building."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"approbation","p":"noun","d":"Formal approval or praise, especially from someone in authority.","lb":"approval, praise","s":["approval","praise","acclaim","endorsement","commendation","sanction"],"k":["authorization","benediction","blessing","go-ahead"],"a":["disapproval","condemnation","criticism","censure"],"ex":["The council's plan won the approbation of residents after a public meeting.","She waited anxiously for her teacher's approbation after reading her essay aloud.","The audience's warm approbation was clear from the long applause at the end of the play."],"b":85,"y":2},{"w":"appropriate","p":"verb","d":"To take something for your own use, often without permission, or to officially set money aside for a purpose.","lb":"take, allocate","s":["take","seize","commandeer","allocate","assign","set aside"],"k":["allot","allow","capture","conquer"],"a":["return","restore","give back","relinquish"],"ex":["The city appropriated money for new streetlights at the end of the budget meeting.","A coworker appropriated my idea and presented it to the boss as his own.","The college appropriated half of this year's budget for new science labs."],"b":405,"y":0},{"w":"appurtenance","p":"noun","d":"An extra item or feature that belongs to something larger and is usually less important than it.","lb":"accessory, add-on","s":["accessory","adjunct","attachment","accompaniment","addition","extra"],"k":["ancillary","appendage","auxiliary","component"],"a":[],"ex":["The deed lists the house and all its appurtenances, including the garden shed and the well.","A silk scarf was just another appurtenance of her carefully styled look.","Gold chains and fancy cars were the appurtenances of his new wealth."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apropos","p":"adjective","d":"Suitable for a particular situation or moment; fitting and relevant.","lb":"appropriate, timely","s":["appropriate","fitting","suitable","apt","relevant","pertinent"],"k":["applicable","apposite","befitting","on the nose"],"a":["inappropriate","irrelevant","unsuitable"],"ex":["Her comment about saving money was apropos, since we were about to book the trip.","The song playing as we left school seemed perfectly apropos.","A warm scarf is an apropos gift for someone moving to a cold city."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"apt","p":"adjective","d":"Suitable for a particular situation, or likely to behave or happen in a certain way.","lb":"suitable, likely","s":["suitable","appropriate","fitting","apposite","likely","liable"],"k":["apropos","clever","disposed","germane"],"a":["unsuitable","inappropriate","unlikely","unfit"],"ex":["Metal is apt to rust quickly in the humid weather near the coast.","Lazy is not an apt description of a student who studies every night.","Young children are apt to forget instructions when they are excited."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aptitude","p":"noun","d":"A natural ability or talent for learning or doing something.","lb":"talent, ability","s":["talent","gift","ability","flair","knack","skill"],"k":["competence","endowment","forte","leaning"],"a":["inability","incompetence","ineptitude","incapacity"],"ex":["She has a natural aptitude for languages and picked up French in a few months.","The school gives an aptitude test to help students choose a subject.","My brother has little interest in cooking but a real aptitude for fixing machines."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"arbiter","p":"noun","d":"A person with the power or authority to settle a dispute or decide what is right.","lb":"judge, authority","s":["judge","referee","umpire","mediator","adjudicator","authority"],"k":["custodian","decider","final authority","gatekeeper"],"a":[],"ex":["The village elder was the arbiter in land disputes between neighbors.","The referee is the final arbiter of what happens on the field.","Fashion magazines used to be the arbiters of what people wore each season."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"arbitrary","p":"adjective","d":"Based on random choice or personal whim rather than on reason or a fair system.","lb":"random, capricious","s":["random","capricious","whimsical","haphazard","erratic","subjective"],"k":["absolute","changeable","despotic","discretionary"],"a":["reasoned","systematic","logical","rational"],"ex":["The fine seemed arbitrary because no one could explain how the amount was decided.","I picked an arbitrary number between one and ten for the guessing game.","The teacher's arbitrary marking made students feel that effort was pointless."],"b":146,"y":0},{"w":"arbitrate","p":"verb","d":"To officially settle a disagreement between two sides as an independent, neutral person.","lb":"mediate, judge","s":["mediate","adjudicate","referee","judge","umpire","settle"],"k":["bring to terms","broker","conciliate","conclude"],"a":[],"ex":["A neutral lawyer was chosen to arbitrate the dispute between the two companies.","The headmaster arbitrated between two students who were arguing about the science fair prize.","Village elders often arbitrate quarrels over land boundaries before they reach the court."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"arbitrator","p":"noun","d":"A neutral person chosen to hear both sides of a dispute and decide how it should be settled.","lb":"judge, mediator","s":["mediator","judge","referee","umpire","adjudicator","peacemaker"],"k":["broker","conciliator","facilitator","intermediary"],"a":[],"ex":["Both companies agreed to let an independent arbitrator settle the payment dispute instead of going to court.","The arbitrator listened to the workers and the factory owner before announcing a fair settlement.","When the two neighbors could not agree on the boundary wall, they asked the village arbitrator for help."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"arcane","p":"adjective","d":"Known or understood by only a few people, and hard to follow because it is secret or highly specialized.","lb":"obscure, esoteric","s":["obscure","esoteric","mysterious","secret","cryptic","recondite"],"k":["ambiguous","deep","enigmatic","hidden"],"a":["common","familiar","simple","public"],"ex":["The tax form was full of arcane rules that even the clerk could not explain.","My uncle collects arcane facts about old railway stations and shares them at every family dinner.","Programmers use arcane commands that look like nonsense to beginners."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"archaic","p":"adjective","d":"Very old-fashioned and no longer in normal use, as if belonging to an earlier period.","lb":"outdated, ancient","s":["outdated","obsolete","old-fashioned","antiquated","ancient","outmoded"],"k":["antediluvian","antique","dated","defunct"],"a":["modern","current","contemporary","new"],"ex":["Words such as thou and thee sound archaic in modern English.","The office still uses an archaic filing system with thousands of paper folders.","A few archaic laws written a century ago are still waiting to be updated."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"archetype","p":"noun","d":"A very typical example of a certain kind of person or thing, or the original model that others copy.","lb":"prototype, ideal example","s":["prototype","model","original","standard","paradigm","pattern"],"k":["blueprint","example","mold","pilot"],"a":["copy","imitation","replica"],"ex":["In many stories, the wise old teacher is an archetype who guides the young hero.","Her grandmother’s kitchen is the archetype of a warm, welcoming home.","The first electric tram was the archetype of the modern metro trains we ride today."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"archipelago","p":"noun","d":"A group of many islands close together in the sea.","lb":"island group","s":["island group","island chain","chain of islands","cluster of islands"],"k":["atoll chain","dry land","earth","ground"],"a":[],"ex":["The Maldives is a famous archipelago in the Indian Ocean, made up of hundreds of islands.","We took a ferry to explore the archipelago, stopping at a new island each day.","Indonesia is the world's largest archipelago, stretching across thousands of islands."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"archives","p":"noun","d":"A collection of old documents and records, or the place where they are stored.","lb":"records, historical files","s":["records","files","annals","documents","registry","repository"],"k":["compendium","deed boxes","depository","ledgers"],"a":[],"ex":["The historian spent weeks in the national archives reading old letters and maps.","The newspaper's online archives let you search articles from fifty years ago.","Our school archives contain photographs from the very first graduation."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ardent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing strong feeling, enthusiasm or devotion toward a person, cause or activity.","lb":"passionate, enthusiastic","s":["passionate","fervent","enthusiastic","zealous","devoted","keen"],"k":["bright","earnest","fervid","fiery"],"a":["apathetic","indifferent","cool","lukewarm"],"ex":["My father is an ardent supporter of the national cricket team and never misses a match.","She is an ardent reader who finishes a novel every week.","The ardent volunteers worked through the night to pack relief bags."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"ardor","p":"noun","d":"Very strong enthusiasm, eagerness or passion for a person, activity or cause.","lb":"passion, enthusiasm","s":["passion","zeal","fervor","eagerness","enthusiasm","devotion"],"k":["dedication","elan","gusto","relish"],"a":["apathy","indifference","coldness","lethargy"],"ex":["She studied for the admission test with great ardor, rising before dawn every day.","The volunteers worked with ardor to clean the riverbank after the flood.","My uncle's ardor for gardening turns every corner of his rooftop into a small farm."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"arduous","p":"adjective","d":"Needing a great deal of effort and energy; very difficult and tiring.","lb":"difficult, tiring","s":["strenuous","laborious","demanding","grueling","exhausting","taxing"],"k":["backbreaking","difficult","exacting","hard"],"a":["easy","effortless","simple","light"],"ex":["The climb to the top of the hill was arduous, and we stopped to rest every ten minutes.","Preparing for the admission test is an arduous process that takes months of daily study.","In the village, fetching water from the distant well was an arduous daily task."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"argument","p":"noun","d":"A set of reasons given to show that an idea is right or wrong.","lb":"reasoning, case","s":["case","reasoning","line of reasoning","logic","justification","contention"],"k":["abstract thought","controversy","debate","line"],"a":[],"ex":["Her argument for a later school start was clear and convincing.","The main argument against the new road is the cost.","He presented a strong argument for saving a little money every month."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"arid","p":"adjective","d":"Very dry, with little or no rain; also dull and lacking interest or imagination.","lb":"dry, barren","s":["dry","parched","barren","desert","desiccated","dull"],"k":["baked","bone-dry","boring","scorched"],"a":["wet","humid","fertile","lush"],"ex":["Little grows in the arid land near the desert, where rain falls once a year.","Camels survive in arid regions because they can go many days without water.","Farmers in the arid north dig deep wells to water their crops."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"arise","p":"verb","d":"To begin to exist or to happen, often unexpectedly.","lb":"occur, emerge","s":["emerge","occur","appear","crop up","come up","develop"],"k":["become","bob up","come out","get up"],"a":["disappear","vanish","end","subside"],"ex":["If any problems arise during the exam, raise your hand and call the invigilator.","A new question arose during the meeting, and nobody knew the answer.","Misunderstandings often arise when people communicate only by text message."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"aristocratic","p":"adjective","d":"Belonging to the highest social class, or having the proud, refined manner of such people.","lb":"noble, upper-class","s":["noble","patrician","highborn","titled","elite","refined"],"k":["blue","courtly","dignified","genteel"],"a":["common","plebeian","humble","proletarian"],"ex":["Her aristocratic family once owned most of the land around the old zamindar house.","He has an aristocratic way of speaking, slow and polite, as if every word were chosen carefully.","The museum displays the elegant furniture of an aristocratic household from the eighteenth century."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"armament","p":"noun","d":"Weapons and military equipment, or the act of equipping a country's forces with them.","lb":"weaponry, arms","s":["weaponry","arms","weapons","munitions","ordnance","arsenal"],"k":["arming","arms buildup","combat gear","defense systems"],"a":["disarmament"],"ex":["The museum displays the armament of a medieval castle, including swords and shields.","The newspaper reported that the country was spending heavily on new armament.","Our history teacher explained how rapid armament raised tensions before the First World War."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"armistice","p":"noun","d":"An agreement between two sides at war to stop fighting for a period, often so they can discuss peace.","lb":"truce, ceasefire","s":["truce","ceasefire","peace","treaty","suspension of arms","lull"],"k":["moratorium","pause","respite","stand-down"],"a":["war","hostilities","fighting","battle"],"ex":["The two armies signed an armistice to stop the fighting while peace talks continued.","Each November, many countries remember the armistice that ended the First World War.","The history teacher asked us to explain why the armistice of 1918 did not bring lasting peace."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"arouse","p":"verb","d":"To cause a feeling, interest or reaction to begin in someone.","lb":"stir up, evoke","s":["evoke","provoke","stir","spark","awaken","kindle"],"k":["brace","conjure","conjure up","create"],"a":["calm","quell","suppress","dampen"],"ex":["The strange noise from the attic aroused her curiosity.","His sudden wealth aroused suspicion among his neighbors.","A good teacher can arouse interest in even the dullest subject."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"aroused","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling a strong emotion, such as interest, anger or excitement, that has been stirred up.","lb":"stirred up","s":["stirred","excited","stimulated","awakened","roused","inflamed"],"k":["ablaze","aflame","emotional","enthusiastic"],"a":["calm","indifferent","apathetic","dormant"],"ex":["The aroused crowd demanded answers from the bus company.","Her aroused curiosity led her to open the old wooden box.","The teacher noticed the aroused interest of the class when he mentioned the experiment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"arraign","p":"verb","d":"To bring someone before a court to hear the charges made against them.","lb":"charge, bring to court","s":["charge","indict","accuse","prosecute","summon","try"],"k":["allege","blame","bring before the bar","bring to book"],"a":["acquit","exonerate","absolve","clear"],"ex":["The shop owner was arraigned on charges of selling fake medicine.","Two men will be arraigned tomorrow morning, and a judge will read the charges aloud.","She was arraigned in court and pleaded not guilty to fraud."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"arrant","p":"adjective","d":"Complete and total, used to emphasise how bad something or someone is.","lb":"utter, complete","s":["utter","complete","total","thorough","downright","absolute"],"k":["consummate","dyed-in-the-wool","egregious","entire"],"a":["partial","slight","mild"],"ex":["The rumour about the school closing was arrant nonsense, as the principal quickly explained.","An arrant coward, he ran away at the first sign of trouble.","Telling customers that the old phone was brand new was an arrant lie."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"arrears","p":"noun","d":"Money that is owed and should already have been paid, such as rent, wages or a bill.","lb":"overdue debt","s":["overdue payments","unpaid debts","back payments","outstanding balance","dues","backlog"],"k":["amounts owed","deficit","delinquency","financial obligation"],"a":["credit","surplus","advance payment","prepayment"],"ex":["The landlord agreed to wait after Karim promised to clear his rent arrears by the end of the month.","Her electricity account was in arrears, so the company sent a final notice.","The factory owner is working to pay off wage arrears to the workers before Eid."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"arsenal","p":"noun","d":"A large collection of weapons and military equipment, or a building where they are made or stored.","lb":"weapons, stockpile","s":["armoury","weapons store","stockpile","magazine","ammunition depot","armament"],"k":["arms","cache","depot","reserves"],"a":[],"ex":["The country has agreed to reduce its nuclear arsenal over the next ten years.","Soldiers guarded the old arsenal, where rifles and ammunition had been stored for decades.","The city museum is housed in a former arsenal built by the army more than a century ago."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"artful","p":"adjective","d":"Clever in a sly way, especially at getting what you want.","lb":"crafty, cunning","s":["crafty","cunning","sly","wily","shrewd","scheming"],"k":["adroit","canny","cute","deep"],"a":["artless","honest","naive","straightforward"],"ex":["With an artful excuse about heavy traffic, he avoided explaining why he was late again.","The artful salesman made the old phone sound like a bargain without telling an outright lie.","She gave an artful answer that avoided the question but still sounded polite."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"articulate","p":"adjective","d":"Able to express thoughts and ideas clearly and fluently in speech or writing.","lb":"eloquent, fluent","s":["eloquent","fluent","expressive","coherent","clear","lucid"],"k":["cogent","communicative","facile","glib"],"a":["incoherent","hesitant","mumbling","unclear"],"ex":["Tania is an articulate speaker who explains difficult ideas in simple words.","The articulate young engineer impressed the interview panel.","Even at ten years old, he was articulate enough to argue his case with his parents."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"artifice","p":"noun","d":"Clever trickery or a skilful plan used to deceive someone.","lb":"trickery, cunning","s":["trickery","deception","cunning","ruse","ploy","subterfuge"],"k":["chicanery","deceit","deviousness","dissimulation"],"a":["honesty","candor","sincerity","openness"],"ex":["The scammer used artifice to convince old people that they had won a prize.","She got the interview through artifice, pretending to be an old friend of the manager.","A salesman's smooth artifice can make a poor product look attractive."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"artisan","p":"noun","d":"A person who makes things by hand using special skill, such as a potter, weaver or carpenter.","lb":"craftsperson, skilled worker","s":["craftsman","skilled worker","tradesman","maker","trained worker"],"k":["cobbler","guild member","journeyman","mechanic"],"a":[],"ex":["An artisan spent two months weaving the jamdani sari by hand.","The market sells wooden toys made by local artisans, so no two are exactly alike.","Artisans in the old part of Dhaka still shape brass pots by hand."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"artless","p":"adjective","d":"Natural and sincere, with no attempt to deceive or to impress other people.","lb":"innocent, sincere","s":["guileless","ingenuous","naive","candid","innocent","simple"],"k":["careless","childlike","gullible","honest"],"a":["cunning","crafty","devious","scheming"],"ex":["The child's artless question about why the man was sad made everyone smile.","She gave an artless laugh, unaware that anyone was watching her.","Her artless way of telling the truth made customers trust her at once."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"ascendancy","p":"noun","d":"A position of power, influence or control over others.","lb":"dominance, supremacy","s":["dominance","supremacy","domination","control","power","authority"],"k":["command","condition","eminence","hegemony"],"a":["subordination","inferiority","weakness","submission"],"ex":["After the first half, the home team gained ascendancy and controlled most of the game.","Online shopping has gained ascendancy over traditional markets in many cities.","The new manager quickly established ascendancy over the sales department."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"ascendant","p":"adjective","d":"Gaining power, influence or success and becoming more dominant.","lb":"rising, dominant","s":["rising","dominant","growing","increasing","prevailing","powerful"],"k":["dominating","emergent","flourishing","on the rise"],"a":["declining","waning","fading","falling"],"ex":["After winning three titles in a row, the young team looked ascendant.","Online shopping is ascendant, and many small bookshops are struggling to survive.","His ascendant career took him from junior clerk to department head in five years."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ascertain","p":"verb","d":"To find out something for certain by checking facts or asking questions.","lb":"determine, find out","s":["determine","establish","find out","verify","confirm","discover"],"k":["calculate","check","find","insure"],"a":["guess","assume","presume","suppose"],"ex":["Investigators are trying to ascertain the cause of the fire at the warehouse.","Please call the hotel to ascertain whether they have a free room tonight.","It is hard to ascertain the age of the tree without cutting it."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"ascetic","p":"adjective","d":"Living a very simple and strict life, without luxuries or pleasures, as a form of self-discipline.","lb":"austere, self-denying","s":["austere","abstinent","spartan","puritanical","strict","frugal"],"k":["bare","harsh","moderate","restrained"],"a":["hedonistic","luxurious","sensual","indulgent"],"ex":["He lives an ascetic life in a small room with just a bed, a desk and a few books.","During exam month, she adopted an ascetic routine: no phone, no sweets and no late nights.","The professor's ascetic habits, such as eating only rice and lentils, surprised his students."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"ascribe","p":"verb","d":"To say that something is caused by, or belongs to, a particular person, thing or reason.","lb":"attribute, credit","s":["attribute","credit","assign","put down","impute","blame"],"k":["evaluate","hold responsible","judge","lay at the door of"],"a":[],"ex":["Doctors ascribe her quick recovery to good food and plenty of rest.","Many people ascribe the poem to a famous writer, but nobody knows who really wrote it.","I ascribe my success in the exam to regular revision, not luck."],"b":100,"y":1},{"w":"askance","p":"adverb","d":"In a way that shows doubt, suspicion or disapproval, usually in the phrase look askance at.","lb":"suspiciously, doubtfully","s":["suspiciously"],"k":["critically","cynically","sidelong","sideways"],"a":["favourably","confidently"],"ex":["Passengers looked askance at the unattended bag left near the bus door.","Customers looked askance at the very cheap watches, suspecting they were fake.","The teacher looked askance at the sudden improvement in his marks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"aspect","p":"noun","d":"One particular part or feature of a situation, idea or problem.","lb":"feature, side","s":["facet","feature","side","element","angle","dimension"],"k":["consideration","detail","expression","face"],"a":[],"ex":["Cost is only one aspect of choosing a university.","The doctor explained every aspect of the operation before we signed the form.","She enjoys most aspects of her job, except the long commute."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"aspersion","p":"noun","d":"An unkind or damaging remark that attacks someone's character or reputation.","lb":"slur, smear","s":["slur","slander","smear","insult","defamation","libel"],"k":["backbiting","character assassination","innuendo","insinuation"],"a":["praise","compliment","tribute","commendation"],"ex":["Nobody should cast aspersions on a colleague's honesty without clear proof.","The rival team cast aspersions on the referee's fairness after losing the final.","Rafi was upset that some classmates cast aspersions on his result, suggesting he had cheated."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"assail","p":"verb","d":"To attack someone or something violently, either physically or with strong words.","lb":"attack, assault","s":["attack","assault","bombard","batter","lash out at","criticize"],"k":["condemn","denounce","knock","lash out"],"a":["defend","protect","praise","support"],"ex":["Critics assailed the new parking rule in letters to the newspaper.","A strong smell of smoke assailed us as soon as we opened the door.","Doubts assailed her as she waited outside the interview room."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"assert","p":"verb","d":"To state something firmly and confidently as true.","lb":"claim, declare","s":["claim","declare","maintain","insist","affirm","state"],"k":["allege","announce","aver","avow"],"a":["deny","retract","disclaim","refute"],"ex":["The witness asserted that she had seen the car leave before midnight.","He asserts that regular exercise is the best medicine for stress.","The company asserted its innocence and promised to cooperate fully with the inquiry."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"assess","p":"verb","d":"To judge or decide the value, quality, size or importance of something after careful thought.","lb":"evaluate, judge","s":["evaluate","judge","appraise","gauge","estimate","rate"],"k":["calculate","guess","measure","scrutinize"],"a":["ignore","overlook","disregard","neglect"],"ex":["Engineers came to assess the damage to the bridge after the heavy flood.","Teachers assess students not only by exams but also by class projects.","Before buying the used phone, he asked a technician to assess its battery."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"assiduous","p":"adjective","d":"Working very hard and carefully, with steady attention to every detail.","lb":"diligent, hardworking","s":["diligent","hardworking","industrious","persevering","painstaking","conscientious"],"k":["careful","dogged","indefatigable","scrupulous"],"a":["lazy","idle","careless","negligent"],"ex":["Thanks to her assiduous study, Maya finished at the top of her class.","The shopkeeper is assiduous in keeping his accounts neat and up to date.","An assiduous reporter checked every fact twice before the story was printed."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"assimilate","p":"verb","d":"To take in information, ideas or experiences and understand them fully.","lb":"absorb, digest","s":["absorb","digest","take in","learn","grasp","soak up"],"k":["acquire","imbibe","ingest","larn"],"a":["reject","ignore","forget","disregard"],"ex":["It takes time to assimilate all the new vocabulary before the exam.","The students struggled to assimilate so much information in a single lecture.","He read the report twice to assimilate its main points before the meeting."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"assimilation","p":"noun","d":"The process by which people or groups gradually become fully part of a different culture or community.","lb":"integration, absorption","s":["integration","absorption","adaptation","incorporation","blending","merging"],"k":["cultural mixing","digestion","enculturation","naturalization"],"a":["segregation","separation","isolation","exclusion"],"ex":["The new students' assimilation into the school community took only a few weeks.","Language classes helped the family with their assimilation into life in a new country.","Cultural assimilation can be hard for children who move abroad but want to keep their own traditions."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"assist","p":"verb","d":"To help someone do something by doing part of the work or by giving support.","lb":"help, aid","s":["help","aid","support","lend a hand","back","serve"],"k":["attend","attend to","back up","bolster"],"a":["hinder","obstruct","hamper","impede"],"ex":["Volunteers assisted the elderly passengers as they climbed off the crowded bus.","A friendly librarian assisted me in finding books for my research paper.","Could you assist me with this form? I do not understand the second page."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"assortment","p":"noun","d":"A mixed collection of different kinds of the same type of thing.","lb":"variety, mixture","s":["variety","selection","mixture","range","medley","array"],"k":["accumulation","assemblage","bundle","classification"],"a":["uniformity","sameness","monotony"],"ex":["The sweet shop sells an assortment of sandesh and rasgulla in a single box.","At the book fair, we found an assortment of novels, comics and dictionaries.","Mum bought an assortment of colourful bangles for the Eid party."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"assuage","p":"verb","d":"To make an unpleasant feeling such as pain, fear, guilt or anger less strong.","lb":"ease, soothe","s":["soothe","ease","relieve","calm","allay","alleviate"],"k":["calm down","diminish","lull","mollify"],"a":["aggravate","intensify","worsen","inflame"],"ex":["The teacher spoke kindly to assuage the students' fears about the final exam.","A cold glass of lemon water assuaged my thirst after the long walk in the sun.","He sent flowers to assuage his guilt for missing her birthday."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"assured","p":"adjective","d":"Confident and showing no doubt about your own abilities.","lb":"confident, certain","s":["confident","poised","composed","certain","unflappable","secure"],"k":["at ease","authoritative","collected","cool"],"a":["insecure","hesitant","uncertain","timid"],"ex":["She gave an assured performance at the school's annual concert.","The new doctor spoke in a calm, assured voice.","He walked into the interview room with an assured smile."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"astound","p":"verb","d":"To surprise someone so much that they can hardly believe it.","lb":"amaze, shock","s":["amaze","astonish","stun","stagger","shock","dumbfound"],"k":["blow away","boggle","bowl over","knock out"],"a":["bore","disappoint"],"ex":["The magician's last trick astounded the children, who clapped for five minutes.","Her test score astounded the teachers, because she had failed the last exam.","The speed of the new internet connection astounded my grandfather."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"astringent","p":"adjective","d":"Sharp and severe in manner, tone or style, especially when criticising someone or something.","lb":"harsh, biting","s":["harsh","caustic","biting","severe","acerbic","sharp"],"k":["bitter","corrosive","pungent","sarcastic"],"a":["gentle","mild","kind","soothing"],"ex":["The critic's astringent review described the play as long, loud and badly acted.","The coach delivered an astringent speech at half-time, listing every mistake the players had made.","The newspaper column was known for its astringent humour about city life."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"astute","p":"adjective","d":"Clever at understanding people and situations and using that understanding to one's own advantage.","lb":"shrewd, sharp","s":["shrewd","sharp","clever","perceptive","canny","smart"],"k":["bright","politic","quick","sagacious"],"a":["naive","foolish","gullible","obtuse"],"ex":["An astute investor, she sold her shares just before the market fell.","The teacher made an astute comment that helped the whole class understand the poem.","Nadia is astute enough to notice when a seller is hiding a flaw in a used phone."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"asylum","p":"noun","d":"Safety and protection given to people fleeing danger in their own country; also, an old word for a mental hospital.","lb":"refuge, sanctuary","s":["refuge","sanctuary","shelter","protection","haven","safety"],"k":["bastion","bolthole","hideout","institution"],"a":[],"ex":["The family fled the war and applied for asylum in a safe country.","The government granted asylum to the writer after she was threatened at home.","The old church offered asylum to travellers caught in the storm."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"atheist","p":"noun","d":"A person who does not believe in the existence of any god.","lb":"nonbeliever","s":["nonbeliever","disbeliever","unbeliever","skeptic"],"k":["godless","heathen","infidel","irreligious"],"a":["believer","devotee","worshipper"],"ex":["Although Karim is an atheist, he respects his family's customs and joins them at festivals.","The survey asked people whether they were religious, agnostic or atheist.","My professor, a self-described atheist, enjoys discussing philosophy with students of all faiths."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"atone","p":"verb","d":"To do something to show that one is sorry for a wrong and to make up for it.","lb":"make amends","s":["make amends","make up for","compensate","redeem oneself","expiate","repent"],"k":["do penance","make reparation","mend one's ways","offset"],"a":["offend","wrong","transgress"],"ex":["He tried to atone for his rude behavior by helping the family move house.","The company promised to atone for the faulty product by replacing it free of charge.","To atone for forgetting her birthday, Rafi cooked her favorite dinner."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"atrophy","p":"verb","d":"To become weaker or smaller because of lack of use, or to waste away gradually.","lb":"waste away, wither","s":["waste away","wither","shrivel","degenerate","decline","deteriorate"],"k":["decrease","dry up","ebb","emaciate"],"a":["grow","strengthen","develop","flourish"],"ex":["After months in a cast, the muscles in his leg began to atrophy.","Language skills atrophy quickly if you never speak the language after leaving the course.","Without regular practice, a musician’s fingers may lose speed and his talent can atrophy."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"attenuate","p":"verb","d":"To make something weaker, thinner or less forceful.","lb":"weaken, reduce","s":["weaken","reduce","thin","dilute","lessen","diminish"],"k":["cut","decrease","shrink","slim"],"a":["strengthen","intensify","amplify","reinforce"],"ex":["Thick walls attenuate the sound of traffic, so the apartment is quiet at night.","Thick concrete can attenuate a phone signal, which is why calls drop in the basement.","The vaccine contains a virus that has been attenuated in the laboratory so it cannot make people ill."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"attest","p":"verb","d":"To state or show that something is true or real, especially as evidence or officially.","lb":"confirm, testify","s":["confirm","testify","certify","verify","prove","bear witness"],"k":["authenticate","corroborate","notarize","show"],"a":["deny","refute","disprove","contradict"],"ex":["Her many awards attest to her talent as a violinist.","Three neighbors attested to his good character in court.","A doctor must attest that the patient was too ill to attend."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"attribute","p":"verb","d":"To say that something is caused by, or belongs to, a particular person or thing.","lb":"ascribe, credit","s":["ascribe","credit","assign","put down to","impute","blame"],"k":["associate with","derive","evaluate","judge"],"a":["deny","disown"],"ex":["Doctors attribute her quick recovery to regular exercise and a healthy diet.","The poem is often attributed to a village poet, though nobody is sure.","Rafi attributes his high score to practicing past papers every evening."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"attrition","p":"noun","d":"A gradual reduction in size, strength or numbers, such as when staff leave and are not replaced.","lb":"gradual loss, wearing down","s":["erosion","reduction","depletion","wearing down","weakening","decline"],"k":["abrasion","attenuation","contrition","decay"],"a":["growth","increase","expansion","buildup"],"ex":["The company reduced its staff through attrition, not layoffs, by not replacing people who retired.","The school has a high rate of attrition among new teachers, who leave within two years.","Years of attrition by wind and water slowly wore down the rocks on the coast."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"attune","p":"verb","d":"To make yourself or something ready to respond to or fit well with a new situation.","lb":"adjust, harmonize","s":["adjust","accustom","adapt","tune","harmonize","acclimatize"],"k":["alter","calibrate","change","fit"],"a":["alienate","estrange","disorient","mismatch"],"ex":["It took her weeks to attune herself to the busy rhythm of city life.","Good teachers are attuned to the moods of their students.","After a month in the village, my ears became attuned to the quiet."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"atypical","p":"adjective","d":"Not typical; different from what is normal or expected for a group or situation.","lb":"unusual, abnormal","s":["unusual","abnormal","uncharacteristic","irregular","exceptional","anomalous"],"k":["deviant","odd","peculiar","uncommon"],"a":["typical","usual","normal","characteristic"],"ex":["Heavy snow in this region is atypical, so people rushed out to take photos.","It was atypical for Rafi to arrive late; he is usually the first student in class.","The doctor said the patient's symptoms were atypical for the flu."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"au courant","p":"adjective","d":"Well informed about the latest news, ideas or trends.","lb":"up to date, informed","s":["up to date","informed","aware","knowledgeable","in the know","abreast"],"k":["cognizant","contemporary","conversant","cutting-edge"],"a":["out of touch","behind the times","unaware","uninformed"],"ex":["My cousin is always au courant with the newest phones and apps.","To work in journalism, you must stay au courant with events at home and abroad.","The café’s menu is au courant, with dishes that are popular on social media this month."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"audacious","p":"adjective","d":"Willing to take bold risks, often in a way that surprises or shocks people.","lb":"bold, daring","s":["bold","daring","fearless","brave","adventurous","brazen"],"k":["adventuresome","barefaced","bodacious","dauntless"],"a":["timid","cautious","cowardly","fearful"],"ex":["The students made an audacious plan to build a solar car using only scrap parts.","It was audacious of him to ask the manager for a raise in his first week.","The designer's audacious use of bright orange and purple made the dress stand out."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"audacity","p":"noun","d":"The nerve to do something bold or rude without fear of what others will think.","lb":"nerve, boldness","s":["nerve","boldness","cheek","gall","impudence","daring"],"k":["brass","cheekiness","chutzpah","courage"],"a":["timidity","shyness","caution","humility"],"ex":["He had the audacity to ask for a refund after eating the whole meal.","It takes real audacity to speak up against a plan the whole team supports.","I admired the audacity of the young designer, who rebuilt the old market in glass."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"augment","p":"verb","d":"To make something bigger or greater by adding to it.","lb":"increase, supplement","s":["increase","enlarge","boost","expand","supplement","raise"],"k":["beef up","build up","extend","fortify"],"a":["decrease","reduce","diminish","lessen"],"ex":["Many students teach evening tuition classes to augment their small allowances.","The hospital hopes to augment its supply of medicine before the monsoon.","She augmented her diet with extra fruit and vegetables to boost her energy."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"augmentation","p":"noun","d":"The act of making something larger or greater by adding to it.","lb":"increase, expansion","s":["increase","expansion","enlargement","addition","growth","boost"],"k":["beefing up","boosting","intensification","reinforcement"],"a":["reduction","decrease","cut","decline"],"ex":["The school plans an augmentation of the library with five hundred new books.","Doctors recommended an augmentation of his daily iron dose after the blood test.","The augmentation of the company's staff helped it finish the project on time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"augur","p":"verb","d":"To be a sign of what is likely to happen in the future, either good or bad.","lb":"foreshadow, signal","s":["bode","portend","foreshadow","presage","herald","signal"],"k":["bespeak","betoken","forebode","foretell"],"a":[],"ex":["Dark clouds in the morning augur heavy rain by evening.","The company's strong first-quarter sales augur well for the rest of the year.","Her calm first day at the new school augured well for the months ahead."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"august","p":"adjective","d":"Impressive and respected because of age, rank or dignity.","lb":"majestic, venerable","s":["majestic","venerable","distinguished","stately","noble","grand"],"k":["baronial","esteemed","exalted","honorable"],"a":["humble","ordinary","lowly","undignified"],"ex":["The august hall of the old university made the new students feel proud and a little shy.","He was invited to speak before an august gathering of scientists and writers.","The august old judge entered the room, and everybody stood in silence."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"auspices","p":"noun","d":"Support, protection or guidance given by an organization or person with authority.","lb":"sponsorship, protection","s":["sponsorship","patronage","backing","aegis","protection","guidance"],"k":["backup","championship","custody","endorsement"],"a":[],"ex":["The science fair was held under the auspices of the district education office.","The peace talks took place under the auspices of a neutral country.","Under the auspices of a local charity, volunteers handed out warm blankets in winter."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"auspicious","p":"adjective","d":"Showing signs that something will go well; promising good fortune.","lb":"promising, favorable","s":["promising","favorable","propitious","fortunate","lucky","encouraging"],"k":["advantageous","blessed","halcyon","heartening"],"a":["unfavorable","ominous","inauspicious","unpromising"],"ex":["The team's first win of the season was an auspicious start to the tournament.","Many shopkeepers open a new account book on Pohela Boishakh, hoping for an auspicious year.","Sunshine on the morning of the interview seemed an auspicious sign."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"austere","p":"adjective","d":"Very plain, simple and strict, with no comforts, decoration or luxuries.","lb":"stern, plain","s":["stern","severe","strict","plain","spartan","bare"],"k":["abstemious","forbidding","minimal","monastic"],"a":["luxurious","lavish","indulgent","ornate"],"ex":["The hostel room was austere, with a narrow bed, a bare wall and a single lamp.","Our headmaster had an austere manner, and students stopped talking the moment he walked in.","After losing his job, the family adopted an austere lifestyle and cut every unnecessary expense."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"autocratic","p":"adjective","d":"Ruling with total power and not asking for other people's opinions; extremely bossy.","lb":"dictatorial, domineering","s":["dictatorial","domineering","tyrannical","authoritarian","imperious","overbearing"],"k":["absolutist","commanding","dominating","hierarchical"],"a":["democratic","liberal","permissive","easygoing"],"ex":["The autocratic principal made every decision alone and never asked the teachers for advice.","In the story, an autocratic king forbade his people from singing in public.","His autocratic style as a team leader made the younger members afraid to share ideas."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"autonomous","p":"adjective","d":"Able to govern or control itself without being controlled by an outside authority.","lb":"independent, self-governing","s":["independent","sovereign","free","separate","self-governing","self-ruling"],"k":["freewheeling","self-contained","self-determining","self-reliant"],"a":["dependent","subordinate","controlled","ruled"],"ex":["The university is an autonomous institution and decides its own courses and exam dates.","Teenagers become more autonomous as they learn to manage their own money and time.","Autonomous cars use sensors and software to drive without a person at the wheel."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"autonomy","p":"noun","d":"The freedom to make your own decisions and govern yourself without outside control.","lb":"independence, self-rule","s":["independence","freedom","sovereignty","self-determination","liberty","free will"],"k":["discretion","individualism","latitude","leeway"],"a":["dependence","control","subordination","servitude"],"ex":["Our manager gives the team autonomy to plan its own schedule.","Earning her own money gave Nadia a sense of autonomy.","The university has the autonomy to set its own admission rules."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"auxiliary","p":"adjective","d":"Giving extra help or support; used as a second or backup when the main one is not enough.","lb":"supporting, backup","s":["supporting","backup","additional","supplementary","secondary","subsidiary"],"k":["accessory","extra","subordinate","supplemental"],"a":["main","primary","principal","chief"],"ex":["The hospital switched to an auxiliary generator when the power cut began.","In the sentence \"She is reading,\" the word \"is\" is an auxiliary verb.","Auxiliary staff such as cleaners and guards keep the school running every day."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"avail","p":"verb","d":"To be of use or help to someone in achieving something.","lb":"help, be of use","s":["help","benefit","serve","assist","profit","aid"],"k":["back up","gain","lend a hand","support"],"a":["hinder","harm","obstruct","hurt"],"ex":["Neither apologies nor gifts availed, and she stayed angry for a week.","Crying and begging did not avail with the strict guard.","No amount of cheering could avail the team once rain flooded the pitch."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"avarice","p":"noun","d":"Extreme greed for money or possessions.","lb":"greed, covetousness","s":["greed","cupidity","materialism","stinginess","covetousness","acquisitiveness"],"k":["deadly sin","grasping","mammonism","mercenariness"],"a":["generosity","charity","benevolence","selflessness"],"ex":["The landlord's avarice led him to raise the rent every few months.","Avarice made the businessman cheat his own partners for a little extra profit.","In the old story, the king's avarice leads to his ruin."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"aver","p":"verb","d":"To state something firmly and confidently as being true.","lb":"declare, assert","s":["declare","assert","affirm","state","maintain","claim"],"k":["announce","argue","asseverate","avouch"],"a":["deny","refute","retract","contradict"],"ex":["The witness averred that she had seen the driver run the red light.","He averred that he had never copied anyone's homework, and the teacher believed him.","The company averred in its statement that the product is safe for children."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"averse","p":"adjective","d":"Strongly unwilling or opposed to something; not liking it at all.","lb":"opposed, unwilling","s":["opposed","reluctant","unwilling","hostile","resistant","disinclined"],"k":["allergic","cautious","chary","grudging"],"a":["keen","willing","eager","fond"],"ex":["I am not averse to a short walk after dinner.","Many young entrepreneurs are averse to taking out large loans.","She is averse to spicy food, so we ordered something mild."],"b":64,"y":4},{"w":"aversion","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of dislike for something, which makes you want to avoid it.","lb":"dislike, distaste","s":["dislike","hatred","distaste","repugnance","antipathy","loathing"],"k":["abomination","animosity","averting","disinclination"],"a":["liking","fondness","affinity","attraction"],"ex":["Many children have an aversion to bitter vegetables like bitter gourd.","He developed an aversion to crowded buses after being stuck in one for hours.","Her aversion to public speaking made group presentations stressful."],"b":96,"y":3},{"w":"avert","p":"verb","d":"To prevent something bad from happening, or to turn your eyes away from something.","lb":"prevent, ward off","s":["prevent","avoid","ward off","stave off","forestall","deflect"],"k":["deter","evade","forbid","foreclose"],"a":["cause","provoke","bring about","invite"],"ex":["A quick-thinking driver averted a crash by braking just in time.","Talks between the workers and the company averted a strike.","Vaccines help avert serious illness in young children."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"avid","p":"adjective","d":"Very enthusiastic and eager about a hobby or activity, and doing it with great interest.","lb":"eager, enthusiastic","s":["eager","enthusiastic","keen","passionate","ardent","fervent"],"k":["desirous","devouring","greedy","impatient"],"a":["indifferent","apathetic","uninterested"],"ex":["My sister is an avid reader and finishes about three novels a month.","He is an avid cricket fan who never misses a live match on television.","The avid gardener spends every weekend planting flowers on her rooftop."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"avoidable","p":"adjective","d":"Possible to prevent or stop from happening.","lb":"preventable","s":["unnecessary","needless","controllable","preventable","escapable"],"k":["dispensable","eliminable","gratuitous","optional"],"a":["unavoidable","inevitable","inescapable","inexorable"],"ex":["Most road accidents are avoidable if drivers follow the traffic rules.","The delay was avoidable, because the tickets could have been booked earlier.","Many illnesses in children are avoidable with clean water and vaccines."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"avow","p":"verb","d":"To state something openly and firmly, or to admit something publicly.","lb":"declare, admit","s":["declare","affirm","assert","profess","state","proclaim"],"k":["announce","aver","claim","confirm"],"a":["deny","disavow","disown","renounce"],"ex":["At the wedding, he avowed his love for her in front of all their relatives.","The player avowed that he had made a mistake and apologized to his teammates.","She avowed her determination to finish the degree, whatever the cost."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"avuncular","p":"adjective","d":"Kind, friendly and generous toward younger people, in the way a good uncle would be.","lb":"uncle-like, kindly","s":["kindly","genial","benevolent","friendly","warm","indulgent"],"k":["amiable","benign","big-brotherly","congenial"],"a":["stern","cold","unfriendly","aloof"],"ex":["The avuncular shopkeeper always slipped an extra toffee into the children's bags.","Our new boss has an avuncular manner that quickly puts nervous interns at ease.","He gave her an avuncular pat on the shoulder and told her not to worry about the exam."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"await","p":"verb","d":"To wait for something that is going to happen or be given to you.","lb":"wait for, expect","s":["expect","anticipate","wait for","look forward to","bide","stay for"],"k":["be in the offing","be on the way","be pending","foresee"],"a":[],"ex":["Thousands of students nervously await their admission test results.","A warm welcome awaits visitors at every village house in the countryside.","We awaited the arrival of the train at the crowded station."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"awe","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of great respect and wonder, sometimes mixed with fear, caused by something very impressive or powerful.","lb":"wonder, reverence","s":["wonder","amazement","reverence","admiration","astonishment","dread"],"k":["esteem","fear","homage","respect"],"a":["contempt","disdain","indifference","scorn"],"ex":["The children stared in awe at the huge skeleton of a blue whale in the museum.","We watched the sun rise over the sea at Cox's Bazar in awe.","She was in awe of her professor, who had written over twenty books."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"awful","p":"adjective","d":"Very bad, unpleasant or of poor quality.","lb":"terrible, very bad","s":["terrible","dreadful","horrible","appalling","dire","atrocious"],"k":["abominable","alarming","amazing","awed"],"a":["wonderful","excellent","pleasant","great"],"ex":["The soup tasted awful because someone had added too much salt.","We had an awful journey: the bus broke down twice.","She felt awful about forgetting her friend's birthday."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"awry","p":"adjective","d":"Not as planned; wrong, off course or out of place.","lb":"amiss, off course","s":["amiss","wrong","askew","off course","crooked","haywire"],"k":["cockeyed","disordered","foiled","gone wrong"],"a":["right","straight","correct","on course"],"ex":["Our plans for the picnic went awry when it began to rain heavily.","Something is awry with the printer, because it keeps ejecting blank pages.","Rafi checked the numbers again, certain that something had gone awry in the calculation."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"axiom","p":"noun","d":"A statement that is accepted as true without proof, and used as a starting point for reasoning.","lb":"principle, postulate","s":["principle","postulate","maxim","premise","adage","dictum"],"k":["a given","aphorism","article of faith","assumption"],"a":[],"ex":["It is a basic axiom of geometry that two points define exactly one straight line.","My father lives by the axiom that honesty is the best policy.","That the customer is always right was an axiom in the old shop, though it was not always true."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"bacchanal","p":"noun","d":"A wild, noisy party with a lot of drinking, or a person who takes part in one.","lb":"wild party, reveller","s":["revel","spree","binge","party animal","orgy"],"k":["bender","booze-up","debauch","debauchery"],"a":["teetotaller","ascetic"],"ex":["The old film shows a Roman bacchanal with music, dancing and wine.","The office party turned into a noisy bacchanal until the manager asked everyone to go home.","The newspaper described the festival's last night as a bacchanal of music and dancing in the streets."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"backstabbing","p":"noun","d":"Secretly doing or saying something harmful to a person who trusts you, especially to damage their reputation.","lb":"betrayal, treachery","s":["betrayal","treachery","disloyalty","deceit","slander","duplicity"],"k":["knifing","sabotage","skulduggery","sneakiness"],"a":["loyalty","faithfulness","honesty","support"],"ex":["There was so much backstabbing in the office that nobody trusted their colleagues.","Nadia was hurt by the backstabbing of a friend who shared her secret with the whole class.","The reality show was full of backstabbing, with contestants plotting against each other."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"baffled","p":"adjective","d":"Unable to understand or explain something, and so confused.","lb":"confused, puzzled","s":["puzzled","confused","bewildered","perplexed","mystified","stumped"],"k":["at a loss","at sea","befuddled","confounded"],"a":["certain","enlightened","sure"],"ex":["The baffled students stared at the strange maths problem for ten minutes.","I was baffled when my phone turned off by itself in the middle of a call.","Doctors were baffled by the child's sudden fever and rash."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"baleful","p":"adjective","d":"Threatening harm or showing evil intentions.","lb":"menacing, sinister","s":["menacing","threatening","sinister","ominous","malevolent","harmful"],"k":["alarming","dark","forbidding","maleficent"],"a":["benign","friendly","kind","harmless"],"ex":["The guard gave us a baleful stare when we walked past the gate.","A baleful silence filled the room after the manager read the email.","Dark clouds gathered with a baleful look over the Bay of Bengal."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"balk","p":"verb","d":"To suddenly refuse to do something, or to stop and refuse to go on, because you are unwilling or afraid.","lb":"refuse, hesitate","s":["refuse","resist","shy away","hesitate","recoil","demur"],"k":["boggle","decline","defy","dig in one's heels"],"a":["agree","comply","accept","proceed"],"ex":["Many people balk at paying extra for a small bag of plain potato chips.","The pony balked at the narrow bridge and would not cross.","She balked when the dentist said she needed three more visits."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"ballyhoo","p":"noun","d":"Noisy, exaggerated publicity or excitement used to attract attention to something.","lb":"hype, fanfare","s":["hype","fanfare","razzmatazz","publicity","hoopla","commotion"],"k":["brouhaha","flimflam","fuss","packaging"],"a":["understatement","modesty","silence"],"ex":["Despite all the ballyhoo before its release, the film turned out to be quite ordinary.","The shop opened amid much ballyhoo, with loudspeakers and free balloons.","I ignore the ballyhoo around new phones and wait for honest reviews."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"balm","p":"noun","d":"A soothing cream or oil that eases pain, or anything that brings comfort.","lb":"soothing ointment, comfort","s":["ointment","salve","lotion","cream","comfort","solace"],"k":["curative","remedy","therapeutic","unction"],"a":["irritant","affliction"],"ex":["She rubbed a little balm on her cracked lips before going out into the cold wind.","My grandmother's soft voice was a balm to everyone after the long, stressful day.","The cool rain was a balm to the village after weeks of burning heat."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"banal","p":"adjective","d":"So ordinary and overused that it is boring and shows no original thought.","lb":"trite, ordinary","s":["trite","hackneyed","commonplace","unoriginal","stale","predictable"],"k":["cliched","insipid","lackluster","overused"],"a":["original","fresh","novel","striking"],"ex":["The movie was so banal that half the audience guessed the ending in the first ten minutes.","He opened his speech with a banal joke about the weather.","Her essay was full of banal phrases that every student uses, so it felt lifeless."],"b":85,"y":2},{"w":"bandwagon","p":"noun","d":"A popular activity or movement that attracts more and more people because it is fashionable or successful.","lb":"popular trend","s":["trend","fad","craze","vogue","fashion","movement"],"k":["cult","flavor of the month","furor","groundswell"],"a":[],"ex":["When the new game became popular, everyone in school jumped on the bandwagon.","Many small shops jumped on the bandwagon and started selling bubble tea.","Some students join the bandwagon of online courses without checking their quality."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"bandy","p":"verb","d":"To pass an idea, rumor or remark from person to person, or to exchange words, often casually.","lb":"exchange, toss around","s":["exchange","toss around","trade","circulate","pass around","swap"],"k":["barter","bat about","bat around","bruit"],"a":["withhold","conceal"],"ex":["Several names were bandied about as possible captains before the team announced its choice.","I won’t bandy words with you about something so small.","Rumors about the new principal were bandied about the staff room all week."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bane","p":"noun","d":"A cause of constant trouble, worry or unhappiness.","lb":"curse, scourge","s":["curse","scourge","plague","blight","torment","nuisance"],"k":["bugbear","cuss","drag","hassle"],"a":["blessing","boon","benefit","advantage"],"ex":["Traffic jams are the bane of every commuter's life in big cities.","Mosquitoes are the bane of summer evenings by the pond.","Weekly spelling tests were the bane of my childhood."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"bankruptcy","p":"noun","d":"The legal state of being unable to pay your debts, when a court takes control of what you own.","lb":"insolvency, ruin","s":["ruin","failure","liquidation","collapse","financial ruin","default"],"k":["chapter 11","debt trap","financial distress","going under"],"a":["solvency","prosperity","wealth","success"],"ex":["After sales dropped for two years, the company was forced to file for bankruptcy.","Medical bills pushed the family to the edge of bankruptcy.","The shop owner avoided bankruptcy by selling some of his equipment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"banter","p":"noun","d":"Friendly, playful talk in which people tease each other and exchange light jokes.","lb":"teasing, repartee","s":["teasing","repartee","joking","badinage","wisecracks","chitchat"],"k":["backchat","chaff","jibes","kidding"],"a":["seriousness","earnestness","silence"],"ex":["The friendly banter between the two cousins made the long train journey pass quickly.","Their cheerful banter at the tea stall drew smiles from everyone nearby.","The team enjoys light banter in the dressing room before every match."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"baroque","p":"adjective","d":"Very elaborate and richly decorated in style, with a lot of detail and curves.","lb":"ornate, elaborate","s":["ornate","elaborate","flamboyant","extravagant","florid","rococo"],"k":["decorative","flashy","flowery","intricate"],"a":["plain","simple","austere","minimalist"],"ex":["The old church has a baroque ceiling covered in gold and painted angels.","The hotel’s lobby is baroque, with curly golden chairs and heavy velvet curtains.","Her wedding invitation was baroque, with flowers, ribbons and swirling letters on every line."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"barrage","p":"noun","d":"A sudden, rapid flood of questions, complaints or other things; also, heavy continuous gunfire.","lb":"onslaught, flood","s":["onslaught","torrent","volley","stream","flood","deluge"],"k":["battery","bombardment","downpour","language"],"a":[],"ex":["The spokesperson faced a barrage of questions from reporters the moment he stepped out.","After the product launch, the customer service desk received a barrage of angry emails.","A barrage of advertisements appears on my phone every time I open the app."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bashful","p":"adjective","d":"Shy and easily embarrassed, especially in front of other people.","lb":"shy, timid","s":["shy","timid","coy","sheepish","diffident","reserved"],"k":["backward","blushing","demure","modest"],"a":["bold","confident","outgoing","brazen"],"ex":["The bashful boy hid behind his mother when the guests arrived.","She felt bashful when the whole class sang happy birthday to her.","Rafi is bashful around new people but chatty with his close friends."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bastion","p":"noun","d":"A strongly protected place, or a person or institution that strongly defends an idea or way of life.","lb":"stronghold, defender","s":["stronghold","fortress","citadel","bulwark","fortification","defense"],"k":["castle","enclave","fort","guardian"],"a":[],"ex":["The old fort on the hill once served as a bastion against invading armies.","The library remains a bastion of quiet study in the noisy heart of the city.","This small bookshop is the last bastion of independent publishing in our town."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bauble","p":"noun","d":"A small, cheap, showy decoration or piece of jewelry that has little real value.","lb":"trinket, ornament","s":["trinket","knickknack","ornament","trifle","charm"],"k":["adornment","bagatelle","bangle","bibelot"],"a":[],"ex":["She hung a red bauble on every branch of the little artificial tree.","The street vendor sold cheap baubles made of colored glass and plastic.","Don't waste your money on shiny baubles that will break in a week."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bedlam","p":"noun","d":"A situation full of noise, confusion and disorder.","lb":"chaos, uproar","s":["chaos","pandemonium","uproar","mayhem","turmoil","madhouse"],"k":["booby hatch","confusion","crazy house","din"],"a":["order","calm","peace","quiet"],"ex":["Bedlam broke out in the classroom when the teacher left for five minutes.","The airport was bedlam after all the flights were canceled by the storm.","It was complete bedlam at the sale, with shoppers grabbing items from every shelf."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"beget","p":"verb","d":"To cause something to exist or happen as a result; formerly, to become the father of a child.","lb":"cause, produce","s":["cause","produce","generate","create","spawn","breed"],"k":["bring forth","get","induce","lead to"],"a":["prevent","stop","end","destroy"],"ex":["Violence only begets more violence, so talking is a better way to settle the quarrel.","Success often begets success, because a good result gives people confidence.","One small lie can beget a hundred more."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"begrudge","p":"verb","d":"To feel unhappy or resentful because someone has something or enjoys something.","lb":"resent, envy","s":["resent","envy","grudge","covet","be jealous of","mind"],"k":["be loath to give","be miserly with","be reluctant to give","be stingy with"],"a":["congratulate","welcome","celebrate","applaud"],"ex":["I don't begrudge my sister her success; she has worked incredibly hard for it.","Some neighbours begrudged the family their new car and said unkind things.","Nobody begrudged the team its victory after such a long season of hard work."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"behest","p":"noun","d":"A command or request from someone with authority, which you are expected to obey.","lb":"command, bidding","s":["command","order","bidding","instruction","directive","request"],"k":["bid","call","dictate","dictation"],"a":[],"ex":["At the principal's behest, all students gathered in the hall.","He came to the meeting at his manager's behest, though he was on leave.","The garden was planted at the behest of the neighborhood committee."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"beholder","p":"noun","d":"A person who looks at or sees something, especially something striking.","lb":"viewer, observer","s":["observer","viewer","spectator","watcher","witness","bystander"],"k":["admirer","connoisseur","critic","evaluator"],"a":[],"ex":["Beauty is in the eye of the beholder, my mother says about my paintings.","The enormous painting left the beholder speechless.","To a casual beholder, the old building looks empty, but a family lives inside."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"belabor","p":"verb","d":"To explain or discuss something for much longer than is necessary.","lb":"overdo, harp on","s":["overdo","harp on","dwell on","drag out","rehash","go on about"],"k":["beat into the ground","chew over","dwell at length","flog to death"],"a":["summarize","skim","gloss over"],"ex":["I don’t want to belabor the point, but please remember to turn in the form by Thursday.","The speaker belabored the same example for twenty minutes, and half the audience began checking their phones.","Reviewers said the film belabors its message, repeating the same lesson in every scene."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"beleaguer","p":"verb","d":"To trouble someone again and again with problems or demands; originally, to surround a place with an army.","lb":"harass, besiege","s":["harass","besiege","hound","plague","badger","pester"],"k":["bedevil","beset","bother","bug"],"a":["help","support","relieve","comfort"],"ex":["Complaints from angry customers beleaguered the call center staff all through the holiday week.","The beleaguered teacher tried to finish the lesson while students kept interrupting her.","Rafi was beleaguered by reminders from the bank about his unpaid credit card bill."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"belie","p":"verb","d":"To give a false impression of something, or to show that something is not true.","lb":"contradict, misrepresent","s":["contradict","misrepresent","disguise","mask","conceal","falsify"],"k":["camouflage","depart","deviate","diverge"],"a":["confirm","reveal","support","show"],"ex":["His calm voice belied the fear he felt before the interview.","Her youthful face belies her age; she is actually over fifty.","The shop's shabby front belies the excellent food served inside."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"belittle","p":"verb","d":"To make someone or something seem unimportant or of little value.","lb":"put down, disparage","s":["disparage","demean","downplay","put down","undermine","minimize"],"k":["criticize","decry","degrade","look down on"],"a":["praise","flatter","compliment","exalt"],"ex":["Good teachers never belittle a student who asks a simple question.","He belittled her small business, but it soon grew bigger than his.","Don’t belittle your own achievements just because other people have done more."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"belligerent","p":"adjective","d":"Aggressive and eager to fight or argue.","lb":"aggressive, hostile","s":["aggressive","hostile","combative","quarrelsome","argumentative","pugnacious"],"k":["bristling","bullish","confrontational","contentious"],"a":["peaceful","friendly","conciliatory","gentle"],"ex":["The belligerent customer shouted at the cashier and refused to wait in line.","Their belligerent tone made a simple disagreement turn into a loud fight.","The two belligerent neighbors argued over the parking space every morning."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bellow","p":"verb","d":"To shout in a deep, loud voice, or to make a loud deep sound like a bull.","lb":"shout, roar","s":["roar","shout","yell","boom","thunder","bawl"],"k":["bluster","call","call out","clamor"],"a":["whisper","murmur","mumble","mutter"],"ex":["The coach bellowed instructions from the sideline as the match grew tense.","A bull bellowed from the muddy field behind our village house.","Please don't bellow at the waiter; he is trying to find your table."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bemoan","p":"verb","d":"To express sadness or disappointment about something.","lb":"lament, regret","s":["lament","mourn","regret","deplore","grieve over","complain about"],"k":["bellyache about","carp about","complain","keen over"],"a":["celebrate","rejoice","welcome","applaud"],"ex":["Older residents bemoan the loss of the open fields where children used to play.","Students often bemoan the heavy workload before final exams.","He bemoaned his bad luck after missing the last train by one minute."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bemuse","p":"verb","d":"To confuse someone, so that they do not know what to think.","lb":"puzzle, confuse","s":["puzzle","confuse","bewilder","baffle","mystify","stump"],"k":["addle","amaze","beat","befog"],"a":["enlighten","clarify","explain","inform"],"ex":["The strange instructions on the box bemused everyone in the shop.","The sudden change in the weather bemused the farmers, who had expected rain.","Her odd question bemused the teacher, who had no idea what she meant."],"b":64,"y":4},{"w":"bemused","p":"adjective","d":"Confused and unable to think clearly; puzzled.","lb":"puzzled, bewildered","s":["puzzled","confused","bewildered","perplexed","baffled","dazed"],"k":["at a loss","at sea","befuddled","confounded"],"a":["enlightened","certain"],"ex":["The tourist looked bemused when the rickshaw puller named three different fares for the same ride.","I was bemused by the instructions, which seemed to contradict each other.","She watched, bemused, as the children argued about who should hold the empty box."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"benediction","p":"noun","d":"A blessing, or a spoken wish for happiness and good fortune.","lb":"blessing, good wishes","s":["blessing","prayer","grace","invocation","good wishes","approval"],"k":["beatitude","benison","commendation","godspeed"],"a":["curse","malediction","condemnation"],"ex":["The old teacher ended the ceremony with a gentle benediction for the graduates.","Before the journey, my grandmother gave us her benediction and a packet of sweets.","The bride and groom received the benediction of both families."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"benefactor","p":"noun","d":"A person who gives money or other help to a person, school or cause.","lb":"donor, patron","s":["donor","patron","sponsor","supporter","philanthropist","contributor"],"k":["angel","financier","good person","grantor"],"a":[],"ex":["An unknown benefactor paid the tuition fees for twenty poor students at the village school.","The library was built thanks to a generous benefactor who loved books.","Rafi never forgot his benefactor, a teacher who bought his textbooks every year."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"beneficent","p":"adjective","d":"Kind and generous, and doing good for other people.","lb":"kind, generous","s":["kind","generous","charitable","benevolent","philanthropic","giving"],"k":["altruistic","bighearted","bounteous","gracious"],"a":["malevolent","harmful","cruel","selfish"],"ex":["A beneficent donor paid the school fees of fifty poor children each year.","The beneficent doctor treated villagers for free every Friday.","The beneficent climate of the valley allows farmers to grow two crops a year."],"b":13,"y":0},{"w":"benevolent","p":"adjective","d":"Kind and generous, wanting to help others and do good.","lb":"kind, generous","s":["kind","generous","charitable","kindly","caring","humane"],"k":["beneficent","gracious","humanitarian","kindhearted"],"a":["malevolent","cruel","unkind","selfish"],"ex":["A benevolent businessman paid for the school's new library and asked for no credit.","The village runs a benevolent fund that helps families during floods.","Our teacher gave us a benevolent smile and let us finish our answers."],"b":592,"y":1},{"w":"benighted","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking knowledge or understanding, often in a way that seems backward or unfortunate.","lb":"ignorant, unenlightened","s":["ignorant","unenlightened","uneducated","backward","uncultured","naive"],"k":["dark","narrow-minded","obtuse","superstitious"],"a":["enlightened","educated","informed","knowledgeable"],"ex":["Reformers fought against benighted ideas that kept girls out of school.","The professor said it was a benighted view to think science is a waste of time.","The old law reflected benighted attitudes toward disabled people, and campaigners worked to change it."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"benign","p":"adjective","d":"Harmless or gentle in effect or manner, and, for a medical growth, not cancerous.","lb":"harmless, gentle","s":["harmless","gentle","kind","mild","kindly","gracious"],"k":["innocent","inoffensive","minor","nonthreatening"],"a":["malignant","harmful","hostile","dangerous"],"ex":["The doctor was relieved to tell her that the lump was benign.","The village has a benign climate, with mild winters and gentle breezes.","The old teacher gave the nervous students a benign smile."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"bequest","p":"noun","d":"Money or property that someone leaves to a person or organization in their will.","lb":"legacy, gift","s":["legacy","inheritance","endowment","gift","donation","estate"],"k":["birthright","contribution","devise","grant"],"a":[],"ex":["Her grandfather left a bequest to the village school in his will.","A bequest from an old teacher paid for the new science lab.","He received a small bequest of land from his uncle after the old man died."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bereave","p":"verb","d":"To leave someone sad and alone by taking a loved one away through death.","lb":"deprive, orphan","s":["deprive","rob","strip","divest","orphan","widow"],"k":["leave desolate","leave grief-stricken","leave in mourning","sever"],"a":[],"ex":["The accident bereaved three families and left the whole village in mourning.","She was bereaved of her husband at a young age and raised the children alone.","The school sent flowers to the bereaved family after the teacher's sudden death."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"bereaved","p":"adjective","d":"Having lost a close relative or friend through death, and feeling the sadness of that loss.","lb":"grieving, mourning","s":["grieving","mourning","bereft","heartbroken","sorrowing","desolate"],"k":["dispirited","heartsick","in mourning","sorrowful"],"a":[],"ex":["Neighbors brought food to the bereaved family for several days after the funeral.","The teacher spoke gently to the bereaved student and told him to take as much time as he needed.","A support group for the bereaved meets at the community center every Saturday evening."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"beset","p":"verb","d":"To trouble or attack someone or something continuously, often with many problems at once.","lb":"trouble, surround","s":["plague","harass","trouble","afflict","torment","hound"],"k":["annoy","bother","chafe","chevy"],"a":["help","aid","assist","protect"],"ex":["The new restaurant was beset by problems from the first week, including power cuts and missing staff.","Beset with doubts, Sadia read the exam instructions three times before she picked up her pen.","Farmers in the region are beset by floods every monsoon and rarely finish a full harvest."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bestow","p":"verb","d":"To give something valuable, such as an honour, a gift or a title, to someone.","lb":"give, award","s":["give","grant","present","confer","award","donate"],"k":["accord","contribute","hand out","lavish"],"a":["withhold","deny","refuse","take away"],"ex":["The university will bestow an honorary degree on the retired scientist next month.","The club bestowed a lifetime membership on its founder to thank her for years of service.","My grandfather bestowed his blessing on the young couple at their wedding."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bewilder","p":"verb","d":"To confuse someone completely so that they do not know what to think or do.","lb":"confuse, puzzle","s":["confuse","puzzle","baffle","mystify","confound","stump"],"k":["amaze","beat","befuddle","bemuse"],"a":["enlighten","clarify","explain","inform"],"ex":["The complicated tax form bewildered my father, so he asked an accountant for help.","The number of choices on the menu bewildered the tourists.","Her sudden change of mind bewildered her friends."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bewilderment","p":"noun","d":"A state of being very confused and unable to understand something.","lb":"confusion, puzzlement","s":["confusion","puzzlement","disorientation","mystification","daze"],"k":["befuddlement","consternation","disarray","dismay"],"a":["understanding","clarity","comprehension","certainty"],"ex":["He stared at the complicated form in bewilderment.","The tourists looked at each other in bewilderment when the train changed platforms.","Her bewilderment grew as the teacher explained the problem a third time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bibliography","p":"noun","d":"A list of the books and articles used or mentioned in a piece of research or writing.","lb":"reference list","s":["reference list","works cited","references","reading list","citations"],"k":["catalog","directory","index","inventory"],"a":[],"ex":["Our teacher said the thesis would lose marks without a proper bibliography.","I found two useful books by checking the bibliography at the end of the article.","List every website in the bibliography, together with the date you visited it."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bilious","p":"adjective","d":"Bad-tempered and easily annoyed, as if feeling sick.","lb":"grumpy, irritable","s":["irritable","grumpy","cranky","peevish","testy","irascible"],"k":["bad-tempered","dyspeptic","fractious","fussy"],"a":["cheerful","genial","amiable","easygoing"],"ex":["My uncle is bilious in the morning and snaps at anyone who speaks before his tea.","The critic's bilious review complained about everything from the food to the napkins.","After the long delay, the bilious passengers shouted at the airline staff."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bitter","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling angry and resentful because of unfair treatment or disappointment.","lb":"resentful, angry","s":["resentful","embittered","aggrieved","sour","acrimonious","spiteful"],"k":["acerbic","acrid","biting","intolerable"],"a":["forgiving","content","cheerful","genial"],"ex":["She is still bitter about the way the company treated her.","A bitter old man sat at the tea stall complaining about his sons.","He felt bitter when his friend got the scholarship he had worked for."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"bivouac","p":"noun","d":"A temporary camp, often without tents, used by soldiers, climbers or hikers for a night.","lb":"temporary camp, campsite","s":["camp","encampment","campsite","shelter","temporary camp"],"k":["billet","bivvy","campground","camping area"],"a":[],"ex":["The climbers set up a bivouac on a narrow ledge before the final climb.","After a long day's march, the soldiers made their bivouac in the forest.","We spent a cold night in a bivouac under the stars during the school trek."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"blacksmith","p":"noun","d":"A person who makes and repairs iron objects by heating the metal and hammering it into shape.","lb":"iron worker","s":["smith","forger"],"k":["armorer","farrier","forgeman","metalsmith"],"a":[],"ex":["The village blacksmith made a new blade for the farmer's plough.","A blacksmith heats iron in a fire until it is soft enough to shape.","We watched a blacksmith make a door hinge at the folk festival."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"blanch","p":"verb","d":"To become pale suddenly because of fear, shock or illness.","lb":"turn pale, whiten","s":["turn pale","pale","go white","whiten","lose colour","fade"],"k":["bleach","color","drain","drain of color"],"a":["blush","flush","glow"],"ex":["She blanched when she saw the huge bill.","He blanched at the sight of blood and had to sit down.","Parents blanched at the thought of their son driving alone through the storm."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bland","p":"adjective","d":"Having little taste, flavor or interest; mild and not exciting.","lb":"tasteless, dull","s":["tasteless","insipid","flavorless","dull","mild","boring"],"k":["diplomatic","flat","lifeless","politic"],"a":["spicy","flavorful","tasty","exciting"],"ex":["The hospital soup was bland, so I added extra salt and pepper.","He gave a bland speech full of long words but no real ideas.","The hotel room was clean but bland, with white walls and no pictures."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"blandishment","p":"noun","d":"Pleasant, flattering words or actions used to gently persuade someone to do what you want.","lb":"flattery, coaxing","s":["flattery","coaxing","sweet talk","soft soap","adulation"],"k":["blarney","come-on","enticement","honeyed words"],"a":["criticism","insult","rebuke"],"ex":["Despite the salesman's blandishments, Nadia refused to buy the expensive laptop.","No amount of blandishment could persuade the old shopkeeper to lower his price.","With sweet blandishments, the little girl convinced her father to buy her an ice cream."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"blasphemous","p":"adjective","d":"Showing great disrespect for God or for things that people consider holy.","lb":"irreverent, profane","s":["irreverent","profane","sacrilegious","impious","ungodly","disrespectful"],"k":["blue","defiant","dirty","dishonoring"],"a":["reverent","pious","devout","respectful"],"ex":["Some viewers found the cartoon blasphemous and asked the channel to remove it.","The film was banned in several countries because officials called it blasphemous.","He apologized for the blasphemous joke after many listeners complained."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"blasphemy","p":"noun","d":"Speech or action that shows great disrespect for God or for something people hold sacred.","lb":"irreverence, profanity","s":["sacrilege","profanity","irreverence","desecration","godlessness","cursing"],"k":["contempt","defiance","dishonor","heresy"],"a":["reverence","piety","devotion","respect"],"ex":["In many societies, mocking a sacred text is considered blasphemy and deeply offends believers.","Historians have studied how laws against blasphemy were used in different countries.","In our literature class, we discussed why some old books were banned for blasphemy."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"blatant","p":"adjective","d":"Done openly and obviously, without any attempt to hide it, especially something bad.","lb":"obvious, shameless","s":["flagrant","obvious","glaring","shameless","brazen","barefaced"],"k":["blazing","blinding","egregious","gross"],"a":["subtle","hidden","discreet","concealed"],"ex":["It was a blatant lie, and everyone in the room knew it.","The driver showed blatant disregard for the red light and sped through the crossing.","Copying a classmate's answers during the test was a blatant act of cheating."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"blatantly","p":"adverb","d":"In a very obvious way, without trying to hide it or caring what others think.","lb":"openly, flagrantly","s":["openly","flagrantly","brazenly","shamelessly","obviously","glaringly"],"k":["boldly","crudely","defiantly","grossly"],"a":["secretly","discreetly","subtly","covertly"],"ex":["The driver blatantly ignored the red light and sped through the crossing.","The advertisement blatantly lied about the price, and customers complained.","The company blatantly broke the safety rules and was fined."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"blight","p":"noun","d":"A disease that makes plants wither, or anything that spoils or damages a place or situation.","lb":"plant disease, ruin","s":["plague","scourge","curse","affliction","bane","menace"],"k":["burden","cancer","eyesore","mildew"],"a":["blessing","boon","benefit","asset"],"ex":["A sudden blight destroyed most of the potato crop in the village this winter.","Heaps of uncollected rubbish are a blight on our neighborhood.","Corruption has been a blight on the country's progress for many years."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"blighted","p":"adjective","d":"Damaged or ruined by disease, neglect or something harmful, so that it cannot grow or prosper.","lb":"ruined, spoiled","s":["ruined","spoiled","damaged","withered","wrecked","afflicted"],"k":["barren","blasted","cursed","dashed"],"a":["thriving","flourishing","healthy","prosperous"],"ex":["Farmers burned the blighted potato plants to stop the disease from spreading.","The blighted neighbourhood was full of empty shops, broken roads and uncollected rubbish.","His blighted hopes of studying abroad left him quiet for weeks."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bliss","p":"noun","d":"Perfect happiness; a state of great joy and peace.","lb":"joy, happiness","s":["joy","ecstasy","happiness","delight","rapture","euphoria"],"k":["beatitude","blessedness","cloud nine","exaltation"],"a":["misery","agony","sorrow","despair"],"ex":["After the exams ended, sleeping late felt like absolute bliss.","A cup of hot tea on a rainy evening is pure bliss.","The newlyweds enjoyed a week of wedded bliss in the hills."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"blithe","p":"adjective","d":"Cheerful and carefree, sometimes in a way that shows too little concern for serious matters.","lb":"carefree, unconcerned","s":["carefree","cheerful","casual","jaunty","nonchalant","lighthearted"],"k":["blasé","buoyant","cavalier","complacent"],"a":["concerned","anxious","worried","careful"],"ex":["He walked into the exam hall with a blithe smile, though he had barely studied.","The driver showed a blithe disregard for the red light and almost hit a rickshaw.","Her blithe attitude toward deadlines drives her teammates crazy."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"bloat","p":"verb","d":"To swell up with gas, liquid or air, or to make something swell.","lb":"swell, puff up","s":["swell","puff up","distend","balloon","inflate","expand"],"k":["bulge","dilate","fatten","fill out"],"a":["shrink","deflate","contract","shrivel"],"ex":["Eating too much salty food can make your face and hands bloat.","My stomach bloated after I drank a large bottle of fizzy drink too quickly.","Many people feel bloated after a heavy dinner of rich biryani and sweets."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bloom","p":"verb","d":"To open into flowers, or to grow and develop in a healthy way.","lb":"flower, blossom","s":["flower","blossom","open","flourish","thrive","bud"],"k":["blush","boom","develop","emerge"],"a":["wither","fade","wilt","decline"],"ex":["Shapla lilies bloom in village ponds after the monsoon rains.","My mother's jasmine plant blooms every evening and fills the balcony with fragrance.","In spring, the cherry trees in the park bloom and attract crowds of visitors."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"blurt","p":"verb","d":"To say something suddenly and without thinking, often when you should have kept it quiet.","lb":"say suddenly","s":["exclaim","blab","let slip","utter","spill","burst out"],"k":["babble","babble out","blab out","blunder"],"a":["withhold","conceal","keep quiet","hold back"],"ex":["Nadia blurted out the answer before the teacher finished the question.","He blurted out the secret of the surprise party by mistake.","I almost blurted that I had already seen the film."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bluster","p":"verb","d":"To talk in a loud, angry or boastful way, often without any real power or effect behind the words.","lb":"rant, boast","s":["rant","bellow","boast","swagger","storm","fume"],"k":["amplify","blow hard","bluff","exaggerate"],"a":["whisper","murmur","speak softly"],"ex":["The neighbour blustered about calling the police, but he never actually made the call.","Rafi blustered through his speech, shouting to hide the fact that he had not prepared.","The shop owner blustered and threatened to sue, yet he had no proof of any wrongdoing."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"boisterous","p":"adjective","d":"Noisy, lively and full of energy, in a way that is not well controlled.","lb":"rowdy, noisy","s":["rowdy","noisy","rambunctious","lively","unruly","rough"],"k":["animated","disorderly","fierce","loud"],"a":["quiet","calm","subdued","restrained"],"ex":["A boisterous group of students filled the tea stall after the match.","The boisterous puppy knocked over a vase while chasing the ball.","Boisterous laughter came from the next room, where the cousins were playing cards."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bolster","p":"verb","d":"To support or strengthen something, making it more secure or more effective.","lb":"support, strengthen","s":["strengthen","support","reinforce","boost","buttress","fortify"],"k":["back up","beef up","encourage","pad"],"a":["weaken","undermine","undercut","erode"],"ex":["Good exam results helped bolster his confidence before the university interview.","The shop hired two more workers to bolster its delivery service during Eid.","Scientists published new evidence to bolster their claim that the river water was unsafe."],"b":67,"y":1},{"w":"bombast","p":"noun","d":"Grand, pompous speech or writing that sounds impressive but has little real meaning.","lb":"pomposity, hot air","s":["pomposity","hot air","rhetoric","bluster","rant"],"k":["blah","claptrap","empty words","flamboyance"],"a":["plain speaking","simplicity","modesty","understatement"],"ex":["The speaker's talk was all bombast, with big promises and no real plans.","His emails are full of bombast, so it takes a while to find the real request.","I ignore the bombast in the advertisement and look only at the facts and the price."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bombastic","p":"adjective","d":"Using grand, important-sounding words that are too exaggerated for what is actually being said.","lb":"pompous, inflated","s":["pompous","grandiose","inflated","pretentious","turgid","windy"],"k":["grandiloquent","large","orotund","ostentatious"],"a":["modest","plain","simple","restrained"],"ex":["The speaker's bombastic address used big words but said very little about real plans.","Her essay sounded bombastic, so the teacher asked her to write in plainer English.","The manager's bombastic emails, full of long words, annoyed his busy colleagues."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"bon vivant","p":"noun","d":"A person who enjoys a luxurious social life, especially good food and fine company.","lb":"epicure, pleasure-seeker","s":["epicure","gourmet","foodie","hedonist","sybarite"],"k":["connoisseur","dandy","libertine","man about town"],"a":["ascetic","puritan","recluse"],"ex":["My uncle is a true bon vivant who knows every good restaurant in town.","Known as a bon vivant, the old professor loved long dinners and lively conversation.","The novel's hero is a charming bon vivant who spends his money on parties and travel."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bona fide","p":"adjective","d":"Real and genuine, not false; done or offered honestly and in good faith.","lb":"genuine, authentic","s":["genuine","authentic","real","legitimate","sincere","honest"],"k":["above board","accredited","actual","certified"],"a":["fake","false","counterfeit","bogus"],"ex":["Only bona fide students are allowed to use the university library after eight o'clock.","The seller asked for a deposit to prove that the buyer's offer was bona fide.","This is a bona fide leather wallet, not a cheap plastic copy."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"boon","p":"noun","d":"Something that is very helpful and makes life easier or better.","lb":"blessing, benefit","s":["blessing","benefit","advantage","godsend","gift","windfall"],"k":["bounty","good fortune","good luck","help"],"a":["curse","drawback","disadvantage","burden"],"ex":["The new metro rail is a boon for commuters who are tired of sitting in Dhaka traffic.","Free online lectures are a boon to students who cannot afford private tutors.","The rain was a boon for the farmers after weeks of dry weather."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"boor","p":"noun","d":"A rude, rough person with bad manners who does not care about other people's feelings.","lb":"lout, rude person","s":["lout","oaf","churl","clod","brute","philistine"],"k":["barbarian","bounder","bumpkin","cad"],"a":["gentleman","lady"],"ex":["He behaved like a boor at the dinner, talking loudly with his mouth full.","The boor at the next table kept laughing at the waiter's mistakes.","Nobody invited the boor who always interrupted and insulted other guests at parties."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"boorish","p":"adjective","d":"Rude, rough and insensitive in manner, with no concern for other people's feelings.","lb":"rude, crude","s":["rude","crude","coarse","uncouth","churlish","vulgar"],"k":["brusque","classless","common","earthy"],"a":["polite","courteous","refined","civil"],"ex":["It was boorish of him to talk loudly on the phone during the film.","The boorish customer shouted at the waiter and left without a tip.","Her cousin's boorish jokes at the dinner table embarrassed the whole family."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"booty","p":"noun","d":"Valuable goods taken by force, especially by soldiers, pirates or thieves.","lb":"loot, plunder","s":["loot","plunder","spoils","haul","swag","takings"],"k":["bounty","cache","contraband","dirty money"],"a":[],"ex":["The pirates buried their booty on a small island and drew a map to find it again.","The thieves fled with their booty, but police caught them at the border.","After the battle, the victorious army divided the booty among the soldiers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"borrower","p":"noun","d":"A person or organization that takes something, usually money, and promises to give it back later.","lb":"one who borrows","s":["debtor","loan taker"],"k":["applicant","cardholder","customer","obligor"],"a":["lender","creditor"],"ex":["A good borrower pays every instalment on time and keeps in touch with the bank.","Small loans from the village cooperative helped many borrowers start tiny businesses.","The library fines every borrower who returns a book after the due date."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"botch","p":"verb","d":"To spoil a task or piece of work by doing it badly or clumsily.","lb":"bungle, mess up","s":["bungle","mess up","ruin","spoil","fumble","muff"],"k":["ball up","bobble","bollocks","bollocks up"],"a":["succeed at","nail","ace","perfect"],"ex":["The barber botched my haircut, so I had to wear a cap for a week.","Rafi botched the first question of the interview and never really recovered.","The workers botched the repair, and the tap was leaking again the next morning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"boulder","p":"noun","d":"A very large rock, often smooth and rounded by weather or water.","lb":"large rock","s":["rock","stone","crag","slab"],"k":["block","bluff","chunk","megalith"],"a":[],"ex":["A huge boulder rolled onto the hill road and blocked the traffic.","The children climbed on a large boulder beside the stream.","It took six men to move the boulder from the middle of the field."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bourgeois","p":"adjective","d":"Typical of the middle class, especially in being conventional and interested in money and possessions.","lb":"middle-class, conventional","s":["conventional","materialistic","conservative","traditional","comfortable","humdrum"],"k":["accepted","capitalist","capitalistic","customary"],"a":["bohemian","unconventional","radical","proletarian"],"ex":["The poet rejected bourgeois comfort and lived in a tiny attic room.","His parents' bourgeois dream was a government job, a flat and a car.","The novel mocks the bourgeois obsession with owning the latest gadgets."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bovine","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to cows or cattle, or slow, calm and rather dull like a cow.","lb":"cowlike, cattle-related","s":["stolid","placid","slow","sluggish","dull","phlegmatic"],"k":["calm","composed","docile","impassive"],"a":["alert","lively","quick","sharp"],"ex":["The vet warned farmers about a bovine disease spreading through nearby villages.","Scientists are testing a new vaccine for bovine tuberculosis in dairy herds.","The waiter stared at us with a bovine expression and forgot our order twice."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bracing","p":"adjective","d":"Making you feel fresh, energetic and alert, especially because of cool air.","lb":"invigorating, refreshing","s":["invigorating","refreshing","stimulating","fresh","energizing","crisp"],"k":["biting","chilly","cold","exciting"],"a":["exhausting","draining","stifling","debilitating"],"ex":["We took a bracing walk along the river before breakfast.","The bracing mountain air made the tired travelers feel alive again.","A cold shower on a hot day can be surprisingly bracing."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brag","p":"verb","d":"To talk about your achievements or possessions with too much pride.","lb":"boast","s":["boast","show off","swagger","crow","gloat","flaunt"],"k":["amplify","blow one's own trumpet","exaggerate","gasconade"],"a":["downplay","understate","be modest"],"ex":["He likes to brag about his new phone to everyone at school.","Don't brag about your marks in front of the students who failed.","My cousin bragged that he could eat ten rasgullas at once."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"brandish","p":"verb","d":"To wave or hold something up in the air, often in a threatening or showy way.","lb":"wave, flourish","s":["wave","flourish","wield","flaunt","shake","swing"],"k":["displace","exhibit","flail","gesticulate"],"a":["sheathe","conceal","hide"],"ex":["The angry customer brandished his receipt and demanded his money back.","Fans brandished flags and banners as the cricket team's bus drove slowly through the street.","The teacher brandished a ruler like a conductor's baton, keeping time as we recited the poem."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"bravado","p":"noun","d":"A show of confidence or courage that is not real, often put on to impress other people.","lb":"false courage, swagger","s":["swagger","bluster","bluff","boasting","bragging","bold front"],"k":["audacity","boast","chutzpah","daring"],"a":["modesty","timidity","humility","cowardice"],"ex":["Out of bravado, he said he was not afraid of the dark, though his voice shook.","The boys' bravado disappeared as soon as the old bridge began to shake.","Her bravado before the interview hid how nervous she really was."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brawn","p":"noun","d":"Great physical strength, especially the kind that comes from having big, strong muscles.","lb":"muscle, strength","s":["muscle","strength","power","might","sinew","toughness"],"k":["beef","bulk","burliness","heft"],"a":["weakness","frailty"],"ex":["Moving the heavy cupboard took more brawn than the two of us had.","He relies on brawn rather than brains when he solves problems.","The rickshaw puller's brawn amazed everyone as he carried three passengers up the slope of the bridge."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brazen","p":"adjective","d":"Shamelessly bold, showing no embarrassment about doing something wrong or rude.","lb":"bold, shameless","s":["shameless","impudent","bold","barefaced","audacious","insolent"],"k":["bodacious","brassy","brave","disrespectful"],"a":["shy","timid","modest","bashful"],"ex":["The brazen thief walked into the shop in daylight and took three phones from the counter.","She told a brazen lie to her manager and showed no sign of guilt.","Students were shocked by his brazen attempt to copy answers while the invigilator stood right beside him."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"breach","p":"noun","d":"A failure to keep a rule, law or promise; also, a gap or opening in a barrier.","lb":"violation, gap","s":["violation","infringement","break","contravention","infraction","gap"],"k":["detachment","falling out","hole","misdemeanour"],"a":["compliance","observance","adherence","obedience"],"ex":["Sharing the exam questions was a serious breach of school rules.","The company faced a data breach, and thousands of customers had to change their passwords.","Floodwater rushed through a breach in the river embankment and covered the fields."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brevity","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being short, especially in speech or writing.","lb":"briefness, conciseness","s":["shortness","economy"],"k":["bluntness","compression","crispness","directness"],"a":["length"],"ex":["For the sake of brevity, I will only mention the three main points.","Text messages are famous for their brevity, so people often skip punctuation.","The brevity of her speech surprised the audience, but everyone enjoyed it."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"brink","p":"noun","d":"The edge of a steep place, or the point just before something big happens.","lb":"edge, verge","s":["edge","verge","threshold","lip","rim","margin"],"k":["abyss","boundary","cusp","eve"],"a":["middle","centre","interior"],"ex":["The little boy stood at the brink of the pond and watched the fish.","The company was on the brink of bankruptcy until a new investor saved it.","After a long argument, the two friends were on the brink of ending their friendship."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brisk","p":"adjective","d":"Quick, active and full of energy.","lb":"quick, energetic","s":["quick","fast","energetic","lively","vigorous","spry"],"k":["active","alert","bracing","dynamic"],"a":["slow","sluggish","lazy","leisurely"],"ex":["A brisk walk before breakfast helps me wake up and stay healthy.","The tea stall did brisk business on the cold winter morning.","She set a brisk pace, and I had to hurry to keep up."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bristle","p":"verb","d":"To react with visible anger or annoyance, especially when you feel criticised or insulted.","lb":"take offence, flare up","s":["bridle","take offence","flare up","seethe","get angry","stiffen"],"k":["abound","burst","chafe","have"],"a":["relax","calm down","take in stride"],"ex":["He bristled when his boss criticised his work in front of everyone.","She bristled at the suggestion that she had cheated in the test.","The cat bristled and hissed when the stranger's dog came too close."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brittle","p":"adjective","d":"Hard but easily broken or snapped, with little ability to bend.","lb":"hard, easily snapped","s":["fragile","breakable","crumbly","frail","inflexible","delicate"],"k":["brickle","chipped","coldhearted","dainty"],"a":["flexible","pliable","elastic","supple"],"ex":["Old plastic becomes brittle in the sun and cracks when you bend it.","Elderly people with brittle bones can break a hip in a simple fall.","Dry autumn leaves are brittle and crunch under your shoes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"broach","p":"verb","d":"To start talking about a subject, especially one that is sensitive or difficult to discuss.","lb":"bring up, raise","s":["raise","bring up","introduce","mention","open","suggest"],"k":["allude to","approach","discuss","float"],"a":["avoid","evade","sidestep","suppress"],"ex":["Rafi waited until after dinner to broach the subject of moving to a bigger flat.","It is never easy to broach the topic of salary with a new boss.","She finally broached the idea of studying abroad when her parents were relaxed on Friday morning."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"bromide","p":"noun","d":"A boring, obvious remark that has been said so often that it has lost its meaning.","lb":"cliché, platitude","s":["cliche","platitude","banality","commonplace","old chestnut","trite remark"],"k":["adage","catchphrase","comment","hackneyed phrase"],"a":[],"ex":["Time heals all wounds is a bromide that does not help someone who is grieving.","The speaker filled her talk with bromides about hard work and success.","He answered my worries with a bromide: everything happens for a reason."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brook","p":"verb","d":"To tolerate or permit something, usually used in negative statements.","lb":"tolerate, allow","s":["tolerate","endure","stand","bear","allow","abide"],"k":["countenance","digest","enable","let"],"a":["forbid","prohibit","reject","refuse"],"ex":["The manager will not brook any excuses for late reports.","Our teacher cannot brook cheating, so anyone caught copying gets zero.","My father brooks no argument when it comes to finishing homework before dinner."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"brouhaha","p":"noun","d":"A noisy, excited reaction or argument about something that is not really very important.","lb":"uproar, fuss","s":["uproar","commotion","fuss","hubbub","furor","ruckus"],"k":["ado","din","hullabaloo","katzenjammer"],"a":["calm","peace","quiet","tranquility"],"ex":["There was a huge brouhaha online when the café changed its logo.","The brouhaha over the missing marker pens ended when we found them in the staff room.","A brouhaha broke out at the ticket counter when someone cut the line."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"brusque","p":"adjective","d":"Speaking or acting in a quick, short and rather rude way.","lb":"abrupt, curt","s":["abrupt","curt","blunt","gruff","terse","short"],"k":["brisk","clipped","disconnected","discourteous"],"a":["polite","courteous","gracious","tactful"],"ex":["The receptionist was brusque and answered every question in two words.","His brusque reply made the new student feel unwelcome.","She apologized for being brusque; she was just very tired after work."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bucolic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the countryside in a pleasant, peaceful way, especially village life.","lb":"rural, pastoral","s":["rural","pastoral","rustic","idyllic","country","agrarian"],"k":["agricultural","bosky","green","peaceful"],"a":["urban","metropolitan","industrial","cosmopolitan"],"ex":["After a year in noisy Dhaka, the bucolic quiet of my grandparents' village felt like a gift.","The painting shows a bucolic scene of cows grazing beside a quiet pond.","They bought a small cottage in a bucolic corner of the hills to escape the stress of the city."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"budding","p":"adjective","d":"Beginning to develop; showing signs of becoming successful or skilled.","lb":"developing, promising","s":["promising","developing","aspiring","emerging","fledgling","potential"],"k":["apprentice","incipient","nascent","novice"],"a":["established","veteran","seasoned","experienced"],"ex":["The school invited a budding poet to read her work at the annual function.","He is a budding engineer who already builds small robots from old toys.","A budding friendship between the two new classmates soon became a close bond."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"buffoon","p":"noun","d":"A person who behaves in a silly way, often to make others laugh, or who seems foolish.","lb":"clown, fool","s":["clown","fool","jester","joker","comic","goofball"],"k":["clod","comedian","dolt","dope"],"a":[],"ex":["Rafi plays the buffoon in school plays and always gets the biggest laughs.","The film's hero is a harmless buffoon who trips over his own feet.","Nobody took the uncle seriously; to them he was a loud buffoon at family gatherings."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"bulk","p":"noun","d":"The main or largest part of something.","lb":"main part, majority","s":["majority","mass","main part","greater part","preponderance","body"],"k":["core","figure","gist","heart"],"a":["minority","fraction","small part"],"ex":["The bulk of my monthly salary goes toward rent and food.","The bulk of the homework can be finished in one evening if you stay focused.","The bulk of the flood water had drained away by Monday morning."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"bulwark","p":"noun","d":"A strong wall built for defense, or anything that protects something from harm.","lb":"barrier, safeguard","s":["rampart","bastion","fortification","barrier","defense","safeguard"],"k":["breakwater","citadel","dike","fortress"],"a":[],"ex":["A high concrete bulwark along the coast protects the town from storm surges.","A free press is a bulwark against corruption.","Good friends are a bulwark against loneliness during difficult times."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"buoyant","p":"adjective","d":"Able to float on a liquid or to rise through air or another gas.","lb":"floating, light","s":["floating","afloat","light","weightless","airy","lighter than water"],"k":["aimless","cheerful","chirpy","floaty"],"a":["sinking","heavy","weighty","submerged"],"ex":["A life jacket is made of buoyant material, so it keeps you afloat.","Salt water is more buoyant than fresh water, so it is easier to float in the sea.","The empty plastic bottle was so buoyant that it bobbed on the pond all day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"bureaucracy","p":"noun","d":"A system of management with many officials and strict rules, often slow and complicated.","lb":"red tape, officialdom","s":["red tape","administration","paperwork","the system","civil service"],"k":["bumf","formalities","governance","government officials"],"a":[],"ex":["Getting a trade license took months because of the endless bureaucracy.","She spent three days going from office to office to deal with the bureaucracy for her visa.","The charity struggled with bureaucracy before it could open its school."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"burgeon","p":"verb","d":"To grow or increase quickly and successfully, like a young plant or a business.","lb":"grow, flourish","s":["flourish","thrive","expand","boom","mushroom","blossom"],"k":["bloom","escalate","increase","multiply"],"a":["shrink","decline","wither","dwindle"],"ex":["Dhaka's burgeoning population has put heavy pressure on housing, roads and schools.","The online shopping business has burgeoned since more people started using mobile payments.","After the spring rain, the rose bushes in our garden began to burgeon."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"burglar","p":"noun","d":"A person who breaks into a building to steal things.","lb":"thief, housebreaker","s":["thief","robber","intruder","raider","stealer"],"k":["cracksman","crook","looter","prowler"],"a":[],"ex":["A burglar broke the back window and stole the laptop while we were away.","The neighbours heard the alarm and the burglar ran away empty-handed.","The police caught the burglar a week later, trying to sell the stolen phone."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"burlesque","p":"noun","d":"A funny, exaggerated imitation of a serious work or subject, meant to make fun of it.","lb":"parody, spoof","s":["parody","spoof","caricature","satire","mockery","travesty"],"k":["farce","imitation","impersonation","pastiche"],"a":[],"ex":["The school drama club performed a burlesque of a famous love story, and the audience laughed all evening.","His burlesque of the headmaster’s speech, complete with a fake mustache, made everyone laugh.","The magazine published a burlesque of the latest hit film, exaggerating every dramatic moment."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"burnish","p":"verb","d":"To polish something by rubbing it until it becomes smooth and shiny.","lb":"polish, shine","s":["polish","shine","buff","rub","brighten","gloss"],"k":["enhance","furbish","scour","spruce up"],"a":["tarnish","dull","stain","corrode"],"ex":["Before the wedding, she burnished the old brass lamps until they glowed.","My father burnishes his leather shoes every Sunday night with a soft cloth.","The potter burnished the clay pot with a smooth stone before baking it."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"buttress","p":"verb","d":"To strengthen or support an argument, idea or structure so that it is more secure.","lb":"support, reinforce","s":["support","reinforce","strengthen","bolster","prop up","shore up"],"k":["anchor","beef up","brace","champion"],"a":["undermine","weaken","undercut","erode"],"ex":["The lawyer brought new documents to buttress her client's version of events.","Workers buttressed the old wall with steel beams before the monsoon arrived.","The charity's work is buttressed by hundreds of volunteers who give up their weekends."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"cabal","p":"noun","d":"A small, secret group of people who work together to gain power or to plan something against others.","lb":"clique, conspiracy","s":["clique","faction","junta","conspiracy","plot","ring"],"k":["brotherhood","camarilla","camp","cell"],"a":[],"ex":["A cabal of senior managers secretly planned to push the founder out of the company.","The club president accused a small cabal of members of rigging the vote.","In the novel, a cabal of rich landowners plots to seize the village's common land."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cache","p":"noun","d":"A secret store of things such as food, money or weapons, or the place where they are hidden.","lb":"hidden store, stash","s":["stash","hoard","store","stockpile","reserve","hideaway"],"k":["depot","dump","fund","hidey-hole"],"a":[],"ex":["Police discovered a cache of stolen phones hidden under the floor of the warehouse.","Squirrels bury a cache of nuts in autumn and dig it up in the cold months.","Hikers found a cache of food and water left by earlier travellers in the mountain hut."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cacophony","p":"noun","d":"A loud, unpleasant mixture of sounds that seem to clash with one another.","lb":"din, racket","s":["din","racket","noise","clamor","uproar","discord"],"k":["babel","blare","blaring","clatter"],"a":["harmony","silence","quiet","melody"],"ex":["A cacophony of car horns filled the street during the evening rush hour in Dhaka.","The classroom was a cacophony of laughter, scraping chairs and shouting before the teacher arrived.","At dawn, a cacophony of crows woke the whole neighborhood."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"cadence","p":"noun","d":"The rhythm or rise and fall of a voice, music or a series of sounds.","lb":"rhythm, intonation","s":["rhythm","beat","tempo","lilt","intonation","inflection"],"k":["cycle","pattern","pitch","poetic rhythm"],"a":[],"ex":["The poet read her verses in a gentle cadence that made the audience lean forward.","I love the cadence of rain falling on the tin roof at night.","A good speaker varies the cadence of his voice instead of speaking in a flat tone."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cajole","p":"verb","d":"To persuade someone to do something by gentle, sweet words or flattery.","lb":"coax, sweet-talk","s":["coax","persuade","wheedle","flatter","inveigle","entice"],"k":["beguile","blarney","butter up","induce"],"a":["force","compel","bully","coerce"],"ex":["She cajoled her father into lending her the car for the weekend.","The shopkeeper tried to cajole us into buying a more expensive carpet.","I had to cajole my stubborn friend into joining the study group."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"calamity","p":"noun","d":"A sudden event that causes great damage, loss or suffering.","lb":"disaster, catastrophe","s":["disaster","catastrophe","tragedy","misfortune","cataclysm","mishap"],"k":["bad luck","crisis","debacle","fiasco"],"a":["blessing","boon","triumph","success"],"ex":["The flood was a calamity for the farmers, who lost their entire crop.","Losing all my files just before the deadline felt like a calamity.","The factory fire was a calamity that left hundreds of people without jobs."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"calcify","p":"verb","d":"To become rigid and fixed, unable to change or develop.","lb":"stiffen, harden","s":["harden","stiffen","ossify","solidify","petrify","set"],"k":["atrophy","crystallize","entrench","go rigid"],"a":["soften","loosen","evolve","adapt"],"ex":["If a company never changes its methods, its habits calcify and it falls behind.","His opinions calcified with age, and he refused to listen to any new idea.","Rules that once helped students can calcify into rigid traditions nobody questions."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"callous","p":"adjective","d":"Showing no sympathy or concern for the feelings and suffering of other people.","lb":"heartless, unfeeling","s":["heartless","unfeeling","cold","insensitive","cruel","hardhearted"],"k":["flint","flinty","thickened","tough"],"a":["compassionate","caring","kind","sympathetic"],"ex":["It was callous of him to laugh at his friend's mistake.","A callous driver left the scene without checking whether the cyclist was hurt.","Her callous remarks about the poor made everyone uncomfortable."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"callow","p":"adjective","d":"Young and inexperienced, and lacking the maturity or judgment that comes with age.","lb":"immature, inexperienced","s":["immature","inexperienced","green","naive","raw","unsophisticated"],"k":["fledgling","fresh","gawky","impressionable"],"a":["mature","experienced","seasoned","sophisticated"],"ex":["The callow intern kept asking if he could leave early, not understanding how an office works.","As a callow first-year student, I believed every senior I met was an expert.","Her callow remarks about money showed that she had never paid a bill in her life."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"calumny","p":"noun","d":"A false statement made on purpose to damage someone's reputation.","lb":"slander, lie","s":["slander","defamation","libel","smear","aspersion","falsehood"],"k":["character assassination","denigration","disparagement","hatchet job"],"a":["praise","compliment","commendation","accolade"],"ex":["The rumor that she cheated on the test was pure calumny, and the teacher soon proved it.","He took the website to court for publishing calumny that cost him several important clients.","Spreading calumny about a classmate online can seriously damage his reputation and your own."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"camaraderie","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of trust and friendship between people who spend a lot of time together.","lb":"friendship, fellowship","s":["fellowship","friendship","comradeship","companionship","solidarity","togetherness"],"k":["bonhomie","company","conviviality","esprit de corps"],"a":["hostility","rivalry","enmity","isolation"],"ex":["The camaraderie among the players made the team stronger.","Shared hostel life creates camaraderie between students from different towns.","There was real camaraderie in the office, with everyone helping each other meet deadlines."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"candid","p":"adjective","d":"Honest and direct in what you say, even when the truth is uncomfortable.","lb":"frank, honest","s":["frank","honest","direct","blunt","open","straightforward"],"k":["artless","ingenuous","no-nonsense","plain-spoken"],"a":["evasive","secretive","guarded","insincere"],"ex":["To be candid, I think your first draft needs a lot of work.","She gave a candid answer about how nervous she felt before the interview.","The doctor was candid about the risks of the operation."],"b":578,"y":1},{"w":"candor","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being honest and open in what you say, even when the truth is uncomfortable.","lb":"honesty, frankness","s":["frankness","honesty","openness","sincerity","directness","truthfulness"],"k":["fairness","integrity","outspokenness","plain speaking"],"a":["dishonesty","deceit","evasiveness","duplicity"],"ex":["The doctor spoke with candor about the risks of the surgery, and I trusted her more for it.","I appreciated your candor when you told me my presentation was too long.","In the interview, the player showed rare candor by admitting that the team had played badly."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"canon","p":"noun","d":"A general rule or principle by which something is judged or by which people guide their behaviour.","lb":"principle, rule","s":["principle","rule","standard","criterion","law","precept"],"k":["belief","canyon","code","conviction"],"a":[],"ex":["Honesty is a basic canon of good journalism.","Fair play is a canon of sport that coaches teach from the very first lesson.","The canons of good taste change from one generation to the next."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cant","p":"noun","d":"Insincere talk, especially about morals or beliefs, that is repeated without real feeling.","lb":"hypocrisy, humbug","s":["hypocrisy","humbug","pretense","claptrap","lip service"],"k":["bank","bevel","bunk","buzzword"],"a":["sincerity","honesty","candor","truthfulness"],"ex":["His speech about honesty was pure cant, because everyone knew he cheated on his taxes.","I am tired of the cant on social media, where people brag while pretending to be humble.","The mayor's promises of clean water sounded like cant to residents who had waited ten years."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"canvass","p":"verb","d":"To ask people for their votes, opinions or support, often by visiting them.","lb":"poll, solicit","s":["poll","survey","solicit","campaign","sound out","question"],"k":["analyze","approach","court","examine"],"a":[],"ex":["Volunteers went door to door to canvass voters before the local election.","The student club canvassed classmates to find out which trip they preferred.","The company canvassed customers for opinions on its new packaging."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"capacious","p":"adjective","d":"Able to hold a large amount; having plenty of space inside.","lb":"roomy, spacious","s":["spacious","roomy","ample","commodious","voluminous","generous"],"k":["big","broad","copious","extensive"],"a":["cramped","small","narrow","tiny"],"ex":["She packed all her books and a lunchbox into her capacious backpack.","The new car has a capacious trunk that fits our whole family's luggage.","We rented a capacious hall in the city for the wedding reception."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"capitalism","p":"noun","d":"An economic system in which private owners, not the state, control most businesses and keep the profits.","lb":"free enterprise","s":["free enterprise","free market","private enterprise","market economy","market system","private ownership"],"k":["entrepreneurialism","free trade","laissez-faire","mercantilism"],"a":["socialism","communism","state ownership","planned economy"],"ex":["In capitalism, businesses compete with each other to win customers and earn profits.","Our economics teacher compared capitalism with socialism using examples from several countries.","Under capitalism, individuals can own factories, shops and land, and keep the profits they make."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"capitulate","p":"verb","d":"To stop resisting and give in to someone's demands or to a stronger opponent.","lb":"surrender, give in","s":["surrender","yield","give in","submit","concede","cave in"],"k":["acquiesce","buckle","cede","deliver"],"a":["resist","fight","hold out","defy"],"ex":["After weeks of complaints from customers, the shop finally capitulated and offered refunds.","The tired parents capitulated and bought their daughter the expensive phone she wanted.","Our team refused to capitulate even when we were five goals behind."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"capricious","p":"adjective","d":"Changing suddenly in mood or behavior, without any clear reason.","lb":"fickle, unpredictable","s":["fickle","unpredictable","changeable","erratic","impulsive","whimsical"],"k":["arbitrary","freakish","moody","random"],"a":["steady","consistent","constant","reliable"],"ex":["The weather in spring is capricious: bright sunshine at noon and heavy rain by four.","Our manager is capricious, praising a plan one day and rejecting it the next.","The toddler's capricious moods meant he laughed one minute and screamed the next."],"b":603,"y":3},{"w":"captivate","p":"verb","d":"To attract and hold someone's attention completely because you are so interesting or charming.","lb":"charm, fascinate","s":["charm","enchant","fascinate","bewitch","delight","entrance"],"k":["absorb","attract","beguile","catch"],"a":["bore","repel","disgust","repulse"],"ex":["The street magician captivated the crowd with a trick that no one could explain.","Her voice captivated the audience from the very first note.","The documentary about the Sundarbans captivated my little brother, and he talked about tigers for days."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"carcinogenic","p":"adjective","d":"Able to cause cancer.","lb":"cancer-causing","s":["toxic","poisonous","harmful"],"k":["damaging","dangerous","deadly","deleterious"],"a":["safe","harmless"],"ex":["Scientists have shown that tobacco smoke contains many carcinogenic chemicals.","Some chemicals in cheap hair dyes may be carcinogenic.","The food agency warned that burnt food may contain carcinogenic substances."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cardinal","p":"adjective","d":"Of the greatest importance; basic and essential.","lb":"chief, fundamental","s":["chief","main","primary","key","fundamental","principal"],"k":["essential","important","leading","major"],"a":["minor","secondary","unimportant","trivial"],"ex":["The cardinal rule of the lab is to wear goggles whenever you handle chemicals.","Honesty is the cardinal virtue in any friendship.","Arriving late to a job interview is a cardinal mistake that is hard to undo."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"careen","p":"verb","d":"To move fast and out of control, swerving from side to side.","lb":"swerve, lurch","s":["swerve","veer","lurch","skid","career","reel"],"k":["cut","keel","sheer","shift"],"a":[],"ex":["The bus careened around the corner and nearly hit a rickshaw.","The shopping cart careened down the slope of the parking lot.","A truck careened across the icy road and stopped against a fence."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"caricature","p":"noun","d":"A picture or description that exaggerates a person's features or behavior to make them look funny or foolish.","lb":"cartoon, parody","s":["cartoon","parody","satire","lampoon","burlesque","spoof"],"k":["grotesque","humor","imitation","impersonation"],"a":["portrait","likeness","accurate depiction","realistic portrayal"],"ex":["The newspaper cartoonist drew a caricature of a local shopkeeper with a huge nose and tiny eyes.","At the fair, an artist drew a funny caricature of me with enormous ears.","The actor's imitation of a strict teacher was a caricature, but it made everyone laugh."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"carriage","p":"noun","d":"One of the separate sections of a train where passengers sit or travel.","lb":"train coach","s":["coach","car","compartment","wagon","bogie","rail coach"],"k":["baby buggy","baby carriage","bearing","berth"],"a":[],"ex":["I found a window seat in the third carriage and put my bag on the rack.","The front carriage was so crowded that we moved to the next one.","The guard walked down the train, checking tickets in every carriage."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"carte blanche","p":"noun","d":"Complete freedom to do whatever you think is best, given by someone in authority.","lb":"free hand, freedom","s":["free hand","free rein","freedom","license","authority","blank check"],"k":["a free pass","an open mandate","authorization","dominance"],"a":["restriction","limitation","restraint","control"],"ex":["The manager gave the design team carte blanche to redesign the whole website.","My parents gave me carte blanche to decorate my room however I liked.","The director had carte blanche in choosing the actors, because the producers trusted him."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cartography","p":"noun","d":"The art or science of drawing and making maps.","lb":"mapmaking, charting","s":["mapmaking","mapping","charting"],"k":["devising","draftsmanship","geodesy","geography"],"a":[],"ex":["Modern cartography uses satellite images to make maps that are accurate to a few meters.","She studies geography and hopes to work in cartography after graduation.","Early cartography was difficult because sailors had only simple tools to measure distances."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"cascade","p":"noun","d":"A waterfall, especially one of several small ones, or anything that pours down in a similar way.","lb":"waterfall, torrent","s":["waterfall","falls","torrent","flood","deluge","shower"],"k":["chute","downpour","rapids","spate"],"a":[],"ex":["We hiked for an hour to see the cascade hidden in the hills of Sylhet.","A cascade of dark hair fell over her shoulders when she took off her cap.","A cascade of notifications flooded my phone as soon as I switched it on."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"castigate","p":"verb","d":"To criticize someone very severely, often in public.","lb":"criticize, rebuke","s":["criticize","rebuke","reprimand","scold","censure","berate"],"k":["admonish","bawl out","call down","call on the carpet"],"a":["praise","commend","applaud","compliment"],"ex":["The principal castigated the students for leaving rubbish all over the playground.","Newspapers castigated the company for ignoring complaints about its unsafe buses.","Our coach castigated the defenders for their careless mistakes."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"castigation","p":"noun","d":"Severe criticism or punishment, especially in words.","lb":"criticism, rebuke","s":["rebuke","reprimand","censure","scolding","criticism","chastisement"],"k":["bawling out","chewing out","diatribe","disapproval"],"a":["praise","commendation","applause","approval"],"ex":["The player faced public castigation from fans after missing an easy goal.","The newspaper's castigation of the builders for ignoring safety rules was harsh but fair.","He accepted his mother's castigation quietly because he knew he was in the wrong."],"b":65,"y":1},{"w":"cataclysm","p":"noun","d":"A sudden, violent event that causes great damage or brings about a major change.","lb":"catastrophe, upheaval","s":["catastrophe","disaster","calamity","upheaval","devastation","convulsion"],"k":["apocalypse","armageddon","bad luck","doom"],"a":[],"ex":["The earthquake was a cataclysm that destroyed many homes in a few seconds.","Scientists believe a cosmic cataclysm wiped out the dinosaurs millions of years ago.","The financial crash was a cataclysm for thousands of small businesses."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"catalyst","p":"noun","d":"A person, event or substance that causes a change or makes something happen faster.","lb":"trigger, spark","s":["trigger","spark","stimulus","impetus","motivator","driver"],"k":["accelerator","activator","enzyme","fillip"],"a":["inhibitor","deterrent","obstacle"],"ex":["In the laboratory, a small amount of the catalyst made the reaction run much faster.","The rise in rice prices acted as a catalyst for the family's decision to grow vegetables on their roof.","Social media can act as a catalyst, turning a small local story into national news."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"categorical","p":"adjective","d":"Absolutely clear and certain, with no doubts, exceptions or conditions.","lb":"absolute, unconditional","s":["absolute","unconditional","unqualified","explicit","definite","unequivocal"],"k":["clear","clear-cut","firm","peremptory"],"a":["qualified","conditional","tentative","vague"],"ex":["The company gave a categorical denial of the rumors about unpaid salaries.","My father's answer was categorical: I could not travel alone at night.","The doctor was categorical that antibiotics do not work against viral colds."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"catharsis","p":"noun","d":"The release of strong, long-held emotions, often through art, talking or crying, that leaves a person feeling relieved.","lb":"emotional release, relief","s":["release","emotional release","relief","purging","cleansing","venting"],"k":["decompression","discharge","exorcism","letting off steam"],"a":["repression","suppression","bottling up"],"ex":["Writing a long letter to her late grandfather was a catharsis for Nadia.","After the final exam, shouting and laughing with friends on the field felt like pure catharsis.","Many viewers found the tragic film a catharsis, because it let them cry about their own losses."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"catholic","p":"adjective","d":"Wide-ranging and including many different things; open to a variety of interests or views.","lb":"broad, wide-ranging","s":["broad","universal","eclectic","liberal","comprehensive","diverse"],"k":["encyclopedic","expansive","extensive","general"],"a":["narrow","limited","restricted","parochial"],"ex":["My uncle has catholic tastes in music, from old Bangla folk songs to jazz.","The library's catholic collection includes comic books, science journals and cookbooks.","She is catholic in her reading, finishing a novel one day and a physics book the next."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"caustic","p":"adjective","d":"Able to burn or eat away at things chemically, or very bitter and sarcastic in speech.","lb":"corrosive, biting","s":["corrosive","acidic","biting","sarcastic","cutting","scathing"],"k":["acrid","barbed","blistering","destructive"],"a":["mild","gentle","kind","soothing"],"ex":["Caustic soda can burn your skin, so wear gloves when you clean the drain.","The critic's caustic review called the film dull, pointless and far too long.","Her caustic reply made everyone in the meeting fall silent."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"cavalier","p":"adjective","d":"Showing a careless or arrogant lack of concern about something serious.","lb":"careless, dismissive","s":["careless","offhand","dismissive","arrogant","flippant","haughty"],"k":["domineering","imperious","informal","nonchalant"],"a":["careful","concerned","serious","respectful"],"ex":["His cavalier attitude to deadlines cost the team an important client.","The doctor was cavalier about the patient’s fears and rushed through the appointment.","She gave a cavalier wave and left without a word of thanks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cavil","p":"verb","d":"To make petty, unnecessary objections or complaints about something that is not really important.","lb":"quibble, carp","s":["quibble","carp","nitpick","complain","find fault","object"],"k":["bicker","fuss","gripe","haggle"],"a":["praise","accept","approve","applaud"],"ex":["Critics cavilled about the colour of the logo and ignored the strength of the main idea.","It is pointless to cavil over tiny errors when the report is excellent overall.","He cavilled at every suggestion his colleagues made, until nobody wanted to work with him."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"celerity","p":"noun","d":"Quickness of movement or action; speed.","lb":"speed, swiftness","s":["speed","swiftness","rapidity","haste","quickness","velocity"],"k":["agility","briskness","expedition","momentum"],"a":["slowness","delay","tardiness","lethargy"],"ex":["The firefighters arrived with celerity and put out the fire before it spread.","She answered every email with celerity, which impressed her manager.","The waiter moved with surprising celerity between the crowded tables."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"celibacy","p":"noun","d":"The state of choosing not to marry or have sexual relations, usually for religious reasons.","lb":"chastity, abstinence","s":["chastity","abstinence","purity"],"k":["austerity","monasticism","renunciation","self-restraint"],"a":["promiscuity","licentiousness","indulgence"],"ex":["Monks in many traditions take a vow of celibacy when they join a monastery.","The documentary explained why some religious orders require celibacy from their members.","He chose celibacy and devoted his whole life to teaching poor children."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"censure","p":"noun","d":"Strong public disapproval, or an official statement that criticizes someone for their behavior.","lb":"disapproval, reprimand","s":["disapproval","condemnation","criticism","reprimand","rebuke","reproach"],"k":["denunciation","disapprobation","exclusion","excommunication"],"a":["praise","approval","commendation","applause"],"ex":["The committee issued a formal censure against the club treasurer for misusing funds.","He faced public censure after posting insulting comments about the team.","The doctor's careless mistake brought censure from the medical board."],"b":82,"y":3},{"w":"cerebral","p":"adjective","d":"Involving or appealing to careful thinking rather than emotion; also, relating to the brain.","lb":"intellectual, thoughtful","s":["intellectual","brainy","thoughtful","academic","highbrow","scholarly"],"k":["abstract","contemplative","esoteric","heady"],"a":["emotional","instinctive","passionate"],"ex":["Chess is a cerebral game that rewards patience and careful planning.","He is a cerebral writer whose novels make readers think more than they feel.","The film was too cerebral for me; I wanted action, not long conversations about ideas."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chaff","p":"noun","d":"The dry outer husks of grain that are separated and thrown away, or anything worthless.","lb":"husks, rubbish","s":["husks","hulls","rubbish","waste","trash","refuse"],"k":["bran","debris","detritus","dregs"],"a":["grain","wheat","kernel"],"ex":["Farmers throw the grain into the air so that the wind can blow the chaff away.","To find good information online, you must learn to separate the wheat from the chaff.","My uncle feeds his cattle a mixture of straw and chaff during the dry season."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"chagrin","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of annoyance or embarrassment caused by failure or disappointment.","lb":"embarrassment, annoyance","s":["embarrassment","annoyance","vexation","mortification","humiliation","dismay"],"k":["botheration","chafe","crossness","discomfort"],"a":["delight","satisfaction","pleasure","pride"],"ex":["To her chagrin, she realized she had left her wallet at home after ordering a big meal.","Much to Rafi's chagrin, his younger cousin beat him at chess again.","He read the email with chagrin, seeing that he had missed a simple spelling mistake."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chameleon","p":"noun","d":"A person who often changes their opinions or behavior to suit the people around them.","lb":"shape-shifter, opportunist","s":["opportunist","trimmer"],"k":["bandwagon jumper","fair-weather friend","hypocrite","individual"],"a":[],"ex":["He is a social chameleon who acts serious with teachers and silly with friends.","A good actor must be a chameleon, changing voice and manner for every role.","At work she was a chameleon, agreeing with whoever had spoken last."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"champion","p":"verb","d":"To support or defend a person, idea or cause publicly and strongly.","lb":"defend, support","s":["defend","support","back","advocate","promote","uphold"],"k":["approve","assist","campaign for","crusade for"],"a":["oppose","attack","undermine","abandon"],"ex":["Our school librarian has always championed free reading for every student.","She championed the idea of a recycling program until the council approved it.","The charity champions the right of every child to attend school."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"channel","p":"verb","d":"To direct something, such as energy, money or water, toward a particular purpose or place.","lb":"direct, funnel","s":["direct","guide","funnel","steer","divert","focus"],"k":["allocate","conduct","feed","harness"],"a":["scatter","waste","squander","disperse"],"ex":["She channeled her nervous energy into cleaning the whole house before the guests arrived.","Farmers channel river water into the fields through small canals.","The charity channels donations directly to flood victims instead of spending on advertising."],"b":416,"y":0},{"w":"charisma","p":"noun","d":"A special personal quality that makes other people admire you and want to follow you.","lb":"charm, appeal","s":["charm","magnetism","appeal","allure","presence","personality"],"k":["aura","dazzle","glamor","interest"],"a":[],"ex":["The new class captain has so much charisma that even shy students follow her ideas.","A good salesperson needs more than product knowledge; a little charisma helps customers trust you.","He is not the best singer, but his charisma on stage keeps the audience clapping."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"charlatan","p":"noun","d":"A person who pretends to have special skills or knowledge, usually to cheat people out of money.","lb":"fraud, quack","s":["fraud","quack","impostor","fake","swindler","cheat"],"k":["cheater","counterfeit","deceiver","faker"],"a":["expert","professional","authority","specialist"],"ex":["The so-called healer was a charlatan who sold colored water as a cure for every illness.","Do not trust any charlatan who promises that you will pass the exam without studying.","The investment adviser turned out to be a charlatan who vanished with his clients' savings."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chasm","p":"noun","d":"A very deep, wide gap in the ground; also, a serious gap between two groups or ideas.","lb":"gorge, gap","s":["gorge","abyss","canyon","ravine","gulf","crevasse"],"k":["breach","cleft","crack","crevice"],"a":[],"ex":["After the earthquake, a wide chasm opened across the road, and cars could not pass.","The hikers crossed the deep chasm on a narrow wooden bridge.","Rocks tumbled into the dark chasm, and we never heard them hit the bottom."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chaste","p":"adjective","d":"Simple and plain in style, or morally pure and avoiding sexual activity.","lb":"pure, plain","s":["pure","simple","plain","unadorned","modest","austere"],"k":["celibate","clear","moral","straightforward"],"a":["ornate","lewd","indecent","immodest"],"ex":["The room had a chaste white design, with no pictures and almost no furniture.","The poet praised the chaste beauty of the snow-covered hills.","The couple exchanged a chaste kiss on the cheek at the railway station."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"chastise","p":"verb","d":"To scold or criticize someone severely for doing something wrong.","lb":"scold, rebuke","s":["scold","rebuke","reprimand","castigate","berate","upbraid"],"k":["bawl out","call down","call on the carpet","chew out"],"a":["praise","commend","compliment","applaud"],"ex":["The coach chastised the team for giving up easily after the first goal.","My mother chastised me for coming home two hours after the agreed time.","The editor chastised the reporter for publishing the story without checking the facts."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cheerful","p":"adjective","d":"Happy and in good spirits, and showing it in the way you look or behave.","lb":"happy, upbeat","s":["happy","merry","jolly","bright","sunny","upbeat"],"k":["beaming","beamish","blithe","buoyant"],"a":["gloomy","sad","miserable","glum"],"ex":["The cheerful shopkeeper greeted every customer with a smile and a joke.","Despite the rain, the children stayed cheerful and played in the puddles.","She painted the kitchen a cheerful yellow to brighten the room."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"cherub","p":"noun","d":"A sweet, chubby-cheeked baby or small child, or a child-like winged angel in paintings.","lb":"angelic child, angel","s":["angel","darling","sweetheart","little angel","babe","innocent"],"k":["baby","cupid","infant","moppet"],"a":[],"ex":["My baby cousin is a chubby little cherub with rosy cheeks and a gummy smile.","The ceiling of the old church was painted with golden cherubs holding tiny trumpets.","In the school play, the smallest child, dressed as a cherub with cardboard wings, stole the show."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"chicanery","p":"noun","d":"The use of clever tricks and dishonest arguments to deceive people or to get what you want.","lb":"trickery, deception","s":["trickery","deception","fraud","deceit","subterfuge","sophistry"],"k":["dissembling","guile","misrepresentation","shenanigan"],"a":["honesty","candor","integrity","sincerity"],"ex":["Accusations of chicanery followed the contest when it emerged that the judges knew the winner in advance.","The salesman resorted to chicanery, hiding the extra fees in tiny print.","The online seller's chicanery came to light when customers received empty boxes."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"chimera","p":"noun","d":"An unrealistic hope or idea that is impossible to achieve; an illusion.","lb":"illusion, fantasy","s":["illusion","fantasy","delusion","pipe dream","fancy","mirage"],"k":["castle in the air","daydream","fallacy","fool's paradise"],"a":["reality","fact","truth","certainty"],"ex":["For many jobless graduates, a stable salary remains a chimera that they keep chasing.","The inventor's dream of a perpetual motion machine turned out to be a chimera.","Perfect health through a single pill is a chimera sold by clever advertisers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"choleric","p":"adjective","d":"Easily made angry and often showing bad temper.","lb":"hot-tempered, irritable","s":["irritable","irascible","cranky","testy","touchy","bad-tempered"],"k":["angry","crabby","fractious","grumpy"],"a":["calm","placid","easygoing","mild"],"ex":["The choleric old professor shouted at anyone who arrived even a minute late.","My choleric uncle turns red whenever someone disagrees with him about the price of vegetables.","The coach was choleric after the defeat and threw his cap on the ground."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chortle","p":"verb","d":"To laugh in a happy, quiet way, as if pleased or amused.","lb":"chuckle, laugh","s":["chuckle","giggle","laugh","snicker","cackle","crow"],"k":["belly-laugh","crack up","express joy","guffaw"],"a":["weep","cry","sob","wail"],"ex":["My grandfather chortled at the cartoons in the Sunday newspaper.","The children chortled with delight when the puppy chased its own tail.","She chortled to herself as she read her friend's funny message."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"chronic","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting for a long time or constantly returning, especially of an illness or a problem.","lb":"long-lasting, persistent","s":["persistent","lingering","recurring","constant","habitual","ongoing"],"k":["continuing","degenerative","endless","inveterate"],"a":["acute","temporary","passing","occasional"],"ex":["My grandfather has chronic back pain, so he takes a short walk every morning.","The city suffers from a chronic shortage of clean drinking water during the dry season.","Chronic traffic jams on this road waste hours of every commuter's day."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"chronicle","p":"noun","d":"A detailed written record of events in the order in which they happened.","lb":"record, account","s":["record","account","history","annals","narrative","log"],"k":["almanac","file","journal","ledger"],"a":[],"ex":["The book is a chronicle of the town's growth from a small market to a busy city.","She kept a daily chronicle of her travels in a notebook.","The old chronicle describes floods and famines that happened centuries ago."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"chronology","p":"noun","d":"The order in which events happened, or a list of events arranged in that order.","lb":"timeline, sequence","s":["sequence","order of events","time frame","record","history","annals"],"k":["chronicle","dating","narrative","order"],"a":[],"ex":["The police asked him to explain the chronology of events on the night of the robbery.","In history class, we drew a chronology of the major events of the twentieth century.","Her novel jumps around in time, so readers must work out the chronology themselves."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"churl","p":"noun","d":"A rude, bad-mannered person who treats others without respect.","lb":"boor, lout","s":["boor","lout","oaf","yob","philistine","barbarian"],"k":["brute","bumpkin","cad","clod"],"a":["gentleman","aristocrat","courtier"],"ex":["Only a churl would refuse to say thank you after a stranger had helped him.","The neighbour behaved like a churl, slamming the door in our faces when we offered sweets.","In the old tale, the rich churl refused to share his bread with the hungry traveller."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"chutzpah","p":"noun","d":"Shocking boldness or nerve, especially in doing something others would be too polite or afraid to do.","lb":"audacity, nerve","s":["audacity","nerve","gall","cheek","impudence","boldness"],"k":["bravado","courage","crust","daring"],"a":["timidity","modesty","shyness","humility"],"ex":["He had the chutzpah to ask the interviewer for a higher salary before getting the job offer.","It takes real chutzpah to return a meal after eating most of it.","The student's chutzpah impressed the professor when she politely challenged his answer."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cipher","p":"noun","d":"A secret way of writing in which letters or numbers replace others, so that only some people can read it.","lb":"code, secret writing","s":["code","secret code","coded message","encryption","secret writing"],"k":["cryptography","cypher","encoding","encrypted message"],"a":[],"ex":["The two friends wrote notes to each other in a cipher so nobody else could read them.","Experts spent years trying to crack the cipher used in the old letters.","In the puzzle game, you have to solve a cipher to open the final door."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"circuitous","p":"adjective","d":"Longer and less direct than necessary; not going straight to the point or place.","lb":"roundabout, indirect","s":["roundabout","indirect","winding","meandering","tortuous","devious"],"k":["circumlocutory","laborious","labyrinthine","serpentine"],"a":["direct","straight","straightforward","short"],"ex":["We took a circuitous route home to avoid the traffic jam near the market.","The river follows a circuitous path through the hills before reaching the plain.","His circuitous explanation took ten minutes, and I still did not understand what he wanted."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"circumlocution","p":"noun","d":"The use of many words to say something that could be said simply, especially to avoid a direct answer.","lb":"wordiness, evasion","s":["evasion","rambling","beating around the bush"],"k":["doublespeak","hedging","hot air","indirect expression"],"a":["directness","bluntness","brevity","plain speaking"],"ex":["Instead of saying no, he used a long circumlocution about being very busy this month.","The official's circumlocution made it impossible to find out whether the office would open.","I lost patience with his circumlocution and asked him to come to the point."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"circumnavigate","p":"verb","d":"To travel all the way around something, such as the world, an island or a lake.","lb":"sail around, go around","s":["sail around","travel around","go around","circle","orbit","round"],"k":["compass","cruise around","encompass","girdle"],"a":[],"ex":["Sailors first circumnavigated the globe in the sixteenth century, proving how large the world really was.","The cruise ship will circumnavigate the island in about three hours, with stops for photographs.","Rafi circumnavigated the lake on foot in under two hours."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"circumscribe","p":"verb","d":"To limit something strictly, such as someone's power, activities or freedom.","lb":"limit, restrict","s":["restrict","limit","confine","restrain","curb","constrain"],"k":["confine to","control","decrease","hold back"],"a":["expand","extend","widen","free"],"ex":["The new rules circumscribe what students may post on the school's social media pages.","Her illness circumscribed her daily activities, so she rarely left the house.","The contract tightly circumscribes the manager's authority to approve large expenses."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"circumspect","p":"adjective","d":"Careful to think about possible risks or consequences before saying or doing anything.","lb":"cautious, careful","s":["cautious","careful","wary","prudent","guarded","discreet"],"k":["alert","attentive","canny","deliberate"],"a":["reckless","rash","careless","imprudent"],"ex":["Be circumspect when sharing personal details online, because you never know who might see them.","The bank clerk was circumspect, checking every document twice before approving the loan.","Rafi gave a circumspect answer, careful not to promise anything he could not deliver."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"circumstance","p":"noun","d":"A fact or condition connected with an event or person that affects what happens or how it should be judged.","lb":"condition, situation","s":["condition","situation","factor","detail","state of affairs","context"],"k":["aspect","backdrop","background","consideration"],"a":[],"ex":["Under the circumstances, the school decided to postpone the sports day.","Her circumstances changed when her father lost his job.","In no circumstances should you share your bank PIN with anyone."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"circumvent","p":"verb","d":"To find a clever way around a rule, obstacle or problem instead of dealing with it directly.","lb":"bypass, evade","s":["bypass","evade","avoid","sidestep","dodge","get around"],"k":["beleaguer","besiege","duck","escape"],"a":["obey","confront","comply with","face"],"ex":["Drivers took the back lanes to circumvent the traffic jam on the main road.","Some companies try to circumvent safety rules to save money, which puts workers at risk.","To circumvent the high delivery fee, we ordered everything from a nearby shop and picked it up ourselves."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"citadel","p":"noun","d":"A strong fortress built on high ground to protect a city.","lb":"fortress, stronghold","s":["fortress","stronghold","fort","castle","bastion","fortification"],"k":["acropolis","alcazar","defense","garrison"],"a":[],"ex":["The ancient citadel stands on a hill above the city and has thick stone walls.","Tourists climbed the steps to the citadel to enjoy the view.","Her small office is a citadel of calm in an otherwise noisy building."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"civil","p":"adjective","d":"Polite and respectful in a basic way, even when you do not like the other person.","lb":"polite, courteous","s":["polite","courteous","respectful","cordial","gracious","decent"],"k":["affable","amiable","decorous","genteel"],"a":["rude","impolite","uncivil","discourteous"],"ex":["We disagreed strongly, but we stayed civil and shook hands at the end.","It costs nothing to be civil to the delivery rider, even when the food is late.","He gave a civil reply to the angry email instead of arguing."],"b":400,"y":0},{"w":"clandestine","p":"adjective","d":"Done or kept secret, especially because it is not allowed or would be disapproved of.","lb":"secret, covert","s":["secret","covert","hidden","furtive","undercover","underground"],"k":["backdoor","cloak-and-dagger","hush-hush","private"],"a":["open","public","overt","aboveboard"],"ex":["The friends planned a clandestine surprise party, hiding every sign from the birthday girl.","Police broke up a clandestine factory that was making fake medicines.","They kept a clandestine friendship because their families disagreed."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"classic","p":"adjective","d":"Of very high quality and lasting value, so that it is accepted as a standard or model.","lb":"excellent, timeless","s":["outstanding","timeless","exemplary","definitive","enduring","superior"],"k":["canonical","consummate","excellent","iconic"],"a":["inferior","mediocre","ordinary","forgettable"],"ex":["Her essay was a classic example of clear and persuasive writing.","We watched a classic film from the sixties, and it still felt fresh.","The classic design of the old wristwatch never goes out of style."],"b":416,"y":0},{"w":"cleave","p":"verb","d":"To split or cut something apart with force; also, to stick or hold firmly to a person, belief or place.","lb":"split, cling","s":["split","cut","divide","sever","chop","hew"],"k":["bind","break up","carve","divvy up"],"a":["join","unite","weld","abandon"],"ex":["The butcher cleaved the whole fish in two with one strong blow of his knife.","Lightning cleaved the old tree in two, and half of it fell across the road.","The boat cleaved through the waves, leaving a long white trail behind it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"clemency","p":"noun","d":"Mercy or leniency shown to someone who is being punished or could be punished.","lb":"mercy, leniency","s":["mercy","leniency","forgiveness","compassion","mildness","pity"],"k":["amnesty","commutation","indulgence","pardon"],"a":["severity","harshness","cruelty","ruthlessness"],"ex":["The young driver pleaded for clemency, promising never to break the speed limit again.","The judge showed clemency to the first-time offender and ordered community service instead of prison.","After his heartfelt apology, the teacher showed clemency and let him retake the test."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"clement","p":"adjective","d":"Mild and pleasant, used about weather that is neither too hot nor too cold nor stormy.","lb":"mild, pleasant","s":["mild","gentle","temperate","balmy","fair","pleasant"],"k":["bright","delicate","genial","halcyon"],"a":["harsh","severe","inclement","stormy"],"ex":["The festival was held outdoors because the weather was clement all week.","In clement weather, we eat breakfast on the roof.","Flights resumed once clement conditions returned to the coast."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"climatic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the climate, meaning the usual weather conditions of an area.","lb":"weather-related, environmental","s":["meteorological","atmospheric","environmental","seasonal"],"k":["barometric","geographical","hygrometric","regional"],"a":[],"ex":["Tea grows well in Sylhet because of the region’s warm, wet climatic conditions.","Climatic changes are making monsoon rains less predictable for farmers.","The study compared different climatic zones, from the cold north to the humid south."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"climax","p":"noun","d":"The most exciting or important point in a story, event or series of events.","lb":"peak, culmination","s":["peak","high point","culmination","height","zenith","pinnacle"],"k":["acme","apogee","coming","crest"],"a":["anticlimax","low point","beginning","start"],"ex":["The film reaches its climax when the hero finally meets the thief on the rooftop.","The climax of the cricket match came in the last over, when six runs were needed.","The speech built slowly to a climax, and the audience stood up and clapped."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"clique","p":"noun","d":"A small group of people who spend time together and do not easily accept other people.","lb":"exclusive group, circle","s":["circle","coterie","set","gang","crowd","clan"],"k":["band","cabal","camp","coven"],"a":[],"ex":["At lunch, the same clique of girls sat together and ignored the newcomer.","A tight clique of senior engineers makes most decisions without asking the rest of the team.","He left the club because he felt it was run by a small clique."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cloister","p":"noun","d":"A covered walkway with arches or columns, usually around a courtyard in a monastery or college.","lb":"arcade, walkway","s":["arcade","covered walk","walkway","gallery","religious residence"],"k":["atrium","loggia","peristyle","portico"],"a":[],"ex":["Tourists walked slowly around the cloister, admiring the carved stone columns.","The students sheltered from the rain under the cloister of the old college.","A quiet garden lies at the centre of the cloister, surrounded by arches on all four sides."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"clone","p":"noun","d":"An exact copy of a living thing made from its cells, or a person or thing that looks very similar to another.","lb":"duplicate, replica","s":["duplicate","copy","replica","twin","carbon copy","double"],"k":["dead ringer","doppelganger","image","knockoff"],"a":["original","prototype"],"ex":["Scientists created a clone of a sheep from a single cell.","The cheap phone is a clone of a famous model and looks almost identical.","Plants grown from cuttings are clones of the parent plant."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"clout","p":"noun","d":"Power or influence over others, especially in business or politics.","lb":"influence, power","s":["influence","power","sway","weight","leverage","pull"],"k":["advantage","command","lick","poke"],"a":["powerlessness","weakness","insignificance"],"ex":["A respected head teacher has enough clout to get the city to fix the road.","Big supermarkets have more clout with suppliers than small shops do.","She has little clout in the committee because she is the newest member."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"cloy","p":"verb","d":"To become unpleasant or tiresome because it is too sweet, rich or sentimental.","lb":"sicken, satiate","s":["sicken","satiate","surfeit","glut","pall","weary"],"k":["bore","churn up","deaden","fill"],"a":["whet","refresh","stimulate","tempt"],"ex":["The dessert was so rich that it quickly began to cloy.","After three pieces of sweet rasgulla, the taste began to cloy.","The perfume's heavy scent cloyed after a few minutes in the small room."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"clunky","p":"adjective","d":"Heavy, awkward or not smooth in design, movement or use.","lb":"awkward, heavy","s":["clumsy","awkward","heavy","cumbersome","bulky","unwieldy"],"k":["audible","chunky","gawky","janky"],"a":["sleek","smooth","graceful","elegant"],"ex":["The old software was so clunky that simple tasks took ages.","He wore clunky boots that made loud noises on the wooden floor.","The translation sounded clunky, with long and awkward sentences."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"coagulate","p":"verb","d":"To change from a liquid into a thick, solid or semi-solid state, as blood does.","lb":"clot, thicken","s":["clot","congeal","thicken","curdle","solidify","set"],"k":["change state","clabber","cohere","crust"],"a":["dissolve","liquefy","melt","thin"],"ex":["When you cut your finger, blood coagulates and slowly forms a seal over the wound.","Adding lemon juice to hot milk makes the protein coagulate into soft white lumps.","Cold weather can cause cooking oil to coagulate in the pipes under the sink."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"coalesce","p":"verb","d":"To come together and join into one group, mass or whole.","lb":"merge, unite","s":["merge","unite","combine","fuse","blend","join"],"k":["change integrity","cohere","consolidate","flux"],"a":["separate","divide","disperse","split"],"ex":["Small streams coalesce into a wide river before reaching the sea.","Several local groups coalesced into one large association to fight for cleaner water.","After weeks of rough notes, her ideas finally coalesced into a clear plan."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"coda","p":"noun","d":"The final part of a piece of music, or a closing section that rounds off a story or event.","lb":"ending, finale","s":["ending","finale","conclusion","epilogue","close","finish"],"k":["addendum","appendix","closing","end"],"a":["introduction","prelude","opening","preface"],"ex":["The symphony ended with a gentle coda that slowly faded into silence.","The film's short coda showed the characters ten years later.","As a coda to the school year, the principal hosted a small tea party for the graduating class."],"b":13,"y":0},{"w":"coddle","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone too gently, protecting them too much from difficulty or hard work.","lb":"pamper, overprotect","s":["pamper","spoil","indulge","baby","cosset","pet"],"k":["cocker","do by","dote on","featherbed"],"a":["neglect","discipline","toughen","mistreat"],"ex":["Some parents coddle their children so much that the kids never learn to solve problems.","The coach refused to coddle the players, saying hard practice makes strong teams.","She was coddled by her grandparents and never had to wash a single dish."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"coerce","p":"verb","d":"To force someone to do something by using threats or pressure.","lb":"force, pressure","s":["force","compel","pressure","bully","pressurize","intimidate"],"k":["blackmail","dragoon","extort","hale"],"a":["persuade","allow","permit","let"],"ex":["No one should be coerced into signing a contract they have not read.","The gang tried to coerce shopkeepers into paying them money every week.","He claimed that his boss coerced him into working late every night without extra pay."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"cogent","p":"adjective","d":"Clearly and logically presented, so that people are persuaded by it.","lb":"convincing, persuasive","s":["convincing","persuasive","compelling","forceful","sound","logical"],"k":["airtight","coherent","lucid","reasoned"],"a":["unconvincing","weak","illogical","feeble"],"ex":["She made a cogent argument for starting school an hour later, citing research on teenage sleep.","The lawyer's cogent closing speech convinced the judge to reduce the fine.","He gave three cogent reasons for choosing a smaller, cheaper flat."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"cogitate","p":"verb","d":"To think deeply and carefully about something.","lb":"ponder, reflect","s":["ponder","think","reflect","meditate","deliberate","contemplate"],"k":["chew over","concoct","dream up","hatch"],"a":[],"ex":["He sat by the window to cogitate on which university to choose.","I need time to cogitate about the offer before I answer.","Nadia cogitated over the math problem for an hour before finding the trick."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cognition","p":"noun","d":"The mental process of gaining knowledge and understanding through thinking, experience and the senses.","lb":"thinking, understanding","s":["thinking","perception","reasoning","understanding","awareness","comprehension"],"k":["apprehension","cognizance","insight","intellection"],"a":[],"ex":["Lack of sleep can harm memory and other areas of cognition in teenagers.","Researchers study how play helps cognition develop in young children.","Regular exercise may slow the decline of cognition in older adults."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"cognitive","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to mental processes such as thinking, learning, remembering and understanding.","lb":"mental, intellectual","s":["mental","intellectual","rational","psychological","perceptual","cerebral"],"k":["brain-based","conceptual","epistemic","neural"],"a":[],"ex":["Reading to young children helps their cognitive development.","Lack of sleep can slow your cognitive ability, making it harder to solve problems.","The test measures cognitive skills such as memory, attention and logic."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cognizant","p":"adjective","d":"Aware of something and understanding its importance.","lb":"aware, conscious","s":["aware","conscious","mindful","informed","knowledgeable","alert"],"k":["alive","awake","careful","evocative"],"a":["unaware","ignorant","oblivious","heedless"],"ex":["Drivers must be cognizant of the risks of speeding in wet weather.","She was fully cognizant of the deadline, yet she still waited until the last day.","The manager is cognizant of the staff's complaints and promises to act."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"coherent","p":"adjective","d":"Logical and well organized, so that the parts fit together and are easy to understand.","lb":"logical, clear","s":["logical","clear","consistent","rational","lucid","articulate"],"k":["adhesive","ordered","plain","reasonable"],"a":["incoherent","confused","muddled","disjointed"],"ex":["Her essay was coherent from start to finish, with each paragraph leading naturally to the next.","After the accident, the injured driver was awake but could not give a coherent account of what happened.","The team needs a coherent plan, not ten different ideas that do not fit together."],"b":208,"y":1},{"w":"cohort","p":"noun","d":"A group of people who share a common feature, such as age, or who go through something together.","lb":"group, batch","s":["group","band","set","class","batch","generation"],"k":["age bracket","bloc","cadre","circle"],"a":[],"ex":["Our cohort of first-year students shares one big lecture hall and a single study group.","Researchers followed a cohort of five thousand children for twenty years.","She and the rest of her cohort graduated together and started work in the same month."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"collaboration","p":"noun","d":"The act of working together with other people to produce or achieve something.","lb":"teamwork","s":["cooperation","teamwork","partnership","alliance","joint effort","coordination"],"k":["affiliation","association","co-production","coalition"],"a":["competition","rivalry","opposition","conflict"],"ex":["The book is the result of close collaboration between a scientist and an artist.","Students completed the project in collaboration with a local NGO.","Good collaboration between doctors and nurses saves lives."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"collapse","p":"verb","d":"To fall down or break apart suddenly, or to fail completely.","lb":"fall down, fail","s":["cave in","crumble","give way","fall down","break down","fail"],"k":["abandon","break","break up","burst"],"a":["hold up","withstand","endure","thrive"],"ex":["The old brick wall collapsed during the heavy monsoon rain last night.","His business collapsed when his biggest customer stopped paying.","After running the marathon, the exhausted runner collapsed at the finish line."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"colloquial","p":"adjective","d":"Used in everyday speech and informal writing, rather than in formal or serious writing.","lb":"informal, conversational","s":["informal","conversational","casual","everyday","familiar","idiomatic"],"k":["demotic","dialectal","homespun","plain"],"a":["formal","literary","academic","stilted"],"ex":["In colloquial English, people often say \"gonna\" instead of \"going to\".","The writer's colloquial style makes the long article feel like a friendly conversation.","Colloquial Bangla in Dhaka differs from the Bangla spoken in Sylhet."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"collusion","p":"noun","d":"A secret agreement between people to act together in a dishonest or illegal way.","lb":"conspiracy, secret deal","s":["conspiracy","complicity","secret deal","plotting","intrigue","conniving"],"k":["agreement","backroom deal","bid-rigging","cabal"],"a":[],"ex":["The authorities suspect collusion between the sellers, who all raised their prices on the same day.","Two students were caught in collusion during the test, passing answers on tiny notes.","The inspector was fired for collusion with the factory owner, who bribed him to ignore safety rules."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"commemorate","p":"verb","d":"To remember and show respect for a person or event by holding a ceremony or making a memorial.","lb":"honour, remember","s":["honour","remember","celebrate","memorialize","mark","observe"],"k":["consecrate","enshrine","eulogize","immortalize"],"a":["forget","ignore","neglect","overlook"],"ex":["On 21 February, people lay flowers at the Shaheed Minar to commemorate those who gave their lives for the Bangla language.","The school planted a tree to commemorate its fiftieth anniversary.","A stamp was issued to commemorate the hundredth birthday of the famous poet."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"commence","p":"verb","d":"To begin, or to start something, especially in a formal way.","lb":"begin, start","s":["begin","start","open","launch","initiate","embark on"],"k":["get","get down","inaugurate","instigate"],"a":["end","finish","conclude","cease"],"ex":["The examination will commence at ten o'clock sharp, so please take your seats.","Construction of the new bridge is due to commence next month.","The ceremony commenced with a short speech by the principal."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"commend","p":"verb","d":"To praise someone or something formally for being good or well done.","lb":"praise, recommend","s":["praise","applaud","compliment","acclaim","congratulate","laud"],"k":["approve","celebrate","cheer","endorse"],"a":["criticize","condemn","censure","blame"],"ex":["The principal commended the students for their excellent results.","I commend you on your honesty in admitting the mistake.","Her manager commended her for finishing the project ahead of time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"commensurate","p":"adjective","d":"Matching something else in size, level or importance; in proper proportion to it.","lb":"proportionate, equal","s":["proportionate","proportional","equivalent","corresponding","equal","consistent"],"k":["analogous","congruent","in keeping with","matched"],"a":["disproportionate","unequal","inadequate","mismatched"],"ex":["The company offers a salary commensurate with experience and qualifications.","The fine was not commensurate with the damage the factory caused to the river.","Her success was commensurate with the hours of practice she had put in."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"commiserate","p":"verb","d":"To show sympathy to someone who is sad or has had bad luck.","lb":"sympathize, console","s":["sympathize","console","empathize","comfort","feel for","offer condolences"],"k":["compassionate","express regret","feel sorry for","grieve with"],"a":["gloat","congratulate","rejoice"],"ex":["Her friends came to commiserate with her after she failed the driving test.","We commiserated over cups of tea about the long wait at the passport office.","Fans commiserated online after the team lost in the last minute."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"commodious","p":"adjective","d":"Having plenty of space inside; roomy and comfortable.","lb":"spacious, roomy","s":["spacious","roomy","capacious","ample","large","generous"],"k":["airy","big","broad","convenient"],"a":["cramped","small","tiny","narrow"],"ex":["We stayed in a commodious apartment with three bedrooms and a large balcony.","The commodious back seat of the car was perfect for our long journey.","Their commodious kitchen could hold the whole family during Eid cooking."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"commotion","p":"noun","d":"A sudden noisy and confused situation, with a lot of excitement or activity.","lb":"uproar, disturbance","s":["uproar","disturbance","fuss","racket","tumult","hubbub"],"k":["bedlam","brawl","clamour","din"],"a":["calm","peace","quiet","order"],"ex":["A sudden commotion in the corridor made the whole class look at the door.","The arrival of the cricket team caused a commotion at the airport.","There was a commotion at the market when a cow ran loose between the stalls."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"compatible","p":"adjective","d":"Able to work, exist or be used together without problems or conflict.","lb":"suited, harmonious","s":["harmonious","consistent","adaptable","interchangeable","matching","congenial"],"k":["consonant","fitting","harmonic","interoperable"],"a":["incompatible","unsuited","conflicting","clashing"],"ex":["This charger is compatible with most mobile phones.","The two roommates have such compatible personalities that they almost never argue.","Make sure the new software is compatible with your old computer."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"compel","p":"verb","d":"To force someone to do something, or to make an action necessary through pressure, rules or circumstances.","lb":"force, oblige","s":["force","oblige","make","coerce","pressure","constrain"],"k":["bind","cause","entail","get"],"a":["deter","dissuade","discourage","prevent"],"ex":["Heavy rain compelled us to cancel the picnic at the last minute.","The law compels all drivers to carry a valid licence.","Rising rent compelled the family to move to a smaller flat."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"compelling","p":"adjective","d":"Very strong and convincing, so that people are persuaded or feel they must act.","lb":"convincing, powerful","s":["convincing","persuasive","powerful","forceful","gripping","riveting"],"k":["absorbing","captivating","engrossing","interesting"],"a":["unconvincing","weak","feeble","dull"],"ex":["She gave a compelling argument, and the committee agreed to give her more time.","There is a compelling reason to leave early: the road to the airport floods in the rain.","The documentary tells such a compelling story that nobody in the room spoke until it ended."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"compendium","p":"noun","d":"A short but complete collection of information about a subject, or a collection of many items.","lb":"summary, collection","s":["digest","summary","anthology","collection","compilation","handbook"],"k":["catalog","encyclopedia","omnibus","publication"],"a":[],"ex":["This compendium of grammar rules fits in a pocket and is perfect for quick revision.","The website is a compendium of recipes from every district of Bangladesh.","She bought a compendium of short stories to read on the long train journey."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"compensation","p":"noun","d":"Money or something else given to make up for a loss, injury or inconvenience.","lb":"payment, reparation","s":["payment","reimbursement","damages","redress","reparation","restitution"],"k":["allowance","bonus","consideration","indemnification"],"a":[],"ex":["The airline paid the passengers compensation for the ten-hour delay.","The factory owner promised compensation to the families of the injured workers.","She received compensation after the shop sold her a faulty fridge."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"competence","p":"noun","d":"The ability to do something well or to the level that is needed.","lb":"ability, skill","s":["ability","skill","proficiency","capability","expertise","capacity"],"k":["gift","knack","power","talent"],"a":["incompetence","inability","ineptitude","inefficiency"],"ex":["The interviewers tested her competence in spoken English.","His competence as a driver is clear from his calm handling of heavy traffic.","Parents trusted the school because of the teachers' competence."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"competent","p":"adjective","d":"Having the skill and knowledge to do something well enough.","lb":"capable, qualified","s":["capable","able","skilled","proficient","qualified","efficient"],"k":["accomplished","effective","equal","passable"],"a":["incompetent","inept","unskilled","incapable"],"ex":["She is a competent driver who stays calm in heavy traffic.","We need a competent electrician to fix the wiring safely.","He is competent in English and can write clear emails."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"compile","p":"verb","d":"To collect information from different places and put it together in a list, report or book.","lb":"collect, assemble","s":["assemble","collect","gather","put together","compose","amass"],"k":["build","build up","congregate","construct"],"a":["scatter","disperse","dismantle"],"ex":["Nadia compiled a list of every word she got wrong in the practice tests.","The teacher asked us to compile data from the class survey into one table.","Our manager compiles a sales report at the end of every month."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"complacent","p":"adjective","d":"So satisfied with how things are that you stop trying or ignore possible dangers.","lb":"smug, self-satisfied","s":["smug","pleased with oneself","unconcerned","indolent","contented","untroubled"],"k":["blasé","carefree","lax","nonchalant"],"a":["vigilant","dissatisfied","anxious","alert"],"ex":["After topping the first test, he grew complacent and stopped revising.","We cannot afford to be complacent about hygiene while cholera is still around.","The champion team became complacent and lost to a weaker side."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"complaisant","p":"adjective","d":"Eager to please other people and willing to agree with them or do what they want.","lb":"obliging, agreeable","s":["obliging","accommodating","agreeable","compliant","deferential","amenable"],"k":["biddable","conformable","malleable","meek"],"a":["stubborn","obstinate","uncooperative","defiant"],"ex":["The complaisant host kept refilling our cups and asking if we needed anything else.","He was too complaisant to say no, so he ended up helping everyone with their projects.","A complaisant waiter changed our table three times without a word of complaint."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"complement","p":"verb","d":"To go well with something, making it more complete or better.","lb":"complete, enhance","s":["complete","round out","enhance","set off","supplement","balance"],"k":["accompany","boost","embellish","fill out"],"a":["clash with","spoil","undermine"],"ex":["A squeeze of lemon complements grilled fish perfectly.","Their skills complement each other: Rafi designs the app and Nadia writes the code.","The curtains were chosen to complement the color of the sofa."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"compliant","p":"adjective","d":"Willing to obey rules or orders, or meeting official requirements.","lb":"obedient, conforming","s":["obedient","submissive","docile","dutiful","cooperative","conforming"],"k":["acquiescent","conformable","manageable","meek"],"a":["defiant","disobedient","rebellious","uncooperative"],"ex":["All our products are compliant with the national safety standards.","The child was compliant at the doctor's office and sat still during the check-up.","The factory must become compliant with the new fire rules before it can reopen."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"complicity","p":"noun","d":"Involvement in a wrongdoing or crime together with others, even if you did not carry it out yourself.","lb":"collusion, involvement","s":["collusion","involvement","participation","collaboration","guilt","conspiracy"],"k":["accessoryship","aiding and abetting","association","criminality"],"a":["innocence","opposition","resistance"],"ex":["The clerk denied any complicity in the fraud, but the records showed he had signed the forms.","Staying silent about cheating can be seen as complicity.","The shop owner’s complicity in selling expired medicine led to his arrest."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"comply","p":"verb","d":"To do what a rule, law, order or request says you must do.","lb":"obey, conform","s":["obey","conform","abide by","follow","observe","adhere to"],"k":["adopt","conform to","espouse","stick to"],"a":["disobey","defy","violate","refuse"],"ex":["All drivers must comply with the traffic rules.","The factory was fined for failing to comply with safety regulations.","Passengers were asked to comply with the airline's baggage limits."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"composed","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and in control of your feelings, even in a stressful situation.","lb":"calm, collected","s":["calm","collected","poised","serene","cool","unruffled"],"k":["dignified","equable","even-tempered","imperturbable"],"a":["agitated","flustered","anxious","nervous"],"ex":["She stayed composed during the interview, even when the questions got difficult.","The pilot remained composed as the plane shook through the storm.","He looked composed on the stage, though his hands were shaking."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"composure","p":"noun","d":"The ability to stay calm and in control of your feelings, especially in a difficult situation.","lb":"calmness, poise","s":["calmness","poise","serenity","equanimity","coolness","tranquility"],"k":["aplomb","assurance","disposition","level-headedness"],"a":["agitation","panic","anxiety","nervousness"],"ex":["Even when the microphone failed, the speaker kept her composure and smiled.","He lost his composure and shouted at the referee after the unfair decision.","The pilot's calm composure reassured the passengers during the rough flight."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adjective","d":"Including all or nearly all the important things about a subject.","lb":"complete, thorough","s":["complete","thorough","full","extensive","exhaustive","broad"],"k":["blanket","citywide","cosmopolitan","countywide"],"a":["partial","incomplete","limited","narrow"],"ex":["This comprehensive guide covers every grammar rule you need for the exam.","The hospital offers comprehensive health checks, from blood tests to eye exams.","She wrote a comprehensive report on the school's water problems."],"b":216,"y":1},{"w":"comprise","p":"verb","d":"To consist of or be made up of particular parts.","lb":"consist of, include","s":["consist of","include","contain","incorporate","encompass","embrace"],"k":["consist","constitute","embody","form"],"a":["exclude","omit","lack","leave out"],"ex":["The committee comprises five teachers, two parents and one student representative.","The course comprises twelve lessons, a mid-term test and a final project.","Our apartment comprises two bedrooms, a small kitchen and a balcony overlooking the lake."],"b":208,"y":1},{"w":"compromise","p":"noun","d":"An agreement in which each side gives up some of what it wants so that both can accept the result.","lb":"settlement, middle ground","s":["settlement","agreement","middle ground","concession","accommodation","deal"],"k":["accord","contract","detente","halfway house"],"a":["deadlock","stalemate","impasse","ultimatum"],"ex":["After a long discussion, we reached a compromise on where to go for the trip.","The siblings found a compromise: one would choose the movie, the other the dinner.","Management and workers agreed on a compromise over working hours."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"compulsive","p":"adjective","d":"Doing something because you cannot stop yourself, even when you know it is not sensible.","lb":"uncontrollable, habitual","s":["obsessive","uncontrollable","addictive","habitual","irresistible","chronic"],"k":["ambitious","determined","neurotic","obsessional"],"a":["controlled","occasional","moderate","casual"],"ex":["Nadia's compulsive checking of her phone made it hard for her to focus on her studies.","He is a compulsive liar, so nobody believes his stories any more.","Compulsive shopping left her with many bags and an empty bank account."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"compunction","p":"noun","d":"A guilty or uneasy feeling about doing something wrong.","lb":"guilt, remorse","s":["remorse","guilt","regret","scruples","qualms","misgiving"],"k":["hesitation","pang","reluctance","repentance"],"a":["callousness","ruthlessness","indifference"],"ex":["He lied to his teacher without compunction and showed no regret afterwards.","She had no compunction about returning the broken toy and asking for a refund.","The thief felt no compunction about stealing from poor families."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"con","p":"verb","d":"To trick someone into giving you money or believing a lie, usually by gaining their trust.","lb":"trick, swindle","s":["swindle","cheat","trick","deceive","dupe","fleece"],"k":["bamboozle","bunco","chisel","diddle"],"a":[],"ex":["A stranger conned my uncle out of five thousand taka by pretending to be a bank officer.","Online sellers sometimes con shoppers by posting photos of products they do not have.","He conned his way into the party by pretending to be the host's cousin."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"concave","p":"adjective","d":"Curving inward, like the inside of a bowl.","lb":"curved inward, hollow","s":["hollow","dished","indented","sunken","depressed","cupped"],"k":["basin-like","bowl-shaped","dented","dimpled"],"a":["convex","bulging","rounded","protruding"],"ex":["A concave lens spreads out light rays, so it is used to correct short-sightedness.","Rain collected in the concave surface of the old metal plate.","The shaving mirror was concave, so it made my face look bigger."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conceal","p":"verb","d":"To keep something hidden so that others cannot see or find it.","lb":"hide, cover up","s":["hide","cover up","mask","disguise","camouflage","screen"],"k":["cover","dissemble","hold back","hold in"],"a":["reveal","expose","show","disclose"],"ex":["He tried to conceal his low marks from his parents.","A thick scarf concealed the scar on her neck.","The thief concealed the stolen phone inside his jacket."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"concede","p":"verb","d":"To admit, often unwillingly, that something is true or that someone else is right.","lb":"admit, yield","s":["admit","acknowledge","grant","accept","yield","allow"],"k":["accede","approve","cede","disclose"],"a":["deny","dispute","contest","insist"],"ex":["I have to concede that your route was faster than mine.","After a long argument, he conceded that his sister was right about the date.","The losing team conceded defeat and warmly congratulated the winners."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"conceited","p":"adjective","d":"Too proud of your own abilities, looks or achievements.","lb":"vain, arrogant","s":["vain","arrogant","egotistical","smug","boastful","cocky"],"k":["big-headed","full of oneself","haughty","proud"],"a":["modest","humble","unassuming"],"ex":["After winning the quiz, Tanvir became so conceited that he stopped listening to his teammates.","Nobody likes a conceited colleague who keeps bragging about his salary.","She is talented but never conceited, and she always thanks the people who helped her."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"concentric","p":"adjective","d":"Having the same centre, as circles of different sizes placed one inside another.","lb":"same-centred","s":["coaxial","nested"],"k":["annular","circular","layered","ringed"],"a":["eccentric"],"ex":["Ripples spread in concentric circles when the stone hit the pond.","The target board has concentric rings, with the bullseye in the middle.","The ancient city was built with concentric walls around the palace."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"concert","p":"noun","d":"Agreement and cooperation between people who are working together toward the same aim.","lb":"unity, accord","s":["unison","harmony","accord","agreement","cooperation","unity"],"k":["cohesion","fellowship","partnership","performance"],"a":["discord","disagreement","conflict","disunity"],"ex":["The two schools worked in concert to organize the flood relief drive.","For the project to succeed, all the departments must move in concert.","Several banks raised their interest rates in concert, which surprised customers."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"conciliatory","p":"adjective","d":"Intended to calm anger or end a disagreement by being friendly and willing to compromise.","lb":"peacemaking, placating","s":["placating","appeasing","peaceable","reconciling","accommodating","diplomatic"],"k":["compromising","flexible","forgiving","irenic"],"a":["hostile","antagonistic","aggressive","belligerent"],"ex":["After the argument, Rafi sent a conciliatory message offering to share the cost of the repair.","The manager took a conciliatory tone in the meeting and listened to every complaint.","Her conciliatory smile helped end the quarrel between the two neighbors."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"concise","p":"adjective","d":"Giving all the necessary information in a few clear words.","lb":"brief, succinct","s":["brief","succinct","short","to the point","compact","pithy"],"k":["cryptic","curt","economical","elliptical"],"a":["wordy","verbose","rambling","lengthy"],"ex":["Please write a concise summary of the chapter in no more than five sentences.","Her answer was concise, clear and exactly what the examiner wanted.","The guidebook gives concise directions to each place on the map."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"concoct","p":"verb","d":"To make something by mixing different things together, or to invent a story or plan.","lb":"devise, brew","s":["devise","invent","create","brew","prepare","make up"],"k":["design","dream up","formulate","hatch"],"a":[],"ex":["Rafi concocted a spicy drink from lemon, ginger and honey for his cold.","She concocted an excuse about the traffic to explain her lateness.","The friends concocted a plan to surprise their teacher on her birthday."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"concomitant","p":"adjective","d":"Happening at the same time as something else, often as a natural result of it.","lb":"accompanying, attendant","s":["accompanying","attendant","associated","related","resultant","incidental"],"k":["accessory","affiliated","allied","coincident"],"a":["unrelated","separate","independent","unconnected"],"ex":["The new job brought a concomitant rise in stress.","Higher wages and the concomitant increase in prices left families no better off.","A fever and its concomitant aches kept her in bed all week."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"concord","p":"noun","d":"A state of peaceful agreement and friendly relations between people or groups.","lb":"harmony, agreement","s":["harmony","agreement","accord","unity","peace","amity"],"k":["bonhomie","cordiality","entente","fraternity"],"a":["discord","conflict","disagreement","strife"],"ex":["The neighbors lived in concord for decades, sharing food during festivals and helping each other in emergencies.","After a long meeting, the committee finally reached concord on how to spend the budget.","The treaty ended the long dispute and brought concord between the two border towns."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"concurrent","p":"adjective","d":"Happening or existing at the same time.","lb":"simultaneous, parallel","s":["simultaneous","concomitant","coinciding","parallel","coexisting","synchronous"],"k":["associated","coincidental","collective","combined"],"a":["consecutive","successive","sequential","separate"],"ex":["The two lectures are concurrent, so students must choose one of them.","The festival had concurrent events: a music show in the hall and a book sale outside.","The judge gave him two concurrent sentences, so he will serve them at the same time."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"condemn","p":"verb","d":"To say very strongly that something is wrong or bad.","lb":"criticize, denounce","s":["denounce","criticize","censure","blame","deplore","slam"],"k":["castigate","decry","doom","excoriate"],"a":["praise","approve","commend","applaud"],"ex":["Teachers and parents condemned the bullying of a new student.","The newspaper condemned the factory owner for ignoring safety rules.","Everyone condemned the driver who sped through the red light."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"condense","p":"verb","d":"To make a piece of writing or speech shorter by keeping only the main points.","lb":"shorten, summarise","s":["shorten","abridge","compress","cut","trim","boil down"],"k":["concentrate","curtail","distill","epitomize"],"a":["expand","lengthen","extend","elaborate"],"ex":["Try to condense your answer into two short paragraphs.","The editor condensed the long report into a single page for busy readers.","Rafi condensed forty pages of notes into a short list of key formulas before the exam."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"condescend","p":"verb","d":"To behave as if one is better or more intelligent than other people, especially by talking down to them.","lb":"talk down, patronize","s":["patronize","talk down to","look down on","deign","stoop","lower oneself"],"k":["act","belittle","descend","despise"],"a":["respect","defer to","look up to"],"ex":["The senior student condescended to the new boys and explained everything very slowly.","Please do not condescend to me; I understand the topic perfectly well.","He would never condescend to ask a junior colleague for help."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"condone","p":"verb","d":"To accept or forgive behavior that most people think is wrong, or to fail to object to it.","lb":"excuse, overlook","s":["excuse","overlook","forgive","tolerate","pardon","disregard"],"k":["absolve","approve","countenance","let pass"],"a":["condemn","denounce","disapprove of","forbid"],"ex":["Our school does not condone cheating, and anyone caught copying will fail the exam.","I can understand why he was upset, but I cannot condone shouting at the waiter.","The company will not condone bullying of any kind in the workplace."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"conducive","p":"adjective","d":"Making a particular result or situation likely or possible; helpful for achieving it.","lb":"helpful, favorable","s":["helpful","favorable","beneficial","supportive","advantageous","productive"],"k":["affirmative","approving","auspicious","causative"],"a":["harmful","detrimental","unfavorable","counterproductive"],"ex":["A quiet room with good light is conducive to studying for long hours.","Loud music at night is not conducive to sleep, especially for people with early shifts.","The manager tried to create a friendly office conducive to teamwork and open discussion."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"confederate","p":"noun","d":"A person who secretly works with others, especially in doing something wrong; an accomplice.","lb":"accomplice, ally","s":["accomplice","ally","partner","accessory","associate","collaborator"],"k":["cohort","colleague","companion","comrade"],"a":["enemy","opponent","rival","adversary"],"ex":["The thief's confederate waited outside and warned him when the guard returned.","Police arrested the cashier and her confederate, who had been copying customers' card numbers.","In the magic show, a confederate in the audience pretended to be a stranger."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"confer","p":"verb","d":"To discuss something with others before deciding, or to formally give someone an award, degree or title.","lb":"consult, bestow","s":["consult","discuss","deliberate","talk over","bestow","grant"],"k":["consider","endow","give","hash out"],"a":["withhold","deny","revoke","take away"],"ex":["The two teachers conferred quietly before announcing the new exam date.","The university will confer degrees on more than a thousand graduates next month.","I need to confer with my parents before accepting the scholarship."],"b":162,"y":0},{"w":"confess","p":"verb","d":"To admit that you have done something wrong or something you feel embarrassed about.","lb":"admit, own up","s":["admit","acknowledge","own up","come clean","reveal","disclose"],"k":["accept","allow","blurt out","expose"],"a":["deny","conceal","hide","disclaim"],"ex":["The boy finally confessed that he had broken the window with his ball.","She confessed to her teacher that she had copied the answer.","I must confess that I have never read this famous novel."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"confidant","p":"noun","d":"A close friend you trust with your secrets and private feelings.","lb":"close friend, intimate","s":["intimate","close friend","bosom friend","confidante","ally","advisor"],"k":["alter ego","best friend","bosom buddy","comrade"],"a":["stranger","enemy","betrayer"],"ex":["My older sister has always been my closest confidant.","Nadia trusted her cousin as her confidant and told him about her plan to study abroad.","A good doctor often becomes a confidant to his patients."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"configuration","p":"noun","d":"The way the parts of something are arranged or set up to work together.","lb":"arrangement, layout","s":["arrangement","layout","setup","structure","formation","design"],"k":["constellation","contour","disposition","form"],"a":[],"ex":["The technician changed the router’s configuration to make the Wi-Fi faster.","The classroom’s new configuration, with desks in a circle, encouraged more discussion.","We tried different configurations of the sofa and table before choosing the best one."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conflagration","p":"noun","d":"A very large, destructive fire that spreads quickly over a wide area.","lb":"great fire, blaze","s":["blaze","inferno","fire","firestorm","wildfire","big fire"],"k":["bushfire","combustion","flare-up","incineration"],"a":[],"ex":["A conflagration swept through the crowded slum, leaving hundreds of families without homes.","Firefighters worked all night to control the conflagration at the old warehouse.","A single careless cigarette started the conflagration that destroyed the dry forest."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conflict","p":"noun","d":"A serious disagreement or fight between people, groups or ideas that have opposing aims.","lb":"clash, disagreement","s":["clash","dispute","disagreement","quarrel","struggle","fight"],"k":["animosity","battle","combat","confrontation"],"a":["harmony","agreement","peace","accord"],"ex":["A conflict between two shop owners over parking was settled by the market committee.","Conflict at home made it hard for her to study.","The conflict between work and family is common among new parents."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"confluence","p":"noun","d":"The place where two rivers flow together, or a coming together of different things.","lb":"meeting point, junction","s":["junction","convergence","meeting point","merging","union","merger"],"k":["concourse","conjunction","crossroads","intersection"],"a":["divergence","separation","split","fork"],"ex":["Chandpur lies at the confluence of the Padma and the Meghna, and fishermen gather there each morning.","The city grew up at the confluence of two rivers, which made it easy to trade by boat.","The festival is a confluence of music, food and art from many different regions."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"confound","p":"verb","d":"To confuse or surprise someone so much that they cannot understand what is happening.","lb":"confuse, baffle","s":["confuse","baffle","bewilder","puzzle","mystify","bemuse"],"k":["amaze","astonish","be","beat"],"a":["clarify","enlighten","explain","reassure"],"ex":["The puzzling test results confounded the doctors, who had expected a simple infection.","The team's sudden win confounded everyone who had predicted a heavy defeat.","Complicated airport signs often confound tourists who are trying to find the right gate."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"congeal","p":"verb","d":"To become thick and almost solid, usually as a liquid cools or dries.","lb":"solidify, thicken","s":["solidify","coagulate","thicken","clot","harden","set"],"k":["cake","crust","firm up","gelatinize"],"a":["liquefy","melt","thaw","dissolve"],"ex":["The curry had congealed into a thick layer of grease by the time we sat down.","Blood congeals quickly to close a small cut.","Oil congeals in the pipes when the kitchen is very cold."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"congenial","p":"adjective","d":"Pleasant and suitable because it matches your own tastes or character.","lb":"agreeable, pleasant","s":["pleasant","agreeable","friendly","compatible","genial","sympathetic"],"k":["affable","amiable","companionable","cordial"],"a":["unpleasant","disagreeable","hostile","unsuitable"],"ex":["I found a congenial group of friends at the university debating club.","The quiet library is a congenial place to study for exams.","She moved to the smaller town in search of a more congenial lifestyle."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"congenital","p":"adjective","d":"Present from birth, especially of a medical condition that develops before a baby is born.","lb":"present at birth, innate","s":["inborn","innate","inherent","natural","native","inbred"],"k":["constitutional","familial","genetic","hereditary"],"a":["acquired","developed","learned","contracted"],"ex":["The baby was born with a congenital heart defect and needed surgery in the first month.","Doctors explained that her hearing loss was congenital and not caused by an infection later.","Some congenital conditions can be detected by a scan before the baby is born."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"congregate","p":"verb","d":"To come together in a group, usually in one place for a purpose.","lb":"gather, assemble","s":["gather","assemble","meet","convene","collect","flock"],"k":["amass","bunch up","crowd together","huddle"],"a":["disperse","scatter","separate","disband"],"ex":["Students congregate in the canteen after the last class to talk and drink tea.","Pigeons congregate in the square, hoping for scraps of food from visitors.","Fans began to congregate outside the stadium three hours before the match."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"conjecture","p":"verb","d":"To form an opinion or guess without having much evidence.","lb":"guess, speculate","s":["guess","speculate","surmise","suppose","theorize","infer"],"k":["anticipate","assume","divine","expect"],"a":["know","prove","confirm","verify"],"ex":["Historians can only conjecture about what life was like in the village a thousand years ago.","Reporters conjectured that the coach would resign, though nobody had confirmed it.","Rafi conjectured from the empty street that the shops had closed early because of the rain."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"conjoin","p":"verb","d":"To join two or more things together or combine them.","lb":"join, combine","s":["join","unite","combine","connect","link","merge"],"k":["affiliate","blend","fasten","get married"],"a":["separate","divide","split","detach"],"ex":["A narrow bridge conjoins the two parts of the town across the river.","The writer conjoins humor and sadness in a single story.","Two small rivers conjoin here to form a much larger one."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"conjugal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to marriage or to the relationship between a husband and wife.","lb":"marital, matrimonial","s":["marital","matrimonial","married","nuptial","wedded","connubial"],"k":["bridal","domestic","familial","household"],"a":[],"ex":["After thirty years of conjugal life, the couple still holds hands during evening walks.","Conjugal harmony depends on trust, respect and open conversation.","The counselor spoke to the couple about their expectations of conjugal life."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conjure","p":"verb","d":"To make something appear as if by magic, or to bring an image or memory to mind.","lb":"summon, evoke","s":["summon","produce","create","evoke","call up","bring about"],"k":["arouse","beseech","bring up","build"],"a":["banish","dispel","dismiss"],"ex":["The magician conjured a bunch of flowers out of an empty hat.","The smell of rain conjures up memories of my childhood in the village.","My mother can conjure a delicious meal from a few leftovers."],"b":88,"y":1},{"w":"connive","p":"verb","d":"To secretly work with others to do something wrong, or to allow wrongdoing by pretending not to see it.","lb":"conspire, collude","s":["conspire","scheme","plot","collude","abet","intrigue"],"k":["be complicit","fudge","go along with","hatch"],"a":["oppose","expose","report","prevent"],"ex":["Two officials connived to hide the real cost of the new road.","The shop owner connived with the supplier to cheat customers on weight.","The children connived to hide the broken vase until their parents came home."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"connoisseur","p":"noun","d":"A person with great knowledge and good judgment in a particular field, especially food, drink or art.","lb":"expert, judge","s":["expert","authority","specialist","aficionado","judge","buff"],"k":["fan","lover","master","practitioner"],"a":["layman","amateur","novice","philistine"],"ex":["My uncle is a tea connoisseur who can tell which garden a leaf came from by its smell.","Art connoisseurs traveled from many countries to see the rare paintings.","As a connoisseur of old Bangla films, she owns hundreds of rare posters."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"connotation","p":"noun","d":"An idea or feeling that a word suggests in addition to its basic meaning.","lb":"implied meaning","s":["implication","suggestion","overtone","nuance","association","hint"],"k":["aura","flavor","inference","innuendo"],"a":["literal meaning"],"ex":["The word cheap has a negative connotation, but inexpensive sounds positive.","In some cultures, the color white carries a connotation of mourning.","Advertisers choose words with a warm connotation to make products sound friendly."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"conscience","p":"noun","d":"The inner feeling that tells you whether your actions are right or wrong.","lb":"moral sense","s":["moral sense","scruples","principles","ethics","inner voice","morals"],"k":["ethical motive","moral compass","morality","qualms"],"a":[],"ex":["My conscience would not let me keep the money I found on the road.","He had a guilty conscience after copying his friend's homework.","She slept well that night with a clear conscience."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"conscientious","p":"adjective","d":"Careful to do your work properly and to do what is right.","lb":"careful, principled","s":["diligent","careful","meticulous","thorough","scrupulous","dutiful"],"k":["assiduous","earnest","exacting","fastidious"],"a":["careless","negligent","irresponsible","sloppy"],"ex":["The conscientious nurse checked each patient's chart before ending her shift.","He is conscientious about returning every book to the library on time.","A conscientious driver always checks the mirrors before changing lanes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"consecrate","p":"verb","d":"To make or declare something sacred in a formal ceremony; also, to devote oneself or something wholly to one purpose.","lb":"sanctify, dedicate","s":["sanctify","hallow","bless","dedicate","devote","ordain"],"k":["commit","declare","give","order"],"a":["desecrate","defile","profane","violate"],"ex":["The villagers gathered to consecrate the new temple with prayers, flowers and music.","Local leaders agreed to consecrate the field as a memorial to those who died in the flood.","She consecrated her life to teaching poor children, working long after retirement."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"consensus","p":"noun","d":"General agreement among all the people in a group.","lb":"agreement, accord","s":["agreement","accord","harmony","concord","consent","unity"],"k":["common ground","common view","general feeling","majority view"],"a":["disagreement","dissent","conflict","discord"],"ex":["After a long discussion, the family reached a consensus to spend the holiday in Cox's Bazar.","There is a growing consensus among doctors that enough sleep is vital for students.","The committee could not reach a consensus, so the members voted."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"consequence","p":"noun","d":"A result or effect of something that happened earlier, often an unwanted one.","lb":"result, outcome","s":["result","outcome","effect","repercussion","upshot","aftermath"],"k":["backlash","conclusion","corollary","event"],"a":["cause","origin","source","root"],"ex":["Skipping meals can have serious consequences for your health.","As a consequence of the heavy rain, many roads in the city were under water.","If you break the school rules, you must accept the consequences."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"conservative","p":"adjective","d":"Preferring traditional ideas and ways of doing things, and unwilling to accept change.","lb":"traditional, cautious","s":["traditional","conventional","cautious","orthodox","old-fashioned","reserved"],"k":["accepted","bourgeois","customary","established"],"a":["progressive","radical","liberal","modern"],"ex":["My grandparents are conservative about clothes and prefer simple, traditional styles.","The bank takes a conservative approach and avoids risky investments.","Some conservative teachers still prefer chalk and blackboards to projectors."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"conservatory","p":"noun","d":"A room with glass walls and roof, joined to a house, used for growing plants or sitting in the sun.","lb":"glasshouse, sunroom","s":["greenhouse","sunroom","hothouse","solarium","garden room"],"k":["atrium","indoor garden","lean-to","orangerie"],"a":[],"ex":["We drink tea in the conservatory on cold mornings because the glass walls trap the sunlight.","They added a conservatory to the back of the house to grow orchids and herbs.","The estate agent said the conservatory was the best feature of the property."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"consign","p":"verb","d":"To hand something over or send it to a place or person, often to get rid of it or for safekeeping.","lb":"hand over, entrust","s":["hand over","entrust","commit","deliver","relegate","assign"],"k":["confide","convey","discard","dispatch"],"a":["keep","retain","withdraw","hold on to"],"ex":["He consigned his old school notes to the dustbin after the final exam.","The company consigned the goods to a shipping agent for delivery to Chittagong.","The old sofa was consigned to the storeroom when we bought a new one."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"consolidate","p":"verb","d":"To combine several things into one stronger or more effective whole, or to make something firmer.","lb":"combine, strengthen","s":["combine","merge","unite","strengthen","fortify","secure"],"k":["blend","fuse","join","mix"],"a":["divide","split","separate","weaken"],"ex":["He took one loan to consolidate all his small debts into a single monthly payment.","The two schools were consolidated into one to save on running costs.","Take a short quiz each night to consolidate what you learned in class."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"consonant","p":"adjective","d":"In agreement or harmony with something; consistent with it.","lb":"consistent, in agreement","s":["consistent","compatible","harmonious","in agreement","congruent","in keeping"],"k":["accordant","coherent","concordant","conformable"],"a":["inconsistent","dissonant","incompatible","conflicting"],"ex":["The company’s actions were not consonant with its promise to protect the environment.","His quiet lifestyle is consonant with his belief in living simply.","Doctors say a plan consonant with your body’s needs works better than a crash diet."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"conspicuous","p":"adjective","d":"Easy to see or notice because it stands out.","lb":"noticeable, obvious","s":["noticeable","obvious","visible","prominent","striking","glaring"],"k":["apparent","big","blazing","bold"],"a":["inconspicuous","hidden","concealed","subtle"],"ex":["The bright red sign was conspicuous from the other side of the street.","He felt conspicuous in a suit when everyone else wore jeans.","The report showed a conspicuous drop in sales after the price rise."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"consternation","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of shock, worry or confusion caused by something unexpected.","lb":"dismay, alarm","s":["dismay","alarm","shock","confusion","anxiety","panic"],"k":["agitation","apprehension","disquiet","fright"],"a":["calm","composure","serenity","equanimity"],"ex":["To my consternation, the shop was closed, and I had no other way to buy the medicine.","The class watched in consternation as the projector burst into smoke.","News of the sudden bus strike caused consternation among commuters in the morning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"constituency","p":"noun","d":"A district whose voters elect a representative, or the group of voters themselves.","lb":"electoral district, voters","s":["electorate","district","ward","voters","electoral district","seat"],"k":["bailiwick","body","borough","division"],"a":[],"ex":["Each member of parliament represents a constituency and listens to its voters' problems.","The candidate visited every village in her constituency before the election.","A new road was the main demand of the people in this constituency."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"construe","p":"verb","d":"To understand or interpret the meaning of words or actions in a particular way.","lb":"interpret, understand","s":["interpret","understand","read","take","translate","deduce"],"k":["analyze","characterize","clarify","consider"],"a":[],"ex":["Please do not construe my silence as agreement; I simply need time to think.","Her joke was construed as an insult by some of the guests.","The rule can be construed in two ways, so ask the teacher to clarify."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"consult","p":"verb","d":"To ask a person, or look in a book or other source, for advice or information.","lb":"ask advice, refer to","s":["ask","confer with","refer to","seek advice from","check with","look up"],"k":["confab","confer","enquire","inquire"],"a":["ignore","disregard","overlook"],"ex":["You should consult a doctor if your fever lasts more than three days.","Before signing the rental agreement, we consulted a lawyer.","Students can consult the dictionary when they meet an unfamiliar word."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"consummate","p":"adjective","d":"Having or showing the highest level of skill; perfect or complete in every way.","lb":"perfect, supremely skilled","s":["perfect","supreme","accomplished","masterful","skilled","expert"],"k":["adept","arrant","completed","excellent"],"a":["unskilled","amateurish","inept","incompetent"],"ex":["The chef is a consummate professional who never loses his calm, even when the restaurant is full.","She handled the angry crowd with consummate skill and sent everyone home smiling.","He is a consummate storyteller, and his grandchildren listen in silence for hours."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"contempt","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of disrespect for someone or something that you think is worthless.","lb":"scorn, disdain","s":["scorn","disdain","disgust","disrespect","derision","mockery"],"k":["aversion","dislike","hostility","rancor"],"a":["respect","admiration","esteem","regard"],"ex":["She looked at the cheating player with contempt and refused to shake his hand.","Many fans felt only contempt for the club’s owner after he sold the best players.","He holds the traffic rules in contempt, driving through red lights without a thought."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"contemptible","p":"adjective","d":"Deserving no respect because of being very bad, dishonest or cowardly.","lb":"despicable, vile","s":["despicable","detestable","shameful","base","vile","low"],"k":["disgraceful","dishonorable","execrable","miserable"],"a":["admirable","honorable","respectable","noble"],"ex":["Stealing money from a charity box is a contemptible act.","I found his decision to blame the cleaner for his own mistake contemptible.","The newspaper called the scam a contemptible trick played on the elderly."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"contention","p":"noun","d":"An opinion or point that someone states and argues for as true.","lb":"claim, assertion","s":["claim","assertion","argument","belief","view","opinion"],"k":["assumption","averment","competition","controversy"],"a":[],"ex":["It is my contention that students learn better when school starts later in the morning.","The lawyer's main contention was that her client was out of town that night.","Scientists studied the data and found little to support his contention."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"contentious","p":"adjective","d":"Likely to cause arguments, or always ready to argue.","lb":"controversial, argumentative","s":["controversial","disputed","argumentative","quarrelsome","combative","divisive"],"k":["aggressive","bellicose","cantankerous","factious"],"a":["agreeable","peaceable","uncontroversial","harmonious"],"ex":["The plan to close the old market became a contentious issue in the neighborhood.","My contentious cousin argues about everything, from football scores to the price of tea.","Dividing the family land was a contentious matter that took years to settle."],"b":91,"y":1},{"w":"contestant","p":"noun","d":"A person who takes part in a competition, quiz or contest.","lb":"competitor, participant","s":["competitor","participant","contender","candidate","player","rival"],"k":["aspirant","bidder","challenger","competition"],"a":["spectator"],"ex":["Each contestant in the spelling bee had two minutes to answer.","The youngest contestant in the cooking show was only twelve years old.","A nervous contestant forgot the answer, and the whole audience whispered hints."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"contiguous","p":"adjective","d":"Sharing a border or touching; next to one another without a gap.","lb":"adjoining, touching","s":["adjoining","adjacent","neighboring","bordering","touching","next to"],"k":["close-set","conterminous","continuous","immediate"],"a":["separate","detached","distant","apart"],"ex":["Bangladesh is contiguous with India along most of its border.","The two rooms are contiguous, so we opened the folding door and made one big hall.","Our house is contiguous to the school playground, so we hear the children all morning."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"contingent","p":"adjective","d":"Depending on something else that may or may not happen.","lb":"dependent, conditional","s":["dependent","conditional","subject","reliant","provisional","uncertain"],"k":["dependent on","hypothetical","iffy","moot"],"a":["independent","unconditional","certain","absolute"],"ex":["Our picnic is contingent on the weather, so we will decide on Friday.","The job offer is contingent upon passing a medical check.","Her scholarship is contingent on keeping her marks above eighty percent."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"continuum","p":"noun","d":"A continuous series in which neighbouring parts are barely different, though the two ends are very different.","lb":"range, spectrum","s":["spectrum","range","scale","sequence","progression","series"],"k":["array","extent","flow","flux"],"a":[],"ex":["Teachers see reading ability as a continuum, not a simple choice between good and poor.","Shy and outgoing are two ends of a continuum, and most people sit somewhere in the middle.","The colours of the rainbow form a continuum, with no clear line where red becomes orange."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"contraband","p":"noun","d":"Goods that are brought into or taken out of a country illegally, or that are forbidden by law.","lb":"smuggled goods, illegal goods","s":["smuggled goods","illegal goods","illicit goods","bootleg goods","banned items"],"k":["counterfeit goods","hot goods","merchandise","moonshine"],"a":["legal goods","legitimate goods"],"ex":["Customs officers seized a large amount of contraband hidden inside a truck full of vegetables.","Mobile phones are treated as contraband in some prisons.","The border guards arrested two men for carrying contraband across the river at night."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"contradict","p":"verb","d":"To say that something someone said is wrong, or to be so different from something that both cannot be true.","lb":"oppose, deny","s":["deny","dispute","challenge","refute","counter","oppose"],"k":["belie","contravene","gainsay","rebut"],"a":["confirm","support","agree with","back up"],"ex":["It is rude to contradict your teacher in front of the whole class.","The two witnesses contradicted each other about what time the accident happened.","The new research contradicts the old belief that sugar makes children hyperactive."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"contrary","p":"adjective","d":"Completely different or opposite in nature, direction or meaning.","lb":"opposite, conflicting","s":["opposite","opposing","conflicting","contradictory","clashing","reverse"],"k":["antagonistic","antithetical","at odds","diametric"],"a":["similar","consistent","matching","compatible"],"ex":["Contrary to what many students believe, studying all night usually lowers your exam score.","Her contrary opinion surprised the committee, which had expected her to agree.","The manager took the contrary view and argued that the project should be delayed."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"contravene","p":"verb","d":"To break a law, rule or agreement.","lb":"break, violate","s":["violate","breach","break","infringe","flout","disobey"],"k":["contradict","crack","go against","negate"],"a":["obey","observe","comply with","follow"],"ex":["Drivers who park here contravene the city's traffic rules.","The factory contravened safety regulations and was fined.","Copying answers from a friend contravenes the school's exam rules."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"contretemps","p":"noun","d":"A small, unexpected and embarrassing disagreement or mishap, especially in public.","lb":"mishap, spat","s":["mishap","squabble","spat","clash","quarrel","setback"],"k":["altercation","bicker","bickering","brush"],"a":[],"ex":["We had a small contretemps at the restaurant when two bills arrived for one table.","A contretemps over seat numbers delayed the start of the show.","A contretemps with a stuck door left the groom late for his own ceremony."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"contrite","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling or showing deep regret for having done something wrong.","lb":"remorseful, sorry","s":["remorseful","sorry","repentant","penitent","apologetic","regretful"],"k":["abashed","chastened","humbled","mortified"],"a":["unrepentant","remorseless","unapologetic","shameless"],"ex":["He looked contrite when he admitted that he had broken his sister's tablet.","The contrite driver apologized to the shopkeeper and offered to pay for the damaged cart.","She wrote a contrite email to her teacher after submitting the assignment late."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"contrive","p":"verb","d":"To plan or make something cleverly, often using skill and effort in a difficult situation.","lb":"devise, engineer","s":["devise","invent","engineer","concoct","arrange","manage"],"k":["conceive","create","create by mental act","create mentally"],"a":[],"ex":["Using old bottles and tape, the students contrived a simple water filter for the science fair.","She contrived a way to attend both events by leaving the first one early.","The two friends contrived to meet outside the cinema without their parents noticing."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"contrived","p":"adjective","d":"Not natural or spontaneous; obviously planned or forced in order to produce an effect.","lb":"forced, unnatural","s":["forced","artificial","unnatural","strained","labored","stilted"],"k":["calculated","engineered","hokey","manufactured"],"a":["natural","spontaneous","genuine","authentic"],"ex":["The movie's ending felt contrived, as if the writer had run out of ideas.","Her contrived excuse about a sick cat did not fool the teacher.","The interview question seemed contrived to make candidates look foolish."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"contumacious","p":"adjective","d":"Stubbornly refusing to obey authority or follow rules.","lb":"rebellious, defiant","s":["defiant","rebellious","disobedient","insubordinate","obstinate","unruly"],"k":["fractious","headstrong","obdurate","resistant"],"a":["obedient","compliant","submissive","docile"],"ex":["The contumacious student ignored every warning and kept using his phone in class.","The court fined the contumacious witness for refusing to answer the judge's questions.","My contumacious little brother refuses to wear a helmet, no matter how often Dad insists."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"contumacy","p":"noun","d":"Stubborn refusal to obey or accept authority, especially an order from a court.","lb":"stubborn defiance","s":["defiance","disobedience","obstinacy","stubbornness","insubordination","rebelliousness"],"k":["contrariness","headstrongness","mulishness","noncompliance"],"a":["obedience","compliance","submission","deference"],"ex":["The witness was fined for contumacy after ignoring three court summonses.","The committee grew tired of the member's contumacy and finally cancelled his membership.","An old legal textbook describes contumacy as a refusal to attend a hearing."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"contumely","p":"noun","d":"Rude and insulting words or behaviour that show a lack of respect.","lb":"insolence, insult","s":["insolence","abuse","scorn","insult","disrespect","contempt"],"k":["cheek","discourtesy","disdain","impudence"],"a":["respect","courtesy","praise","politeness"],"ex":["The prisoner was treated with contumely by the guards, who laughed at him.","She endured the contumely of her classmates for months because she wore old clothes.","Honest workers should not have to face contumely from rude customers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conundrum","p":"noun","d":"A confusing and difficult problem or question.","lb":"puzzle, dilemma","s":["puzzle","riddle","enigma","dilemma","problem","mystery"],"k":["difficulty","gordian knot","head-scratcher","impasse"],"a":["solution","answer","explanation"],"ex":["How to pay for university without a loan is a conundrum for many families.","The missing keys were a real conundrum: we had searched every room twice.","Choosing between a well-paid job and a happy one is a conundrum many graduates face."],"b":43,"y":0},{"w":"convene","p":"verb","d":"To come together for a meeting, or to call people together for one.","lb":"assemble, meet","s":["assemble","gather","meet","summon","call","congregate"],"k":["amass","bring together","call together","collect"],"a":["disperse","adjourn","scatter","dismiss"],"ex":["The principal convened a meeting of all teachers to discuss the exam schedule.","The committee will convene at ten o'clock tomorrow in the conference room.","Family members convened at my grandmother's house for Eid lunch."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"convenient","p":"adjective","d":"Easy to use or reach, and saving you time or trouble.","lb":"handy, suitable","s":["handy","suitable","practical","accessible","useful","nearby"],"k":["commodious","expedient","functional","ready to hand"],"a":["inconvenient","awkward","inaccessible","impractical"],"ex":["Our apartment is convenient for work because the bus stop is right outside.","Would Thursday afternoon be a convenient time for the meeting?","Mobile banking is convenient because you can pay bills without standing in line."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"convention","p":"noun","d":"A way of behaving or doing something that most people in a society accept as normal or correct.","lb":"custom, norm","s":["custom","tradition","norm","practice","etiquette","protocol"],"k":["canon","formula","habit","mores"],"a":["innovation","originality"],"ex":["In our family, it is a convention to greet the elders first.","By convention, the host serves the guests before eating.","The artist ignored convention and painted the sky green."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"conventional","p":"adjective","d":"Following the usual, accepted way of doing things, rather than being new or unusual.","lb":"traditional, ordinary","s":["traditional","orthodox","standard","customary","ordinary","usual"],"k":["ceremonious","common","conservative","established"],"a":["unconventional","unorthodox","original","radical"],"ex":["My parents hoped I would choose a conventional career, such as medicine or engineering.","The restaurant serves only conventional dishes, with nothing unusual on the menu.","Conventional wisdom says you should save part of every paycheck."],"b":280,"y":0},{"w":"converge","p":"verb","d":"To move toward the same point and meet there, or to become similar or joined.","lb":"meet, come together","s":["meet","join","merge","unite","gather","come together"],"k":["affiliate","approach","assemble","cluster"],"a":["diverge","separate","part","scatter"],"ex":["Fans from all over the city converged on the stadium before the final match.","The two rivers converge near the town and flow on as one wide stream.","The two lines on the graph converge at the point where supply meets demand."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"conversant","p":"adjective","d":"Familiar with a subject or skill because you have learned about it or used it.","lb":"familiar, knowledgeable","s":["familiar","knowledgeable","versed","acquainted","experienced","informed"],"k":["au courant","au fait","educated","in the know"],"a":["unfamiliar","ignorant","inexperienced","unacquainted"],"ex":["The new teacher is conversant with the latest software for online classes.","You should be conversant with the exam format before test day.","My grandfather is not conversant with smartphones, so he asks me for help."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"converse","p":"noun","d":"The opposite or reverse of something, especially of a statement or an idea.","lb":"opposite, reverse","s":["opposite","reverse","contrary","antithesis","inverse","flip side"],"k":["antonym","mirror image","negative","other side"],"a":["same","equivalent"],"ex":["All dogs are animals, but the converse is not true: not all animals are dogs.","If a triangle has three equal sides, it has three equal angles, and the converse is also true.","Exercise improves sleep, and the converse holds too: good sleep makes exercise easier."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"convey","p":"verb","d":"To carry something from one place to another, or to make an idea or feeling known to someone.","lb":"communicate, transport","s":["communicate","transport","carry","express","transmit","impart"],"k":["channel","conduct","dispatch","fetch"],"a":["withhold","conceal","hide","keep back"],"ex":["Pipes convey clean water from the treatment plant to homes across the city.","Please convey my thanks to your parents for the lovely dinner.","His tired eyes conveyed more than his words about how hard the week had been."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"conviction","p":"noun","d":"A very strong belief or opinion; also an official court decision that someone is guilty of a crime.","lb":"belief, certainty","s":["belief","faith","certainty","persuasion","creed","confidence"],"k":["article of faith","commitment","condemnation","credo"],"a":["doubt","uncertainty","hesitation","acquittal"],"ex":["She spoke with great conviction about the need to protect the river.","It is my conviction that hard work matters more than talent.","He lacked the conviction to say no, so he agreed to every request."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"convivial","p":"adjective","d":"Friendly, lively and enjoyable, especially when people share food and drink.","lb":"sociable, jovial","s":["sociable","jovial","festive","cordial","genial","merry"],"k":["boisterous","carousing","clubby","expansive"],"a":["unsociable","gloomy","solitary","cold"],"ex":["Eid morning brought a convivial atmosphere to our home, with guests and sweets everywhere.","The restaurant owner is a convivial man who greets every customer by name.","We spent a convivial evening on the roof, sharing snacks and old stories."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"convoluted","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely complicated and difficult to follow, with many twists and turns.","lb":"complicated, twisted","s":["complicated","complex","intricate","tortuous","tangled","involved"],"k":["baroque","coiled","contorted","difficult"],"a":["simple","straightforward","clear","plain"],"ex":["The visa application process was so convoluted that I needed help to fill in the forms.","The movie's convoluted plot left me confused about who was working for whom.","He gave a convoluted explanation that took ten minutes and answered nothing."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"convolution","p":"noun","d":"A twist, coil or fold in something, or a very complicated part of a story or argument.","lb":"twist, coil","s":["twist","coil","curl","spiral","fold","loop"],"k":["contortion","furrow","gyre","meander"],"a":["simplicity"],"ex":["The river's lazy convolutions can be seen clearly from the window of the plane.","I could not follow the convolutions of the film's plot, with its many twists and flashbacks.","The surface of the human brain is covered with convolutions that increase its area."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"copious","p":"adjective","d":"Existing or produced in large amounts; plentiful.","lb":"abundant, plentiful","s":["abundant","plentiful","ample","profuse","generous","lavish"],"k":["bumper","liberal","lush","overflowing"],"a":["scanty","meager","sparse","scarce"],"ex":["She took copious notes during the lecture and shared them with the class.","The monsoon brought copious rain, and the ponds overflowed.","The cook added copious amounts of garlic to the curry."],"b":114,"y":1},{"w":"cordial","p":"adjective","d":"Warm, friendly and polite in the way someone speaks to or welcomes other people.","lb":"warm, friendly","s":["warm","friendly","affable","genial","amiable","hearty"],"k":["congenial","hospitable","kind","neighborly"],"a":["cold","hostile","unfriendly","frosty"],"ex":["The two neighbours kept cordial relations despite occasional arguments about the shared wall.","The hotel manager gave us a cordial welcome and a glass of cool juice.","Although the interview was formal, the interviewer's tone was cordial."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"corollary","p":"noun","d":"A natural result or effect of something, or a further fact that follows from another.","lb":"consequence, result","s":["consequence","result","effect","outcome","upshot","implication"],"k":["adjunct","appendage","complement","deduction"],"a":["cause","source","origin"],"ex":["Higher prices are a natural corollary of rising fuel costs.","More traffic is an unfortunate corollary of the city’s fast growth.","Stress and tiredness are often a corollary of staying up late before exams."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"corporeal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the physical body, or having a physical form that can be touched rather than being spiritual.","lb":"physical, bodily","s":["physical","bodily","material","tangible","corporal","concrete"],"k":["anatomical","earthly","embodied","incarnate"],"a":["spiritual","ethereal","immaterial","intangible"],"ex":["Ghosts in the story have no corporeal form, so they can pass through walls.","Hunger and thirst are corporeal needs that must be met before anything else.","Poets often write about the soul as separate from the corporeal body."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"correlate","p":"verb","d":"To have a mutual connection, so that a change in one thing goes with a change in the other.","lb":"relate, connect","s":["relate","connect","associate","link","tie in","match"],"k":["align","attach","covary","go hand in hand"],"a":[],"ex":["Studies show that hours of sleep correlate with exam performance.","Ice cream sales correlate with temperature, since people buy more in hot weather.","The village's rainfall records correlate closely with its crop yields year after year."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"correlation","p":"noun","d":"A connection between two things, where a change in one is linked with a change in the other.","lb":"relationship, link","s":["relationship","connection","link","association","correspondence","parallel"],"k":["bond","co-variation","concomitance","contact"],"a":["independence","randomness"],"ex":["Researchers found a strong correlation between hours of sleep and exam scores.","There is a clear correlation between rainfall and the price of vegetables.","The doctor explained that there is a correlation between high salt intake and high blood pressure."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"corroborate","p":"verb","d":"To give extra evidence or information that supports a statement or belief.","lb":"confirm, support","s":["confirm","support","verify","back up","substantiate","validate"],"k":["affirm","attest","bolster","document"],"a":["contradict","refute","disprove","dispute"],"ex":["A second witness corroborated her account of the accident.","The security camera footage corroborates his claim that he was at the shop.","Several studies corroborate the idea that sleep improves memory."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"corrosive","p":"adjective","d":"Slowly wearing away or destroying something, either by chemical action or by a steady harmful effect.","lb":"eroding, harmful","s":["caustic","acidic","harsh","destructive","damaging","eroding"],"k":["acerbic","biting","sarcastic","scathing"],"a":["soothing","protective","harmless","healing"],"ex":["Wear gloves when using this cleaner because it is corrosive and can burn your skin.","Salty sea air is highly corrosive and quickly rusts the metal railings along the Cox's Bazar seafront.","A leaking battery can release a corrosive liquid that damages the inside of your remote control."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"corrugated","p":"adjective","d":"Shaped into a series of parallel ridges and grooves, like waves, to make it stronger or more flexible.","lb":"ridged, grooved","s":["grooved","furrowed","rippled","channelled","creased","wrinkled"],"k":["crimped","pleated","ribbed","rugged"],"a":["smooth","flat","even","level"],"ex":["Many village houses have corrugated tin roofs that roar in heavy rain.","The parcel was packed in a corrugated cardboard box for extra strength.","The dirt road had become corrugated after months of heavy trucks, so the bus shook all the way."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cosmopolitan","p":"adjective","d":"Including people and influences from many parts of the world, and at ease in many cultures.","lb":"worldly, international","s":["worldly","international","global","sophisticated","multicultural","urbane"],"k":["comprehensive","cultivated","cultured","diverse"],"a":["provincial","parochial","insular","local"],"ex":["Dhaka's food scene has become more cosmopolitan, serving Thai, Italian and Korean dishes.","After years of working abroad, she had a cosmopolitan outlook and friends on every continent.","The university has a cosmopolitan student body, with classmates from over thirty countries."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"coterie","p":"noun","d":"A small, close group of people who share interests and keep outsiders away.","lb":"clique, circle","s":["clique","circle","set","inner circle","group","band"],"k":["brotherhood","camp","cell","confraternity"],"a":[],"ex":["At school, a coterie of senior students decided who could sit at the best table.","The manager relies on a coterie of advisers who rarely disagree with him.","A coterie of poets met every Friday at the tea stall near the university."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"council","p":"noun","d":"A group of people chosen to make decisions, give advice or manage the affairs of a town, school or organization.","lb":"committee, assembly","s":["committee","board","assembly","panel","cabinet","commission"],"k":["chamber","convocation","delegation","diet"],"a":[],"ex":["The city council voted to build a new playground near the river.","Our student council organizes the annual cultural program every winter.","The village council met under the banyan tree to settle the dispute."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"countenance","p":"verb","d":"To approve of or tolerate something, usually used in negative sentences.","lb":"tolerate, approve","s":["tolerate","approve","allow","permit","condone","accept"],"k":["abide","authorize","bear","brook"],"a":["forbid","reject","oppose","condemn"],"ex":["The school will not countenance bullying of any kind.","My father would never countenance lying, even about small things.","The landlord refused to countenance any delay in paying the rent."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"coup","p":"noun","d":"A sudden seizure of power from a government by force; also, a remarkable and unexpected success.","lb":"takeover, triumph","s":["takeover","overthrow","putsch","revolt","uprising","triumph"],"k":["group action","insurrection","rebellion","scoop"],"a":["failure","fiasco","blunder","defeat"],"ex":["Rebel officers seized the airport and the radio station in a sudden coup.","News of the coup spread quickly, and shops closed early as people rushed home.","Landing the biggest client in the region was a real coup for the small design firm."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"covenant","p":"noun","d":"A formal, serious agreement or promise between two or more people or groups.","lb":"agreement, pledge","s":["agreement","pact","contract","treaty","pledge","compact"],"k":["accord","arrangement","charter","deal"],"a":[],"ex":["The two villages signed a covenant promising to share the river water fairly in the dry months.","Their marriage was a covenant, and both partners promised to support each other in good times and bad.","Residents signed a covenant that forbids building anything above three floors on the street."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"covert","p":"adjective","d":"Secret or hidden, and not openly shown or admitted.","lb":"secret, hidden","s":["secret","hidden","concealed","clandestine","undercover","furtive"],"k":["backstairs","black","cloaked","confidential"],"a":["overt","open","public","obvious"],"ex":["He took a covert look at his phone during the meeting.","The police ran a covert operation to catch the gang that sold fake medicines.","There was a covert agreement among the friends to surprise their teacher with a cake."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"covet","p":"verb","d":"To strongly want something, especially something that belongs to someone else.","lb":"crave, envy","s":["crave","desire","envy","long for","yearn for","lust after"],"k":["aspire to","eye","hunger","hunger for"],"a":["spurn","scorn","reject","shun"],"ex":["He openly coveted his friend's new bicycle and kept asking to borrow it.","She coveted her cousin's long hair and always asked how she took care of it.","Every young footballer in the academy covets the captain's armband and the respect it brings."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cower","p":"verb","d":"To bend low or move back in fear, especially because of a threat or a loud noise.","lb":"cringe, shrink","s":["cringe","flinch","shrink","quail","recoil","crouch"],"k":["bend","blench","bow","crawl"],"a":["confront","stand up","face","defy"],"ex":["The puppy cowered under the bed during the thunderstorm.","She refused to cower before the bully and told the teacher what had happened.","Passengers cowered in their seats when the plane shook in the storm."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"crass","p":"adjective","d":"Showing a lack of sensitivity, taste or good judgement; rude and thoughtless.","lb":"tasteless, insensitive","s":["insensitive","tasteless","boorish","coarse","vulgar","crude"],"k":["brutish","callous","clumsy","common"],"a":["refined","tactful","sensitive","polite"],"ex":["It was crass to boast about his salary in front of friends who had just lost their jobs.","Her crass joke about the waiter's mistake embarrassed everyone at the table.","The advertisement was criticised as crass for using a flood disaster to sell shoes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"craven","p":"adjective","d":"Completely lacking in courage; shamefully cowardly.","lb":"cowardly, timid","s":["cowardly","fearful","spineless","timid","pusillanimous","gutless"],"k":["chicken","dastardly","lily-livered","recreant"],"a":["brave","courageous","bold","fearless"],"ex":["It was craven of him to blame his friend instead of admitting his own mistake.","The craven guard ran away at the first sign of trouble.","She felt craven for staying silent while her classmate was being teased."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"credulous","p":"adjective","d":"Too ready to believe things without enough proof, and therefore easily fooled.","lb":"gullible, trusting","s":["gullible","naive","trusting","unsuspecting","easily fooled","green"],"k":["confiding","credible","easy mark","impressionable"],"a":["skeptical","suspicious","wary","doubtful"],"ex":["Credulous shoppers believed the ad and paid for a cream that promised to make them taller.","My credulous aunt forwards every unchecked message about miracle cures.","The credulous tourist bought a fake gemstone from a street seller."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"creep","p":"verb","d":"To move slowly and quietly, often low to the ground or so that nobody notices.","lb":"crawl, sneak","s":["crawl","sneak","tiptoe","steal","slink","inch"],"k":["cringe","fawn","go","move"],"a":["rush","dash","stride","charge"],"ex":["The cat crept slowly towards the bird, keeping its body close to the ground.","I crept into the room so that I would not wake the baby.","Traffic crept forward at walking speed along the flooded road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"crescendo","p":"noun","d":"A gradual increase in loudness or intensity, or the peak that it builds up to.","lb":"build-up, climax","s":["climax","peak","rise","swell","height","culmination"],"k":["apex","eruption","escalation","high point"],"a":["decline","fade","lull","decrease"],"ex":["The orchestra's music rose to a crescendo, and the audience held its breath.","The noise from the crowd built to a crescendo as the batsman walked toward the crease.","Her complaints grew to a crescendo until the manager finally listened."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"crestfallen","p":"adjective","d":"Sad and disappointed because of a failure or something that went wrong.","lb":"dejected, disappointed","s":["dejected","disappointed","downcast","deflated","despondent","glum"],"k":["chapfallen","depressed","disconsolate","downhearted"],"a":["elated","jubilant","delighted","triumphant"],"ex":["He looked crestfallen when he saw that his name was not on the list.","The children were crestfallen when the picnic was canceled because of rain.","She returned from the interview crestfallen, sure that she had not got the job."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"crevice","p":"noun","d":"A narrow crack or opening in a rock, wall or other surface.","lb":"crack, fissure","s":["crack","fissure","cleft","gap","split","chink"],"k":["breach","chap","groove","hole"],"a":[],"ex":["A small plant grew in a crevice between the bricks.","The climber wedged her fingers into a narrow crevice in the cliff.","Cockroaches hide in the crevices behind the kitchen cabinets."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cringe","p":"verb","d":"To move back or crouch down in fear, pain or disgust, often because you feel threatened.","lb":"cower, flinch","s":["cower","flinch","recoil","shrink","quail","wince"],"k":["crawl","creep","fawn","funk"],"a":["confront","face","defy","stand firm"],"ex":["The puppy cringed in the corner whenever it heard the loud thunder.","Nadia cringed when the dentist picked up the drill.","The workers cringed before their angry boss, too afraid to say a word."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"crisp","p":"adjective","d":"Firm, dry and easy to break, especially food that makes a sharp sound when you bite it.","lb":"firm, crunchy","s":["crunchy","crispy","brittle","firm","fresh","dry"],"k":["cold","concise","curly","curt"],"a":["soft","soggy","limp","stale"],"ex":["Fresh samosas from the stall are crisp outside and soft inside.","Keep the lettuce in the fridge so that it stays crisp.","The chips lost their crisp texture after sitting out in the humid air."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"criterion","p":"noun","d":"A standard or rule used for judging or deciding something.","lb":"standard, benchmark","s":["standard","benchmark","yardstick","measure","test","norm"],"k":["basis","metric","model","precept"],"a":[],"ex":["The main criterion for the scholarship is high marks in the final exam.","Price is not the only criterion when choosing a good phone.","Applicants must meet several criteria, including age and experience."],"b":272,"y":0},{"w":"critic","p":"noun","d":"A person who gives opinions about the quality of something, such as a film, a book or a policy.","lb":"reviewer, fault-finder","s":["reviewer","commentator","judge","analyst","pundit","expert"],"k":["authority","carper","dissenter","knocker"],"a":["admirer","supporter","fan","advocate"],"ex":["The film critic gave the new movie four stars in the weekend paper.","Critics of the plan say it will cost too much.","My brother is his own harshest critic and rewrites every essay three times."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"critical","p":"adjective","d":"Expressing disapproval by pointing out what is wrong or bad about someone or something.","lb":"fault-finding, disapproving","s":["disapproving","disparaging","judgmental","scathing","carping","negative"],"k":["acute","appraising","crucial","dangerous"],"a":["complimentary","approving","praising","appreciative"],"ex":["The review was highly critical of the film's long and confusing ending.","My manager is critical of work that arrives even a few minutes late.","Don't be so critical of yourself; you did your best."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"critique","p":"noun","d":"A detailed written or spoken evaluation of a piece of work, an idea or a performance.","lb":"review, evaluation","s":["review","analysis","assessment","evaluation","appraisal","commentary"],"k":["assay","dissection","exegesis","explication"],"a":[],"ex":["The teacher gave a thoughtful critique of each student's essay.","In her critique of the film, the reviewer praised the acting but disliked the plot.","Before the final submission, ask a friend for a critique of your design."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"crooked","p":"adjective","d":"Not straight; bent, twisted or not properly lined up.","lb":"bent, twisted","s":["bent","twisted","curved","winding","askew","lopsided"],"k":["akimbo","asymmetrical","cockeyed","coiled"],"a":["straight","upright","aligned","even"],"ex":["The picture on the wall is crooked, so please straighten it.","A crooked path led through the rice fields to the river.","He drew a crooked line because his ruler slipped."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"croquet","p":"noun","d":"A lawn game in which players hit wooden balls through small hoops using long-handled mallets.","lb":"lawn game","s":[],"k":["bocce","boules","bowls","lawn bowls"],"a":[],"ex":["On Sunday afternoons, the family played croquet on the lawn behind the old house.","In croquet, you score points by hitting your ball through the hoops in order.","She won the croquet game by knocking her cousin's ball far away from the last hoop."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"crux","p":"noun","d":"The most important or most difficult part of a problem or issue.","lb":"heart, essence","s":["heart","core","essence","nub","gist","kernel"],"k":["bottom line","center","focal point","heart and soul"],"a":["periphery","side issue","trivia"],"ex":["The crux of the problem is that we have too many tasks and too little time.","After an hour of debate, we finally got to the crux of the issue.","The crux of her argument was that cheaper fares would bring more visitors."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"cryptic","p":"adjective","d":"Having a hidden or unclear meaning that is hard to understand.","lb":"mysterious, puzzling","s":["mysterious","puzzling","enigmatic","obscure","baffling","mystifying"],"k":["cabalistic","concise","confusing","deep"],"a":["clear","plain","obvious","straightforward"],"ex":["She left a cryptic note on the fridge that read only, \"Look behind the clock.\"","The teacher's cryptic comment on my essay was just \"Think again,\" and I had no idea what to change.","My uncle gave a cryptic smile and refused to tell us about the surprise."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cue","p":"noun","d":"A signal, such as a word or action, that tells someone when to start doing something.","lb":"signal, prompt","s":["signal","prompt","reminder","hint","sign","nod"],"k":["beat","clue","lead","pointer"],"a":[],"ex":["When the lights dimmed, that was our cue to walk onto the stage.","The drummer waited for the singer's nod as his cue to start.","Take your cue from the teacher, and stand up when she does."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"cuisine","p":"noun","d":"A particular style of cooking, especially one that belongs to a country, region or restaurant.","lb":"cooking style, food","s":["cooking","cookery","food","fare","dishes","gastronomy"],"k":["culinary art","culinary tradition","food culture","kitchen tradition"],"a":[],"ex":["Bengali cuisine is famous for its fish dishes, sweets and rich use of mustard.","We tried Thai cuisine for the first time and loved the spicy soup.","The hotel restaurant serves local cuisine alongside international dishes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"culinary","p":"adjective","d":"Connected with cooking, food preparation or the kitchen.","lb":"cooking, kitchen","s":["cooking","kitchen","food"],"k":["alimentary","cookery","dietary","dining"],"a":[],"ex":["She joined a culinary school to learn how to bake bread and cakes.","Sylhet is known for its culinary use of shatkora, a tangy citrus fruit added to curries.","My uncle's culinary skills are limited to boiling eggs and making instant noodles."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"cull","p":"verb","d":"To choose or collect something, such as information or items, from a larger group.","lb":"select, gather","s":["select","choose","gather","pick","glean","collect"],"k":["catch","decide on","dig up","discover"],"a":["reject","discard","scatter"],"ex":["The editor culled the best quotes from hours of interviews.","I culled a few useful tips from many online videos.","The teacher culled ten problems from the textbook for the class test."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"culminate","p":"verb","d":"To reach a final, highest or most important point after a long process.","lb":"climax, end","s":["climax","end","peak","conclude","finish","result"],"k":["cease","close","crown","end up"],"a":["begin","start","open","launch"],"ex":["Years of hard training culminated in a gold medal for the young swimmer.","The long argument culminated in a quarrel that ended their friendship.","The festival culminates with a fireworks show on the final night."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"culpable","p":"adjective","d":"Deserving blame for something wrong that has happened.","lb":"guilty, blameworthy","s":["guilty","at fault","responsible","to blame","liable","answerable"],"k":["accountable","errant","remiss","reprehensible"],"a":["innocent","blameless","guiltless"],"ex":["The investigation found the builder culpable for ignoring the safety rules.","Drivers who use their phones at the wheel are culpable when accidents happen.","The factory owner was held culpable for polluting the canal."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"curb","p":"verb","d":"To control or limit something that is harmful or that you do not want to increase.","lb":"restrain, limit","s":["restrain","control","limit","check","restrict","hold back"],"k":["curtail","cut back","hold","hold in"],"a":["encourage","boost","unleash","free"],"ex":["The city introduced new rules to curb air pollution.","You should curb your spending until you find a steady job.","The school's strict phone policy aims to curb cheating during exams."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"curious","p":"adjective","d":"Eager to know or learn about something.","lb":"interested, eager","s":["inquisitive","interested","inquiring","questioning","keen","nosy"],"k":["enthusiastic","funny","nosey","odd"],"a":["uninterested","indifferent","apathetic","bored"],"ex":["I was curious about the strange box on the table, so I opened it.","Children are naturally curious and love to explore new places.","She was curious to know how her classmates had done in the test."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"curmudgeon","p":"noun","d":"A bad-tempered, difficult person, often an older one, who complains a lot.","lb":"grouch, crank","s":["grouch","crank","grump","sourpuss","killjoy","crab"],"k":["churl","crosspatch","grumbler","malcontent"],"a":["optimist","charmer"],"ex":["Our neighbor is a curmudgeon who complains whenever children play cricket in the lane.","Behind the old curmudgeon's gruff manner was a man who secretly paid for a poor student's books.","My grandfather can be a curmudgeon in the morning, but after his tea he becomes friendly."],"b":100,"y":1},{"w":"cursory","p":"adjective","d":"Done quickly, without attention to detail, and therefore not thorough.","lb":"hasty, superficial","s":["hasty","superficial","perfunctory","quick","brief","casual"],"k":["careless","desultory","fast","glancing"],"a":["thorough","careful","detailed","meticulous"],"ex":["The guard gave my bag only a cursory glance and waved me through the gate.","A cursory reading of the contract missed the clause about extra fees.","The mechanic’s cursory check did not find the real problem with the engine."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"curtail","p":"verb","d":"To reduce or limit something, or to end it earlier than planned.","lb":"cut short, reduce","s":["cut","reduce","shorten","limit","restrict","trim"],"k":["abridge","circumscribe","clip","confine to"],"a":["extend","prolong","lengthen","expand"],"ex":["The heavy rain forced the organizers to curtail the outdoor concert by an hour.","We had to curtail our holiday when my father suddenly fell ill.","The company plans to curtail spending on travel until sales improve."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"customary","p":"adjective","d":"Done or used by most people in a place or situation because of habit or tradition.","lb":"usual, traditional","s":["usual","traditional","habitual","conventional","normal","accepted"],"k":["accustomed","everyday","ordinary","prevailing"],"a":["unusual","unconventional","rare","exceptional"],"ex":["It is customary to remove your shoes before entering a Bangladeshi home.","The manager gave the customary speech at the end-of-year dinner.","Tipping the driver is customary in many cities, but not everywhere."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"cynic","p":"noun","d":"A person who believes people are mostly selfish and dishonest, and doubts that anyone acts for good reasons.","lb":"skeptic, pessimist","s":["skeptic","pessimist","naysayer","misanthrope","defeatist"],"k":["disagreeable person","doubting thomas","killjoy","mocker"],"a":["optimist","idealist","believer","romantic"],"ex":["Only a cynic would believe that nobody ever helps a stranger without wanting something back.","My uncle is a cynic who says every advertisement hides a trick.","After many disappointments, he turned into a cynic who trusted no one's promises."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"dais","p":"noun","d":"A raised platform at the front of a hall, where speakers or important guests stand or sit.","lb":"platform, stage","s":["platform","stage","podium","rostrum","stand","riser"],"k":["bandstand","estrade","level","perch"],"a":[],"ex":["The chief guest walked up onto the dais and waved to the cheering crowd.","At the graduation ceremony, the principal stood on the dais and handed out the certificates.","The bride and groom sat on a flower-covered dais while relatives took photos."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dart","p":"verb","d":"To move suddenly and very quickly in a particular direction.","lb":"dash, rush","s":["dash","rush","bolt","race","shoot","sprint"],"k":["belt along","buck","bucket along","cannonball along"],"a":["crawl","amble","dawdle","stroll"],"ex":["A small boy darted across the road without looking, and the driver braked hard.","The fish darted away when I put my hand in the pond.","She darted into the shop to escape the sudden rain."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"daunt","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel afraid or less confident about doing something difficult.","lb":"discourage, intimidate","s":["discourage","intimidate","deter","dismay","unnerve","frighten"],"k":["cow","dash","dissuade","faze"],"a":["encourage","inspire","embolden","reassure"],"ex":["The long syllabus did not daunt Mina; she made a study plan and started that evening.","A steep hill daunts many new cyclists, but the view at the top is worth the effort.","Do not let one failed attempt daunt you; most drivers need to take the test twice."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"dazzled","p":"adjective","d":"Unable to see clearly for a moment because of a very bright light.","lb":"blinded, amazed","s":["blinded","bedazzled","stunned","overwhelmed","bewildered"],"k":["blind","confused","dazed","disoriented"],"a":[],"ex":["Dazzled by the headlights, the driver slowed down and held up his hand.","I was dazzled by the sun on the water and could not see the boat.","The dazzled child blinked for a minute after the camera flash."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dazzling","p":"adjective","d":"So bright or impressive that it is hard to look at or hard to stop admiring.","lb":"brilliant, stunning","s":["brilliant","stunning","blinding","glittering","spectacular","sparkling"],"k":["arresting","blazing","breathtaking","bright"],"a":["dull","dim","drab","ordinary"],"ex":["The dazzling sunlight on the water forced me to put on my sunglasses.","She wore a dazzling smile when she received the gold medal.","The fireworks put on a dazzling display above the river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"de facto","p":"adjective","d":"Existing or happening in reality, even if not officially or legally recognized.","lb":"actual, in practice","s":["actual","real","effective","practical","existing","virtual"],"k":["authentic","concrete","existent","factual"],"a":["official","legal","legitimate","nominal"],"ex":["Although Nadia has no official title, she is the de facto manager of the small shop.","English has become the de facto language of international business, even though no law says so.","The rule was never written down, but it became the de facto standard in our office."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"de rigueur","p":"adjective","d":"Required by fashion, custom or good manners, so that people feel they must do it.","lb":"required, expected","s":["obligatory","required","essential","mandatory","expected","necessary"],"k":["a must","in vogue","must-have","needed"],"a":["optional","unnecessary","unfashionable","voluntary"],"ex":["At that formal dinner, a suit and tie are de rigueur for every guest.","A new outfit is de rigueur for Eid, and the shops are packed for weeks beforehand.","In some offices, checking emails constantly is de rigueur, even outside working hours."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"dearness","p":"noun","d":"The quality of costing a lot of money; being expensive.","lb":"high price, expense","s":["high cost","high price","exorbitance","costliness","expensiveness"],"k":["overpricing","preciousness","premium","price tag"],"a":["low price","reasonableness"],"ex":["Many families complain about the dearness of rice, oil and onions in the market.","The dearness of city rents forces students to share small rooms.","Because of the dearness of fresh fruit in winter, we mostly eat bananas."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dearth","p":"noun","d":"A lack or shortage of something that is needed.","lb":"scarcity, shortage","s":["shortage","scarcity","lack","deficiency","paucity","want"],"k":["depletion","drought","famine","privation"],"a":["abundance","plenty","surplus","glut"],"ex":["There is a dearth of good public libraries in our town.","A dearth of rainfall this year has hurt the farmers' harvest.","The company faces a dearth of skilled workers who can repair the machines."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"debacle","p":"noun","d":"A sudden and complete failure or disaster that causes embarrassment.","lb":"fiasco, disaster","s":["disaster","fiasco","catastrophe","collapse","failure","rout"],"k":["bomb","botch","cataclysm","dud"],"a":["triumph","success","victory","win"],"ex":["The school concert turned into a debacle when the microphones failed and the lights went out.","Our team's six-goal loss was a complete debacle from the first minute.","The product launch was a debacle, with the website crashing on the very first day."],"b":88,"y":1},{"w":"debase","p":"verb","d":"To lower the quality, value or moral standing of something.","lb":"degrade, cheapen","s":["degrade","cheapen","devalue","demean","lower","corrupt"],"k":["belittle","demoralize","dilute","disgrace"],"a":["elevate","raise","enhance","improve"],"ex":["Printing too much money can debase a country's currency.","Constant cheating debases the value of a degree.","He refused to debase himself by begging for favors."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"debauchery","p":"noun","d":"Excessive indulgence in drinking, partying and other harmful pleasures.","lb":"dissipation, excess","s":["dissipation","depravity","decadence","excess","indulgence","licentiousness"],"k":["bacchanal","bacchanalia","binge","carousing"],"a":["restraint","temperance","moderation","virtue"],"ex":["The novel describes a rich young man's slide from comfort into a life of debauchery.","He wasted his inheritance on debauchery, endless parties and expensive cars.","Years of debauchery left the former star broke and in poor health."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"debilitate","p":"verb","d":"To make someone or something physically or mentally weak.","lb":"weaken, drain","s":["weaken","sap","exhaust","cripple","undermine","incapacitate"],"k":["deplete","erode","knock out","paralyze"],"a":["strengthen","invigorate","energize","fortify"],"ex":["A severe bout of dengue fever can debilitate a healthy adult for several weeks.","Constant worry about money can debilitate even the strongest person.","The long drought debilitated the local economy, and many farms closed."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"debt","p":"noun","d":"An amount of money that you owe to someone.","lb":"money owed, liability","s":["liability","obligation","arrears","dues","bill","loan"],"k":["borrowings","encumbrance","financial obligation","indebtedness"],"a":["credit","savings","asset","surplus"],"ex":["He took a second job to pay off his debt before the end of the year.","Many students leave university with a large debt from education loans.","The farmer fell into debt after the flood destroyed his harvest."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"debunk","p":"verb","d":"To show that a belief, claim or story is false or exaggerated.","lb":"disprove, expose","s":["disprove","expose","refute","discredit","explode","deflate"],"k":["blackguard","invalidate","jest at","laugh at"],"a":["prove","confirm","verify","validate"],"ex":["A science teacher debunked the myth that we use only ten percent of our brains.","Fact-checkers quickly debunked the viral message about a free phone.","The video debunks the rumor that mixing certain foods is dangerous."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"decadent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing a fall in moral standards, or enjoying luxury and pleasure in an excessive way.","lb":"self-indulgent, declining","s":["hedonistic","luxurious","dissolute","debauched","corrupt","degenerate"],"k":["depraved","dissipated","immoral","licentious"],"a":["austere","virtuous","ascetic","moral"],"ex":["The decadent dessert came with three layers of chocolate, cream and caramel.","Historians say the empire grew decadent and careless just before it collapsed.","After winning the lottery, he lived a decadent life of expensive dinners and endless parties."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"decay","p":"noun","d":"The slow process of rotting, breaking down or getting worse in quality or condition.","lb":"rot, deterioration","s":["rot","rotting","decomposition","deterioration","decline","disintegration"],"k":["atrophy","breakdown","decrepitude","degeneration"],"a":["growth","flourishing","improvement","development"],"ex":["Eating too many sweets and not brushing can cause tooth decay.","The old mansion had fallen into decay, with broken windows and cracked walls.","Fallen leaves in the forest slowly turn into soil through decay."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"deceitful","p":"adjective","d":"Dishonest and likely to trick or mislead other people.","lb":"dishonest, lying","s":["dishonest","deceptive","lying","treacherous","fraudulent","underhanded"],"k":["ambidextrous","corrupt","crooked","dishonorable"],"a":["honest","truthful","sincere","trustworthy"],"ex":["The deceitful seller hid the cracks in the phone and sold it at full price.","Don't trust deceitful advertisements that promise to make you rich in a week.","I felt betrayed when I discovered that my friend had been deceitful about where he was."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"decelerate","p":"verb","d":"To reduce speed, or to make a vehicle or process move more slowly.","lb":"slow down","s":["slow down","brake","slacken","ease off","retard","reduce speed"],"k":["coast","decrease","diminish","downshift"],"a":["accelerate","speed up","quicken","hasten"],"ex":["Drivers should decelerate near schools, because children may run into the road.","The train began to decelerate as it approached the station platform.","The economy is expected to decelerate next year as prices rise."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"decimate","p":"verb","d":"To destroy or kill a very large part of something.","lb":"devastate, wipe out","s":["devastate","ravage","wipe out","destroy","annihilate","gut"],"k":["carry off","desolate","eliminate","eradicate"],"a":["restore","rebuild","revive","protect"],"ex":["A sudden disease decimated the chicken farms in the district, and prices rose sharply.","Floods decimated the rice crop, leaving many farmers without income for the year.","Online shopping has decimated small bookshops in many towns."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"decipher","p":"verb","d":"To work out the meaning of something that is hard to read or understand.","lb":"decode, interpret","s":["decode","interpret","make out","crack","translate","unravel"],"k":["construe","decrypt","deduce","divine"],"a":["encode","encrypt","scramble","obscure"],"ex":["I could barely decipher the doctor's handwriting on the prescription.","Experts worked for weeks to decipher the faded writing on the old letter.","It took me ten minutes to decipher a text message full of strange abbreviations."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"decomposition","p":"noun","d":"The process by which dead plants, animals or other material rot and break down into simpler parts.","lb":"rotting, breakdown","s":["decay","rot","rotting","putrefaction","breakdown","disintegration"],"k":["biodegradation","composting","dissolution","fermentation"],"a":["growth","preservation","formation","synthesis"],"ex":["Warm, wet weather speeds up the decomposition of leaves on the forest floor.","Farmers mix kitchen waste into the soil so that decomposition can feed the crops.","The smell from the bin showed that decomposition of the food had already begun."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"decontaminate","p":"verb","d":"To remove dangerous substances or germs from a place, object or person.","lb":"clean, purify","s":["purify","disinfect","sterilize","cleanse","sanitize","clean"],"k":["bleach","delouse","distill","fumigate"],"a":["contaminate","pollute","infect","poison"],"ex":["Workers in protective suits decontaminated the lab after the chemical spill.","Hospitals must decontaminate surgical tools before every operation.","The team used special filters to decontaminate the well water in the flooded village."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"decorous","p":"adjective","d":"Polite and proper in behavior, in a way that follows good manners and good taste.","lb":"proper, polite","s":["proper","polite","seemly","dignified","correct","mannerly"],"k":["becoming","civil","comely","considerate"],"a":["rude","improper","unseemly","unruly"],"ex":["The guests were quiet and decorous at the formal dinner.","Students were expected to be decorous during the graduation ceremony.","She gave a decorous nod to the elderly neighbors and walked on."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"decorum","p":"noun","d":"Polite, respectful and proper behavior in a formal or serious situation.","lb":"propriety, etiquette","s":["propriety","etiquette","politeness","good manners","dignity","respectability"],"k":["composure","courtliness","formality","gravity"],"a":["rudeness","impropriety","vulgarity","disorder"],"ex":["The principal asked students to behave with decorum while the guests were visiting the school.","Even when the debate became heated, the speakers kept their decorum.","Good decorum in the library means speaking softly and keeping your phone silent."],"b":65,"y":1},{"w":"decree","p":"noun","d":"An official order, usually from a ruler or government, that has the force of law.","lb":"order, edict","s":["edict","order","command","ruling","proclamation","mandate"],"k":["fiat","injunction","instruction","regulation"],"a":[],"ex":["In the story, the king issued a decree ordering all villagers to pay a new tax.","The court's decree ended the long dispute over the land.","By government decree, schools were closed for a week because of the extreme heat."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"decry","p":"verb","d":"To publicly say that something is bad, wrong or harmful.","lb":"denounce, condemn","s":["denounce","condemn","censure","deplore","blame","slam"],"k":["bash","berate","castigate","criticize"],"a":["praise","applaud","commend","extol"],"ex":["Doctors decried the sale of strong medicines without a prescription as dangerous.","Residents decried the dumping of waste near the school as a health risk.","The newspaper decried the high cost of textbooks, saying many families could not afford them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deduce","p":"verb","d":"To reach a conclusion about something by thinking carefully about the facts you already know.","lb":"infer, conclude","s":["infer","conclude","gather","reason","work out","figure out"],"k":["assume","discern","divine","extrapolate"],"a":[],"ex":["From the muddy shoes by the door, I deduced that my brother had played football in the rain.","Detectives deduced from the broken window and the open safe that the thief knew the house.","You can often deduce the meaning of a new word from the sentences around it."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"deem","p":"verb","d":"To judge or consider something to be of a particular kind or quality.","lb":"consider, judge","s":["consider","judge","regard","think","hold","believe"],"k":["adjudge","appraise","assess","count"],"a":[],"ex":["The school deemed the old building unsafe and closed it.","The committee will deem your application complete only after all the documents arrive.","Doctors deemed him fit to travel after a week of rest."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"defame","p":"verb","d":"To damage a person’s good reputation by saying or writing false things about them.","lb":"slander, smear","s":["slander","libel","smear","malign","vilify","disparage"],"k":["accuse","bad-mouth","blacken","impugn"],"a":["praise","honor","defend","commend"],"ex":["The newspaper was sued for trying to defame a local doctor with false stories.","Posting lies online to defame a classmate can lead to serious trouble.","She felt that the rumor was meant to defame her and ruin her chance at the job."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"default","p":"noun","d":"Failure to do something that you are required to do, especially to pay back a loan.","lb":"failure, nonpayment","s":["failure","nonpayment","neglect","omission","lapse","dereliction"],"k":["arrears","bankruptcy","breach","breach of contract"],"a":["payment","fulfillment","compliance","performance"],"ex":["The company went into default when it could no longer repay its loan to the bank.","The player lost the match by default because he did not appear on court.","Many borrowers fall into default when interest rates rise suddenly."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"deference","p":"noun","d":"Polite respect for someone's opinion, wishes or authority, shown by giving way to them.","lb":"respect, submission","s":["respect","regard","courtesy","submission","obedience","esteem"],"k":["acquiescence","admiration","civility","compliance"],"a":["disrespect","contempt","defiance","insolence"],"ex":["In deference to the elders, the young people stood up and offered their seats.","He spoke with deference to the professor, never interrupting her answers.","Out of deference to her grandmother's wishes, she wore a traditional saree to the wedding."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"defiance","p":"noun","d":"Open refusal to obey a rule or a person, showing no fear of the consequences.","lb":"disobedience, resistance","s":["disobedience","resistance","rebellion","insubordination","opposition","challenge"],"k":["audacity","bravado","impudence","insolence"],"a":["obedience","compliance","submission","deference"],"ex":["In defiance of the doctor's advice, he went back to work the next day.","The teenager's silence was a quiet act of defiance against his strict father.","Some drivers park in defiance of the clear no-parking signs."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"defiant","p":"adjective","d":"Refusing openly to obey someone or something, often in a bold or proud way.","lb":"rebellious, resisting","s":["rebellious","disobedient","insubordinate","resistant","bold","challenging"],"k":["contrary","contumacious","difficult","fearless"],"a":["obedient","submissive","compliant","meek"],"ex":["The defiant teenager refused to turn off the music, even after three warnings.","She gave a defiant smile and walked out of the meeting.","Despite the heavy rain, the defiant fans kept singing in the stadium."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"deficient","p":"adjective","d":"Not having enough of something that is necessary; below the required level.","lb":"lacking, inadequate","s":["inadequate","lacking","insufficient","short","scanty","wanting"],"k":["absent","depleted","inferior","jejune"],"a":["sufficient","adequate","ample","abundant"],"ex":["The doctor said my diet was deficient in iron and advised me to eat more spinach.","Soil that is deficient in nutrients will produce a poor harvest.","The school's science lab is deficient in basic equipment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"deficit","p":"noun","d":"The amount by which money, or something else needed, is less than what is required or expected.","lb":"shortfall, shortage","s":["shortfall","shortage","deficiency","gap","lack","loss"],"k":["budget gap","dearth","debt","inadequacy"],"a":["surplus","excess","profit","surfeit"],"ex":["The shop ran a deficit last month because of repair costs and low sales.","The country's trade deficit grew as imports became more expensive.","Our club has a small deficit, so we must raise money before the trip."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"defile","p":"verb","d":"To make something dirty, impure or no longer sacred or respected.","lb":"pollute, desecrate","s":["pollute","contaminate","desecrate","dirty","soil","taint"],"k":["deflower","foul","impair","mar"],"a":["purify","cleanse","sanctify","honor"],"ex":["Factories that dump waste into the river defile the water that villagers drink.","Vandals defiled the war memorial by spraying paint across its walls.","He felt that cheap advertising would defile the name of his grandfather's old shop."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"definitive","p":"adjective","d":"Final and complete, and accepted as the best or most reliable of its kind.","lb":"conclusive, authoritative","s":["conclusive","final","authoritative","decisive","ultimate","complete"],"k":["canonical","eventual","exemplary","explicit"],"a":["tentative","provisional","inconclusive","uncertain"],"ex":["The doctor could not give a definitive answer until the test results arrived.","This book is the definitive guide to Bengali cooking.","The final match was definitive proof that the young team was the best in the league."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"deft","p":"adjective","d":"Quick, skillful and neat in the way you move your hands or handle a situation.","lb":"skillful, nimble","s":["skillful","adroit","nimble","dexterous","agile","adept"],"k":["delicate","dextrous","light-fingered","lively"],"a":["clumsy","awkward","inept","bungling"],"ex":["With a deft movement, the tailor threaded the needle on the first try.","The goalkeeper made a deft save just before the final whistle.","She handled the angry customer with a deft mix of patience and humor."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"defunct","p":"adjective","d":"No longer existing, working or in use.","lb":"obsolete, dead","s":["obsolete","extinct","dead","inoperative","expired","out of use"],"k":["archaic","bankrupt","discontinued","dissolved"],"a":["active","functioning","operating","alive"],"ex":["The defunct factory on the river bank is now home to birds and stray dogs.","I tried to open the website, but it is defunct and shows only an error page.","That law is defunct; nobody has enforced it for fifty years."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"degenerate","p":"verb","d":"To become worse in quality, condition or behavior.","lb":"deteriorate, decline","s":["deteriorate","decline","decay","worsen","regress","sink"],"k":["corrupt","crumble","debase","decrease"],"a":["improve","advance","progress","flourish"],"ex":["The friendly discussion degenerated into a shouting match about who was to blame.","Without regular exercise, muscles slowly degenerate with age.","The old building degenerated into a ruin after nobody repaired it for twenty years."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"degeneration","p":"noun","d":"A gradual decline to a worse physical, mental or moral condition.","lb":"decline, deterioration","s":["decline","deterioration","decay","decadence","worsening","regression"],"k":["debasement","decline in quality","decomposition","dilapidation"],"a":["improvement","progress","regeneration","recovery"],"ex":["Doctors say the old man's eyesight problem is caused by slow degeneration of the retina.","Some teachers worry about the degeneration of reading habits among teenagers.","Without exercise, muscle degeneration begins surprisingly quickly in elderly patients."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"degrade","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone in a way that takes away their dignity and self-respect.","lb":"demean, humiliate","s":["demean","humiliate","debase","disgrace","shame","belittle"],"k":["abase","adulterate","brutalize","dehumanize"],"a":["elevate","honour","dignify","uplift"],"ex":["No job should degrade a person; honest work deserves respect.","She refused to degrade herself by begging for forgiveness.","Online bullies try to degrade others by mocking their looks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deign","p":"verb","d":"To do something that you think is below your dignity, as if you are doing a favor.","lb":"condescend, stoop","s":["condescend","stoop","lower oneself","consent","see fit","bother"],"k":["accede","act","bring oneself","descend"],"a":["refuse","decline","scorn","disdain"],"ex":["The rude customer did not even deign to look at the waiter when ordering.","He never deigns to reply to messages from his junior colleagues.","The famous author finally deigned to sign a few books for the waiting fans."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deity","p":"noun","d":"A god or goddess.","lb":"god, divinity","s":["god","goddess","divinity","immortal","godhead","supreme being"],"k":["angel","avatar","demigod","guardian spirit"],"a":[],"ex":["In ancient Greece, Athena was the deity of wisdom and craft.","The museum has a stone carving of a deity from a thousand years ago.","Each village in the story worshipped its own deity of rain or harvest."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dejected","p":"adjective","d":"Sad and discouraged, usually because you have failed or been disappointed.","lb":"downhearted, depressed","s":["downhearted","depressed","discouraged","despondent","downcast","glum"],"k":["blue","deflated","distressed","down in the mouth"],"a":["cheerful","elated","encouraged","optimistic"],"ex":["He walked home dejected after failing the driving test.","The dejected players sat quietly in the dressing room after the final.","Nadia felt dejected when her application was rejected."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"delectable","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely pleasant to taste or smell; delicious.","lb":"delicious, tasty","s":["delicious","tasty","scrumptious","appetizing","luscious","palatable"],"k":["aromatic","dainty","desirable","heavenly"],"a":["disgusting","tasteless","unappetizing","revolting"],"ex":["Her delectable biryani filled the whole house with the smell of saffron and spices.","The bakery's window was full of delectable cakes and pastries.","At iftar, the table was covered with delectable fried snacks and fresh fruit."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"delegate","p":"verb","d":"To give part of your work, power or responsibility to someone else.","lb":"assign, entrust","s":["assign","entrust","hand over","pass on","allocate","devolve"],"k":["allot","authorize","consign","designate"],"a":["keep","retain","take on","hold on to"],"ex":["A good manager knows when to delegate tasks instead of doing everything personally.","The principal delegated the organisation of sports day to two senior teachers.","I delegated the shopping to my brother while I finished the cooking."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"deleterious","p":"adjective","d":"Causing harm or damage, especially to health.","lb":"harmful, damaging","s":["harmful","damaging","detrimental","injurious","unhealthy","destructive"],"k":["corrosive","hazardous","hurtful","insalubrious"],"a":["beneficial","healthy","helpful","advantageous"],"ex":["Too much screen time can have deleterious effects on children's eyesight.","Smoking has a deleterious effect on the lungs of both smokers and people near them.","Years of drought had a deleterious impact on the farmers' crops."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"deliberate","p":"adjective","d":"Done on purpose and after thought, not by accident.","lb":"intentional, planned","s":["intentional","planned","calculated","conscious","purposeful","premeditated"],"k":["aforethought","careful","contrived","designed"],"a":["accidental","unintentional","unplanned","inadvertent"],"ex":["The fire was not an accident; police believe it was a deliberate act.","He made a deliberate choice to study medicine, not just follow his friends.","Her mistake was deliberate; she wanted to test whether anyone read the report."],"b":320,"y":3},{"w":"delicate","p":"adjective","d":"Easily broken or damaged, and needing careful handling.","lb":"fragile, fine","s":["fragile","frail","breakable","dainty","fine","flimsy"],"k":["difficult","ethereal","exquisite","feeble"],"a":["sturdy","strong","tough","robust"],"ex":["Handle the delicate glass bowls carefully when you pack them.","Babies have delicate skin that burns easily in the sun.","The delicate wings of the butterfly were damaged by the rain."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"delineate","p":"verb","d":"To describe or draw something clearly and in detail, showing its outline or boundaries.","lb":"outline, describe","s":["outline","describe","depict","sketch","portray","define"],"k":["draft","draw","explain","paint"],"a":["blur","obscure","confuse","muddle"],"ex":["A white fence delineates the boundary between our garden and the neighbor's.","The contract clearly delineates each worker's duties and working hours.","In her essay, she delineated three causes of the flood and explained each one."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"delinquent","p":"adjective","d":"Failing to meet an obligation, especially by not paying money that is owed by the required date.","lb":"overdue, negligent","s":["overdue","late","unpaid","outstanding","in default","behind"],"k":["behind schedule","belated","delayed","derelict"],"a":["punctual","prompt","paid up","up to date"],"ex":["The bank sent several reminders about her delinquent loan before calling to arrange a payment plan.","Tenants who stay delinquent for more than two months may be asked to leave the flat.","Delinquent taxpayers must pay a penalty on top of the amount they originally owed."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"delude","p":"verb","d":"To make someone believe something that is not true, or to fool yourself.","lb":"deceive, mislead","s":["deceive","mislead","fool","trick","hoodwink","dupe"],"k":["bamboozle","bluff","con","defraud"],"a":["enlighten","inform","disillusion"],"ex":["Don't delude yourself into thinking you can pass without studying.","The salesman deluded customers into believing the old phones were brand new.","Many young people are deluded by glamorous pictures on social media."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"deluge","p":"noun","d":"A heavy fall of rain or a flood of water; also an overwhelming amount of things arriving at once.","lb":"flood, torrent","s":["flood","torrent","downpour","avalanche","barrage","spate"],"k":["batch","cascade","cloudburst","deal"],"a":["trickle","drizzle","dribble","drought"],"ex":["A sudden deluge turned the streets of Dhaka into rivers within an hour.","After the announcement, the office received a deluge of emails from angry customers.","The online store was hit by a deluge of orders during the festival sale."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"delusion","p":"noun","d":"A false belief that someone holds strongly, even when the facts show it is wrong.","lb":"false belief, illusion","s":["illusion","misconception","fallacy","fantasy","misapprehension","mistaken belief"],"k":["conceit","folly","head game","hubris"],"a":["reality","truth","fact","clarity"],"ex":["He was under the delusion that he could pass the exam without opening a book.","Many people live under the delusion that money alone will make them happy.","The doctor explained that the patient's delusion made him believe strangers were following him."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"delusive","p":"adjective","d":"Giving a false idea of the truth; misleading, especially in a way that makes people hopeful.","lb":"misleading, false","s":["misleading","deceptive","false","unreal","fallacious","fanciful"],"k":["bogus","chimerical","dreamlike","fictitious"],"a":["real","genuine","truthful","accurate"],"ex":["The advertisement gave a delusive picture of life in the new apartment.","He clung to the delusive hope that the problem would solve itself.","A delusive sense of safety made the hikers ignore the weather warning."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"delve","p":"verb","d":"To search deeply for information or to study something in great detail.","lb":"probe, investigate","s":["dig","probe","investigate","explore","research","search"],"k":["cut into","dig in","dig out","dig up"],"a":["skim","glance","overlook","ignore"],"ex":["In this lesson, we will delve into the causes of river erosion.","She delved into old family letters to learn about her great-grandmother.","Before buying a used car, delve into its service history."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"demagogue","p":"noun","d":"A leader who wins support by appealing to people's emotions and prejudices rather than to reason.","lb":"agitator, rabble-rouser","s":["agitator","instigator","provocateur"],"k":["charlatan","fanatic","fearmonger","hothead"],"a":["statesman","moderate","peacemaker"],"ex":["The history teacher explained how a demagogue can win a crowd by blaming every problem on one group.","A demagogue makes promises that sound wonderful but never explains how to pay for them.","In the class debate, Rafi was accused of acting like a demagogue because he only appealed to people's fears."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"demeanor","p":"noun","d":"The way a person looks and behaves, which shows their character or mood.","lb":"manner, bearing","s":["manner","bearing","behavior","conduct","attitude","air"],"k":["approach","carriage","comportment","countenance"],"a":[],"ex":["The nurse's calm demeanor helped the frightened child relax during the injection.","In the interview, his confident demeanor impressed everyone on the panel.","Despite the bad news, she kept a cheerful demeanor at work all day."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"demise","p":"noun","d":"The end or failure of something that existed for a long time, or a person's death.","lb":"death, end","s":["death","end","collapse","downfall","passing","ruin"],"k":["decline","dissipation","dissolution","eclipse"],"a":["birth","rise","start","beginning"],"ex":["The demise of the old cinema hall saddened everyone who grew up in our town.","Experts blame poor management for the company's sudden demise.","Streaming services have led to the demise of video rental shops."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"demography","p":"noun","d":"The study of population statistics, such as birth rates, death rates, age and migration.","lb":"population studies","s":["population studies","population statistics","census study","vital statistics","population science"],"k":["census","census data","human ecology","human geography"],"a":[],"ex":["A student of demography studies birth rates, death rates and how people move between cities.","The demography of Dhaka has changed fast as thousands of people arrive from villages each year.","Planners use demography to decide where new schools and hospitals are needed."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"demonstration","p":"noun","d":"A practical showing of how something works or is done.","lb":"display, showing","s":["display","presentation","exhibition","exposition","showing","illustration"],"k":["dry run","expo","manifestation","preview"],"a":[],"ex":["The chemistry teacher gave a demonstration of how acid reacts with metal.","At the store, a salesman gave a demonstration of the new blender.","Nurses attended a demonstration on how to use the new heart monitor."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"demur","p":"verb","d":"To object to something or show reluctance to do it, often politely.","lb":"object, hesitate","s":["object","protest","balk","hesitate","take exception","hold back"],"k":["complain","equivocate","hang back","oppose"],"a":["agree","consent","comply","accept"],"ex":["When we asked her to lead the project, she demurred, saying she was too busy.","Rafi demurred when his friends suggested skipping class to watch the match.","The doctor demurred at prescribing more medicine until the test results came back."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"demure","p":"adjective","d":"Quiet, modest and a little shy in manner, often in a polite and well-behaved way.","lb":"modest, shy","s":["modest","reserved","shy","bashful","reticent","retiring"],"k":["diffident","docile","meek","prim"],"a":["bold","brazen","forward","outgoing"],"ex":["She gave a demure smile when the teacher praised her essay.","The bride looked demure in her red dress as the guests took photos.","Her demure manner at the interview hid a sharp mind and big ambitions."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"denigrate","p":"verb","d":"To say unfair or harsh things about someone or something to make them seem less good.","lb":"belittle, disparage","s":["belittle","disparage","slander","defame","malign","vilify"],"k":["accuse","bad-mouth","cut down","decry"],"a":["praise","extol","applaud","commend"],"ex":["He often denigrates his classmates' ideas to make himself look more intelligent.","A good manager corrects mistakes without denigrating the staff in front of others.","Some online comments denigrate the work of volunteers who clean the river."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"denizen","p":"noun","d":"A person, animal or plant that lives in or often visits a particular place.","lb":"inhabitant, resident","s":["inhabitant","resident","dweller","occupant","citizen","native"],"k":["individual","mortal","person","somebody"],"a":["outsider","stranger","foreigner","visitor"],"ex":["The denizens of this old Dhaka lane all know each other and share news over morning tea.","Tigers and deer are the best-known denizens of the Sundarbans forest.","Late at night, the library’s regular denizens are students with coffee mugs and heavy textbooks."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"denomination","p":"noun","d":"A named class or category of things, especially a unit of value on money or a branch of a religion.","lb":"category, value","s":["category","class","kind","sort","unit","value"],"k":["appellation","branch","church","communion"],"a":[],"ex":["The ATM gives out banknotes only in large denominations, so I could not get small change.","The shopkeeper refused a banknote of such high denomination because he had no change.","Tourists should carry banknotes in several denominations, including small ones for rickshaws and tea stalls."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"denote","p":"verb","d":"To be a sign or name for something, or to have a particular meaning.","lb":"signify, indicate","s":["signify","indicate","mean","represent","symbolize","designate"],"k":["announce","bespeak","betoken","evoke"],"a":[],"ex":["On this map, a blue line denotes a river.","In math, the symbol pi denotes the ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter.","A red light on the dashboard denotes a problem with the engine."],"b":162,"y":0},{"w":"denounce","p":"verb","d":"To publicly criticize someone or something as wrong, bad or harmful.","lb":"condemn, criticize","s":["condemn","criticize","censure","decry","castigate","vilify"],"k":["accuse","bang","betray","blame"],"a":["praise","applaud","commend","defend"],"ex":["Community leaders denounced the attack and urged everyone to stay calm.","Human rights groups denounced the use of child labour in the factory.","She denounced the company's false advertising in a letter to the newspaper."],"b":96,"y":3},{"w":"dense","p":"adjective","d":"Thick and closely packed together, so that it is hard to see or move through.","lb":"thick, packed","s":["thick","compact","crowded","packed","heavy","solid"],"k":["bulky","dim","dull","dumb"],"a":["sparse","thin","scattered","light"],"ex":["Dense fog covered the highway, so the bus driver had to move very slowly.","The Sundarbans is a dense forest where sunlight barely reaches the ground.","Cities with a dense population need good buses and clean drains."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"depict","p":"verb","d":"To show something or someone in a picture, or to describe it in words or on film.","lb":"portray, show","s":["portray","show","illustrate","represent","describe","paint"],"k":["capture","chronicle","clarify","delineate"],"a":["distort","misrepresent","hide","conceal"],"ex":["The mural depicts scenes from village life, with farmers and boats.","The film depicts the struggles of a young garment worker.","Her essay depicts the city as a place of both hope and hardship."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deplete","p":"verb","d":"To use up a large part of a supply of something so that little is left.","lb":"use up, drain","s":["use up","exhaust","drain","consume","reduce","empty"],"k":["drop","eat","eat up","expend"],"a":["replenish","refill","restock","increase"],"ex":["Heavy use of groundwater for irrigation has depleted wells across the region.","Buying gifts for everyone depleted my savings.","Long hours of work depleted her energy, and she fell asleep on the bus."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deplorable","p":"adjective","d":"Very bad and deserving strong disapproval; shocking in its poor quality or conditions.","lb":"shameful, terrible","s":["disgraceful","shameful","terrible","dreadful","lamentable","appalling"],"k":["abominable","awful","bad","base"],"a":["admirable","excellent","praiseworthy","commendable"],"ex":["The hostel's kitchen was in a deplorable state, with dirty floors and broken taps.","Throwing rubbish into the river is deplorable behaviour.","Workers complained about the deplorable conditions in the factory."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"deplore","p":"verb","d":"To feel and express strong disapproval or deep regret about something.","lb":"condemn, regret","s":["condemn","lament","regret","bemoan","denounce","deprecate"],"k":["blame","bridle at","complain","criticize"],"a":["praise","applaud","welcome","approve"],"ex":["The principal deplored the students' habit of leaving rubbish in the playground.","Many parents deplore how much time children spend on mobile games.","I deplore the lack of clean drinking water in some parts of the city."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deploy","p":"verb","d":"To place people or equipment in a particular position so that they are ready for action.","lb":"station, position","s":["station","position","post","arrange","assign","dispatch"],"k":["bring to bear","employ","field","marshal"],"a":["withdraw","recall","pull back","retreat"],"ex":["Extra police were deployed along the main road to manage the Eid crowds.","The navy deployed two ships to search for the missing fishing boats.","The council deployed volunteers and boats to rescue families trapped by the rising water."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"depose","p":"verb","d":"To remove someone from a position of power or authority, especially a ruler or leader.","lb":"remove, oust","s":["oust","remove","overthrow","dethrone","topple","unseat"],"k":["boot out","drive out","drum out","eject"],"a":["install","crown","appoint","restore"],"ex":["In the story, rebels deposed the cruel king and made his brother the ruler.","Shareholders voted to depose the chairman after the company lost money for three years.","Club members deposed their captain after a series of heavy defeats."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"depravity","p":"noun","d":"Extreme moral wickedness or corruption in a person's behavior.","lb":"wickedness, corruption","s":["wickedness","corruption","immorality","vice","degeneracy","evil"],"k":["debauchery","dissipation","malevolence","perfidy"],"a":["virtue","goodness","morality","decency"],"ex":["The judge spoke of the depravity of a crime in which a trusted guardian stole from orphans.","Newspapers were shocked by the depravity of fraudsters who cheated elderly people of their savings.","Many classic novels show the depravity of characters who ruin others for money."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"deprecate","p":"verb","d":"To express disapproval of something, or to treat it as less important or worthy than it really is.","lb":"disapprove, belittle","s":["disapprove of","condemn","criticize","disparage","belittle","denounce"],"k":["decry","denigrate","discount","dismiss"],"a":["praise","approve","commend","applaud"],"ex":["The principal deprecated the habit of cheating and warned students about serious punishment.","Doctors deprecate the use of antibiotics for ordinary colds, because they do not work.","She always deprecates her own cooking, even though the guests keep asking for more."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"depredate","p":"verb","d":"To attack and rob a place or people, causing great damage.","lb":"plunder, prey on","s":["plunder","pillage","ravage","prey on","loot","raid"],"k":["devastate","harry","lay waste","maraud"],"a":["protect","defend","guard","preserve"],"ex":["Bandits once depredated the villages along the river, taking crops and cattle.","Illegal loggers depredate the forest at night, cutting trees that are decades old.","Foxes depredate the chicken coops in the village whenever the dogs are asleep."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deprivation","p":"noun","d":"The state of not having enough of something basic that people need, like food, sleep or comfort.","lb":"lack, hardship","s":["want","privation","hardship","need","poverty","lack"],"k":["adversity","austerity","dearth","famine"],"a":["abundance","plenty","luxury","comfort"],"ex":["Sleep deprivation made it hard for him to concentrate during the exam.","Children living in areas of severe deprivation often miss school to work.","Deprivation of food and clean water is common in the flooded villages."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"derelict","p":"adjective","d":"Abandoned by its owner and left in a bad, neglected condition.","lb":"abandoned, neglected","s":["abandoned","deserted","neglected","dilapidated","ruined","forsaken"],"k":["creaky","damaged","delinquent","neglectful"],"a":["occupied","maintained","inhabited","restored"],"ex":["The derelict factory by the river has stood empty for twenty years.","Children were warned not to play in the derelict building because its roof could fall in.","Rusting derelict cars were scattered across the vacant lot."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"deride","p":"verb","d":"To laugh at someone or something in a cruel, scornful way.","lb":"mock, ridicule","s":["mock","ridicule","scorn","jeer","scoff at","sneer at"],"k":["despise","gibe at","guy","heckle"],"a":["praise","respect","admire","honor"],"ex":["Some classmates derided his old shoes, but he ignored them and kept studying.","Critics derided the new building as an ugly concrete box.","Early in his career, the inventor was derided for his strange ideas."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"derivative","p":"adjective","d":"Copied from or based on something else, with little that is new or original.","lb":"unoriginal, imitative","s":["unoriginal","copied","secondary","borrowed","uninspired","hackneyed"],"k":["banal","cliched","cold","commonplace"],"a":["original","innovative","creative","groundbreaking"],"ex":["The critics called the film derivative because it copied ideas from three older movies.","Her first poems were derivative, but over time she found her own voice.","The app felt derivative; every feature looked borrowed from a more famous one."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"derogatory","p":"adjective","d":"Showing a low opinion of someone or something in a way that is insulting or disrespectful.","lb":"insulting, disrespectful","s":["insulting","disparaging","belittling","offensive","critical","demeaning"],"k":["abusive","catty","condescending","contemptuous"],"a":["complimentary","flattering","respectful","praising"],"ex":["The coach apologized for his derogatory remark about the weaker players.","Using derogatory names for classmates is bullying, and the school does not allow it.","The customer left a derogatory review that attacked the staff instead of describing the problem."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"desiccate","p":"verb","d":"To remove all the water from something so that it becomes completely dry.","lb":"dry out, dehydrate","s":["dehydrate","dry up","dry out","wither","shrivel","bake"],"k":["crisp","drain","dry","embrittle"],"a":["moisten","soak","hydrate","wet"],"ex":["The hot wind desiccated the crops, and the fields turned brown within weeks.","Desiccated coconut is often used in sweets and cakes.","Villagers desiccate fish in the sun to make dried fish that can be stored for months."],"b":91,"y":1},{"w":"desire","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of wanting to have something or do something.","lb":"wish, longing","s":["wish","longing","yearning","craving","want","urge"],"k":["appetite","dream","fancy","hankering"],"a":["aversion","dislike","disgust","indifference"],"ex":["She has a strong desire to become a doctor and serve her village.","His desire for success kept him studying late every night.","There is a growing desire among citizens for cleaner air."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"desist","p":"verb","d":"To stop doing something, especially when you are told to.","lb":"stop, refrain","s":["stop","cease","refrain","halt","quit","abstain"],"k":["break off","cut out","forbear","forgo"],"a":["continue","persist","carry on","resume"],"ex":["The officer asked the crowd to desist from throwing garbage on the street.","The company was ordered to desist from using misleading advertisements.","I asked my neighbor to desist from playing loud music after midnight."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"desperate","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely worried and ready to try anything because your situation is very bad.","lb":"hopeless, frantic","s":["frantic","hopeless","despairing","urgent","anxious","wretched"],"k":["abject","agitated","brave","courageous"],"a":["hopeful","calm","confident","optimistic"],"ex":["The farmers were desperate for rain after three months without a single shower.","I made a desperate phone call to the bank when my card stopped working abroad.","Desperate for a job, he applied to more than fifty companies in a month."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"despise","p":"verb","d":"To feel strong dislike and disrespect for someone or something you think is unworthy.","lb":"hate, scorn","s":["scorn","detest","loathe","hate","abhor","disdain"],"k":["abominate","belittle","contemn","dislike"],"a":["admire","respect","love","adore"],"ex":["Nadia despises cheating, so she refused to share her answers during the admission test.","Commuters in Dhaka despise the long traffic jams that waste hours of their day.","The staff secretly despised their manager because he took credit for their hard work."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"despite","p":"preposition","d":"Used to show that something happens or is true although something else might have prevented it.","lb":"in spite of","s":["in spite of","notwithstanding","regardless of","even with","in defiance of","in the face of"],"k":["against","albeit","all the same","contempt"],"a":["because of","owing to","thanks to"],"ex":["Despite the heavy rain, thousands of fans waited outside the stadium.","She passed the exam despite studying for only two weeks.","Despite his age, my grandfather walks to the market every morning."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"despondent","p":"adjective","d":"Very sad and without hope, usually because of failure or disappointment.","lb":"hopeless, depressed","s":["dejected","downhearted","hopeless","miserable","gloomy","depressed"],"k":["abject","bleak","disconsolate","discouraged"],"a":["hopeful","cheerful","optimistic","elated"],"ex":["After failing the admission test twice, Rafi felt despondent and stopped studying for weeks.","The despondent farmers looked at their flooded fields and said nothing.","She grew despondent when none of her job applications received a reply."],"b":80,"y":4},{"w":"despot","p":"noun","d":"A ruler who has total power and uses it cruelly and unfairly.","lb":"tyrant, dictator","s":["tyrant","dictator","oppressor","absolute ruler","strongman","authoritarian"],"k":["absolutist","martinet","monarch","potentate"],"a":["democrat","liberator"],"ex":["The history book describes a despot who taxed farmers until they had no food.","The people celebrated when the old despot finally lost power.","At home, he behaved like a despot, deciding what everyone could eat and wear."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"destitute","p":"adjective","d":"Having no money, food or possessions; extremely poor.","lb":"penniless, impoverished","s":["penniless","impoverished","needy","indigent","insolvent","hard up"],"k":["bankrupt","barren","bereft","broke"],"a":["wealthy","rich","affluent","prosperous"],"ex":["The flood left hundreds of families destitute, without homes, food or clothes.","After the factory closed, many workers became destitute within a few months.","The charity runs a shelter for destitute children who live on the streets."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"desultory","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking a plan or purpose, and done without enthusiasm or steady effort.","lb":"aimless, halfhearted","s":["aimless","random","haphazard","sporadic","erratic","casual"],"k":["arbitrary","disjointed","inconsistent","irregular"],"a":["methodical","purposeful","systematic","determined"],"ex":["He made a desultory attempt to study, but mostly he scrolled through his phone.","The audience gave only desultory applause after the long and dull speech.","They kept up a desultory conversation about the weather while waiting for the bus."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"deter","p":"verb","d":"To make someone decide not to do something, usually by making it seem risky or difficult.","lb":"discourage, prevent","s":["discourage","dissuade","prevent","put off","deflect","scare off"],"k":["check","cow","curb","daunt"],"a":["encourage","urge","motivate","spur"],"ex":["Bright street lights help deter thieves from entering the neighborhood at night.","The high cost of tuition deterred many families from sending their children abroad.","Fines for littering are meant to deter people from throwing waste onto the road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"deterrent","p":"noun","d":"Something that discourages people from doing something, especially by making them afraid of the results.","lb":"discouragement, hindrance","s":["discouragement","hindrance","obstacle","impediment","restraint","check"],"k":["bogey","bugbear","countermeasure","difficulty"],"a":["incentive","encouragement","inducement","motivation"],"ex":["Heavy fines are a deterrent to people who might throw trash on the street.","Security cameras act as a deterrent to thieves.","The high cost of tickets was a deterrent for many students who wanted to attend."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"deviant","p":"adjective","d":"Different in an unusual way from what is normal, expected or accepted.","lb":"abnormal, atypical","s":["abnormal","atypical","aberrant","anomalous","irregular","unusual"],"k":["eccentric","heterodox","maverick","nonconformist"],"a":["normal","typical","standard","conventional"],"ex":["The scientist removed the deviant result from the graph because the instrument had failed.","The sociology teacher asked us to explain why a society labels some behavior as deviant.","A deviant spelling such as thru may appear in texts, but not in exams."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"devoid","p":"adjective","d":"Completely without something that would usually be there, such as a quality or feature.","lb":"lacking, empty","s":["lacking","empty","bereft","void","wanting","free"],"k":["absent","bare","clear","denuded"],"a":["full","rich","endowed","possessed"],"ex":["The speech was devoid of any real ideas and left the audience bored.","Her answer was devoid of emotion, as if she was reading from a card.","After the flood, the fields were devoid of crops and the villagers were worried."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"devotion","p":"noun","d":"Great love, loyalty or commitment shown to a person, cause or activity.","lb":"dedication, loyalty","s":["dedication","loyalty","commitment","fidelity","allegiance","attachment"],"k":["adoration","affection","ardor","constancy"],"a":["indifference","disloyalty","apathy","neglect"],"ex":["Her devotion to her sick mother touched everyone in the neighbourhood.","The coach's devotion to the team meant he never missed a single training session.","The doctor worked with devotion, often staying at the clinic until midnight."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"devout","p":"adjective","d":"Deeply religious and committed to the practices of your faith.","lb":"pious, religious","s":["pious","religious","faithful","reverent","observant","godly"],"k":["dear","earnest","heartfelt","holy"],"a":["impious","godless","lax"],"ex":["My grandmother is a devout woman who prays five times a day and fasts every Ramadan.","The devout pilgrims walked for hours to reach the temple before sunrise.","He was a devout man, yet he always listened kindly to friends who believed differently."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dexterous","p":"adjective","d":"Skilful and quick, especially in the way you use your hands.","lb":"skilful, nimble","s":["skilful","nimble","adroit","deft","agile","handy"],"k":["able","accomplished","capable","clever"],"a":["clumsy","awkward","inept","bungling"],"ex":["The dexterous tailor stitched the whole shirt in under an hour.","A dexterous surgeon's hands move with great care and precision.","The dexterous young goalkeeper caught the ball with one hand."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dextrous","p":"adjective","d":"Skilled at using your hands, or quick and clever in the way you handle things.","lb":"skillful, nimble","s":["skillful","adroit","nimble","deft","agile","handy"],"k":["able","capable","clever","dexterous"],"a":["clumsy","awkward","inept","ungainly"],"ex":["The dextrous tailor finished stitching the sleeve in only a few minutes.","With dextrous fingers, the potter shaped the wet clay into a smooth bowl.","A dextrous negotiator, she calmed the angry customer without giving in on the price."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"dialectical","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the method of testing ideas by comparing opposing arguments in order to reach the truth.","lb":"logical, argumentative","s":["logical","analytical","argumentative","rational","discursive"],"k":["analytic","antithetical","coherent","contrapuntal"],"a":[],"ex":["Our philosophy teacher uses a dialectical method, asking students to defend one view and then attack it.","The debate club follows a dialectical approach, where each argument is tested against its strongest opposite.","Her dialectical thinking helped her see that both sides of the dispute held part of the truth."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"diatribe","p":"noun","d":"A long, angry speech or piece of writing that strongly criticizes someone or something.","lb":"rant, tirade","s":["tirade","rant","harangue","invective","attack","outburst"],"k":["dressing-down","fulmination","jeremiad","philippic"],"a":["praise","tribute","compliment","eulogy"],"ex":["He launched into a diatribe about the slow internet as soon as he reached the office.","The blogger's long diatribe against the new bus fares attracted thousands of readers.","My uncle delivered a ten-minute diatribe about teenagers and their phones."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"dichotomy","p":"noun","d":"A sharp division between two things that are opposite or completely different.","lb":"division, split","s":["division","split","contrast","divide","separation","gulf"],"k":["antithesis","bifurcation","binary","bipolarity"],"a":["unity","union","merger","agreement"],"ex":["There is a sharp dichotomy between the busy city center and the quiet villages nearby.","Many students feel a dichotomy between studying for exams and enjoying their youth.","The report points to a dichotomy between what the company says and what it actually does."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"dictum","p":"noun","d":"A short, well-known saying that states a rule or principle, or an official statement of opinion.","lb":"saying, pronouncement","s":["saying","maxim","adage","proverb","saw","axiom"],"k":["aphorism","catchphrase","declaration","epigram"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandmother's favorite dictum was that a clean kitchen makes a happy home.","The coach lived by the dictum that champions are made in practice, not in games.","The old dictum to measure twice and cut once saved the carpenter from wasting good wood."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"didactic","p":"adjective","d":"Intended to teach a lesson, often in a way that seems too serious or preachy.","lb":"instructive, preachy","s":["instructive","educational","moralizing","preachy","pedantic","edifying"],"k":["clarifying","heavy-handed","instructional","moralistic"],"a":["entertaining","amusing","frivolous"],"ex":["The story was too didactic, ending with a long speech about the value of honesty.","Fables are didactic tales that teach children how to behave.","My uncle has a didactic tone and turns every conversation into a lesson."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"diffidence","p":"noun","d":"A lack of confidence in yourself, shown by shyness and a reluctance to speak or act.","lb":"shyness, timidity","s":["shyness","timidity","reserve","insecurity","modesty","meekness"],"k":["apprehension","awkwardness","humbleness","introversion"],"a":["confidence","boldness","assurance","audacity"],"ex":["She spoke with diffidence at first, but her voice grew stronger as the presentation went on.","His diffidence kept him from raising his hand even though he knew the answer.","With some diffidence, the new employee asked whether he could suggest a change."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"diffident","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking confidence in yourself, so that you are shy about speaking or acting.","lb":"shy, timid","s":["shy","timid","bashful","reserved","hesitant","reticent"],"k":["apprehensive","coy","inhibited","insecure"],"a":["confident","bold","assertive","outgoing"],"ex":["The diffident new student sat in the back row and hardly spoke all week.","She was diffident about showing her drawings, though they were wonderful.","In interviews, a diffident candidate may speak softly and avoid eye contact."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"diffuse","p":"adjective","d":"Spread out over a large area instead of being concentrated, or using too many words to say something.","lb":"spread out, wordy","s":["scattered","dispersed","widespread","spread out","wordy","rambling"],"k":["diluted","disjointed","distributed","loose"],"a":["concentrated","concise","focused","compact"],"ex":["The lamp gave a soft, diffuse light that made the room feel calm.","Her essay was diffuse and rambling, so the main point got lost.","The pain was diffuse, spread across his whole back rather than in one spot."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"digress","p":"verb","d":"To move away from the main subject while speaking or writing.","lb":"stray, wander","s":["stray","wander","deviate","drift","go off topic","ramble"],"k":["branch off","detour","err","go astray"],"a":["stick to the point","focus","stay on topic","concentrate"],"ex":["Sorry to digress, but I just remembered something funny from last week.","The teacher often digressed from the lesson to tell stories from his own school days.","If you digress too much in your essay, the examiner will lose track of your argument."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"digression","p":"noun","d":"A temporary move away from the main subject when you are speaking or writing.","lb":"tangent, deviation","s":["tangent","deviation","aside","detour","departure","divergence"],"k":["deflection","excursion","excursus","footnote"],"a":["focus","relevance","directness"],"ex":["Forgive the digression, but this story about my first job explains why I changed careers.","The teacher's digression about her childhood made the lesson much more interesting.","After a long digression about football, the committee returned to the budget."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"dilapidated","p":"adjective","d":"In very bad condition because of age, damage or lack of care.","lb":"run-down, ruined","s":["decrepit","derelict","crumbling","shabby","neglected","rickety"],"k":["abandoned","battered","bedraggled","broken-down"],"a":["restored","renovated","pristine","immaculate"],"ex":["The dilapidated bus stopped twice on the way, and the passengers had to push it.","They rented a dilapidated house with a leaking roof and broken windows.","The school building was so dilapidated that the walls were cracked and the doors would not close."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"dilate","p":"verb","d":"To become wider or larger, or to make something wider or larger.","lb":"widen, expand","s":["widen","expand","enlarge","swell","open up","broaden"],"k":["balloon","bulge","elaborate","extend"],"a":["constrict","contract","narrow","shrink"],"ex":["In dim light, the pupils of your eyes dilate to let in more light.","The eye doctor put drops in my eyes to dilate the pupils before the exam.","Warm water makes blood vessels dilate, which is why a hot bath can turn your skin pink."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"dilemma","p":"noun","d":"A difficult situation in which you must choose between two options, neither of which is good.","lb":"quandary, predicament","s":["quandary","predicament","bind","plight","impasse","double bind"],"k":["conundrum","crossroads","fix","hard choice"],"a":[],"ex":["I am in a dilemma: one job pays better, but the other is closer to my family.","Parents face a dilemma when the best school in town is too far from home.","Nadia had a dilemma over whether to spend her scholarship money on a laptop or save it."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"dilettante","p":"noun","d":"A person who takes up an activity for pleasure, without serious effort or deep knowledge.","lb":"amateur, dabbler","s":["amateur","hobbyist","layman","novice"],"k":["aesthete","layperson","lightweight","neophyte"],"a":["professional","expert","specialist","master"],"ex":["He is a dilettante who tried the guitar, painting and photography but kept none of them.","Experts called the writer a dilettante because he had never studied history seriously.","At the chess club, the serious players had little patience for a dilettante who played only on weekends."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"diligence","p":"noun","d":"Careful and steady effort in doing a task or duty.","lb":"hard work, care","s":["industry","perseverance","application","care","persistence","effort"],"k":["dedication","earnestness","elbow grease","exertion"],"a":["laziness","idleness","negligence","carelessness"],"ex":["Her diligence in revising every night earned her a place at Dhaka University.","The accountant checked every invoice with great diligence before signing the report.","The farmer's diligence paid off when his field of rice survived the dry season."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"diligent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing steady, careful effort in your work or duties.","lb":"hardworking, careful","s":["hardworking","industrious","conscientious","assiduous","persistent","thorough"],"k":["attentive","busy","committed","earnest"],"a":["lazy","idle","careless","negligent"],"ex":["Nadia is a diligent student who finishes her homework before dinner.","The diligent accountant checked every figure twice before sending the report.","Thanks to diligent practice, he finally mastered the guitar."],"b":576,"y":1},{"w":"diminish","p":"verb","d":"To become smaller, weaker or less important, or to make something do so.","lb":"decrease, reduce","s":["decrease","reduce","lessen","shrink","decline","dwindle"],"k":["belittle","change magnitude","cut","drop"],"a":["increase","grow","expand","enlarge"],"ex":["Pain from the injury began to diminish after two days of rest.","A long period of stress can diminish your ability to concentrate.","The value of an old car diminishes quickly every year."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"diminution","p":"noun","d":"A reduction in the size, amount, strength or importance of something.","lb":"decrease, reduction","s":["reduction","decrease","decline","lessening","shrinkage","cut"],"k":["attenuation","contraction","depletion","dwindling"],"a":["increase","growth","rise","expansion"],"ex":["Doctors noticed a gradual diminution in his hearing over several years.","The factory's closure led to a sharp diminution in the town's income.","There has been a noticeable diminution of traffic on our road since the new bypass opened."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"dinginess","p":"noun","d":"The dull, dirty-looking quality of a place or object that is dark or poorly kept.","lb":"dullness, shabbiness","s":["dullness","griminess","drabness","gloominess","dirtiness"],"k":["filth","grime","grubbiness","mustiness"],"a":["brightness","freshness","brilliance"],"ex":["A coat of bright paint removed the dinginess of the old classroom.","The dinginess of the small flat made him long for a window with sunlight.","We were put off by the dinginess of the cafe, with its dim lights and stained walls."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"noun","d":"The work of managing relations between countries peacefully, through talks and agreements.","lb":"statecraft","s":["negotiation","foreign relations","international relations","mediation","bargaining","statesmanship"],"k":["delicacy","discretion","finesse","intercession"],"a":["war","hostility","aggression"],"ex":["The two countries solved their trade dispute through patient diplomacy.","She wants to study diplomacy at university and work for the foreign ministry.","Quiet diplomacy helped both sides reach an agreement on river water sharing."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dire","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely serious, urgent or bad, with the threat of terrible results.","lb":"dreadful, desperate","s":["dreadful","terrible","grave","desperate","severe","calamitous"],"k":["abominable","alarming","appalling","atrocious"],"a":["fortunate","promising","favorable","hopeful"],"ex":["Flood victims were in dire need of clean water and dry food.","The doctor gave a dire warning about the dangers of skipping medication.","The company is in dire financial trouble and may close next month."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"dirge","p":"noun","d":"A slow, sad song or piece of music played at a funeral or to express grief.","lb":"lament, funeral song","s":["lament","elegy","requiem","funeral song","keen"],"k":["coronach","death march","funeral march","hymn"],"a":[],"ex":["The band played a slow dirge as the procession moved through the town.","Hearing the violin's sad dirge, many guests wiped their eyes.","On the rainy evening, the radio played a mournful dirge that matched our mood."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"disabuse","p":"verb","d":"To free someone from a false idea or mistaken belief.","lb":"correct, enlighten","s":["enlighten","correct","set straight","educate","disillusion","clear up"],"k":["awaken","debunk","dispel","edify"],"a":["deceive","mislead","delude","fool"],"ex":["A single day in the lab quickly disabused him of the idea that science is easy.","The guide disabused tourists of the myth that the old fort was haunted.","Let me disabuse you of the notion that I will lend you money again."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"disaffect","p":"verb","d":"To make people who were loyal or friendly feel unhappy and less supportive.","lb":"alienate, estrange","s":["alienate","estrange","antagonize","turn away","disillusion","offend"],"k":["alter","change","disenchant","disgruntle"],"a":["win over","reconcile","attract","endear"],"ex":["Constant unfair treatment can disaffect even the most loyal employees.","The new fees disaffected many loyal customers, and some switched to rival shops.","Long delays and rude staff disaffected passengers who had used the bus service for years."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disarray","p":"noun","d":"A state of disorder and confusion, when things are not neat or well organised.","lb":"disorder, mess","s":["disorder","confusion","chaos","mess","muddle","clutter"],"k":["bedlam","cognitive state","jumble","mental confusion"],"a":["order","neatness","harmony"],"ex":["After the burglary, the whole house was in disarray, with drawers pulled out and clothes on the floor.","The sudden resignation of the chairman left the company in disarray.","Heavy monsoon rain threw bus schedules across Dhaka into disarray, and many commuters were stranded."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disavow","p":"verb","d":"To say publicly that you have no knowledge of, connection with, or responsibility for something.","lb":"deny, disown","s":["deny","disown","repudiate","reject","disclaim","renounce"],"k":["abandon","contradict","dismiss","dissociate from"],"a":["acknowledge","admit","confess","accept"],"ex":["The company quickly disavowed the offensive advertisement made by one of its partners.","He disavowed any knowledge of the missing money.","After the scandal, the club disavowed its former coach."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"discern","p":"verb","d":"To notice or recognize something that is not obvious, or to tell the difference between things.","lb":"perceive, distinguish","s":["perceive","detect","notice","recognize","distinguish","make out"],"k":["apprehend","descry","espy","fathom"],"a":["overlook","miss","ignore","confuse"],"ex":["In the thick fog, we could barely discern the shape of the bus.","It takes a trained ear to discern the difference between two similar musical notes.","A good teacher can discern which students need extra help, even when they stay quiet."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"discernible","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be seen, heard or understood, even if only with difficulty.","lb":"noticeable, perceptible","s":["perceptible","noticeable","visible","detectable","observable","apparent"],"k":["appreciable","audible","clear","conspicuous"],"a":["imperceptible","invisible","indistinct","hidden"],"ex":["There was no discernible difference between the original painting and the copy.","In the fog, the shape of the boat was barely discernible.","A discernible improvement in her handwriting appeared after a month of practice."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"discerning","p":"adjective","d":"Having or showing good judgment, especially in recognizing quality or what is true.","lb":"perceptive, astute","s":["perceptive","astute","discriminating","judicious","shrewd","insightful"],"k":["apprehensive","canny","clear","clever"],"a":["indiscriminate","naive","gullible","careless"],"ex":["Discerning customers check the quality of the fabric before buying a saree.","She has a discerning eye for fake news and checks every source.","The judges were discerning and noticed the small mistakes in the otherwise excellent performance."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"disclaim","p":"verb","d":"To say officially that you have no connection with something or no responsibility for it.","lb":"deny, disown","s":["deny","renounce","disown","repudiate","disavow","reject"],"k":["abdicate","abnegate","absolve oneself","decline responsibility"],"a":["claim","accept","acknowledge","admit"],"ex":["The company disclaimed any responsibility for items left in the cloakroom.","After the scandal, the club disclaimed any link with its former coach.","The author disclaimed any intention of hurting readers' feelings with the story."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"discomfit","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel confused, embarrassed or uneasy.","lb":"embarrass, fluster","s":["embarrass","disconcert","fluster","unsettle","confuse","abash"],"k":["agitate","arouse","bewilder","chagrin"],"a":["reassure","comfort","soothe","calm"],"ex":["The interviewer's sudden question discomfited the nervous candidate.","She was discomfited by the stranger's long stare on the bus.","A loud laugh from the audience discomfited the speaker, who lost his place."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"disconcert","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel confused, embarrassed or slightly worried.","lb":"unsettle, fluster","s":["unsettle","fluster","confuse","ruffle","rattle","perturb"],"k":["abash","agitate","baffle","bewilder"],"a":["reassure","calm","soothe","compose"],"ex":["The interviewer's sudden question disconcerted her, and she lost her train of thought.","It disconcerted the speaker when someone's phone rang loudly in the middle of his speech.","Rafi was disconcerted by the silence that followed his joke."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"discordant","p":"adjective","d":"Not in harmony; clashing, whether in sound or in opinions and ideas.","lb":"clashing, harsh","s":["clashing","harsh","jarring","conflicting","grating","dissonant"],"k":["at variance","contradictory","contrary","disparate"],"a":["harmonious","melodious","agreeable","compatible"],"ex":["The out-of-tune guitar made a discordant sound that stopped the singing.","A discordant note in the meeting came from one manager who opposed the whole plan.","The bright orange sofa looked discordant in the plain gray room."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"discourse","p":"noun","d":"Serious spoken or written discussion of a subject.","lb":"discussion, talk","s":["discussion","conversation","dialogue","debate","talk","speech"],"k":["communicating","exchange","gossip","preaching"],"a":[],"ex":["The professor's discourse on climate change held the students' attention for an hour.","Respectful discourse is rare in the comments section of many websites.","Public discourse about school fees has grown louder this year."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"discredit","p":"verb","d":"To damage someone's reputation, or to make people stop trusting or believing something.","lb":"disgrace, disprove","s":["disgrace","defame","dishonor","smear","undermine","disprove"],"k":["belittle","besmirch","denigrate","disbelieve"],"a":["vindicate","credit","honor","confirm"],"ex":["Lawyers tried to discredit the witness by showing that she had lied before.","The scandal discredited the company, and many customers stopped buying its products.","New research has discredited the old belief that cold weather causes colds."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"discreet","p":"adjective","d":"Careful about what one says or does, so as not to cause embarrassment or reveal private matters.","lb":"careful, tactful","s":["tactful","careful","prudent","cautious","diplomatic","circumspect"],"k":["confidential","discerning","low-key","private"],"a":["indiscreet","tactless","careless","blunt"],"ex":["Please be discreet about the surprise party, because my sister must not hear a word of it.","The doctor made discreet inquiries about the patient's family without upsetting anyone.","A good assistant is discreet and never discusses the manager's private calls with colleagues."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"discrepancy","p":"noun","d":"A difference between things that should be the same, or a lack of agreement between facts.","lb":"difference, inconsistency","s":["inconsistency","difference","disparity","variance","gap","mismatch"],"k":["anomaly","contrast","disagreement","error"],"a":["agreement","consistency","similarity","match"],"ex":["The accountant found a discrepancy of five hundred taka between the receipts and the cash.","There is a discrepancy between the date on the ticket and the date in the email.","Doctors noticed a discrepancy between the patient's story and his test results."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"discrete","p":"adjective","d":"Separate and distinct, forming an individual part rather than being joined to others.","lb":"separate, distinct","s":["separate","distinct","individual","detached","unconnected","independent"],"k":["autonomous","discontinuous","isolated","modular"],"a":["connected","joined","continuous","combined"],"ex":["The course is divided into three discrete units, each with its own exam.","Scientists sorted the animals into discrete groups based on their diet.","The computer stores music as discrete numbers instead of a continuous wave."],"b":149,"y":0},{"w":"discriminate","p":"verb","d":"To see or recognize the difference between two or more things.","lb":"distinguish, differentiate","s":["distinguish","differentiate","tell apart","discern","separate","tell the difference"],"k":["identify","isolate","know apart","make out"],"a":["confuse","confound","mix up","blur"],"ex":["Young children cannot always discriminate between a real danger and an imaginary one.","Experienced tailors can discriminate between pure cotton and a blend just by touching the cloth.","The app uses a camera to discriminate ripe mangoes from unripe ones."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"discursive","p":"adjective","d":"Moving from one topic to another in a rambling way, without sticking to a clear plan.","lb":"rambling, wandering","s":["rambling","wandering","meandering","roundabout","diffuse","wordy"],"k":["chatty","episodic","expansive","free-ranging"],"a":["concise","focused","succinct","direct"],"ex":["The professor's lecture was so discursive that we never found out what the main point was.","His discursive emails wander from football to the weather to what he ate for lunch.","Grandfather's stories are discursive, moving from the village to his school days and back again."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disdain","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling that someone or something is unworthy of respect or attention.","lb":"contempt, scorn","s":["contempt","scorn","derision","disrespect","condescension","loathing"],"k":["aloofness","arrogance","disgust","dismissiveness"],"a":["respect","admiration","esteem","regard"],"ex":["He looked at the cheap notebook with disdain and asked the clerk for something more expensive.","She spoke of her classmates’ hobbies with open disdain, which made her unpopular.","Some customers treat delivery riders with disdain, forgetting that they work long hours in heavy traffic."],"b":80,"y":3},{"w":"disempowering","p":"adjective","d":"Taking away someone's power, confidence or ability to control their own life.","lb":"weakening, undermining","s":["undermining","weakening","demoralizing","crushing","belittling","discouraging"],"k":["debilitating","disheartening","domineering","enfeebling"],"a":["empowering","encouraging","enabling","strengthening"],"ex":["Being told your ideas are worthless can be a disempowering experience for a young employee.","Poverty can be disempowering, because it limits people's choices about education and health.","The new rule felt disempowering to teachers, who lost control over how they graded."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"disgruntle","p":"verb","d":"To make someone annoyed, sulky and dissatisfied.","lb":"annoy, displease","s":["annoy","displease","irritate","upset","vex","sour"],"k":["aggrieve","bother","chafe","embitter"],"a":["please","satisfy","delight","content"],"ex":["The long delay left the passengers disgruntled and tired.","A disgruntled employee posted complaints about the company online.","Cutting the bonus disgruntled the whole sales team."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disincline","p":"verb","d":"To make someone unwilling or less likely to do something.","lb":"make unwilling","s":["dissuade","discourage","deter","put off","turn off","make reluctant"],"k":["cool on","dampen","determine","hinder"],"a":["incline","encourage","persuade","motivate"],"ex":["The high ticket price disinclined many fans from attending the match.","The long queue disinclined her to wait for a table.","I am disinclined to lend him money after what happened last time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"disingenuous","p":"adjective","d":"Not sincere; pretending to know less or to be more honest than you really are.","lb":"insincere, deceitful","s":["insincere","dishonest","deceitful","devious","false","hypocritical"],"k":["calculating","crafty","crooked","distorted"],"a":["sincere","honest","candid","genuine"],"ex":["It was disingenuous of him to say he knew nothing when he had planned the whole trip.","The seller's disingenuous smile hid the fact that the phone had been repaired twice.","She gave a disingenuous apology, saying sorry only because the boss was watching."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"disinterested","p":"adjective","d":"Fair and impartial because you have nothing personal to gain or lose from the result.","lb":"impartial, unbiased","s":["impartial","unbiased","neutral","objective","fair","unprejudiced"],"k":["equitable","independent","indifferent","just"],"a":["biased","partial","prejudiced","interested"],"ex":["We asked a disinterested third person to decide who had won the argument.","A good judge must be disinterested and ignore friendship or money.","Look for disinterested advice from a bank officer who does not earn commission on the product."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"disjointed","p":"adjective","d":"Not smoothly connected, so that it is difficult to follow or understand.","lb":"disconnected, incoherent","s":["disconnected","incoherent","rambling","jumbled","fragmented","confused"],"k":["choppy","disjunct","dislocated","disordered"],"a":["coherent","connected","logical","smooth"],"ex":["His presentation was disjointed, jumping from one slide to another without any clear link.","She told a disjointed story, and nobody could understand what had happened.","Because of the fever, his speech was disjointed and he forgot where he was."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"dismal","p":"adjective","d":"Causing or showing sadness, gloom or hopelessness; very poor or depressing.","lb":"gloomy, bleak","s":["gloomy","dreary","bleak","depressing","miserable","grim"],"k":["abysmal","black","blue","dark"],"a":["cheerful","bright","cheery","pleasant"],"ex":["The dismal weather kept everyone indoors for three days of continuous rain.","After a dismal first half, the home team finally scored just before the whistle.","The hostel room was cold and dismal, with one small window facing a wall."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dismay","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel shocked, worried or discouraged by something unexpected.","lb":"alarm, discourage","s":["alarm","distress","shock","disconcert","discourage","daunt"],"k":["cast down","depress","fright","frighten"],"a":["reassure","encourage","cheer","comfort"],"ex":["The sudden rise in rice prices dismayed many families in our neighborhood.","It dismayed Nadia to find that her laptop had not saved her essay.","The coach was dismayed by how few players turned up for practice."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dismiss","p":"verb","d":"To refuse to take an idea, suggestion or person seriously, usually after only brief thought.","lb":"reject, brush off","s":["reject","brush aside","disregard","discount","spurn","wave away"],"k":["brush off","can","cut","decline"],"a":["accept","consider","welcome","embrace"],"ex":["The manager dismissed the complaint as unimportant without even reading it.","Do not dismiss your friend's worries; they may be bigger than they sound.","Scientists dismissed the rumor that the water was poisoned after testing it."],"b":259,"y":0},{"w":"disparage","p":"verb","d":"To speak about someone or something as if they are unimportant or of little value.","lb":"belittle, criticize","s":["belittle","denigrate","deprecate","run down","criticize","put down"],"k":["condemn","defame","denounce","diminish"],"a":["praise","flatter","extol","compliment"],"ex":["It is unkind to disparage a classmate's work just because it is simple.","Some people disparage online degrees without knowing how much work they involve.","The coach never disparaged his players, even after a heavy defeat."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"disparate","p":"adjective","d":"So different from each other that they cannot easily be compared or combined.","lb":"different, dissimilar","s":["different","dissimilar","distinct","contrasting","unlike","divergent"],"k":["assorted","discordant","heterogeneous","incongruous"],"a":["similar","alike","comparable","uniform"],"ex":["The team was made up of people from disparate backgrounds, including a nurse and a pilot.","The two cousins have disparate tastes: one loves rock music and the other prefers folk songs.","Her essay linked disparate ideas from history, biology and art into one clear argument."],"b":85,"y":1},{"w":"dispassionate","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and fair, and not influenced by strong feelings or personal interest.","lb":"impartial, calm","s":["impartial","objective","calm","unbiased","detached","neutral"],"k":["clinical","composed","cool-headed","disinterested"],"a":["emotional","passionate","biased","partial"],"ex":["The referee made a dispassionate decision, ignoring the shouting from the crowd.","A good journalist gives a dispassionate account of events.","Try to look at your exam results in a dispassionate way and plan how to improve."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"disperse","p":"verb","d":"To spread in different directions, or to make a crowd or group scatter.","lb":"scatter, spread","s":["scatter","spread","dissipate","break up","dispel","dissolve"],"k":["break ranks","circulate","disappear","disband"],"a":["gather","assemble","collect","concentrate"],"ex":["The crowd dispersed quietly after the match ended.","The wind helped to disperse the thick smoke from the burning rubbish.","Seeds disperse in many ways: some float on water, and others stick to animals."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"dispirit","p":"verb","d":"To make someone lose enthusiasm, hope or confidence.","lb":"discourage, dishearten","s":["discourage","depress","dampen","sadden","deflate","daunt"],"k":["cast down","chill","cow","demoralize"],"a":["encourage","cheer","inspire","motivate"],"ex":["Failing the first test did not dispirit her; she simply studied harder for the next one.","Weeks of heavy rain dispirited the farmers, who had hoped for a good harvest.","The harsh feedback dispirited the young designer so much that she almost quit."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disposition","p":"noun","d":"A person's natural way of feeling and behaving, especially in dealing with other people.","lb":"temperament, nature","s":["temperament","nature","character","personality","mood","makeup"],"k":["attitude","bent","frame of mind","humor"],"a":[],"ex":["My little sister has a cheerful disposition and smiles at everyone she meets.","The doctor's gentle disposition put the nervous child at ease.","He has a stubborn disposition, so arguing with him is usually a waste of time."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"disproportionate","p":"adjective","d":"Too large or too small when compared with something else.","lb":"unequal, excessive","s":["unequal","excessive","uneven","unbalanced","lopsided","out of proportion"],"k":["exaggerated","extravagant","immoderate","mismatched"],"a":["proportionate","balanced","equal","proportional"],"ex":["The punishment was disproportionate to the small mistake the student had made.","A disproportionate share of the city's money goes to a few wealthy areas.","His reaction was disproportionate; he shouted at the waiter over a missing napkin."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disquiet","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel worried or uneasy.","lb":"worry, unsettle","s":["worry","trouble","disturb","unsettle","perturb","alarm"],"k":["discomfit","disorder","distract","fret"],"a":["calm","soothe","reassure","comfort"],"ex":["The sudden change in his tone disquieted her, though she could not say why.","News of the factory closure disquieted the workers and their families.","Rising food prices disquiet many families before the festival season."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"disruptive","p":"adjective","d":"Causing disorder or interruption that stops something from continuing normally.","lb":"disorderly, upsetting","s":["troublesome","disorderly","unruly","upsetting","unsettling","interfering"],"k":["boisterous","rambunctious","raucous","riotous"],"a":["orderly","quiet","calm","cooperative"],"ex":["A disruptive student kept talking loudly while the teacher was explaining the lesson.","Frequent load-shedding is highly disruptive to small factories and shops.","The disruptive noise from the road repairs made it hard to study."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"dissect","p":"verb","d":"To carefully cut something apart in order to study its inner structure.","lb":"cut apart, analyze","s":["cut up","dismember","examine","analyze","take apart","carve"],"k":["autopsy","break down","chop","deconstruct"],"a":["assemble","join","combine","sew"],"ex":["In biology class, we dissected a flower to study its parts.","Medical students dissect a cadaver to learn the structure of the human body.","The scientist dissected the fish to find out what it had eaten."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dissemble","p":"verb","d":"To hide your true feelings or intentions by pretending to feel or think something else.","lb":"pretend, conceal","s":["pretend","feign","conceal","disguise","hide","mask"],"k":["act","affect","belie","bluff"],"a":["reveal","disclose","confess","expose"],"ex":["He dissembled his disappointment with a bright smile when his friend won the prize.","The suspect dissembled during the interview, pretending he had never met the victim.","She could not dissemble; her face always showed exactly what she was thinking."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"disseminate","p":"verb","d":"To spread information, ideas or knowledge widely among many people.","lb":"spread, distribute","s":["spread","distribute","circulate","broadcast","publish","propagate"],"k":["bare","disperse","go around","pass around"],"a":["suppress","withhold","hide","conceal"],"ex":["Health workers disseminate information about clean drinking water through posters and radio.","Social media allows rumors to be disseminated within minutes.","The university disseminates research findings through free online journals."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"dissent","p":"verb","d":"To publicly disagree with an official or generally accepted opinion or decision.","lb":"disagree, object","s":["disagree","object","differ","protest","demur","take issue"],"k":["argue","buck","challenge","contest"],"a":["agree","concur","assent","consent"],"ex":["Two members of the committee dissented from the decision to raise the fees.","One judge dissented, saying the evidence was not strong enough.","Few students dared to dissent when the principal announced the new rule."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"disservice","p":"noun","d":"A harmful action that hurts someone, even when you meant to help.","lb":"harm, bad turn","s":["harm","injury","wrong","bad turn","ill turn","injustice"],"k":["blunder","detriment","hindrance","ill service"],"a":["favor","service","kindness","good turn"],"ex":["You do your children a disservice if you never let them make their own choices.","The teacher said that giving students all the answers does them a disservice.","The misleading headline did a disservice to the hard-working nurses."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dissident","p":"noun","d":"A person who openly disagrees with and criticises the authorities or an official policy.","lb":"dissenter, protester","s":["protester","objector","nonconformist","rebel","critic","agitator"],"k":["activist","contestant","iconoclast","individual"],"a":["conformist","loyalist","supporter","traditionalist"],"ex":["As a dissident in the committee, he voted against every proposal the chairman made.","The dissident writer was forced to leave his country because of his articles.","Within the club, a small group of dissidents demanded a change in the rules."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dissipate","p":"verb","d":"To gradually disappear or spread out until nothing is left, or to make something do so.","lb":"disperse, vanish","s":["disperse","vanish","scatter","evaporate","dissolve","disappear"],"k":["break up","disband","dispel","divide"],"a":["gather","accumulate","concentrate","collect"],"ex":["By mid-morning, the thick fog over the river had dissipated, and the ferries started again.","The crowd slowly dissipated after the match ended, and the streets became quiet.","His anger dissipated as soon as his sister apologized."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"dissolute","p":"adjective","d":"Living in an immoral, careless way, especially by wasting time and money on drink, gambling or pleasure.","lb":"immoral, reckless","s":["debauched","immoral","depraved","wild","reckless","corrupt"],"k":["decadent","degraded","fast","hedonistic"],"a":["virtuous","moral","upright","disciplined"],"ex":["After inheriting his father's fortune, he lived a dissolute life and wasted everything within five years.","The novel describes a dissolute young man who gambles away his salary every month.","Her parents worried that her dissolute friends would be a bad influence on her studies."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dissolution","p":"noun","d":"The ending or breaking up of a group, organization, agreement or relationship.","lb":"breakup, termination","s":["breakup","termination","ending","collapse","disintegration","separation"],"k":["adjournment","conclusion","dissipation","dissolving"],"a":["formation","union","creation","establishment"],"ex":["The dissolution of the partnership left both brothers free to start their own businesses.","The court granted the dissolution of the marriage after both sides agreed on the terms.","The dissolution of the old empire reshaped the map of the region."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"dissolve","p":"verb","d":"To mix with a liquid and become part of it, or to make a solid do this.","lb":"melt, liquefy","s":["melt","liquefy","thaw","disperse","break down","disintegrate"],"k":["absorb","break up","deliquesce","dilute"],"a":["solidify","crystallize","precipitate","harden"],"ex":["Stir the sugar well so that it dissolves completely in the hot tea.","The doctor told me to let the tablet dissolve under my tongue.","In science class we watched salt dissolve quickly in warm water but slowly in cold."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"dissonance","p":"noun","d":"A harsh clash of sounds, or a lack of agreement between ideas, feelings or actions.","lb":"discord, clash","s":["discord","clash","cacophony","harshness","disharmony","conflict"],"k":["ambiguity","ambivalence","clamor","commotion"],"a":["harmony","agreement","accord","concord"],"ex":["The orchestra's tuning created a loud dissonance before the concert began.","There was a painful dissonance between what he said and how he behaved.","Cognitive dissonance can make a smoker uncomfortable when he reads about the health risks."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"dissonant","p":"adjective","d":"Harsh-sounding and out of harmony; also clashing or not in agreement.","lb":"discordant, clashing","s":["discordant","harsh","jarring","clashing","grating","conflicting"],"k":["at odds","at variance","atonal","contrary"],"a":["harmonious","melodious","consonant","agreeable"],"ex":["The out-of-tune guitar made the song sound harsh and dissonant.","Dissonant chords can create tension in a piece of music before it finally resolves.","His cheerful words sounded dissonant against the sad look on his face."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"dissuade","p":"verb","d":"To persuade someone not to do something.","lb":"discourage, deter","s":["discourage","deter","talk out of","advise against","put off","divert"],"k":["advise","argue against","caution","counsel"],"a":["persuade","encourage","urge","convince"],"ex":["My parents tried to dissuade me from quitting my job without another one lined up.","High ticket prices may dissuade families from going to the cinema.","The teacher dissuaded him from copying the answers by explaining the risks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"distend","p":"verb","d":"To swell or stretch outward because of pressure from the inside.","lb":"swell, expand","s":["swell","expand","bloat","inflate","balloon","bulge"],"k":["belly out","blow up","broaden","extend"],"a":["shrink","contract","deflate","shrivel"],"ex":["His stomach was distended after he ate too many sweets at the Eid party.","Veins in the legs can distend when a person stands for many hours.","The balloon distended more and more as the boy blew into it."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"distill","p":"verb","d":"To purify a liquid by heating it and cooling the vapor, or to extract the essential part of something.","lb":"purify, condense","s":["purify","refine","extract","condense","concentrate","boil down"],"k":["abstract","change","crystallize","digest"],"a":["dilute","adulterate","pad","expand"],"ex":["The school lab distills seawater to produce clean water for experiments.","She distilled three hours of lectures into a one-page summary before the exam.","Perfume makers distill flower petals to capture their scent in oil."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"distinct","p":"adjective","d":"Clearly different from something else, or easy to see, hear or notice.","lb":"separate, clear","s":["separate","different","individual","clear","definite","noticeable"],"k":["apparent","chiseled","conspicuous","crisp"],"a":["similar","identical","vague","indistinct"],"ex":["The twins look alike, but their personalities are quite distinct.","I could hear a distinct knock at the door, so I went to open it.","Bangla has several distinct dialects, such as those of Chattogram and Sylhet."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"distinguish","p":"verb","d":"To recognize the difference between two or more things or people.","lb":"tell apart, differentiate","s":["differentiate","tell apart","discriminate","separate","discern","tell the difference"],"k":["characterize","demarcate","detect","discover"],"a":["confuse","mix up","confound","blur"],"ex":["Young children cannot always distinguish between a real danger and an imaginary one.","It is hard to distinguish the twins unless you look at their haircuts.","In poor light, I could not distinguish a green bus from a blue one."],"b":336,"y":1},{"w":"distress","p":"noun","d":"Extreme worry, pain or sadness.","lb":"suffering, anxiety","s":["anguish","suffering","anxiety","agony","torment","misery"],"k":["affliction","grief","ordeal","pain"],"a":["comfort","ease","relief","calm"],"ex":["The child's cries of distress brought the neighbors running to the door.","Fireworks cause distress to many pets, which hide under beds or sofas.","Her face showed deep distress when she heard that the flight had been canceled."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"disunity","p":"noun","d":"A lack of agreement and cooperation among the members of a group.","lb":"division, discord","s":["division","discord","disagreement","dissension","conflict","disharmony"],"k":["breakdown","clash","disarray","dispute"],"a":["unity","harmony","agreement","solidarity"],"ex":["Disunity among the players cost the team the championship.","Family disunity grew after the argument over the inheritance of the land.","Constant quarrels created disunity in the student club."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dither","p":"verb","d":"To hesitate or be unable to make a decision, usually over something small.","lb":"hesitate, waver","s":["hesitate","waver","vacillate","dally","procrastinate","hem and haw"],"k":["delay","dilly-dally","flap","fluctuate"],"a":["decide","resolve","commit","act"],"ex":["Stop dithering and choose a flavor, because the ice-cream shop is closing in five minutes.","I dithered for an hour over which shirt to wear to the interview.","While the manager dithered, the competitor launched its new product."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"diurnal","p":"adjective","d":"Happening during the day, or happening once every day.","lb":"daily, daytime","s":["daily","daytime","everyday","quotidian","regular"],"k":["active by day","circadian","habitual","light"],"a":["nocturnal","nightly","nighttime"],"ex":["Butterflies are diurnal, so you will see them in gardens in the morning sun.","Most songbirds are diurnal and fall silent as soon as the sun goes down.","The diurnal temperature range in the desert is huge, with scorching days and freezing nights."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"diverge","p":"verb","d":"To separate and go in different directions, or to become different from something.","lb":"split, branch off","s":["split","branch off","part","separate","fork","deviate"],"k":["bifurcate","break away","divide","drift apart"],"a":["converge","meet","merge","agree"],"ex":["The road diverges at the bridge: one branch goes to the city and the other to the village.","Our tastes diverge when it comes to music: I like jazz and she likes pop.","After school, the friends' paths diverged, with one going abroad and the other staying at home."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"divergent","p":"adjective","d":"Developing or moving in different directions; differing from each other or from a standard.","lb":"differing, conflicting","s":["differing","different","conflicting","contrasting","disparate","varying"],"k":["branching","contrary","distinct","radiating"],"a":["similar","identical","alike","matching"],"ex":["The committee members held divergent views on how to spend the budget.","After college, the two friends took divergent paths, one into medicine and the other into art.","Divergent opinions about the menu made it hard to plan the party."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"diverse","p":"adjective","d":"Made up of many different kinds of people or things.","lb":"varied, different","s":["varied","assorted","mixed","miscellaneous","varying","different"],"k":["eclectic","kaleidoscopic","manifold","motley"],"a":["uniform","similar","identical","homogeneous"],"ex":["Dhaka University attracts a diverse group of students from every district.","The market sells a diverse range of fruit, from lychees to pineapples.","A diverse team can solve problems from many different angles."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"divest","p":"verb","d":"To take away a title, power or possession from someone, or to sell off what you own.","lb":"strip, deprive","s":["strip","deprive","dispossess","rid","relieve","remove"],"k":["cede","disinvest","dispose of","forfeit"],"a":["invest","endow","equip","clothe"],"ex":["The board divested the manager of his authority after the audit found serious mistakes.","The fund plans to divest its shares in the tobacco companies by the end of the year.","The thieves divested the traveler of his wallet and phone."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"divine","p":"verb","d":"To discover or guess something by intuition or insight, without clear evidence.","lb":"guess, intuit","s":["guess","perceive","sense","deduce","foresee","infer"],"k":["assume","augur","comprehend","detect"],"a":[],"ex":["My mother could always divine when I was hiding bad news.","From the way he kept looking at the door, she divined that he wanted to leave.","It was impossible to divine what the shopkeeper was thinking from his blank face."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"divulge","p":"verb","d":"To tell someone information that was supposed to be kept secret.","lb":"reveal, disclose","s":["reveal","disclose","leak","let out","make known","confide"],"k":["break","bring out","discover","get around"],"a":["conceal","hide","withhold","keep secret"],"ex":["Bank staff are not allowed to divulge customers' account details.","Nadia promised not to divulge the surprise party to her brother.","The journalist refused to divulge the name of his source."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"dizzy","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling as if everything is spinning around you, so that you may fall over.","lb":"giddy, lightheaded","s":["giddy","lightheaded","faint","woozy","unsteady","wobbly"],"k":["frivolous","ill","sick","swooning"],"a":["steady","stable","balanced","composed"],"ex":["I felt dizzy after standing up too quickly from the floor.","The roller coaster made my little brother so dizzy that he sat down on the grass.","She had a dizzy spell in the heat and had to sit down in the shade."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"docile","p":"adjective","d":"Quiet, gentle and willing to obey or be controlled, with little argument.","lb":"obedient, gentle","s":["obedient","compliant","meek","submissive","tame","manageable"],"k":["acquiescent","agreeable","amenable","biddable"],"a":["stubborn","unruly","defiant","rebellious"],"ex":["The village cow was so docile that even small children could lead her to the pond.","Despite its size, the dog is docile and sits quietly while visitors pet it.","The new employees were docile at first, but soon began to question the unfair rules."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"doctrinaire","p":"adjective","d":"Rigidly sticking to a theory or set of beliefs without thinking about practical reality.","lb":"dogmatic, rigid","s":["dogmatic","rigid","inflexible","uncompromising","fanatical","hidebound"],"k":["fundamentalist","ideological","informative","instructive"],"a":["flexible","pragmatic","adaptable","practical"],"ex":["The new manager's doctrinaire approach ignored what the workers actually needed on the shop floor.","A doctrinaire teacher insists on one method of solving problems and rejects any other.","Her doctrinaire diet rules made family meals stressful, since nobody could eat what she banned."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"doctrine","p":"noun","d":"A belief or set of beliefs taught and accepted by a group, such as a church, party or school of thought.","lb":"belief, teaching","s":["creed","belief","teaching","principle","dogma","ideology"],"k":["canon","conviction","gospel","ism"],"a":[],"ex":["The coach's doctrine is simple: practise hard, play fair and never blame the referee.","Students of philosophy study many doctrines, from Stoicism to existentialism.","The doctrine of non-violence shaped many peaceful movements across the world."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"document","p":"verb","d":"To record something in writing, photographs or other forms so that there is clear evidence of it.","lb":"record, report","s":["record","register","chronicle","report","detail","log"],"k":["archive","check in","enroll","enter"],"a":[],"ex":["Photographers documented the damage left by the flood in dozens of villages.","Keep your receipts and document every repair so you can prove the cost later.","The nurse carefully documented the patient's temperature every two hours."],"b":419,"y":0},{"w":"dodge","p":"verb","d":"To move quickly aside to avoid something, or to cleverly avoid a duty or a difficult question.","lb":"avoid, sidestep","s":["sidestep","evade","duck","avoid","swerve","shirk"],"k":["circumvent","escape","fudge","hedge"],"a":["face","confront","meet","tackle"],"ex":["The cyclist dodged a pothole at the last second and kept riding.","Rafi dodged the cricket ball just before it hit the wall behind him.","The manager dodged the question about layoffs by changing the subject."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"doggerel","p":"noun","d":"Poor, silly verse that is badly written but often funny.","lb":"bad verse, jingle","s":["bad verse","jingle","rhyme","silly verse","trivial poetry","rhymed nonsense"],"k":["couplet","ditty","jangle","light verse"],"a":[],"ex":["He wrote doggerel for his sister's birthday card, and everyone laughed at the silly rhymes.","The advertisement's doggerel was so catchy that children sang it all day.","Her early poems were mostly doggerel, but she improved with practice."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"dogmatic","p":"adjective","d":"Stating your opinions as if they are certainly true and refusing to consider other views.","lb":"opinionated, rigid","s":["opinionated","rigid","inflexible","doctrinaire","dictatorial","stubborn"],"k":["adamant","bigoted","headstrong","immovable"],"a":["flexible","tolerant","adaptable","reasonable"],"ex":["My uncle is dogmatic about diet and will not listen to any other advice.","A dogmatic teacher punishes students who suggest a different way to solve the problem.","Do not be dogmatic about the plan; we may need to change it if the weather turns bad."],"b":17,"y":0},{"w":"doldrums","p":"noun","d":"A state of sadness, boredom or lack of activity, when nothing seems to be improving.","lb":"slump, low spirits","s":["slump","gloom","depression","stagnation","malaise","dullness"],"k":["blahs","economic crisis","ennui","funk"],"a":["boom","high spirits","excitement","prosperity"],"ex":["The shop has been in the doldrums since a big new mall opened nearby.","After the exams ended, I spent a week in the doldrums with nothing to do.","The football team has been in the doldrums ever since it lost its best player."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"doleful","p":"adjective","d":"Looking, sounding or feeling very sad and full of sorrow.","lb":"sad, mournful","s":["sad","mournful","sorrowful","gloomy","melancholy","woeful"],"k":["depressed","despondent","dolorous","funereal"],"a":["cheerful","joyful","happy","merry"],"ex":["The old man sang a doleful song about the village he had left behind.","She gave a doleful look when she saw her low marks.","The doleful sound of the ferry horn drifted across the foggy river."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dolt","p":"noun","d":"A stupid person who is slow to understand things.","lb":"fool, idiot","s":["fool","idiot","dunce","blockhead","dimwit","simpleton"],"k":["ass","bonehead","chump","dullard"],"a":["genius","scholar","intellectual","brain"],"ex":["I felt like a complete dolt when I realised I had locked my keys inside the car.","Don't be such a dolt; read the instructions before you start the machine!","He called himself a dolt for forgetting his sister's birthday for the second year in a row."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"domestic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the home or family; also, relating to one's own country rather than foreign countries.","lb":"home, national","s":["household","home","family","internal","national","native"],"k":["familial","home-based","homebound","homey"],"a":["foreign","international","overseas","external"],"ex":["He shares domestic chores like cooking and cleaning equally with his wife.","Domestic flights between Dhaka and Chattogram take less than an hour.","The factory sells most of its goods in the domestic market, not abroad."],"b":400,"y":0},{"w":"dominate","p":"verb","d":"To have the most power, influence or importance in a situation or place.","lb":"control, command","s":["control","command","rule","govern","overshadow","prevail"],"k":["eclipse","manage","order","overlook"],"a":["submit","yield","follow","serve"],"ex":["One loud student tends to dominate every group discussion.","The home team dominated the game from the first minute.","Two large companies dominate the mobile phone market."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"dormant","p":"adjective","d":"Temporarily inactive or not growing, but able to become active again later.","lb":"inactive, sleeping","s":["inactive","sleeping","latent","asleep","resting","hibernating"],"k":["dozing","fallow","passive","slumbering"],"a":["active","awake","erupting","growing"],"ex":["The volcano has been dormant for centuries, but scientists still monitor it.","Many seeds stay dormant in the soil until the monsoon rains arrive.","My old bank account has been dormant for years, so the bank closed it."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"dotage","p":"noun","d":"The weak, forgetful period of very old age, when a person's mind is no longer sharp.","lb":"old age, senility","s":["senility","old age","second childhood","infirmity","senescence"],"k":["age","autumn years","declining years","dementia"],"a":["youth","prime","vigor"],"ex":["In his dotage, my great-uncle often forgot our names but still remembered every old song.","The retired judge, now in his dotage, repeated the same story three times at dinner.","She promised herself she would save enough money to live comfortably in her dotage."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dour","p":"adjective","d":"Serious, unfriendly and gloomy in manner or appearance.","lb":"gloomy, stern","s":["gloomy","stern","sullen","severe","grim","glum"],"k":["austere","dark","dim","dismal"],"a":["cheerful","friendly","jolly","warm"],"ex":["The dour clerk barely looked up when I asked a question.","He wore a dour expression all morning, so nobody dared to joke with him.","Their dour landlord never smiled, even when we paid the rent early."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"downcast","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling sad and discouraged, often with your eyes looking downward.","lb":"dejected, sad","s":["dejected","depressed","despondent","glum","gloomy","crestfallen"],"k":["blue","discouraged","down in the mouth","downhearted"],"a":["cheerful","happy","elated","upbeat"],"ex":["He looked downcast after reading the low marks on his test paper.","She walked home with downcast eyes, afraid to tell her parents.","The team was downcast after losing the final by a single point."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"downgrade","p":"verb","d":"To move someone or something to a lower level, rank or value.","lb":"lower, demote","s":["lower","reduce","degrade","devalue","relegate","belittle"],"k":["bring down","debase","depreciate","diminish"],"a":["upgrade","promote","raise","elevate"],"ex":["The rating agency downgraded the country's credit score after the budget shock.","The airline downgraded me to economy class even though I had paid for business class.","After the poor review, the website downgraded the hotel from four stars to three."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"downplay","p":"verb","d":"To make something seem less important or serious than it really is.","lb":"minimize, understate","s":["minimize","play down","understate","belittle","trivialize","make light of"],"k":["curtail","decrease","inform","lessen"],"a":["exaggerate","overstate","emphasize","highlight"],"ex":["The airline tried to downplay the delay by calling it a short wait.","He downplayed his injury so that the coach would let him play.","Don't downplay your achievements in the interview; explain what you did."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"draconian","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely strict and severe, especially of laws or punishments that seem too cruel for the offence.","lb":"harsh, severe","s":["harsh","severe","cruel","strict","brutal","oppressive"],"k":["hardline","iron-fisted","rigorous","stern"],"a":["lenient","mild","gentle","merciful"],"ex":["Students complained that the draconian dress code banned even plain wristbands.","The city's draconian parking fines left drivers furious.","Draconian cost-cutting meant that staff could not even order new pens."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dread","p":"verb","d":"To feel very afraid or anxious about something that is going to happen.","lb":"fear greatly","s":["fear","be afraid of","be terrified of","shrink from","worry about","quail at"],"k":["agonize over","be apprehensive about","be wary of","brood over"],"a":["welcome","relish","embrace","look forward to"],"ex":["I dread the dentist's chair, even though a check-up only takes ten minutes.","Rafi dreads speaking in front of the whole class.","She dreaded telling her parents about the broken window."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"droll","p":"adjective","d":"Amusing in an odd, quiet or unexpected way.","lb":"amusing, quirky","s":["amusing","funny","comical","witty","whimsical","wry"],"k":["comic","deadpan","dry","entertaining"],"a":["serious","solemn","dull","humorless"],"ex":["My uncle has a droll way of telling stories, with a straight face and a surprise ending.","The teacher's droll remark about homework made even the sleepy students laugh.","She wrote a droll review of the film that made her friends laugh out loud."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"drone","p":"verb","d":"To make a continuous, low humming sound.","lb":"hum, buzz","s":["hum","buzz","thrum","purr","murmur","vibrate"],"k":["drum","go","hiss","pound"],"a":[],"ex":["The old ceiling fan droned all night, so I could hardly sleep.","During load-shedding, the generator droned outside the shop until the power returned.","A plane droned high above the field while the children played cricket."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dross","p":"noun","d":"Worthless or low-quality material that should be thrown away.","lb":"waste, rubbish","s":["rubbish","waste","trash","junk","refuse","slag"],"k":["detritus","garbage","impurity","leftovers"],"a":["treasure","gold","cream"],"ex":["The jeweller melted the metal to remove the dross and keep the pure gold.","My inbox is full of dross, so important emails are easy to miss.","Most of the programmes on television are dross, so we hardly ever watch it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"drown","p":"verb","d":"To die because you are under water and cannot breathe.","lb":"submerge, suffocate","s":["suffocate","asphyxiate","go under","sink","submerge","perish"],"k":["cover","go down","overwhelm","smother"],"a":["survive","float","be rescued","swim"],"ex":["Swimming lessons help children avoid drowning in ponds and rivers.","The lifeguard dived into the pool and saved a boy who was about to drown.","Parents in the village warn small children to stay away from the pond during the monsoon, because a child can drown quickly."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dubious","p":"adjective","d":"Doubtful or suspicious; not certain to be true, honest or good.","lb":"doubtful, questionable","s":["doubtful","questionable","suspect","suspicious","uncertain","iffy"],"k":["apocryphal","bogus","dodgy","improbable"],"a":["certain","reliable","trustworthy","genuine"],"ex":["I am dubious about buying a phone from a seller with no shop address.","The restaurant's hygiene was dubious, so we left without ordering.","He made a dubious claim that he could cure any illness in one day."],"b":82,"y":2},{"w":"dull","p":"adjective","d":"Not interesting or exciting; lacking energy or lively qualities.","lb":"boring, uninteresting","s":["boring","tedious","dreary","uninteresting","monotonous","lifeless"],"k":["arid","blunt","blunted","bovine"],"a":["exciting","lively","interesting","stimulating"],"ex":["The lecture was so dull that half the students fell asleep.","Without friends, the long train journey felt dull and endless.","He wrote a dull report full of numbers and no explanations."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"duly","p":"adverb","d":"In the proper or expected way, and at the right time.","lb":"properly, as expected","s":["properly","correctly","rightly","appropriately","fittingly","as expected"],"k":["accurately","aptly","as required","conscientiously"],"a":["improperly","wrongly","inappropriately","incorrectly"],"ex":["The form was duly signed and sent to the admission office.","She was duly elected class captain after the vote.","We duly arrived at the station at six, just as planned."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"dupe","p":"noun","d":"A person who is easily tricked or used by others.","lb":"sucker, victim","s":["sucker","pawn","fool","victim","patsy","stooge"],"k":["chump","cod","dope","easy mark"],"a":[],"ex":["The old man was a dupe of the online scammers and lost his savings.","She refused to be anyone's dupe and checked every claim before signing.","The fake company used students as dupes, promising jobs that did not exist."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"duplicity","p":"noun","d":"Dishonest behavior in which you say or do one thing while secretly planning another.","lb":"deceit, double-dealing","s":["deceit","deception","treachery","dishonesty","trickery","guile"],"k":["artifice","bad faith","chicanery","dissembling"],"a":["honesty","sincerity","candor","openness"],"ex":["Nadia was shocked by her friend's duplicity when she learned that he had shared her plans with a rival.","The salesman's duplicity was clear when he smiled at customers but mocked them behind their backs.","I could not forgive his duplicity: he praised my plan to my face and criticized it to the boss."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"duress","p":"noun","d":"The use of force or threats to make someone do something against their will.","lb":"coercion, pressure","s":["coercion","compulsion","force","pressure","intimidation","threat"],"k":["blackmail","bludgeoning","browbeating","bullying"],"a":["free will","choice","consent","volition"],"ex":["He claimed he signed the contract under duress after being threatened.","A confession made under duress is not accepted as reliable evidence in court.","The witness said she had changed her story only because she was under duress."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"dust","p":"noun","d":"Tiny dry particles of earth or dirt that lie on surfaces or float in the air.","lb":"fine powder","s":["grime","dirt","powder","soot","grit","sand"],"k":["debris","filth","grunge","junk"],"a":[],"ex":["A thick layer of dust covered the books on the old shelf.","The truck raised a cloud of dust on the dry village road.","Dust in the air makes my brother sneeze every morning."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"dwindling","p":"adjective","d":"Gradually becoming smaller, fewer or weaker.","lb":"shrinking, decreasing","s":["shrinking","decreasing","declining","diminishing","waning","fading"],"k":["contracting","petering out","sinking","sliding"],"a":["growing","increasing","rising","swelling"],"ex":["With dwindling supplies of clean water, the village had to dig a new well.","The small bookshop is struggling because of dwindling numbers of customers.","As the day went on, our dwindling hope of catching the train faded away."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"earnest","p":"adjective","d":"Serious and sincere in what you say or do, with a strong, honest purpose.","lb":"serious, sincere","s":["serious","sincere","sober","heartfelt","solemn","committed"],"k":["acute","businesslike","dear","devout"],"a":["frivolous","flippant","insincere","casual"],"ex":["The earnest young teacher stayed after class to help every student.","He made an earnest request for more time to repay the loan.","Her earnest face showed how much the interview meant to her."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ebb","p":"verb","d":"To flow back, as the sea does, or to slowly become weaker or less.","lb":"recede, decline","s":["recede","retreat","wane","subside","fade","decline"],"k":["abate","decrease","draw back","fall away"],"a":["flow","rise","surge","swell"],"ex":["As the tide ebbed, children ran onto the wet sand to look for shells.","Her excitement slowly ebbed as the long meeting dragged on.","The pain in his knee began to ebb after he rested and took some medicine."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ebullient","p":"adjective","d":"Full of cheerful energy and excitement.","lb":"enthusiastic, exuberant","s":["exuberant","enthusiastic","lively","cheerful","bubbly","buoyant"],"k":["active","animated","chirpy","dynamic"],"a":["gloomy","subdued","depressed","apathetic"],"ex":["Rafi was ebullient after hearing that he had passed the admission test.","The ebullient crowd cheered and waved flags as the team bus arrived.","Our ebullient teacher greets every class with a joke and a wide smile."],"b":533,"y":0},{"w":"eccentric","p":"adjective","d":"Behaving in an unusual way that is different from what most people think of as normal, often harmlessly.","lb":"odd, unconventional","s":["odd","peculiar","unconventional","quirky","strange","idiosyncratic"],"k":["bizarre","curious","flaky","freakish"],"a":["conventional","normal","ordinary","conformist"],"ex":["My eccentric uncle wears a woolen hat even in the hot summer.","The professor was famously eccentric and kept a parrot that answered the telephone.","She has the eccentric habit of eating dessert before the main meal."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"ecclesiastical","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the Christian church or its priests and officials.","lb":"church, clerical","s":["clerical","religious","priestly","church"],"k":["canonical","devotional","holy","monastic"],"a":["secular","lay","civil","temporal"],"ex":["The museum has a collection of ecclesiastical robes and silver cups from old churches.","The village's ecclesiastical records show births and marriages from the 1700s.","Historians studied ecclesiastical law to understand how church courts once worked."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"eclectic","p":"adjective","d":"Choosing or using ideas, styles or tastes from many different sources.","lb":"diverse, varied","s":["diverse","varied","mixed","broad","assorted","multifaceted"],"k":["different","discriminating","heterogeneous","miscellaneous"],"a":["narrow","limited","uniform","restricted"],"ex":["Her taste in music is eclectic: she listens to folk songs, jazz and classical on the same day.","The café has an eclectic mix of furniture, from old wooden chairs to modern lamps.","The library's eclectic collection includes cookbooks, science fiction and old maps."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"eclipse","p":"verb","d":"To make someone or something seem less important, talented or impressive by being much better or greater.","lb":"outshine, overshadow","s":["outshine","overshadow","surpass","upstage","dwarf","exceed"],"k":["brood","bulk large","dominate","eliminate"],"a":[],"ex":["The younger sister's talent soon eclipsed that of her older brother in the school choir.","Online shopping has eclipsed visits to the market for many busy families.","His loud personality eclipsed everyone else at the meeting."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"economical","p":"adjective","d":"Using money, time or resources carefully, without waste.","lb":"thrifty, cost-effective","s":["thrifty","frugal","sparing","efficient","inexpensive","budget"],"k":["careful","conserving","cost-saving","low-cost"],"a":["wasteful","extravagant","expensive","costly"],"ex":["A small, fuel-efficient motorbike is the most economical way to travel to work.","She is economical with her words and never wastes time on small talk.","Cooking at home is far more economical than eating out every day."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"ecstatic","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling extremely happy, excited and full of joy, often because of good news.","lb":"overjoyed, thrilled","s":["overjoyed","elated","thrilled","euphoric","jubilant","rapturous"],"k":["beatific","enraptured","exultant","flushed with joy"],"a":["miserable","despondent","gloomy","dejected"],"ex":["The whole class was ecstatic when the teacher cancelled the surprise test.","My little sister was ecstatic about her first bicycle.","Rafi was ecstatic to hear that he had passed the admission test."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"edgy","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling nervous, tense and easily upset.","lb":"nervous, tense","s":["nervous","tense","jumpy","anxious","uneasy","jittery"],"k":["apprehensive","fidgety","fretful","highly strung"],"a":["relaxed","calm","easygoing","composed"],"ex":["Everyone felt edgy while waiting for the exam results.","Too much coffee made her edgy and unable to sleep.","The passengers grew edgy as the delayed train still did not arrive."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"edible","p":"adjective","d":"Safe and good enough to be eaten.","lb":"eatable","s":["eatable","safe to eat","palatable","digestible","fit to eat","wholesome"],"k":["comestible","fresh","harmless","nontoxic"],"a":["inedible","poisonous","toxic","unfit"],"ex":["Not all wild mushrooms are edible, so never eat one you cannot identify.","The cake was burnt, but the middle was still edible.","Banana flowers are edible and are used in many Bengali dishes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"edict","p":"noun","d":"An official order or announcement given by a ruler or an authority.","lb":"decree, order","s":["decree","order","proclamation","command","ruling","mandate"],"k":["bull","charter","dictate","diktat"],"a":[],"ex":["In the history book, the emperor issued an edict forbidding anyone from leaving the city.","The headmaster's edict that no phones are allowed in class surprised the students.","The company issued an edict that all staff must be in the office by nine."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"edifice","p":"noun","d":"A large, impressive building.","lb":"building, structure","s":["building","structure","construction","monument","pile"],"k":["castle","cathedral","citadel","fortress"],"a":[],"ex":["The old library is an imposing edifice with tall stone columns.","Tourists took photos of the white marble edifice at sunset.","The bank's glass edifice dominates the city's skyline."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"edify","p":"verb","d":"To teach or improve someone morally or intellectually, in a helpful way.","lb":"enlighten, uplift","s":["enlighten","instruct","educate","uplift","improve","inform"],"k":["civilize","cultivate","guide","illuminate"],"a":["corrupt","mislead","degrade","deprave"],"ex":["The museum's guided tour was designed to edify visitors as well as entertain them.","My grandfather's stories about his village school edified us as much as they amused us.","She reads biographies of great scientists because they edify her and spark new ideas."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"efface","p":"verb","d":"To rub out or remove something completely so that it can no longer be seen or remembered.","lb":"erase, wipe out","s":["erase","rub out","wipe out","obliterate","delete","expunge"],"k":["annihilate","eliminate","score out","take"],"a":["inscribe","record","restore","preserve"],"ex":["Years of rain and wind had effaced the writing on the old stone tablet.","Nothing could efface the memory of that terrible bus journey from her mind.","The painter effaced the old marks on the wall before putting on fresh paint."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"effectual","p":"adjective","d":"Producing the result that was intended; able to do what is needed.","lb":"effective, successful","s":["effective","efficient","productive","successful","potent","powerful"],"k":["competent","impressive","legal","stiff"],"a":["ineffectual","useless","futile","ineffective"],"ex":["Rest and warm fluids were the most effectual remedy for her cold.","The new lock proved effectual, and no one has broken into the shop since.","Only an effectual plan, with clear steps and a budget, will convince the bank."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"efficacy","p":"noun","d":"The ability to produce the result that you want.","lb":"effectiveness, power","s":["effectiveness","power","potency","success","strength","efficiency"],"k":["authority","benefit","dominance","effectualness"],"a":["futility","uselessness","weakness","failure"],"ex":["Doctors tested the efficacy of the new medicine on two hundred patients.","There is little proof of the efficacy of expensive hair oils.","The teacher doubted the efficacy of memorizing facts without understanding them."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"effigy","p":"noun","d":"A model or statue of a person, sometimes a rough one made to be mocked or destroyed.","lb":"statue, likeness","s":["statue","likeness","image","figure","dummy","model"],"k":["bust","carving","doll","graven image"],"a":[],"ex":["In the museum, a stone effigy of a medieval knight lies on top of a carved tomb.","At the winter festival, villagers made a straw effigy of the old year and burned it at midnight.","The sculptor carved an effigy of her late grandfather from a single block of wood."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"effluvium","p":"noun","d":"An unpleasant smell or waste that flows out from something.","lb":"stench, fumes","s":["stench","odor","fumes","emanation","vapor","smell"],"k":["emission","fetor","malodor","niff"],"a":["fragrance","perfume","aroma","scent"],"ex":["A foul effluvium rose from the blocked drain after the heavy rain.","The effluvium from the leather factory made the whole neighborhood hold its breath.","Walking past the garbage dump, we were hit by an awful effluvium."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"effrontery","p":"noun","d":"Shameless boldness; rude behavior that shows no respect or embarrassment.","lb":"nerve, impudence","s":["impudence","audacity","nerve","cheek","gall","insolence"],"k":["assumption","brass neck","chutzpah","courage"],"a":["respect","politeness","humility","deference"],"ex":["He had the effrontery to ask for a discount after eating the whole meal.","It was sheer effrontery for the stranger to cut in front of the elderly people in the queue.","She had the effrontery to blame her teammates for a mistake that was her own."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"effusion","p":"noun","d":"A sudden outpouring of feeling, praise or words, with little self-control.","lb":"outpouring, outburst","s":["outpouring","outburst","gush","flood","torrent","eruption"],"k":["blowup","deluge","ebullience","effervescence"],"a":["restraint","reserve","reticence","suppression"],"ex":["The winner's speech was an effusion of gratitude toward her parents, teachers and friends.","After the long separation, their meeting at the airport was an effusion of tears and laughter.","His letter was a long effusion of praise for the hospitality he had received."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"egalitarian","p":"adjective","d":"Based on the belief that all people should have equal rights and opportunities.","lb":"equal, fair","s":["equal","equitable","fair","democratic","classless","just"],"k":["collectivist","communal","humanitarian","inclusive"],"a":["elitist","hierarchical","authoritarian","unequal"],"ex":["Our office has an egalitarian culture where interns and managers eat lunch together.","The school wants an egalitarian system in which every child gets the same chances.","In an egalitarian family, both parents share the housework equally."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"egocentric","p":"adjective","d":"Thinking only about oneself and one's own needs, and unable to see things from other people's point of view.","lb":"self-centered, selfish","s":["selfish","egotistical","narcissistic","conceited"],"k":["egomaniacal","inward-looking","megalomaniacal","preening"],"a":["selfless","altruistic","considerate","unselfish"],"ex":["Her egocentric behavior made group projects difficult, because she never listened to anyone else's ideas.","Small children are naturally egocentric and often believe the world revolves around them.","He is so egocentric that he talked about his own promotion throughout his friend's wedding dinner."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"egregious","p":"adjective","d":"Shockingly bad, in a way that is very easy to notice.","lb":"outrageous, flagrant","s":["outrageous","flagrant","glaring","shocking","blatant","gross"],"k":["barefaced","brazen","conspicuous","crying"],"a":["minor","slight","trivial","excellent"],"ex":["The printer made an egregious mistake: the wrong date appeared on every invitation.","Charging customers twice for the same meal was an egregious error by the restaurant.","The teacher said that copying an entire essay from the internet was an egregious case of cheating."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"elated","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely happy and excited, usually because something good has happened.","lb":"overjoyed, thrilled","s":["overjoyed","thrilled","delighted","ecstatic","jubilant","euphoric"],"k":["blissful","exhilarated","glad","gleeful"],"a":["dejected","depressed","miserable","despondent"],"ex":["Rafi was elated when he saw his name on the admission list.","The whole family felt elated after hearing that Nadia had won the scholarship.","She was elated by the crowd's cheering after her first big speech."],"b":66,"y":2},{"w":"elation","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of great joy, pride and excitement, usually after good news or success.","lb":"joy, delight","s":["joy","delight","euphoria","jubilation","exhilaration","glee"],"k":["bliss","happiness","high spirits","lightness"],"a":["despair","misery","gloom","sadness"],"ex":["She felt pure elation when she found her name on the admission test result list.","The crowd erupted in elation as the home team scored in the final minute.","There was elation in the office when the manager announced that everyone would get an Eid bonus."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"electorate","p":"noun","d":"All the people in a country or area who are allowed to vote in an election.","lb":"voters, citizens","s":["voters","voting public","constituents","citizens","constituency","voting population"],"k":["body politic","citizenry","franchise","people"],"a":[],"ex":["Almost the whole electorate in our town had voted by noon.","Reporters asked members of the electorate what mattered most to them before the election.","A young electorate means that issues like tuition fees can decide a campaign."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"elegy","p":"noun","d":"A sad poem or song, especially one written to remember someone who has died.","lb":"lament, mourning poem","s":["lament","dirge","requiem","tribute","memorial poem"],"k":["epicedium","funeral poem","keening","ode"],"a":[],"ex":["The poet wrote an elegy for his teacher, thanking him for years of guidance.","In class, we read an elegy about a village that disappeared under rising water.","The band played an elegy at the memorial service for the school's old caretaker."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"elemental","p":"adjective","d":"Basic and powerful, like the natural forces of fire, water, wind and earth; fundamental in nature.","lb":"basic, primal","s":["fundamental","basic","primal","primitive","essential","raw"],"k":["basal","central","first","instinctive"],"a":["complex","artificial","secondary","refined"],"ex":["Watching the cyclone, we felt the elemental power of wind and water.","Hunger is an elemental human need, just like thirst and sleep.","Her poems deal with elemental feelings such as fear, love and loss."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"elicit","p":"verb","d":"To get a reaction, answer or piece of information from someone, often with some effort.","lb":"draw out, evoke","s":["evoke","draw out","extract","obtain","provoke","bring out"],"k":["arouse","awaken","conjure","construe"],"a":["suppress","stifle","repress","withhold"],"ex":["The teacher asked clear questions to elicit answers from the shy students.","The comedian's joke elicited loud laughter from the audience.","Police tried to elicit more details from the witness without frightening her."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"elite","p":"noun","d":"A small group of people who have more power, wealth or ability than most others in a society.","lb":"upper class, best","s":["upper class","aristocracy","cream","best","pick","high society"],"k":["establishment","gentry","grandees","hierarchy"],"a":["masses","commoners","rank and file","majority"],"ex":["Only a tiny elite can afford to send their children to such expensive private schools.","Critics say the festival is organised for the cultural elite, not for ordinary families.","She trained for ten years to join the elite of international chess players."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"elliptical","p":"adjective","d":"Leaving out words so that the meaning is hard to follow; also, shaped like a flattened circle.","lb":"vague, terse","s":["cryptic","terse","obscure","vague","abbreviated","oblique"],"k":["abstruse","allusive","ambiguous","brief"],"a":["explicit","clear","plain","detailed"],"ex":["His elliptical reply, \"We'll see,\" left everyone unsure whether he had agreed to come.","The poet's elliptical style leaves out so many words that readers must guess the connections.","The note was elliptical, just \"usual place, usual time,\" but my sister knew exactly what it meant."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"elocution","p":"noun","d":"The skill of speaking clearly and effectively in public, with good pronunciation and voice control.","lb":"diction, public speaking","s":["diction","oratory","delivery","articulation","speech","enunciation"],"k":["cadence","declamation","intonation","locution"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandfather took elocution lessons to improve his voice for the radio.","The school holds an annual elocution contest where students recite poems.","Clear elocution helps a teacher be understood in a big classroom."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"eloquence","p":"noun","d":"The ability to speak or write in a clear, fluent and persuasive way.","lb":"fluent speech","s":["oratory","rhetoric","command of language","silver tongue","smoothness"],"k":["articulateness","expressive style","facility","flair"],"a":["awkwardness"],"ex":["The debate champion won the final with her eloquence and calm logic.","The speaker moved the audience to tears with the eloquence of his words.","He lacks eloquence, but everyone trusts what he says."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"elude","p":"verb","d":"To escape from or avoid someone or something, often cleverly, or to be out of reach of someone's memory or understanding.","lb":"evade, escape","s":["evade","escape","dodge","avoid","shake off","slip away from"],"k":["bilk","circumvent","duck","fudge"],"a":["catch","capture","grasp","understand"],"ex":["The thief eluded the police for weeks by changing his hiding place every night.","The answer to the last puzzle eluded me, no matter how long I thought about it.","Sleep eluded her the night before the big exam."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"elusive","p":"adjective","d":"Difficult to find, catch or achieve, because it keeps escaping or avoiding you.","lb":"slippery, evasive","s":["slippery","evasive","fleeting","shifty","intangible","baffling"],"k":["artful","difficult","hard","knotty"],"a":["obvious","tangible","accessible","easy to find"],"ex":["The Bengal tiger is elusive, and most visitors to the Sundarbans never see one.","A good night's sleep has been elusive for me during the exam season.","The correct answer proved elusive, even after Rafi checked all his notes."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"emaciate","p":"verb","d":"To make a person or animal extremely thin and weak, usually through illness or lack of food.","lb":"make thin, waste","s":["waste","starve","wither","shrivel","weaken","debilitate"],"k":["attenuate","dry up","famish","pare down"],"a":["fatten","nourish","strengthen","build up"],"ex":["Months of illness had emaciated him, and his clothes now hung loose on his body.","The rescue team found an emaciated puppy under the bridge and took it to a vet.","Hunger and a lack of clean water can emaciate even the strongest adults."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"emanate","p":"verb","d":"To come out from a source, as a smell, sound, light, feeling or idea does.","lb":"issue, radiate","s":["issue","come out","flow","radiate","originate","arise"],"k":["appear","breathe out","come","come up"],"a":["absorb","enter"],"ex":["A delicious smell of frying onions emanated from the kitchen.","Loud music emanated from the wedding hall across the road.","The rumours seem to emanate from one person in the office."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"emancipate","p":"verb","d":"To free someone from legal, social or political restrictions, or from slavery.","lb":"liberate, free","s":["liberate","free","release","unchain","set free","enfranchise"],"k":["absolve","deliver from bondage","discharge","disenthrall"],"a":["enslave","confine","imprison","oppress"],"ex":["The new law emancipated women from many old restrictions on owning property.","Education can emancipate people from poverty and fear.","In the nineteenth century, many countries passed laws to emancipate enslaved people."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"embargo","p":"noun","d":"An official order that stops trade with another country, or that bans something for a period of time.","lb":"ban, blockade","s":["ban","prohibition","blockade","boycott","restriction","bar"],"k":["blacklist","censor","freeze","moratorium"],"a":["permission","license","approval","clearance"],"ex":["The government placed an embargo on the export of rice during the shortage.","The trade embargo made imported medicine very expensive for months.","The report is under embargo until Monday morning, so journalists cannot publish it yet."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"embellish","p":"verb","d":"To make something more attractive by adding decoration, or to make a story more interesting with extra details that may not be true.","lb":"decorate, exaggerate","s":["decorate","adorn","ornament","garnish","enhance","exaggerate"],"k":["alter","change","deck","grace"],"a":["simplify","strip","understate","deface"],"ex":["The tailor embellished the wedding dress with tiny gold beads along the sleeves.","Uncle likes to embellish his stories, so the fish he caught grows bigger every year.","The cook embellished the plain rice with fried onions, nuts and raisins."],"b":99,"y":1},{"w":"embezzler","p":"noun","d":"A person who secretly steals money that has been trusted to them, usually from an employer.","lb":"fraudster, thief","s":["thief","swindler","crook","fraudster","stealer"],"k":["cheater","criminal","deceiver","defalcator"],"a":[],"ex":["The accountant turned out to be an embezzler who had stolen a huge sum from the company.","Police arrested the embezzler after auditors found false entries in the books.","The club treasurer was an embezzler; he used the members' fees to pay his own bills."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"embodied","p":"adjective","d":"Having a body or a clear physical form; shown in a real, visible way.","lb":"in physical form","s":["incarnate","personified","tangible","physical","bodily","concrete"],"k":["actualized","corporal","corporate","corporeal"],"a":["disembodied","abstract","spiritual"],"ex":["To the young players, their old coach was discipline embodied.","The statue stood in the square as honesty embodied for generations of students.","In the story, the villain is evil embodied, with no kindness at all."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"embolden","p":"verb","d":"To give someone more courage or confidence to do something.","lb":"encourage, hearten","s":["encourage","inspire","fortify","strengthen","motivate","reassure"],"k":["animate","bolster","boost","buck up"],"a":["discourage","intimidate","deter","dismay"],"ex":["The teacher's praise emboldened the shy girl to speak in class.","Emboldened by his first sale, the young trader decided to open a second stall.","Her friends' support emboldened her to apply for the manager's post."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"embroil","p":"verb","d":"To involve someone deeply in an argument, fight or difficult situation.","lb":"involve, entangle","s":["involve","entangle","implicate","mix up","drag in","ensnare"],"k":["bog down","drag","hook","mire"],"a":["extricate","free","disentangle","exempt"],"ex":["I do not want to be embroiled in my neighbors' quarrel about the fence.","The company became embroiled in a long legal battle over the contract.","Don't embroil me in your argument; I was not even there."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"embryonic","p":"adjective","d":"Still at a very early stage of development and not yet fully formed.","lb":"undeveloped, early","s":["undeveloped","rudimentary","immature","nascent","budding","fledgling"],"k":["developing","emerging","formative","germinal"],"a":["developed","mature","advanced","established"],"ex":["Our start-up is still embryonic, with only two members and a rough sketch of the app.","The plan for a new bus route in Dhaka is at an embryonic stage, so nothing is decided.","Her English writing was embryonic when she joined the class, but it improved quickly."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"emergence","p":"noun","d":"The process of coming into existence or becoming noticed.","lb":"appearance, rise","s":["appearance","arrival","rise","advent","dawn","development"],"k":["beginning","coming","egress","evolution"],"a":["disappearance","decline","vanishing","withdrawal"],"ex":["The emergence of smartphones changed the way students study.","Scientists watched the emergence of the butterfly from its cocoon.","The emergence of new shops along the road improved the local economy."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"emigrate","p":"verb","d":"To leave one's own country to live permanently in another one.","lb":"leave country","s":["migrate","move abroad","relocate","expatriate","settle abroad","go abroad"],"k":["abscond","decamp","depart","exile oneself"],"a":["immigrate","repatriate","return","stay"],"ex":["Many skilled workers emigrate from Bangladesh each year in search of higher wages.","After finishing her degree, Nadia decided to emigrate to Canada with her family.","His grandparents emigrated from Italy in the 1950s and opened a small bakery."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"eminent","p":"adjective","d":"Famous and respected, especially for achievements in a particular profession or field.","lb":"distinguished, prominent","s":["distinguished","prominent","renowned","famous","celebrated","respected"],"k":["famed","high","imposing","known"],"a":["unknown","obscure","insignificant","undistinguished"],"ex":["An eminent surgeon visited our college to talk about careers in medicine.","The conference was attended by eminent scholars from many countries.","She became an eminent writer, and her books are now taught in schools."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"emissary","p":"noun","d":"A person sent on a mission to represent another person, group or government.","lb":"envoy, messenger","s":["envoy","representative","messenger","ambassador","delegate","agent"],"k":["attache","go-between","intermediary","liaison"],"a":[],"ex":["The country sent a special emissary to talk about the new trade agreement.","A young emissary from the head office visited the branch to explain the new rules.","The village chief sent an emissary to the neighbouring village with a message of peace."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"empathy","p":"noun","d":"The ability to understand and share another person's feelings, as if you were in their place.","lb":"compassion, understanding","s":["compassion","understanding","sympathy","sensitivity","fellow feeling","rapport"],"k":["awareness","comprehension","kindness","perception"],"a":["apathy","indifference","callousness","coldness"],"ex":["A good doctor listens with empathy, trying to understand how the patient really feels.","The teacher showed empathy for students who were nervous about the exam.","Reading novels can build empathy by letting us see the world through other people's eyes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"emphatic","p":"adjective","d":"Said or done in a strong, clear way that leaves no doubt.","lb":"forceful, firm","s":["forceful","firm","insistent","definite","vigorous","categorical"],"k":["adamant","decided","explicit","resolute"],"a":["hesitant","uncertain","tentative","weak"],"ex":["The manager gave an emphatic no when we asked for extra holidays.","Her emphatic reply made it clear she would not change her mind.","The home team recorded an emphatic victory by ten wickets."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"empirical","p":"adjective","d":"Based on what is observed or experienced in practice, rather than on theory.","lb":"observed, experimental","s":["observational","experimental","practical","factual","firsthand","actual"],"k":["demonstrated","documented","existential","hands-on"],"a":["theoretical","hypothetical","speculative","abstract"],"ex":["The scientist needs empirical evidence, not just theory, before the claim can be accepted.","Our empirical study of bus waiting times involved timing buses at ten stops for a month.","Doctors rely on empirical data from clinical trials to decide which treatment works best."],"b":211,"y":1},{"w":"empower","p":"verb","d":"To give someone the confidence, skills or legal authority to take control or do something.","lb":"authorize, enable","s":["authorize","enable","allow","equip","entitle","license"],"k":["appoint","approve","arm","capacitate"],"a":["disable","forbid","prevent"],"ex":["Microloans empower village women to start their own small businesses.","The new law empowers tenants to challenge unfair rent increases.","Good teachers empower students to think for themselves instead of memorizing facts."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"emulate","p":"verb","d":"To copy someone's behavior or achievements because you admire them, trying to equal or surpass them.","lb":"imitate, rival","s":["imitate","copy","mimic","follow","match","rival"],"k":["ape","idolize","model oneself on","parrot"],"a":[],"ex":["Young cricketers try to emulate the great players they watch on television.","She hopes to emulate her mother's success as a surgeon.","Many small shops tried to emulate the bakery's friendly service and neat displays."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"emulation","p":"noun","d":"The effort to equal or do better than someone you admire, often by copying what they do.","lb":"imitation, rivalry","s":["imitation","rivalry","competition","copying","striving","mimicry"],"k":["ambition","aspiration","contention","contest"],"a":[],"ex":["The young cricketers practiced daily in emulation of their heroes.","Her generosity is worthy of emulation by all of us.","The students worked harder in emulation of the class topper."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"encroach","p":"verb","d":"To gradually move into someone's space, land or rights, going beyond what is allowed.","lb":"intrude, trespass","s":["intrude","trespass","infringe","impinge","invade","overstep"],"k":["advance","contravene","go on","march on"],"a":["withdraw","retreat","recede","keep off"],"ex":["Illegal shops have started to encroach on the footpath, forcing pedestrians onto the road.","Rising sea levels encroach on the coastal villages a little more every year.","The neighbor's new wall encroaches on our land by almost half a meter."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"encryption","p":"noun","d":"The process of changing information into a secret code so that only authorized people can read it.","lb":"coding, scrambling","s":["encoding","coding","scrambling","secret writing","cryptography"],"k":["codification","enciphering","encipherment","obfuscation"],"a":["decryption","decoding","deciphering"],"ex":["Messaging apps use encryption so that only you and the receiver can read your chats.","The bank protects your card details with strong encryption.","Our school's Wi-Fi uses encryption, so strangers cannot read what students send."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"endangered","p":"adjective","d":"In danger of disappearing completely, especially a species of plant or animal.","lb":"threatened, at risk","s":["threatened","at risk","vulnerable","imperilled","rare","dying out"],"k":["few and far between","hanging by a thread","in jeopardy","on the brink"],"a":["thriving","abundant","plentiful","flourishing"],"ex":["The Bengal tiger is an endangered animal, and rangers protect it in the Sundarbans.","Many river dolphins are endangered because of pollution and fishing nets.","Deforestation has left several bird species endangered across the country."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"endear","p":"verb","d":"To make someone loved or liked by other people.","lb":"win affection, charm","s":["charm","win over","captivate","attach","ingratiate","enchant"],"k":["beguile","bewitch","capture","delight"],"a":["alienate","estrange","repel","offend"],"ex":["His honesty and sense of humour endeared him to everyone in the office.","The little girl's shy smile endeared her to her new classmates at once.","Her willingness to carry groceries for elderly neighbours during the flood endeared her to the whole street."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"endemic","p":"adjective","d":"Regularly found in a particular place or among a particular group of people, and usually limited to it.","lb":"native, local","s":["native","indigenous","local","regional","localized","restricted"],"k":["aboriginal","chronic","domestic","entrenched"],"a":["foreign","exotic","alien","imported"],"ex":["Dengue fever is endemic in many tropical cities, and cases rise after the rains.","This rare orchid is endemic to a few mountain valleys and grows nowhere else on Earth.","Several species of lemur are endemic to Madagascar."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"endorse","p":"verb","d":"To say publicly that you support or approve of someone or something.","lb":"approve, support","s":["support","back","approve","recommend","champion","sanction"],"k":["assist","authorize","certify","defend"],"a":["oppose","reject","condemn","criticize"],"ex":["The school board endorsed the plan to build a new science lab.","A famous cricketer endorsed the sports drink in a television advertisement.","Our professor endorsed my scholarship application with a strong letter of recommendation."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"endure","p":"verb","d":"To suffer something painful or unpleasant patiently, without giving up.","lb":"bear, tolerate","s":["bear","tolerate","withstand","suffer","undergo","stand"],"k":["abide","allow","brave out","brook"],"a":["give up","yield","surrender","succumb"],"ex":["Patients had to endure a long wait at the crowded clinic.","Farmers endured months of drought before the first rains arrived.","I cannot endure the noise from the construction site any longer."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"enervate","p":"verb","d":"To drain someone of energy and strength, leaving them weak or tired.","lb":"weaken, exhaust","s":["weaken","exhaust","drain","tire","sap","debilitate"],"k":["deaden","deplete","droop","faze"],"a":["energize","invigorate","strengthen","refresh"],"ex":["The humid summer heat can enervate even the fittest runners.","A long day of meetings left her feeling enervated and unable to cook dinner.","Days of fever enervated him so much that he could hardly climb the stairs."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"enfranchise","p":"verb","d":"To give a person or group the right to vote.","lb":"give the vote, empower","s":["give the vote to","empower","emancipate","liberate","admit to citizenship","free"],"k":["confer rights","endow","entrust","grant suffrage"],"a":["exclude","deprive"],"ex":["Women were enfranchised in many countries during the twentieth century after long campaigns.","The new law will enfranchise young people by lowering the voting age.","Campaigners worked to enfranchise citizens living in remote areas who had no identity cards."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"engaging","p":"adjective","d":"Pleasant and attractive in a way that holds people's interest and makes them like you.","lb":"charming, appealing","s":["charming","appealing","delightful","winning","captivating","likable"],"k":["likeable","lovely","piquant","pleasing"],"a":["boring","unappealing","tedious","repellent"],"ex":["Our new teacher has an engaging manner, and even shy students enjoy speaking in her class.","The author writes in an engaging style that makes complex science easy to follow.","Rafi's engaging smile put the nervous customers at ease within seconds."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"engender","p":"verb","d":"To cause a feeling, situation or condition to exist.","lb":"cause, produce","s":["cause","produce","generate","create","provoke","breed"],"k":["beget","do","get","make"],"a":["prevent","stifle","destroy","end"],"ex":["Honest answers from the manager engendered trust among the workers.","Poor planning engendered confusion on the first day of the event.","A friendly classroom can engender a love of learning in young children."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"enhance","p":"verb","d":"To improve the quality, value or strength of something.","lb":"improve, boost","s":["improve","boost","increase","strengthen","upgrade","heighten"],"k":["ameliorate","augment","complement","deepen"],"a":["reduce","diminish","worsen","spoil"],"ex":["A few green plants can enhance the look of a small balcony.","Reading English newspapers every day will enhance your vocabulary before the GRE.","The new camera features enhance the quality of photos taken in low light."],"b":131,"y":0},{"w":"enigma","p":"noun","d":"A person, thing or situation that is mysterious and difficult to understand.","lb":"mystery, puzzle","s":["mystery","puzzle","riddle","conundrum","paradox","secret"],"k":["cipher","closed book","inscrutable thing","labyrinth"],"a":["answer","solution","explanation","clarity"],"ex":["The sudden disappearance of the ship remains an enigma to experts.","Our new neighbor is an enigma; nobody knows where he works or what he does.","Why the old clock stopped at exactly noon was an enigma to the family."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"enmity","p":"noun","d":"A deep feeling of hatred or hostility between people or groups.","lb":"hostility, hatred","s":["hostility","hatred","animosity","antagonism","ill will","bitterness"],"k":["acrimony","discord","feud","grudge"],"a":["friendship","goodwill","amity","harmony"],"ex":["Years of enmity between the two families began with a quarrel over a boundary wall.","Despite the tough match, there was no enmity between the players, who shared a meal afterward.","Her sharp comments created enmity among her colleagues."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ennui","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of tired boredom because nothing seems interesting or exciting.","lb":"boredom, weariness","s":["boredom","tedium","weariness","apathy","dullness","languor"],"k":["acedia","blahs","dissatisfaction","funk"],"a":["excitement","enthusiasm","interest","energy"],"ex":["During the long summer holidays, ennui settled over the teenagers with nothing to do.","A sense of ennui came over him as he sorted the same files for the tenth day.","The novel's hero drifts through rich parties in a state of ennui."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"enormity","p":"noun","d":"The great seriousness or wickedness of something bad, such as a crime or mistake.","lb":"evil, seriousness","s":["wickedness","atrocity","gravity","seriousness","horror","evil"],"k":["criminality","depravity","egregiousness","heinousness"],"a":["triviality","innocence","goodness","insignificance"],"ex":["The judge spoke of the enormity of the crime before announcing the sentence.","Only after the fire did the owner realize the enormity of his mistake in ignoring the safety warnings.","The enormity of the building collapse shocked the whole country."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"enormous","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely large in size, amount or degree.","lb":"huge, immense","s":["huge","immense","gigantic","vast","massive","colossal"],"k":["big","gargantuan","hefty","jumbo"],"a":["tiny","small","minute","little"],"ex":["An enormous crowd gathered at the stadium to watch the final.","The company made an enormous profit last year.","She felt enormous relief when the doctor said the tests were clear."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"enrage","p":"verb","d":"To make someone extremely angry.","lb":"anger, infuriate","s":["infuriate","anger","incense","madden","provoke","outrage"],"k":["affront","antagonize","bait","gall"],"a":["calm","soothe","placate","pacify"],"ex":["The unfair penalty enraged the football fans, who booed loudly for several minutes.","It enrages me when people talk loudly on their phones inside the library.","News of the factory dumping waste into the river enraged the villagers."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ensue","p":"verb","d":"To happen afterwards, especially as a result of something that has just taken place.","lb":"follow, result","s":["follow","result","arise","happen","develop","come next"],"k":["appear","come up","originate","prove"],"a":["precede","come before","lead up to"],"ex":["A heated argument ensued when two drivers both claimed the last parking space.","When the lights went out during the concert, confusion ensued, but staff calmed everyone quickly.","She asked a simple question about the exam, and a long discussion ensued."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"entail","p":"verb","d":"To have something as a necessary part or result; to make something unavoidable.","lb":"involve, require","s":["involve","require","demand","call for","mean","imply"],"k":["bring about","bring with it","carry","cause"],"a":["exclude","preclude","rule out"],"ex":["Opening a small shop entails a lot of paperwork, from trade licences to tax registration.","Moving to a new city entails living far away from your family for a while.","The job entails working on weekends during busy seasons, so think carefully before accepting it."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"entangle","p":"verb","d":"To catch someone or something in a net, rope or tangle, or to involve them in a difficult situation.","lb":"ensnare, tangle","s":["ensnare","trap","snare","tangle","snarl","catch"],"k":["distort","entrap","hitch","hook"],"a":["free","release","extricate","untangle"],"ex":["A turtle was entangled in an old fishing net near the shore.","The kite's string became entangled in the branches of the tamarind tree.","Don't entangle yourself in other people's quarrels at work."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"entanglement","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which something is twisted together, or in which someone is caught up in a difficult, complicated situation.","lb":"tangle, involvement","s":["tangle","snarl","knot","complication","involvement","mess"],"k":["affair","association","commitment","complicity"],"a":["freedom","independence","detachment","separation"],"ex":["Seabirds often die from entanglement in old fishing nets.","She wanted to avoid any romantic entanglement while she prepared for her final exams.","A legal entanglement over the land delayed the new building by two years."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of excitement and interest in something that you enjoy or admire.","lb":"eagerness, excitement","s":["eagerness","zeal","passion","excitement","keenness","zest"],"k":["ardor","dash","devotion","elan"],"a":["apathy","indifference","boredom","lethargy"],"ex":["The new teacher taught with such enthusiasm that even the shy students joined in.","Fans greeted the team with great enthusiasm at the airport.","My enthusiasm for cooking began when I helped my grandmother make pitha."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"entice","p":"verb","d":"To attract someone to do something by offering something pleasant or exciting.","lb":"lure, attract","s":["lure","tempt","attract","tantalize","seduce","persuade"],"k":["allure","bait","beguile","cajole"],"a":["repel","deter","discourage","put off"],"ex":["Shops entice customers with big discount signs before the Eid holidays.","The smell of fresh parathas enticed us into the small tea stall.","The airline hopes cheap tickets will entice more travelers to visit during the monsoon."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"entity","p":"noun","d":"Something that exists as a separate and complete thing, such as a person, company or country.","lb":"being, thing","s":["being","thing","body","object","organization","unit"],"k":["agency","article","corporation","creature"],"a":[],"ex":["A company is a legal entity, separate from the people who own it.","Each of the two schools is an independent entity with its own rules.","The charity is a separate entity from the university, though they share a campus."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"entreat","p":"verb","d":"To ask someone in a very serious, emotional way to do something for you.","lb":"beg, implore","s":["beg","implore","plead with","beseech","appeal to","petition"],"k":["adjure","call on","conjure","crave"],"a":["demand","command","order"],"ex":["She entreated the guard to let her see her sick father.","The mother entreated her son to stay home and rest.","He entreated the shopkeeper to give him more time to pay."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"entrepreneur","p":"noun","d":"A person who starts their own business, taking financial risks in the hope of making a profit.","lb":"business owner, founder","s":["businessman","businesswoman","business owner","founder","startup founder","merchant"],"k":["adventurer","developer","enterpriser","go-getter"],"a":[],"ex":["Nadia, a young entrepreneur, started selling handmade bags online from her bedroom.","Many entrepreneurs fail at first, but they learn from their mistakes and try again.","The university runs a club where student entrepreneurs can pitch their business ideas."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"enumerate","p":"verb","d":"To name or list items one by one, or to count them.","lb":"list, count","s":["list","itemize","count","name","number","detail"],"k":["add up","catalog","delineate","identify"],"a":[],"ex":["The teacher asked us to enumerate three causes of the flood.","Can you enumerate the items you want to buy before we go to the market?","In her speech, she enumerated the club's achievements over the past year."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"enunciate","p":"verb","d":"To say words clearly and carefully so that other people can understand you.","lb":"pronounce, articulate","s":["articulate","pronounce","speak clearly","voice","utter","vocalize"],"k":["declare","formulate","phrase","proclaim"],"a":["mumble","mutter","slur","murmur"],"ex":["When you speak on the phone, enunciate each word so the listener can follow you.","The newsreader enunciates every word clearly, so even beginners understand the bulletin.","The singer enunciated the lyrics so carefully that the whole audience could sing along."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"envision","p":"verb","d":"To picture something in your mind as a future possibility, especially something you hope will happen.","lb":"imagine, picture","s":["imagine","picture","visualize","foresee","conceive","anticipate"],"k":["conceive of","dream up","fancy","realize"],"a":[],"ex":["Before opening the shop, Nadia tried to envision how customers would move between the shelves.","I can't envision myself living abroad, away from my family and our daily evening tea.","The architect envisions a public park with a small lake where the old factory now stands."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ephemeral","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting for a very short time.","lb":"short-lived, fleeting","s":["fleeting","transient","temporary","brief","passing","momentary"],"k":["cursory","evanescent","flitting","frail"],"a":["permanent","lasting","enduring","eternal"],"ex":["Fame on social media can be ephemeral, lasting only until the next trend appears.","The beauty of shiuli flowers is ephemeral; they bloom at night and fall by morning.","Morning dew is ephemeral and vanishes as soon as the sun rises."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"epicure","p":"noun","d":"A person who enjoys fine food and drink and knows a lot about it.","lb":"gourmet, food lover","s":["gourmet","foodie","connoisseur","bon vivant","food lover","aesthete"],"k":["bon viveur","hedonist","luxury-lover","oenophile"],"a":[],"ex":["My uncle is an epicure who travels across the country just to taste a famous kacchi biryani.","As an epicure, she can tell good tea from average tea after one sip.","The restaurant's menu is written for epicures, with rare spices and carefully chosen ingredients."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"epigram","p":"noun","d":"A short, clever and often funny saying that expresses an idea in a memorable way.","lb":"witty saying, quip","s":["aphorism","witticism","quip","maxim","saying","adage"],"k":["apothegm","axiom","dictum","expression"],"a":[],"ex":["My uncle ended every speech with a funny epigram that guests repeated for weeks.","The poster carried a short epigram about time, saying that lost minutes never return.","She loves collecting epigrams and writes her favorite ones on sticky notes above her desk."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"epilogue","p":"noun","d":"A short section at the end of a book, play or film that gives a final comment or tells what happened later.","lb":"afterword, conclusion","s":["postscript","coda","conclusion","finale","closing"],"k":["addendum","afterpiece","appendix","codicil"],"a":["prologue","preface","introduction","foreword"],"ex":["In the epilogue, the author tells us what happened to the characters ten years later.","The film ends with a short epilogue showing the family back at the old house.","My teacher read the epilogue of the novel aloud, and the class went silent."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"epitome","p":"noun","d":"A perfect or typical example of a quality or type of thing.","lb":"perfect example, embodiment","s":["embodiment","personification","essence","model","ideal","archetype"],"k":["example","illustration","image","incarnation"],"a":["antithesis"],"ex":["With her calm voice and patient smile, our teacher is the epitome of kindness.","That glass-fronted mall, full of imported goods, is the epitome of modern city life in Dhaka.","For many students, a quiet library with fast Wi-Fi is the epitome of a good study place."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"epoch","p":"noun","d":"A long period of time in history that is marked by important events or changes.","lb":"era, age","s":["era","age","period","time","generation","stage"],"k":["aeon","date of reference","dispensation","duration"],"a":[],"ex":["The invention of the printing press began a new epoch in human communication.","The arrival of the internet marked a new epoch in the way people work.","Historians call that period the epoch of great discoveries."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"equanimity","p":"noun","d":"A calm and balanced state of mind, especially in difficult situations.","lb":"calmness, composure","s":["composure","calmness","poise","serenity","coolness","tranquility"],"k":["assurance","disposition","evenness","imperturbability"],"a":["agitation","anxiety","panic","distress"],"ex":["She accepted the bad exam result with equanimity and began planning her next attempt.","The pilot's equanimity during the storm helped the passengers stay calm.","He faced the long traffic jam with equanimity, listening to music instead of complaining."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"equestrian","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to riding horses, especially as a sport or skill.","lb":"horse riding","s":["horseback","mounted","riding","horsey"],"k":["cavalier","chivalric","horse-riding","jockeying"],"a":[],"ex":["She won a medal at the national equestrian championship last spring.","The school has an equestrian club where students learn to ride and care for horses.","Equestrian events at the Olympics include jumping and dressage."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"equilateral","p":"adjective","d":"Having all sides of the same length, as in a triangle with three equal sides.","lb":"equal-sided","s":["regular"],"k":["balanced","congruent","equal","identical"],"a":[],"ex":["Draw an equilateral triangle and measure each side to check that they match.","The road sign was shaped like an equilateral triangle with a red border.","Each equilateral triangle in the pattern had sides of exactly five centimeters."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"equitable","p":"adjective","d":"Fair and reasonable to everyone involved, treating each person or side justly.","lb":"fair, just","s":["fair","just","impartial","reasonable","unbiased","balanced"],"k":["above board","disinterested","egalitarian","equal"],"a":["unfair","unjust","biased","partial"],"ex":["The brothers agreed on an equitable way to divide their father's land.","An equitable distribution of food after the flood helped everyone in the village.","The teacher gave every group an equitable share of the lab equipment."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"equivalence","p":"noun","d":"The state of being equal in value, amount, meaning or importance.","lb":"equality, parity","s":["equality","parity","sameness","equivalency","correspondence","similarity"],"k":["affinity","alikeness","analogy","commensurability"],"a":["difference","disparity","inequality","imbalance"],"ex":["The university checks the equivalence of foreign degrees before offering admission.","There is no exact equivalence between the two words in Bangla and English.","The chart shows the equivalence of kilometres and miles."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"equivocal","p":"adjective","d":"Having more than one possible meaning, and often deliberately unclear.","lb":"ambiguous, evasive","s":["ambiguous","vague","unclear","evasive","uncertain","indefinite"],"k":["dubious","forked","inconclusive","indeterminate"],"a":["clear","unambiguous","definite","explicit"],"ex":["When I asked if he would come, his equivocal reply left me unsure.","The test results were equivocal, so the doctor ordered another scan.","Her equivocal answer about the missing money made everyone suspicious."],"b":600,"y":1},{"w":"equivocate","p":"verb","d":"To use unclear or evasive language to avoid giving a direct answer or to mislead someone.","lb":"hedge, dodge","s":["hedge","dodge","evade","prevaricate","waffle","sidestep"],"k":["avoid","circumvent","duck","elude"],"a":["commit","clarify","answer directly","state plainly"],"ex":["When asked who broke the window, Tom equivocated and changed the subject.","The salesman equivocated about the warranty, giving vague answers whenever I asked for details.","Stop equivocating and tell me whether you are coming to the wedding or not."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"eradicate","p":"verb","d":"To destroy something completely so that none of it remains.","lb":"wipe out, destroy","s":["eliminate","wipe out","exterminate","abolish","uproot","annihilate"],"k":["carry off","decimate","do away with","extinguish"],"a":["create","introduce","establish","foster"],"ex":["Vaccination campaigns helped to eradicate polio from many countries.","The farmers used a safe spray to eradicate the insects from the vegetable field.","Charities hope to eradicate hunger in the slums of big cities."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"erratic","p":"adjective","d":"Not regular, steady or predictable in behavior, movement or quality.","lb":"unpredictable, inconsistent","s":["unpredictable","inconsistent","irregular","unsteady","changeable","unstable"],"k":["fickle","freakish","mercurial","occasional"],"a":["steady","consistent","regular","predictable"],"ex":["The bus service is so erratic that students never know when to leave home.","His erratic marks, high one term and low the next, worried his parents.","The driver's erratic movement across lanes frightened other motorists."],"b":74,"y":3},{"w":"erudite","p":"adjective","d":"Having or showing great knowledge gained through serious study.","lb":"learned, scholarly","s":["learned","scholarly","knowledgeable","educated","cultured","intellectual"],"k":["bookish","deep","highbrow","knowing"],"a":["ignorant","uneducated","unschooled","illiterate"],"ex":["The erudite professor could discuss history, poetry and physics with equal ease.","Her erudite essay quoted sources from five different languages.","My grandfather was an erudite man who spent his evenings reading old books."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"eruption","p":"noun","d":"A sudden, powerful release of lava, ash and gas from a volcano.","lb":"volcanic outburst","s":["explosion","blast","outburst","discharge","burst","outbreak"],"k":["bang","blowup","convulsion","effusion"],"a":[],"ex":["The eruption sent a thick cloud of ash high into the sky.","Flights were cancelled for days after the volcano's eruption.","Villagers were moved to safety hours before the eruption began."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"esoteric","p":"adjective","d":"Understood or enjoyed by only a small group of people who have special knowledge.","lb":"obscure, specialized","s":["obscure","arcane","abstruse","specialized","cryptic","recondite"],"k":["ambiguous","cabalistic","cultish","deep"],"a":["common","familiar","popular","simple"],"ex":["The professor's lecture on esoteric mathematics lost most of the class within five minutes.","Collecting rare stamps may seem esoteric, but the hobby has many devoted fans.","The magazine is full of esoteric jokes that only experienced programmers understand."],"b":531,"y":0},{"w":"espouse","p":"verb","d":"To publicly support an idea, belief or way of life, and often to adopt it as your own.","lb":"support, adopt","s":["support","advocate","champion","adopt","embrace","back"],"k":["accept","approve","assist","conjoin"],"a":["oppose","reject","renounce","abandon"],"ex":["The new principal espouses the idea that students learn best when they are allowed to ask questions.","Many young people today espouse healthy habits like cycling to work and eating less sugar.","The charity espouses education for every child, and it runs free evening classes in the slums."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"esprit de corps","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of pride, loyalty and shared purpose among the members of a group.","lb":"team spirit","s":["team spirit","morale","camaraderie","solidarity","unity","fellowship"],"k":["allegiance","brotherhood","cohesion","collegiality"],"a":["disunity","discord","low morale","division"],"ex":["The captain worked hard to build esprit de corps before the tournament.","Team lunches helped to improve esprit de corps among the new staff.","A strong esprit de corps kept the rescue volunteers going through the long night."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"estimable","p":"adjective","d":"Deserving respect and admiration for good qualities or achievements.","lb":"admirable, respectable","s":["admirable","respectable","praiseworthy","worthy","commendable","honorable"],"k":["creditable","dignified","exemplary","good"],"a":["contemptible","despicable","disreputable","unworthy"],"ex":["Our headmistress is an estimable woman whom the whole town respects.","He is an estimable colleague who always helps new staff settle in.","Raising three children while studying is an estimable achievement."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"estrange","p":"verb","d":"To make someone who was close to you become distant, unfriendly or unwilling to talk to you.","lb":"alienate, separate","s":["alienate","separate","divide","distance","drive apart","isolate"],"k":["alter","antagonize","break up","change"],"a":["reconcile","unite","bring together","befriend"],"ex":["The argument over the inheritance estranged the two brothers for more than ten years.","Her constant criticism estranged her from many of her friends.","He felt estranged from his family after moving abroad and rarely calling home."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ethereal","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely light and delicate, so much so that it seems not to belong to this world.","lb":"delicate, heavenly","s":["delicate","airy","light","heavenly","celestial","dainty"],"k":["aerial","breakable","brittle","flimsy"],"a":["earthly","solid","heavy","material"],"ex":["Morning mist floated over the paddy fields, giving the village an ethereal look.","The singer's ethereal voice seemed to float above the quiet audience.","Soft lanterns gave the wedding garden an ethereal glow."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"ethics","p":"noun","d":"The moral rules and principles that guide how people behave or how a profession works.","lb":"morals, principles","s":["morals","principles","moral code","values","standards","morality"],"k":["decency","fairness","justice","moral philosophy"],"a":["immorality","dishonesty","corruption","wrongdoing"],"ex":["Doctors must follow strict medical ethics, including keeping patient information private.","The journalist was sacked for breaking the ethics of her profession.","Our university offers a course on business ethics."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ethnic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to a group of people who share the same culture, language or national origin.","lb":"cultural, national","s":["cultural","racial","national","tribal","indigenous","native"],"k":["customary","domestic","heathen","pagan"],"a":[],"ex":["Bangladesh is home to many ethnic groups, each with its own language and festivals.","The university held an ethnic food fair, with dishes from many countries.","She wore an ethnic dress made of handwoven cloth."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"eulogy","p":"noun","d":"A speech or piece of writing that praises someone highly, especially after their death.","lb":"tribute, praise","s":["tribute","praise","panegyric","commendation","homage","accolade"],"k":["congratulations","elegy","hymn","kudos"],"a":["condemnation","criticism","attack","insult"],"ex":["At the funeral, Nadia gave a moving eulogy for her grandfather, who had been a teacher.","The newspaper printed a long eulogy for the town's beloved doctor.","The class teacher read a short eulogy for the classmate who had died last year."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"euphemism","p":"noun","d":"A mild or polite word or phrase used instead of one that seems harsh, rude or too direct.","lb":"polite term, softener","s":["understatement","substitute","polite term","circumlocution","softening","gloss"],"k":["diplomatic language","expression","hedging","innuendo"],"a":["blunt term","plain speaking","bluntness"],"ex":["Passed away is a common euphemism for died.","The company used the euphemism restructuring to avoid saying that hundreds of people were losing their jobs.","Telling a child that the pet went to live on a farm is a euphemism parents often regret later."],"b":85,"y":1},{"w":"euphoric","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling intense happiness and excitement.","lb":"elated, ecstatic","s":["elated","ecstatic","overjoyed","jubilant","thrilled","blissful"],"k":["buoyant","expansive","flushed","giddy"],"a":["depressed","miserable","gloomy","dejected"],"ex":["Fans were euphoric when their team scored in the last minute.","I felt euphoric on the day my admission result came out.","The bride's family was euphoric as the wedding finally began."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"evanescent","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting only a very short time and quickly disappearing.","lb":"fleeting, ephemeral","s":["fleeting","momentary","transient","ephemeral","passing","brief"],"k":["dissolving","elusive","ethereal","evaporating"],"a":["lasting","permanent","enduring","eternal"],"ex":["The beauty of the rainbow was evanescent, gone within minutes.","Fame can be evanescent, especially for stars of viral videos.","Morning mist over the river is evanescent and vanishes with the first sunlight."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"evasive","p":"adjective","d":"Avoiding giving a direct or honest answer.","lb":"indirect, elusive","s":["elusive","equivocal","vague","cagey","shifty","slippery"],"k":["cryptic","doubtful","indefinable","indefinite"],"a":["direct","frank","straightforward","candid"],"ex":["He gave an evasive answer when I asked where the money had gone.","The shop owner was evasive about when my order would arrive.","Her evasive reply made the interviewer suspicious."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"evince","p":"verb","d":"To show clearly that you have a particular feeling or quality.","lb":"show, display","s":["show","display","demonstrate","reveal","exhibit","manifest"],"k":["attest","bear witness to","bespeak","betoken"],"a":["hide","conceal","mask","suppress"],"ex":["The new student evinced great curiosity about every experiment in the lab.","He evinced no sign of nervousness during the interview.","Her paintings evince a deep love of the countryside."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"evoke","p":"verb","d":"To bring a feeling, memory or image into someone's mind.","lb":"summon, stir","s":["summon","call up","elicit","arouse","conjure","awaken"],"k":["bring up","call down","call forth","cite"],"a":["suppress","stifle","dampen","quell"],"ex":["The smell of fried onions evokes happy memories of my grandmother's kitchen.","The old photographs evoke the quiet streets of Dhaka before the traffic grew.","The speaker's story evoked sympathy from everyone in the room."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"evolution","p":"noun","d":"The slow, gradual process of change and development into a different or more advanced form.","lb":"development, gradual change","s":["development","growth","progress","advance","progression","transformation"],"k":["adaptation","advancement","emergence","flowering"],"a":["regression","stagnation","decline"],"ex":["The evolution of mobile phones has been rapid, from simple calls to powerful computers.","Our history teacher described the evolution of the city from a small port to a large capital.","Biologists study the evolution of birds from small dinosaurs over millions of years."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"exacerbate","p":"verb","d":"To make a bad situation, problem or feeling worse.","lb":"worsen, aggravate","s":["worsen","aggravate","intensify","inflame","compound","heighten"],"k":["alter","change","complicate","exasperate"],"a":["alleviate","relieve","improve","ease"],"ex":["Scratching the insect bite will only exacerbate the itching and may cause an infection.","Heavy rain exacerbated the traffic jam, and some buses were stuck for hours.","Skipping breakfast can exacerbate headaches in people who are prone to migraines."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"exacerbation","p":"noun","d":"The act of making a problem, illness or bad situation worse.","lb":"worsening, aggravation","s":["aggravation","worsening","escalation","compounding","intensification"],"k":["agitation","complication","exasperation","fanning"],"a":["relief","improvement","easing","soothing"],"ex":["Doctors blamed the exacerbation of her asthma on dust and cold air.","Heavy traffic is a major cause of the exacerbation of air pollution in the city.","Skipping meals led to an exacerbation of his stomach problem."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"exacting","p":"adjective","d":"Demanding a great deal of effort, care or high standards from other people.","lb":"demanding, strict","s":["demanding","strict","rigorous","stringent","tough","challenging"],"k":["difficult","exigent","fastidious","finicky"],"a":["easygoing","lenient","undemanding","relaxed"],"ex":["The chef is exacting and sends back any dish that is not perfect.","Becoming a pilot requires exacting training that takes years.","My exacting math teacher insists on neat work and correct units."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"exaggerate","p":"verb","d":"To describe something as bigger, better or worse than it really is.","lb":"overstate, inflate","s":["overstate","inflate","embellish","overdo","magnify","amplify"],"k":["blow up","dramatize","embroider","enhance"],"a":["understate","minimize","downplay","play down"],"ex":["My brother likes to exaggerate; the fish he caught was not that big.","Don't exaggerate your skills in the interview, because they may test you.","The news report exaggerated the damage caused by the storm."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"exalt","p":"verb","d":"To praise someone or something very highly, or to raise them to a higher rank.","lb":"praise, glorify","s":["praise","glorify","extol","laud","elevate","honor"],"k":["animate","applaud","bless","commend"],"a":["humble","disgrace","belittle","degrade"],"ex":["The speaker exalted teachers as the quiet builders of the nation.","Fans exalted the young cricketer after his brilliant performance in the final.","The poem exalts the beauty of the river and the farmers who live beside it."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"exasperate","p":"verb","d":"To make someone very annoyed or angry, especially by doing something again and again.","lb":"irritate, infuriate","s":["infuriate","irritate","annoy","anger","madden","irk"],"k":["bother","exacerbate","incense","nettle"],"a":["please","soothe","calm","delight"],"ex":["It exasperates me when my phone freezes in the middle of an important call.","The little boy exasperated his sister by repeating every word she said.","Dhaka's slow traffic exasperated the passengers, who had been stuck in the same spot for an hour."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"excerpt","p":"noun","d":"A short piece taken from a longer text, film or piece of music.","lb":"extract, passage","s":["extract","passage","quotation","selection","citation","snippet"],"k":["abridgment","abstract","acknowledgment","cutting"],"a":[],"ex":["Our teacher read an excerpt from the novel before we began the test.","The newspaper printed an excerpt of the author's new memoir.","I only listened to a short excerpt of the song before buying the album."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"excise","p":"verb","d":"To remove something completely by cutting it out, as from a text or from the body.","lb":"cut out, remove","s":["cut out","remove","delete","extract","erase","strike out"],"k":["amputate","cancel","chop","clip off"],"a":["insert","add","include","graft"],"ex":["The editor excised two long paragraphs from the article to make it shorter.","Surgeons excised the small growth from her shoulder in a short operation.","The censors excised several scenes from the film before it was shown."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"exculpate","p":"verb","d":"To show or declare that someone is not guilty of something.","lb":"clear, acquit","s":["acquit","absolve","clear","exonerate","vindicate","pardon"],"k":["clear the name of","indemnify","judge","label"],"a":["blame","accuse","incriminate","condemn"],"ex":["The video from the shop camera exculpated the young man, who had been wrongly accused.","New evidence exculpated the driver and showed that the brakes had failed.","The investigation exculpated the teacher of any wrongdoing in the exam hall incident."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"execrable","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely bad or unpleasant; of very poor quality.","lb":"awful, abysmal","s":["awful","dreadful","terrible","atrocious","abysmal","appalling"],"k":["cursed","curst","damnable","deplorable"],"a":["excellent","superb","wonderful","splendid"],"ex":["The hotel's food was execrable, and we left most of it on the plate.","The film had an execrable script and even worse acting.","The weather was execrable throughout our trip, with rain every single day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"exemplify","p":"verb","d":"To be a typical example of something, or to give an example to show it.","lb":"illustrate, typify","s":["illustrate","typify","embody","represent","demonstrate","personify"],"k":["be","bespeak","cite","depict"],"a":["contradict","oppose","belie"],"ex":["The teacher's patience and kindness exemplify what a good educator should be.","Can you exemplify your point with a real-life case?","The old market exemplifies the busy, noisy charm of Old Dhaka."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"exempt","p":"adjective","d":"Free from a rule, duty or payment that other people must follow or pay.","lb":"excused, immune","s":["excused","free","immune","spared","released","absolved"],"k":["dispensed","excluded","relieved","unaffected"],"a":["subject","liable","bound","obliged"],"ex":["Students with high scores are exempt from the extra math course.","Charities are usually exempt from paying tax on donations.","Children under five are exempt from the entry fee at the zoo."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adjective","d":"Making you feel extremely tired, in body or mind.","lb":"tiring, draining","s":["tiring","draining","gruelling","wearing","strenuous","taxing"],"k":["bone-tiring","debilitating","enervating","hard"],"a":["refreshing","relaxing","invigorating","easy"],"ex":["The six-hour bus journey through Dhaka traffic was exhausting.","Looking after a newborn baby is joyful but exhausting.","Exam week was exhausting, and I slept for twelve hours afterwards."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"exhaustive","p":"adjective","d":"Complete and thorough, covering every possible detail or possibility.","lb":"thorough, comprehensive","s":["thorough","comprehensive","complete","full","extensive","detailed"],"k":["all-encompassing","broad","encyclopedic","entire"],"a":["superficial","partial","incomplete","cursory"],"ex":["Police carried out an exhaustive search of the riverbank but found nothing.","The guidebook has an exhaustive list of hotels and restaurants.","After an exhaustive review of the data, the team found three errors."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"exhort","p":"verb","d":"To urge someone strongly and sincerely to do something.","lb":"urge, encourage","s":["urge","encourage","press","implore","entreat","push"],"k":["adjure","admonish","barrack","beseech"],"a":["discourage","dissuade","deter","restrain"],"ex":["The captain exhorted his players to keep fighting until the final whistle.","Health officials exhort people to wash their hands often during an outbreak.","The teacher exhorted the class to start revising early instead of waiting for the last week."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"exhume","p":"verb","d":"To dig up something buried, especially a dead body, usually for official examination or reburial.","lb":"dig up, disinter","s":["disinter","unearth","dig up","uncover","excavate"],"k":["bring to light","dig","discover","disentomb"],"a":["bury","inter","entomb"],"ex":["Officials ordered the body to be exhumed so that doctors could examine the cause of death.","Archaeologists exhumed ancient pots and tools from the ground beneath the old village.","The family asked permission to exhume their grandfather’s remains and move them to the village graveyard."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"exigency","p":"noun","d":"An urgent need or situation that requires immediate action.","lb":"emergency, urgency","s":["emergency","urgency","crisis","necessity","pressure","demand"],"k":["catastrophe","constraint","contingency","dilemma"],"a":[],"ex":["In an exigency, such as a fire, everyone must leave the building quickly.","The exigencies of the school year left her little time to relax.","Because of the exigency, the clinic stayed open all night to treat people injured in the storm."],"b":17,"y":0},{"w":"exigent","p":"adjective","d":"Urgent and needing immediate attention or action.","lb":"urgent, pressing","s":["urgent","pressing","critical","acute","imperative","crucial"],"k":["clamorous","crying","dire","exacting"],"a":["trivial","minor","unimportant","insignificant"],"ex":["The hospital called an exigent meeting after the power failure threatened the intensive care ward.","Because of exigent circumstances, the landlord had to repair the broken water pipe that same night.","She put her hobbies aside to focus on the exigent task of finishing her thesis before the deadline."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"existential","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to human existence and its meaning, or to the basic fact of whether something survives.","lb":"of existence, survival","s":["ontological","metaphysical","philosophical","fundamental"],"k":["abstract","critical","crucial","decisive"],"a":[],"ex":["After graduating, Nadia went through an existential crisis and kept asking what she really wanted from life.","Scientists warn that rising seas are an existential threat to low-lying coastal villages.","Late at night, my brother loves asking existential questions, like why we are here at all."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"exodus","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which many people leave a place at the same time.","lb":"mass departure, flight","s":["departure","exit","flight","migration","evacuation","withdrawal"],"k":["depopulation","diaspora","dispersal","egress"],"a":["influx","arrival","return","entry"],"ex":["Before Eid, there is a mass exodus of workers from Dhaka to their villages.","The company faced an exodus of talented engineers after the pay cut.","Heavy flooding caused an exodus from the low-lying areas by the river."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"exonerate","p":"verb","d":"To officially show or declare that someone is not to blame for something.","lb":"clear, absolve","s":["absolve","acquit","clear","vindicate","exculpate","pardon"],"k":["discharge","forgive","indemnify","judge"],"a":["blame","accuse","condemn","convict"],"ex":["Security camera footage exonerated the driver and proved that the other car had run the red light.","The audit exonerated the company's accountant, who had been wrongly suspected of hiding losses.","A new DNA test exonerated the man after he had spent ten years in prison."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"exorbitance","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being far too high or great, especially in price or demands.","lb":"excess, extravagance","s":["excess","extravagance","extortion","overcharging"],"k":["greed","inflation","lavishness","overindulgence"],"a":["moderation","reasonableness","modesty"],"ex":["Students complained about the exorbitance of the fees at the private coaching center.","The exorbitance of the hotel's prices surprised us, since a plain room cost more than a week's food.","Everyone talked about the exorbitance of ticket prices for the cricket final."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"exorbitant","p":"adjective","d":"Much higher in price or amount than is reasonable or fair.","lb":"excessive, extortionate","s":["excessive","outrageous","steep","unreasonable","inflated","extravagant"],"k":["daylight robbery","enormous","immoderate","inordinate"],"a":["reasonable","modest","cheap","affordable"],"ex":["The airport shop charged an exorbitant price for a small bottle of water.","Taxi drivers asked exorbitant fares during the rainstorm.","Rents in the city centre are exorbitant, so students share small rooms."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"expatriate","p":"verb","d":"To leave your own country to live in another, or to force someone to leave their homeland.","lb":"exile, move abroad","s":["exile","banish","deport","expel","emigrate","move abroad"],"k":["ban","decamp","kick out","leave home"],"a":["repatriate","return","welcome home","readmit"],"ex":["After the company closed, he decided to expatriate himself and look for work in Dubai.","Many young engineers expatriate themselves for a few years to earn more and gain experience.","The poet was expatriated for his writing and lived abroad for fifteen years."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"expedient","p":"adjective","d":"Useful or convenient for a particular purpose, even if not completely fair or right.","lb":"convenient, advantageous","s":["advantageous","convenient","practical","pragmatic","politic","opportune"],"k":["carpetbag","favorable","functional","good"],"a":["impractical","unwise","inadvisable","detrimental"],"ex":["It was expedient for the company to blame the weather rather than admit its poor planning.","Taking a rickshaw seemed the expedient choice, since the main road was blocked by a procession.","The mayor chose the expedient solution of painting over the cracks instead of repairing the bridge."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"expedite","p":"verb","d":"To make a process or task happen faster or more smoothly.","lb":"speed up, hasten","s":["speed up","hasten","accelerate","facilitate","quicken","advance"],"k":["assist","fast-forward","help","hurry along"],"a":["delay","slow down","hinder","obstruct"],"ex":["For an extra fee, the office will expedite your passport application.","A second cashier was added to expedite the long line at the supermarket.","The manager called the supplier to expedite the delivery before the weekend sale."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"expiate","p":"verb","d":"To make up for a wrong you have done by accepting punishment or by doing something good.","lb":"atone, make amends","s":["atone","make amends","redeem","pay for","make up for","repent"],"k":["absolve oneself","cleanse","make reparation","make restitution"],"a":[],"ex":["He tried to expiate his guilt by volunteering at the shelter every weekend.","She expiated her mistake by working extra hours to fix the damaged accounts.","The company expiated its error by refunding every customer and apologizing in public."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"explicate","p":"verb","d":"To explain an idea, text or problem in careful detail so that its meaning is fully clear.","lb":"explain, analyse","s":["explain","interpret","clarify","analyse","elucidate","expound"],"k":["clear up","construe","define","develop"],"a":["obscure","confuse","muddle","complicate"],"ex":["The professor spent an hour explicating a single paragraph of the poem.","In her essay, Nadia explicates how the author uses weather to show the character's mood.","The lawyer explicated the clauses of the contract so the clients could understand them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"explicit","p":"adjective","d":"Stated clearly and in detail, leaving no doubt about what is meant.","lb":"clear, direct","s":["clear","direct","plain","specific","definite","precise"],"k":["apparent","declared","definitive","distinct"],"a":["implicit","vague","implied","ambiguous"],"ex":["The teacher gave explicit instructions: use blue ink and write on one side only.","You need explicit permission from your parents before joining the school trip.","The contract is explicit about when payments must be made."],"b":210,"y":1},{"w":"exposition","p":"noun","d":"A clear, detailed explanation of an idea, theory or subject.","lb":"explanation, account","s":["explanation","explication","account","description","interpretation","commentary"],"k":["discourse","disquisition","dissertation","essay"],"a":[],"ex":["The professor's clear exposition of the theory made a difficult topic easy to follow.","Her book offers a simple exposition of how vaccines work.","The first chapter is a short exposition of the author's main argument."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"expostulate","p":"verb","d":"To argue strongly with someone in order to warn them or to make them change their mind.","lb":"protest, remonstrate","s":["remonstrate","protest","object","argue","reason","plead"],"k":["admonish","berate","chide","demur"],"a":["agree","consent","approve","acquiesce"],"ex":["My father expostulated with me for hours about quitting my course, but I had made up my mind.","The old man expostulated with the driver, saying the bus was far too crowded to be safe.","She tried to expostulate with her friend about spending all his savings on a new phone."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"expunge","p":"verb","d":"To remove or delete something completely, such as a name, a record or a memory.","lb":"erase, delete","s":["erase","delete","remove","eradicate","wipe out","obliterate"],"k":["annihilate","annul","blot out","eliminate"],"a":["add","insert","record","include"],"ex":["After ten years, the court agreed to expunge his minor offense from the record.","The editor expunged every mention of the rumor from the final article.","She tried to expunge the embarrassing memory from her mind."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"exquisite","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely beautiful and carefully made, with very fine detail.","lb":"beautiful, delicate","s":["beautiful","delicate","elegant","fine","lovely","refined"],"k":["attractive","exceptional","finely wrought","fragile"],"a":["ugly","coarse","crude","clumsy"],"ex":["The bride wore an exquisite silk sari with delicate gold embroidery along the border.","The jeweller showed us an exquisite necklace made of tiny pearls.","The pastry chef's tiny cakes were exquisite, each one decorated with a single sugar flower."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"extant","p":"adjective","d":"Still existing, especially of old things that could have been lost or destroyed.","lb":"existing, surviving","s":["surviving","existing","living","remaining","in existence","current"],"k":["continuing","endured","existent","intact"],"a":["extinct","lost","vanished","defunct"],"ex":["Only three copies of the ancient manuscript are still extant.","The oldest extant building in the city is a small brick gate from the 1600s.","Few of the artist's paintings are extant, because most were lost in a fire."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"extinguish","p":"verb","d":"To stop a fire, flame or light from burning or shining.","lb":"put out","s":["put out","snuff out","douse","quench","smother","stamp out"],"k":["annihilate","crush out","do away with","eliminate"],"a":["ignite","light","kindle","start"],"ex":["Firefighters took two hours to extinguish the blaze in the garment factory.","Please extinguish your cigarette before entering the hospital.","She extinguished the candles with a gentle puff and made a wish."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"extol","p":"verb","d":"To praise something or someone very highly and enthusiastically.","lb":"praise, laud","s":["praise","laud","acclaim","glorify","celebrate","applaud"],"k":["compliment","congratulate","cry up","exult"],"a":["criticize","condemn","denounce","belittle"],"ex":["The teacher extolled the virtues of reading every day before bed.","Travel bloggers extol the beauty of the Sundarbans in glowing posts.","Reviewers extolled the film's honest story and strong acting."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"extort","p":"verb","d":"To obtain money or something else from a person by using force, threats or pressure.","lb":"blackmail, force","s":["extract","wring","wrest","blackmail","exact","coerce"],"k":["bleed","fleece","gouge","hold to ransom"],"a":[],"ex":["The gang tried to extort money from local shopkeepers by threatening to damage their stalls.","Hackers locked the hospital's computers and tried to extort a large payment before returning the data.","Police arrested two men who had extorted money from truck drivers at the roadside checkpoint."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"extraneous","p":"adjective","d":"Not relevant or necessary, and not really part of the subject you are dealing with.","lb":"irrelevant, unnecessary","s":["irrelevant","unnecessary","superfluous","immaterial","unrelated","redundant"],"k":["adventitious","ancillary","beside the point","digressive"],"a":["relevant","essential","necessary","pertinent"],"ex":["Delete the extraneous details from your essay so that the main idea is easier to follow.","Extraneous noise from the street made it hard to hear the lecturer.","The manager asked us to avoid extraneous questions during the short meeting."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"extrapolate","p":"verb","d":"To use known facts or trends to make a guess about something unknown or about what will happen later.","lb":"project, infer","s":["project","predict","infer","estimate","forecast","deduce"],"k":["anticipate","assume","divine","foresee"],"a":[],"ex":["Scientists extrapolate from last year's data to predict how many people will use the metro.","You cannot extrapolate a whole country's opinion from the answers of ten friends.","If sales keep growing at this rate, we can extrapolate that profits will double within three years."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"extrapolation","p":"noun","d":"An estimate or prediction about the future or the unknown, based on what is already known.","lb":"projection, inference","s":["projection","inference","prediction","estimate","forecast","conjecture"],"k":["assumption","hunch","hypothesis","hypothesizing"],"a":[],"ex":["By extrapolation from this year's sales, the shop expects to double its income in three years.","The forecast is only an extrapolation from past weather data, so it may be wrong.","Scientists used extrapolation to estimate how many people will live in the city by 2050."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"extravagance","p":"noun","d":"Spending much more money than is sensible, or something costly that you do not really need.","lb":"overspending, excess","s":["excess","indulgence","splurge","luxury","high life"],"k":["dissipation","extremity","fancifulness","flamboyance"],"a":["thrift","frugality","economy","moderation"],"ex":["Buying a new phone every year is an extravagance we cannot afford.","The wedding was a show of extravagance, with hundreds of guests and a stage covered in flowers.","Her only extravagance is a cup of good coffee every morning."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"extravagant","p":"adjective","d":"Spending or costing much more money than is sensible or necessary.","lb":"lavish, wasteful","s":["lavish","wasteful","spendthrift","profligate","prodigal","excessive"],"k":["exuberant","fanciful","flamboyant","grandiose"],"a":["thrifty","frugal","economical","sparing"],"ex":["They held an extravagant wedding with five hundred guests and a stage full of flowers.","Buying a new phone every year is an extravagant habit for a student.","My cousin is extravagant and spends his whole salary in the first week."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"extremity","p":"noun","d":"The farthest point or outer edge of something, or the greatest degree of a feeling or condition.","lb":"edge, limit","s":["edge","limit","end","tip","boundary","border"],"k":["apex","apogee","appendage","brink"],"a":["centre","middle","core","heart"],"ex":["Teknaf lies at the southern extremity of Bangladesh, where the land narrows into a thin strip.","The ship sailed slowly to the far extremity of the bay before turning back.","In the extremity of her grief, she could hardly speak to anyone."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"extricate","p":"verb","d":"To free someone or something from a difficult situation or from a place where they are stuck.","lb":"free, release","s":["free","release","disentangle","rescue","liberate","untangle"],"k":["disengage","free up","get clear","loosen"],"a":["entangle","trap","involve","ensnare"],"ex":["Firefighters worked for an hour to extricate the driver from the crushed car.","It took Rafi weeks to extricate himself from the bad business deal.","She tried to extricate her scarf from the closing train door."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"extrovert","p":"noun","d":"An outgoing, confident person who enjoys being with other people and talking to them.","lb":"outgoing person","s":["people person","mixer","life of the party","outgoing person","social butterfly"],"k":["bon vivant","chatterbox","go-getter","gregarious"],"a":["introvert","loner","recluse","wallflower"],"ex":["Nadia is a real extrovert who makes friends with everyone on the bus within minutes.","As an extrovert, Rafi gets his energy from parties, while his brother prefers reading at home.","Companies often hire extroverts for sales jobs because they enjoy talking to strangers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"exuberant","p":"adjective","d":"Full of energy, excitement and cheerfulness.","lb":"lively, high-spirited","s":["lively","enthusiastic","ebullient","cheerful","vivacious","animated"],"k":["abundant","active","bubbly","dynamic"],"a":["subdued","gloomy","listless","reserved"],"ex":["The exuberant children ran onto the school ground as soon as the bell rang.","Fans gave the cricketers an exuberant welcome at the airport.","She was exuberant after hearing that she had passed the admission test."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"exult","p":"verb","d":"To feel and show great happiness, especially because of a success or victory.","lb":"rejoice, celebrate","s":["rejoice","celebrate","revel","delight","glory","crow"],"k":["be on cloud nine","cheer","cheer up","jump for joy"],"a":["mourn","grieve","lament","despair"],"ex":["The fans exulted in the streets when their team won the final in the last minute.","Nadia exulted when she saw her name on the admission list.","He exulted over his promotion by treating the whole office to sweets."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fabled","p":"adjective","d":"Famous because of many old stories, often so wonderful that they are hard to believe.","lb":"legendary, famous","s":["legendary","storied","famous","renowned","celebrated","mythical"],"k":["apocryphal","bygone","chimerical","eminent"],"a":["unknown","obscure","ordinary","undistinguished"],"ex":["Tourists visit Old Dhaka to taste the fabled biryani served in its narrow lanes.","The explorers searched for the fabled city of gold for years.","My grandmother often spoke of the fabled hospitality of her home village."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fabricated","p":"adjective","d":"Made up in order to deceive; not true.","lb":"invented, false","s":["invented","false","fake","fictitious","concocted","forged"],"k":["bastard","counterfeit","fancied","fictional"],"a":["true","genuine","authentic","real"],"ex":["The newspaper apologized for printing a fabricated story about the school principal.","He gave a fabricated excuse about a sick uncle to avoid going to the meeting.","The fabricated reviews on the website made the hotel look much better than it was."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fabrication","p":"noun","d":"A false story or statement that someone has invented, especially in order to deceive.","lb":"lie, invention","s":["lie","falsehood","invention","fiction","untruth","fib"],"k":["assembly","cock-and-bull story","fable","fairy tale"],"a":["truth","fact","reality","honesty"],"ex":["His story about meeting a famous footballer was a complete fabrication.","The newspaper apologized for printing a fabrication that had spread on social media.","The police found that the witness’s account was a fabrication from beginning to end."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"facade","p":"noun","d":"A false outward appearance that hides the real, usually less pleasant, truth about someone or something.","lb":"false front, pretence","s":["front","pretence","mask","veneer","guise","show"],"k":["appearance","charade","cover","frontage"],"a":["reality","truth","substance","honesty"],"ex":["Behind his cheerful facade, he was worried about losing his job.","The glossy brochure was only a facade; the hotel itself was dirty and noisy.","Her calm facade cracked when the results were announced."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"facet","p":"noun","d":"One side or aspect of a subject, problem or personality that has many different parts.","lb":"aspect, side","s":["aspect","side","feature","element","dimension","angle"],"k":["factor","hallmark","ingredient","nuance"],"a":[],"ex":["Cooking is just one facet of my mother's busy, creative life.","Before deciding, the committee examined every facet of the proposal.","Shyness is only one facet of his personality; with close friends he is loud and funny."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"facetious","p":"adjective","d":"Joking in a way that is not appropriate, treating a serious matter as if it were funny.","lb":"joking, flippant","s":["flippant","joking","jesting","playful","frivolous","glib"],"k":["bantering","impish","ironic","jocose"],"a":["serious","earnest","solemn","sincere"],"ex":["He made a facetious remark about the exam being easy, and the teacher did not laugh.","Please do not be facetious; this is a serious problem with the budget.","She gave a facetious answer when asked about her plans, saying she would become a pirate."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"facile","p":"adjective","d":"Too simple or too easily achieved, and showing little real thought or depth.","lb":"superficial, simplistic","s":["superficial","simplistic","shallow","glib","oversimplified","hasty"],"k":["articulate","effortless","eloquent","fluent"],"a":["thoughtful","profound","deep","thorough"],"ex":["It is facile to blame poor exam results only on lazy students.","The speaker offered a facile solution to the traffic problem: just tell everyone to stay home.","Comparing a school to a factory is a facile idea that ignores how different children are."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"facilitate","p":"verb","d":"To make an action or process easier, or to help it happen smoothly.","lb":"ease, assist","s":["ease","assist","help","simplify","expedite","promote"],"k":["alleviate","back up","lend a hand","mitigate"],"a":["hinder","impede","obstruct","block"],"ex":["A new bridge will facilitate trade between the two towns.","The teacher uses group work to facilitate discussion among shy students.","Mobile banking apps facilitate payments, so people no longer have to stand in long queues."],"b":195,"y":1},{"w":"faction","p":"noun","d":"A small organized group within a larger group, with its own aims, often causing disagreement.","lb":"group, clique","s":["clique","camp","bloc","splinter group","sect","wing"],"k":["alliance","breakaway group","caucus","cell"],"a":[],"ex":["One faction of the student club wanted a picnic, while another preferred a charity drive.","The village committee broke into two factions over where to build the new well.","A small faction of fans started booing, but most of the crowd kept cheering for the team."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"fait accompli","p":"noun","d":"Something that has already happened or been decided, so that it is too late to change or oppose it.","lb":"done deal","s":["done deal","accomplished fact","settled matter","foregone conclusion","irrevocable act","finished business"],"k":["accomplishment","achievement","closed matter","fixed outcome"],"a":[],"ex":["By the time the neighbors objected, the new floor was already built, and it was a fait accompli.","The manager presented the team with a fait accompli: the office had already moved to the new building.","Our parents booked the tickets first and then told us, so the trip was a fait accompli."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fallacious","p":"adjective","d":"Based on a mistaken belief or faulty reasoning; false or misleading.","lb":"false, misleading","s":["false","misleading","erroneous","illogical","unsound","incorrect"],"k":["bogus","deceitful","dishonest","dishonorable"],"a":["sound","valid","logical","accurate"],"ex":["The idea that you can lose weight by skipping every meal is fallacious.","His argument was fallacious because he assumed that one example proved the rule.","The fallacious belief that expensive tutors guarantee top marks makes some families spend more than they can afford."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"fallacy","p":"noun","d":"A mistaken belief, or an error in reasoning that makes an argument seem sound when it is not.","lb":"misconception, false belief","s":["misconception","false belief","error","myth","delusion","flaw"],"k":["chimera","fantasy","fudge","half-truth"],"a":["truth","fact","reality","sound reasoning"],"ex":["It is a fallacy that you must study all night to do well in exams.","The advertisement rests on the fallacy that expensive products are always better than cheaper ones.","In the debate, Nadia pointed out the fallacy in her opponent's argument: correlation does not prove cause."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"falter","p":"verb","d":"To lose strength or confidence and begin to stop, stumble or hesitate.","lb":"hesitate, weaken","s":["hesitate","waver","stumble","stammer","wobble","flag"],"k":["bumble","dither","hobble","limp"],"a":["persevere","continue","strengthen","press on"],"ex":["Her voice faltered when she began to speak about her late grandfather.","The runner faltered near the finish line but did not stop.","Sales faltered after a new competitor opened across the street."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"familiarity","p":"noun","d":"Good knowledge or understanding of something because you have experienced it many times.","lb":"knowledge, acquaintance","s":["knowledge","acquaintance","understanding","awareness","experience","grasp"],"k":["closeness","commonness","ease","expertise"],"a":["ignorance","strangeness","inexperience"],"ex":["Her familiarity with the city helped her find the shortest route home.","The job requires some familiarity with spreadsheets.","Familiarity with the exam format will make you feel less nervous on the day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"familiarize","p":"verb","d":"To make yourself or someone else know something well by learning about it or using it.","lb":"acquaint, introduce","s":["acquaint","introduce","accustom","orient","brief","inform"],"k":["coach","enlighten","immerse","inculcate"],"a":[],"ex":["Please familiarize yourself with the exam rules before the day of the test.","The company held a short session to familiarize new employees with its software.","Visiting the campus early helped me familiarize myself with the buildings."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"farce","p":"noun","d":"A situation or event so badly organised or absurd that it seems like a joke.","lb":"mockery, sham","s":["mockery","sham","travesty","joke","charade","absurdity"],"k":["burlesque","comedy","debacle","fiasco"],"a":[],"ex":["The exam turned into a farce when the lights failed and the invigilator lost the papers.","Many viewers called the final match a farce because of the referee's strange decisions.","The meeting was a farce, with no agenda, no chairperson and everyone talking at once."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"farcical","p":"adjective","d":"So silly, badly organized or unlikely that it seems like a comedy.","lb":"absurd, ridiculous","s":["absurd","ridiculous","ludicrous","laughable","comical","preposterous"],"k":["amusing","cockeyed","comic","foolish"],"a":["serious","sensible","logical","reasonable"],"ex":["Sports day turned farcical when the microphone failed, the tent collapsed and the winner was announced twice.","The meeting became farcical as three people argued over who should take the notes.","The queue at the bank became farcical when two counters closed and the guard began shouting random numbers."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"fascinate","p":"verb","d":"To interest someone so strongly that they cannot stop looking at it or thinking about it.","lb":"captivate, intrigue","s":["captivate","intrigue","absorb","charm","bewitch","enchant"],"k":["attract","beguile","capture","catch"],"a":["bore","repel","disgust","tire"],"ex":["Space has always fascinated my little brother, who reads about planets every night.","The street magician fascinated the children with his card tricks.","Old maps fascinate me because they show how people once saw the world."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fascination","p":"noun","d":"A strong interest in or attraction to something that you find wonderful or unusual.","lb":"interest, attraction","s":["interest","allure","enchantment","charm","obsession","attraction"],"k":["appeal","awe","curiosity","enthusiasm"],"a":["boredom","indifference","disinterest","apathy"],"ex":["My little brother has a fascination with trains and knows every timetable.","The children watched the magician with open-mouthed fascination.","Her fascination with stars led her to study physics."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fastidious","p":"adjective","d":"Very careful about details and cleanliness, and difficult to please.","lb":"picky, meticulous","s":["meticulous","finicky","fussy","particular","picky","choosy"],"k":["careful","conscientious","dainty","demanding"],"a":["careless","sloppy","slapdash","easygoing"],"ex":["My aunt is fastidious about cleanliness and wipes the kitchen counter after every single meal.","Before Eid, the tailor was fastidious about every stitch and would not hand over the panjabi until the sleeves were perfect.","Fastidious about spelling, the editor sent the article back because of one missing comma."],"b":596,"y":2},{"w":"fatalist","p":"noun","d":"A person who believes that all events are decided in advance by fate and that people cannot change them.","lb":"believer in fate","s":["defeatist","pessimist","stoic","believer in destiny"],"k":["doom-monger","karma believer","kismet believer","passive observer"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandfather is a fatalist and says that everything in life happens as it is written.","As a fatalist, she refused to worry about the exam, saying the result was already decided.","The coach is no fatalist; he believes hard training can change any result."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fathom","p":"verb","d":"To understand something difficult or mysterious after thinking about it very hard.","lb":"understand, comprehend","s":["understand","comprehend","grasp","figure out","work out","make out"],"k":["apprehend","get the picture","savvy","solve"],"a":["misunderstand","misread","misjudge","mistake"],"ex":["I cannot fathom why anyone would leave a good job without another plan.","She could not fathom how the lost keys ended up in the refrigerator.","It is hard to fathom the size of the universe."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"fatuous","p":"adjective","d":"Silly and pointless, showing a lack of intelligence, often in a smug way.","lb":"silly, foolish","s":["silly","foolish","inane","stupid","idiotic","asinine"],"k":["cockeyed","complacent","dopey","goofy"],"a":["wise","sensible","intelligent","clever"],"ex":["His fatuous remark that the flood was just a little water annoyed everyone who had lost their homes.","The talk show was full of fatuous questions about celebrity diets.","She wore a fatuous grin while the teacher explained why her answer was wrong."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"fauna","p":"noun","d":"All the animals that live in a particular area or period of time.","lb":"animal life, wildlife","s":["animal life","wildlife","animals","creatures","zoology"],"k":["accumulation","animal","assemblage","beast"],"a":[],"ex":["The Sundarbans is famous for its rich fauna, including tigers, crocodiles and many kinds of birds.","Our biology class studied the fauna of the pond near school, from frogs to tiny fish.","Tourists are asked not to disturb the local fauna during the jungle walk."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"faux","p":"adjective","d":"Not real; made to look like a more expensive or natural material.","lb":"fake, imitation","s":["fake","imitation","artificial","false","mock","synthetic"],"k":["bogus","counterfeit","make-believe","manufactured"],"a":["real","genuine","authentic","natural"],"ex":["Her jacket is made of faux leather, so no animals were harmed.","The sofa has a faux wood finish that looks real but costs much less.","He wore a faux gold chain that left a green mark on his neck."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"faux pas","p":"noun","d":"An embarrassing mistake in social behavior, such as saying or doing something that offends or shames someone.","lb":"social blunder","s":["gaffe","blunder","indiscretion","misstep","slip","social error"],"k":["bloomer","blooper","boner","bungle"],"a":[],"ex":["Arriving at a formal dinner in a T-shirt was a serious faux pas.","Asking the host how much the house cost was a terrible faux pas.","She turned red after her faux pas of calling the manager by the wrong name."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fawn","p":"verb","d":"To flatter someone and act too eagerly to please them in order to gain their favor.","lb":"flatter, grovel","s":["flatter","grovel","toady","kowtow","crawl","butter up"],"k":["bootlick","cajole","cozy up","creep"],"a":["snub","defy","scorn"],"ex":["Some employees fawn over the new manager, laughing at every joke he tells.","The shop assistants fawned over the wealthy customer, bringing tea and praising every choice she made.","I refuse to fawn over my teachers just to get better marks."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"fawning","p":"adjective","d":"Trying too hard to please someone powerful by flattering them or giving them extra attention.","lb":"flattering, servile","s":["servile","obsequious","groveling","flattering","toadying","subservient"],"k":["bootlicking","deferential","effusive","gushing"],"a":["independent","candid","assertive","blunt"],"ex":["The fawning assistant laughed at every joke the boss made, even the bad ones.","Some fans are so fawning that they follow the singer everywhere with gifts.","She was tired of the fawning guests who praised her house before even stepping inside."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"feasibility","p":"noun","d":"The possibility that something can be done or achieved successfully.","lb":"practicality","s":["viability","practicality","possibility","workability","achievability"],"k":["applicability","chances","likelihood","plausibility"],"a":["impossibility"],"ex":["The engineers carried out a study on the feasibility of building a bridge here.","We questioned the feasibility of finishing the project in two weeks.","Before opening the café, Rafi checked the feasibility of the idea with a simple budget."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"feasible","p":"adjective","d":"Possible to do or achieve in practice, with the time and resources available.","lb":"possible, practicable","s":["possible","workable","viable","doable","realistic","attainable"],"k":["affordable","likely","manageable","plausible"],"a":["impossible","impracticable","unworkable","unrealistic"],"ex":["Building a new school in the village is feasible if the community raises some money.","The engineer said it was not feasible to finish the bridge before the monsoon.","Working from home two days a week is a feasible option for most of our staff."],"b":74,"y":1},{"w":"fecund","p":"adjective","d":"Able to produce many young, crops or ideas; very fertile and productive.","lb":"fertile, productive","s":["fertile","fruitful","productive","prolific","rich","lush"],"k":["bountiful","copious","creative","effective"],"a":["barren","infertile","sterile","unproductive"],"ex":["The delta's fecund soil lets farmers grow several rice crops in a single year.","Rabbits are famously fecund animals, and one pair can raise dozens of young in a year.","The poet's most fecund years were spent in a quiet village, where she wrote three collections."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"feeble","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking physical strength, or lacking force or effectiveness.","lb":"weak, ineffective","s":["weak","frail","puny","infirm","ineffective","faint"],"k":["decrepit","delicate","fragile","rickety"],"a":["strong","powerful","robust","vigorous"],"ex":["The old man spoke in a feeble voice, so we leaned closer to hear him.","After three days of fever, she felt too feeble to climb the stairs.","His feeble excuse for being late convinced nobody."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"feign","p":"verb","d":"To pretend to have a feeling, illness or quality that you do not really have.","lb":"pretend, fake","s":["pretend","fake","simulate","put on","sham","affect"],"k":["assume","belie","dissemble","make"],"a":["reveal","show","express","display"],"ex":["Rafi feigned illness so that he could stay home from school.","She feigned surprise when we brought out the birthday cake.","The driver feigned ignorance of the traffic rules when the officer stopped him."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"feint","p":"noun","d":"A deceptive movement meant to mislead an opponent about what you will really do.","lb":"fake move, ruse","s":["ruse","decoy","bluff","dodge","ploy","trick"],"k":["artifice","fake-out","gambit","head fake"],"a":[],"ex":["The striker made a feint to the left and then ran to the right.","The boxer's feint tricked his opponent into lowering his guard.","In chess, a sacrifice can be a feint that hides a bigger plan."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"felicitous","p":"adjective","d":"Well chosen and suitable for the occasion; also pleasant or fortunate.","lb":"apt, fitting","s":["apt","fitting","suitable","appropriate","happy","fortunate"],"k":["adroit","apposite","congratulatory","deft"],"a":["inappropriate","unsuitable","unfortunate","awkward"],"ex":["Her felicitous choice of words made the difficult speech sound warm and gentle.","The name Sunrise Bakery is felicitous, since the shop opens before dawn.","It was a felicitous coincidence that both friends arrived at the station at the same time."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"felicity","p":"noun","d":"Great happiness, especially a state of deep contentment and joy.","lb":"happiness, joy","s":["happiness","joy","bliss","contentment","delight","cheer"],"k":["blessedness","ecstasy","emotional state","euphoria"],"a":["misery","sorrow","unhappiness","grief"],"ex":["The newlyweds wished each other lifelong felicity as they cut the wedding cake.","There was felicity in the house on Eid morning, with laughter and the smell of sweets.","The card wished the new parents every felicity in the years ahead."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"felony","p":"noun","d":"A very serious crime, such as robbery or arson, that carries a heavy punishment.","lb":"serious crime","s":["serious crime","major offence","grave offence","capital crime","major crime"],"k":["break of the law","crime","criminal act","criminal offense"],"a":["misdemeanor","minor offence","petty crime","infraction"],"ex":["Stealing a car is a felony and can lead to many years in prison.","He was charged with a felony after the bank discovered the forged cheques.","In some countries, a felony conviction can stop a person from working in government."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fermentation","p":"noun","d":"A natural process in which yeast or bacteria break down sugar, changing a food or drink.","lb":"chemical breakdown","s":["working","brewing","turmoil","ferment","agitation"],"k":["bubbling","curing","decay","disorder"],"a":[],"ex":["Fermentation turns milk into yoghurt by letting good bacteria grow overnight.","The dough needs an hour of fermentation before it can be baked.","Pickles get their sour taste from fermentation in a sealed jar."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fervent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing very strong and sincere feeling, especially enthusiasm or belief.","lb":"passionate, intense","s":["passionate","ardent","zealous","intense","eager","heartfelt"],"k":["avid","committed","devoted","enthusiastic"],"a":["apathetic","indifferent","cold"],"ex":["He is a fervent supporter of the national cricket team and never misses a match.","She made a fervent plea to the landlord to give her family more time.","The speaker's fervent belief in education inspired the audience."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"fervor","p":"noun","d":"Very strong and sincere feeling, especially enthusiasm or passion.","lb":"passion, intensity","s":["passion","intensity","zeal","ardor","enthusiasm","fire"],"k":["animation","elan","excitation","excitement"],"a":["apathy","indifference","coolness","calmness"],"ex":["The crowd cheered with fervor as the cricket team scored the winning run.","She studied with great fervor in the weeks before the admission test.","The speaker's fervor made even bored listeners lean forward."],"b":17,"y":0},{"w":"fester","p":"verb","d":"To become infected, with a build-up of pus, because a cut or sore has not been cleaned or treated.","lb":"become infected","s":["become infected","go septic","rot","decay"],"k":["brood","decompose","discharge","eject"],"a":["heal","mend","recover","clear up"],"ex":["The scraped knee festered because he never cleaned it properly after the fall.","If a wound begins to fester, see a doctor at once.","The farmer's cut festered after he worked barefoot in the muddy field."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"fetish","p":"noun","d":"Something that a person pays far too much attention to or treats as more important than it is.","lb":"obsession, fixation","s":["obsession","fixation","mania","preoccupation","craze","compulsion"],"k":["bee in your bonnet","compulsive habit","eros","fad"],"a":["indifference","disregard","neglect"],"ex":["He makes a fetish of punctuality, arriving thirty minutes early to every meeting.","Some companies make a fetish of data and ignore common sense.","Our school's fetish for rankings leaves little time for creativity."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"fetter","p":"verb","d":"To restrict someone’s freedom or hold something back so that it cannot develop.","lb":"restrain, hamper","s":["restrain","hamper","shackle","hinder","constrain","restrict"],"k":["check","confine","contain","control"],"a":["free","liberate","release","unleash"],"ex":["Strict rules can fetter creativity, so the studio lets its designers try wild ideas.","Poverty fettered her dreams for years, but a scholarship finally set her free.","He felt fettered by a job that gave him no power to make decisions."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fiasco","p":"noun","d":"A complete and embarrassing failure, especially of something that was carefully planned.","lb":"disaster, debacle","s":["disaster","debacle","flop","catastrophe","failure","washout"],"k":["blunder","botch","breakdown","bust"],"a":["success","triumph","hit","victory"],"ex":["The school picnic turned into a fiasco when the bus never arrived.","The product launch was a fiasco because the website crashed within minutes.","My first attempt at baking bread was a total fiasco; it came out hard as a rock."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"fiat","p":"noun","d":"An official order given by someone in authority, often without discussion or explanation.","lb":"decree, order","s":["decree","order","command","edict","dictate","directive"],"k":["authorization","diktat","imposition","injunction"],"a":[],"ex":["The principal changed the school timetable by fiat, without asking a single teacher.","The club's old president ruled by fiat, so members stopped attending meetings.","The company director announced by fiat that everyone must work on Saturdays."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"fickle","p":"adjective","d":"Changing often and without good reason, especially in your loyalty, feelings or choices.","lb":"changeable, unreliable","s":["changeable","capricious","unpredictable","inconstant","erratic","unreliable"],"k":["freakish","giddy","impulsive","irresolute"],"a":["constant","loyal","steady","reliable"],"ex":["The weather in April is fickle, with sunshine in the morning and thunderstorms by afternoon.","Fashion is fickle; yesterday's bestseller is today's leftover stock.","He was a fickle friend who forgot everyone as soon as he became popular."],"b":96,"y":3},{"w":"fidelity","p":"noun","d":"Loyalty to a person or promise, or accuracy in copying or reproducing something.","lb":"loyalty, accuracy","s":["loyalty","faithfulness","devotion","allegiance","constancy","accuracy"],"k":["adherence","clarity","commitment","fealty"],"a":["disloyalty","betrayal","infidelity","treachery"],"ex":["The dog's fidelity to its owner was clear when it waited at the gate every evening.","Marriage vows promise fidelity in good times and in bad.","Employees were praised for their fidelity to the company during the difficult years."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"fiduciary","p":"noun","d":"A person or organization with a legal duty to manage money or property for someone else's benefit.","lb":"trustee, guardian","s":["trustee","custodian","guardian","steward","administrator","executor"],"k":["conservator","depositary","escrow agent","individual"],"a":[],"ex":["A financial adviser acting as a fiduciary must put the client's interests before their own.","As executor of her uncle's will, Farhana became a fiduciary responsible for sharing his property fairly.","The bank, as a fiduciary, manages the trust fund until the children turn twenty-one."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"figment","p":"noun","d":"Something that someone imagines or invents and believes is real, but that does not exist.","lb":"invention, fantasy","s":["fabrication","fantasy","invention","illusion","delusion","fiction"],"k":["apparition","chimera","concoction","daydream"],"a":["fact","reality","truth"],"ex":["I thought I heard footsteps upstairs, but it was just a figment of my imagination.","The supervisor insisted the problem was a figment of the staff's imagination, but the data proved otherwise.","The rumour that the school would close for a month was a figment, invented by a bored student."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"figurative","p":"adjective","d":"Using a word or phrase in an imaginative, non-literal way to create a picture or effect.","lb":"metaphorical, nonliteral","s":["metaphorical","symbolic","allegorical","representative","imaginative","poetic"],"k":["allusive","analogical","emblematic","extended"],"a":["literal","factual","exact","plain"],"ex":["When she said she was drowning in homework, she meant it in a figurative sense.","Poets use figurative language, such as comparing sadness to a heavy stone.","The phrase break a leg has a figurative meaning of good luck."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"filthiness","p":"noun","d":"The state of being extremely dirty or disgusting.","lb":"dirtiness, foulness","s":["dirtiness","grime","squalor","muck","contamination","nastiness"],"k":["decay","dirt","grunge","messiness"],"a":["cleanliness","purity","hygiene","freshness"],"ex":["The filthiness of the public toilet made everyone avoid it.","Health inspectors closed the kitchen because of its filthiness.","The filthiness of the river water worries the families living along its banks."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"finesse","p":"noun","d":"Great skill and delicacy in handling a difficult situation or doing something.","lb":"skill, subtlety","s":["skill","subtlety","tact","delicacy","diplomacy","flair"],"k":["adroitness","competence","craft","dexterity"],"a":["clumsiness","awkwardness","ineptitude","bluntness"],"ex":["She handled the angry customer with such finesse that he left smiling.","The pianist played the difficult piece with great finesse.","Negotiating a lower rent takes finesse, not shouting."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"fiscal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to money, especially government income, taxes and spending.","lb":"financial, budgetary","s":["financial","monetary","economic","budgetary","pecuniary","commercial"],"k":["exchequer","public finance","revenue","tax"],"a":[],"ex":["Bangladesh's fiscal year starts in July and ends in June.","The government announced a new fiscal policy to reduce the budget deficit.","Our company must submit its tax report before the end of the fiscal year."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"flag","p":"verb","d":"To become tired, or to lose energy, enthusiasm or strength.","lb":"tire, weaken","s":["tire","weaken","wilt","fade","droop","sag"],"k":["decrease","diminish","drop","drop down"],"a":["revive","rally","strengthen","perk up"],"ex":["By the last lap, the runner's energy began to flag, and others passed him.","Interest in the project flagged after the first month, and fewer volunteers came.","Our spirits flagged when the bus broke down for the third time that day."],"b":267,"y":0},{"w":"flagrant","p":"adjective","d":"Obviously and openly wrong or bad, with no attempt to hide it.","lb":"blatant, shocking","s":["blatant","glaring","outrageous","shameless","brazen","obvious"],"k":["appalling","conspicuous","crying","gross"],"a":["subtle","hidden","concealed","covert"],"ex":["Parking across the entrance of a hospital is a flagrant disregard for other people's safety.","The referee sent the player off for a flagrant foul on the goalkeeper.","Copying whole paragraphs from the internet is a flagrant breach of the university's rules."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"flair","p":"noun","d":"A natural talent for doing something well, often with an attractive or stylish touch.","lb":"talent, style","s":["talent","gift","knack","aptitude","bent","panache"],"k":["ability","elan","elegance","endowment"],"a":["ineptitude","incompetence","inability","clumsiness"],"ex":["She has a real flair for languages and picked up Japanese in less than a year.","My cousin has a flair for cooking; even simple rice and lentils taste special when she makes them.","The young designer showed great flair in the way she mixed traditional fabrics with modern cuts."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flamboyant","p":"adjective","d":"Very noticeable because of bright colors, a confident style or an exaggerated manner.","lb":"showy, colorful","s":["showy","flashy","extravagant","ostentatious","colorful","theatrical"],"k":["excessive","florid","garish","gaudy"],"a":["restrained","subdued","modest","understated"],"ex":["The singer arrived at the party in a flamboyant red jacket covered in sequins.","Our flamboyant uncle tells stories with big gestures and loud laughter.","The restaurant's flamboyant decorations, with giant lanterns and bright murals, attract many tourists."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flattery","p":"noun","d":"Excessive praise that is not sincere, given to win someone's favour.","lb":"false praise","s":["adulation","blandishment","sweet talk","fawning","toadying","compliments"],"k":["bootlicking","coaxing","compliment","gushing"],"a":["criticism","insult","honesty","candor"],"ex":["The salesman tried flattery, saying I had excellent taste, but I still refused to buy.","Flattery from classmates who only want your notes is not real friendship.","He used flattery to win over his boss and get an early holiday."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flaunt","p":"verb","d":"To show off something you own or have achieved, so that others notice it.","lb":"show off, parade","s":["show off","parade","display","brandish","exhibit","boast"],"k":["brag","broadcast","demonstrate","expose"],"a":["hide","conceal","downplay","cover up"],"ex":["He likes to flaunt his new phone in front of his classmates.","She never flaunts her wealth and dresses very simply.","Rich guests flaunted their jewelry at the wedding reception."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"flea","p":"noun","d":"A tiny jumping insect without wings that lives on animals and bites them to drink their blood.","lb":"biting insect","s":[],"k":["bedbug","chigger","insect","louse"],"a":[],"ex":["Our cat scratched all day because of a flea in her fur.","The vet gave the puppy a bath to get rid of every flea.","A single flea can jump many times its own height."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fledgling","p":"adjective","d":"Just beginning to develop, or having little experience.","lb":"new, inexperienced","s":["new","inexperienced","budding","emerging","young","beginning"],"k":["callow","fresh","immature","juvenile"],"a":["established","experienced","mature","veteran"],"ex":["The fledgling company had only three employees and one small office.","As a fledgling writer, she sent her first story to ten magazines.","The fledgling cricket team lost its first five matches but kept improving."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"flee","p":"verb","d":"To run away quickly from danger or a frightening situation.","lb":"run away","s":["run away","escape","bolt","take flight","abscond","retreat"],"k":["break away","bunk","elope","fly"],"a":["stay","remain","stand","face"],"ex":["Pigeons fled from the park when the dog ran towards them.","When smoke filled the corridor, the staff fled down the stairs.","The thief fled on a motorbike before the guard could stop him."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fleet","p":"noun","d":"A group of ships, aircraft or vehicles that are controlled or owned by one organization.","lb":"vehicles, ships","s":["armada","convoy","squadron","navy","motorcade","line"],"k":["accumulation","assemblage","carrier group","collection"],"a":[],"ex":["The delivery company has added fifty electric vans to its fleet this year.","A fleet of fishing boats set out from the harbour before sunrise.","The city bus fleet is old, so breakdowns happen almost every week."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flimsy","p":"adjective","d":"Thin, light or badly made, so that it is easily torn, broken or damaged.","lb":"weak, fragile","s":["fragile","frail","weak","thin","rickety","insubstantial"],"k":["brittle","decrepit","delicate","faint"],"a":["sturdy","strong","solid","durable"],"ex":["The flimsy bookshelf collapsed under the weight of the heavy dictionaries.","A flimsy plastic bag split open as I carried the groceries home.","The tin shed was so flimsy that the storm blew its roof away."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flippant","p":"adjective","d":"Not showing proper respect or seriousness about something important.","lb":"disrespectful, glib","s":["disrespectful","glib","cheeky","offhand","frivolous","irreverent"],"k":["breezy","careless","dismissive","jocular"],"a":["serious","respectful","earnest","solemn"],"ex":["His flippant answer to the teacher's question made the whole class gasp.","It was flippant of her to joke about the accident in front of the injured man's family.","Don't be flippant about exams; they decide your future."],"b":104,"y":1},{"w":"flock","p":"noun","d":"A group of birds, sheep or goats that feed or travel together.","lb":"group of birds, herd","s":["herd","drove","group","cluster","gathering","gaggle"],"k":["batch","congregation","crowd","deal"],"a":[],"ex":["A flock of white birds rose from the paddy field as we walked past.","The shepherd led his flock of sheep to the river every morning.","A flock of starlings turned together in the evening sky like one dark cloud."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"florid","p":"adjective","d":"Too elaborate or decorated, especially in writing, speech or design.","lb":"ornate, flowery","s":["ornate","flowery","elaborate","ostentatious","showy","overdone"],"k":["decorative","embellished","extravagant","gaudy"],"a":["plain","simple","restrained","understated"],"ex":["The invitation was written in such florid language that I needed a minute to find the date.","Critics found the novel's florid descriptions tiring and wished the author would simply tell the story.","The wedding hall was decorated in a florid style, with gold curtains and enormous flower arches."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"flounder","p":"verb","d":"To struggle clumsily, or to have difficulty and not know what to do or say.","lb":"struggle, stumble","s":["struggle","flail","stumble","blunder","falter","fumble"],"k":["bumble","fight","lurch","muddle through"],"a":["succeed","thrive","flourish","excel"],"ex":["The child floundered in the deep end of the pool until the lifeguard pulled him out.","I floundered through the interview because I had not prepared any answers.","The truck floundered in the thick mud after a night of rain."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"flout","p":"verb","d":"To openly ignore a rule, law or custom, showing no respect for it.","lb":"defy, disregard","s":["defy","disregard","ignore","break","violate","scorn"],"k":["barrack","brush aside","brush off","dismiss"],"a":["obey","follow","observe","respect"],"ex":["Many motorcyclists flout the traffic rules and ride without helmets on busy roads.","The students flouted the school's dress code by wearing bright caps.","Companies that flout safety laws can be fined or closed down."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"flu","p":"noun","d":"A common infectious illness caused by a virus, with fever, body aches, a sore throat and a cough.","lb":"influenza, illness","s":["influenza","viral fever"],"k":["contagion","contagious disease","respiratory disease","respiratory disorder"],"a":[],"ex":["I caught the flu last week and stayed in bed with a high fever.","Many students missed school because the flu spread quickly through the class.","Doctors advise older people to get a flu vaccine before winter starts."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"fodder","p":"noun","d":"Rough dried plants such as hay and straw fed to farm animals; also, raw material used for something else.","lb":"animal feed","s":["forage","feed","hay"],"k":["ammunition","bran","cannon fodder","fresh fish"],"a":[],"ex":["Farmers store dry fodder in the barn so their cattle can eat during the monsoon floods.","After the flood, the government sent fodder to villages where the cattle were starving.","He cuts fresh grass every morning as fodder for the family's two goats."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"foible","p":"noun","d":"A small weakness or odd habit in someone’s character that is harmless or amusing.","lb":"quirk, weakness","s":["quirk","weakness","failing","flaw","idiosyncrasy","eccentricity"],"k":["crotchet","defect","habit","kink"],"a":["strength","virtue","merit","talent"],"ex":["My father’s one foible is that he cannot pass a sweet shop without buying something.","We tolerate each other’s foibles, such as Rafi’s habit of arriving ten minutes late.","Her favorite foible is rearranging the books on the shelf by color."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"foil","p":"noun","d":"A very thin, flexible sheet of metal, used especially for wrapping food.","lb":"metal sheet","s":["tinfoil","metal leaf","silver paper"],"k":["aluminum","enhancer","gold leaf","kitchen wrap"],"a":[],"ex":["Wrap the leftover bread in foil so that it stays soft until tomorrow.","I pressed the last tablet out of the foil packet and swallowed it with water.","Children peeled the shiny foil from the chocolate coins and ate them at once."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"folly","p":"noun","d":"A foolish action, idea or behavior that is likely to have bad results.","lb":"foolishness, madness","s":["foolishness","stupidity","madness","silliness","idiocy","recklessness"],"k":["blunder","craziness","escapade","foolery"],"a":["wisdom","sense","prudence","good judgment"],"ex":["It would be folly to drive through deep floodwater just to save time.","He realized the folly of spending his savings on a gadget he did not need.","Ignoring the doctor's advice was a folly he soon regretted."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"foment","p":"verb","d":"To encourage or stir up trouble, anger or unrest.","lb":"stir up, incite","s":["incite","stir up","provoke","instigate","agitate","whip up"],"k":["arouse","motivate","move","prompt"],"a":["calm","suppress","quell","soothe"],"ex":["False rumors on social media can foment panic and make people rush to the shops.","Some people foment trouble at school by spreading gossip about classmates.","The article fomented anger among residents by exaggerating the plan's costs."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"fondness","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of liking and affection for someone or something.","lb":"liking, affection","s":["affection","liking","love","warmth","tenderness","attachment"],"k":["fancy","inclination","kindness","predilection"],"a":["dislike","hatred","aversion","antipathy"],"ex":["She spoke of her old teacher with great fondness.","His fondness for sweets means he never says no to dessert.","My grandmother's fondness for gardening turned the balcony into a jungle of pots."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"forager","p":"noun","d":"A person or animal that searches wild areas for food.","lb":"food gatherer","s":["scavenger","searcher"],"k":["browser","collector","gleaner","grazer"],"a":[],"ex":["Early humans were foragers who gathered fruit, roots and nuts.","The squirrel is a busy forager in autumn, storing nuts for the winter.","As an experienced forager, he can tell which wild berries are safe to eat."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"foray","p":"noun","d":"A first attempt to do something new or different from what you usually do.","lb":"venture, first attempt","s":["venture","attempt","excursion","expedition","sortie","initiative"],"k":["adventure","enterprise","experiment","jaunt"],"a":[],"ex":["The bakery's first foray into online sales was a big success.","Rafi's first foray into gardening gave the family fresh tomatoes by June.","The telecom company made a foray into banking services."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"forbear","p":"verb","d":"To hold yourself back from doing or saying something, especially to stay patient or polite.","lb":"refrain, hold back","s":["refrain","abstain","hold back","desist","resist","withhold"],"k":["be patient","bear","endure","give up"],"a":["indulge","persist","proceed","go ahead"],"ex":["I wanted to shout at him, but I managed to forbear and stayed silent.","Please forbear from using your phone while the exam is going on.","Parents should forbear from comparing their children with other students."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"forebode","p":"verb","d":"To be a sign that something bad is going to happen, or to have a feeling that it will.","lb":"foreshadow, portend","s":["foreshadow","portend","predict","presage","warn","augur"],"k":["anticipate","betoken","call","expect"],"a":[],"ex":["The sudden drop in the river’s level foreboded a long and difficult dry season.","Dark clouds and a strong wind foreboded a storm, so the fishermen returned early.","The long silence on the phone foreboded bad news."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"foreboding","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling that something bad is going to happen.","lb":"premonition, dread","s":["premonition","presentiment","apprehension","dread","misgiving","unease"],"k":["dark cloud","fear","gloom","intuition"],"a":["confidence","reassurance","optimism","assurance"],"ex":["She felt a sense of foreboding as the sky turned dark before the cyclone.","A deep foreboding settled over him as he opened the envelope with his results.","The strange silence in the house filled me with foreboding."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"foreclose","p":"verb","d":"To take back a property because the owner has failed to repay the loan used to buy it.","lb":"repossess, seize","s":["repossess","seize","take back","reclaim","confiscate","recover"],"k":["auction","dispossess","distrain","evict"],"a":[],"ex":["The bank threatened to foreclose on the family's house after they missed six payments.","Many homes were foreclosed during the financial crisis when people lost their jobs.","If you stop paying the loan, the lender can foreclose and sell the property."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"forego","p":"verb","d":"To do without something, or to choose not to have or do it; also spelled forgo.","lb":"give up, do without","s":["give up","do without","waive","renounce","sacrifice","relinquish"],"k":["abandon","dispense with","drop","forfeit"],"a":["indulge in","accept","claim","take up"],"ex":["Because I have a long exam tomorrow, I will forego the party and study.","Many families forego a holiday trip when the cost of living rises.","She chose to forego her salary for a month to help the small company survive."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"foregoing","p":"adjective","d":"Mentioned or written just before the present point in a text or speech.","lb":"preceding, previous","s":["preceding","previous","former","above","prior","earlier"],"k":["above-cited","aforesaid","before-mentioned","erstwhile"],"a":["following","subsequent","ensuing","forthcoming"],"ex":["Based on the foregoing paragraphs, we can say that the plan has three main problems.","The foregoing statement is true to the best of my knowledge.","Please read the foregoing instructions carefully before you start the test."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"forensic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the use of science to investigate crimes and provide evidence in a court of law.","lb":"legal, investigative","s":["legal","judicial","courtroom","investigative","scientific"],"k":["applied","ballistic","crime-scene","criminal"],"a":[],"ex":["Forensic experts collected fingerprints and hair samples from the empty office.","The court accepted the forensic report as proof of when the fire started.","My cousin is studying forensic science because she loves solving puzzles."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"forestall","p":"verb","d":"To prevent something from happening by acting before it does.","lb":"prevent, preempt","s":["prevent","preempt","avert","anticipate","ward off","head off"],"k":["avoid","block","deflect","fend off"],"a":["allow","permit","facilitate","encourage"],"ex":["To forestall arguments, the teacher gave every group the same materials.","The bank sent a warning message to forestall fraud before the weekend.","Villagers raised the embankment to forestall flooding during the next monsoon."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"forfeit","p":"verb","d":"To lose something, or give up the right to it, as a penalty for a mistake or crime.","lb":"lose, surrender","s":["lose","surrender","give up","relinquish","sacrifice","waive"],"k":["abandon","be stripped of","cede","deliver"],"a":["keep","retain","gain","earn"],"ex":["If you cancel the booking late, you forfeit your deposit.","The team had to forfeit the match because only seven players arrived.","A driver who ignores the court order may forfeit the right to drive."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"forsake","p":"verb","d":"To leave someone or something behind completely, or to give up a belief, habit or way of life.","lb":"abandon, desert","s":["abandon","desert","leave","quit","renounce","give up"],"k":["desolate","ditch","dump","jilt"],"a":["stay with","support","keep","cherish"],"ex":["He promised he would never forsake his aging parents, whatever job offers came his way.","Many young people forsake village life for the chance of a better salary in Dhaka.","She forsook sugary drinks completely after her doctor warned her about diabetes."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"forswear","p":"verb","d":"To promise to give something up or stop doing it, often in a formal and serious way.","lb":"renounce, give up","s":["renounce","abandon","give up","abjure","disavow","relinquish"],"k":["abdicate","deny","disown","forego"],"a":["embrace","adopt","take up","resume"],"ex":["After his heart surgery, my uncle forswore fried food and started walking every morning.","She forswore social media for a month to focus on her exams.","The company has forsworn plastic packaging and will use paper from next year."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"forte","p":"noun","d":"Something that a person does especially well; their strong point.","lb":"strong point, specialty","s":["strength","strong point","specialty","talent","gift","skill"],"k":["asset","bag","bent","calling"],"a":["weakness","weak point","shortcoming","failing"],"ex":["Math is not my forte, so I always ask my sister for help.","Cooking is Tania’s forte, and her biryani is famous in the neighborhood.","Public speaking is his forte; he can calm any crowd."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"forthcoming","p":"adjective","d":"About to happen or appear soon.","lb":"upcoming, approaching","s":["upcoming","approaching","impending","imminent","coming","expected"],"k":["anticipated","available","due","extroverted"],"a":["past","previous","former","bygone"],"ex":["The school will announce the forthcoming exam schedule next week.","Posters for the forthcoming book fair are on every wall.","I am nervous about the forthcoming interview and cannot sleep."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"forthright","p":"adjective","d":"Honest and direct in speech or manner, saying exactly what you think without hiding anything.","lb":"frank, direct","s":["frank","direct","candid","blunt","outspoken","honest"],"k":["no-nonsense","outright","point-blank","uncompromising"],"a":["evasive","indirect","secretive","devious"],"ex":["She gave a forthright answer when the interviewer asked about her weaknesses.","My doctor was forthright about the risks and did not hide anything.","He is a forthright person who always says exactly what he thinks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"fortuitous","p":"adjective","d":"Happening by chance, especially with a lucky or pleasant result.","lb":"lucky, accidental","s":["chance","lucky","accidental","fortunate","providential","serendipitous"],"k":["auspicious","blessed","felicitous","heaven-sent"],"a":["planned","deliberate","intentional","premeditated"],"ex":["It was a fortuitous meeting, because I ran into my old teacher at the bus stop just when I needed advice.","A fortuitous delay at the station kept us off the train that broke down later.","The company's fortuitous discovery of a cheaper supplier saved it thousands of taka."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"fortunate","p":"adjective","d":"Having good luck, or bringing or resulting from good luck.","lb":"lucky","s":["lucky","blessed","favored","providential","charmed","prosperous"],"k":["better off","blest","felicitous","fortuitous"],"a":["unfortunate","unlucky","hapless","cursed"],"ex":["I was fortunate to find a seat on the crowded morning train.","She felt fortunate to have teachers who believed in her.","It was fortunate that we had an umbrella when the sudden storm started."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"foster","p":"verb","d":"To encourage something to develop or grow over time.","lb":"encourage, nurture","s":["encourage","promote","nurture","cultivate","support","stimulate"],"k":["champion","endorse","fuel","heighten"],"a":["hinder","stifle","discourage","suppress"],"ex":["Good teachers foster curiosity by encouraging students to ask questions.","The club fosters friendship among students from different departments.","The new law aims to foster small businesses in rural areas."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"founder","p":"verb","d":"To fail completely, or, of a ship, to fill with water and sink.","lb":"fail, sink","s":["fail","collapse","sink","fall through","come to grief","break down"],"k":["be scuttled","capsize","cave in","come unstuck"],"a":["succeed","thrive","flourish","prosper"],"ex":["The business foundered within a year because it could not pay its rent.","Our picnic plans foundered when the rain started and the bus never came.","The project foundered after two key engineers left the company."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fragile","p":"adjective","d":"Easily broken, damaged or harmed; needing careful handling.","lb":"delicate, breakable","s":["delicate","breakable","brittle","flimsy","frail","weak"],"k":["crumbly","feeble","friable","insignificant"],"a":["sturdy","strong","durable","robust"],"ex":["Please mark the box fragile, because it contains glass cups.","The old manuscript is so fragile that readers must wear gloves.","My grandmother's health is fragile in the cold winter months."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fragmentary","p":"adjective","d":"Made up of small separate pieces and not complete or connected.","lb":"incomplete, broken","s":["incomplete","partial","piecemeal","disconnected","scattered","sketchy"],"k":["disjointed","jagged","splintered","sporadic"],"a":["complete","whole","entire","continuous"],"ex":["Police had only fragmentary evidence, so they could not yet charge anyone.","Because of the power cut, we received only fragmentary news of the cyclone's path.","The patient's memory of the accident is fragmentary; he recalls just a few images."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"frail","p":"adjective","d":"Physically weak and easily harmed, especially because of old age or illness.","lb":"weak, delicate","s":["weak","feeble","delicate","fragile","infirm","puny"],"k":["breakable","brittle","dainty","failing"],"a":["strong","sturdy","robust","hardy"],"ex":["My frail grandmother needs help to climb the stairs.","After a long illness, the frail child could barely walk to the door.","The frail old man leaned on his stick while crossing the road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fraternal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to brothers, or friendly and supportive in the way brothers are.","lb":"brotherly, friendly","s":["brotherly","comradely","friendly","familial","affectionate","kindred"],"k":["collegial","companionable","cordial","filial"],"a":["hostile","unfriendly","antagonistic","estranged"],"ex":["Despite their quarrels, there was a strong fraternal bond between the two brothers.","The coach wanted the team to feel a fraternal loyalty, like a family.","The two schools have a friendly rivalry, but they show fraternal support for each other in finals."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"fraudulent","p":"adjective","d":"Intended to deceive people in order to gain money or an advantage illegally.","lb":"dishonest, fake","s":["dishonest","deceitful","fake","counterfeit","bogus","crooked"],"k":["bastard","dishonorable","dubious","fallacious"],"a":["honest","genuine","legitimate","authentic"],"ex":["Police found fraudulent certificates in the office of the fake training centre.","The bank blocked her card after noticing a fraudulent payment.","He made a fraudulent claim for an accident that never happened."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"frenetic","p":"adjective","d":"Done in a fast, excited and uncontrolled way, often because of stress or rush.","lb":"frantic, hectic","s":["frantic","frenzied","hectic","feverish","wild","manic"],"k":["breakneck","excited","harried","high-octane"],"a":["calm","relaxed","leisurely","peaceful"],"ex":["The kitchen was frenetic an hour before the wedding feast, with cooks shouting and pans clattering.","The markets are at their most frenetic in the last days before Eid, when everyone rushes to shop.","After weeks of frenetic studying, she finally slept for ten hours the night after the exam."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"fret","p":"verb","d":"To worry continually about something, especially small or unimportant problems.","lb":"worry, agonize","s":["worry","brood","agonize","stew","fuss","panic"],"k":["chafe","choke","eat away","eat into"],"a":["relax","calm down","unwind"],"ex":["Don't fret about the exam; you have prepared very well.","My mother frets whenever I travel alone at night.","He fretted over every small detail of the presentation."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"frog","p":"noun","d":"A small amphibian with smooth skin, long back legs and no tail, which lives near water.","lb":"amphibian","s":["toad","toad frog"],"k":["amphibian","bullfrog","newt","salamander"],"a":[],"ex":["After the monsoon rain, a loud chorus of frogs filled the night.","The frog jumped into the pond with a small splash.","In biology class, we studied how a tadpole turns into a frog."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"frown","p":"verb","d":"To pull your eyebrows together and wrinkle your forehead, showing anger, worry or dislike.","lb":"scowl","s":["scowl","glower","glare","grimace","pout"],"k":["furrow","look askance","lour","lower"],"a":["smile","grin","beam"],"ex":["The teacher frowned when she saw the messy handwriting.","He frowned at the screen, trying to understand the error message.","My father frowns whenever I come home after ten."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"frugal","p":"adjective","d":"Careful about spending money and not wasting anything.","lb":"thrifty, economical","s":["thrifty","economical","sparing","prudent","careful","provident"],"k":["budget-minded","canny","cautious","modest"],"a":["wasteful","extravagant","lavish","spendthrift"],"ex":["My frugal mother saves every plastic bag and reuses it many times.","Students on a small budget learn to be frugal with their pocket money.","We had a frugal dinner of rice and lentils after the expensive Eid shopping."],"b":90,"y":2},{"w":"frugality","p":"noun","d":"Careful use of money and resources, avoiding waste.","lb":"thrift, economy","s":["thrift","economy","prudence","saving","husbandry","moderation"],"k":["abstemiousness","austerity","conservation","discretion"],"a":["extravagance","squandering"],"ex":["Her frugality let the family save enough for a small house in five years.","Frugality means buying only what you need and comparing prices first.","He was known for his frugality, always reusing paper and walking instead of taking a rickshaw."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"fruitful","p":"adjective","d":"Producing good results or a useful outcome; worth the time and effort spent.","lb":"productive, rewarding","s":["productive","successful","rewarding","profitable","worthwhile","useful"],"k":["bountiful","breeding","constructive","fat"],"a":["fruitless","unproductive","useless","barren"],"ex":["We had a fruitful meeting and agreed on a plan for the project.","The long hours of practice proved fruitful when she won the debate.","The delta's fruitful soil allows farmers to grow three crops a year."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"fuel","p":"verb","d":"To make a feeling, activity or situation stronger or more active.","lb":"stimulate, stoke","s":["stimulate","feed","stoke","fan","inflame","encourage"],"k":["arouse","excite","inspire","provoke"],"a":["dampen","quench","extinguish","suppress"],"ex":["Rising food prices have fueled anger among shoppers.","His praise fueled her desire to become a doctor.","Silence from the company only fueled rumors about the product recall."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"fugitive","p":"noun","d":"A person who is running away or hiding, especially from the police.","lb":"runaway, escapee","s":["runaway","escapee","outlaw","deserter","wanted person"],"k":["bolter","evader","exile","fleer"],"a":[],"ex":["Police searched the whole district for the fugitive who had escaped from the prison van.","The fugitive hid in a village for two months before the police found him.","The newspaper printed a photo of the fugitive and asked readers for information."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"fulminate","p":"verb","d":"To express strong anger or criticism loudly about something.","lb":"rage, denounce","s":["rail","rant","rage","storm","thunder","denounce"],"k":["blow up","bluster","flare up","harangue"],"a":["praise","commend","applaud","extol"],"ex":["My uncle fulminates against the noisy loudspeakers every time a wedding procession passes his house.","Customers fulminated online about the delayed deliveries and the shop's poor service.","The coach fulminated about the team's careless mistakes for ten minutes in the changing room."],"b":100,"y":1},{"w":"fulsome","p":"adjective","d":"Overdone and insincere, especially in praise or thanks, so that it sounds false.","lb":"excessive, insincere","s":["excessive","effusive","gushing","flattering","insincere","unctuous"],"k":["burbling","buttery","extravagant","fawning"],"a":["sincere","restrained","moderate","genuine"],"ex":["The salesman's fulsome compliments made me feel he just wanted to sell me something.","The speaker gave fulsome thanks to the chief guest, but it sounded rehearsed and false.","I distrust fulsome praise; honest feedback is far more useful."],"b":72,"y":1},{"w":"fur","p":"noun","d":"The soft, thick hair that covers the bodies of some animals, such as cats and rabbits.","lb":"animal hair","s":["coat","hair","pelt","hide","fleece"],"k":["animal skin","ermine","mink","sable"],"a":[],"ex":["The kitten's soft fur felt warm against my hands.","Dogs shed more fur in spring, so we brush ours every day.","Many shops now sell winter coats made without real fur."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"further","p":"adverb","d":"To a greater degree, distance or extent.","lb":"more, farther","s":["farther","more","beyond","onward","deeper","in addition"],"k":["in more depth","more so","still","to a greater extent"],"a":["nearer","closer","less"],"ex":["We can't drive any further because the road is flooded.","The company plans to expand its business further next year.","Nadia studied the topic further and found several mistakes in the textbook."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"furtive","p":"adjective","d":"Done quietly and secretly, as if you do not want to be noticed.","lb":"secret, sneaky","s":["secretive","stealthy","sly","sneaky","surreptitious","covert"],"k":["backstairs","cloak-and-dagger","concealed","hidden"],"a":["open","frank","candid","blatant"],"ex":["During the lecture, she took a furtive look at her phone under the desk.","The cat made a furtive dash across the kitchen and snatched a piece of fish.","My little sister's furtive smile told me she had already found her birthday present."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"fuss","p":"noun","d":"Unnecessary worry, excitement or complaint about something unimportant.","lb":"commotion, bother","s":["bother","commotion","stir","ado","trouble","flap"],"k":["bicker","bickering","bustle","din"],"a":["calm","peace","quiet","composure"],"ex":["Please don't make a fuss; it is only a small scratch.","The baby made a fuss when he was put in his cot.","There was a big fuss at the airport when the airline lost our luggage."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"futile","p":"adjective","d":"Having no chance of success; pointless.","lb":"useless, pointless","s":["useless","pointless","vain","fruitless","hopeless","unproductive"],"k":["abortive","bootless","forlorn","ineffectual"],"a":["useful","productive","effective","fruitful"],"ex":["It is futile to argue with someone who refuses to listen.","All our attempts to start the old motorbike were futile.","The search for the lost cat was futile, though we looked all night."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"futility","p":"noun","d":"The quality of having no purpose or chance of success.","lb":"pointlessness","s":["uselessness","vanity","hopelessness","emptiness","pointlessness"],"k":["absurdity","frustration","idleness","impotence"],"a":["usefulness","effectiveness","value","utility"],"ex":["The futility of arguing with the broken ticket machine became obvious to everyone.","She felt the futility of studying all night without a plan.","Many people recognize the futility of complaining without offering a solution."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gaffe","p":"noun","d":"A social mistake or careless remark that embarrasses you or other people.","lb":"blunder, faux pas","s":["blunder","faux pas","mistake","slip","error","indiscretion"],"k":["bloomer","blooper","boner","boob"],"a":[],"ex":["He made a terrible gaffe by asking the bride’s uncle whether he was her grandfather.","The company apologized for a gaffe in its advertisement that spelled the product name wrong.","Calling the new manager by the wrong name was an embarrassing gaffe."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gainsay","p":"verb","d":"To deny or contradict something, or to speak against it.","lb":"deny, contradict","s":["deny","contradict","dispute","challenge","oppose","refute"],"k":["contend","controvert","discredit","impugn"],"a":["affirm","confirm","support","agree with"],"ex":["Nobody can gainsay her talent; she wins every singing contest at school.","The facts are clear, and no one can gainsay them.","He would not gainsay his father's decision, even though he disagreed with it."],"b":11,"y":0},{"w":"galvanize","p":"verb","d":"To shock or excite someone so that they suddenly start to take action.","lb":"spur, rouse","s":["spur","stimulate","energize","rouse","motivate","provoke"],"k":["animate","arouse","ball over","blow out of the water"],"a":["discourage","dampen","deter"],"ex":["The cyclone warning galvanized villagers into moving to the shelters.","The coach's speech galvanized the team at half-time.","A news report on the polluted river galvanized students to start a cleaning campaign."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gambit","p":"noun","d":"A clever or risky first move made to gain an advantage in a game, negotiation or conversation.","lb":"ploy, opening move","s":["ploy","manoeuvre","move","stratagem","tactic","ruse"],"k":["artifice","bid","feint","maneuver"],"a":[],"ex":["Offering a free trial was a clever gambit to attract new customers.","In chess, giving up a pawn at the start can be a good opening gambit.","His opening gambit in the salary talks was to ask for double what he really wanted."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gamut","p":"noun","d":"The complete range of things of a particular type that something covers.","lb":"range, spectrum","s":["range","spectrum","scope","span","sweep","extent"],"k":["breadth","catalog","continuum","field"],"a":[],"ex":["Her feelings ran the gamut from excitement to fear on the first day of university.","The shop sells the whole gamut of phone accessories, from cheap cables to premium speakers.","The course covers the full gamut of writing skills, from emails to research essays."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"garner","p":"verb","d":"To gather or earn something such as praise, support or information, usually through effort.","lb":"gather, earn","s":["gather","collect","earn","acquire","amass","attract"],"k":["assemble","build up","congregate","gain"],"a":["scatter","lose","squander","forfeit"],"ex":["The short film garnered praise from critics and won three awards at the student festival.","Her online post about plastic waste garnered thousands of shares in a single day.","To garner support for the new library, the students collected signatures at the school gate."],"b":108,"y":1},{"w":"garrulous","p":"adjective","d":"Talking a lot, especially about unimportant things.","lb":"talkative, chatty","s":["talkative","chatty","loquacious","voluble","wordy","verbose"],"k":["blabby","communicative","gabby","jabbering"],"a":["quiet","taciturn","reserved","silent"],"ex":["My garrulous neighbor can talk for an hour about the price of fish.","The garrulous taxi driver told us his life story during a ten-minute ride.","After two cups of tea, the shy boy became surprisingly garrulous."],"b":603,"y":1},{"w":"gasp","p":"verb","d":"To take a quick, sharp breath through the mouth because of surprise, pain or effort.","lb":"breathe sharply","s":["pant","puff","wheeze","choke","heave","huff"],"k":["catch your breath","gape","hiss","sob"],"a":[],"ex":["He gasped for air after running up five flights of stairs.","The audience gasped when the magician made the car disappear.","She gasped in pain as the hot oil splashed onto her hand."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gastronomy","p":"noun","d":"The art and knowledge of good food and cooking, especially of a particular region.","lb":"cuisine, fine dining","s":["cuisine","cookery","culinary arts","fine dining","haute cuisine"],"k":["cooking","culinary art","culinary heritage","epicureanism"],"a":[],"ex":["My sister plans to study gastronomy and open a small restaurant someday.","The festival celebrates the gastronomy of our coastal region, from spicy beef curries to fresh seafood.","The travel magazine praised the island for its gastronomy as much as its beaches."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gauche","p":"adjective","d":"Awkward and clumsy in social situations, often saying or doing the wrong thing.","lb":"awkward, tactless","s":["awkward","tactless","clumsy","unsophisticated","inept","uncouth"],"k":["clunky","cumbersome","gawky","inelegant"],"a":["tactful","graceful","polished","suave"],"ex":["It was gauche of him to ask how much the gift had cost.","The gauche young man spilled tea on the host's carpet and made things worse by laughing.","She felt gauche at the formal dinner because she did not know which fork to use."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"gauge","p":"verb","d":"To estimate or judge something, such as a feeling, amount or situation, by careful observation or measurement.","lb":"estimate, judge","s":["assess","judge","estimate","evaluate","measure","size up"],"k":["analyze","appraise","check","compute"],"a":[],"ex":["The teacher asked questions to gauge how much the students had understood.","It is hard to gauge how deep the river is from the bank.","The company sent a survey to gauge customers' satisfaction with the new app."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gay","p":"adjective","d":"Cheerful, lively and bright; an old-fashioned sense, since the word now more often means homosexual.","lb":"cheerful, bright","s":["cheerful","merry","lively","jolly","bright","colourful"],"k":["brave","cheery","genial","gleeful"],"a":["gloomy","sad","dull","sombre"],"ex":["The street was gay with coloured lights and music during the festival.","Her gay laughter filled the whole garden on the sunny afternoon.","The old novel describes a gay party with dancing and lanterns."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"generic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to a whole group or type rather than a specific one; or sold without a brand name.","lb":"general, unbranded","s":["general","common","universal","nonspecific","standard","plain"],"k":["broad","ordinary","overall","typical"],"a":["specific","particular","branded","special"],"ex":["A generic version of the medicine costs half the price of the branded one.","Paracetamol is the generic name of a common painkiller.","The email was so generic that it could have been sent to anyone."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"genesis","p":"noun","d":"The origin or beginning of something, the point at which it first comes into being.","lb":"origin, beginning","s":["origin","beginning","birth","start","source","creation"],"k":["commencement","cradle","embryo","fountainhead"],"a":["end","conclusion","death","finish"],"ex":["The genesis of the project was a casual chat between two friends at a tea stall.","Historians study the genesis of the conflict to understand why it began.","The genesis of the city's flooding problem lies in blocked drains and years of poor planning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"genial","p":"adjective","d":"Friendly, cheerful and pleasant in manner.","lb":"friendly, cheerful","s":["friendly","cordial","affable","warm","amiable","congenial"],"k":["breezy","convivial","easygoing","gregarious"],"a":["unfriendly","cold","hostile","gloomy"],"ex":["Our genial landlord always greets the tenants with a smile and a cup of tea.","The genial host made every guest feel welcome at the wedding.","Mr. Alam is a genial teacher who jokes with his students before every class."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"genocide","p":"noun","d":"The deliberate killing of a large number of people from a particular nation, race or ethnic group.","lb":"mass murder, extermination","s":["extermination","ethnic cleansing","mass murder","annihilation","mass killing","holocaust"],"k":["atrocity","bloodbath","butchery","carnage"],"a":[],"ex":["Our history class studied how the world responded to genocide in the twentieth century.","The United Nations adopted a convention to prevent and punish the crime of genocide.","Museums about genocide help young people understand why such horrors must never be repeated."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"genre","p":"noun","d":"A particular type or category of art, writing, film or music.","lb":"type, category","s":["type","kind","category","style","class","sort"],"k":["group","literary genre","music genre","musical genre"],"a":[],"ex":["Mystery is my favorite genre, and I read a new detective novel every week.","Hip-hop is a music genre that began in New York.","The bookshop arranges its shelves by genre, such as romance, history and science fiction."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"genteel","p":"adjective","d":"Polite and refined in manner, sometimes in an exaggerated way that tries to seem upper-class.","lb":"refined, polite","s":["refined","polite","cultured","elegant","courteous","civilized"],"k":["affected","civil","cultivated","decorous"],"a":["coarse","rude","vulgar","uncouth"],"ex":["The genteel old lady served tea in tiny china cups and spoke in a soft voice.","He tried to sound genteel on the phone, but his excitement kept breaking through.","The small hotel had a genteel atmosphere, with quiet piano music and polite waiters."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"gerbil","p":"noun","d":"A small furry desert rodent with long back legs, often kept as a pet.","lb":"pet rodent","s":[],"k":["dormouse","hamster","jerboa","jird"],"a":[],"ex":["My little sister feeds her pet gerbil a few seeds every morning.","The gerbil ran inside its wheel all night and kept me awake.","A gerbil digs tunnels in sand, so its cage needs a deep layer of bedding."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"germane","p":"adjective","d":"Directly related to the subject being discussed, and therefore appropriate.","lb":"relevant, pertinent","s":["relevant","pertinent","applicable","related","apposite","appropriate"],"k":["bearing","cognate","on point","on topic"],"a":["irrelevant","unrelated","extraneous","immaterial"],"ex":["The teacher said my question was germane and spent time answering it.","Please include only information germane to the job in your application.","That story about your holiday is interesting, but it is not germane to today's meeting."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"gerrymander","p":"verb","d":"To draw the boundaries of a voting area unfairly so that one side gains an advantage.","lb":"manipulate, rig","s":["manipulate","rig","fix","skew","distort","tamper with"],"k":["bend","carve up","cheat","divide"],"a":[],"ex":["Critics said officials were trying to gerrymander the districts to help their own candidates.","The city council was accused of gerrymandering the school zones to keep certain schools full.","A court ordered the state to redraw its map after finding that it had been gerrymandered."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"gesticulate","p":"verb","d":"To move one's hands and arms to express something, especially while speaking or instead of speaking.","lb":"gesture, wave","s":["gesture","motion","signal","wave","sign","indicate"],"k":["communicate","emote","flail","flap"],"a":[],"ex":["The tourist could not speak Bangla, so he gesticulated until the shopkeeper understood what he wanted.","My uncle gesticulates wildly whenever he argues about cricket.","The traffic officer gesticulated at the rickshaws to move into the left lane."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"gesture","p":"noun","d":"A movement of the hands, head or body that expresses an idea or feeling.","lb":"movement, sign","s":["signal","motion","sign","wave","nod","indication"],"k":["action","bow","cue","flow"],"a":[],"ex":["The traffic police officer made a gesture with his hand for the bus to stop.","When she could not speak the language, she used gestures to order food.","A friendly wave is a gesture that people understand in every country."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ghastly","p":"adjective","d":"Shockingly horrible, frightening or very unpleasant; also looking pale and sick.","lb":"horrible, terrible","s":["horrible","dreadful","awful","terrible","frightful","appalling"],"k":["abominable","alarming","atrocious","charnel"],"a":["pleasant","lovely","delightful","wonderful"],"ex":["The highway accident was so ghastly that many drivers could not look at the scene.","The soup tasted ghastly, so I pushed the bowl away.","She looked ghastly after three nights without sleep, with pale skin and dark circles."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gigantic","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely large in size, amount or degree, like a giant.","lb":"huge, enormous","s":["huge","enormous","massive","colossal","immense","vast"],"k":["big","hulking","jumbo","large"],"a":["tiny","minute","small","miniature"],"ex":["A gigantic wave rolled toward the beach, and everyone ran back.","The new shopping mall is gigantic, and we got lost on the third floor.","Dinosaurs were gigantic animals that lived millions of years ago."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gingerly","p":"adverb","d":"In a very careful or cautious way, to avoid causing damage, pain or noise.","lb":"carefully, cautiously","s":["carefully","cautiously","delicately","tentatively","hesitantly","softly"],"k":["circumspectly","gently","guardedly","nervously"],"a":["carelessly","roughly","boldly","recklessly"],"ex":["He stepped gingerly onto the wet floor so he would not slip.","She touched the sore tooth gingerly with her tongue.","The boy gingerly carried the full cup of tea across the room."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"girth","p":"noun","d":"The measurement around the middle of something, such as a person's waist or a tree trunk.","lb":"circumference, size","s":["circumference","perimeter","waistline","thickness","bulk","width"],"k":["breadth","cinch","corpulence","heft"],"a":[],"ex":["The tailor measured my chest and waist to check my girth before cutting the cloth.","It took three people holding hands to circle the girth of the ancient banyan tree.","The doctor said that waist girth is a useful sign of certain health risks."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"glaze","p":"verb","d":"To cover pottery or food with a thin, shiny layer that gives a smooth finish.","lb":"coat, polish","s":["coat","varnish","enamel","lacquer","gloss","polish"],"k":["brush","burnish","candy","frost"],"a":["dull"],"ex":["The potter glazed each bowl before placing it in the hot kiln.","Mum glazed the cake with a thin layer of sugar and lemon juice.","Bakers glaze the buns with egg so that they come out golden and shiny."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gleam","p":"noun","d":"A soft, bright light or reflection, often seen on a shiny surface.","lb":"flash, glint","s":["glint","glimmer","flash","sparkle","shimmer","glow"],"k":["brilliance","flicker","glisten","luster"],"a":["darkness","dullness","gloom"],"ex":["A gleam of moonlight fell across the quiet water of the pond.","The gleam of the new car caught everyone's attention in the car park.","I saw a gleam of light under the door and knew someone was awake."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"glean","p":"verb","d":"To collect information, facts or knowledge slowly and with some effort, often from different sources.","lb":"gather, collect","s":["gather","collect","learn","extract","pick up","harvest"],"k":["accumulate","acquire","amass","assemble"],"a":["scatter","disperse","lose","waste"],"ex":["From the reports, we could glean that sales had dropped sharply in March.","Journalists glean information from many sources before writing a story.","I gleaned a few useful tips about the interview from older students."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"glide","p":"verb","d":"To move smoothly and quietly, without effort or sudden movements.","lb":"move smoothly","s":["slide","coast","sail","skim","slip","float"],"k":["breeze","cruise","move","soar"],"a":["lurch","jerk","stumble"],"ex":["The swans glided across the lake without a sound.","The skater glided over the ice as if she had no weight.","Eagles glide above the valley without moving their wings."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"glitter","p":"verb","d":"To shine brightly with many small flashes of light.","lb":"sparkle, shine","s":["sparkle","glisten","shimmer","twinkle","flash","glint"],"k":["appear","coruscate","dazzle","flicker"],"a":["dim","fade"],"ex":["Dew glittered on the paddy leaves in the early morning sun.","Her sequin dress glittered under the stage lights.","The sea glittered in the afternoon light as the boat moved slowly forward."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gloat","p":"verb","d":"To show great pleasure, in an unkind way, at your own success or at someone else's bad luck.","lb":"boast, rejoice","s":["crow","exult","rub it in","revel","relish","triumph"],"k":["bluster","chortle","jeer","preen"],"a":["sympathize","commiserate","console","empathize"],"ex":["Don't gloat about your higher score; your friend studied hard too.","The rival team's fans gloated over our defeat all week.","He gloated when his old classmate's business failed, which showed how petty he was."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gloomy","p":"adjective","d":"Dark, dull and depressing to look at or to be in.","lb":"dark, dismal","s":["dark","dim","dull","dismal","murky","cloudy"],"k":["black","blue","boring","dejected"],"a":["bright","sunny","cheerful","light"],"ex":["The sky stayed gloomy all day, and it rained again in the evening.","We rented a gloomy basement flat that never got any sunlight.","It was a gloomy morning in Dhaka, with thick clouds hanging over the city."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"glut","p":"noun","d":"A supply of something that is much larger than people need or want, often making prices fall.","lb":"surplus, oversupply","s":["surplus","excess","surfeit","overabundance","saturation","overload"],"k":["abundance","avalanche","deluge","mountain"],"a":["shortage","scarcity","dearth","lack"],"ex":["A glut of mangoes in June pushed prices so low that farmers hardly covered their costs.","There is a glut of graduates in the job market, so many accept jobs below their skills.","The shop had a glut of winter jackets after the warm season and offered half-price deals."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"goad","p":"verb","d":"To urge or provoke someone to do something, usually by annoying or pushing them.","lb":"provoke, urge","s":["provoke","prod","spur","urge","incite","push"],"k":["arouse","badger","bait","egg on"],"a":["restrain","discourage","deter","dissuade"],"ex":["His friends goaded him into jumping from the high rock, and he regretted it.","The coach tried to goad the team into playing harder at half time.","Do not let their teasing goad you into losing your temper."],"b":13,"y":0},{"w":"gouge","p":"verb","d":"To cut or dig a rough hole or groove in something, or to charge someone far too much money.","lb":"dig out, overcharge","s":["dig","scoop","gash","hollow out","carve","scrape"],"k":["cheat","cut","extort","force out"],"a":[],"ex":["The sharp rock gouged a deep scratch into the side of our boat.","He used a small tool to gouge a groove in the piece of wood.","The heavy truck gouged deep ruts in the muddy field road."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"grain","p":"noun","d":"A tiny hard piece of something such as sand, salt or rice.","lb":"tiny particle","s":["particle","speck","crumb","seed","fleck"],"k":["atom","cereal","corpuscle","food grain"],"a":[],"ex":["A single grain of sand in my shoe made the long walk painful.","Not a single grain of rice was wasted at the family dinner.","Add only a few grains of salt to the soup, because the stock is already salty."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"grandiloquent","p":"adjective","d":"Using long, impressive-sounding words and a grand style in order to seem important.","lb":"pompous, bombastic","s":["pompous","bombastic","pretentious","inflated","windy","turgid"],"k":["affected","declamatory","elevated","highfalutin"],"a":["plain","simple","unpretentious","modest"],"ex":["The mayor's grandiloquent speech about a small road repair made the audience smile.","Her grandiloquent email, packed with long words, hid the fact that she had little to say.","I prefer a plain style to the grandiloquent language some students copy from old textbooks."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"grandiose","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming impressive but too large, ambitious or showy to be practical or believable.","lb":"pompous, showy","s":["pompous","ostentatious","extravagant","showy","pretentious","lofty"],"k":["flashy","highfalutin","impressive","lavish"],"a":["modest","humble","simple","unpretentious"],"ex":["The new student made grandiose promises about changing the school, but nothing happened.","Their grandiose wedding hall had golden chairs and a fountain that nobody needed.","The company announced grandiose plans for a flying taxi service, even though it had no money."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"gratify","p":"verb","d":"To please someone, or to satisfy a wish or need.","lb":"please, satisfy","s":["please","satisfy","delight","indulge","fulfill","humor"],"k":["appease","cheer","flatter","pander"],"a":["disappoint","frustrate","displease","deny"],"ex":["It gratified the teacher to see her weakest student score top marks.","The mayor was gratified by the large crowd that came to the opening.","Fast food can gratify your hunger quickly, but it rarely gives good nutrition."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gratis","p":"adverb","d":"Without having to pay anything; given or done free of charge.","lb":"free, at no cost","s":["free","free of charge","for nothing","without charge","at no cost","for free"],"k":["as a courtesy","as a freebie","for a song","on us"],"a":["at a price","for payment","for a fee"],"ex":["The mobile shop gave me a screen protector gratis when I bought the new phone.","Children under five travel gratis on all the ferry routes.","The clinic offers eye tests gratis to elderly people every Friday morning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gratitude","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of being thankful and wanting to show appreciation for something kind that someone has done.","lb":"thankfulness, appreciation","s":["thankfulness","appreciation","thanks","acknowledgment","indebtedness","recognition"],"k":["debt","esteem","feeling","goodwill"],"a":["ingratitude"],"ex":["She wrote a card to express her gratitude to the nurse who cared for her.","He showed his gratitude by bringing sweets for the whole neighbourhood.","The villagers felt deep gratitude to the volunteers who rebuilt their bridge."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gratuitous","p":"adjective","d":"Done or given without any good reason or need, and often unkind or unwelcome.","lb":"unnecessary, unjustified","s":["unnecessary","unwarranted","uncalled for","unjustified","needless","unprovoked"],"k":["complimentary","excessive","free","groundless"],"a":["justified","necessary","warranted","deserved"],"ex":["His gratuitous comment about her weight upset her and ruined the whole evening.","Many viewers complained that the film contained gratuitous violence that added nothing to the story.","The referee gave a gratuitous warning to a player who had done nothing wrong."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"gravity","p":"noun","d":"The serious or worrying importance of a situation, event or mistake.","lb":"seriousness, severity","s":["seriousness","severity","importance","weight","significance","magnitude"],"k":["consequence","earnestness","import","materiality"],"a":["triviality","levity","insignificance","lightness"],"ex":["The doctor explained the gravity of the situation and urged the family to act quickly.","Some students did not understand the gravity of cheating until they were suspended.","The gravity of the flood became clear when whole villages disappeared under the water."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"gregarious","p":"adjective","d":"Enjoying the company of other people and being very sociable.","lb":"sociable, outgoing","s":["sociable","outgoing","friendly","extroverted","convivial","companionable"],"k":["chummy","clubbable","clustered","collegial"],"a":["introverted","reserved","unsociable","withdrawn"],"ex":["My gregarious uncle makes friends with everyone he meets on the train.","Nadia is so gregarious that she loved the crowded dining hall in her hostel.","Wolves are gregarious animals that live and hunt together in packs."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"grievous","p":"adjective","d":"Very serious and causing great pain, sorrow or harm.","lb":"serious, painful","s":["severe","serious","grave","dire","painful","heavy"],"k":["acute","atrocious","critical","dangerous"],"a":["minor","trivial","slight","mild"],"ex":["The driver made a grievous error and pulled out in front of a speeding truck.","The earthquake caused grievous damage to the old buildings in the town.","Losing her grandmother was a grievous blow to the whole family."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"grimace","p":"verb","d":"To twist your face into an ugly expression to show pain, disgust or disapproval.","lb":"scowl, wince","s":["scowl","frown","wince","pull a face","glower","make a face"],"k":["communicate","contort","cringe","distort"],"a":["smile","beam","grin"],"ex":["Rafi grimaced when he tasted the bitter medicine.","She tried not to grimace as the nurse cleaned the deep cut on her knee.","The audience grimaced at the loud screech from the microphone."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"griminess","p":"noun","d":"The state of being covered with dirt, especially black dust or oil.","lb":"dirtiness, grubbiness","s":["dirtiness","grime","filth","soot","grubbiness"],"k":["dirt","grease","grunge","mire"],"a":["cleanliness","freshness"],"ex":["The griminess of the factory walls showed years of smoke and oil.","She scrubbed the pots until all the griminess was gone.","The griminess of the bus window made the city outside look grey."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"grind","p":"verb","d":"To crush something such as grain, coffee or spices into very small pieces or powder.","lb":"crush, pulverize","s":["crush","mill","pound","pulverize","powder","mash"],"k":["break up","chop","crumple","crunch"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandmother still grinds fresh spices on a stone slab for her curry.","The shop will grind the coffee beans while you wait.","He ground the dry chilies into a fine red powder."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"gruesome","p":"adjective","d":"Very unpleasant to see or hear about because it involves violence, injury or death.","lb":"horrible, grisly","s":["grisly","ghastly","horrific","grim","hideous","shocking"],"k":["alarming","appalling","bloody","dreadful"],"a":["pleasant","delightful","charming","lovely"],"ex":["The photographs of the road accident were too gruesome to show on television.","He described the gruesome injuries he saw as a volunteer after the factory fire.","The detective story begins with a gruesome discovery in an empty house."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"guile","p":"noun","d":"Clever, sly behavior used to trick or deceive people.","lb":"cunning, deceit","s":["cunning","deceit","trickery","duplicity","cleverness"],"k":["chicanery","craft","deception","machination"],"a":["honesty","candor","sincerity","openness"],"ex":["The fox in the story uses guile to steal the farmer's chickens.","She won the negotiation through guile rather than force, never showing her real plan.","The scammer used guile to convince old people that he worked for the bank."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"guileless","p":"adjective","d":"Honest and innocent, with no wish or ability to trick other people.","lb":"innocent, honest","s":["artless","naive","innocent","honest","open","candid"],"k":["childlike","credulous","direct","gullible"],"a":["deceitful","cunning","crafty","sly"],"ex":["The toddler gave our guest a guileless smile and handed her his toy car.","Her guileless answer made it clear she had nothing to hide about the missing money.","Nobody could suspect such a guileless young man of cheating in the exam."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"guise","p":"noun","d":"A false or different outward appearance that hides what someone or something really is.","lb":"disguise, false appearance","s":["appearance","semblance","disguise","pretence","facade","front"],"k":["cloak","color","garb","gloss"],"a":["reality","truth","actuality"],"ex":["The thief entered the house in the guise of a delivery man.","Under the guise of friendship, he was collecting information about her.","The scam arrived in the guise of an email from the bank."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"gullible","p":"adjective","d":"Too ready to believe what other people say, and therefore easy to trick.","lb":"naive, credulous","s":["credulous","naive","trusting","unsuspecting","easily fooled","innocent"],"k":["artless","dupable","easy mark","ingenuous"],"a":["skeptical","suspicious","wary","cynical"],"ex":["Only a gullible person would believe an email promising a million dollars for nothing.","Scammers often phone gullible old people and pretend to be bank officials.","I was gullible enough to believe my brother when he said the exam was cancelled."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"gypsy","p":"noun","d":"An old word, now often considered offensive, for a member of the Romani people; Romani is the preferred word.","lb":"outdated term","s":["gipsy","bohemian"],"k":["itinerant","nomad","rover","traveler"],"a":[],"ex":["Many Romani people dislike the word gypsy, so writers now prefer to say Romani.","The museum label said Romani rather than gypsy because the older word can be hurtful.","In older novels, the word gypsy is often used for travelling people, but it carries unfair stereotypes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"habituate","p":"verb","d":"To make someone or something used to a situation or activity by repeating it regularly.","lb":"accustom, train","s":["accustom","condition","adapt","inure","season","harden"],"k":["acclimatize","adjust","alter","break in"],"a":[],"ex":["Parents should habituate children to a regular bedtime from an early age.","After a few weeks in Dhaka, she was habituated to the noise of the traffic.","Regular practice habituates the body to long-distance running."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"hackneyed","p":"adjective","d":"Used so often that it has become boring and has lost its freshness.","lb":"overused, trite","s":["overused","trite","stale","cliched","banal","stereotyped"],"k":["corny","hoary","predictable","rehashed"],"a":["original","fresh","novel","innovative"],"ex":["The hackneyed plot of the film, with a poor boy winning a rich girl, bored the audience.","Starting every speech by saying that time flies sounds hackneyed to modern audiences.","Her essay was full of hackneyed phrases, so the examiner gave it low marks for originality."],"b":594,"y":1},{"w":"haggard","p":"adjective","d":"Looking very tired, thin and worried, usually because of illness, stress or lack of sleep.","lb":"exhausted, drawn","s":["drawn","gaunt","worn","tired","exhausted","wan"],"k":["drained","emaciated","fatigued","lean"],"a":["fresh","healthy","rested","radiant"],"ex":["After a week of night shifts, the nurse looked haggard and pale.","The haggard father sat beside his sick daughter's bed through the night.","Exam week left the whole class looking haggard, with dark circles under their eyes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"halcyon","p":"adjective","d":"Calm, peaceful and happy, often describing a pleasant time in the past.","lb":"peaceful, idyllic","s":["peaceful","calm","tranquil","serene","idyllic","carefree"],"k":["composed","peaceable","prosperous","quiet"],"a":["turbulent","stormy","troubled","chaotic"],"ex":["My grandfather often talks about the halcyon days of his childhood by the river.","We spent a halcyon week at the seaside, with no phones, no deadlines and no worries.","After the noise of the city, the halcyon calm of the village felt almost unreal."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"hammer","p":"noun","d":"A tool with a heavy metal head on a handle, used for hitting nails or breaking things.","lb":"hand tool","s":["mallet","sledgehammer","gavel"],"k":["beetle","bludgeon","cock","cudgel"],"a":[],"ex":["He used a hammer to drive the nail into the wall.","The carpenter keeps a hammer, a saw and a tape measure in his bag.","Be careful with the hammer; it is easy to hit your own thumb."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"hanker","p":"verb","d":"To want something very much, especially something that you cannot easily have.","lb":"crave, long for","s":["yearn","long","crave","hunger","thirst","pine"],"k":["covet","dream of","fancy","itch"],"a":["loathe","shun","reject","dislike"],"ex":["After a week of hospital food, I hankered for my mother's rice and fish curry.","Living in a small town, she hankered after the lights and excitement of the capital.","He hankered for a new phone but could not afford one yet."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hapless","p":"adjective","d":"Unlucky, in a way that makes you feel sorry for the person.","lb":"unlucky, unfortunate","s":["unlucky","unfortunate","wretched","jinxed","pitiful","doomed"],"k":["beleaguered","cursed","deplorable","forlorn"],"a":["lucky","fortunate","blessed","charmed"],"ex":["The hapless tourist lost his wallet, then missed his flight, and finally lost his hotel booking.","A hapless goalkeeper dropped the ball, and the other team scored the winning goal.","The hapless clerk was blamed for the error, although the computer had caused it."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"harangue","p":"noun","d":"A long, loud and forceful speech that criticizes people or tells them what they should do.","lb":"tirade, lecture","s":["tirade","diatribe","lecture","rant","sermon","broadside"],"k":["address","discourse","homily","invective"],"a":[],"ex":["Our coach delivered a ten-minute harangue about punctuality before the match began.","I tried to explain, but she only gave me another harangue about my messy room.","The shopkeeper's harangue against late payments embarrassed every customer standing in the queue."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"harass","p":"verb","d":"To bother or trouble someone again and again in a way that is unpleasant and unwanted.","lb":"pester, torment","s":["pester","torment","hound","badger","bother","persecute"],"k":["annoy","beleaguer","beset","bug"],"a":["protect","assist","comfort","leave alone"],"ex":["Several students were harassed by older boys near the bus stop until the school stepped in.","Debt collectors may not harass customers with phone calls at midnight.","The caller kept harassing her with messages even after she asked him to stop."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"harbinger","p":"noun","d":"A person or thing that shows that something important or unwelcome is coming.","lb":"sign, forerunner","s":["herald","forerunner","omen","precursor","sign","signal"],"k":["early warning","foretaste","forewarning","indicator"],"a":[],"ex":["Cool morning fog over the paddy fields is a harbinger of winter in the countryside.","Dark clouds in the west were a harbinger of the storm that would flood our street.","Some economists see falling exports as a harbinger of a slow year ahead."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"harp","p":"verb","d":"To keep talking about the same subject in a tiresome and repetitive way.","lb":"nag, repeat","s":["dwell","go on","nag","keep on","rehash","drone on"],"k":["carry on","chant","continue","hammer on"],"a":[],"ex":["My mother keeps harping on about my messy room every single morning.","Please stop harping on my mistake; I have already apologised twice.","The manager harped on the same safety rules in every meeting, and we began to tune out."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"harry","p":"verb","d":"To bother or pressure someone again and again, causing them stress.","lb":"harass, pester","s":["harass","pester","hound","badger","plague","nag"],"k":["annoy","assail","beleaguer","beset"],"a":["leave alone","soothe","comfort","help"],"ex":["Reporters harried the winner with questions as she left the stadium.","The landlord harried the tenants for the rent two days before it was due.","Mosquitoes harried us all night, so nobody could sleep."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"hasty","p":"adjective","d":"Done or decided too quickly, without thinking carefully about it.","lb":"rash, hurried","s":["rash","hurried","rushed","impulsive","precipitate","reckless"],"k":["breakneck","headlong","heedless","perfunctory"],"a":["careful","cautious","deliberate","slow"],"ex":["Don't make a hasty decision about your career; take some time to think.","After a hasty breakfast, she ran to catch the bus.","Hasty conclusions about a news story can spread false information online."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hedonism","p":"noun","d":"The belief or way of life in which pursuing pleasure is the most important thing.","lb":"pleasure-seeking, self-indulgence","s":["indulgence","luxury","gratification","decadence"],"k":["carpe diem","dissipation","ethical motive","ethics"],"a":["abstinence","austerity"],"ex":["Ancient Greek thinkers debated hedonism, asking whether pleasure alone makes a good life.","His weekend hedonism of parties, long sleep and fast food left him tired and broke.","The movie criticizes the hedonism of rich young people who care only about fun."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"heedlessly","p":"adverb","d":"Without paying attention to danger, warnings or the effects of what you do.","lb":"carelessly, recklessly","s":["carelessly","recklessly","thoughtlessly","rashly","blindly","mindlessly"],"k":["headlong","incautiously","nonchalantly","obliviously"],"a":["carefully","cautiously","attentively"],"ex":["The boy ran heedlessly across the busy road to catch his ball.","She spent her salary heedlessly and had nothing left by the middle of the month.","Heedlessly, the driver ignored the warning signs about the flooded road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hegemony","p":"noun","d":"Control or leadership held by one country, group or organization over others.","lb":"dominance, leadership","s":["dominance","supremacy","control","leadership","domination","ascendancy"],"k":["clout","form of government","imperium","overlordship"],"a":["subordination","dependence"],"ex":["For decades, one company held hegemony over the local mobile phone market.","Historians study how an empire gained hegemony over the trade routes of the region.","The cultural hegemony of a few global film studios means children everywhere know their movies well."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"heinous","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely evil or shocking, used especially of crimes.","lb":"atrocious, wicked","s":["atrocious","monstrous","wicked","villainous","abominable","vile"],"k":["appalling","awful","egregious","execrable"],"a":["admirable","noble","virtuous","honorable"],"ex":["The newspaper called the attack on the elderly shopkeeper a heinous crime.","Cheating people out of their life savings is a heinous act.","The judge said the heinous crime deserved a long sentence."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"herald","p":"noun","d":"A person or thing that announces or signals that something important is about to happen.","lb":"harbinger, forerunner","s":["harbinger","forerunner","precursor","messenger","announcer","omen"],"k":["antecedent","bearer","bellwether","crier"],"a":[],"ex":["The first cool breeze in the evening is a herald of winter.","In the old days, a herald rode ahead of the king to announce his arrival.","Many people saw the factory's closing as a herald of harder times for the town."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"herb","p":"noun","d":"A plant whose leaves, stems or seeds are used to flavor food or to make medicine.","lb":"plant, seasoning","s":["seasoning","flavoring","flavouring"],"k":["basil","mint","oregano","rosemary"],"a":[],"ex":["My mother grows fresh herbs like mint and coriander on our balcony.","Basil is a popular herb in Italian cooking.","In many villages, people use local herbs to treat colds and coughs."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"heresy","p":"noun","d":"A belief or opinion that strongly disagrees with what is generally accepted, especially in religion, science or a group.","lb":"unorthodox belief","s":["dissent","apostasy","schism"],"k":["blasphemy","deviation","freethinking","impiety"],"a":["orthodoxy","conformity","conventionality","dogma"],"ex":["When the scientist first claimed that the Earth moves around the Sun, many people called it a heresy.","In the old football club, suggesting a new captain was almost a heresy.","To the strict chef, adding sugar to a classic curry was nothing short of heresy."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"heretical","p":"adjective","d":"Opposed to what most people in a group or field accept as true or correct.","lb":"unorthodox, dissenting","s":["unorthodox","dissenting","nonconformist","unconventional","radical","iconoclastic"],"k":["apostate","blasphemous","deviant","impious"],"a":["orthodox","conventional","mainstream","traditional"],"ex":["Putting pineapple on pizza is considered heretical by some food lovers.","At first, the doctor's heretical theory about stomach ulcers was laughed at.","The coach's heretical decision to play without a striker shocked the fans."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"heritage","p":"noun","d":"The traditions, buildings and culture that a society has had for many years and values highly.","lb":"tradition, legacy","s":["legacy","tradition","inheritance","birthright","background","culture"],"k":["ancestry","bequest","customs","endowment"],"a":[],"ex":["Our school teaches children to take pride in the country's rich cultural heritage.","Many families keep their heritage alive by cooking traditional dishes at home.","The city council plans to protect its old buildings as part of the national heritage."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hermetic","p":"adjective","d":"Completely sealed so that no air can get in or out.","lb":"airtight, sealed","s":["airtight","sealed","impermeable","watertight","impervious","closed"],"k":["gastight","impenetrable","resistant","shut tight"],"a":["open","porous","leaky","permeable"],"ex":["The jar has a hermetic lid, so the pickles stay fresh for months.","Astronauts' suits need a hermetic seal to keep air in and harmful gases out.","The medicine is stored in hermetic packets to protect it from damp air."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"heyday","p":"noun","d":"The time when someone or something was at its most successful, powerful or popular.","lb":"prime, golden age","s":["prime","peak","golden age","glory days","zenith","height"],"k":["acme","apex","apogee","bloom"],"a":["decline","downfall","twilight","nadir"],"ex":["In its heyday, the old cinema hall near our house sold out every show.","My grandfather still talks about his heyday as a kabaddi player in the village.","The factory town was busy in its heyday, but now many shops stand empty."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"hiatus","p":"noun","d":"A pause or gap in an activity or a series, during which nothing happens.","lb":"pause, break","s":["break","pause","gap","interval","lull","interruption"],"k":["abatement","breach","breather","foramen"],"a":["continuation","continuity","persistence"],"ex":["The band went on hiatus for two years while its members studied abroad.","After a long hiatus, the school reopened its library.","There was a brief hiatus in the conversation while the waiter served the tea."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"hierarchy","p":"noun","d":"A system that arranges people or things in levels, from the highest to the lowest.","lb":"ranking, pecking order","s":["ranking","pecking order","chain of command","grading","ladder","order"],"k":["caste system","echelon","organization","power structure"],"a":["equality"],"ex":["In a large hospital, the hierarchy runs from junior doctors to senior consultants.","My new office has a flat hierarchy, so everyone can talk to the director.","Wolves live in packs with a clear hierarchy among the males and females."],"b":146,"y":0},{"w":"histrionic","p":"adjective","d":"Too dramatic and emotional, as if acting in order to get attention.","lb":"theatrical, melodramatic","s":["theatrical","melodramatic","overdramatic","dramatic","affected","exaggerated"],"k":["camp","feigned","hammy","hysterical"],"a":["restrained","calm","understated","subdued"],"ex":["Her histrionic sobbing over a small scratch embarrassed her brother in front of his friends.","The manager’s histrionic outburst about a late report made everyone uncomfortable.","He gave a histrionic sigh and fell onto the sofa when asked to wash the dishes."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"hoary","p":"adjective","d":"Very old, often with grey or white hair; also old and overused, like a joke.","lb":"ancient, stale","s":["ancient","aged","venerable","grizzled","stale","antiquated"],"k":["antique","archaic","bygone","corny"],"a":["young","youthful","fresh","new"],"ex":["A hoary old fisherman sat on the riverbank, mending his net as he had done for fifty years.","The teacher told the same hoary joke at every farewell party, and everyone smiled politely.","The hoary banyan tree in the village square has shaded generations of children."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"homage","p":"noun","d":"Respect or honor shown publicly to someone or something you admire.","lb":"tribute, respect","s":["tribute","respect","honor","reverence","admiration","deference"],"k":["acclaim","accolade","appreciation","court"],"a":["disrespect","contempt","dishonor","insult"],"ex":["Every February 21, people walk barefoot to the Shaheed Minar to pay homage to the language martyrs.","The film is a homage to old black-and-white comedies, with the same slow jokes and silent scenes.","She cooked her grandmother's recipe as homage to the woman who taught her to love food."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"homeostasis","p":"noun","d":"The body's ability to keep its inner conditions, such as temperature, steady and balanced.","lb":"equilibrium, balance","s":["equilibrium","balance","stability","steady state","constancy"],"k":["equipoise","internal balance","poise","regulation"],"a":["imbalance","instability"],"ex":["Sweating is one way the body maintains homeostasis when the weather is hot.","The kidneys help maintain homeostasis by controlling the water and salt in the blood.","In biology class, we learned that homeostasis keeps body temperature near thirty-seven degrees."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"homily","p":"noun","d":"A talk, often given at a religious gathering, that offers moral advice; also, any long lecture on right behavior.","lb":"sermon, moral talk","s":["sermon","lecture","address","preaching","talk","lesson"],"k":["admonition","harangue","lecturing","moralizing"],"a":[],"ex":["At the end of the ceremony, the village elder gave a short homily about kindness to neighbors.","My father turned a small mistake into a long homily about responsibility.","The film stops for a homily on honesty, and the audience grows restless."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"homogeneous","p":"adjective","d":"Made up of parts or people that are all of the same kind.","lb":"uniform, similar","s":["uniform","alike","similar","identical","consistent","comparable"],"k":["analogous","monolithic","monotone","parallel"],"a":["heterogeneous","diverse","varied","mixed"],"ex":["Stir the paint until the mixture looks smooth and homogeneous.","The village was fairly homogeneous, with most families sharing the same language and customs.","A homogeneous team may lack the fresh ideas that people from different backgrounds bring."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"hone","p":"verb","d":"To improve and perfect a skill or ability, usually through long practice.","lb":"sharpen, refine","s":["sharpen","polish","refine","improve","perfect","develop"],"k":["ameliorate","amend","buff","file"],"a":["dull","blunt","weaken","neglect"],"ex":["She honed her speaking skills by practicing with friends every evening.","Years of cooking in the family restaurant helped him hone his sense of taste.","The coach drilled the players to hone their passing."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"horde","p":"noun","d":"A very large, noisy crowd of people or animals, often one that causes trouble.","lb":"crowd, mob","s":["crowd","mob","throng","swarm","multitude","mass"],"k":["crush","flock","gathering","herd"],"a":["handful","few","scattering"],"ex":["Hordes of tourists arrive at Cox's Bazar every winter weekend.","A horde of ants had found the sweets I left on the kitchen table.","A horde of reporters waited outside the court for any news."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"horrendous","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely bad, shocking or frightening.","lb":"terrible, awful","s":["dreadful","terrible","awful","appalling","horrific","atrocious"],"k":["abominable","alarming","dire","dreaded"],"a":["wonderful","pleasant","delightful","marvelous"],"ex":["We spent three hours stuck in horrendous traffic on the way to the airport.","The weather during our trip was horrendous, with storms every single afternoon.","The newspaper described the factory fire as a horrendous tragedy."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"horrid","p":"adjective","d":"Very unpleasant, unkind or bad.","lb":"awful, nasty","s":["awful","dreadful","nasty","horrible","terrible","vile"],"k":["abominable","alarming","appalling","atrocious"],"a":["lovely","pleasant","nice","delightful"],"ex":["The medicine tasted so horrid that the child refused to swallow it.","We had a horrid journey home, with a cancelled bus and heavy rain.","She wrote a horrid comment about my drawing, and I felt hurt."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"horrific","p":"adjective","d":"Very shocking and frightening; causing great horror.","lb":"terrifying, shocking","s":["horrifying","terrifying","appalling","shocking","gruesome","dreadful"],"k":["abysmal","alarming","atrocious","awful"],"a":["pleasant","delightful","comforting","charming"],"ex":["The news showed pictures of a horrific accident on the highway.","She still has nightmares about the horrific storm that destroyed her village.","The film was so horrific that half the audience left early."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hostility","p":"noun","d":"Strong unfriendly or angry feelings toward someone, often shown in behavior.","lb":"unfriendliness, enmity","s":["enmity","animosity","antagonism","aggression","ill will","hatred"],"k":["antipathy","bad blood","bellicosity","belligerence"],"a":["friendliness","goodwill","kindness","warmth"],"ex":["The new student was met with hostility by some of his classmates.","There was open hostility between the two neighbors over the shared wall.","Her hostility toward the plan was clear from the way she folded her arms."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hubris","p":"noun","d":"Dangerous and excessive pride or self-confidence that often leads to a person's downfall.","lb":"arrogance, overconfidence","s":["arrogance","pride","conceit","overconfidence","vanity","presumption"],"k":["cockiness","egotism","megalomania","narcissism"],"a":["humility","modesty","meekness"],"ex":["His hubris led him to ignore the doctor's warnings.","The company's hubris, believing it could never fail, eventually ruined it.","The team's hubris was clear when they skipped practice before the final."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"hurdle","p":"noun","d":"A problem or difficulty that you must deal with before you can succeed.","lb":"obstacle, barrier","s":["obstacle","barrier","obstruction","snag","setback","challenge"],"k":["bottleneck","catch","drawback","hitch"],"a":["help","aid","advantage","boost"],"ex":["Passing the entrance exam was the first hurdle on her path to medical school.","Language is the biggest hurdle for students studying abroad.","Getting a loan was the main hurdle for the young entrepreneur."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"hurriedly","p":"adverb","d":"In a quick, rushed way because there is not much time.","lb":"quickly, hastily","s":["hastily","quickly","rapidly","speedily","swiftly","in haste"],"k":["at once","breathlessly","briskly","frantically"],"a":["slowly","leisurely","carefully"],"ex":["She hurriedly packed her bag when she saw how late it was.","He ate his breakfast hurriedly and ran to catch the bus.","The students hurriedly wrote down the last few answers before the bell."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"husbandry","p":"noun","d":"The care and management of farm crops and animals, or of resources in general.","lb":"farming, management","s":["farming","agriculture","cultivation","thrift","management","conservation"],"k":["horticulture","ranching","stewardship","tending"],"a":[],"ex":["Animal husbandry is an important source of income for many rural families.","Students at the agricultural college study crop husbandry and soil science.","Good husbandry of the water supply helped the village survive the dry season."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"hyperbole","p":"noun","d":"A way of speaking in which things are made to sound much bigger or worse than they really are.","lb":"exaggeration, overstatement","s":["exaggeration","overstatement","amplification","magnification","inflation","extravagance"],"k":["bombast","figure","figure of speech","fustian"],"a":["understatement","underplaying"],"ex":["When he said he waited a thousand years for the bus, that was just hyperbole.","Calling the flood a disaster is not hyperbole, because whole villages are under water.","Advertisements are full of hyperbole, such as claiming a cream makes you look ten years younger."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"hypocrisy","p":"noun","d":"Pretending to have beliefs or standards that you do not really follow in your own behavior.","lb":"insincerity, two-facedness","s":["duplicity","pretense","double standards","deceit","phoniness","cant"],"k":["bad faith","deception","double-dealing","feigning"],"a":["sincerity","honesty","integrity","candor"],"ex":["It is hypocrisy to tell children not to lie and then lie to the neighbors.","The hypocrisy of a manager who demands punctuality but arrives late every day annoyed the staff.","My sister accused me of hypocrisy for criticizing her phone use while I scrolled all day."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"hypothetical","p":"adjective","d":"Based on an imagined situation or idea rather than on known facts or real events.","lb":"imaginary, theoretical","s":["theoretical","imaginary","supposed","speculative","assumed","putative"],"k":["conditional","fictitious","fictive","make-believe"],"a":["actual","real","factual","proven"],"ex":["The teacher gave us a hypothetical situation: what would you do if you found a wallet?","These numbers are only hypothetical, so please don’t treat them as real sales figures.","I can’t answer hypothetical questions about what I would do if I won the lottery."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"iconoclast","p":"noun","d":"A person who attacks or rejects widely accepted beliefs, customs or institutions.","lb":"rebel, nonconformist","s":["nonconformist","rebel","maverick","radical","heretic","dissident"],"k":["contrarian","destroyer","gadfly","image breaker"],"a":["conformist","traditionalist","conservative","follower"],"ex":["The young chef is an iconoclast who serves dessert first and mixes foods nobody expects.","As an iconoclast in the art world, she painted portraits using only rubbish and old newspapers.","My uncle, an iconoclast in our traditional family, left his law job to become a farmer."],"b":532,"y":0},{"w":"iconoclastic","p":"adjective","d":"Attacking or rejecting traditional beliefs, customs and respected institutions.","lb":"rebellious, unconventional","s":["unconventional","rebellious","nonconformist","radical","dissenting","irreverent"],"k":["anti-establishment","contrarian","destructive","disruptive"],"a":["conventional","traditional","orthodox","conformist"],"ex":["The iconoclastic young chef ignored every traditional recipe and invented dishes of his own.","Her iconoclastic essay challenged the idea that exams are the best way to measure talent.","The magazine is known for its iconoclastic views on fashion, school and family life."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"ideology","p":"noun","d":"A system of ideas and beliefs that shapes how a person or group thinks about society, politics or the economy.","lb":"belief system","s":["belief system","doctrine","philosophy","creed","principles","dogma"],"k":["belief","credo","ethics","isms"],"a":[],"ex":["The professor compared different political ideologies and explained how each one views the role of government.","Some companies run on a clear ideology, such as putting customers first in every decision.","He joined the group because he shared its ideology of protecting the environment."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"idiosyncrasy","p":"noun","d":"A strange or personal habit or way of behaving that is typical of one particular person or thing.","lb":"quirk, peculiarity","s":["quirk","peculiarity","eccentricity","oddity","foible","trait"],"k":["kink","oddness","speciality","specialness"],"a":["norm","convention","normality","standard"],"ex":["One of my father's idiosyncrasies is that he never eats before he reads the newspaper.","Every old computer has its own idiosyncrasies, such as turning on only after two tries.","Her idiosyncrasy of writing in green ink made her notes easy to spot."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"idolatry","p":"noun","d":"Excessive, uncritical admiration for a person or thing, as if it deserved to be worshipped.","lb":"worship, adoration","s":["worship","adoration","devotion","reverence","idol worship"],"k":["fanaticism","fandom","fetishism","infatuation"],"a":["contempt","disdain","disrespect","scorn"],"ex":["Some teenagers' idolatry of film stars makes them copy every detail of their lives.","The idolatry of money can make people forget their family and friends.","The fans' idolatry of the team captain turned into anger when he played badly."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"idyllic","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely peaceful, simple and beautiful, like a perfect picture of country life.","lb":"peaceful, picturesque","s":["peaceful","picturesque","charming","tranquil","serene","pastoral"],"k":["calm","perfect","placid","pleasant"],"a":["grim","dreary","harsh","unpleasant"],"ex":["We spent the weekend in an idyllic village with green fields, a quiet pond and no traffic.","The travel poster showed an idyllic beach with white sand and calm blue water.","Her childhood in a small riverside town was idyllic, full of boat rides and mango trees."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"ignominy","p":"noun","d":"Public shame and loss of respect caused by something dishonorable.","lb":"disgrace, shame","s":["disgrace","shame","dishonor","humiliation","infamy","disrepute"],"k":["abasement","discredit","embarrassment","ill repute"],"a":["honor","glory","respect","pride"],"ex":["The team suffered the ignominy of losing by seven goals to nothing against a much smaller school.","He left the company in ignominy after the audit found that he had faked his expense reports.","The official resigned in ignominy after photos of his luxury trips appeared online."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"illicit","p":"adjective","d":"Not allowed by law or by the rules of society; illegal or forbidden.","lb":"illegal, forbidden","s":["illegal","unlawful","forbidden","prohibited","banned","criminal"],"k":["adulterous","bootleg","dirty","extramarital"],"a":["legal","lawful","legitimate","permitted"],"ex":["Customs officers seized a large shipment of illicit goods hidden inside the truck.","The police shut down an illicit factory that was making fake medicines.","Selling exam questions before the test is an illicit practice that can end a teacher's career."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"illusive","p":"adjective","d":"Not real but seeming real, and likely to deceive you.","lb":"deceptive, unreal","s":["deceptive","misleading","false","unreal","delusive","imaginary"],"k":["chimerical","fallacious","fictitious","insubstantial"],"a":["real","genuine","actual","true"],"ex":["The scheme's promise of easy money proved illusive.","Thirst made the lake in the distance seem real, but it was an illusive image.","Winning the lottery is an illusive dream that keeps many people buying tickets."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"imbue","p":"verb","d":"To fill someone or something completely with a feeling, quality or idea.","lb":"fill, infuse","s":["infuse","instill","permeate","fill","inspire","saturate"],"k":["animate","charge","color","endow"],"a":["drain","strip","deprive"],"ex":["Her grandmother imbued the children with a deep love of books by reading aloud every night.","The coach imbued the young team with confidence before the final match.","The old teacher's lessons were imbued with kindness, and students remembered them for years."],"b":100,"y":1},{"w":"imitate","p":"verb","d":"To copy the way someone speaks, looks or behaves.","lb":"copy, mimic","s":["copy","mimic","mirror","echo","ape","emulate"],"k":["caricature","follow","parody","replicate"],"a":["originate","create","invent","innovate"],"ex":["My little brother likes to imitate our father's deep voice.","Children learn language by listening to adults and imitating the sounds they hear.","The comedian can imitate any teacher's voice perfectly, and the students love it."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"imitation","p":"noun","d":"A copy of something, or the act of copying how someone speaks or behaves.","lb":"copy, fake","s":["copy","replica","reproduction","duplicate","mimicry","fake"],"k":["caricature","clone","forgery","mock-up"],"a":["original","prototype","real thing"],"ex":["Children learn to talk mainly by imitation of the adults around them.","The bag looked expensive, but it was only a cheap imitation.","Her imitation of the teacher's voice made the whole class laugh."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"immaculate","p":"adjective","d":"Perfectly clean, neat and tidy, with no mistakes or marks.","lb":"spotless, flawless","s":["spotless","pristine","impeccable","flawless","neat","clean"],"k":["exquisite","perfect","polished","pure"],"a":["dirty","messy","filthy","stained"],"ex":["The hotel room was immaculate, with fresh sheets and shining floors.","He arrived at the interview in an immaculate white shirt and polished shoes.","My mother keeps the kitchen immaculate, even on busy days."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"immigrate","p":"verb","d":"To come to live permanently in a country that is not your own.","lb":"settle abroad, move in","s":["migrate","settle","relocate","move","take up residence"],"k":["arrive","make a new home","naturalize","put down roots"],"a":["emigrate","repatriate","return home"],"ex":["My cousin hopes to immigrate to Canada next year to work as a software engineer.","Her grandparents immigrated from India in the 1970s and opened a small tailoring shop.","Many skilled workers immigrate to countries with better pay, even though they miss their families."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"imminent","p":"adjective","d":"About to happen very soon, especially something unpleasant or important.","lb":"impending, approaching","s":["impending","approaching","looming","coming","near","forthcoming"],"k":["close at hand","in the offing","menacing","nigh"],"a":["distant","remote","unlikely","improbable"],"ex":["Dark clouds and strong winds warned us that a storm was imminent.","The company's closure is imminent, so the employees are looking for new jobs.","With exams imminent, the library was packed with anxious students."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"immutable","p":"adjective","d":"Never changing, or not able to be changed.","lb":"unchangeable, fixed","s":["unchangeable","fixed","permanent","unalterable","constant","unchanging"],"k":["changeless","entrenched","indelible","inviolable"],"a":["changeable","mutable","variable","flexible"],"ex":["The laws of physics are immutable, so a stone always falls when you drop it.","Many students believe their ability is immutable, but steady practice can change it.","The company's rule that every refund needs a receipt seems immutable."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"impair","p":"verb","d":"To damage something or make it weaker, so that it works less well.","lb":"damage, weaken","s":["damage","weaken","harm","diminish","undermine","hinder"],"k":["deflower","mar","ruin","vitiate"],"a":["improve","enhance","strengthen","repair"],"ex":["Lack of sleep can impair your memory and make studying much harder.","Listening to loud music through headphones for years may impair your hearing.","Thick smoke impaired visibility on the highway, so drivers slowed down."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"impartial","p":"adjective","d":"Fair, and not favoring one side or person more than another.","lb":"fair, unbiased","s":["fair","unbiased","neutral","objective","unprejudiced","disinterested"],"k":["balanced","dispassionate","indifferent","judicious"],"a":["biased","partial","prejudiced","partisan"],"ex":["A good referee must be impartial, even when his own city's team is playing.","The teacher gave impartial marks to every student, regardless of who they were.","We asked an impartial neighbor to settle the argument over the boundary wall."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"impasse","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which no progress is possible because the sides cannot agree.","lb":"deadlock, stalemate","s":["deadlock","stalemate","standoff","dead end","gridlock","standstill"],"k":["bind","cul-de-sac","dilemma","fix"],"a":["breakthrough","agreement","progress","compromise"],"ex":["The talks between the union and the factory owners reached an impasse over wages.","My sister and I hit an impasse when we both wanted the same room after our cousin moved out.","The group project was stuck at an impasse until Nadia suggested splitting the tasks by strength."],"b":100,"y":4},{"w":"impassive","p":"adjective","d":"Showing no emotion or reaction, especially when other people expect you to.","lb":"expressionless, unmoved","s":["expressionless","stoic","unemotional","deadpan","stolid","emotionless"],"k":["aloof","composed","detached","inscrutable"],"a":["emotional","expressive","animated","excitable"],"ex":["The judge stayed impassive as the nervous witness told his long story.","My father listened to the bad news with an impassive face and said nothing.","Her impassive expression made it impossible to guess whether she liked the gift."],"b":69,"y":1},{"w":"impatient","p":"adjective","d":"Annoyed by delay or lack of progress, or too eager for something to happen.","lb":"restless, eager","s":["restless","irritable","eager","edgy","hasty","fidgety"],"k":["fractious","raring","restive","tense"],"a":["patient","calm","tolerant","easygoing"],"ex":["Impatient drivers honked their horns as the signal stayed red.","She was impatient to open her exam results.","Don't be impatient with your little brother; he is still learning."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"impeach","p":"verb","d":"To formally accuse a public official of serious wrongdoing, or to challenge someone's honesty.","lb":"accuse, charge","s":["accuse","charge","indict","arraign","challenge","question"],"k":["allege","blame","censure","cite"],"a":["acquit","exonerate","vindicate","clear"],"ex":["Lawmakers voted to impeach the governor after an investigation found he had misused public money.","The lawyer tried to impeach the witness by showing that he had lied in an earlier statement.","In civics class, we discussed how a country can impeach a president who breaks the constitution."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"impeccable","p":"adjective","d":"Perfect and without any fault or mistake.","lb":"flawless, perfect","s":["flawless","perfect","spotless","immaculate","exquisite","unblemished"],"k":["clean","dapper","ideal","meticulous"],"a":["flawed","faulty","imperfect","defective"],"ex":["The waiter's impeccable manners impressed every guest at the wedding dinner.","She spoke impeccable English and was offered the job right after the interview.","His impeccable record at work earned him a promotion after only two years."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"impecunious","p":"adjective","d":"Having very little or no money to live on.","lb":"poor, penniless","s":["penniless","poor","broke","destitute","needy","hard up"],"k":["down and out","impoverished","in reduced circumstances","on the breadline"],"a":["wealthy","rich","affluent","prosperous"],"ex":["As an impecunious student, he walked to the campus every day to save the bus fare.","The impecunious young artist sold sketches at the roadside to pay for rice and tea.","Her impecunious uncle borrowed small sums from relatives until he found a steady job."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"impede","p":"verb","d":"To make it harder for someone or something to move forward or make progress.","lb":"hinder, obstruct","s":["hinder","obstruct","hamper","block","delay","slow"],"k":["blockade","close up","occlude","prevent"],"a":["help","aid","assist","facilitate"],"ex":["Heavy rain and broken roads impeded the rescue team's progress toward the village.","Parked rickshaws on the narrow lane impede traffic every evening in our neighborhood.","Shyness may impede a student from asking questions in class."],"b":107,"y":1},{"w":"impediment","p":"noun","d":"Something that makes it difficult or impossible for someone to move, do or achieve something.","lb":"obstacle, hindrance","s":["obstacle","barrier","hindrance","obstruction","hurdle","handicap"],"k":["constraint","difficulty","drag","encumbrance"],"a":["aid","help","assistance","advantage"],"ex":["Lack of money is the biggest impediment to higher education for many students.","Fallen trees on the road were an impediment to the rescue team.","A speech impediment never stopped him from becoming an excellent teacher."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"impending","p":"adjective","d":"About to happen soon, especially something important or unpleasant.","lb":"approaching, imminent","s":["imminent","approaching","looming","coming","forthcoming","upcoming"],"k":["anticipated","at hand","close at hand","expected"],"a":["past","distant","remote","unlikely"],"ex":["Dark clouds warned the fishermen of the impending storm.","Her impending exams made her too anxious to sleep.","The manager warned staff about the impending changes to office hours."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"impenetrable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to get through, see through or understand.","lb":"impassable, incomprehensible","s":["impassable","solid","dense","thick","inaccessible","impermeable"],"k":["airtight","compact","cryptic","fortified"],"a":["passable","clear","accessible","transparent"],"ex":["The thick fog on the highway was impenetrable, and we could barely see the road ahead.","The bank's vault is made of thick steel and is impenetrable to thieves.","Parts of the Sundarbans are so thick with mangrove roots that they are nearly impenetrable."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"imperative","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely important and needing to be done immediately.","lb":"essential, urgent","s":["essential","vital","crucial","urgent","critical","pressing"],"k":["assertive","crying","decisive","desperate"],"a":["optional","unnecessary","trivial","voluntary"],"ex":["It is imperative that you submit the form before Friday's deadline.","Doctors said it was imperative to start treatment immediately.","For a long bus trip, it is imperative to carry drinking water."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"imperial","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to an empire, or to an emperor or empress.","lb":"of an empire","s":["royal","regal","sovereign","majestic","kingly","ruling"],"k":["colonial","domineering","dynastic","expansionist"],"a":[],"ex":["The imperial palace in the old city is now a museum open to visitors.","Historians study how imperial powers once controlled trade across large parts of Asia.","The emperor lived in an imperial garden filled with fountains and rare trees."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"impermeable","p":"adjective","d":"Not allowing liquids or gases to pass through.","lb":"waterproof, sealed","s":["impervious","waterproof","watertight","airtight","impenetrable","sealed"],"k":["airproof","closed","dense","immune"],"a":["permeable","porous","absorbent","leaky"],"ex":["Raincoats are made from impermeable fabric so that water cannot soak through.","Clay soil is almost impermeable, so after monsoon rain the water stays in the fields for days.","The pharmacist stored the tablets in an impermeable bag to keep out moisture."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"impertinent","p":"adjective","d":"Rude and disrespectful, especially to someone older or more important.","lb":"rude, cheeky","s":["rude","cheeky","insolent","impudent","disrespectful","saucy"],"k":["audacious","bold","brash","extraneous"],"a":["respectful","polite","courteous","deferential"],"ex":["The teacher was shocked by the student's impertinent reply in front of the class.","It would be impertinent to ask my host how much the house cost.","The impertinent child stuck out his tongue at the old man."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"imperturbable","p":"adjective","d":"Staying calm and not easily upset, even in difficult or stressful situations.","lb":"calm, composed","s":["calm","composed","unflappable","serene","cool","placid"],"k":["equable","even-tempered","level-headed","nerveless"],"a":["excitable","anxious","flustered","agitated"],"ex":["The imperturbable pilot kept smiling and spoke calmly while the plane shook in the storm.","Our teacher stayed imperturbable even when the whole class started shouting at once.","She is imperturbable at work, so tight deadlines never seem to bother her."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"impervious","p":"adjective","d":"Not affected or influenced by something, such as criticism, danger, weather or advice.","lb":"unaffected, resistant","s":["unaffected","immune","resistant","untouched","insensitive","indifferent"],"k":["fast","hardened","impermeable","insensible"],"a":["susceptible","vulnerable","sensitive","responsive"],"ex":["He seems impervious to criticism and keeps working no matter what people say.","The old tent was impervious to rain, so we stayed dry all night.","Rafi was impervious to his mother's advice and kept playing video games until midnight."],"b":93,"y":1},{"w":"impetuous","p":"adjective","d":"Acting quickly and without thinking carefully about the results.","lb":"impulsive, hasty","s":["impulsive","rash","hasty","reckless","spontaneous","headlong"],"k":["careless","forceful","hurried","madcap"],"a":["cautious","careful","deliberate","prudent"],"ex":["In an impetuous moment, he quit his job without having another one lined up.","My impetuous younger brother jumped into the river without checking how deep it was.","She regretted her impetuous reply and sent a polite apology the next morning."],"b":116,"y":1},{"w":"implacable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to calm down or satisfy, and refusing to stop being angry or opposed.","lb":"relentless, unforgiving","s":["relentless","unforgiving","merciless","ruthless","inflexible","unyielding"],"k":["adamant","dogged","grim","hard-line"],"a":["forgiving","merciful","lenient","flexible"],"ex":["The two neighbors became implacable enemies after arguing for years over a boundary wall.","She faced implacable opposition from the committee, who refused to listen to any compromise.","The manager was implacable and refused to reconsider, even after the staff begged for more time."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"implausible","p":"adjective","d":"Not seeming reasonable or likely to be true.","lb":"unlikely, unbelievable","s":["unlikely","improbable","unbelievable","doubtful","dubious","unconvincing"],"k":["astounding","cockamamie","farfetched","incredible"],"a":["plausible","believable","likely","credible"],"ex":["His excuse that a monkey stole his homework sounded implausible.","Many viewers found the film's ending implausible and unrealistic.","It seems implausible that the bus could arrive on time during the rush hour."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"implement","p":"verb","d":"To put a plan, decision or system into action.","lb":"carry out, execute","s":["carry out","execute","apply","enforce","enact","perform"],"k":["carry through","conduct","do","finish"],"a":["abandon","neglect","shelve","ignore"],"ex":["The school will implement the new timetable from the first week of January.","It took the company six months to implement the new payment system.","Our team implemented the manager's suggestion and cut waiting time in half."],"b":152,"y":0},{"w":"implication","p":"noun","d":"A suggestion or meaning that is not stated directly but can be understood from what is said.","lb":"suggestion, inference","s":["suggestion","inference","hint","insinuation","innuendo","meaning"],"k":["bearing","conditional relation","consequence","deduction"],"a":["statement","declaration","assertion"],"ex":["The implication of her question was that I had forgotten her birthday.","Do you mean, by implication, that the food at our house is not good?","I resent the implication that students from small towns cannot do well in the admission test."],"b":290,"y":0},{"w":"implicit","p":"adjective","d":"Suggested or understood without being stated directly.","lb":"implied, unspoken","s":["implied","tacit","unspoken","understood","indirect","unstated"],"k":["absolute","assumed","built-in","covert"],"a":["explicit","stated","direct","express"],"ex":["Her silence was an implicit agreement that she would help us move house.","The manager's comment contained an implicit criticism of the way we had planned the project.","There is an implicit rule in our house that nobody uses the phone during dinner."],"b":139,"y":0},{"w":"implode","p":"verb","d":"To collapse suddenly inward, because of outside pressure or inner weakness.","lb":"collapse, cave in","s":["collapse","cave in","fall in","crumble","disintegrate","buckle"],"k":["break","break down","crash","crumple"],"a":["explode","expand","burst","blow up"],"ex":["The old television screen imploded with a loud pop when it fell off the shelf.","Demolition experts made the empty factory implode so that it fell neatly into its own space.","Deep-sea submarines are built strong so that they will not implode under the huge water pressure."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"implore","p":"verb","d":"To ask someone in an emotional, urgent way to do something; to beg.","lb":"beg, beseech","s":["beg","beseech","entreat","plead with","appeal to","petition"],"k":["adjure","beg off","call on","crave"],"a":["command","demand","order"],"ex":["The mother implored the doctor to save her sick child.","I implore you to reconsider before you quit your studies.","Passengers implored the driver to stop the bus because a child felt ill."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"imply","p":"verb","d":"To suggest something without saying it directly.","lb":"suggest, hint","s":["suggest","hint","insinuate","indicate","signal","intimate"],"k":["betoken","connote","denote","entail"],"a":["state","declare","say outright","express"],"ex":["When my boss called the report \"interesting,\" I knew he was implying that it was weak.","Are you implying that I forgot your birthday on purpose?","The long silence on the phone seemed to imply that she was upset."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"importune","p":"verb","d":"To ask for something again and again in an annoying or persistent way.","lb":"pester, implore","s":["beg","plead with","pester","badger","nag","press"],"k":["beleaguer","beseech","bother","bug"],"a":[],"ex":["Street vendors importune tourists to buy souvenirs outside the museum.","The little boy importuned his father for a new bicycle all week.","Salesmen importuned residents at their doors until the guards sent them away."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"impose","p":"verb","d":"To force a rule, tax, opinion or decision on people, whether they want it or not.","lb":"force, enforce","s":["force","enforce","inflict","levy","apply","enact"],"k":["administer","bring down","coerce","compel"],"a":["withdraw","lift","remove","revoke"],"ex":["The government decided to impose a new tax on sugary drinks.","Parents should not impose their own career choices on their children.","The school imposed a strict rule against using phones during class."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"imposing","p":"adjective","d":"Large, impressive and powerful in appearance, making people admire or respect it.","lb":"impressive, grand","s":["impressive","grand","majestic","stately","commanding","striking"],"k":["august","awe-inspiring","baronial","dignified"],"a":["unimpressive","modest","humble","plain"],"ex":["The imposing gates of the old university made me feel nervous on my first day.","He is an imposing man, tall and broad, with a deep voice.","An imposing stone bridge crosses the river at the edge of the town."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"impotent","p":"adjective","d":"Powerless and unable to take effective action or change a situation.","lb":"powerless, helpless","s":["powerless","helpless","ineffective","weak","feeble","incapable"],"k":["effete","futile","incapacitated","infertile"],"a":["powerful","strong","effective","potent"],"ex":["He felt impotent watching the floodwater rise while rescue boats were still far away.","The teacher felt impotent when students ignored every rule she announced.","The weak law proved impotent against companies that dumped waste in the river."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"impoverish","p":"verb","d":"To make a person, family or place very poor.","lb":"make poor, ruin","s":["bankrupt","ruin","beggar","break","cripple","deplete"],"k":["deprive","dispossess","drain","leave destitute"],"a":["enrich","make rich","benefit"],"ex":["Years of drought have impoverished thousands of farming families in the region.","A long illness can impoverish a family that has no health insurance.","The sudden closure of the factory impoverished the whole town."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"impracticable","p":"adjective","d":"Not able to be done or used successfully in real conditions.","lb":"unworkable, not feasible","s":["unworkable","impossible","unrealistic","unattainable","out of the question"],"k":["fanciful","far-fetched","hare-brained","idealistic"],"a":["feasible","workable","viable","realistic"],"ex":["Walking to the airport with three heavy suitcases was clearly impracticable.","Because of the flood, it was impracticable to hold the exam in the village school.","The architect's design looked beautiful but proved impracticable on such a narrow plot."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"impregnable","p":"adjective","d":"Too strong to be broken into, defeated or captured.","lb":"unconquerable, impenetrable","s":["invincible","unassailable","impenetrable","indestructible","secure","invulnerable"],"k":["bulletproof","fertile","guarded","insuperable"],"a":["vulnerable","weak","defenseless","exposed"],"ex":["The old fort on the hill seemed impregnable, with thick walls and a deep moat.","The bank claims its vault is impregnable, but it still keeps guards there at night.","Their defense was impregnable, and the visiting team could not score all afternoon."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"impresario","p":"noun","d":"A person who organizes and finances concerts, plays or other public entertainments.","lb":"promoter, producer","s":["promoter","producer","manager","organizer","showman","sponsor"],"k":["agent","booker","booking agent","empresario"],"a":[],"ex":["The impresario booked the biggest hall in the city for the music festival.","A local impresario helped the young band find places to perform.","As an impresario, she spent her days calling singers, designers and ticket sellers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"impromptu","p":"adjective","d":"Done or said on the spur of the moment, without planning or preparation.","lb":"spontaneous, unplanned","s":["unrehearsed","spontaneous","improvised","unplanned","ad-lib","unprepared"],"k":["casual","extemporaneous","impulsive","instant"],"a":["planned","prepared","rehearsed","scripted"],"ex":["When the guest speaker was late, the principal gave an impromptu speech.","We held an impromptu picnic on the roof when the power went out.","Her impromptu visit surprised everyone, since she had told nobody she was coming."],"b":104,"y":2},{"w":"improvident","p":"adjective","d":"Careless about saving money or planning for the future.","lb":"wasteful, thriftless","s":["wasteful","careless","prodigal","extravagant","spendthrift","reckless"],"k":["carefree","feckless","hand-to-mouth","happy-go-lucky"],"a":["thrifty","prudent","frugal","careful"],"ex":["He was improvident in his youth and spent every salary within a week.","Improvident farmers who sold all their rice after the harvest had nothing left for the lean months.","Her improvident habits left her with no savings when the shop closed."],"b":72,"y":1},{"w":"improvise","p":"verb","d":"To make, say or do something without preparation, using whatever you have available.","lb":"ad-lib, make do","s":["ad-lib","make do","wing it","devise","invent","throw together"],"k":["busk","cobble together","do","execute"],"a":["plan","prepare","rehearse","script"],"ex":["When the load-shedding began, we improvised a reading lamp using a candle and a steel glass.","The speaker forgot his notes and had to improvise.","Jazz musicians often improvise, inventing melodies as they play."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"impudent","p":"adjective","d":"Rude and disrespectful, especially towards someone older or more important.","lb":"rude, cheeky","s":["cheeky","insolent","impertinent","disrespectful","rude","brazen"],"k":["audacious","brash","flip","insulting"],"a":["respectful","polite","courteous","humble"],"ex":["The impudent boy stuck out his tongue at the teacher and ran away.","It was impudent of the waiter to roll his eyes at the customer.","She gave an impudent reply that made her father furious."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"impugn","p":"verb","d":"To question or attack someone's honesty, motives or the truth of what they say.","lb":"challenge, question","s":["challenge","question","dispute","contest","attack","disparage"],"k":["besmirch","denigrate","gainsay","malign"],"a":["defend","support","uphold","vindicate"],"ex":["I do not mean to impugn your honesty, but the numbers in your report do not match.","The lawyer tried to impugn the witness's memory by pointing out contradictions in her story.","Nobody wants to impugn the referee's decision, but the replay clearly showed a different result."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"impulsive","p":"adjective","d":"Acting suddenly on a feeling, without thinking carefully about what might happen.","lb":"rash, spontaneous","s":["rash","spontaneous","hasty","reckless","impetuous","hotheaded"],"k":["arbitrary","capricious","careless","dynamic"],"a":["cautious","careful","deliberate","thoughtful"],"ex":["It was an impulsive purchase; I bought the shoes without checking the price.","Rafi is so impulsive that he booked the tickets before asking his parents.","An impulsive reply in anger can hurt a friendship."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"impunity","p":"noun","d":"Freedom from punishment, harm or other bad results of your actions.","lb":"immunity, exemption","s":["immunity","exemption","freedom from punishment","license","protection","amnesty"],"k":["carte blanche","clemency","dispensation","free pass"],"a":["punishment","liability","penalty","accountability"],"ex":["Drivers who ignore red lights with impunity put every pedestrian at risk.","Online bullies often act with impunity because nobody knows who they are.","Factories dumped waste in the river with impunity until the new inspection team arrived."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inadequate","p":"adjective","d":"Not enough in quantity, or not good enough in quality, for a particular purpose.","lb":"insufficient, lacking","s":["insufficient","lacking","deficient","poor","scant","meager"],"k":["depleted","incapable","incompetent","jejune"],"a":["adequate","sufficient","ample","enough"],"ex":["The village has inadequate medical facilities, so patients must travel to the city.","My salary is inadequate to cover rent, food and transport.","The lighting in the study room is inadequate, so many students strain their eyes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"inadvertent","p":"adjective","d":"Not done on purpose, but happening by accident because of not paying attention.","lb":"accidental, unintentional","s":["accidental","unintentional","unplanned","unwitting","chance","careless"],"k":["casual","innocent","random","uncalculated"],"a":["deliberate","intentional","purposeful","planned"],"ex":["His inadvertent mistake in the form delayed my visa application by two weeks.","An inadvertent click on the wrong button sent the email to the whole class.","I apologize for the inadvertent noise, because the door slipped from my hand."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"inadvertently","p":"adverb","d":"Without intending to, by accident or because of not paying attention.","lb":"accidentally, unintentionally","s":["accidentally","unintentionally","unwittingly","by mistake","by accident","carelessly"],"k":["blindly","by chance","fortuitously","incidentally"],"a":["deliberately","intentionally","purposely","knowingly"],"ex":["I inadvertently deleted the whole folder while trying to clear space on my phone.","She inadvertently took her brother's umbrella instead of her own.","The waiter inadvertently gave us someone else's bill, so we paid far too little."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"inalienable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to take away or give up, because it belongs to someone by right.","lb":"inherent, untransferable","s":["inherent","absolute","unalterable","fundamental","sacred","undeniable"],"k":["basic","birthright","essential","god-given"],"a":["transferable","revocable","conditional","removable"],"ex":["Every child has an inalienable right to education and safe shelter.","The constitution describes freedom of speech as an inalienable right.","Her ancestors’ land was inalienable under the old village law and could not be sold."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inane","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely silly or empty of meaning, showing a lack of sense or intelligence.","lb":"silly, senseless","s":["silly","foolish","senseless","pointless","fatuous","asinine"],"k":["cockeyed","dopey","goofy","mindless"],"a":["sensible","intelligent","meaningful","wise"],"ex":["He kept asking inane questions during the lecture, and the whole class began to sigh.","I stopped reading the comments under the video because they were so inane.","The sitcom's inane jokes made me switch off the television after ten minutes."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"inaugurate","p":"verb","d":"To begin or open something officially with a ceremony, or to formally install someone in office.","lb":"launch, open","s":["launch","open","begin","initiate","commence","start"],"k":["establish","kick off","lead off","set off"],"a":["close","end","conclude","finish"],"ex":["The mayor will inaugurate the new bridge with a ribbon-cutting ceremony on Friday.","Our school inaugurated its science fair with a speech by the principal.","The company inaugurated its new office with tea, sweets and a short speech."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"incandescent","p":"adjective","d":"Glowing brightly because of great heat, or shining with extreme brilliance or intensity.","lb":"glowing, brilliant","s":["glowing","luminous","radiant","brilliant","shining","blazing"],"k":["aglow","beaming","bright","flaming"],"a":["dim","dull","dark","faint"],"ex":["The old incandescent bulb gave off a warm yellow light, but it wasted a lot of electricity.","The blacksmith pulled the incandescent iron rod out of the fire and hammered it into shape.","The incandescent afternoon sun made the tin roofs too hot to touch."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"incantation","p":"noun","d":"A set of words spoken or sung as a magic spell.","lb":"chant, spell","s":["spell","chant","charm","formula","invocation","hex"],"k":["conjuration","hocus-pocus","magic spell","magical spell"],"a":[],"ex":["In the fairy tale, the witch whispered an incantation and the door swung open.","The magician repeated a mysterious incantation before pulling a rabbit out of his hat.","The children made up a silly incantation to stop the rain on the day of the picnic."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"incapacitating","p":"adjective","d":"Causing such serious injury, illness or fear that a person cannot work or do normal activities.","lb":"disabling, crippling","s":["disabling","crippling","debilitating","weakening","paralyzing"],"k":["handicapping","hobbling","neutralizing","sidelining"],"a":["strengthening","energizing","invigorating","empowering"],"ex":["A sudden, incapacitating back pain kept him in bed for two weeks.","The virus can cause an incapacitating fever that leaves patients too weak to stand.","Some people suffer from an incapacitating fear of speaking in public."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"incarnation","p":"noun","d":"A person who perfectly represents a quality or idea, as if it had taken human form.","lb":"embodiment, personification","s":["embodiment","personification","epitome","manifestation","avatar","image"],"k":["archetype","essence","exemplar","paragon"],"a":[],"ex":["Our grandmother is the incarnation of patience; nothing ever seems to upset her.","The new manager is the incarnation of everything the staff wanted in a leader.","Critics called the singer the incarnation of the country's hopes after the difficult year."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"incendiary","p":"adjective","d":"Designed to start fires, or likely to stir up strong anger and conflict.","lb":"inflammatory, provocative","s":["inflammatory","provocative","explosive","fiery","seditious","divisive"],"k":["agitating","firebrand","flammable","inciting"],"a":["calming","soothing","conciliatory","peaceful"],"ex":["The fire investigators found an incendiary device near the back door of the warehouse.","His incendiary comments about the neighboring village started a fight at the market.","The editor removed the incendiary headline because it could cause panic."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"incense","p":"verb","d":"To make someone extremely angry, especially by something unfair or insulting.","lb":"enrage, infuriate","s":["infuriate","enrage","anger","madden","outrage","provoke"],"k":["affront","aggravate","gall","irk"],"a":["calm","soothe","pacify","appease"],"ex":["The unfair penalty incensed the home fans, who started shouting at the referee.","She was incensed when she found that her little brother had read her diary.","The rude reply from the customer service agent incensed him even more."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"incessant","p":"adjective","d":"Continuing without pause, often in an annoying or tiring way.","lb":"nonstop, endless","s":["constant","ceaseless","nonstop","unending","continual","endless"],"k":["ageless","chronic","continuous","eternal"],"a":["intermittent","occasional","sporadic","periodic"],"ex":["The incessant noise from the road made it difficult to sleep.","Her incessant phone calls annoyed everyone in the library.","Incessant rain during the monsoon turned the village paths into mud."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"inchoate","p":"adjective","d":"Only just begun and not yet fully formed or clear.","lb":"undeveloped, rudimentary","s":["rudimentary","undeveloped","incipient","embryonic","formless","shapeless"],"k":["amorphous","budding","crude","early"],"a":["developed","formed","mature","complete"],"ex":["My plan to open a bakery was still inchoate, just a few notes in a notebook.","She felt an inchoate sadness that she could not explain to her friends.","The students' inchoate ideas needed a lot of discussion before they became a proper project."],"b":75,"y":1},{"w":"incidental","p":"adjective","d":"Happening as a minor or less important part of something else.","lb":"minor, secondary","s":["minor","secondary","subordinate","accidental","casual","peripheral"],"k":["accompanying","ancillary","attendant","auxiliary"],"a":["essential","major","central","primary"],"ex":["Please keep receipts for incidental expenses such as taxi fares and snacks.","The music in the film was incidental and barely noticeable.","Reading novels improved my vocabulary as an incidental benefit."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"incipient","p":"adjective","d":"Just beginning to appear or develop, and still in an early stage.","lb":"beginning, emerging","s":["beginning","emerging","budding","nascent","developing","starting"],"k":["burgeoning","emergent","fledgling","formative"],"a":["advanced","developed","mature","established"],"ex":["The doctor noticed incipient signs of the disease and started treatment early.","There was an incipient crack in the wall that nobody had noticed.","An incipient friendship began between the two new students on the first day of class."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"incisive","p":"adjective","d":"Clear, sharp and direct in thinking or expression, showing a deep understanding.","lb":"sharp, perceptive","s":["sharp","acute","penetrating","perceptive","trenchant","keen"],"k":["clever","discerning","discriminating","piercing"],"a":["vague","dull","superficial","muddled"],"ex":["The professor's incisive comments helped me see the real weakness in my argument.","She asked an incisive question that exposed the gap in the plan.","The reporter wrote an incisive article on why food prices keep rising."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"inclination","p":"noun","d":"A natural tendency or preference to do, like or choose a particular thing.","lb":"tendency, preference","s":["tendency","leaning","preference","liking","bent","disposition"],"k":["angle of dip","angle of inclination","attitude","dip"],"a":["aversion","dislike","reluctance","antipathy"],"ex":["He has a natural inclination for music and plays three instruments.","I had no inclination to go out after such a long day at work.","Her inclination is to trust people, which sometimes gets her into trouble."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"incline","p":"verb","d":"To make someone more likely to think or act in a certain way, or to have a tendency to do so.","lb":"tend, persuade","s":["tend","dispose","predispose","lean","persuade","influence"],"k":["be","be given","bend","bias"],"a":["deter","discourage","dissuade","disincline"],"ex":["I am inclined to agree with you about the new schedule.","Her kind words inclined me to forgive him.","High petrol prices incline many people to use public buses instead."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"incoherent","p":"adjective","d":"Not clear or logical, so that people cannot understand it.","lb":"confused, unclear","s":["unintelligible","confused","rambling","muddled","disjointed","garbled"],"k":["babbling","delirious","disconnected","disorganized"],"a":["coherent","clear","logical","articulate"],"ex":["After the shock, she was so upset that her speech became incoherent.","The essay was incoherent, jumping from one topic to another without any link.","His incoherent explanation made the police officers even more confused."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"incongruity","p":"noun","d":"A lack of fit or harmony between things that seem out of place together.","lb":"mismatch, absurdity","s":["inconsistency","mismatch","discrepancy","disparity","oddity","absurdity"],"k":["anomaly","asymmetry","conflict","contradiction"],"a":["harmony","consistency","compatibility","agreement"],"ex":["She wore a torn jacket, and its incongruity with her expensive watch surprised us.","Many people laugh at the incongruity of a fancy wedding dress at a muddy village fair.","The report noticed an incongruity between the company's promises and its actual working conditions."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"incongruous","p":"adjective","d":"Strange or out of place because it does not fit with its surroundings.","lb":"out of place, inappropriate","s":["out of place","inappropriate","incompatible","discordant","odd","unsuitable"],"k":["anomalous","antagonistic","bizarre","clashing"],"a":["appropriate","fitting","harmonious","consistent"],"ex":["A modern glass tower looked incongruous next to the old wooden houses.","It seemed incongruous to hear loud party music in a quiet hospital waiting room.","His bright orange tie was incongruous with the serious mood of the ceremony."],"b":82,"y":3},{"w":"inconsequential","p":"adjective","d":"Of little or no importance, so not worth worrying about.","lb":"unimportant, trivial","s":["unimportant","insignificant","trivial","trifling","minor","negligible"],"k":["footling","illogical","marginal","nugatory"],"a":["important","significant","crucial","vital"],"ex":["Whether we meet at five or six is inconsequential, so choose whichever time suits you.","Small spelling errors in a text message are inconsequential, but not in a job application.","He dismissed the scratch on his car as an inconsequential problem."],"b":67,"y":1},{"w":"inconspicuous","p":"adjective","d":"Not easily seen or noticed; not attracting attention.","lb":"unnoticeable, discreet","s":["unobtrusive","hidden","discreet","subtle","camouflaged","modest"],"k":["concealed","invisible","muted","nondescript"],"a":["conspicuous","noticeable","obvious","prominent"],"ex":["The small shop is so inconspicuous that many people walk past it without noticing.","She tried to look inconspicuous at the back of the hall because she was late.","An inconspicuous crack in the wall turned out to be a serious problem."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"incorporate","p":"verb","d":"To make something a part of a larger whole, or to include it as one part.","lb":"include, combine","s":["include","integrate","merge","absorb","blend","combine"],"k":["bring in","comprise","consolidate","contain"],"a":["exclude","leave out","omit","remove"],"ex":["The teacher asked us to incorporate three new words into our essay.","Our company plans to incorporate customer feedback into the next version of the app.","Try to incorporate more vegetables into your diet, such as spinach and carrots."],"b":131,"y":0},{"w":"incorrigible","p":"adjective","d":"Having bad habits or faults that cannot be changed or corrected.","lb":"hopeless, incurable","s":["hopeless","incurable","habitual","inveterate","irredeemable","hardened"],"k":["delinquent","difficult","disobedient","impenitent"],"a":["redeemable","tractable","amenable"],"ex":["My little brother is an incorrigible prankster who hides my shoes however often he is scolded.","Rafi is an incorrigible latecomer; even with three alarms he arrives after class begins.","The incorrigible gambler borrowed money again, despite all his family's pleas."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"incredulous","p":"adjective","d":"Unable or unwilling to believe something because it seems too strange or surprising.","lb":"disbelieving, doubtful","s":["doubtful","sceptical","unconvinced","distrustful","suspicious","dubious"],"k":["doubting","in question","incredible","mistrustful"],"a":["credulous","trusting","believing","gullible"],"ex":["She gave an incredulous laugh when he said he had won a car.","The teacher looked incredulous when the whole class said they had finished the homework.","Fans were incredulous when their team scored three goals in five minutes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"increment","p":"noun","d":"A small increase, especially one of a series of regular increases in pay or amount.","lb":"increase, raise","s":["increase","raise","rise","addition","gain","supplement"],"k":["accretion","augmentation","boost","bump"],"a":["decrease","reduction","cut","decline"],"ex":["Employees at the bank receive a small increment in their salary every January.","The temperature rose in increments of one degree every ten minutes during the experiment.","She built her savings by adding a modest increment to the account each month."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"inculcate","p":"verb","d":"To teach an idea, habit or belief firmly by repeating it often.","lb":"instill, teach","s":["instill","implant","drill","impress","infuse","teach"],"k":["brainwash","condition","educate","groom"],"a":["eradicate","uproot"],"ex":["Good parents inculcate habits like honesty and kindness in their children from an early age.","The school tries to inculcate a love of reading by giving students time to read every day.","My father inculcated the value of saving by giving me a small piggy bank when I was six."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"incumbent","p":"adjective","d":"Currently holding a job or official position; also, necessary as a duty (incumbent on someone).","lb":"current, obligatory","s":["current","present","sitting","in office","obligatory","binding"],"k":["bound","duty-bound","essential","existing"],"a":["former","previous","outgoing","optional"],"ex":["The incumbent mayor is asking voters for another four years in office.","It is incumbent on every driver to stop at a red light.","As the incumbent champion, she had to defend her title against younger players."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"incursion","p":"noun","d":"A sudden hostile entry into another country or area, especially by armed forces.","lb":"raid, invasion","s":["raid","invasion","attack","foray","assault","intrusion"],"k":["breach","encroachment","infiltration","irruption"],"a":["retreat","withdrawal","defense","evacuation"],"ex":["Border guards reported an incursion by armed men during the night.","Villagers feared another incursion by raiders from across the river.","The army's incursion into the neighboring territory lasted only a few hours."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"indecent","p":"adjective","d":"Not following accepted standards of decent behaviour or good taste, especially in a way that shocks people.","lb":"improper, offensive","s":["improper","offensive","vulgar","inappropriate","unseemly","indecorous"],"k":["bawdy","common","dirty","disgusting"],"a":["decent","proper","respectable","modest"],"ex":["Using indecent language in front of young children is not acceptable.","The comedian was criticised for telling indecent jokes at a family event.","Leaving the funeral so quickly seemed indecent to the other guests."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indecisive","p":"adjective","d":"Unable to make decisions quickly, or not sure what to choose.","lb":"hesitant, undecided","s":["hesitant","irresolute","undecided","uncertain","wavering","unsure"],"k":["ambivalent","doubtful","halfhearted","hesitating"],"a":["decisive","resolute","determined","firm"],"ex":["I am so indecisive that choosing a restaurant takes my friends an hour.","An indecisive leader makes the whole team feel uncertain and slow.","She felt indecisive about which university course to choose after the results."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indelible","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to remove, erase or forget.","lb":"permanent, lasting","s":["permanent","lasting","ineradicable","enduring","unforgettable","indestructible"],"k":["abiding","ageless","branded","etched"],"a":["removable","temporary","washable","fleeting"],"ex":["Be careful with that pen; its ink is indelible and will not wash out of your shirt.","My first trip to the sea left an indelible impression on me.","The teacher made an indelible mark on every student she taught."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indeterminate","p":"adjective","d":"Not exactly known, fixed or decided, and therefore unclear or vague.","lb":"unclear, indefinite","s":["indefinite","uncertain","vague","unspecified","unclear","undetermined"],"k":["ambiguous","amorphous","doubtful","equivocal"],"a":["definite","specific","fixed","certain"],"ex":["The old photograph shows a woman of indeterminate age standing near a river.","The match was delayed for an indeterminate period because of heavy rain.","The fossil is of indeterminate origin, so scientists are still studying it."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"indict","p":"verb","d":"To formally accuse someone of a crime, usually through an official legal document or decision.","lb":"charge, accuse","s":["charge","accuse","prosecute","arraign","summon","impeach"],"k":["allege","blame","bring charges against","denounce"],"a":["acquit","exonerate","clear","absolve"],"ex":["A grand jury indicted the businessman on charges of fraud and tax evasion.","Three officials were indicted for taking bribes from building contractors.","The prosecutor said she would indict anyone found selling fake medicine."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adjective","d":"Not interested in or caring about something or someone.","lb":"uninterested, unconcerned","s":["uninterested","apathetic","unconcerned","detached","cold","aloof"],"k":["blithe","cool","deaf","heedless"],"a":["interested","concerned","caring","enthusiastic"],"ex":["He seemed indifferent to the results, even though everyone else was nervous.","The shopkeeper was indifferent to the customers' complaints about the prices.","Many people are indifferent to news about faraway places."],"b":82,"y":2},{"w":"indigence","p":"noun","d":"Extreme poverty, in which a person lacks the money for basic needs such as food and shelter.","lb":"poverty, destitution","s":["poverty","penury","need","privation","want","hardship"],"k":["beggary","deprivation","hardscrabble","impoverishment"],"a":["wealth","affluence","prosperity","riches"],"ex":["After losing his job and all his savings, the old man spent his last years in indigence.","Charities in the city try to help families living in indigence during the cold months.","Her grandfather rose from childhood indigence to become a respected school headmaster."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"indigenous","p":"adjective","d":"Naturally existing in, or originally belonging to, a particular place.","lb":"native, original","s":["native","original","aboriginal","local","homegrown","endemic"],"k":["ancestral","autochthonous","earliest","first"],"a":["foreign","imported","alien","exotic"],"ex":["Mango trees are indigenous to South Asia and have grown here for thousands of years.","Indigenous communities in the hill regions have their own languages and festivals.","The museum shows indigenous crafts made from bamboo and cane."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"indigent","p":"adjective","d":"So poor that one lacks basic necessities and needs help from other people.","lb":"poor, needy","s":["poor","needy","destitute","impoverished","penniless","impecunious"],"k":["bereft","dependent","hard up","in want"],"a":["wealthy","rich","affluent","prosperous"],"ex":["The charity offers free meals to indigent families during the cold winter months.","Indigent patients can receive treatment at the hospital at a much lower cost.","The law student volunteered to help indigent clients who could not afford a lawyer."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"indignant","p":"adjective","d":"Angry because you feel that something is unfair or insulting.","lb":"angry, resentful","s":["angry","resentful","outraged","annoyed","offended","incensed"],"k":["affronted","bitter","disgruntled","displeased"],"a":["pleased","delighted","calm","content"],"ex":["The customers were indignant when the shop refused to take back the broken fan.","She felt indignant at being accused of cheating when she had studied for weeks.","My brother gave an indignant shout when I borrowed his bike without asking."],"b":88,"y":2},{"w":"indiscrete","p":"adjective","d":"Not divided into separate parts; forming a single mass.","lb":"undivided","s":["undivided","united","continuous","compact","solid","whole"],"k":["blended","consolidated","indivisible","integrated"],"a":["discrete","separate","distinct","divided"],"ex":["Under the microscope, the sample looked like an indiscrete mass with no clear cell walls.","The wet flour turned into an indiscrete lump at the bottom of the bowl.","From the hilltop, the village looked like one indiscrete blur of tin roofs."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indolence","p":"noun","d":"A lazy habit of avoiding work or effort.","lb":"laziness, idleness","s":["laziness","idleness","sloth","inertia","lethargy","inactivity"],"k":["apathy","ennui","languor","lassitude"],"a":["diligence","industry","energy","activity"],"ex":["His indolence showed in the pile of unwashed dishes and unread books.","The teacher warned that indolence, not lack of ability, was the reason for the poor results.","After the long holidays, a feeling of indolence made it hard to start studying again."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indolent","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to work or make an effort; lazy.","lb":"lazy, idle","s":["lazy","idle","slothful","lethargic","sluggish","lackadaisical"],"k":["apathetic","dilatory","inert","listless"],"a":["industrious","diligent","hardworking","energetic"],"ex":["Rafi was an indolent student who preferred sleeping to attending morning lectures.","On the holiday, we spent an indolent afternoon on the sofa watching old films.","The manager complained that indolent staff members left all the difficult work to others."],"b":85,"y":2},{"w":"induce","p":"verb","d":"To cause a particular condition, feeling or reaction to happen.","lb":"cause, bring about","s":["cause","bring about","produce","trigger","prompt","provoke"],"k":["bring on","create","get","give rise"],"a":["prevent","stop","inhibit","suppress"],"ex":["This medicine can induce drowsiness, so avoid driving after taking it.","Doctors sometimes induce labour when a pregnancy goes beyond its due date.","A heavy lunch tends to induce sleepiness during the afternoon classes."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"induct","p":"verb","d":"To formally accept someone into a group, organization or position, usually with a ceremony.","lb":"install, admit","s":["install","admit","initiate","enroll","swear in","enlist"],"k":["anoint","commission","consecrate","inaugurate"],"a":["expel","dismiss","remove","reject"],"ex":["The club will induct ten new members at a short ceremony on Friday.","The retired cricketer was inducted into the national sports hall of fame.","After six months of training, the recruits were inducted into the fire service."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indulge","p":"verb","d":"To let yourself or someone else have something enjoyable, especially more than is good for you.","lb":"pamper, treat","s":["pamper","spoil","humor","treat","gratify","satisfy"],"k":["binge","cocker","coddle","cosset"],"a":["deny","deprive","restrain","refuse"],"ex":["At weddings, everyone indulges in rich food and sweets.","Grandparents often indulge their grandchildren with extra chocolate and gifts.","After finishing my exams, I indulged in a whole weekend of films."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"indulgent","p":"adjective","d":"Allowing someone to have or do whatever they want, usually too easily.","lb":"lenient, permissive","s":["lenient","permissive","tolerant","lax","soft","easygoing"],"k":["accommodating","coddling","decadent","dissipated"],"a":["strict","harsh","stern","severe"],"ex":["My indulgent grandmother lets us eat sweets before dinner.","An indulgent teacher may let students hand in late work every week without any penalty.","The manager was too indulgent with his staff, so deadlines were often missed."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"ineffable","p":"adjective","d":"Too great, beautiful or powerful to be put into words.","lb":"indescribable, inexpressible","s":["indescribable","inexpressible","unspeakable","beyond words","indefinable","overwhelming"],"k":["awe-inspiring","mysterious","mystical","numinous"],"a":["explainable"],"ex":["She felt an ineffable joy when she held her newborn niece for the first time.","The ineffable beauty of the sunrise over the Sundarbans left the tourists silent.","Some feelings of homesickness are ineffable, and no letter can describe them."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"ineluctable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to avoid or escape, whatever you do.","lb":"inevitable, unavoidable","s":["inevitable","unavoidable","inescapable","certain","inexorable","unstoppable"],"k":["bound","bound to happen","decreed","foreordained"],"a":["avoidable","uncertain"],"ex":["Old age is an ineluctable part of life, so we should prepare for it.","After seeing the data, the ineluctable conclusion was that the plan had failed.","The ineluctable rise of the river forced the families to leave their homes."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"inept","p":"adjective","d":"Having no skill or ability; clumsy and unable to do something properly.","lb":"incompetent, clumsy","s":["incompetent","clumsy","unskilled","awkward","bungling","incapable"],"k":["clunky","cumbersome","feckless","gawky"],"a":["skilled","competent","capable","adept"],"ex":["He is inept at cooking and once set off the smoke alarm while making toast.","The inept goalkeeper let in five easy goals in the first half.","Her inept handling of the complaint made the angry customer even angrier."],"b":88,"y":1},{"w":"inequitable","p":"adjective","d":"Not fair or reasonable because it treats some people better than others.","lb":"unfair, unjust","s":["unfair","unjust","biased","partial","discriminatory","lopsided"],"k":["below the belt","disproportionate","partisan","skewed"],"a":["equitable","fair","just","impartial"],"ex":["Students called the grading policy inequitable because it favored those with private tutors.","The inequitable distribution of relief supplies left several villages with nothing.","Dividing the inheritance in such an inequitable way caused a family quarrel."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ineradicable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to remove, destroy or get rid of completely.","lb":"indelible, permanent","s":["indelible","permanent","ingrained","lasting","persistent","entrenched"],"k":["durable","enduring","established","everlasting"],"a":["removable","temporary","curable","passing"],"ex":["The flood left an ineradicable memory in the minds of everyone in the village.","Some stains on cloth seem ineradicable, no matter how much you scrub.","He had an ineradicable habit of biting his nails whenever he felt nervous."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inert","p":"adjective","d":"Not moving or acting, and without any power to move or react.","lb":"motionless, inactive","s":["motionless","inactive","still","immobile","lifeless","dormant"],"k":["indifferent","neutral","sluggish","soggy"],"a":["active","mobile","lively","dynamic"],"ex":["The cat lay inert on the warm tiles, too tired to chase even a fly.","After the long flight, I sat inert in my seat while everyone else rushed off.","Light bulbs are often filled with an inert gas that does not react with the hot filament."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"inevitable","p":"adjective","d":"Certain to happen and impossible to avoid or prevent.","lb":"unavoidable, certain","s":["unavoidable","inescapable","certain","fated","sure","destined"],"k":["assured","confident","convinced","definite"],"a":["avoidable","uncertain","unlikely"],"ex":["With so many cars on the road, traffic jams are inevitable in Dhaka.","After weeks of ignoring his studies, failure was inevitable.","It was inevitable that the old bridge would collapse sooner or later."],"b":448,"y":3},{"w":"inexorable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to stop or change; continuing in a relentless way.","lb":"relentless, unstoppable","s":["relentless","unstoppable","inevitable","unyielding","implacable","unavoidable"],"k":["adamant","dogged","grim","ineluctable"],"a":["yielding","avoidable","flexible","lenient"],"ex":["The inexorable rise of sea levels threatens villages along the southern coast.","He felt the inexorable march of the exam date as the days slipped by.","The inexorable spread of mobile payments has changed how people shop in small towns."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"infamous","p":"adjective","d":"Well known for something bad, wicked or shameful.","lb":"notorious, disreputable","s":["notorious","disreputable","scandalous","disgraceful","wicked","shameful"],"k":["black","crooked","discreditable","dubious"],"a":["reputable","honorable","respected","admired"],"ex":["The road is infamous for its potholes, and drivers avoid it after heavy rain.","He became infamous in the neighborhood for never returning the things he borrowed.","The restaurant was infamous for its dirty kitchen until the owner finally cleaned it up."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"infamy","p":"noun","d":"The state of being widely known for something very bad or shameful.","lb":"disgrace, notoriety","s":["notoriety","disgrace","dishonor","disrepute","shame","ignominy"],"k":["bad name","censure","humiliation","obloquy"],"a":["fame","honor","glory","renown"],"ex":["The company earned lasting infamy after it dumped chemical waste into the river.","His infamy as a cheat followed him from school to his first job.","The junction has gained a certain infamy among drivers for its endless traffic jams."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"infatuated","p":"adjective","d":"Filled with a strong but foolish or short-lived love or admiration for someone or something.","lb":"besotted, obsessed","s":["besotted","smitten","obsessed","enamored","captivated","enchanted"],"k":["charmed","crazy about","gaga over","hooked on"],"a":["indifferent","disenchanted","disillusioned"],"ex":["Rafi was infatuated with his classmate and wrote her a poem every single day.","At fifteen, she was infatuated with a pop singer and covered her wall with his posters.","The young entrepreneur became infatuated with a risky idea and ignored all warnings."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"infectious","p":"adjective","d":"Describing a disease that can spread from one person or animal to another.","lb":"contagious, catching","s":["contagious","catching","communicable","spreading","transmissible"],"k":["airborne","contaminating","corrupting","epidemic"],"a":["harmless","benign"],"ex":["Measles is a highly infectious disease, so sick children must stay home.","The doctor said my cold was no longer infectious after three days.","Wash your hands often to stop infectious germs from spreading in the hostel."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"infer","p":"verb","d":"To reach a conclusion from evidence or clues, rather than from a direct statement.","lb":"deduce, conclude","s":["deduce","conclude","gather","reason","work out","derive"],"k":["deduct","divine","extrapolate","figure out"],"a":[],"ex":["From her red eyes, I inferred that she had been crying.","Readers can infer the writer's opinion even though she never states it.","We inferred from the empty shelves that the shop had sold out."],"b":216,"y":6},{"w":"infinitesimal","p":"adjective","d":"So extremely small that it is almost impossible to measure or notice.","lb":"tiny, minute","s":["tiny","minute","microscopic","minuscule","negligible","imperceptible"],"k":["diminutive","hairline","little","miniature"],"a":["huge","enormous","immense","vast"],"ex":["The chance of winning the lottery is infinitesimal, yet millions of people still play.","A drop of food coloring made an infinitesimal change to the color of the water.","Compared with the whole universe, our planet is of infinitesimal size."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"inflammatory","p":"adjective","d":"Likely to make people angry, violent or very emotional.","lb":"provocative, incendiary","s":["provocative","incendiary","inciting","fiery","explosive","controversial"],"k":["agitating","heated","hot-button","polemical"],"a":["calming","soothing","peaceful","conciliatory"],"ex":["Inflammatory posts on social media made the argument between the two groups worse.","The coach regretted his inflammatory remarks about the referee after the match.","Teachers asked students to avoid inflammatory language during the debate."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inflation","p":"noun","d":"A general rise in prices over time, which reduces what money can buy.","lb":"price rise","s":["price rise","rising prices","price hikes","cost increase"],"k":["currency debasement","economic process","escalation","money devaluation"],"a":["deflation"],"ex":["Inflation made rice, oil and vegetables much more expensive this year.","Because of inflation, my pocket money does not buy as much as before.","The bank raised interest rates in an effort to control inflation."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"inflict","p":"verb","d":"To make someone suffer something unpleasant, such as pain, damage or punishment.","lb":"impose, deal","s":["impose","deal","administer","wreak","cause","deliver"],"k":["bring down","burden with","communicate","dish out"],"a":["spare","withhold","relieve","protect"],"ex":["The storm inflicted heavy damage on the fishing villages along the coast.","Bullies inflict pain on others because they want to feel powerful.","I would never inflict my bad mood on my friends."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"influx","p":"noun","d":"The arrival of a large number of people or things in a place at the same time.","lb":"inflow, rush","s":["inflow","flood","rush","surge","stream","deluge"],"k":["glut","migration","onslaught","spate"],"a":["exodus","outflow","departure","drain"],"ex":["Dhaka sees a big influx of travelers returning to the city after the Eid holidays.","An influx of new students made the school’s classrooms very crowded this year.","The small café struggled to cope with the sudden influx of customers at lunchtime."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"infraction","p":"noun","d":"An act of breaking a rule or law, usually a minor one.","lb":"violation, offence","s":["violation","breach","offence","infringement","misdemeanour","transgression"],"k":["crime","criminal offense","fault","indiscretion"],"a":["compliance","obedience","observance","conformity"],"ex":["Parking in front of a hospital gate is a serious traffic infraction.","The player was sent off for a rule infraction in the second half.","Copying from a classmate is an infraction of the exam rules and can lead to disqualification."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"infrastructure","p":"noun","d":"The basic systems and structures, such as roads, power and water supply, that a country or organization needs to work.","lb":"framework, facilities","s":["framework","foundation","base","substructure","facilities","services"],"k":["backbone","basis","cornerstone","grid"],"a":[],"ex":["The city is spending billions on new roads, bridges and other infrastructure.","Poor infrastructure makes it hard for farmers to bring crops to market.","The company invests in digital infrastructure to keep its website running smoothly."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"infringe","p":"verb","d":"To break a law, rule or agreement, or to limit someone's rights or freedom.","lb":"violate, break","s":["violate","breach","break","contravene","trespass on","transgress"],"k":["crack","encroach","go against","impinge"],"a":["obey","respect","honor","comply with"],"ex":["Copying a singer's songs and selling them online will infringe copyright.","The new rule infringes on students' freedom to choose their own clothes.","Building on a public footpath infringes the rights of everyone who walks there."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"infuse","p":"verb","d":"To fill someone or something with a quality, feeling or idea.","lb":"instil, fill","s":["imbue","fill","inspire","inject","impart","pervade"],"k":["fill up","impregnate","inculcate","instill"],"a":["drain","deplete","strip","sap"],"ex":["The new coach infused the team with confidence before the final match.","Her warm speech infused the whole class with a love of poetry.","The manager tried to infuse new energy into the tired office after the merger."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"infusion","p":"noun","d":"A drink or medicine made by soaking leaves, herbs or fruit in hot water.","lb":"herbal brew","s":["brew","tea","herbal tea","extract","tincture","concoction"],"k":["cordial","draught","elixir","essence"],"a":[],"ex":["Grandmother made an infusion of ginger and honey to soothe my sore throat.","A mint infusion is a refreshing drink on hot afternoons.","The café serves a fruit infusion that is naturally sweet and has no tea in it."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ingenuous","p":"adjective","d":"Honest and open in a childlike way, often because of having little experience of the world.","lb":"naive, innocent","s":["naive","innocent","artless","trusting","candid","open"],"k":["credulous","green","gullible","honest"],"a":["devious","sophisticated","worldly","cunning"],"ex":["The new intern's ingenuous questions made the experienced staff smile and then think again.","She gave an ingenuous laugh and admitted that she had never seen the sea.","His ingenuous belief that everyone tells the truth made him an easy target for scammers."],"b":91,"y":1},{"w":"ingestion","p":"noun","d":"The act of taking food, drink or another substance into the body through the mouth.","lb":"swallowing, eating","s":["swallowing","eating","drinking","consumption","intake","taking in"],"k":["activity","bodily function","bodily process","body process"],"a":["excretion","expulsion","elimination"],"ex":["Accidental ingestion of cleaning liquid is a common reason children are taken to hospital.","The label warns that ingestion of more than two tablets a day may cause stomach pain.","Doctors traced the outbreak to the ingestion of contaminated water after the flood."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ingrate","p":"noun","d":"A person who shows no thanks for the help or kindness they have received.","lb":"ungrateful person","s":["ungrateful wretch","thankless person","thankless wretch","ungrateful person"],"k":["boor","cad","churl","freeloader"],"a":[],"ex":["After we paid for his studies, he never even called to say thanks; what an ingrate!","Don't be an ingrate; your aunt spent a whole week cooking for your guests.","The manager called the former employee an ingrate for criticising the firm that had trained him."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"ingratiate","p":"verb","d":"To try to make someone like you by being very nice or flattering, usually for your own benefit.","lb":"flatter, win over","s":["curry favor","flatter","fawn","butter up","court","toady"],"k":["bootlick","control","cozy up to","grovel"],"a":["alienate","antagonize","offend","repel"],"ex":["The new intern tried to ingratiate himself with the boss by bringing him tea every morning.","She ingratiated herself with her future in-laws by praising every dish they served.","Some students ingratiate themselves with teachers by agreeing with everything they say."],"b":100,"y":1},{"w":"ingratiation","p":"noun","d":"Behaviour in which you try to win someone's favour by flattery or by being very helpful to them.","lb":"flattery, fawning","s":["flattery","fawning","toadying","grovelling","courting favour"],"k":["adulation","apple-polishing","blandishment","bootlicking"],"a":["independence","candour","honesty","defiance"],"ex":["His constant ingratiation with the manager annoyed his colleagues.","The student's ingratiation, bringing sweets for the teacher and praising every lesson, fooled nobody.","Honest feedback is more useful to a leader than daily ingratiation from the staff."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ingredient","p":"noun","d":"One of the foods or substances that are mixed together to make a dish or product.","lb":"component","s":["component","constituent","element","part","factor"],"k":["additive","aspect","division","fixings"],"a":[],"ex":["Fresh coriander is a key ingredient in this chicken curry.","Check the list of ingredients on the packet if you have an allergy.","The recipe has only three ingredients: flour, sugar and butter."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"inherent","p":"adjective","d":"Existing as a natural and permanent part of something, so that it cannot be removed.","lb":"built-in, intrinsic","s":["intrinsic","innate","natural","essential","fundamental","basic"],"k":["characteristic","congenital","constitutional","crucial"],"a":["acquired","external","learned","incidental"],"ex":["Every investment has some inherent risk, even the ones that look safe.","The problem is inherent in the design, so a small repair will not solve it.","Kindness is an inherent part of her character, and she helps strangers without thinking."],"b":155,"y":0},{"w":"inheritance","p":"noun","d":"Money, property or possessions that you receive from someone after they die.","lb":"legacy, bequest","s":["legacy","bequest","heritage","birthright","patrimony","estate"],"k":["acquisition","dowry","gift","heirloom"],"a":[],"ex":["She used her inheritance to pay for her brother's university fees.","The brothers argued over the inheritance after their father passed away.","Under the law, every child has the right to a fair share of the inheritance."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"inimical","p":"adjective","d":"Harmful or hostile; likely to damage something or work against it.","lb":"hostile, harmful","s":["hostile","harmful","adverse","unfriendly","antagonistic","detrimental"],"k":["belligerent","negative","opposing","prejudicial"],"a":["friendly","helpful","beneficial","favorable"],"ex":["Constant noise is inimical to good study habits, so find a quiet corner.","Smoking is inimical to your health, however calm it makes you feel for a moment.","Frequent power cuts are inimical to small factories that depend on machines."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"inimitable","p":"adjective","d":"So special or individual that nobody else can copy it.","lb":"unique, matchless","s":["unique","matchless","unrivalled","peerless","incomparable","distinctive"],"k":["exceptional","idiosyncratic","one","one and only"],"a":["ordinary","typical","commonplace","derivative"],"ex":["The old singer's inimitable voice made every song sound like a story.","Her inimitable style of teaching made even grammar fun.","Grandmother's inimitable fish curry has defeated every attempt to copy it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"injunction","p":"noun","d":"An official order, especially from a court, telling someone to do something or to stop doing it.","lb":"court order, command","s":["order","ruling","command","directive","mandate","prohibition"],"k":["cease and desist order","edict","embargo","fiat"],"a":["permission","consent","authorization"],"ex":["The court issued an injunction stopping the factory from dumping waste into the river.","Residents obtained an injunction to prevent the builder from cutting down the old trees.","The singer got an injunction to stop the magazine from printing her private photos."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"innate","p":"adjective","d":"Existing in a person or animal from birth, rather than learned.","lb":"inborn, natural","s":["inborn","inherent","natural","instinctive","congenital","intrinsic"],"k":["basic","born","constitutional","essential"],"a":["acquired","learned","taught","conditioned"],"ex":["Babies have an innate ability to suck milk, which no one has to teach them.","Some people believe musical talent is innate, while others think it comes only from practice.","Birds have an innate sense of direction that helps them migrate across thousands of kilometers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"innocuous","p":"adjective","d":"Not harmful and not likely to offend or upset anyone.","lb":"harmless, inoffensive","s":["harmless","safe","inoffensive","benign","mild","innocent"],"k":["anodyne","banal","nonthreatening","ordinary"],"a":["harmful","dangerous","offensive","toxic"],"ex":["His innocuous joke about the weather started a long and friendly conversation.","The doctor said the small lump was innocuous and needed no treatment.","Most household plants are innocuous, but a few can make small children ill."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"innuendo","p":"noun","d":"An indirect remark that suggests something unpleasant or improper without saying it openly.","lb":"insinuation, hint","s":["insinuation","hint","implication","suggestion","allusion","aspersion"],"k":["backhanded compliment","connotation","double entendre","nudge"],"a":["frankness","candour","directness"],"ex":["She did not accuse him directly, but her innuendo made everyone suspect that he had cheated.","The article was full of innuendo about the businessman's wealth, but it offered no proof.","I don't like the innuendo in your question; if you think I lied, say so."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inordinate","p":"adjective","d":"Much greater than is reasonable or normal.","lb":"excessive, extreme","s":["excessive","extreme","undue","immoderate","unreasonable","exorbitant"],"k":["outrageous","overblown","prodigious","uncalled-for"],"a":["moderate","reasonable","modest","restrained"],"ex":["The repair took an inordinate amount of time for such a simple job.","He spends an inordinate number of hours on his phone and sleeps very little.","The restaurant charged an inordinate price for a plate of plain rice and lentils."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"inquisition","p":"noun","d":"A long and harsh series of questions, or a formal official investigation.","lb":"interrogation, grilling","s":["interrogation","questioning","grilling","investigation","inquiry","probe"],"k":["crackdown","dragnet","enquiry","heresy trial"],"a":[],"ex":["My mother's inquisition about where I had been all evening lasted an hour.","The manager conducted a harsh inquisition into who had leaked the report.","Reporters turned the press conference into an inquisition, shouting questions at him."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"inquisitive","p":"adjective","d":"Very interested in learning things, and asking a lot of questions.","lb":"curious, inquiring","s":["curious","inquiring","questioning","probing","nosy","prying"],"k":["eager","intrigued","investigative","keen"],"a":["uninterested","indifferent","apathetic","unconcerned"],"ex":["My inquisitive little brother asks a hundred questions about every machine he sees.","Good scientists have inquisitive minds and never stop asking why.","The inquisitive neighbor leaned over the fence to see what we were doing."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insatiable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to satisfy; always wanting more.","lb":"unsatisfiable, greedy","s":["unquenchable","voracious","ravenous","greedy","gluttonous","avid"],"k":["avaricious","boundless","consuming","covetous"],"a":["satisfied","sated","content","moderate"],"ex":["Growing boys often have an insatiable appetite and can eat three plates of rice.","Her insatiable curiosity led her to read every science book in the school library.","The collector's insatiable desire for old coins left him with no money for rent."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"inscribe","p":"verb","d":"To write, carve or print words or a name on a surface so that they last.","lb":"engrave, write","s":["engrave","carve","etch","write","imprint","incise"],"k":["autograph","brand","chip at","cypher"],"a":["erase","efface","rub out","delete"],"ex":["The jeweler will inscribe your initials inside the ring.","The class inscribed a thank-you message on a wooden plaque for the principal.","She inscribed the book with a short note for her grandfather."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insensible","p":"adjective","d":"Not able to feel or notice something, such as pain, cold or danger.","lb":"numb, unaware","s":["numb","unaware","unfeeling","oblivious","unconscious","insensitive"],"k":["anaesthetic","anesthetic","asleep","blind"],"a":["sensitive","aware","conscious","responsive"],"ex":["His fingers were so cold that he was almost insensible to pain.","The boxer was knocked insensible, and the referee stopped the fight at once.","She seemed insensible to the danger as she crossed the busy road while texting."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"insidious","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming harmless but secretly causing harm, often slowly, so the danger is not noticed until it is serious.","lb":"sneaky, harmful","s":["treacherous","sneaky","stealthy","sly","subtle","creeping"],"k":["dangerous","furtive","harmful","hazardous"],"a":["harmless","open","straightforward","obvious"],"ex":["High blood pressure is an insidious illness because many people feel fine while it damages their hearts.","Social media can have an insidious effect on teenagers, quietly lowering their confidence over many months.","The insidious rumor spread through the office, and by Friday nobody trusted the new manager."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"insight","p":"noun","d":"A clear, deep understanding of a person, situation or problem.","lb":"understanding, perception","s":["understanding","perception","awareness","intuition","comprehension","wisdom"],"k":["apprehension","brainstorm","brainwave","knowledge"],"a":["ignorance","incomprehension"],"ex":["Her years of teaching gave her real insight into why some students struggle with maths.","The interview with the old shopkeeper offered a useful insight into how small businesses survive.","It took a long talk with my brother before I gained any insight into his decision."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"insinuate","p":"verb","d":"To suggest something unpleasant in an indirect, sly way, without saying it openly.","lb":"hint, imply","s":["imply","hint","suggest","intimate","allude","indicate"],"k":["adumbrate","cast aspersions","drop hints","mutter"],"a":["state","declare","assert","announce"],"ex":["Are you insinuating that I copied her answers during the test?","He insinuated that the manager had been promoted only because of his uncle.","My aunt kept insinuating that I was lazy without ever saying it directly."],"b":85,"y":2},{"w":"insipid","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking flavor, or lacking interest, excitement and character.","lb":"bland, dull","s":["bland","tasteless","flavorless","dull","boring","uninspiring"],"k":["colorless","dreary","jejune","lukewarm"],"a":["tasty","flavorful","spicy","lively"],"ex":["The soup was so insipid that we had to add a lot of salt and pepper.","I could not finish the insipid tea that the canteen served in plastic cups.","The film's insipid story made half the audience check their phones."],"b":85,"y":2},{"w":"insistence","p":"noun","d":"The act of firmly demanding something, or saying something is true, and refusing to accept anything else.","lb":"firm demand","s":["demand","urging","persistence","firmness","assertion","stress"],"k":["adamance","dogmatism","earnestness","obstinacy"],"a":["flexibility","acquiescence","indifference"],"ex":["At my mother's insistence, I wore a jacket to the cold morning class.","The teacher's insistence on neat handwriting improved our notebooks.","Despite his insistence that he was fine, we took him to the clinic."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insolence","p":"noun","d":"Rude, disrespectful behavior, especially toward someone who has more authority than you.","lb":"rudeness, cheek","s":["impertinence","rudeness","cheek","impudence","disrespect","audacity"],"k":["backchat","crust","discourtesy","effrontery"],"a":["respect","politeness","courtesy","deference"],"ex":["The teacher was shocked by the student's insolence when he laughed at the correction.","Talking back to your elders with such insolence is not acceptable in our home.","The waiter's insolence made us leave the restaurant before ordering."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insolent","p":"adjective","d":"Rude and disrespectful, especially to someone in authority or someone you should respect.","lb":"rude, disrespectful","s":["rude","impertinent","impudent","cheeky","disrespectful","insulting"],"k":["audacious","barefaced","bodacious","bold"],"a":["polite","respectful","courteous","deferential"],"ex":["The student’s insolent reply made the whole class go quiet.","The waiter was fired after making an insolent remark to a customer.","She gave him an insolent smile and walked away without answering."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"insolvent","p":"adjective","d":"Unable to pay the money you owe; having less money than debts.","lb":"bankrupt, broke","s":["bankrupt","broke","ruined","bust","penniless","failed"],"k":["belly up","cash-strapped","debt-ridden","in debt"],"a":["solvent","wealthy","prosperous","rich"],"ex":["The small factory became insolvent after its biggest customer stopped paying.","The court declared him insolvent after he failed to pay his debts for years.","An insolvent company cannot pay its workers or its suppliers."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"insouciant","p":"adjective","d":"Cheerfully relaxed and unworried, especially when other people think you should be concerned.","lb":"carefree, nonchalant","s":["carefree","nonchalant","unconcerned","casual","blithe","easygoing"],"k":["cavalier","cool","devil-may-care","happy-go-lucky"],"a":["anxious","worried","concerned","careful"],"ex":["He walked into the exam hall with an insouciant smile, as if it were an ordinary day.","The insouciant waiter ignored the angry customer and kept humming a tune.","Her insouciant attitude to deadlines drove her manager crazy."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"instigate","p":"verb","d":"To cause something bad, such as trouble or a fight, to start by encouraging others.","lb":"incite, provoke","s":["incite","provoke","stir up","spark","trigger","foment"],"k":["activate","agitate","arouse","bring about"],"a":["prevent","stop","quell","suppress"],"ex":["Two students instigated a quarrel in the canteen by spreading a false rumor.","Police say a small group instigated the trouble at the match by throwing bottles.","Nobody knew who had instigated the argument between the two neighbors."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"instinct","p":"noun","d":"A natural, inborn way of behaving or reacting that does not need to be learned.","lb":"natural urge","s":["impulse","urge","intuition","drive","gut feeling","reflex"],"k":["aptitude","bent","feel","feeling"],"a":["reason","logic","thought","learning"],"ex":["Newborn babies have an instinct to suck when they are hungry.","She followed her instinct and chose the shorter road, which saved an hour.","A mother's instinct is often to protect her child from any danger."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insufferable","p":"adjective","d":"So unpleasant or annoying that you can hardly bear it.","lb":"unbearable, intolerable","s":["unbearable","intolerable","unendurable","impossible","unacceptable","unspeakable"],"k":["bitter","exasperating","galling","grating"],"a":["bearable","tolerable","pleasant","agreeable"],"ex":["The heat in the crowded bus was insufferable.","My cousin is insufferable when he wins at cards; he boasts for hours.","The noise from the construction site was insufferable during exam week."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"insular","p":"adjective","d":"Interested only in your own small group or place, and unwilling to accept new ideas or people.","lb":"narrow-minded, isolated","s":["parochial","provincial","isolated","closed","cut off","petty"],"k":["clannish","cloistered","isolationist","limited"],"a":["cosmopolitan","worldly"],"ex":["The small town was so insular that visitors were stared at and new ideas were treated with suspicion.","Living abroad changed my insular view of the world and made me curious about other cultures.","An insular group of friends, they rarely invited anyone new to join their table at lunch."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"insularity","p":"noun","d":"A narrow-minded attitude that comes from having little contact with other cultures or ideas.","lb":"narrow-mindedness, isolation","s":["isolation","detachment","separateness","parochialism","narrow-mindedness"],"k":["clannishness","insulation","isolationism","myopia"],"a":["worldliness","sophistication","tolerance"],"ex":["The insularity of the small town meant that visitors were stared at for days.","Studying abroad cured him of the insularity he had grown up with in a tiny village.","Critics accused the club of insularity because it never invited outside speakers or new members."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"insulation","p":"noun","d":"Material that stops heat, cold, sound or electricity from passing through.","lb":"heat barrier, lagging","s":["lagging","padding","protection","covering","shielding","barrier"],"k":["batting","cladding","detachment","fiberglass"],"a":[],"ex":["Good insulation in the roof keeps the house cooler during the hot summer.","Rubber is used as insulation around electrical wires to prevent shocks.","We added insulation to the walls to reduce the noise from the busy road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"insuperable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to overcome or get past; too great or difficult to be beaten.","lb":"insurmountable, unbeatable","s":["insurmountable","unconquerable","impassable","overwhelming","invincible","unbeatable"],"k":["daunting","impregnable","intractable","monumental"],"a":["surmountable","manageable","minor","easy"],"ex":["Poverty seemed an insuperable barrier to her dream of becoming a doctor, until a scholarship changed things.","The difference in language seemed insuperable at first, but the two negotiators found a translator.","The flooded road was an insuperable obstacle for the bus, and we had to turn back."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"insurgent","p":"noun","d":"A person who fights against the government or ruling authority of their own country.","lb":"rebel, revolutionary","s":["rebel","revolutionary","mutineer","agitator","dissident","guerrilla"],"k":["crusader","extremist","freedom fighter","guerilla"],"a":["loyalist","supporter"],"ex":["The news reported that insurgents had taken control of a small town near the border.","The government offered talks to the insurgents in the hope of ending the conflict.","In the novel, the young insurgent hides in the hills and plans his next move."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"insurrection","p":"noun","d":"An organized, often violent, uprising against a government or other established authority.","lb":"uprising, revolt","s":["uprising","revolt","rebellion","mutiny","revolution","insurgency"],"k":["battle","civil unrest","conflict","coup"],"a":["obedience","submission","loyalty","order"],"ex":["Textbooks describe the sepoy insurrection of 1857 as a turning point in the history of South Asia.","The soldiers crushed the insurrection within a week, but tension remained in the region.","News channels showed footage of the insurrection as crowds took over the city's main square."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"integral","p":"adjective","d":"Necessary and important as a basic part of a whole, so that you cannot do without it.","lb":"essential, fundamental","s":["essential","fundamental","vital","necessary","indispensable","basic"],"k":["central","constitutional","critical","entire"],"a":["unnecessary","optional","dispensable","peripheral"],"ex":["Practice tests are an integral part of preparing for the GRE.","Rice is integral to Bangladeshi meals, and many people feel a day without it is incomplete.","Teamwork is integral to our office, so every project begins with a group discussion."],"b":176,"y":0},{"w":"integrate","p":"verb","d":"To combine two or more things so that they work together as one whole.","lb":"combine, merge","s":["combine","merge","unify","incorporate","blend","fuse"],"k":["amalgamate","assimilate","flux","homogenize"],"a":["separate","divide","segregate","disconnect"],"ex":["The school plans to integrate computer lessons into every subject instead of teaching them separately.","Our new accounting software integrates with the bank's app, so payments are recorded automatically.","It took Rafi a few months to integrate into the team after moving to the Chattogram office."],"b":208,"y":1},{"w":"intelligible","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be understood, and clear enough for people to make sense of.","lb":"understandable, clear","s":["understandable","comprehensible","clear","plain","lucid","legible"],"k":["approachable","articulate","distinct","evident"],"a":["unintelligible","incomprehensible","unclear","confusing"],"ex":["The instructions were written in plain, intelligible English so that anyone could follow them.","On the bad phone line, his voice was barely intelligible.","A good teacher makes difficult ideas intelligible to young students."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"intense","p":"adjective","d":"Very strong, great or serious in degree.","lb":"extreme, strong","s":["extreme","strong","powerful","fierce","severe","acute"],"k":["aggravated","bad","big","brutal"],"a":["mild","weak","gentle","moderate"],"ex":["The intense heat of the summer afternoon made everyone stay indoors.","Competition for seats in the university is intense every year.","She felt intense pain in her ankle after falling off the bicycle."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"intensifying","p":"adjective","d":"Becoming stronger, greater or more extreme over time.","lb":"growing, escalating","s":["growing","increasing","escalating","rising","strengthening","mounting"],"k":["accelerating","aggravating","amplifying","burgeoning"],"a":["weakening","fading","diminishing","easing"],"ex":["The intensifying storm forced the ferries to stay at the dock.","Intensifying competition among phone companies has pushed prices down.","Her intensifying headache made it hard to continue the exam."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"interim","p":"adjective","d":"Temporary; used or in place during the time between one thing ending and another starting.","lb":"temporary, provisional","s":["temporary","provisional","acting","caretaker","stopgap","makeshift"],"k":["contingent","emergency","improvised","passing"],"a":["permanent","lasting","final","definitive"],"ex":["The school appointed an interim principal until a permanent one could be found.","An interim report on the project will be shared with the team in March.","The court granted an interim order to stop the demolition until the case is decided."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"interloper","p":"noun","d":"A person who enters a place or group where they are not wanted or invited.","lb":"intruder, trespasser","s":["intruder","trespasser","outsider","invader","meddler","uninvited guest"],"k":["busybody","crasher","fifth wheel","interferer"],"a":["insider","member","host"],"ex":["The guard stopped the interloper who had climbed over the wall of the school.","At the family wedding, the stranger who ate quietly in the corner felt like an interloper.","Nadia felt like an interloper when she joined the group after they had been friends for years."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"interlude","p":"noun","d":"A short period of time or event that comes between two longer ones, especially a pleasant break.","lb":"break, pause","s":["break","pause","interval","intermission","respite","breather"],"k":["digression","diversion","entr'acte","episode"],"a":[],"ex":["A short musical interlude kept the audience entertained while the stage was being changed.","The weekend at the beach was a pleasant interlude between two busy weeks of exams.","During a brief interlude in the storm, the family hurried across the road to a shelter."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"interminable","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming to last forever because it is boring or tiring.","lb":"endless, tedious","s":["endless","unending","ceaseless","tedious","perpetual","incessant"],"k":["ageless","constant","dragging","drawn-out"],"a":["brief","short","finite","fleeting"],"ex":["The interminable wait at the passport office made everyone restless and hungry.","We sat through an interminable speech before the prizes were finally given out.","The bus journey felt interminable because of the traffic and the broken air conditioning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"intermittent","p":"adjective","d":"Starting and stopping repeatedly, not continuous.","lb":"on and off, occasional","s":["sporadic","occasional","periodic","irregular","broken","spasmodic"],"k":["erratic","infrequent","jerky","scattered"],"a":["continuous","constant","steady","uninterrupted"],"ex":["Intermittent showers fell all afternoon, so we kept opening and closing our umbrellas.","The village has an intermittent power supply, and the lights go out several times a day.","I could not finish the call because of the intermittent mobile signal."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"internalize","p":"verb","d":"To absorb an idea, rule or belief so deeply that it becomes part of your own thinking and behaviour.","lb":"absorb, take in","s":["absorb","assimilate","take in","adopt","embrace","digest"],"k":["ascribe","assign","attribute","comprehend"],"a":["express","reject","disown"],"ex":["Children internalize the habits they see at home long before they can explain them.","After years of practice, the pianist had internalized the rhythm and no longer counted beats.","If you internalize every piece of criticism, you may begin to doubt your own talent."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"interpolate","p":"verb","d":"To add a remark or extra piece of text in the middle of something else.","lb":"insert, interject","s":["insert","interject","introduce","add","inject","slip in"],"k":["alter","calculate","compute","cypher"],"a":["omit","delete","remove","cut"],"ex":["Rafi kept interpolating jokes into his speech, which made the audience laugh.","The editor discovered that someone had interpolated extra sentences into the old manuscript.","She interpolated a quick question while the manager was explaining the budget."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"intersperse","p":"verb","d":"To scatter or place things at various points among other things.","lb":"scatter, mix in","s":["scatter","sprinkle","dot","mix","intermingle","intermix"],"k":["blend","disperse","enclose","fleck"],"a":["group","cluster","concentrate","gather"],"ex":["The teacher interspersed her lecture with short stories to keep the class awake.","Tall palm trees are interspersed among the rice fields along the road.","He interspersed his speech with jokes, so the audience stayed cheerful."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"intervene","p":"verb","d":"To step into a situation in order to stop or change what is happening.","lb":"step in, interfere","s":["step in","intercede","interfere","mediate","interrupt","intrude"],"k":["barge in","butt in","chip in","come to the rescue"],"a":["stand back","ignore","withdraw","neglect"],"ex":["The teacher intervened when the two boys began shouting at each other.","Neighbors intervened to stop the argument before it became a fight.","The central bank may intervene if the price of the dollar rises too sharply."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"intimate","p":"verb","d":"To suggest something indirectly without saying it openly.","lb":"hint, imply","s":["hint","imply","suggest","indicate","insinuate","signal"],"k":["adumbrate","cue","gesture","lead on"],"a":["state","declare","announce","assert"],"ex":["The manager intimated that some jobs might be cut next year.","She intimated her disappointment by leaving the room without saying goodbye.","My aunt intimated that she would like to visit us during Eid without asking directly."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"intolerant","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to accept opinions, beliefs or ways of living that are different from your own.","lb":"narrow-minded","s":["bigoted","prejudiced","biased","dogmatic","rigid"],"k":["chauvinistic","doctrinaire","narrow","parochial"],"a":["tolerant","accepting","liberal","understanding"],"ex":["Our manager is intolerant of any opinion that differs from his own.","An intolerant attitude can make a classroom a difficult place for shy students.","People who are intolerant of other languages miss the chance to learn from them."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"intractable","p":"adjective","d":"Very difficult to control, solve or change.","lb":"stubborn, unmanageable","s":["stubborn","unmanageable","unruly","obstinate","uncontrollable","difficult"],"k":["balking","bullheaded","cantankerous","cumbersome"],"a":["manageable","docile","compliant","obedient"],"ex":["The city's traffic problem seems intractable, however many new roads are built.","The intractable toddler refused to wear shoes, however nicely we asked.","Doctors tried many medicines, but the patient's intractable cough did not improve."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"intransigence","p":"noun","d":"Refusal to change your opinion or to compromise, even when other people ask you to.","lb":"stubbornness, inflexibility","s":["stubbornness","obstinacy","rigidity","unwillingness","inflexibility"],"k":["bloody-mindedness","defiance","dogmatism","entrenchment"],"a":["flexibility","compromise","willingness","adaptability"],"ex":["The workers' intransigence made it impossible for the owners to reach a quick settlement.","Her intransigence about the wedding date upset both families.","The landlord's intransigence over the rent meant that several tenants moved out."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"intransigent","p":"adjective","d":"Refusing to change your opinion or to reach a compromise.","lb":"stubborn, uncompromising","s":["uncompromising","stubborn","inflexible","obstinate","unyielding","intractable"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","dogged","dour"],"a":["flexible","compromising","accommodating","yielding"],"ex":["The landlord remained intransigent and refused to lower the rent, even after the tenants explained their situation.","Both sides were intransigent, so the meeting ended without any agreement.","My intransigent grandfather refuses to use a mobile phone, whatever we say."],"b":92,"y":2},{"w":"intricate","p":"adjective","d":"Having many small, carefully arranged parts, so that it is complicated and detailed.","lb":"complex, elaborate","s":["complex","elaborate","complicated","detailed","involved","tangled"],"k":["convoluted","dense","fiddly","filigreed"],"a":["simple","plain","straightforward","basic"],"ex":["The bride's hands were covered with intricate henna designs.","The plot of the detective novel is so intricate that I had to take notes.","A watch has an intricate mechanism of tiny wheels and springs."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"intrigue","p":"noun","d":"Secret and clever planning by a group of people to gain power or harm others.","lb":"plot, scheming","s":["plot","scheme","conspiracy","machination","cabal","manoeuvring"],"k":["game","ploy","secret plan","stratagem"],"a":["openness","honesty","candour","transparency"],"ex":["The novel is full of palace intrigue, with ministers secretly plotting against one another.","Office intrigue made the department an unpleasant place to work, with rumours and secret alliances everywhere.","He lost his job after being drawn into a web of intrigue among senior managers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"intrinsic","p":"adjective","d":"Belonging to something naturally, as an essential part of its character.","lb":"inherent, essential","s":["inherent","innate","essential","basic","fundamental","natural"],"k":["congenital","constitutional","crucial","inalienable"],"a":["external","acquired","outside","superficial"],"ex":["Gold has an intrinsic value, even if the price changes from day to day.","Students with intrinsic motivation study because they enjoy learning, not for prizes.","Trust is intrinsic to any friendship, and without it nothing lasts."],"b":146,"y":0},{"w":"introspective","p":"adjective","d":"Inclined to think carefully about your own thoughts and feelings.","lb":"reflective, thoughtful","s":["reflective","thoughtful","contemplative","pensive","meditative","brooding"],"k":["broody","dreamy","introverted","philosophical"],"a":["extroverted","outgoing","thoughtless","shallow"],"ex":["After failing the test, Rafi became quiet and introspective for several days.","She keeps an introspective diary where she writes about her fears and hopes.","The long train ride made me introspective, and I began to question my career plans."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"intuition","p":"noun","d":"A quick feeling or understanding that something is true, without needing proof or careful thought.","lb":"instinct, hunch","s":["instinct","hunch","gut feeling","sixth sense","insight","feeling"],"k":["belief","clairvoyance","feeling in your bones","foresight"],"a":["reasoning","logic","analysis","proof"],"ex":["My intuition told me something was wrong when the phone rang at midnight.","She trusted her intuition and chose the smaller company, and it paid off.","Experienced doctors often rely on intuition as well as test results."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"intuitive","p":"adjective","d":"Based on feeling or instinct rather than on facts or careful thought.","lb":"instinctive, natural","s":["instinctive","innate","natural","spontaneous","perceptive","instinctual"],"k":["congenital","emotional","gut-level","illogical"],"a":["rational","analytical","logical","calculated"],"ex":["Mothers often have an intuitive sense of when their children are unwell.","Her intuitive understanding of people made her an excellent counselor.","He made an intuitive guess that the shop would be closed, and he was right."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"inundate","p":"verb","d":"To flood a place with water, or to overwhelm someone with far too much to deal with.","lb":"flood, overwhelm","s":["flood","swamp","overwhelm","deluge","engulf","submerge"],"k":["besiege","bombard","fill","fill up"],"a":["drain","dry out"],"ex":["After the advertisement, the shop was inundated with phone calls from excited customers.","Heavy monsoon rain inundated the low-lying villages along the river.","Teachers are often inundated with homework to mark just before the holidays."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"inundated","p":"adjective","d":"Flooded with water, or overwhelmed by far more things than can be dealt with.","lb":"flooded, overwhelmed","s":["flooded","submerged","swamped","overwhelmed","deluged","engulfed"],"k":["afloat","awash","besieged","bombarded"],"a":["dry","drained","parched"],"ex":["After three days of heavy rain, the low-lying villages were inundated.","The help desk was inundated with calls on the day the results were announced.","I am inundated with homework this week and cannot go out."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"inured","p":"adjective","d":"Used to something unpleasant after experiencing it for a long time, so that it no longer troubles you.","lb":"accustomed, hardened","s":["accustomed","hardened","used","habituated","toughened","seasoned"],"k":["blunted","callous","dulled","hard"],"a":["sensitive","unaccustomed","unused","vulnerable"],"ex":["After years of load-shedding, most families are inured to the sudden dark evenings.","Doctors become inured to the sight of blood after their first year in the hospital.","News viewers can become inured to bad headlines if they see them every day."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"invalidate","p":"verb","d":"To make something, such as a ticket, an argument or a result, no longer valid or acceptable.","lb":"nullify, cancel","s":["nullify","void","cancel","annul","undermine","discredit"],"k":["avoid","negate","quash","repeal"],"a":["validate","confirm","authorize","approve"],"ex":["A single mistake on the form can invalidate your whole application.","Cheating will invalidate your test result.","If you break the seal on the box, you may invalidate the warranty."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"invective","p":"noun","d":"Angry, rude and insulting language used to attack or blame someone.","lb":"abuse, insults","s":["abuse","insults","vitriol","tirade","diatribe"],"k":["bile","broadside","contumely","harangue"],"a":["praise","compliment","flattery","tribute"],"ex":["The driver shouted a stream of invective at the rickshaw that blocked his way.","Online comment sections are often full of invective rather than honest discussion.","The coach was ashamed of the invective he had hurled at the referee after the match."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"inveterate","p":"adjective","d":"Having a habit or attitude for so long that it is very unlikely to change.","lb":"habitual, confirmed","s":["habitual","chronic","confirmed","hardened","incorrigible","entrenched"],"k":["accustomed","constant","continual","customary"],"a":["occasional","casual","infrequent","reformed"],"ex":["My uncle is an inveterate tea drinker who has at least six cups before noon.","She is an inveterate reader who carries a book wherever she goes.","Nadia is an inveterate shopper who cannot walk past a sale without buying something."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"invidious","p":"adjective","d":"Likely to cause anger or resentment because it is unfair or offensive.","lb":"unfair, resentful","s":["unfair","unjust","discriminatory","odious","objectionable","offensive"],"k":["below the belt","detestable","inequitable","obnoxious"],"a":["fair","just","impartial","equitable"],"ex":["The teacher avoided invidious comparisons between the two sisters and praised each for her own strengths.","As referee, he was in an invidious position, since any decision would anger one of the teams.","It is invidious to single out one student for praise when the whole group worked equally hard."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"inviolate","p":"adjective","d":"Not harmed, broken or disturbed; kept safe and treated as sacred.","lb":"intact, sacred","s":["intact","untouched","unbroken","sacred","pure","unspoiled"],"k":["entire","hallowed","immaculate","invulnerable"],"a":["violated","broken","damaged","breached"],"ex":["The doctor promised that her patients' secrets would remain inviolate.","Our family treats Friday dinner as an inviolate tradition.","The rules of the exam hall are inviolate; no phones are allowed under any circumstances."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"invoke","p":"verb","d":"To call on a law, rule or authority to support one's action, or to ask a higher power for help.","lb":"call upon, cite","s":["call upon","cite","appeal to","summon","conjure up","call forth"],"k":["adduce","arouse","bring up","call down"],"a":[],"ex":["The tenant invoked his legal right to a written agreement before he paid the deposit.","When the argument got heated, she invoked the club rule that no one may shout in meetings.","The accused invoked his right to remain silent until his lawyer arrived."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"ipso facto","p":"adverb","d":"Because of that very fact; as a direct and automatic result of something.","lb":"by that fact, therefore","s":["thereby","consequently","automatically","by definition","necessarily","inevitably"],"k":["accordingly","as such","ergo","for this reason"],"a":[],"ex":["Anyone who signs the form is, ipso facto, agreeing to follow the club's rules.","If you miss the deadline, you are ipso facto out of the competition.","A person who lies to a friend cannot, ipso facto, be called honest."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"irascible","p":"adjective","d":"Easily made angry, and often in a bad temper.","lb":"irritable, short-tempered","s":["irritable","bad-tempered","cranky","grumpy","testy","touchy"],"k":["angry","choleric","fractious","fussy"],"a":["calm","easygoing","placid","patient"],"ex":["Our irascible neighbor shouts at the children whenever their ball lands in his garden.","The old teacher was irascible in the mornings and much more gentle by the afternoon.","Hunger made me irascible, so I snapped at my sister for no reason."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"iridescent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing bright, shiny colours that seem to change when seen from different angles.","lb":"shimmering, rainbow-like","s":["shimmering","pearly","lustrous","glittering","bright"],"k":["changeable","chatoyant","colorful","glistening"],"a":["dull","matt","drab","plain"],"ex":["The peacock's iridescent feathers shine blue and green in the sunlight.","Soap bubbles look iridescent when light falls on them.","A dragonfly with iridescent wings rested on a lotus leaf by the pond."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ironic","p":"adjective","d":"Using words to mean the opposite of what they say, usually for humor or criticism; also, oddly different from what was expected.","lb":"sarcastic, mocking","s":["sarcastic","wry","mocking","sardonic","satirical","dry"],"k":["caustic","humorous","incongruous","scornful"],"a":["sincere","literal","straightforward","earnest"],"ex":["When the rain soaked everyone, Rafi gave an ironic cheer and said, \"What lovely weather for a picnic.\"","Her ironic tone made it clear that she did not really admire his new haircut.","The teacher's ironic comment, \"Wonderful, another early arrival,\" made the late students blush."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"irrepressible","p":"adjective","d":"Too lively or strong to be held back or controlled.","lb":"uncontainable, exuberant","s":["unstoppable","exuberant","ebullient","effervescent","unquenchable","boundless"],"k":["bubbly","buoyant","cheerful","enthusiastic"],"a":["subdued","restrained","gloomy","controlled"],"ex":["The toddler's irrepressible giggles made everyone on the bus smile.","Her irrepressible curiosity led her to take apart the old radio.","Even after the long journey, the team showed irrepressible energy on the field."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"irresolute","p":"adjective","d":"Unable to make up your mind, and uncertain or hesitating about what to do.","lb":"indecisive, hesitant","s":["indecisive","hesitant","undecided","wavering","uncertain","unsure"],"k":["discouraged","dubious","hesitating","infirm"],"a":["resolute","decisive","determined","firm"],"ex":["I stood irresolute at the bus stop, unsure whether to go home or visit my friend.","The irresolute committee delayed its decision for weeks, and the project fell behind.","She felt irresolute about changing her university subject, even after talking to three advisers."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"irreversible","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to change back or undo once it has happened.","lb":"irrevocable, permanent","s":["irrevocable","permanent","final","unalterable","irreparable","unchangeable"],"k":["durable","enduring","everlasting","fatal"],"a":["reversible","temporary","changeable","revocable"],"ex":["Cutting down the old forest caused irreversible damage to the local wildlife.","Once you delete the file from the recycle bin, the action is irreversible.","She made an irreversible decision to leave the company, so there was no turning back."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"irrevocable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to change, reverse or cancel once it has been made.","lb":"irreversible, final","s":["irreversible","final","permanent","unalterable","binding","fixed"],"k":["absolute","decisive","incontrovertible","indelible"],"a":["revocable","reversible","changeable","temporary"],"ex":["Once you submit the admission form online, the decision is irrevocable and cannot be changed.","Deleting the folder from the server is irrevocable, so please make a copy first.","The manager warned that the contract was irrevocable, so no one could back out after signing."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"itinerant","p":"adjective","d":"Travelling from place to place, especially in order to work.","lb":"travelling, wandering","s":["travelling","wandering","roving","nomadic","migrant","roaming"],"k":["drifting","footloose","migratory","mobile"],"a":["settled","stationary","sedentary","resident"],"ex":["Itinerant workers move from farm to farm during the harvest season in search of work.","An itinerant tailor visits our village once a month, carrying his sewing machine on a bicycle.","The circus's itinerant life meant the children changed schools every few months."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"itinerary","p":"noun","d":"A detailed plan of a journey, listing the places to visit and the times.","lb":"travel plan, schedule","s":["schedule","route","travel plan","program","timetable","tour"],"k":["calendar","direction","line","path"],"a":[],"ex":["Our itinerary for the trip to Cox's Bazar includes two nights at a hotel near the beach.","The travel agent emailed us a full itinerary with flight times and hotel addresses.","I shared my itinerary with my parents so they would know where I was each day."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"jaunt","p":"noun","d":"A short trip taken for pleasure, usually lasting only a few hours or a day.","lb":"short trip, outing","s":["outing","excursion","trip","expedition","tour","ramble"],"k":["amble","journeying","joyride","junket"],"a":[],"ex":["After the final exam, we took a weekend jaunt to Cox's Bazar to celebrate.","Our family enjoys a short Sunday jaunt to the lake park, with snacks and a ball.","A jaunt through the old city is a pleasant way to spend a free afternoon."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"jeopardize","p":"verb","d":"To put something or someone in a situation where it may be harmed, damaged or lost.","lb":"endanger, risk","s":["endanger","risk","imperil","threaten","compromise","hazard"],"k":["be","exist","gamble","menace"],"a":["protect","safeguard","secure","defend"],"ex":["Missing the deadline could jeopardize your chance of getting the scholarship.","Smoking can jeopardize your health long before you notice any symptoms.","Loud arguments in front of clients may jeopardize the deal."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"jingoism","p":"noun","d":"Extreme, aggressive patriotism, especially a readiness to support hostility toward other countries.","lb":"chauvinism, patriotism","s":["chauvinism","nationalism","militarism","xenophobia","patriotism"],"k":["bellicism","belligerence","bigotry","flag waving"],"a":["pacifism"],"ex":["The newspaper's jingoism, with its constant attacks on foreign countries, made many readers uneasy.","Some commentators warned that jingoism before the match was turning a friendly game into a hostile contest.","Teachers worry that textbooks full of jingoism teach students to dislike other nations."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"jocular","p":"adjective","d":"Fond of joking, or said in a playful and humorous way.","lb":"humorous, playful","s":["humorous","joking","playful","jovial","witty","jolly"],"k":["comical","entertaining","funny","jesting"],"a":["serious","solemn","humorless","grave"],"ex":["In a jocular tone, he told the waiter that the soup was too hot to handle.","Our jocular uncle makes the whole family laugh at every wedding.","The manager's jocular remark about Monday mornings relaxed the tired team."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"joie de vivre","p":"noun","d":"A cheerful enjoyment of life; great zest for living.","lb":"zest, exuberance","s":["zest","exuberance","enthusiasm","high spirits","vitality","gusto"],"k":["bonhomie","buoyancy","elan","enjoyment"],"a":["apathy","gloom","melancholy","despondency"],"ex":["Even at eighty, my grandmother has so much joie de vivre that she dances at weddings.","The street musician played with such joie de vivre that passers-by stopped to clap.","The painting is full of bright colors and joie de vivre."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"jubilation","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of great happiness and excitement, especially because of a success.","lb":"joy, elation","s":["joy","elation","exultation","triumph","glee","rejoicing"],"k":["bliss","cheering","festivity","gaiety"],"a":["sorrow","misery","gloom","despair"],"ex":["There was wild jubilation in the streets when the national team won the match.","She hugged her mother in jubilation when she saw her name on the admission list.","A shout of jubilation went up from the office when the contract was signed."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"judicious","p":"adjective","d":"Showing good judgment and careful thought, especially when making a decision or choosing how to act.","lb":"wise, sensible","s":["wise","sensible","prudent","sound","shrewd","discerning"],"k":["canny","circumspect","considered","discreet"],"a":["unwise","foolish","rash","imprudent"],"ex":["A judicious use of her savings helped Nadia pay for university without taking a loan.","The coach made a judicious decision to rest the injured player before the final.","It would be judicious to check the weather forecast before planning a picnic by the river."],"b":90,"y":1},{"w":"jumbled","p":"adjective","d":"Mixed together in a confused, untidy way, with no clear order.","lb":"mixed up, disordered","s":["muddled","disordered","tangled","confused","chaotic","messy"],"k":["befuddled","disjointed","disorderly","disorganized"],"a":["organized","orderly","neat","tidy"],"ex":["My notes were so jumbled that I could not find the formula.","A jumbled pile of shoes lay near the door of the prayer hall.","The jumbled letters on the card spelled a word when arranged properly."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"junction","p":"noun","d":"A point where two or more things, such as roads, railway lines or rivers, meet or join.","lb":"crossing, meeting point","s":["intersection","crossing","meeting point","convergence","confluence","crossroads"],"k":["articulation","conjunction","crossroad","fork"],"a":[],"ex":["Turn left at the next junction and you will see the bus stand.","The train waited at the junction for twenty minutes because of a signal fault.","Traffic builds up at the busy junction in the center of Dhaka every evening."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"junta","p":"noun","d":"A small group, usually of army officers, that rules a country after taking power by force.","lb":"military rulers, regime","s":["clique","cabal","regime","faction","council","military government"],"k":["camarilla","camp","circle","coterie"],"a":[],"ex":["After the coup, a junta of army officers took over the government and closed the airports.","The country was ruled by a military junta for almost ten years before holding elections.","In history class, we studied how the junta banned newspapers and public meetings."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"juxtapose","p":"verb","d":"To place two things close together so that their differences or similarities become clear.","lb":"compare, contrast","s":["contrast","compare","set side by side","set against","pair","line up"],"k":["align","bring together","collate","confront"],"a":["separate","isolate","divide"],"ex":["The photographer juxtaposed a luxury car with a rickshaw to show the contrast on Dhaka's streets.","The museum juxtaposes old maps with satellite images so visitors can see how the coastline has changed.","In the essay, she juxtaposed her grandmother's village childhood with her own life in the city."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"kernel","p":"noun","d":"The soft, edible part inside the hard shell of a nut or fruit stone.","lb":"seed, core","s":["seed","nut","core","heart","pip"],"k":["center","cognitive content","content","crux"],"a":[],"ex":["Crack the shell carefully, because the almond kernel inside breaks easily.","In the hot pan, every kernel of corn popped one after another.","Allergy warnings on the packet mention walnut kernels, so he put it back on the shelf."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"kindle","p":"verb","d":"To start a fire burning, or to arouse a feeling or interest in someone.","lb":"ignite, arouse","s":["ignite","light","spark","arouse","stir","awaken"],"k":["activate","elicit","inflame","provoke"],"a":["extinguish","douse","quench","smother"],"ex":["We kindled a small fire with dry twigs and leaves to boil water for tea.","A good teacher can kindle a lifelong interest in science with a single experiment.","Her kind words kindled new hope in the worried family."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"kinetic","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to, or produced by, movement.","lb":"moving, motion-related","s":["moving","dynamic","active","energetic","mobile"],"k":["animated","driving","energizing","lively"],"a":["static","stationary","motionless","inert"],"ex":["A fast-moving cricket ball has a lot of kinetic energy, which is why it can hurt your hand.","In physics class, we calculated the kinetic energy of a falling stone.","The artist's kinetic sculpture spins slowly in the wind and changes shape as it turns."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"kinship","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of close connection with people because of shared family, interests or character.","lb":"affinity, bond","s":["affinity","bond","relationship","closeness","connection","family ties"],"k":["alliance","association","brotherhood","camaraderie"],"a":["estrangement","alienation","distance","separation"],"ex":["Strangers on the long train journey felt a sudden kinship after sharing food.","In many villages, kinship ties decide who helps whom during the harvest.","She felt a deep kinship with other students who had come to the city from small towns."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"labyrinth","p":"noun","d":"A complicated network of paths or passages where it is easy to get lost.","lb":"maze, tangle","s":["maze","warren","network","tangle","web","jungle"],"k":["inner ear","internal ear","snarl","structure"],"a":[],"ex":["The narrow alleys of Old Dhaka form a labyrinth that confuses every first-time visitor.","Visitors paid to walk through a hedge labyrinth in the garden and find the center.","The airport was such a labyrinth of corridors that we nearly missed our flight."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"lackadaisical","p":"adjective","d":"Showing little interest, effort or energy in what you are doing.","lb":"careless, listless","s":["listless","apathetic","careless","lazy","languid","indifferent"],"k":["casual","dreamy","drowsy","idle"],"a":["energetic","enthusiastic","keen","diligent"],"ex":["His lackadaisical attitude towards revision worried his parents.","The waiter's lackadaisical service made us wait forty minutes for tea.","A lackadaisical effort in the first half cost the team the match."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"lackluster","p":"adjective","d":"Not exciting or impressive; lacking energy, brightness or enthusiasm.","lb":"dull, uninspired","s":["dull","uninspired","mediocre","flat","lifeless","drab"],"k":["boring","dim","dreary","lusterless"],"a":["brilliant","exciting","dazzling","vibrant"],"ex":["The team gave a lackluster performance and lost the match by three goals.","Sales were lackluster during the holidays because customers were spending less money.","Her lackluster reply made it clear she had no interest in the job."],"b":66,"y":2},{"w":"laconic","p":"adjective","d":"Using very few words when speaking or writing.","lb":"brief, terse","s":["terse","concise","brief","curt","succinct","pithy"],"k":["abrupt","blunt","clipped","compact"],"a":["wordy","verbose","talkative","chatty"],"ex":["When I asked how the exam went, his laconic reply was, “Fine.”","My laconic grandfather answers most questions with just a nod or a single word.","Her laconic text messages never contain more than three or four words."],"b":539,"y":0},{"w":"laissez-faire","p":"noun","d":"A policy of letting things develop freely with little control, especially by government in the economy.","lb":"non-interference","s":["free enterprise","free market","deregulation"],"k":["capitalist","economic liberalism","free rein","libertarianism"],"a":["intervention","regulation","interference","control"],"ex":["Supporters of laissez-faire argue that markets set fairer prices than officials can.","Critics say the government's laissez-faire toward the housing market let rents rise unchecked.","The manager's laissez-faire left the team without direction, and deadlines kept slipping."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"lament","p":"verb","d":"To express deep sadness or regret about something, often by saying so openly.","lb":"mourn, regret","s":["mourn","grieve","bemoan","regret","deplore","weep"],"k":["ache","cry","fret","grieve over"],"a":["rejoice","celebrate","exult","applaud"],"ex":["Many older residents lament the loss of the old tea stall at the corner.","Shoppers lament that prices keep rising while salaries stay the same.","She lamented the missed chance to study abroad and wondered if she should have applied earlier."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"lampoon","p":"verb","d":"To make fun of a person or idea in public, usually in a clever and exaggerated way.","lb":"mock, satirize","s":["mock","ridicule","parody","caricature","spoof","send up"],"k":["belittle","laugh at","scoff at","sneer at"],"a":["praise","flatter","honor","glorify"],"ex":["The student magazine lampooned the long cafeteria queues in a funny cartoon series.","A TV comedy show lampoons the way people behave in traffic jams.","Her brother lampooned their father's habit of narrating every cricket match by imitating him at dinner."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"languish","p":"verb","d":"To lose strength or energy and fail to make progress, especially in an unpleasant situation that lasts a long time.","lb":"weaken, waste away","s":["wither","decline","waste away","fade","flag","droop"],"k":["ache","diminish","hanker","pine away"],"a":["thrive","flourish","prosper","bloom"],"ex":["The files languished in a drawer for months because nobody had time to read them.","Without sunlight and water, the plants on the balcony began to languish.","Many talented young people languish in jobs that do not use their skills."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"lapse","p":"noun","d":"A small mistake or failure caused by a short loss of attention, memory or self-control.","lb":"slip, mistake","s":["slip","mistake","error","oversight","failure","blunder"],"k":["backsliding","blip","boo-boo","faux pas"],"a":[],"ex":["A brief lapse in concentration caused the driver to miss his exit.","I had a memory lapse during the speech and forgot my second point.","The bank blamed the error on a lapse in its security checks."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"larceny","p":"noun","d":"The crime of stealing someone else's property.","lb":"theft, stealing","s":["theft","stealing","thievery","robbery","pilferage","burglary"],"k":["embezzlement","felony","filching","peculation"],"a":[],"ex":["The young man was charged with larceny after taking a bicycle that did not belong to him.","In law class, we learned the difference between larceny and robbery, which involves force.","Stealing a wallet from a bag on a crowded bus counts as larceny."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"largess","p":"noun","d":"Generous giving of money or gifts to others, or the gifts themselves.","lb":"generosity, gifts","s":["generosity","bounty","charity","donations","gifts","handouts"],"k":["alms","beneficence","magnanimity","open-handedness"],"a":["stinginess","greed","meanness","selfishness"],"ex":["Thanks to the largess of an anonymous donor, the school library bought two hundred new books.","The wealthy uncle distributed largess to all the cousins every Eid.","The festival depends on the largess of local shopkeepers who donate food and decorations."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"lascivious","p":"adjective","d":"Showing an unpleasant, open interest in sex in a way that offends other people.","lb":"lewd, indecent","s":["lewd","lustful","lecherous","indecent","obscene","salacious"],"k":["dirty","libidinous","prurient","raunchy"],"a":["chaste","decent","modest","pure"],"ex":["The film was heavily criticised for its lascivious jokes and was banned from school screenings.","The manager's lascivious comments made the new employee uncomfortable, so she reported him to the company.","Teachers asked the students to report any lascivious messages they received from strangers online."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"lassitude","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of being very tired and weak, with no energy or interest in doing anything.","lb":"weariness, fatigue","s":["weariness","fatigue","lethargy","languor","exhaustion","torpor"],"k":["debility","enervation","faintness","feebleness"],"a":["energy","vigor","vitality","enthusiasm"],"ex":["A strange lassitude after the fever kept her in bed for three more days.","The summer heat brought a feeling of lassitude, and no one wanted to move.","After the exams ended, a deep lassitude settled over the whole class."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"latent","p":"adjective","d":"Existing but not yet active, visible or developed.","lb":"dormant, hidden","s":["dormant","hidden","potential","concealed","undeveloped","inactive"],"k":["covert","idle","incipient","inert"],"a":["active","apparent","obvious","visible"],"ex":["The teacher believed every child has latent talent that only needs a chance to show.","The virus can stay latent in the body for years before it causes any symptoms.","Her latent fear of water returned when we boarded the small boat."],"b":85,"y":1},{"w":"laud","p":"verb","d":"To praise someone or something highly, often in public.","lb":"praise, applaud","s":["praise","applaud","commend","acclaim","extol","celebrate"],"k":["cheer","congratulate","eulogize","exalt"],"a":["criticize","condemn","censure","belittle"],"ex":["The newspaper lauded the young scientist for her simple and cheap water filter.","Teachers lauded the class for raising money to help the flood victims.","Critics lauded the new film as a fresh and honest story about family life."],"b":81,"y":1},{"w":"lavish","p":"adjective","d":"Very generous, rich or expensive, and often more than is really necessary.","lb":"extravagant, generous","s":["extravagant","opulent","sumptuous","luxurious","generous","abundant"],"k":["ample","bountiful","deluxe","munificent"],"a":["frugal","meager","stingy","sparing"],"ex":["The wedding was a lavish event, with hundreds of guests and ten kinds of dishes.","Her uncle is known for his lavish gifts, especially during Eid.","The hotel lobby has lavish decorations, including gold lamps and a huge crystal chandelier."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"lax","p":"adjective","d":"Not strict, careful or firm enough about rules or standards.","lb":"careless, slack","s":["slack","careless","negligent","lenient","loose","remiss"],"k":["baggy","drooping","droopy","floppy"],"a":["strict","rigorous","stringent","firm"],"ex":["The airport was criticised for lax security after a visitor walked through a gate unchecked.","Our teacher is lax about deadlines, so many students hand in their work late.","A lax attitude to hygiene in the kitchen can make customers ill."],"b":44,"y":0},{"w":"layman","p":"noun","d":"A person who does not have professional or specialist knowledge of a subject.","lb":"non-expert, amateur","s":["amateur","outsider","novice","layperson","secular"],"k":["beginner","common man","common person","commoner"],"a":["expert","specialist","professional","authority"],"ex":["The doctor explained the test results in simple words that any layman could understand.","As a layman, I find legal contracts almost impossible to follow.","Even a layman could see that the old wall was cracked and unsafe."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"legacy","p":"noun","d":"Something valuable or important that a person or the past leaves for those who come after.","lb":"inheritance, heritage","s":["inheritance","bequest","heritage","birthright","endowment","tradition"],"k":["aftermath","donation","estate","footprint"],"a":[],"ex":["My grandfather’s legacy was not money but a love of reading that he passed to all his grandchildren.","The old library is a lasting legacy of the town’s first teacher.","She hopes to leave a legacy of clean rivers for the children of tomorrow."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"lethargic","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling very tired and slow, with no energy or wish to do anything.","lb":"sluggish, drowsy","s":["sluggish","drowsy","listless","torpid","tired","languid"],"k":["dazed","dreamy","dull","foggy"],"a":["energetic","lively","alert","active"],"ex":["After a heavy lunch of biryani, everyone in the office felt lethargic.","The fever left the child lethargic and unwilling to play.","Staying up late every night makes me lethargic during morning lectures."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"lethargy","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of being very tired, slow and without energy or interest.","lb":"sluggishness, tiredness","s":["torpor","drowsiness","apathy","inertia","languor","fatigue"],"k":["dormancy","dullness","flatness","inactivity"],"a":["energy","vigor","vitality","alertness"],"ex":["A heavy lunch in the afternoon heat can fill the whole class with lethargy.","Doctors say constant tiredness and lethargy can be signs of low iron.","After weeks of rain, a feeling of lethargy settled over the town."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"levee","p":"noun","d":"A long wall or bank built beside a river to stop it from flooding the land.","lb":"embankment, flood bank","s":["embankment","dike","dyke","flood bank","bank","barrier"],"k":["berm","breakwater","bund","butch"],"a":[],"ex":["Villagers worked all night to strengthen the levee before the river rose any further.","The levee broke during the storm, and water poured into the nearby fields.","Children fly kites on the grassy levee along the river every evening."],"b":9,"y":0},{"w":"levity","p":"noun","d":"Humor or lightness in a situation where a serious attitude would be more suitable.","lb":"humor, frivolity","s":["frivolity","humor","silliness","jocularity","playfulness","giddiness"],"k":["badinage","banter","gaiety","jest"],"a":["seriousness","gravity","solemnity","earnestness"],"ex":["The teacher's joke added a moment of levity to a long and tense exam briefing.","Some guests felt his levity at the memorial was disrespectful.","A little levity can help calm a nervous team before an important match."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"lexicon","p":"noun","d":"All the words and phrases used in a language, a subject or by a particular person.","lb":"vocabulary, word stock","s":["vocabulary","dictionary","terminology","word list","word stock"],"k":["idiolect","lingo","nomenclature","sociolect"],"a":[],"ex":["The word 'selfie' entered the English lexicon only a few years ago.","Every profession has its own lexicon that outsiders find hard to follow.","Reading widely is the best way to grow your personal lexicon."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"liaison","p":"noun","d":"A link or connection that allows two groups to share information and work together.","lb":"link, contact","s":["link","contact","connection","communication","cooperation","intermediary"],"k":["affair","association","bridge","broker"],"a":["separation","isolation","disconnection","estrangement"],"ex":["The hospital works in close liaison with local clinics to track disease outbreaks.","Nadia acts as the liaison between the engineers and the sales team.","A police liaison visits the school every month to talk about road safety."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"libel","p":"noun","d":"A false written or published statement that damages a person's reputation.","lb":"defamation, slander","s":["defamation","slander","smear","calumny","character assassination","aspersion"],"k":["disparagement","distortion","fabrication","falsehood"],"a":["praise","commendation","tribute"],"ex":["The actor sued the magazine for libel after it printed a false story about his family.","Posting false accusations about a classmate online can be considered libel.","The newspaper apologized and paid damages after the court found the article to be libel."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"licentious","p":"adjective","d":"Showing no moral restraint, especially in sexual behaviour, and ignoring accepted standards of decency.","lb":"immoral, dissolute","s":["dissolute","immoral","debauched","depraved","wanton","libertine"],"k":["bawdy","corrupt","degraded","dissipated"],"a":["chaste","virtuous","moral","restrained"],"ex":["The preacher warned the townspeople against a licentious life of wild parties and wasted money.","Historians describe the king's licentious court as a sign that the kingdom was losing its way.","The novel follows a licentious aristocrat whose reckless pleasures slowly destroy his family."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"ligneous","p":"adjective","d":"Made of wood or woody in texture.","lb":"woody, wooden","s":["woody","wooden","timber","tough","fibrous"],"k":["arboreal","cellulosic","lignified","stiff"],"a":["soft","fleshy","green"],"ex":["Bushes like roses have ligneous stems that become hard and brown with age.","The ligneous part of a plant, called wood, supports the whole tree.","A ligneous root is too tough to eat, even after long cooking."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"limpid","p":"adjective","d":"Completely clear and easy to see through; also clear and easy to understand.","lb":"clear, transparent","s":["clear","transparent","translucent","pellucid","lucid","pure"],"k":["bright","crystal clear","crystalline","glassy"],"a":["cloudy","murky","opaque","muddy"],"ex":["The mountain stream was so limpid that we could count the pebbles at the bottom.","The baby looked up with limpid eyes and smiled at the stranger.","The professor's limpid explanation made a hard theory seem simple."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"listless","p":"adjective","d":"Having no energy or interest; tired and uninterested in doing anything.","lb":"lethargic, apathetic","s":["lethargic","apathetic","languid","sluggish","lifeless","indifferent"],"k":["dispirited","dull","enervated","heavy-eyed"],"a":["energetic","lively","spirited","animated"],"ex":["The hot, humid afternoon made everyone listless, and the class barely listened to the lesson.","She felt listless after a week of fever and did not want to leave her bed.","The listless crowd watched the dull match in silence."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"litany","p":"noun","d":"A long, boring list of complaints, problems or mistakes that someone repeats.","lb":"long list, tedious recital","s":["list","catalog","recital","string","series","rundown"],"k":["drone","mantra","rehash","rigmarole"],"a":[],"ex":["My uncle delivered a litany of complaints about the food, the music and the long speeches at the wedding.","The report offers a litany of failures, from late buses to broken ticket machines.","She listened to his litany of excuses and then asked him to just apologize."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"litigate","p":"verb","d":"To take a disagreement to court, or to be involved in a legal case.","lb":"sue, go to court","s":["sue","contest","take to court","bring suit","go to law","dispute"],"k":["arraign","bring charges","charge","indict"],"a":["settle","compromise","mediate","reconcile"],"ex":["The two brothers decided to litigate over their father's land instead of talking it through.","Small businesses often cannot afford to litigate against large companies.","She hired a lawyer to litigate the dispute with her landlord."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"litter","p":"noun","d":"Rubbish such as paper, bottles and wrappers that people carelessly leave on the ground in public places.","lb":"rubbish, trash","s":["rubbish","trash","garbage","waste","debris","refuse"],"k":["bedding","bedding material","clutter","detritus"],"a":[],"ex":["The park was covered with litter after the weekend picnic.","Please put your litter in the bin instead of dropping it on the pavement.","Volunteers spent the morning picking up litter along the riverbank."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"lively","p":"adjective","d":"Full of energy, enthusiasm and activity.","lb":"energetic, spirited","s":["energetic","spirited","animated","vivacious","vibrant","active"],"k":["alert","alive","boisterous","bouncing"],"a":["dull","lifeless","sluggish","listless"],"ex":["The lively market was full of shouting sellers, bright colours and music.","We had a lively discussion in class about the new school rules.","My lively grandmother still walks two kilometres every morning."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"livid","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely angry, often showing it clearly in your face or voice.","lb":"furious, enraged","s":["furious","enraged","irate","fuming","incensed","seething"],"k":["angered","angry","ashen","ballistic"],"a":["calm","pleased","happy","delighted"],"ex":["My father was livid when he found out I had skipped class to watch the match.","The customer was livid after waiting two hours for a meal that never arrived.","Rafi was livid at his teammate for missing the easy catch in the final over."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"loath","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling or reluctant to do something.","lb":"reluctant, unwilling","s":["reluctant","unwilling","averse","disinclined","hesitant","resistant"],"k":["backward","chary","dubious","indisposed"],"a":["willing","eager","keen","ready"],"ex":["I am loath to leave the house in this heavy rain.","He was loath to ask for help, even though the work was too heavy.","The shopkeeper was loath to lower his prices because costs had gone up."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"loathe","p":"verb","d":"To hate someone or something very strongly.","lb":"hate, detest","s":["hate","detest","despise","abhor","abominate","dislike"],"k":["recoil from","resent","revile","scorn"],"a":["love","adore","like","cherish"],"ex":["I loathe waking up early on cold winter mornings.","My little brother loathes bitter gourd and hides it under his rice.","She loathes traffic so much that she walks to work whenever she can."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"loathsome","p":"adjective","d":"So unpleasant or offensive that it causes strong hatred or disgust.","lb":"detestable, vile","s":["detestable","hateful","vile","repulsive","revolting","odious"],"k":["abhorrent","disgusting","distasteful","execrable"],"a":["lovable","delightful","pleasant","admirable"],"ex":["Cheating in exams is a loathsome habit that ruins a student's reputation.","I find the loathsome smell of rotting fish in the market almost unbearable.","The villain in the drama was so loathsome that the audience booed him."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"lobby","p":"verb","d":"To try to persuade politicians or officials to support a law, policy or decision you want.","lb":"campaign, push","s":["campaign","press","push","petition","persuade","urge"],"k":["beg","buttonhole","drive","shove"],"a":[],"ex":["Teachers have been lobbying the education ministry for better pay and smaller classes.","Residents lobbied the city council for months to build a footbridge across the busy road.","A group of students lobbied the principal to keep the library open until ten at night."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"lobbyist","p":"noun","d":"A person who is paid to try to persuade politicians or officials to support a particular law or policy.","lb":"advocate, campaigner","s":["advocate","campaigner","persuader","spokesperson","promoter","agent"],"k":["fixer","go-between","inducer","influence peddler"],"a":[],"ex":["A lobbyist for the farmers met officials to ask for cheaper fertiliser.","The lobbyist explained why the new safety law would help small businesses.","Health groups hired a lobbyist to push for clearer labels on food packaging."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"log","p":"verb","d":"To write down or record facts, events or times officially or regularly, in a book or on a computer.","lb":"record, note","s":["record","note","register","enter","chart","document"],"k":["clock up","enroll","log up","lumber"],"a":["delete","erase","omit","ignore"],"ex":["Pilots must log every flight in a book so the airline can check their hours.","I log my study hours in an app to see how much I really revise.","The nurse logged the patient's temperature every two hours during the night."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"loquacious","p":"adjective","d":"Talking a lot, especially in a lively and enthusiastic way.","lb":"talkative, chatty","s":["talkative","chatty","garrulous","voluble","verbose","wordy"],"k":["effusive","expansive","glib","gushing"],"a":["taciturn","quiet","silent","reserved"],"ex":["My loquacious aunt can talk for an hour about a single wedding invitation.","The taxi driver was so loquacious that I knew his whole family history before we arrived.","Normally shy, Rafi became loquacious once the conversation turned to cricket."],"b":531,"y":0},{"w":"lout","p":"noun","d":"A rude, rough and badly behaved man or boy.","lb":"boor, oaf","s":["boor","oaf","yob","brute","ruffian","clod"],"k":["bounder","bully","churl","clumsy person"],"a":["gentleman","aristocrat"],"ex":["A group of louts shouted rude jokes at passers-by outside the tea stall.","He behaved like a lout at the wedding, pushing past guests to get to the food.","Don’t be such a lout; hold the door for the elderly lady."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"lucid","p":"adjective","d":"Clearly expressed and easy to understand, or able to think in a clear, sensible way.","lb":"clear, understandable","s":["clear","understandable","comprehensible","intelligible","plain","coherent"],"k":["accessible","crystal clear","crystalline","distinct"],"a":["unclear","confusing","obscure","vague"],"ex":["The teacher gave a lucid explanation of the problem, and everyone finally understood it.","Her lucid writing makes complicated science easy for ordinary readers.","The lawyer gave a lucid summary of the contract, so my parents knew exactly what they were signing."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"ludicrous","p":"adjective","d":"So silly or unreasonable that it makes people laugh or refuse to take it seriously.","lb":"absurd, ridiculous","s":["ridiculous","absurd","laughable","preposterous","silly","farcical"],"k":["amusing","cockeyed","comic","foolish"],"a":["sensible","reasonable","logical","sane"],"ex":["It is ludicrous to expect one cleaner to look after the whole six-storey building.","The idea that you can learn a language in one week is ludicrous.","He looked ludicrous in his father's oversized suit."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"lugubrious","p":"adjective","d":"Looking or sounding very sad and serious, sometimes in an exaggerated way.","lb":"gloomy, mournful","s":["mournful","gloomy","sorrowful","doleful","melancholy","woeful"],"k":["bleak","dark","downcast","drab"],"a":["cheerful","joyful","merry","jolly"],"ex":["He gave a lugubrious sigh when he saw the pile of homework waiting for him.","The lugubrious music made the quiet street feel even sadder on the rainy evening.","With a lugubrious face, the shopkeeper told us the price of onions had doubled again."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"luminous","p":"adjective","d":"Giving out or reflecting light, so that it shines or glows, especially in the dark.","lb":"shining, glowing","s":["shining","glowing","bright","radiant","brilliant","lustrous"],"k":["aglow","dazzling","effulgent","fluorescent"],"a":["dark","dull","dim","murky"],"ex":["The luminous dial of my grandfather's watch glowed softly in the dark bedroom.","Children stuck luminous stars on the ceiling so their room shone at night.","A luminous full moon rose over the river and lit up the whole boat."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"lyrical","p":"adjective","d":"Expressing strong feeling in a beautiful, poetic way, like a song.","lb":"poetic, musical","s":["poetic","musical","melodious","expressive","emotional","flowing"],"k":["elegiac","euphonious","evocative","harmonious"],"a":["prosaic","dull","flat","plain"],"ex":["The novel is written in lyrical prose that describes the monsoon like a song.","Her lyrical voice made even a simple lullaby sound magical.","He waxed lyrical about his mother’s cooking, praising every dish on the table."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"macabre","p":"adjective","d":"Disturbing and frightening because it involves death, decay or horror.","lb":"gruesome, eerie","s":["gruesome","grisly","ghastly","eerie","morbid","grim"],"k":["alarming","appalling","bloodcurdling","creepy"],"a":["cheerful","pleasant","delightful","lighthearted"],"ex":["The museum's macabre display of old surgical tools made some visitors feel faint.","She enjoys macabre stories about haunted houses and graveyards.","Police made a macabre discovery of old bones buried in the garden."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"machinate","p":"verb","d":"To secretly make clever, harmful plans, especially to gain power or to hurt someone.","lb":"plot, scheme","s":["plot","scheme","conspire","intrigue","contrive","connive"],"k":["collude","conjure","design","devise"],"a":[],"ex":["Two jealous employees machinated to get their colleague fired before the promotion.","In the novel, the minister machinates behind the scenes to take control of the company.","He spent months machinating against his cousin to win control of the family shop."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"machination","p":"noun","d":"A secret, clever plan made to gain power or to harm someone.","lb":"scheming, plot","s":["plot","scheme","intrigue","conspiracy","ploy","maneuver"],"k":["collusion","connivance","double-dealing","gambit"],"a":[],"ex":["The family lost the old land through the machinations of a greedy cousin.","She discovered the machinations of a colleague who was secretly trying to take her job.","The novel follows a clerk who survives the machinations of his scheming bosses."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"magnanimity","p":"noun","d":"Generous and forgiving behavior toward other people, especially toward a rival or someone who has wronged you.","lb":"generosity, nobility","s":["generosity","nobility","charity","benevolence","kindness","graciousness"],"k":["chivalry","clemency","forbearance","largess"],"a":["pettiness","meanness","spite","selfishness"],"ex":["The winning team showed magnanimity by praising their opponents' brave effort.","Her magnanimity amazed us, because she forgave her cousin and even helped pay his debt.","The shopkeeper's magnanimity during Eid, giving free sweets to poor children, was talked about for weeks."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"magnanimous","p":"adjective","d":"Generous and forgiving, especially toward a rival or someone who has treated you badly.","lb":"generous, forgiving","s":["generous","forgiving","noble","charitable","gracious","benevolent"],"k":["big","bountiful","chivalrous","clement"],"a":["petty","spiteful","vindictive","mean"],"ex":["The winning team was magnanimous and praised its opponents for playing so well.","My boss was magnanimous about my mistake and simply asked me to be more careful.","In a magnanimous gesture, she invited the classmate who had insulted her to her birthday party."],"b":84,"y":2},{"w":"magnate","p":"noun","d":"A very rich and powerful person in business or industry.","lb":"tycoon, business leader","s":["tycoon","mogul","baron","industrialist","financier","captain of industry"],"k":["big businessman","business leader","businessman","king"],"a":[],"ex":["The shipping magnate donated a new wing to the city hospital.","A textile magnate opened three new factories last year, creating thousands of jobs.","She dreams of becoming a business magnate who builds her own chain of bookshops."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"malady","p":"noun","d":"A disease or illness, or a serious problem that affects a person, a group or society.","lb":"illness, ailment","s":["illness","ailment","disease","disorder","sickness","affliction"],"k":["bane","blight","contagion","curse"],"a":["health","wellness","fitness"],"ex":["The doctor could not name the strange malady that kept the child weak for months.","Corruption is a malady that slowly weakens public trust in every institution.","My grandfather's old malady returns every winter, leaving his joints swollen and stiff."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"malaise","p":"noun","d":"A vague feeling of being unwell, unhappy or uneasy.","lb":"unease, discomfort","s":["unease","discomfort","weariness","depression","sickness","anxiety"],"k":["angst","blues","dissatisfaction","doldrums"],"a":["health","vigor","contentment","comfort"],"ex":["A strange malaise kept her in bed all weekend, though she had no fever.","Many office workers feel a general malaise during the gray days of winter.","The long power cuts brought a mood of malaise to the neighborhood."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"malapropism","p":"noun","d":"The mistake of using a wrong word that sounds like the right one, often with a funny result.","lb":"wrong word","s":["verbal slip","slip of the tongue","wrong word","solecism","verbal blunder","misuse"],"k":["eggcorn","howler","misnomer","mondegreen"],"a":[],"ex":["We laughed at the malapropism when my aunt said the doctor had given her a perspiration instead of a prescription.","The sitcom's landlady is famous for her malapropisms, such as calling a respected neighbour a pillow of the community.","A malapropism slipped into his speech when he called the guests very hostile instead of hospitable."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"malevolent","p":"adjective","d":"Wishing harm to other people; showing a desire to do evil.","lb":"spiteful, hostile","s":["malicious","spiteful","hostile","evil","vicious","malign"],"k":["baleful","bitter","ill-willed","maleficent"],"a":["benevolent","kind","friendly","kindly"],"ex":["The villain in the film has a malevolent smile that frightens children.","A malevolent rumour spread through the office and ruined her reputation.","The old neighbour gave us a malevolent look whenever our ball landed in her garden."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"malfeasance","p":"noun","d":"Illegal or dishonest behavior by a public official or by someone in a position of trust.","lb":"misconduct, wrongdoing","s":["misconduct","wrongdoing","corruption","malpractice","graft","abuse of office"],"k":["bribery","defalcation","delinquency","dereliction"],"a":["integrity","honesty","probity"],"ex":["The auditor discovered financial malfeasance in the city office, including payments to workers who did not exist.","The council member resigned after accusations of malfeasance in awarding road contracts.","Workers who report malfeasance should be protected from losing their jobs."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"malignant","p":"adjective","d":"Harmful or dangerous, especially of a tumor that grows uncontrollably, or of a person who wishes to harm others.","lb":"harmful, cancerous","s":["harmful","cancerous","deadly","destructive","evil","malevolent"],"k":["bitter","damaging","injurious","malicious"],"a":["benign","harmless","kind","benevolent"],"ex":["The biopsy showed that the lump was malignant, so the doctors began treatment immediately.","A malignant tumor can spread to other parts of the body if it is not removed early.","His malignant gossip poisoned the friendship between the two sisters."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"malinger","p":"verb","d":"To pretend to be ill or hurt in order to avoid work or duty.","lb":"fake illness, shirk","s":["shirk","slack off","feign illness","fake","dodge","pretend"],"k":["bluff","dissemble","fiddle","goldbrick"],"a":[],"ex":["He was malingering when he said his back hurt, because he walked normally as soon as the boss left.","The doctor suspected that the student was malingering to avoid the exam.","Employees who malinger put extra work on their honest colleagues."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"malingerer","p":"noun","d":"A person who pretends to be ill or hurt in order to avoid work or duty.","lb":"shirker, faker","s":["shirker","slacker","dodger","loafer","goldbrick","faker"],"k":["deadbeat","good-for-nothing","layabout","lounge lizard"],"a":[],"ex":["The coach suspected that Rafi was a malingerer when he limped only during running practice.","Doctors can usually tell a real fever from a malingerer's story.","The manager called him a malingerer after he took a sick day every Monday."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"malleable","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be hammered or pressed into shape without breaking, or easy to influence and change.","lb":"pliable, adaptable","s":["pliable","flexible","workable","plastic","supple","adaptable"],"k":["adjustable","compliant","docile","elastic"],"a":["rigid","brittle","stiff","inflexible"],"ex":["Gold is so malleable that it can be hammered into very thin sheets.","Warm clay is malleable, so children can easily shape it into animals and bowls.","Young children's minds are malleable, which is why good role models matter so much."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"mammoth","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely large; very big in size, amount or effort.","lb":"huge, gigantic","s":["huge","enormous","gigantic","colossal","massive","immense"],"k":["big","large","titanic","towering"],"a":["tiny","small","minute","miniature"],"ex":["Cleaning the whole house before Eid was a mammoth task for the family.","The store announced a mammoth discount sale that drew thousands of shoppers.","A mammoth wave knocked the small fishing boat off its course."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mandate","p":"noun","d":"An official order or authority to do something, especially the authority given to a leader or group by voters.","lb":"authority, order","s":["authority","order","command","commission","instruction","directive"],"k":["brief","charge","franchise","injunction"],"a":[],"ex":["The new class representative said she had a clear mandate from students to ask for longer library hours.","The committee was given a mandate to review the school's exam rules.","The mayor claimed the election result gave her a mandate to rebuild the city's roads."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"mandatory","p":"adjective","d":"Required by a rule or law, so that you must do it.","lb":"compulsory, required","s":["compulsory","obligatory","required","binding","necessary","essential"],"k":["de rigueur","incumbent","indispensable","needed"],"a":["optional","voluntary","elective","discretionary"],"ex":["Attendance at the orientation session is mandatory for all new students.","Wearing a helmet is mandatory for motorcycle riders in the city.","Safety training is mandatory before anyone can use the laboratory equipment."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"mania","p":"noun","d":"An extreme, uncontrolled enthusiasm for something, or a strong obsession with it.","lb":"craze, obsession","s":["craze","obsession","fad","passion","fixation","frenzy"],"k":["cult","fanaticism","furor","fury"],"a":["indifference","apathy","calm","disinterest"],"ex":["Gaming mania has kept many teenagers awake until dawn in the past year.","Her mania for cleaning means the house is spotless, but she is always tired.","Selfie mania has led some tourists to take dangerous risks near cliff edges."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"manifest","p":"adjective","d":"Clear and obvious to the eye or to the mind.","lb":"obvious, evident","s":["obvious","evident","apparent","plain","clear","patent"],"k":["conspicuous","discernible","glaring","observable"],"a":["hidden","concealed","obscure","unclear"],"ex":["Her joy was manifest when she saw her exam result and jumped up from her seat.","It was manifest from the empty seats that the concert had not been advertised well.","The judge pointed to a manifest error in the calculation of the fine."],"b":92,"y":2},{"w":"manifesto","p":"noun","d":"A public written statement of the beliefs, aims and plans of a person or group.","lb":"declaration, platform","s":["declaration","proclamation","platform","program","statement","pronouncement"],"k":["agenda","blueprint","credo","policy paper"],"a":[],"ex":["The student club published a manifesto promising cleaner classrooms and a bigger library.","Voters compared the parties' manifestos before deciding whom to support.","The artists' manifesto declared that art should be open to everyone, not only the rich."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"marginal","p":"adjective","d":"Very small in amount or importance, and only just enough to be noticed or to count.","lb":"slight, minor","s":["slight","minor","small","minimal","negligible","modest"],"k":["bare","little","narrow","peripheral"],"a":["significant","substantial","major","considerable"],"ex":["The new tyres made only a marginal difference to the car's performance.","She won the election for class captain by a marginal lead of three votes.","Marginal improvements in sleep and diet added up to a big change over six months."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"marshal","p":"verb","d":"To gather and arrange people, facts or resources carefully so they can be used effectively.","lb":"gather, organize","s":["gather","assemble","organize","arrange","muster","mobilize"],"k":["amass","congregate","convene","coordinate"],"a":["scatter","disperse","disband","squander"],"ex":["Before the debate, Nadia marshaled her facts and arranged them in a clear order.","The relief committee marshaled volunteers and boats to rescue villagers from the floodwater.","The lawyer marshaled evidence from many sources to build a strong case."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"martial","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to war, fighting or the army, or suited to a soldier.","lb":"military, warlike","s":["military","warlike","soldierly","combative","belligerent","militant"],"k":["armed","chivalrous","heroic","militaristic"],"a":["peaceful","civil","civilian","pacific"],"ex":["My cousin trains in martial arts like karate twice a week.","The band played martial music as the soldiers marched past.","The museum displays martial equipment such as swords, shields and old cannons."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"martyr","p":"noun","d":"A person who is killed or made to suffer greatly because of their beliefs or for a cause.","lb":"sufferer, hero","s":["victim","sufferer","sacrifice","hero","saint","casualty"],"k":["confessor","dissident","injured party","prisoner of conscience"],"a":["persecutor","oppressor","tormentor"],"ex":["Every February, people lay flowers at the Shaheed Minar to honor the martyrs of the Language Movement.","Nurses who died while treating patients during the epidemic were remembered as martyrs of public service.","The novel's hero is a young journalist who becomes a martyr for freedom of speech."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"materialistic","p":"adjective","d":"Caring too much about money and possessions, and too little about more important things.","lb":"money-minded, acquisitive","s":["acquisitive","worldly","greedy","mercenary","grasping"],"k":["avaricious","bourgeois","brand-obsessed","commercial"],"a":["spiritual","idealistic","selfless"],"ex":["Critics say modern society has become too materialistic, always chasing the next gadget.","He was so materialistic that he judged his friends by how expensive their watches were.","My grandfather taught us not to be materialistic, because kindness matters more than possessions."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"matriculate","p":"verb","d":"To officially enroll as a student at a college or university.","lb":"enroll, register","s":["enroll","register","sign up","enlist","be admitted","get in"],"k":["be accepted","begin studies","enter","gain entry"],"a":["graduate","drop out","withdraw","leave"],"ex":["She will matriculate at Dhaka University in July after passing her admission test.","Students who matriculate in engineering must complete a math course in the first semester.","He matriculated at the age of seventeen, one of the youngest in his class."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"maudlin","p":"adjective","d":"Too sentimental, especially in a silly or tearful way.","lb":"sentimental, weepy","s":["sentimental","mawkish","tearful","soppy","weepy","slushy"],"k":["bathetic","bittersweet","cloying","drippy"],"a":["unsentimental","stoic","cool","dispassionate"],"ex":["The movie was so maudlin that I rolled my eyes through the final scene.","He gets maudlin whenever he looks at old school photographs and begins to tell the same stories.","The writer's maudlin letter, full of self-pity, made the editor cringe."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"maverick","p":"noun","d":"A person who thinks and acts independently and refuses to follow the rules or ideas of a group.","lb":"nonconformist, rebel","s":["nonconformist","rebel","loner","free spirit","iconoclast","eccentric"],"k":["bohemian","dissident","free agent","freethinker"],"a":["conformist","follower","traditionalist"],"ex":["Our chemistry teacher is a maverick who ignores the textbook and teaches through experiments.","The company hired a maverick designer whose strange ideas made its products popular.","As the maverick of the family, she became a pilot while everyone else studied medicine."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"mawkish","p":"adjective","d":"Showing feelings in a weak, silly or exaggerated way that is hard to take seriously.","lb":"sentimental, soppy","s":["sentimental","maudlin","soppy","cloying","slushy","saccharine"],"k":["drippy","emotional","hokey","icky"],"a":["restrained","unsentimental","cool"],"ex":["The film's mawkish ending, with everyone crying and hugging, felt forced.","Her mawkish poem about lost love made her friends giggle.","The greeting card contained a mawkish verse about eternal friendship."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"maxim","p":"noun","d":"A short saying that expresses a general truth or a rule of behaviour.","lb":"saying, proverb","s":["saying","proverb","adage","axiom","aphorism","motto"],"k":["byword","catchphrase","expression","rule of thumb"],"a":[],"ex":["My father's favourite maxim is that honesty is the best policy.","The old maxim \"practice makes perfect\" is true when you are learning a language.","The company follows the maxim that the customer is always right."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"may","p":"verb","d":"Used to say that something is possible, or to ask for or give permission.","lb":"possibility, permission","s":["might","could","can","possibly will","be allowed to","be permitted to"],"k":["be apt to","be at liberty to","be entitled to","be free to"],"a":["cannot","must not"],"ex":["It may rain this evening, so take an umbrella when you leave.","May I borrow your pen for a moment?","You may leave the exam hall after the first hour."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mea culpa","p":"noun","d":"An admission that one has made a mistake or is to blame.","lb":"admission of guilt","s":["admission","confession","apology","acknowledgment","owning up","concession"],"k":["acknowledgement","amends","atonement","penance"],"a":["denial","excuse","justification"],"ex":["Mea culpa, I forgot to save the file, so we have to start again.","The company issued a public mea culpa after its app deleted customers' saved photos.","In a short mea culpa, the captain admitted that his poor decision had cost the team the match."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"meander","p":"verb","d":"To follow a winding path, or to wander slowly and aimlessly without a fixed direction.","lb":"wind, wander","s":["wind","twist","wander","zigzag","ramble","snake"],"k":["amble","bend","dally","go"],"a":["go straight","hurry","rush"],"ex":["The river meanders through green fields before it finally reaches the sea.","We meandered along the narrow lanes of the old town without any plan.","The path meanders up the hill, so the climb feels gentle."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"measles","p":"noun","d":"A contagious disease, mostly affecting children, that causes a red rash and fever.","lb":"viral disease","s":[],"k":["chickenpox","contagion","contagious disease","mumps"],"a":[],"ex":["Measles spreads easily among unvaccinated children in crowded areas.","The clinic gives a measles vaccine to babies at nine months.","She stayed at home for a week because she caught measles."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mediate","p":"verb","d":"To try to help two sides in a disagreement reach an agreement.","lb":"arbitrate, intervene","s":["arbitrate","intervene","negotiate","intercede","referee","settle"],"k":["act","act as go-between","adjudicate","bridge the gap"],"a":[],"ex":["The headmaster mediated between the two students and helped them end their fight.","A neutral lawyer was asked to mediate the dispute between the landlord and the tenants.","My aunt always mediates when the cousins argue over who gets the last piece of cake."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"medieval","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the Middle Ages, the period of European history from about the year 500 to 1500.","lb":"Middle Ages","s":["feudal","gothic","of the Middle Ages","old-world","mediaeval"],"k":["ancient","antiquated","archaic","bygone"],"a":["modern","contemporary","current"],"ex":["We toured a medieval castle with thick stone walls and narrow windows.","Our history teacher explained how medieval merchants traveled along the Silk Road.","Many medieval manuscripts were copied by hand and decorated with gold."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"mediocre","p":"adjective","d":"Not very good; of only average or slightly poor quality.","lb":"average, second-rate","s":["average","ordinary","indifferent","middling","uninspired","undistinguished"],"k":["bad","commonplace","fair","humdrum"],"a":["excellent","outstanding","exceptional","superb"],"ex":["The restaurant looked fancy, but the food was mediocre and far too expensive.","Rafi got mediocre marks in physics, so he decided to join extra classes.","Critics called the film mediocre, with a predictable story and weak acting."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"meditator","p":"noun","d":"A person who meditates, sitting quietly to calm the mind or think deeply.","lb":"person who meditates","s":["thinker"],"k":["guru","hermit","monk","mystic"],"a":[],"ex":["My aunt has been a daily meditator for ten years and says it helps her stay calm.","Studies suggest that experienced meditators handle stress better than other people.","As a beginner meditator, I could only sit still for five minutes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"medium","p":"noun","d":"A way or channel through which information, ideas or sound are communicated or carried.","lb":"means, channel","s":["means","channel","vehicle","avenue","instrument","mode"],"k":["conduit","culture medium","forum","instrumentation"],"a":[],"ex":["English is the medium of instruction at many private universities in Dhaka.","Radio is still an important medium for reaching people in remote villages.","Video is the best medium for teaching cooking, because you can see every step."],"b":416,"y":0},{"w":"melancholy","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling or causing a deep, thoughtful sadness.","lb":"sad, gloomy","s":["sad","gloomy","sorrowful","mournful","wistful","downcast"],"k":["dejected","depressing","despondent","dismal"],"a":["cheerful","happy","joyful","upbeat"],"ex":["The rainy afternoon put him in a melancholy mood.","She played a slow, melancholy song on her guitar.","The old railway station had a melancholy air after the last train left."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"melee","p":"noun","d":"A confused, noisy fight or struggle involving a crowd of people.","lb":"brawl, scuffle","s":["brawl","scuffle","fracas","tussle","scrum","fray"],"k":["battle royal","commotion","disturbance","dogfight"],"a":["peace","calm","order"],"ex":["A melee broke out at the stadium gate when hundreds of fans tried to get in at once.","In the melee at the clearance sale, two shoppers grabbed the same jacket and began to shout.","The teacher rushed into the playground to break up a melee between two groups of boys."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"mellifluous","p":"adjective","d":"Sweet and smooth to hear, like honey.","lb":"melodious, sweet-sounding","s":["melodious","sweet","smooth","soothing","dulcet","harmonious"],"k":["euphonious","fluent","golden-voiced","liquid"],"a":["harsh","grating","raspy","shrill"],"ex":["The radio host's mellifluous voice made even the weather report pleasant to hear.","A mellifluous flute melody drifted from the open window.","Her mellifluous singing of old folk songs filled the quiet evening."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"mellow","p":"adjective","d":"Soft, smooth and pleasant in taste, sound or light, or relaxed and gentle in manner.","lb":"soft, relaxed","s":["smooth","soft","gentle","rich","relaxed","easygoing"],"k":["drunk","high","intoxicated","mature"],"a":["harsh","sharp","bitter","tense"],"ex":["The cello produced a mellow tone that filled the small concert hall.","My uncle has become much more mellow since he retired from the bank.","A spoonful of honey gives the tea a mellow flavor."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"melodious","p":"adjective","d":"Having a pleasant, musical sound.","lb":"tuneful, musical","s":["musical","harmonious","sweet","dulcet","mellifluous","lyrical"],"k":["chiming","harmonic","lilting","resonant"],"a":["discordant","harsh","grating","tuneless"],"ex":["Every morning I wake up to the melodious song of a bird outside my window.","The new teacher has a melodious voice that makes even grammar lessons pleasant.","A melodious flute tune drifted from the tea stall as the evening came."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"melting","p":"adjective","d":"Turning from solid to liquid because of heat.","lb":"thawing","s":["thawing","dissolving","softening","defrosting","fusing"],"k":["fluid","liquescent","molten","mushy"],"a":["freezing","solidifying","hardening","setting"],"ex":["Melting ice from the glaciers is raising sea levels around the world.","The melting ice cream dripped down the child's hand.","A melting candle left wax all over the table."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"memoranda","p":"noun","d":"Short written notes or messages, used especially in offices to inform or remind people.","lb":"office notes, memos","s":["memos","notes","reminders","notices","circulars","minutes"],"k":["advisories","bulletins","communiqués","directives"],"a":[],"ex":["The manager sent two memoranda to all staff about the new working hours.","Old memoranda from the 1990s were stored in boxes in the basement.","The clerk filed the memoranda in order of date so they were easy to find."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mendacious","p":"adjective","d":"Not telling the truth, or in the habit of lying.","lb":"lying, dishonest","s":["lying","dishonest","untruthful","deceitful","false","deceptive"],"k":["crooked","disingenuous","fibbing","guileful"],"a":["truthful","honest","sincere","candid"],"ex":["The newspaper later admitted that its story about the school was completely mendacious.","Nobody trusted the mendacious salesman, who had lied about prices many times.","She gave a mendacious excuse about a sick aunt to avoid the meeting."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"mendicant","p":"noun","d":"A person who lives by begging, especially a religious beggar.","lb":"beggar, pauper","s":["beggar","pauper","supplicant","panhandler","vagrant","scrounger"],"k":["almsman","dervish","drifter","friar"],"a":["benefactor","donor","giver"],"ex":["A mendicant sat at the railway station gate, thanking everyone who dropped a coin into his bowl.","Wandering mendicants have long travelled from village to village, living on food given by strangers.","The old mendicant in the market sang songs in exchange for a few taka."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"menial","p":"adjective","d":"Describing work that is boring, unskilled and low in status.","lb":"lowly, unskilled","s":["lowly","humble","unskilled","routine","servile","mundane"],"k":["dreary","dull","grunt","inferior"],"a":["skilled","professional","prestigious","senior"],"ex":["After university, he took a menial job at a warehouse until he found a better one.","She was bored by the menial task of copying figures all day.","No honest work should be looked down on, even menial work like cleaning or carrying loads."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mentor","p":"noun","d":"An experienced person who gives advice and support to a less experienced person, especially at work or school.","lb":"adviser, guide","s":["advisor","guide","counselor","coach","teacher","tutor"],"k":["champion","confidant","godfather","intellect"],"a":[],"ex":["My university mentor helped me choose courses and introduced me to a company that offered an internship.","Every new nurse at the hospital is paired with a mentor for the first six months.","A good mentor listens carefully and gives honest advice, even when it is not easy to hear."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"mercenary","p":"noun","d":"A person who works only for money, especially a soldier who fights for pay for any side.","lb":"hired soldier, hireling","s":["hired soldier","soldier of fortune","hireling","gun for hire","opportunist","freelance fighter"],"k":["adventurer","bravo","condottiere","free lance"],"a":["patriot","volunteer","idealist"],"ex":["The film follows a mercenary who agrees to guard a village, but only after the villagers pay him.","Historians say the kingdom hired foreign mercenaries because its own army was too small.","Fans called the footballer a mercenary after he moved to the club that offered the most money."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"mercurial","p":"adjective","d":"Likely to change mood or opinion suddenly and without any warning.","lb":"changeable, unpredictable","s":["capricious","fickle","volatile","unpredictable","changeable","moody"],"k":["giddy","mutable","quicksilver","restless"],"a":["steady","stable","constant","dependable"],"ex":["Our manager is mercurial: cheerful in the morning and furious by lunch for no clear reason.","The actor's mercurial temper made rehearsals tense for the whole cast.","Because of her mercurial moods, her friends never knew whether to expect a hug or a lecture."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"meritorious","p":"adjective","d":"Deserving praise or reward because of great quality or effort.","lb":"praiseworthy, deserving","s":["praiseworthy","commendable","admirable","laudable","worthy","deserving"],"k":["creditable","distinguished","estimable","honorable"],"a":["undeserving","unworthy","contemptible","reprehensible"],"ex":["The firefighter received a medal for his meritorious service during the flood.","The school gave a certificate to the most meritorious students of each class.","Her meritorious research on clean water earned her a scholarship."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"merry","p":"adjective","d":"Cheerful and happy, often laughing and enjoying time with others.","lb":"cheerful, joyful","s":["cheerful","jolly","joyful","festive","happy","gleeful"],"k":["alert","brisk","energetic","gay"],"a":["gloomy","sad","miserable","sullen"],"ex":["The merry crowd sang and clapped at the village fair.","Grandfather's merry laugh filled the room whenever the grandchildren visited.","We had a merry evening, telling stories and eating biryani on the roof."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"meshed","p":"adjective","d":"Fitted closely together, like the teeth of gears or the strands of a net.","lb":"interlocked, fitted together","s":["interlocked","engaged","entangled","interwoven","linked","connected"],"k":["cross-linked","dovetailed","geared","involved"],"a":["separate","disconnected","detached","unconnected"],"ex":["The meshed gears of the old clock turned smoothly without a sound.","Their schedules were so closely meshed that missing one meeting would delay the whole project.","The fishermen mended the meshed nets along the riverbank."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"metamorphosis","p":"noun","d":"A complete change in form, appearance or character, as when a caterpillar becomes a butterfly.","lb":"transformation, change","s":["transformation","change","conversion","mutation","evolution","alteration"],"k":["metabolism","morphing","regeneration","reincarnation"],"a":["stasis","constancy","permanence","stability"],"ex":["A caterpillar goes through metamorphosis before it emerges as a butterfly.","University life brought a remarkable metamorphosis in him, from a shy boy into a confident speaker.","The metamorphosis of the old railway station into a busy shopping center surprised the whole town."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"mete","p":"verb","d":"To give out a punishment, reward or treatment to someone, usually in an official or fair way.","lb":"dole out, administer","s":["dole out","hand out","deal out","dispense","administer","allot"],"k":["allocate","dish out","give out","grant"],"a":["withhold","keep back","spare","retain"],"ex":["The judge meted out a heavy fine to the shop owner for selling expired medicine.","The school meted out the same punishment to every student who cheated.","In the story, the king meted out justice fairly to rich and poor alike."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"meticulous","p":"adjective","d":"Very careful and exact, giving great attention to small details.","lb":"careful, painstaking","s":["careful","precise","painstaking","thorough","scrupulous","fastidious"],"k":["assiduous","detail-oriented","diligent","finicky"],"a":["careless","sloppy","negligent","slapdash"],"ex":["The accountant was meticulous and checked every figure twice before sending the report.","Her meticulous notes helped the whole class prepare for the final exam.","The tailor in our neighborhood is meticulous and measures three times before cutting the Eid fabric."],"b":611,"y":2},{"w":"microcosm","p":"noun","d":"A small place, group or system that has the same features as a much larger one.","lb":"miniature, model","s":["miniature","epitome","model","replica","world in miniature","sample"],"k":["archetype","emblem","embodiment","example"],"a":["universe"],"ex":["Our school is a microcosm of the country, with students from every region and background.","The crowded railway station is a microcosm of the whole city, full of noise, hurry and hope.","Economists sometimes study a small village market as a microcosm of a national economy."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"milieu","p":"noun","d":"The social or physical environment in which someone lives or something happens.","lb":"environment, setting","s":["environment","setting","surroundings","background","context","atmosphere"],"k":["ambit","arena","climate","conditions"],"a":[],"ex":["Children from a milieu where books are valued often become strong readers.","The writer grew up in a poor rural milieu and often wrote about it.","The novel captures the milieu of old Dhaka, from busy tea stalls to narrow lanes of sweet shops."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"milled","p":"adjective","d":"Processed in a mill, especially rice or grain that has had its husk or outer layer removed.","lb":"polished, processed","s":["polished","processed","refined","ground"],"k":["crushed","minced","pounded","pulped"],"a":["unpolished","unrefined"],"ex":["Milled rice looks white and shiny because the outer brown layer has been removed.","Doctors say brown rice has more fiber than milled rice.","Most families in the city buy milled rice from the shop rather than husking paddy at home."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"millennium","p":"noun","d":"A period of one thousand years.","lb":"thousand years","s":["thousand years","ten centuries","era","age"],"k":["aeon","chiliad","eon","epoch"],"a":[],"ex":["The history of the city spans more than a millennium, from small village to busy capital.","The temple has stood on this hill for more than a millennium.","People celebrated all over the world when the new millennium began in the year 2000."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"minority","p":"noun","d":"The smaller part of a group; fewer than half of the people or things.","lb":"smaller number, small group","s":["smaller number","fewer","handful","small group","lesser part"],"k":["faction","fraction","fringe","remnant"],"a":["majority","bulk","mass","greater part"],"ex":["In the survey, only a small minority of customers said they preferred paying in cash.","Most of the class wanted a picnic, but a minority preferred a visit to the museum.","He found himself in the minority at the meeting, because nearly everyone else wanted to move the deadline."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"minuscule","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely small in size, amount or importance.","lb":"tiny, minute","s":["tiny","minute","microscopic","miniature","diminutive","infinitesimal"],"k":["bitty","little","miniscule","small"],"a":["huge","enormous","giant","gigantic"],"ex":["The ant carried a minuscule crumb of bread across the kitchen floor.","The terms and conditions were printed in minuscule letters that nobody could read without glasses.","He earns a minuscule salary, so he shares a room to save on rent."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"mirth","p":"noun","d":"Happy laughter and amusement, especially when shared among people.","lb":"laughter, cheer","s":["merriment","laughter","joy","glee","amusement","cheer"],"k":["cheerfulness","delight","elation","exuberance"],"a":["sadness","gloom","sorrow","misery"],"ex":["The room was filled with mirth when my uncle began to tell his funny stories.","She could not hide her mirth when the teacher accidentally sat on the chalk.","The children's mirth echoed through the garden as they chased soap bubbles."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"misanthrope","p":"noun","d":"A person who dislikes other people and avoids them.","lb":"people-hater, recluse","s":["hermit","recluse","loner","cynic","curmudgeon","grouch"],"k":["bear","churl","crank","grump"],"a":["philanthropist","humanitarian","people person","socialite"],"ex":["After years of living alone, the old writer became a misanthrope who avoided all visitors.","My uncle is a bit of a misanthrope and hates crowded markets and noisy parties.","The novel's hero is a misanthrope who finally learns to trust a kind neighbor."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"misanthropic","p":"adjective","d":"Disliking and distrusting other people in general, and avoiding their company.","lb":"people-hating, bitter","s":["antisocial","unsociable","cynical","embittered","unfriendly","reclusive"],"k":["bitter","curmudgeonly","distrustful","gloomy"],"a":["philanthropic","sociable","friendly","humane"],"ex":["After years of being cheated by customers, the shopkeeper became bitter and misanthropic.","The old poet lived alone in the hills, writing misanthropic verses about the foolishness of crowds.","His misanthropic jokes made new colleagues uneasy, since he seemed to dislike everybody."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"misconstrue","p":"verb","d":"To understand the meaning of something wrongly.","lb":"misunderstand","s":["misinterpret","misunderstand","misread","misjudge","mistake","get wrong"],"k":["be amiss","construe","distort","garble"],"a":["understand","grasp","comprehend","decipher"],"ex":["Please don't misconstrue my silence as agreement.","He misconstrued her joke as an insult and left the room.","Text messages are easy to misconstrue because they carry no tone of voice."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"misdemeanor","p":"noun","d":"A minor crime or small wrongdoing that is less serious than a felony.","lb":"minor offence","s":["minor offence","petty crime","infraction","offence","violation","lapse"],"k":["breach","crime","criminal offense","infringement"],"a":["felony","serious crime","major offence"],"ex":["Dropping litter in the park may count as a misdemeanor in some cities.","The student was fined for a minor misdemeanor and let go with a warning.","Cutting in line is a social misdemeanor that annoys everyone behind you."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"miserly","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to spend or give money, even when you can easily afford to.","lb":"stingy, tight-fisted","s":["stingy","mean","parsimonious","cheap","grasping"],"k":["cheeseparing","grudging","hoarding","penurious"],"a":["generous","lavish","liberal","charitable"],"ex":["The miserly landlord refused to repair the leaking roof, even after repeated complaints.","He was so miserly that he walked home to save a few taka on rickshaw fare.","Her uncle is miserly with money but very generous with his time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mistrust","p":"verb","d":"To feel that a person, group or thing cannot be trusted or relied on.","lb":"distrust, doubt","s":["distrust","doubt","suspect","question","disbelieve","be wary of"],"k":["be cynical of","be leery of","be skeptical of","discredit"],"a":["trust","believe","rely on","depend on"],"ex":["Many customers mistrust online shops that ask for full payment before showing real photos.","After being cheated once, Rafi began to mistrust every stranger who offered him a bargain.","Patients may mistrust a doctor who never explains the treatment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mitigate","p":"verb","d":"To make something bad, such as pain, damage or risk, less serious or severe.","lb":"lessen, alleviate","s":["reduce","lessen","alleviate","ease","diminish","moderate"],"k":["allay","curtail","cut","decrease"],"a":["aggravate","worsen","intensify","increase"],"ex":["Planting trees along the road can mitigate the noise and dust from traffic.","Doctors gave her medicine to mitigate the pain after the surgery.","The company offered free repairs to mitigate customers' anger about the faulty phones."],"b":595,"y":2},{"w":"mode","p":"noun","d":"A way or manner of doing something, or a particular setting in which a machine or device works.","lb":"method, manner","s":["method","manner","way","style","fashion","form"],"k":["condition","function","mood","musical mode"],"a":[],"ex":["Walking is the cheapest mode of transport in a crowded city.","Please put your phone in silent mode before the exam begins.","Online learning is now a common mode of study at many universities."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"modulate","p":"verb","d":"To adjust or control the strength, tone or level of something.","lb":"regulate, adjust","s":["adjust","regulate","tone down","temper","moderate","vary"],"k":["alter","attenuate","calibrate","change"],"a":[],"ex":["A good speaker knows how to modulate his voice to keep the audience interested.","Thermostats modulate the temperature so that the room stays comfortable.","She tried to modulate her anger and speak calmly to the customer."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"mollify","p":"verb","d":"To calm someone who is angry or upset, often by saying or giving something that makes them feel better.","lb":"soothe, placate","s":["placate","pacify","appease","soothe","calm","assuage"],"k":["alleviate","calm down","cool down","disarm"],"a":["anger","enrage","provoke","infuriate"],"ex":["The waiter offered a free dessert to mollify the angry customer.","My mother's warm hug and a cup of tea mollified me after the argument.","The airline gave passengers free meals to mollify them after the long delay."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"momentum","p":"noun","d":"The force or speed that a moving object or an ongoing process gains as it develops.","lb":"impetus, drive","s":["impetus","drive","force","energy","thrust","propulsion"],"k":["forward motion","headway","impulse","pace"],"a":["inertia","stagnation","stasis"],"ex":["The campaign gained momentum after a video about it went viral online.","The bike gained momentum as it rolled down the long hill.","After two wins in a row, the team had real momentum going into the final."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"monolithic","p":"adjective","d":"Large, solid and unchanging, often too rigid or uniform to adapt to new needs.","lb":"massive, rigid","s":["massive","rigid","uniform","inflexible","huge","solid"],"k":["big","enormous","gigantic","immense"],"a":["flexible","diverse","varied","fragmented"],"ex":["The monolithic concrete building stood out against the small houses around it.","Critics said the bank was a monolithic organization that ignored the needs of small customers.","It is wrong to treat the youth as a monolithic group, because young people hold many different views."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"monotonous","p":"adjective","d":"Always the same and therefore boring; lacking variety or change.","lb":"boring, repetitive","s":["tedious","repetitive","dull","boring","humdrum","uniform"],"k":["dreary","flat","grinding","irksome"],"a":["varied","exciting","lively","interesting"],"ex":["Working on the same assembly line all day can be monotonous.","The lecturer's monotonous voice made half the class fall asleep.","I find eating the same lunch every day monotonous, so I try new recipes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"monumental","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely large, important or impressive.","lb":"huge, significant","s":["huge","enormous","colossal","immense","momentous","historic"],"k":["big","giant","important","large"],"a":["tiny","trivial","minor","insignificant"],"ex":["Building the bridge across the river was a monumental task for the engineers.","The discovery of vaccines was a monumental achievement for medicine.","I made a monumental mistake when I deleted the only copy of my thesis."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"morale","p":"noun","d":"The level of confidence, enthusiasm and hope felt by a person or group.","lb":"spirit, confidence","s":["spirit","confidence","esprit de corps","heart","mood","team spirit"],"k":["ardor","backbone","camaraderie","disposition"],"a":["despair","discouragement","pessimism"],"ex":["Free lunches on Fridays helped to boost morale in the busy office.","Morale was low in the team after three defeats in a row.","The teacher's kind words improved the students' morale before the final exam."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"moratorium","p":"noun","d":"An official agreement or order to stop an activity or payment for a fixed period of time.","lb":"suspension, freeze","s":["suspension","freeze","halt","pause","ban","postponement"],"k":["abeyance","adjournment","cessation","deferment"],"a":["resumption","continuation"],"ex":["The city declared a moratorium on new construction until the drainage system could be repaired.","Banks offered a three-month moratorium on loan repayments to families hit by the floods.","Authorities announced a moratorium on fishing during the breeding season to protect fish stocks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"morbid","p":"adjective","d":"Having or showing an unhealthy interest in death, disease or other unpleasant things.","lb":"gloomy, unhealthy","s":["ghoulish","gruesome","macabre","gloomy","grim","unhealthy"],"k":["brooding","dark","diseased","dismal"],"a":["cheerful","healthy","wholesome","upbeat"],"ex":["Drivers slowed down to stare at the crash out of morbid curiosity.","He has a morbid fear of hospitals after spending much of his childhood in one.","My cousin's morbid jokes about funerals made the whole family uncomfortable."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"more","p":"adverb","d":"To a greater degree or extent; used before many adjectives and adverbs to make comparisons.","lb":"to a greater degree","s":["to a greater degree","further","increasingly","additionally","besides","over"],"k":["all the more","considerably","even","much"],"a":["less","to a lesser degree"],"ex":["This phone is more expensive than the one I had before.","Please speak more slowly so that everyone can follow you.","I enjoy cricket more than football."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"mores","p":"noun","d":"The accepted customs and moral values of a particular group or society.","lb":"customs, norms","s":["customs","traditions","conventions","norms","standards","manners"],"k":["convention","ethics","ethos","etiquette"],"a":[],"ex":["Visitors should learn the local mores before attending a family gathering in a new country.","Social mores about clothing and behavior change slowly from one generation to the next.","The novel shows how the mores of a small village can limit a young person's choices."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"moribund","p":"adjective","d":"Close to death or in a state of decline, with little life or activity left.","lb":"dying, stagnant","s":["dying","declining","stagnant","failing","fading","on its last legs"],"k":["ailing","decrepit","dormant","languishing"],"a":["thriving","flourishing","healthy","booming"],"ex":["The moribund jute mill closed its gates after years of falling orders.","Doctors said the moribund patient had only a few hours left.","The town's moribund market came back to life when a new bus route brought shoppers back."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"morose","p":"adjective","d":"Sad, bad-tempered and unwilling to talk or be cheerful.","lb":"gloomy, sullen","s":["gloomy","sullen","glum","sulky","moody","dejected"],"k":["crestfallen","dark","depressed","despondent"],"a":["cheerful","happy","jolly","upbeat"],"ex":["He sat in the corner, morose and silent, after failing the admission test.","My brother has been morose since his best friend moved to another city.","The morose waiter barely looked at us when he took our order."],"b":85,"y":1},{"w":"mortify","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel extremely embarrassed or ashamed.","lb":"embarrass, humiliate","s":["embarrass","humiliate","shame","abash","chagrin","humble"],"k":["abase","bruise","crucify","disconcert"],"a":["flatter","delight","gratify","please"],"ex":["She was mortified when her phone rang loudly in the middle of the silent exam hall.","It mortified Rafi to realize he had been calling the new teacher by the wrong name for a week.","My father mortified me by telling my childhood stories to all my friends."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"motif","p":"noun","d":"An idea, subject or pattern that is repeated in a story, a piece of music or a design.","lb":"theme, pattern","s":["theme","pattern","design","idea","topic","emblem"],"k":["concept","device","focus","image"],"a":[],"ex":["Rain is a recurring motif in the poet's work, standing for sadness.","The nakshi kantha quilt is stitched with a fish motif along its border.","A motif of betrayal runs through the whole novel."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"motility","p":"noun","d":"The ability of a living thing or its parts to move on its own.","lb":"mobility, movement","s":["mobility","movement","locomotion","motion","activity"],"k":["action","agility","animation","gesture"],"a":["stillness","paralysis","inertia","inactivity"],"ex":["Bacteria with high motility can swim quickly through liquid.","Under the microscope, we studied the motility of the tiny cells as they swam across the slide.","Poor gut motility can cause stomach pain and constipation."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"motley","p":"adjective","d":"Made up of many different kinds of people or things that do not seem to belong together.","lb":"varied, mixed","s":["varied","diverse","mixed","assorted","miscellaneous","heterogeneous"],"k":["calico","colored","colorful","different"],"a":["uniform","homogeneous","matching","similar"],"ex":["A motley crowd of students, vendors and tourists filled the station.","The football team was a motley group of players who had never trained together.","She wore a motley collection of bracelets, each from a different trip."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"mount","p":"verb","d":"To fix something firmly onto a wall, frame or other support so that it stays in place.","lb":"fix, attach","s":["fix","attach","install","fasten","affix","set"],"k":["anchor","bolt","brace","clamp"],"a":["remove","detach","take down","unfasten"],"ex":["We mounted the television on the wall so the children could not knock it over.","She mounted the photo on a card before putting it in a frame.","The technician will mount the security camera above the shop door tomorrow."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"mourning","p":"noun","d":"The feeling or expression of deep sadness after someone has died.","lb":"grief, sorrow","s":["grief","sorrow","lamentation","grieving","bereavement","heartache"],"k":["desolation","dolor","heartbreak","keening"],"a":["celebration","rejoicing","joy","jubilation"],"ex":["The whole village was in mourning after the sudden death of the popular teacher.","The country declared three days of mourning after the bus accident.","She wore black during her period of mourning for her grandmother."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"multifaceted","p":"adjective","d":"Having many different parts, sides or aspects.","lb":"many-sided, complex","s":["varied","complex","diverse","versatile","multidimensional","manifold"],"k":["assorted","composite","different","elaborate"],"a":["simple","narrow","limited","uniform"],"ex":["Poverty is a multifaceted problem that cannot be solved with money alone.","Our teacher is a multifaceted person: a poet, a cricket coach and a gardener.","The job is multifaceted, involving writing, teaching and managing a small team."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"mumble","p":"verb","d":"To speak quietly and unclearly, so that the words are hard to understand.","lb":"mutter, murmur","s":["mutter","murmur","grumble","slur","whisper","swallow your words"],"k":["babble","drone","gabble","garble"],"a":["enunciate","articulate","pronounce","speak up"],"ex":["Please don't mumble during your presentation; the people at the back cannot hear you.","He mumbled an apology and hurried out of the classroom.","My grandfather often mumbles to himself while he reads the newspaper."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"mundane","p":"adjective","d":"Ordinary and dull, because it happens every day and is not exciting.","lb":"ordinary, everyday","s":["ordinary","everyday","routine","humdrum","commonplace","banal"],"k":["common","daily","earthly","monotonous"],"a":["exciting","extraordinary","unusual","remarkable"],"ex":["Washing dishes and paying bills are mundane tasks, but someone has to do them.","He wrote a funny blog about the mundane details of his daily commute.","After the exciting trip, life at the office felt mundane again."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"municipal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the government or administration of a city or town.","lb":"civic, city","s":["civic","city","urban","town","local","metropolitan"],"k":["borough","citywide","civil","communal"],"a":["national","rural","federal"],"ex":["Municipal workers collect garbage from every ward each morning.","The municipal library offers free membership to all residents.","The municipal water supply was cut for a day during the pipe repairs."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"munificent","p":"adjective","d":"Very generous, giving or donating a great deal.","lb":"generous, lavish","s":["generous","lavish","liberal","bountiful","charitable","philanthropic"],"k":["altruistic","beneficent","benevolent","big-hearted"],"a":["stingy","miserly","mean","tightfisted"],"ex":["A munificent donor paid for the school's new science laboratory.","She gave a munificent tip to the waiter who had patiently served her large family.","The company's munificent bonus allowed every employee to celebrate Eid with ease."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"muse","p":"verb","d":"To think about something deeply and slowly, often in a dreamy or thoughtful way.","lb":"ponder, reflect","s":["ponder","reflect","meditate","contemplate","think","brood"],"k":["chew over","cogitate","consider","mull"],"a":[],"ex":["He sat on the roof in the evening breeze and mused about his plans for the future.","I wonder where we will all be in ten years, he mused, stirring his tea.","The writer mused about how much the city had changed since her youth."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"muster","p":"verb","d":"To gather people together for a purpose, or to gather up courage, strength or support.","lb":"gather, summon","s":["gather","assemble","rally","summon","collect","marshal"],"k":["amass","come up","congregate","convene"],"a":["disperse","scatter","dismiss","disband"],"ex":["Rafi finally mustered the courage to ask the teacher about his low marks.","The principal mustered all the students in the hall for the fire drill.","It took all her strength to muster a smile at the farewell party."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"myopia","p":"noun","d":"Nearsightedness of the eyes; figuratively, a lack of foresight or a narrow, short-term view.","lb":"short-sightedness","s":["lack of foresight","tunnel vision","insularity"],"k":["blindness","imprudence","parochialism","provincialism"],"a":["foresight","vision","perspective"],"ex":["Many children develop myopia from spending long hours looking at small screens.","He had to wear thick glasses to correct his myopia, since he could not read the board.","The company's myopia led it to focus on this quarter's profits and ignore future customers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"myriad","p":"noun","d":"A huge, countless number of things; also used before a noun to mean countless.","lb":"countless number","s":["multitude","host","legion","swarm","mass","thousands"],"k":["concourse","countless","crowd","endless"],"a":["handful","few","scarcity","shortage"],"ex":["A myriad of lights shone on the river from the boats and the shops along the bank.","There are myriads of stars visible from the village on a clear night.","Online shopping offers myriad choices, which sometimes makes it hard to decide."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"mystic","p":"adjective","d":"Having a hidden or spiritual meaning that is mysterious and hard for ordinary people to understand.","lb":"mysterious, spiritual","s":["mysterious","spiritual","otherworldly","enigmatic","occult","esoteric"],"k":["inexplicable","inscrutable","preternatural","puzzling"],"a":["ordinary","worldly","plain","mundane"],"ex":["The old village poet had a mystic way of speaking that fascinated young listeners.","A mystic silence settled over the forest at dawn.","The folk songs of Bengal often carry a mystic message about the soul and the universe."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"mystically","p":"adverb","d":"In a mysterious way that seems to be connected with hidden or spiritual powers.","lb":"mysteriously, enigmatically","s":["mysteriously","inexplicably","magically","enigmatically","cryptically"],"k":["arcanely","esoterically","metaphysically","spiritually"],"a":["plainly","clearly","openly","straightforwardly"],"ex":["The singer closed her eyes and swayed mystically to the sound of the flute.","Fog drifted mystically over the river at dawn.","The old poem speaks mystically of becoming one with nature."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"naive","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking experience of life and too ready to trust people or believe what they say.","lb":"innocent, gullible","s":["innocent","gullible","credulous","trusting","inexperienced","unsophisticated"],"k":["callow","childlike","easily fooled","guileless"],"a":["worldly","sophisticated","experienced","shrewd"],"ex":["It is naive to believe that every message offering a free prize is honest.","As a naive first-year student, Rafi lent money to anyone with a sad story.","She was too naive to see that the shopkeeper was overcharging her."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"narcissism","p":"noun","d":"An excessive interest in and admiration of oneself, especially of one's own looks or abilities.","lb":"self-love, vanity","s":["vanity","egotism","conceit","arrogance"],"k":["hubris","pride","self-centeredness","self-importance"],"a":["humility","modesty","selflessness","altruism"],"ex":["Taking fifty selfies a day may look like narcissism, but some people just enjoy photography.","His narcissism made him unable to accept any criticism of his work.","The psychologist explained that narcissism often hides a person's deep insecurity."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nebulous","p":"adjective","d":"Unclear, vague and not well defined.","lb":"vague, hazy","s":["vague","hazy","unclear","indistinct","fuzzy","ambiguous"],"k":["amorphous","blurred","blurry","impalpable"],"a":["clear","definite","distinct","precise"],"ex":["Her plans for the future are still nebulous, and she has not decided on a career.","The teacher said my answer was nebulous because it never gave specific examples.","The company's nebulous rules left employees unsure what was allowed."],"b":112,"y":1},{"w":"neck","p":"noun","d":"The part of the body that joins the head to the shoulders.","lb":"body part","s":["nape","scruff","throat","cervix"],"k":["cervical region","external body part","gullet","nuchal region"],"a":[],"ex":["After sleeping on the sofa, I woke up with a stiff neck.","She wrapped a warm scarf around her neck before leaving on the cold morning.","The giraffe stretched its long neck to reach the leaves at the top of the tree."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"nefarious","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely wicked or criminal, especially in a way that involves secret planning.","lb":"wicked, evil","s":["wicked","evil","villainous","sinister","criminal","vile"],"k":["dastardly","despicable","devious","diabolical"],"a":["virtuous","honorable","noble","righteous"],"ex":["The police uncovered a nefarious plot to steal money from elderly bank customers.","In the movie, the nefarious villain hides his true plans behind a friendly smile.","Some websites use nefarious tricks to steal people's passwords."],"b":528,"y":0},{"w":"negate","p":"verb","d":"To make something useless or ineffective, or to show that it is not true.","lb":"nullify, cancel out","s":["nullify","cancel","invalidate","void","undo","counteract"],"k":["belie","contravene","disprove","obviate"],"a":["confirm","validate","affirm","support"],"ex":["Eating a lot of sweets can negate the benefit of an hour at the gym.","One rude comment can negate all the good work a salesperson has done.","New evidence negated the claim that the suspect had been at the shop that night."],"b":131,"y":0},{"w":"nemesis","p":"noun","d":"A powerful opponent or a problem that is very hard to defeat and often causes someone's failure.","lb":"arch-enemy, downfall","s":["adversary","bane","foe","opponent","downfall","undoing"],"k":["affliction","albatross","antagonist","blight"],"a":["ally","friend","supporter","partner"],"ex":["Mathematics has always been my nemesis, no matter how hard I study.","In the final, the champion at last met his old nemesis, the player who had beaten him three times.","For the small shopkeeper, the big supermarket was a nemesis."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"neologism","p":"noun","d":"A newly invented word or expression, or an existing word used with a new meaning.","lb":"new word, coinage","s":["coinage","new word","new expression","buzzword","invention","innovation"],"k":["argot","catchphrase","jargon","portmanteau"],"a":["obsolete word"],"ex":["The word \"selfie\" was once a neologism, but now everyone uses it.","Teenagers constantly invent neologisms for chatting online, and older people often cannot follow them.","Dictionary editors decide whether a neologism has been used widely enough to be included."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"neophyte","p":"noun","d":"A person who is new to a subject, skill or activity; a beginner.","lb":"beginner, novice","s":["beginner","novice","newcomer","tyro","learner","rookie"],"k":["amateur","fledgling","freshman","newbie"],"a":["expert","veteran","master","professional"],"ex":["As a neophyte in the office, she spent her first week learning how everything worked.","The neophyte climber needed help with every knot and rope on the mountain.","Even a neophyte chess player can learn the basic rules in an hour."],"b":45,"y":0},{"w":"nepotism","p":"noun","d":"Unfair favoritism shown to relatives or close friends, especially in giving them jobs.","lb":"favoritism, cronyism","s":["favoritism","patronage","bias","partiality","preferential treatment"],"k":["backscratching","clannishness","discrimination","jobbery"],"a":["fairness","impartiality","objectivity","equity"],"ex":["Many applicants complained of nepotism when the owner's relatives were hired without any interview.","The school's hiring practices were criticized as nepotism after three teachers turned out to be relatives.","Nepotism in a family business can upset hardworking employees who are not related to the owner."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nihilism","p":"noun","d":"The belief that life has no meaning and that moral values have no real basis.","lb":"belief in nothing","s":["cynicism","pessimism","disbelief","denial","skepticism","hopelessness"],"k":["amorality","anomie","apathy","defeatism"],"a":["idealism","optimism","faith","belief"],"ex":["After losing his job and his savings, he fell into nihilism and stopped caring about anything.","The philosophy class discussed how nihilism challenges the idea that life has any built-in purpose.","Some critics say the novel promotes nihilism because none of its characters believes in anything."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nimble","p":"adjective","d":"Able to move quickly and lightly, or to think quickly.","lb":"agile, quick","s":["agile","spry","quick","sprightly","deft","lively"],"k":["active","brisk","fast","intelligent"],"a":["clumsy","awkward","slow","stiff"],"ex":["The nimble goat jumped from rock to rock without slipping.","A tailor with nimble fingers can sew a button in seconds.","Even at seventy, my aunt is nimble enough to climb stairs two at a time."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"nirvana","p":"noun","d":"A state of perfect happiness and peace, free from pain and worry.","lb":"bliss, perfect peace","s":["bliss","paradise","heaven","utopia","ecstasy","serenity"],"k":["beatitude","delight","eden","elysium"],"a":["hell","misery","torment","agony"],"ex":["After a long exam week, sleeping until noon felt like nirvana.","For book lovers, a quiet library with a comfortable chair is nirvana.","A cold glass of lemon juice on a hot afternoon was pure nirvana."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"noisome","p":"adjective","d":"Having a very bad smell that is disgusting or harmful to breathe.","lb":"foul, offensive","s":["foul","offensive","putrid","stinking","fetid","rank"],"k":["distasteful","funky","malodorous","nauseating"],"a":["fragrant","pleasant","wholesome","sweet"],"ex":["A noisome smell rose from the open drain beside the bus stand.","The factory released noisome fumes that made nearby residents close their windows.","We cleaned the noisome fridge, which had been unplugged for a month with fish still inside."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"nolo contendere","p":"phrase","d":"A plea in court in which a defendant does not admit guilt but accepts the punishment.","lb":"no contest plea","s":["no contest","plea of no contest"],"k":["alford plea","answer","non-admission plea"],"a":[],"ex":["The driver pleaded nolo contendere to the traffic charge to avoid a long trial.","By entering a nolo contendere plea, he accepted the fine without admitting he was at fault.","In some countries, a nolo contendere plea cannot be used against a person in a later civil case."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nomadic","p":"adjective","d":"Moving from place to place instead of living in one permanent home.","lb":"wandering, roaming","s":["wandering","itinerant","roaming","migratory","roving","peripatetic"],"k":["footloose","migrant","mobile","peregrine"],"a":["settled","sedentary","stationary","rooted"],"ex":["Nomadic herders move their sheep to new grassland every few months.","After college, she led a nomadic life, working in a different city every year.","My cousin works online and enjoys a nomadic lifestyle, never staying anywhere longer than a month."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"nomenclature","p":"noun","d":"A system of names or technical terms used in a particular subject, or the process of naming things.","lb":"naming system, terms","s":["terminology","vocabulary","classification","naming system","terms","lexicon"],"k":["appellation","denomination","jargon","labeling"],"a":[],"ex":["Chemistry students must learn the nomenclature used for naming organic compounds.","Medical nomenclature can confuse patients because so many of the terms come from Latin.","The botanist explained that plant nomenclature gives every species a two-part Latin name."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"nominal","p":"adjective","d":"Very small in amount, especially when compared with the real cost or value.","lb":"token, minimal","s":["token","minimal","symbolic","small","trifling","insignificant"],"k":["formal","marginal","minor","paltry"],"a":["substantial","considerable","large","significant"],"ex":["The library charges only a nominal fee for borrowing books.","The club offers membership to students for a nominal charge of fifty taka.","He rented the small room from his uncle for a nominal rent."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"non sequitur","p":"noun","d":"A statement or reply that does not follow logically from what came before.","lb":"illogical remark","s":["fallacy","inconsistency","red herring","tangent","digression","deviation"],"k":["aside","change of subject","logical leap","off-topic remark"],"a":["logical conclusion","deduction","inference","relevant remark"],"ex":["When I asked about her exams, her answer about the weather was a total non sequitur.","His speech was full of non sequiturs, so the audience could not follow his argument.","Saying that a student is lazy because he likes cricket is a non sequitur."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nonchalance","p":"noun","d":"A relaxed, calm manner that shows no worry or concern about something.","lb":"calmness, indifference","s":["composure","coolness","indifference","calmness","poise","detachment"],"k":["blasé attitude","carelessness","casualness","equanimity"],"a":["anxiety","concern","worry","agitation"],"ex":["He shrugged with nonchalance when told that the exam was tomorrow.","She faced the crowd with a nonchalance that surprised everyone.","The bus driver steered through the crowded street with calm nonchalance."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"nonchalant","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and relaxed, showing no worry or interest, especially when others would be concerned.","lb":"unconcerned, casual","s":["casual","unconcerned","indifferent","calm","relaxed","offhand"],"k":["aloof","apathetic","blithe","cold"],"a":["anxious","worried","concerned","nervous"],"ex":["Rafi seemed nonchalant about the exam, though he had barely slept all week.","She gave a nonchalant shrug when asked whether she minded waiting.","The goalkeeper stayed nonchalant, even though the match was tied."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"nostalgia","p":"noun","d":"A warm, slightly sad feeling of longing for a happy time or place in the past.","lb":"longing, wistfulness","s":["longing","yearning","homesickness","reminiscence","sentimentality","pining"],"k":["bittersweet feeling","fond recollection","hankering","retrospection"],"a":[],"ex":["The smell of rain on dry earth fills me with nostalgia for my grandmother's village.","Old school photos brought a wave of nostalgia as the friends scrolled through them together.","He felt deep nostalgia for home during his first winter studying abroad."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"notorious","p":"adjective","d":"Widely known for something bad or shameful.","lb":"infamous, disreputable","s":["infamous","disreputable","scandalous","dishonorable","unsavory"],"k":["disgraceful","dodgy","dubious","seedy"],"a":["respected","reputable","honorable","esteemed"],"ex":["This road is notorious for traffic jams, especially during evening rush hour.","The restaurant became notorious for its rude waiters and cold food.","The area was notorious for pickpockets, so tourists were told to hold their bags tightly."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"novel","p":"adjective","d":"New and different from anything known or done before, often in a clever way.","lb":"new, original","s":["new","original","fresh","innovative","unusual","unconventional"],"k":["avant-garde","cutting-edge","experimental","modern"],"a":["old","familiar","conventional","traditional"],"ex":["The students came up with a novel way to turn plastic bottles into flower pots.","Her novel approach to teaching grammar through songs made the class far more fun.","A novel idea for a mobile app helped the young team win the competition."],"b":274,"y":0},{"w":"november","p":"noun","d":"The eleventh month of the year, between October and December.","lb":"month","s":["nov"],"k":["11th month","autumn month","eleventh month","fall month"],"a":[],"ex":["Our final exams begin in the second week of November.","The weather in Bangladesh turns cooler and drier in November.","My sister was born on 12 November, so we always have cake that day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"novice","p":"noun","d":"A person who is new to an activity or job and has little experience or skill.","lb":"beginner, learner","s":["beginner","newcomer","learner","rookie","trainee","amateur"],"k":["fledgling","freshman","greenhorn","neophyte"],"a":["expert","veteran","professional","master"],"ex":["I am a complete novice at cooking, so please explain every step.","The course is designed for novices who have never written a line of code.","As a novice driver, my brother is extra careful on busy roads."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"noxious","p":"adjective","d":"Harmful to health or likely to cause damage, especially a gas, smell or substance.","lb":"harmful, poisonous","s":["harmful","poisonous","toxic","unhealthy","damaging","foul"],"k":["corrupting","dangerous","degrading","detrimental"],"a":["harmless","wholesome","healthy","benign"],"ex":["Noxious fumes from the factory chimney made the neighbors cough and close their windows.","Burning plastic releases noxious gases that can damage the lungs.","The farmer pulled up noxious weeds before they could spread across the field."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"nuance","p":"noun","d":"A very small difference in meaning, tone, feeling or color that is easy to miss.","lb":"subtle difference, shade","s":["subtlety","shade","distinction","gradation","refinement","fine point"],"k":["flavor","hue","meaning","significance"],"a":[],"ex":["A good translator must capture every nuance of the original poem.","The nuance between “angry” and “furious” becomes clear once you see how people use them.","He did not notice the nuance in her tone and thought she was only joking."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"nullified","p":"adjective","d":"Made legally invalid or cancelled, so that it no longer has any effect.","lb":"cancelled, void","s":["cancelled","annulled","void","invalidated","revoked","voided"],"k":["abrogated","countermanded","defunct","ineffective"],"a":["valid","confirmed","enforced","upheld"],"ex":["The nullified contract meant neither company had to follow its terms.","The nullified results were removed from the website and the students were told to retake the test.","She held up the nullified ticket, which the airline refused to accept."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"nullify","p":"verb","d":"To make something legally invalid, or to cancel its effect completely.","lb":"cancel, void","s":["cancel","void","annul","invalidate","revoke","repeal"],"k":["abolish","abrogate","avoid","countermand"],"a":["validate","confirm","uphold","enforce"],"ex":["The court nullified the contract because one of the signatures had been forged.","Cheating nullified his exam result, and he had to retake the paper.","Eating a large dessert will nullify the benefit of your morning run."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"numerous","p":"adjective","d":"Many; existing or happening in large numbers.","lb":"many, plentiful","s":["many","countless","plentiful","abundant","multiple","innumerable"],"k":["ample","copious","galore","incalculable"],"a":["few","scarce","limited","sparse"],"ex":["I have called the repair shop on numerous occasions, but nobody answers.","Numerous students applied for the scholarship this year.","The city park has numerous benches where people rest in the evening."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"obdurate","p":"adjective","d":"Stubbornly refusing to change your mind or feelings, even when people ask you kindly.","lb":"stubborn, hard-hearted","s":["stubborn","obstinate","inflexible","unyielding","adamant","intransigent"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","cussed","dogged"],"a":["flexible","yielding","compliant","amenable"],"ex":["The landlord remained obdurate and refused to lower the rent even slightly.","Despite our tears, the obdurate guard would not let us in without tickets.","My obdurate uncle will not accept help, even when he is clearly struggling."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"obeisance","p":"noun","d":"A bow or other gesture that shows deep respect for, or obedience to, someone.","lb":"bow, deep respect","s":["bow","homage","deference","reverence","respect","salaam"],"k":["admiration","bowing","esteem","fealty"],"a":["disrespect","contempt","insolence","defiance"],"ex":["The dancer made a graceful obeisance to the audience before leaving the stage.","Junior staff showed obeisance to the chairman, standing up whenever he walked past.","In the old film, villagers paid obeisance to the landlord whenever he rode through the village."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"obey","p":"verb","d":"To do what you are told to do by a person, rule or law.","lb":"comply, follow","s":["comply with","follow","abide by","heed","observe","submit to"],"k":["adapt","adjust","adopt","comply"],"a":["disobey","defy","disregard","ignore"],"ex":["Drivers must obey traffic signals, even when the road looks empty.","The well-trained dog obeys every command its owner gives.","Children usually obey their parents more when the rules are explained clearly."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"obfuscate","p":"verb","d":"To make something unclear or hard to understand, often on purpose.","lb":"confuse, obscure","s":["confuse","obscure","muddy","cloud","blur","complicate"],"k":["alter","baffle","change","mix up"],"a":["clarify","explain","illuminate","simplify"],"ex":["The company used confusing legal language to obfuscate the real cost of the loan.","Instead of answering directly, the spokesperson tried to obfuscate the facts with long speeches.","Writers who obfuscate their ideas with long, fancy words lose many readers."],"b":528,"y":0},{"w":"obfuscation","p":"noun","d":"The act of making something deliberately unclear or confusing so that people cannot easily understand it.","lb":"confusion, evasion","s":["obscurity","confusion","evasion","vagueness","muddying","mystification"],"k":["bewilderment","disarray","equivocation","gobbledygook"],"a":["clarity","transparency","clearness","candor"],"ex":["The contract was full of legal obfuscation, so few customers understood it.","His obfuscation of the facts only made the manager more suspicious.","Teachers encourage clear writing and warn against obfuscation in essays."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"objective","p":"adjective","d":"Based on facts rather than personal feelings or opinions, and therefore fair.","lb":"unbiased, factual","s":["unbiased","impartial","neutral","fair","detached","unprejudiced"],"k":["clinical","concrete","equitable","existent"],"a":["subjective","biased","prejudiced","partial"],"ex":["A good judge must stay objective and decide the case only on the evidence.","It is hard to be objective about your own work, so ask a friend to read it.","The news report gave an objective account of the accident, with no opinions added."],"b":418,"y":0},{"w":"oblique","p":"adjective","d":"Not stated directly or clearly; expressed in an indirect way.","lb":"indirect, vague","s":["indirect","roundabout","vague","evasive","circuitous","implicit"],"k":["ambiguous","convoluted","devious","meandering"],"a":["direct","straightforward","explicit","blunt"],"ex":["She made an oblique remark about the messy kitchen instead of asking us directly to clean it.","The letter contained only an oblique reference to the problem, so nobody understood the warning.","He gave an oblique answer to the interviewer's question about his salary."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"oblivion","p":"noun","d":"The state of being completely forgotten, or of being unaware of what is happening around you.","lb":"forgottenness, unawareness","s":["obscurity","forgetfulness","limbo","anonymity","unconsciousness","nothingness"],"k":["annihilation","dormancy","eclipse","extinction"],"a":["fame","remembrance","awareness","recognition"],"ex":["Many wonderful old songs have faded into oblivion because nobody records them anymore.","After months of nonstop work, he fell into bed and sank into blissful oblivion.","The small town's name drifted into oblivion after the new highway bypassed it."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"obscure","p":"adjective","d":"Hard to understand because it is not clearly expressed, or little known and not famous.","lb":"unclear, little-known","s":["unclear","vague","cryptic","ambiguous","unknown","hidden"],"k":["concealed","dark","enigmatic","incomprehensible"],"a":["clear","obvious","plain","famous"],"ex":["The instructions were so obscure that nobody in the office could set up the printer.","She wrote her thesis on an obscure poet whom almost nobody has heard of.","My grandfather often uses obscure village sayings that even my father has to explain."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"obsequious","p":"adjective","d":"Too eager to please or obey an important person, in a way that seems weak or insincere.","lb":"servile, fawning","s":["servile","fawning","groveling","subservient","toadying","unctuous"],"k":["bootlicking","cringing","docile","insincere"],"a":["assertive","independent","arrogant","defiant"],"ex":["The obsequious assistant laughed at every joke the director made, even the boring ones.","I dislike obsequious waiters who bow low and keep praising every choice a guest makes.","He became obsequious whenever the teacher entered, offering to carry her bag and clean the board."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"obstinate","p":"adjective","d":"Refusing to change your opinion or behavior, even when there are good reasons to do so.","lb":"stubborn, headstrong","s":["stubborn","headstrong","pigheaded","willful","mulish","inflexible"],"k":["adamant","bullheaded","cantankerous","contrary"],"a":["flexible","yielding","compliant","docile"],"ex":["My little brother is so obstinate that he refuses to wear a jacket even in winter.","The obstinate donkey would not move, no matter how hard the farmer pulled.","She remained obstinate about the plan, ignoring all the warnings from her friends."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"obstreperous","p":"adjective","d":"Noisy, difficult to control and stubbornly unwilling to follow rules or orders.","lb":"noisy, unruly","s":["unruly","rowdy","disorderly","boisterous","unmanageable","rebellious"],"k":["aggressive","belligerent","defiant","fractious"],"a":["docile","obedient","quiet","orderly"],"ex":["The obstreperous child kicked the chair and refused to sit quietly.","An obstreperous guest shouted at the waiter and refused to leave.","The substitute teacher struggled with an obstreperous class."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"obtrusive","p":"adjective","d":"Noticeable in an unpleasant or unwelcome way, especially because it sticks out or draws too much attention.","lb":"noticeable, intrusive","s":["noticeable","conspicuous","intrusive","prominent","unwelcome","jarring"],"k":["brash","evident","flashy","garish"],"a":["unobtrusive","discreet","inconspicuous","subtle"],"ex":["The large advertisement boards were obtrusive and spoiled the view of the lake.","A good waiter is attentive but never obtrusive.","The speaker's obtrusive gestures distracted the audience from his message."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"obtuse","p":"adjective","d":"Slow to understand something obvious, or unable to notice other people’s feelings.","lb":"dense, insensitive","s":["dense","slow","dull","insensitive","dim"],"k":["dumb","purblind","simple","sluggish"],"a":["sharp","perceptive","quick","bright"],"ex":["Are you being deliberately obtuse, or do you really not see why she is upset?","The manager was obtuse about the staff’s complaints and kept insisting nothing was wrong.","I felt obtuse when everyone else understood the joke before I did."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"obviate","p":"verb","d":"To remove a problem or need so that it is no longer necessary to do something.","lb":"prevent, make unnecessary","s":["prevent","preclude","avert","remove","eliminate","forestall"],"k":["avoid","bypass","deflect","deter"],"a":["require","create","cause","demand"],"ex":["A direct train would obviate the need for changing buses twice.","Online banking has obviated the need to stand in long queues at the branch.","Clear instructions at the start can obviate many questions later in the project."],"b":99,"y":1},{"w":"occlude","p":"verb","d":"To block or close something, such as a passage, vessel or opening, so that nothing can pass through.","lb":"block, obstruct","s":["block","obstruct","clog","close","stop up","plug"],"k":["blockade","close up","hinder","impede"],"a":["open","clear","unblock","free"],"ex":["A blood clot occluded the artery, so the patient needed urgent surgery.","A tall new building occludes our view of the river from the balcony.","Fallen leaves occluded the drain, and the street flooded after the first rain."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"occult","p":"noun","d":"Mysterious magical or supernatural powers, beliefs and practices, usually used with the word the.","lb":"supernatural, magic","s":["supernatural","magic","sorcery","witchcraft","mysticism","black magic"],"k":["alchemy","astrology","divination","hermeticism"],"a":[],"ex":["The library has a small shelf of old books about the occult.","Her interest in the occult began after she watched a documentary about ancient magic.","The horror film is full of the occult, with strange symbols, spells and mysterious rituals."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"odious","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely unpleasant and deserving of hatred.","lb":"hateful, vile","s":["hateful","detestable","repugnant","vile","loathsome","abhorrent"],"k":["abominable","disgusting","execrable","foul"],"a":["lovable","delightful","pleasant","admirable"],"ex":["Cleaning the blocked drain was an odious job that nobody wanted to do.","Everyone found his odious habit of insulting waiters impossible to ignore.","The villagers despised the odious moneylender who charged very high interest."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"odyssey","p":"noun","d":"A long, difficult journey full of adventures and changes.","lb":"long journey, quest","s":["journey","voyage","trek","quest","expedition","adventure"],"k":["crusade","exodus","journeying","peregrination"],"a":[],"ex":["Our bus trip home during Eid turned into a twelve-hour odyssey of traffic jams and broken bridges.","She wrote a book about her odyssey across Asia by train and bus.","For the refugees, the journey was a painful odyssey that lasted many months."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"offended","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling upset, hurt or angry because someone has said or done something rude or unfair.","lb":"hurt, insulted","s":["insulted","hurt","upset","resentful","aggrieved","wounded"],"k":["affronted","huffy","injured","miffed"],"a":["pleased","flattered","delighted","appeased"],"ex":["Rafi felt offended when his friends laughed at his accent.","She was offended that nobody thanked her for organizing the party.","Please don't be offended, but I think your essay needs a clearer conclusion."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"officious","p":"adjective","d":"Too eager to give orders or advice that nobody asked for.","lb":"meddlesome, bossy","s":["meddlesome","interfering","bossy","intrusive","pushy","overbearing"],"k":["authoritarian","autocratic","busy","fussy"],"a":["unobtrusive","reserved","retiring","modest"],"ex":["An officious security guard stopped us and told us how to hold our own bags.","My officious neighbor keeps telling us how to raise our children.","The officious clerk insisted on checking our papers three times, though they were already stamped."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"offspring","p":"noun","d":"A person's child or children, or the young of an animal or plant.","lb":"children, young","s":["children","descendants","young","progeny","kids","brood"],"k":["litter","offshoot","posterity","relation"],"a":["parent","parents","ancestor","forebear"],"ex":["The couple's offspring all became teachers, just like their parents.","A mother tiger fiercely protects her offspring from danger.","Parents should be proud of their offspring's effort, not only their marks."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"olfactory","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the sense of smell or to the act of smelling.","lb":"of smell","s":["nasal"],"k":["aromatic","odoriferous","osmatic","scent-based"],"a":[],"ex":["Dogs have a far more powerful olfactory sense than humans, which helps them track missing people.","The scientist studied how the olfactory nerve sends signals about smells to the brain.","A heavy cold can dull your olfactory sense, so food seems to have no flavour."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"oligarchy","p":"noun","d":"A system of government, or a country, in which a small group of people holds all the power.","lb":"elite rule","s":["elite rule","ruling clique","cabal","clique","minority rule","aristocracy"],"k":["coterie","establishment","faction","form of government"],"a":["democracy","majority rule","popular rule"],"ex":["In our history lesson, we learned that some Greek city-states were ruled by an oligarchy of rich families.","The article warned that a country can become an oligarchy when a few families control the banks and media.","A student club run by three friends who never ask for opinions is more of an oligarchy than a democracy."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ominous","p":"adjective","d":"Giving the feeling that something bad or dangerous is about to happen.","lb":"threatening, foreboding","s":["threatening","menacing","sinister","foreboding","inauspicious","unpromising"],"k":["alarming","baleful","dire","forbidding"],"a":["promising","auspicious","encouraging","favourable"],"ex":["Dark, ominous clouds gathered over the Bay of Bengal, warning of a cyclone.","An ominous silence followed the loud crash in the next room.","The doctor's serious tone sounded ominous."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"omission","p":"noun","d":"Something that has been left out, or the act of leaving it out.","lb":"exclusion, oversight","s":["exclusion","oversight","gap","lapse","neglect","deletion"],"k":["deficiency","disuse","hiatus","lacuna"],"a":["inclusion","addition","insertion"],"ex":["The omission of his name from the list upset him.","A single omission in the report can mislead the whole committee.","The teacher marked the omission of the final step as a serious error."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"omit","p":"verb","d":"To leave something out, either on purpose or by mistake.","lb":"leave out, exclude","s":["leave out","exclude","skip","miss","drop","neglect"],"k":["bypass","disregard","forget","gloss over"],"a":["include","add","insert","incorporate"],"ex":["Please do not omit any steps when you solve the problem.","The editor omitted two paragraphs to make the article fit on one page.","I accidentally omitted my phone number from the application form."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"omnipotent","p":"adjective","d":"Having complete, unlimited power to do anything.","lb":"all-powerful, almighty","s":["almighty","supreme","invincible","sovereign","mighty","unstoppable"],"k":["absolute","boundless","divine","godlike"],"a":["powerless","helpless","weak","impotent"],"ex":["In the story, the omnipotent wizard can change the weather with one wave of his hand.","No manager is omnipotent; even the top boss needs the support of the team.","Small children often think their parents are omnipotent and can fix every problem."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"omnipresence","p":"noun","d":"The state of being present everywhere at the same time.","lb":"ubiquity, being everywhere","s":["ubiquity"],"k":["constant presence","pervasion","presence","prevalence"],"a":["absence","scarcity","rarity"],"ex":["The omnipresence of cameras in the shopping mall made some customers uncomfortable.","The omnipresence of advertising makes it hard to find a quiet space free from ads.","Locals complained about the omnipresence of noise from the nearby highway."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"omnipresent","p":"adjective","d":"Present in every place at the same time, or seeming to be found everywhere.","lb":"ubiquitous, everywhere","s":["ubiquitous","universal","pervasive","widespread","inescapable","everywhere"],"k":["common","commonplace","extensive","general"],"a":["absent","rare","scarce","localized"],"ex":["Smartphones are omnipresent now, even in small villages and tea stalls.","Advertisements have become omnipresent, appearing on buses, buildings, apps and even shop receipts.","In the weeks before Eid, discount banners are omnipresent along every shopping street."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"omniscient","p":"adjective","d":"Knowing everything, or seeming to know everything.","lb":"all-knowing","s":["infinitely wise","wise"],"k":["clairvoyant","erudite","prescient","sapient"],"a":["ignorant","uninformed","unknowing"],"ex":["No teacher is omniscient; sometimes they have to look up an answer.","In the novel, an omniscient narrator reveals what every character is thinking.","Children often think their parents are omniscient until they grow up."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"onerous","p":"adjective","d":"Needing a lot of effort or work and causing worry; hard to bear.","lb":"burdensome, demanding","s":["heavy","demanding","taxing","oppressive","arduous","exacting"],"k":["grueling","hard","rigorous","stringent"],"a":["easy","light","effortless","simple"],"ex":["Filling in the visa forms was an onerous task that took the whole weekend.","The new tax rules placed an onerous burden on small shop owners.","She found the long night shifts so onerous that she asked for a change."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"opaque","p":"adjective","d":"Not allowing light to pass through, so that you cannot see through it.","lb":"not transparent, cloudy","s":["cloudy","murky","frosted","impenetrable","dark","blurred"],"k":["fogged","foggy","incomprehensible","indistinct"],"a":["transparent","clear","translucent","limpid"],"ex":["The bathroom window is made of opaque glass, so nobody can see inside.","After the storm, the river water turned brown and opaque.","A thick layer of fog made the car windshield opaque, and the driver had to stop."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"oppressive","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling heavy and hard to bear, such as very hot, damp air or a gloomy atmosphere.","lb":"stifling, heavy","s":["stifling","suffocating","sultry","muggy","close","heavy"],"k":["airless","clammy","domineering","humid"],"a":["refreshing","pleasant","airy","comfortable"],"ex":["The oppressive heat during load-shedding made it impossible to sleep.","An oppressive silence filled the room after the manager announced the layoffs.","The oppressive humidity before the storm left everyone sticky and tired."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"opprobrious","p":"adjective","d":"Expressing strong criticism or scorn in an abusive and offensive way.","lb":"abusive, scornful","s":["abusive","insulting","scornful","contemptuous","derogatory","vituperative"],"k":["black","demeaning","disdainful","disgraceful"],"a":["complimentary","respectful","flattering","polite"],"ex":["Fans hurled opprobrious remarks at the referee after the unfair decision.","The newspaper apologised for its opprobrious description of the local school.","Teachers must never use opprobrious language when correcting students."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"opprobrium","p":"noun","d":"Strong public criticism and shame that follow shameful or offensive behavior.","lb":"disgrace, censure","s":["disgrace","shame","infamy","disrepute","censure","condemnation"],"k":["calumny","castigation","denunciation","humiliation"],"a":["honor","praise","esteem","glory"],"ex":["The footballer's rude gesture drew public opprobrium from fans and newspapers alike.","The company faced widespread opprobrium after it was found dumping waste into the river.","He endured the opprobrium of his neighbors for years after the scandal."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"optical disk","p":"noun","d":"A flat round plate, such as a CD or DVD, that stores digital data which a laser reads.","lb":"data disc","s":["compact disc"],"k":["cd-r","cd-rom","dvd-rom","laserdisc"],"a":[],"ex":["An optical disk can hold music, films or computer files that a laser reads.","Our old computer can read an optical disk, though most new laptops no longer include a drive for one.","Scratches on the surface of an optical disk can make the data impossible to read."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"optimistic","p":"adjective","d":"Hopeful and confident that good things will happen in the future.","lb":"hopeful, positive","s":["hopeful","positive","confident","upbeat","sanguine","bright"],"k":["affirmative","buoyant","certain","encouraged"],"a":["pessimistic","gloomy","negative","hopeless"],"ex":["Rafi is optimistic about his results because he studied hard all year.","The doctor was optimistic that the patient would recover quickly.","Farmers are optimistic about a good harvest after the early rains."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"opulence","p":"noun","d":"Great wealth shown through a very rich, luxurious style of living or decoration.","lb":"luxury, wealth","s":["luxury","affluence","richness","splendor","wealth","grandeur"],"k":["glitz","magnificence","munificence","pomp"],"a":["poverty","austerity","simplicity","frugality"],"ex":["Visitors were amazed by the opulence of the hotel lobby, with its marble floors and chandeliers.","The family lived in opulence, with servants, three cars and a huge garden.","The documentary compared the opulence of the city's richest neighborhood with life in nearby slums."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"opulent","p":"adjective","d":"Very rich and luxurious, in a way that shows great wealth.","lb":"luxurious, lavish","s":["luxurious","lavish","sumptuous","plush","rich","wealthy"],"k":["affluent","deluxe","gilded","lush"],"a":["modest","plain","austere","simple"],"ex":["The wedding was held in an opulent hall decorated with gold curtains and hundreds of fresh flowers.","Guests were amazed by the opulent lobby, with its marble floor and giant crystal lights.","She grew up in an opulent house, but she still learned to cook and clean for herself."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"ordeal","p":"noun","d":"A very difficult or painful experience that tests your strength and patience.","lb":"hardship, trial","s":["trial","hardship","nightmare","torment","suffering","test"],"k":["affliction","baptism of fire","crucible","examination"],"a":["pleasure","delight","joy","ease"],"ex":["Waiting eight hours at the airport after the flight was canceled was a real ordeal.","The rescued hikers described their three-day ordeal in the cold mountains.","For many students, the oral exam is more of an ordeal than the written test."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ordinance","p":"noun","d":"A rule or law made by a government, especially by a local authority such as a city council.","lb":"law, regulation","s":["law","regulation","rule","statute","bylaw","decree"],"k":["act","code","command","fiat"],"a":[],"ex":["A city ordinance forbids loud music after ten o'clock at night.","The council passed an ordinance requiring dog owners to keep their pets on a lead in the park.","Under the local ordinance, you need a permit to hold a street party."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ornate","p":"adjective","d":"Decorated with many detailed patterns or shapes; very elaborate in style.","lb":"decorated, elaborate","s":["elaborate","decorative","fancy","intricate","embellished","flowery"],"k":["curlicued","filigreed","flamboyant","florid"],"a":["plain","simple","unadorned","austere"],"ex":["The old palace has an ornate ceiling covered with tiny painted flowers.","She wore an ornate gold necklace to her cousin's wedding.","I prefer simple furniture to the ornate chairs my aunt collects."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"orthodox","p":"adjective","d":"Following traditional or generally accepted beliefs, customs or methods.","lb":"conventional, traditional","s":["conventional","traditional","standard","accepted","established","customary"],"k":["by the book","canonical","conforming","doctrinaire"],"a":["unorthodox","unconventional","radical","nonconformist"],"ex":["The teacher is not orthodox; she uses games and songs instead of long lectures.","Many doctors now combine orthodox medicine with healthy changes in diet and exercise.","His orthodox approach to cooking means he follows his grandmother's recipe exactly."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"oscillate","p":"verb","d":"To swing or move back and forth regularly, or to keep changing between two opinions or moods.","lb":"swing, waver","s":["swing","sway","fluctuate","vacillate","waver","seesaw"],"k":["dither","falter","hesitate","hover"],"a":["stabilize","hold steady","settle","persist"],"ex":["The pendulum of the old clock oscillates once every second.","My mood oscillates between excitement and fear before every big exam.","Prices oscillated between low and high levels throughout the week at the vegetable market."],"b":43,"y":0},{"w":"osmosis","p":"noun","d":"The slow, natural absorption of something, such as ideas and habits picked up without effort, or water passing through a thin membrane.","lb":"absorption, soaking up","s":["absorption","assimilation","diffusion","infiltration","seepage","soaking up"],"k":["contagion","cross-pollination","filtration","transfer"],"a":[],"ex":["Living abroad, she learned the language almost by osmosis, just by listening to people every day.","Don’t expect to pass the test by osmosis; sleeping on your textbook won’t help.","In biology class, we watched water move into the potato slices by osmosis."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ossify","p":"verb","d":"To become rigid and unwilling to change, often because of age or routine.","lb":"harden, stagnate","s":["harden","stiffen","stagnate","calcify","solidify","freeze"],"k":["cement","crystallize","dig in","entrench"],"a":["adapt","evolve","loosen","soften"],"ex":["Without fresh ideas, the old company ossified and lost customers to smaller, faster rivals.","Some school rules have ossified over the years, even though nobody remembers their purpose.","Habits can ossify if you never try anything new."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"ostensible","p":"adjective","d":"Appearing or claimed to be true, though it may not be the real reason.","lb":"apparent, supposed","s":["apparent","supposed","professed","alleged","purported","seeming"],"k":["avowed","counterfeit","nominal","on paper"],"a":["real","actual","genuine","true"],"ex":["The ostensible reason for the meeting was to discuss the budget, but everyone wanted to talk about layoffs.","His ostensible purpose in visiting was to return a book, but he really wanted to meet her family.","The ostensible winner of the contest was later disqualified for breaking the rules."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"ostentatious","p":"adjective","d":"Designed to attract attention and impress people, especially by showing off wealth.","lb":"showy, flashy","s":["showy","flashy","pretentious","flamboyant","gaudy","boastful"],"k":["brassy","cheap","conceited","grandiose"],"a":["modest","simple","unpretentious","subdued"],"ex":["The ostentatious wedding, with hundreds of guests and a golden stage, was the talk of the town.","He drove an ostentatious sports car that nobody on the street could miss.","Her ostentatious jewelry made the simple family gathering feel awkward."],"b":541,"y":0},{"w":"ostracize","p":"verb","d":"To deliberately keep someone out of a group by refusing to talk to them or include them.","lb":"shun, exclude","s":["shun","exclude","banish","snub","blacklist","boycott"],"k":["ban","blackball","eschew","excommunicate"],"a":["welcome","include","accept","embrace"],"ex":["The new student was ostracized by his classmates for no good reason.","After the argument, she felt ostracized by her friends at work.","Villagers once ostracized families who broke old customs."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"oust","p":"verb","d":"To force someone out of a position or place, especially by using pressure or power.","lb":"expel, remove","s":["expel","remove","eject","dismiss","depose","topple"],"k":["boot out","chuck out","dethrone","dislodge"],"a":["install","appoint","welcome","reinstate"],"ex":["The members voted to oust the club president after the money went missing.","The landlord tried to oust the family from the flat because they had paid no rent.","Rival teams are always trying to oust the champions from the top of the table."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"outcry","p":"noun","d":"A strong public reaction of anger or protest about something that people think is wrong.","lb":"public protest","s":["protest","uproar","clamor","furor","objection","commotion"],"k":["din","hubbub","noise","racket"],"a":["approval","acceptance","applause","silence"],"ex":["The decision to cut the bus service caused a public outcry in the town.","After the outcry from parents, the school withdrew the new fee.","Social media users raised an outcry against the unsafe construction site."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"outline","p":"verb","d":"To describe the main points of something briefly, without giving every detail.","lb":"summarize, sketch","s":["summarize","sketch","review","recap","draft","delineate"],"k":["adumbrate","depict","describe","draw"],"a":["elaborate","detail","expand"],"ex":["The manager outlined the new project plan in a five-minute meeting.","Before writing your essay, outline your main arguments on a single page.","The chairman outlined the company's budget in a short speech and left the details for later."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"outwit","p":"verb","d":"To defeat or gain an advantage over someone by being cleverer than they are.","lb":"outsmart","s":["outsmart","outmaneuver","outthink","trick","get the better of","overcome"],"k":["bamboozle","beat out","circumvent","crush"],"a":[],"ex":["The young chess champion outwitted the older players with a clever trap.","The fox outwits the hunters in the old folk tale.","Cyber criminals try to outwit security systems, so banks update their software often."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"overdraw","p":"verb","d":"To take more money out of a bank account than it contains.","lb":"overspend, exceed balance","s":["go into the red","exceed your balance","withdraw too much","exceed your limit"],"k":["bounce","dip into reserves","draw","draw off"],"a":["stay in credit","save","deposit"],"ex":["If you overdraw your account, the bank may charge you a heavy fee.","Rafi was careful not to overdraw his account while he waited for his salary.","Overdrawing your account every month is a sign that you need a simpler budget."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"overdue","p":"adjective","d":"Not paid, returned or done by the expected or agreed time.","lb":"late, delayed","s":["late","delayed","belated","unpaid","behind schedule","tardy"],"k":["delinquent","due","in arrears","owing"],"a":["early","prompt","punctual","timely"],"ex":["My library book is two weeks overdue, so I must pay a small fine.","The electricity bill is overdue, and they may cut the connection.","A holiday is long overdue after months of hard work."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"overlooked","p":"adjective","d":"Not noticed, or not given enough attention or credit.","lb":"unnoticed, ignored","s":["neglected","ignored","unnoticed","disregarded","missed","forgotten"],"k":["obscure","sidelined","underrated","underused"],"a":["noticed","recognized","appreciated","valued"],"ex":["She found the error in an overlooked line at the bottom of the page.","Small shops are often overlooked by tourists who prefer the big malls.","The overlooked student at the back of the class turned out to be the top scorer."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"override","p":"verb","d":"To cancel or overrule a decision, or to take control away from something that works automatically.","lb":"overrule, cancel","s":["overrule","overturn","cancel","reverse","veto","countermand"],"k":["annul","bypass","disregard","invalidate"],"a":["uphold","approve","confirm","support"],"ex":["The manager can override the committee's decision, but she rarely uses that power.","In an emergency, the pilot can override the autopilot and fly the plane by hand.","You can override the phone's automatic brightness by moving the slider yourself."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"overtake","p":"verb","d":"To catch up with and pass a vehicle or person moving in the same direction.","lb":"pass, outstrip","s":["pass","go past","outstrip","overhaul","leave behind","get ahead of"],"k":["advance","catch","catch up with","exceed"],"a":["fall behind","lag behind","trail","follow"],"ex":["It is dangerous to overtake a truck on a narrow road.","The bus driver overtook three rickshaws before the traffic light turned red.","A younger runner overtook him in the last hundred metres."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"overture","p":"noun","d":"A first step or offer made to start a discussion, friendship or agreement.","lb":"approach, proposal","s":["approach","advance","proposal","offer","initiative","proposition"],"k":["bid","gambit","olive branch","plan"],"a":[],"ex":["The two companies made friendly overtures to each other before agreeing to merge.","After years of silence, Rafi made an overture to his old friend by sending him a message.","The manager made an overture to the striking workers by offering to meet their leaders."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"oxymoron","p":"noun","d":"A phrase that joins two words with opposite meanings, such as “deafening silence”.","lb":"contradiction, paradox","s":["contradiction in terms","paradox","antithesis","incongruity"],"k":["absurdity","antinomy","catachresis","contradiction"],"a":[],"ex":["“Jumbo shrimp” is a funny oxymoron because jumbo means huge and shrimp means small.","My brother says “working holiday” is an oxymoron, since a holiday should mean rest.","“Deafening silence” is an oxymoron that writers use to show how heavy a quiet moment feels."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pacify","p":"verb","d":"To calm someone who is angry, upset or crying, often by giving them something.","lb":"calm, soothe","s":["calm","soothe","placate","appease","mollify","comfort"],"k":["assuage","calm down","ease","humor"],"a":["anger","agitate","provoke","inflame"],"ex":["The mother gave the crying baby a toy to pacify him.","The shop manager offered a refund to pacify the angry customer.","Nothing could pacify my cousin after she lost her phone on the bus."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"painstaking","p":"adjective","d":"Done with great care, effort and attention to every small detail.","lb":"thorough, meticulous","s":["meticulous","careful","thorough","diligent","scrupulous","conscientious"],"k":["exact","fastidious","finicky","particular"],"a":["careless","sloppy","negligent","slapdash"],"ex":["The restorers did painstaking work to bring the old painting back to its original colors.","After painstaking research, the students found the exact source of the quote.","She counted the money with painstaking care so that nothing would go missing."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"palatable","p":"adjective","d":"Pleasant enough to eat or drink, or acceptable enough to be agreed to.","lb":"tasty, acceptable","s":["tasty","edible","pleasant","acceptable","agreeable","appetizing"],"k":["appealing","digestible","eatable","lovely"],"a":["disgusting","unacceptable","distasteful","bitter"],"ex":["Adding a little sugar made the bitter medicine palatable for the child.","The new rules were made more palatable by a small pay rise.","The manager offered a compromise that was palatable to both sides."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pale","p":"adjective","d":"Having very little color; light in shade, or, of a face, lacking its normal color.","lb":"light, colorless","s":["light","pallid","pasty","colorless","faded","wan"],"k":["anemic","sick","thin","weak"],"a":["dark","deep","vivid","rosy"],"ex":["She turned pale with fear when she heard the strange noise downstairs.","The doctor said my pale face and tired eyes were signs of low iron.","The walls of the nursery are painted a pale yellow."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"palliate","p":"verb","d":"To make a pain or problem less severe without curing it.","lb":"ease, relieve","s":["alleviate","relieve","ease","soothe","mitigate","lessen"],"k":["ameliorate","amend","appease","diminish"],"a":["aggravate","worsen","intensify","exacerbate"],"ex":["The nurse gave him medicine to palliate the pain, though it could not cure the disease.","Temporary bus lanes may palliate traffic jams, but they will not solve the underlying problem.","Relief workers tried to palliate the villagers' hunger with packets of food."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"pallor","p":"noun","d":"An unhealthy paleness of the face, often caused by illness, fear or shock.","lb":"paleness, whiteness","s":["whiteness","lack of colour","lividity"],"k":["ashiness","bloodlessness","complexion","sallowness"],"a":["flush","colour","glow","blush"],"ex":["The nurse noticed the pallor of the patient's face and called the doctor immediately.","Fear drained the colour from her cheeks, leaving a ghostly pallor.","Weeks of illness had left him with a thin face and an unhealthy pallor."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"palpable","p":"adjective","d":"So strong or obvious that it can almost be felt or touched.","lb":"obvious, tangible","s":["obvious","tangible","noticeable","evident","clear","perceptible"],"k":["concrete","conspicuous","intense","patent"],"a":["imperceptible","intangible","hidden","vague"],"ex":["The tension in the exam hall was palpable as the invigilator handed out the papers.","There was palpable relief in the room when the doctor said the surgery had gone well.","The excitement in the stadium was almost palpable before the cricket match started."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"paltry","p":"adjective","d":"Very small in amount or value, and so disappointing or not worth considering.","lb":"meager, trifling","s":["meager","trifling","trivial","measly","miserly","petty"],"k":["inconsequential","meagre","minor","miserable"],"a":["generous","substantial","ample","considerable"],"ex":["The factory workers were paid a paltry wage that hardly covered their rent.","He offered a paltry excuse for missing the meeting, and nobody believed it.","A paltry sum of fifty taka was all she had left at the end of the week."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"panacea","p":"noun","d":"A single solution believed to cure all problems or diseases.","lb":"cure-all, remedy","s":["elixir","nostrum","magic bullet","universal remedy","miracle cure","quick fix"],"k":["catholicon","curative","panpharmacon","remedy"],"a":[],"ex":["Technology is not a panacea; it cannot solve every problem in education.","Some websites sell herbal drinks as a panacea for every illness.","Exercise helps many conditions, but doctors warn that it is not a panacea."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"pandemic","p":"adjective","d":"Spreading across a very large area or the whole world, especially of a disease.","lb":"widespread, global","s":["widespread","global","worldwide","universal","epidemic","prevalent"],"k":["common","extensive","general","intercontinental"],"a":["local","isolated","limited","contained"],"ex":["Doctors feared that the new flu would become pandemic within a few weeks.","Pandemic diseases spread quickly because people travel by air so easily.","Health officials track pandemic outbreaks using reports from hospitals in many countries."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"panegyric","p":"noun","d":"A speech or piece of writing that praises someone or something very highly.","lb":"tribute, eulogy","s":["eulogy","tribute","praise","accolade","encomium","homage"],"k":["acclaim","compliment","congratulations","hymn"],"a":["attack","criticism","diatribe","condemnation"],"ex":["At her retirement party, the principal delivered a panegyric on her thirty years of teaching.","The newspaper's panegyric to the young scientist filled the whole front page.","His speech at the wedding was a panegyric to his late father's kindness."],"b":44,"y":0},{"w":"parable","p":"noun","d":"A short, simple story that teaches a moral or spiritual lesson.","lb":"allegory, moral tale","s":["allegory","fable","moral tale","morality tale","lesson","story"],"k":["anecdote","fiction","homily","illustration"],"a":[],"ex":["The teacher told a parable about two farmers to show why honesty matters.","My grandfather often explained difficult ideas by telling a short parable.","The film works as a parable about greed and what it does to families."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"parade","p":"noun","d":"A public event in which people march or drive in a line along a street, often to celebrate something.","lb":"procession, march","s":["procession","march","cavalcade","motorcade","pageant","display"],"k":["carnival","cortege","promenade","review"],"a":[],"ex":["The school band led the parade through the main street on Independence Day.","Children watched the parade from their balconies and waved colourful flags.","A parade of decorated trucks moved slowly through the city during the festival."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"paradigm","p":"noun","d":"A typical model or pattern of how something is done, understood or thought about.","lb":"model, pattern","s":["model","pattern","example","template","standard","archetype"],"k":["blueprint","epitome","frame of reference","image"],"a":[],"ex":["The smartphone changed the old paradigm of how people take photos and share them.","This village school became a paradigm for how a small team can teach well.","The discovery forced scientists to abandon the old paradigm and build a new theory."],"b":146,"y":0},{"w":"paradox","p":"noun","d":"A statement or situation that seems impossible or self-contradictory but may actually be true.","lb":"contradiction, puzzle","s":["contradiction","anomaly","puzzle","enigma","inconsistency","oxymoron"],"k":["catch-22","contradiction in terms","dilemma","double bind"],"a":[],"ex":["It is a paradox that the more friends we have online, the lonelier we sometimes feel.","The paradox of the big city is that you can feel alone among millions of people.","“Less is more” sounds like a paradox, but a simple design often works best."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"paragon","p":"noun","d":"A person or thing that is an excellent example of a particular good quality.","lb":"model, ideal","s":["model","ideal","exemplar","epitome","standard","pattern"],"k":["apotheosis","beau ideal","example","good example"],"a":["failure","disgrace"],"ex":["Our headmaster is a paragon of patience, even on the noisiest days.","She is a paragon of honesty and once returned a lost wallet with all the money inside.","Nobody is a paragon of perfection, so do not expect your new manager to know everything."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"parallel","p":"adjective","d":"Very similar or closely matching, so that the two things can be compared.","lb":"similar, comparable","s":["similar","comparable","analogous","matching","corresponding","equivalent"],"k":["collateral","equal","related","symmetric"],"a":["different","unlike","dissimilar","opposite"],"ex":["Two parallel cases reached the court on the same day, and the judge treated both alike.","The sisters led parallel lives, both becoming teachers and both marrying young.","The two stories follow parallel plots, though one is set in a village and the other in a city."],"b":424,"y":0},{"w":"paramecia","p":"noun","d":"Tiny single-celled organisms, shaped like slippers, that live in pond water and move using tiny hairs.","lb":"microscopic organisms","s":["protozoa","microorganisms"],"k":["microbe","single-celled organism","slipper animalcule","unicellular organism"],"a":[],"ex":["In biology class, we saw paramecia swimming across a drop of pond water under the microscope.","Paramecia move by beating thousands of tiny hairs called cilia.","The students added a little cotton fibre to slow the paramecia so they could draw them."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"paranoia","p":"noun","d":"An unreasonable and extreme fear or suspicion that other people want to harm or trick you.","lb":"suspicion, distrust","s":["suspicion","distrust","persecution complex","delusion","mistrust","obsession"],"k":["apprehension","doubt","dread","hypervigilance"],"a":["trust","confidence","faith","openness"],"ex":["After the data leak, his paranoia grew, and he covered his laptop camera.","Paranoia made her believe that her colleagues were secretly talking about her.","A little paranoia about security is healthy online, but too much is exhausting."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"paranormal","p":"adjective","d":"Not explainable by science or normal experience, such as ghosts or mind reading.","lb":"supernatural, unexplained","s":["supernatural","unexplained","psychic","mystical","otherworldly","occult"],"k":["clairvoyant","eerie","eldritch","extrasensory"],"a":["natural","normal","ordinary","explainable"],"ex":["My cousin loves paranormal stories and reads about ghosts every night before bed.","The scientist said there was no paranormal explanation for the strange noises; the pipes were old.","Many people claim paranormal experiences, but few can prove them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"parochial","p":"adjective","d":"Concerned only with your own small area or group, and not interested in wider issues or other views.","lb":"narrow-minded, provincial","s":["provincial","insular","narrow","petty","local","limited"],"k":["blinkered","cloistered","hidebound","inward-looking"],"a":["cosmopolitan","worldly","universal"],"ex":["The council’s parochial attitude meant it refused to share its flood-control plans with the next district.","Travelling abroad for a year cured him of the parochial view that his town was the center of everything.","A good manager avoids parochial thinking and listens to ideas from every department, not just her own."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"parody","p":"noun","d":"A funny imitation of a serious work or style, made to make fun of it.","lb":"spoof, send-up","s":["spoof","satire","mockery","takeoff","lampoon","burlesque"],"k":["farce","impersonation","mock-heroic","pastiche"],"a":[],"ex":["The students performed a parody of the school assembly, and even the principal laughed.","His video is a parody of a famous cooking show, with burnt toast as the main dish.","The magazine published a parody of the newspaper's front page."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"paroxysm","p":"noun","d":"A sudden, strong attack or outburst of an emotion, an action or an illness.","lb":"fit, outburst","s":["fit","outburst","spasm","convulsion","attack","seizure"],"k":["effusion","flare-up","frenzy","outbreak"],"a":["calm","lull","remission"],"ex":["A paroxysm of coughing forced him to leave the lecture hall.","She burst into a paroxysm of laughter when her little brother tried to talk in a funny voice.","In a paroxysm of rage, he threw his phone across the room."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"parsimonious","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely unwilling to spend money or give anything away.","lb":"stingy, miserly","s":["stingy","miserly","tightfisted","cheap","mean"],"k":["cheeseparing","economical","frugal","grasping"],"a":["generous","lavish","extravagant","liberal"],"ex":["My parsimonious uncle gives only a small note as Eid money, even to his favorite nephews.","The company was so parsimonious with salaries that its best engineers left within a year.","She is parsimonious with praise, so a simple \"good\" from her feels like a medal."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"part","p":"noun","d":"A piece or section of something, rather than the whole.","lb":"piece, portion","s":["piece","portion","section","segment","fraction","share"],"k":["character","component part","constituent","contribution"],"a":["whole","entirety","total","sum"],"ex":["The first part of the exam is multiple choice, and the second part is writing.","Rice is an important part of every meal in Bangladesh.","Part of the road was closed for repairs, so the bus took a longer way."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"partake","p":"verb","d":"To take part in an activity, or to eat or drink something that is offered.","lb":"participate, share","s":["participate","share","join in","take part","engage","consume"],"k":["dig in","dine","have","imbibe"],"a":["abstain","refrain","decline","refuse"],"ex":["All students are welcome to partake in the school's annual sports day.","The guests partook of a simple meal of rice, lentils and fried fish.","Doctors advise people with heart problems not to partake in heavy exercise without a checkup."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"partisan","p":"adjective","d":"Strongly supporting one person, group or cause, often without being fair to others.","lb":"biased, one-sided","s":["biased","prejudiced","partial","committed","devoted","slanted"],"k":["bigoted","colored","lopsided","one-eyed"],"a":["impartial","neutral","unbiased","objective"],"ex":["The referee faced a noisy, partisan crowd that booed every decision against the home team.","A partisan reviewer praised the book only because the author was his close friend.","Our class debate became partisan, with each group refusing to admit any good point from the other."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"partition","p":"noun","d":"A wall or screen that divides a room or space into parts; also the act of dividing something.","lb":"divider, division","s":["divider","screen","wall","barrier","separation","division"],"k":["bulkhead","carve-up","demarcation","fence"],"a":["union","merger","unification","combination"],"ex":["A thin plywood partition separates the office into two small rooms.","We put up a partition to give each child a private space in the bedroom.","The glass partition between the driver and the passengers keeps the taxi quiet."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"passionate","p":"adjective","d":"Having or showing very strong feelings or great enthusiasm for something.","lb":"intense, enthusiastic","s":["ardent","fervent","intense","enthusiastic","zealous","fiery"],"k":["ablaze","aflame","aroused","choleric"],"a":["apathetic","indifferent","cool","dispassionate"],"ex":["My sister is passionate about astronomy and spends her nights watching the stars.","The coach gave a passionate speech at half-time.","He is a passionate teacher who stays after school to help students."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pastoral","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to peaceful country life, with fields, farms and animals.","lb":"rural, rustic","s":["rural","rustic","country","bucolic","idyllic","agrarian"],"k":["agricultural","georgic","grazing","sylvan"],"a":["urban","city","metropolitan","industrial"],"ex":["The painting shows a pastoral scene of cows grazing beside a quiet river.","After years in the city, he dreamed of a calm, pastoral life in the village.","The poet wrote pastoral verses about green fields and flowing streams."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"patent","p":"adjective","d":"Very obvious and easy to see, especially when describing something bad such as a lie or an error.","lb":"obvious, plain","s":["obvious","evident","clear","apparent","plain","blatant"],"k":["conspicuous","distinct","flagrant","lucid"],"a":["hidden","concealed","obscure","latent"],"ex":["His excuse for missing the class was a patent lie, and everyone knew it.","It was patent from her smile that the interview had gone well.","The advertisement made claims that were patent nonsense, so I did not buy the product."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"paternal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to a father, or showing the caring and protective manner of a father.","lb":"fatherly, protective","s":["fatherly","protective","caring","kindly","benevolent","parental"],"k":["agnate","avuncular","patriarchal","prophylactic"],"a":["maternal","uncaring","neglectful"],"ex":["My paternal grandfather lived in a small village near Rajshahi and grew mangoes.","The coach took a paternal interest in the young players and often asked about their families.","She inherited her curly hair from the paternal side of the family."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"pathological","p":"adjective","d":"Extreme, compulsive and impossible to control, as if caused by an illness.","lb":"compulsive, obsessive","s":["compulsive","obsessive","habitual","irrational","uncontrollable","chronic"],"k":["deranged","diseased","dyed-in-the-wool","incorrigible"],"a":["normal","healthy","rational","moderate"],"ex":["My cousin is a pathological liar who invents stories even when the truth would be easier.","He has a pathological fear of heights and cannot even climb a short ladder.","Her pathological need to win every argument made her friends avoid debates with her."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"pathology","p":"noun","d":"The study of diseases and how they affect the body, especially their causes and effects.","lb":"study of disease","s":["study of disease","diagnostics","etiology","medical science","disease research"],"k":["cytology","epidemiology","histology","toxicology"],"a":[],"ex":["She is studying pathology because she wants to find the causes of diseases.","The hospital's pathology lab tests blood and tissue samples every day.","A pathology report confirmed that the lump was harmless."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"pathos","p":"noun","d":"A quality in a person, event or work of art that makes you feel pity or sadness.","lb":"poignancy, sadness","s":["sadness","pity","sorrow","tragedy","melancholy","sympathy"],"k":["affecting quality","compassion","emotional appeal","emotive quality"],"a":["humor","levity","mirth"],"ex":["The film's pathos comes from a poor boy who saves coins to buy his mother a gift.","The old man's pathos was clear as he waited every evening at the empty bus stop.","Her letter to her late father was full of pathos, and the audience wept."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"patina","p":"noun","d":"A thin green or brown layer that forms on metal over time, or a soft shine that old things get from use.","lb":"tarnish, sheen","s":["sheen","tarnish","film","coating","gloss","luster"],"k":["aged look","coat","glaze","lacquer"],"a":[],"ex":["The old copper pot had developed a green patina after years near the sea.","A soft patina covers the wooden table where generations have eaten their meals.","The new café tried to create a patina of age with scratched furniture."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"patriarch","p":"noun","d":"A man who is the head of a family or tribe, or a respected older man in a group.","lb":"family head, elder","s":["elder","head","father figure","founder","grandfather"],"k":["adult male","archbishop","dean","grand old man"],"a":["matriarch"],"ex":["At family gatherings, Grandfather sits in the middle as the patriarch, and everyone waits for his blessing.","The patriarch of the village settled the land dispute between the two brothers.","After the patriarch died, his three sons took over the family business."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"patrician","p":"noun","d":"A person from a noble or high-ranking family, especially one with refined manners.","lb":"aristocrat, noble","s":["aristocrat","noble","nobleman","blue blood","gentleman","grandee"],"k":["brahmin","gentry","highborn person","leader"],"a":["commoner","plebeian","peasant","proletarian"],"ex":["In ancient Rome, a patrician belonged to one of the oldest and most powerful families.","The old man carried himself like a patrician, always dressed neatly and speaking softly.","The novel is about a patrician who loses his fortune and must learn to work."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"patrimony","p":"noun","d":"Property or heritage passed down from a father or from earlier generations.","lb":"inheritance, heritage","s":["inheritance","legacy","heritage","birthright","bequest","estate"],"k":["ancestral estate","ancestral home","family fortune","family wealth"],"a":[],"ex":["The old farmhouse was the only patrimony he received from his father.","The brothers argued over how to divide their patrimony after their father's death.","The government protects historic buildings as part of the nation's cultural patrimony."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"patronize","p":"verb","d":"To talk or behave toward someone as if they were less intelligent or less important than you.","lb":"talk down to, condescend","s":["condescend to","talk down to","look down on","belittle","baby","demean"],"k":["coddle","condescend","indulge","lord it over"],"a":["respect","defer to","honor","admire"],"ex":["Please don’t patronize me; I understand the instructions perfectly well.","The senior doctor patronized the young intern by explaining basic things very slowly.","Some customers patronize shop assistants and speak to them as if they know nothing."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"paucity","p":"noun","d":"A very small amount or number of something, less than is needed.","lb":"scarcity, shortage","s":["scarcity","shortage","lack","dearth","deficiency","insufficiency"],"k":["absence","deficit","famine","inadequacy"],"a":["abundance","plenty","surplus","excess"],"ex":["There is a paucity of good libraries in our district, so students study at home.","The paucity of evidence meant that the case against him was dropped.","Because of a paucity of volunteers, the school fair was smaller this year."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"peak","p":"noun","d":"The highest point or level of something, such as activity, demand or performance.","lb":"highest point","s":["height","maximum","climax","zenith","top","pinnacle"],"k":["acme","bill","crescendo","crest"],"a":["low","bottom","minimum","nadir"],"ex":["Traffic in Dhaka reaches its peak between five and seven in the evening.","Mango sales hit their peak in June, when the fruit is ripest.","The athlete was at the peak of his fitness before the race."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"pebble","p":"noun","d":"A small, smooth, rounded stone, often found on beaches or in rivers.","lb":"small stone","s":["stone","cobble","rock","shingle"],"k":["boulder","cobblestone","flint","gravel"],"a":[],"ex":["The children skipped flat pebbles across the calm surface of the pond.","A small pebble got stuck in my sandal, so I stopped to shake it out.","The riverbank near our village is covered with smooth, colourful pebbles."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"peccadillo","p":"noun","d":"A small, unimportant mistake or bad habit that is easy to forgive.","lb":"minor fault, slip","s":["petty fault","misdemeanor","indiscretion","slip","lapse","foible"],"k":["fault","faux pas","gaffe","infraction"],"a":[],"ex":["Forgetting to return a library book is only a small peccadillo, not a crime.","Her friends forgave her little peccadillo of always arriving ten minutes late.","The newspaper wasted pages on the actor's harmless peccadilloes instead of real news."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"peculiar","p":"adjective","d":"Strange or unusual in a way that is hard to explain; also belonging only to one person or place.","lb":"odd, unusual","s":["odd","strange","unusual","curious","bizarre","weird"],"k":["characteristic","distinctive","freakish","funny"],"a":["normal","ordinary","usual","typical"],"ex":["There is a peculiar smell in the kitchen, and nobody can find where it comes from.","My uncle has a peculiar habit of laughing quietly before he speaks.","This kind of red soil is peculiar to the hills of this region."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pecuniary","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to or involving money.","lb":"financial, monetary","s":["financial","monetary","fiscal","economic","budgetary","cash"],"k":["commercial","mercantile","moneyed","remunerative"],"a":[],"ex":["The manager denied any pecuniary interest in the company that won the contract.","He had no pecuniary motive; he simply wanted to help the school.","The family faced serious pecuniary difficulties after their shop was destroyed by fire."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"pedagogue","p":"noun","d":"A teacher, especially one who is strict or likes to show off knowledge.","lb":"teacher, educator","s":["teacher","educator","instructor","schoolmaster","tutor","lecturer"],"k":["coach","dominie","don","guru"],"a":[],"ex":["My old math teacher was a stern pedagogue who made us repeat every formula aloud.","A good pedagogue knows that students learn best when they feel safe to ask questions.","The village pedagogue taught every child to read under the big banyan tree."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"pedantic","p":"adjective","d":"Too concerned with small rules or details, especially in order to show how much you know.","lb":"fussy, nitpicking","s":["fussy","hairsplitting","precise","bookish","academic","finicky"],"k":["donnish","meticulous","niggling","persnickety"],"a":["relaxed","casual","easygoing","practical"],"ex":["It may sound pedantic, but a report should say fewer students, not less students.","My pedantic uncle corrects everyone's grammar at the dinner table.","Don't be so pedantic, because nobody cares whether the meeting starts at ten or two minutes past."],"b":17,"y":0},{"w":"pedestrian","p":"adjective","d":"Ordinary and dull, without any imagination, excitement or originality.","lb":"dull, ordinary","s":["dull","ordinary","mundane","uninspired","boring","banal"],"k":["dreary","earthbound","everyday","humdrum"],"a":["exciting","imaginative","original","inspired"],"ex":["The film had a pedestrian plot, so I guessed the ending in the first ten minutes.","Her pedestrian writing style made the long essay hard to finish.","The restaurant's menu was pedestrian: plain rice, plain curry and nothing special."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"pejorative","p":"adjective","d":"Expressing disapproval, criticism or disrespect; meant to make something seem bad or unimportant.","lb":"derogatory, insulting","s":["derogatory","disparaging","belittling","negative","insulting","critical"],"k":["censorious","contemptuous","demeaning","invidious"],"a":["complimentary","flattering","approving","positive"],"ex":["Calling someone \"bossy\" can be pejorative if you mean it as a criticism.","The word \"cheap\" can sound pejorative when it is used about someone's clothes.","She objected to the pejorative way the article described students from small towns."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"penchant","p":"noun","d":"A strong liking or habit of doing a particular thing.","lb":"liking, inclination","s":["liking","fondness","inclination","taste","weakness","partiality"],"k":["affinity","appetite","disposition","predisposition"],"a":["dislike","aversion","distaste","antipathy"],"ex":["My sister has a penchant for collecting old coins from every country she visits.","He has a penchant for arriving late to meetings, which annoys his boss.","The chef's penchant for spicy food shows in almost every dish on the menu."],"b":27,"y":0},{"w":"penitent","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling or showing sorrow for having done something wrong.","lb":"remorseful, sorry","s":["repentant","remorseful","contrite","sorry","regretful","apologetic"],"k":["abashed","atoning","bad","chastened"],"a":["unrepentant","unapologetic","shameless","defiant"],"ex":["The penitent boy handed back the stolen pencil and apologised to his classmate.","She looked penitent as she told her mother she had broken the vase.","A penitent driver admitted to the judge that he should have slowed down."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"pensive","p":"adjective","d":"Deeply thoughtful, often in a quiet and slightly sad way.","lb":"thoughtful, wistful","s":["thoughtful","reflective","contemplative","meditative","wistful","brooding"],"k":["absorbed","broody","distracted","lost in thought"],"a":["carefree","cheerful","lighthearted","thoughtless"],"ex":["She sat by the window in a pensive mood, watching the rain fall on the street.","After reading the letter, my grandfather grew pensive and said nothing for a long time.","The pensive student stared at the exam question for a minute before writing."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"penury","p":"noun","d":"Extreme poverty; a state of having almost no money.","lb":"poverty, destitution","s":["poverty","indigence","privation","want","need","hardship"],"k":["deprivation","distress","impecuniousness","neediness"],"a":["wealth","affluence","riches","prosperity"],"ex":["The writer died in penury, although his books are now very popular.","A series of bad harvests reduced the farmer's family to penury.","After the business failed, they lived in penury and relied on relatives for rice and clothes."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"perceived","p":"adjective","d":"Believed or thought of in a particular way, although it may not actually be true.","lb":"believed, apparent","s":["apparent","supposed","assumed","believed","seeming","imagined"],"k":["accepted","conceived","conventional","detected"],"a":["actual","real","factual","proven"],"ex":["Some people avoid flying because of the perceived danger, although planes are very safe.","The perceived unfairness of the marking system made students angry.","The perceived value of a degree has changed as more people go to university."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"perceptible","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be noticed or felt with the senses or the mind, even if only slightly.","lb":"noticeable, detectable","s":["noticeable","detectable","visible","discernible","observable","apparent"],"k":["conspicuous","evident","faint","marked"],"a":["imperceptible","invisible","undetectable"],"ex":["There was a barely perceptible smile on the boy's face when the teacher praised him.","Even a one-degree rise in temperature is perceptible to most people.","A faint but perceptible smell of smoke came from the kitchen."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"peregrination","p":"noun","d":"A long journey, especially one made on foot or from place to place.","lb":"wandering, journey","s":["wandering","journey","travels","voyage","trek","roaming"],"k":["globetrotting","junket","meandering","sojourn"],"a":[],"ex":["Her peregrinations across Asia took three years and filled five notebooks.","After his peregrinations through the hills, he returned home with many stories.","The book follows the author's peregrinations from village to village on foot."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"peremptory","p":"adjective","d":"Commanding and expecting immediate obedience, without allowing questions or refusal.","lb":"commanding, imperious","s":["bossy","commanding","imperious","dictatorial","domineering","authoritative"],"k":["authoritarian","autocratic","decisive","dominating"],"a":["polite","gentle","tentative","courteous"],"ex":["The officer gave a peremptory wave and told the cars to stop.","Her peremptory tone made it clear that she would not accept excuses.","The boss sent a peremptory message ordering everyone to return at once."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"perennial","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting for a very long time, or returning again and again.","lb":"enduring, recurring","s":["enduring","lasting","perpetual","recurrent","constant","persistent"],"k":["ageless","ceaseless","durable","eternal"],"a":["temporary","fleeting","brief","transient"],"ex":["Traffic jams are a perennial problem in Dhaka, whatever the season.","Rice and lentils are perennial favorites at our family dinners.","The question of what to do after school is a perennial worry for teenagers."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"perfidious","p":"adjective","d":"Disloyal and untrustworthy, betraying someone who trusted you.","lb":"treacherous, disloyal","s":["treacherous","disloyal","faithless","deceitful","traitorous","false"],"k":["backstabbing","deceptive","judas-like","punic"],"a":["loyal","faithful","trustworthy","honest"],"ex":["She felt hurt by her perfidious friend, who had shared her secret with the whole class.","The perfidious partner emptied the company's bank account and left the country.","In the story, a perfidious minister betrays the king who trusted him."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"perfidy","p":"noun","d":"The act of breaking someone’s trust by deceiving or betraying them.","lb":"betrayal, treachery","s":["treachery","betrayal","disloyalty","deceit","duplicity","treason"],"k":["backstabbing","dishonesty","sellout","two-timing"],"a":["loyalty","fidelity","faithfulness","honesty"],"ex":["She could not forgive his perfidy when she learned he had shared her secrets with the whole class.","The partner’s perfidy became clear when he secretly sold the shop and left town with the money.","In the film, the hero is shocked by the perfidy of his closest friend."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"perfunctory","p":"adjective","d":"Done quickly and without much care or interest, only because it is expected.","lb":"cursory, superficial","s":["cursory","hasty","superficial","careless","routine","token"],"k":["brief","casual","desultory","formal"],"a":["thorough","careful","attentive","thoughtful"],"ex":["The officer gave my passport a perfunctory glance and waved me through.","His perfunctory apology, made without even looking up, did not satisfy her.","The doctor's perfunctory check-up lasted two minutes, and she left without any real answers."],"b":597,"y":1},{"w":"peripatetic","p":"adjective","d":"Moving from place to place, never staying long in one spot.","lb":"wandering, traveling","s":["traveling","wandering","itinerant","roving","nomadic","roaming"],"k":["gadabout","globetrotting","on the move","peregrine"],"a":["settled","stationary","sedentary","fixed"],"ex":["His peripatetic childhood, moving between six cities, taught him to make friends quickly.","The college hired a peripatetic music teacher who visits each branch on a different day.","A peripatetic photographer, she spent years travelling between villages for her project."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"periphery","p":"noun","d":"The outer edge or boundary of an area, object or group.","lb":"edge, outskirts","s":["edge","outskirts","border","boundary","fringe","margin"],"k":["brink","circumference","confines","extremities"],"a":["center","middle","core","heart"],"ex":["Many factories are built on the periphery of the city, where land is cheaper.","She noticed a movement at the periphery of her vision and turned around quickly.","Several small villages lie on the periphery of the national park."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"perjury","p":"noun","d":"The crime of telling a lie in a court of law after promising to tell the truth.","lb":"lying under oath","s":["false testimony","false swearing","lying under oath","false witness","false evidence"],"k":["bearing false witness","dishonesty","fabrication","falsehood"],"a":[],"ex":["The witness was charged with perjury after the court found that he had lied about the date.","Lying on a sworn statement is perjury, and it can lead to a prison sentence.","The lawyer warned his client that committing perjury would only make his situation worse."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"permeable","p":"adjective","d":"Allowing liquids or gases to pass through it.","lb":"porous, penetrable","s":["porous","absorbent","spongy","open","leaky"],"k":["holey","osmotic","perforated","semipermeable"],"a":["impermeable","impervious","waterproof","airtight"],"ex":["Sandy soil is permeable, so rainwater drains away quickly after a storm.","Tea bags are made of thin paper that is permeable to hot water.","Cell walls are permeable to some substances but block others."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"permeate","p":"verb","d":"To spread through every part of something and be present in all of it.","lb":"pervade, spread through","s":["pervade","saturate","fill","penetrate","infuse","suffuse"],"k":["diffuse","filter","infiltrate","invade"],"a":[],"ex":["The smell of fried onions permeated the whole house before lunch.","Rainwater slowly permeated the old wall and left damp patches on the inside.","A spirit of teamwork permeates the whole company, from the drivers to the managers."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"pernicious","p":"adjective","d":"Very harmful, especially in a gradual or hidden way.","lb":"harmful, destructive","s":["harmful","destructive","damaging","deadly","injurious","toxic"],"k":["blasting","corrosive","dangerous","detrimental"],"a":["harmless","beneficial","benign","helpful"],"ex":["Spreading false rumours online can have a pernicious effect on a school's reputation.","Gambling is a pernicious habit that has ruined many families.","The pernicious influence of constant comparison on social media can make teenagers feel inadequate."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"perpetrator","p":"noun","d":"A person who commits a crime or does something harmful or wrong.","lb":"culprit, offender","s":["culprit","offender","criminal","guilty party","lawbreaker","miscreant"],"k":["delinquent","evildoer","felon","transgressor"],"a":["victim","sufferer"],"ex":["Police are still searching for the perpetrator of last night's robbery.","CCTV footage helped officers identify the perpetrator within a day.","The teacher could not find the perpetrator of the prank, because nobody would say who had hidden the chalk."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"perpetuate","p":"verb","d":"To make something, usually something bad, continue for a long time.","lb":"continue, preserve","s":["continue","maintain","preserve","prolong","sustain","extend"],"k":["bear on","carry on","conserve","go on"],"a":["end","stop","halt","abolish"],"ex":["Some advertisements perpetuate the myth that only men can be good engineers.","Skipping school can perpetuate a cycle of poverty.","The family restaurant perpetuates the old recipes of its founder."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"perplexed","p":"adjective","d":"Confused and slightly worried because you cannot understand something.","lb":"confused, puzzled","s":["puzzled","confused","baffled","bewildered","mystified","bemused"],"k":["at sea","befuddled","confounded","dazed"],"a":["certain","enlightened","sure"],"ex":["The perplexed tourist stared at the map, unable to find the station.","I was perplexed by the sudden change in the exam timetable.","She gave me a perplexed look when I said I had no phone."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"perquisite","p":"noun","d":"An extra benefit that you get from a job in addition to your salary.","lb":"perk, benefit","s":["perk","fringe benefit","benefit","bonus","privilege","extra"],"k":["benefit in kind","boon","emolument","exclusive right"],"a":[],"ex":["A company car is one of the perquisites that come with the manager’s job.","Free lunch and health insurance are popular perquisites at many technology firms.","Teachers at the private school enjoy perquisites such as discounted tuition for their own children."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"perseverance","p":"noun","d":"The quality of continuing to try hard to achieve something despite difficulties.","lb":"persistence, determination","s":["persistence","determination","tenacity","resolve","endurance","grit"],"k":["backbone","pertinacity","purpose","resolution"],"a":["laziness","apathy","indecision","surrender"],"ex":["With great perseverance, Nadia finally passed her driving test on the fourth try.","Learning a new language takes patience and perseverance.","The coach praised the team for its perseverance in the second half."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"persevere","p":"verb","d":"To keep trying to do something difficult without giving up.","lb":"persist, carry on","s":["persist","continue","keep going","carry on","press on","stick with it"],"k":["bear on","go on","hang in","hang on"],"a":["give up","quit","surrender","stop"],"ex":["If you persevere with your English practice, you will soon speak fluently.","She persevered in her studies despite the load-shedding every night.","The climbers persevered through the storm and reached the camp."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"persona non grata","p":"phrase","d":"A person who is not welcome or accepted in a place or group.","lb":"unwelcome person","s":["outcast","pariah","unwelcome person","outsider","exile","reject"],"k":["blackballed person","blacklisted person","castaway","individual"],"a":["favorite","honored guest","welcome guest","friend"],"ex":["After he leaked the secret plan, he became persona non grata at every meeting of the club.","The ambassador was declared persona non grata and had to leave the country within a week.","Since my cousin broke the old man's window, she has been persona non grata on that street."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"pertinent","p":"adjective","d":"Directly connected with and important to the matter being discussed.","lb":"relevant, applicable","s":["relevant","applicable","appropriate","germane","fitting","apt"],"k":["apropos","cogent","on topic","pointed"],"a":["irrelevant","unrelated","immaterial","inappropriate"],"ex":["The lawyer asked only pertinent questions and ignored everything unrelated to the contract.","Please include all pertinent information about your health when you fill in the form.","Her comment was pertinent to the discussion and helped the group choose a plan."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"perturb","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel anxious, worried or mentally uneasy.","lb":"upset, worry","s":["disturb","unsettle","trouble","worry","upset","disquiet"],"k":["discomfit","discompose","disconcert","disorder"],"a":["calm","soothe","reassure","pacify"],"ex":["The sudden silence on the phone perturbed Rafi, because his mother usually answered within a minute.","Nothing seemed to perturb the pilot, even when the plane bumped through heavy storm clouds.","The doctor was perturbed by the unusual results of the blood test and ordered another one."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"perturbed","p":"adjective","d":"Worried or upset because something unexpected has happened.","lb":"worried, upset","s":["worried","anxious","disturbed","troubled","upset","uneasy"],"k":["apprehensive","concerned","discomfited","discomposed"],"a":["calm","unruffled","untroubled","composed"],"ex":["My mother was perturbed when I came home two hours later than usual.","The pilot was not perturbed by the turbulence and calmly continued the flight.","Perturbed by the strange noise from the engine, the driver pulled over."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"perusal","p":"noun","d":"The act of reading something carefully and thoroughly.","lb":"careful reading","s":["reading","study","examination","scrutiny","inspection","review"],"k":["browsing","close reading","research","scan"],"a":["glance","skimming"],"ex":["A careful perusal of the contract revealed several hidden fees.","On perusal of your application, we found some missing documents.","The lawyer asked for time for a full perusal of the files."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"peruse","p":"verb","d":"To read something slowly and carefully, paying attention to the details.","lb":"read carefully, study","s":["study","examine","scrutinize","inspect","pore over","go through"],"k":["analyze","check","investigate","probe"],"a":["skim","glance at","skip","ignore"],"ex":["Before signing the rental agreement, she perused every page with a pen in her hand.","The lawyer perused the contract for an hour and marked three risky clauses.","I spent the whole afternoon perusing old letters in my grandfather's wooden trunk."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"pervade","p":"verb","d":"To spread through every part of something and be noticeable everywhere.","lb":"permeate, fill","s":["permeate","fill","saturate","penetrate","spread through","infuse"],"k":["flood","overrun","percolate","perforate"],"a":[],"ex":["The smell of freshly baked bread pervaded the whole house.","A feeling of excitement pervaded the campus on the first day of the festival.","Smartphones now pervade almost every part of modern life."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"pervasive","p":"adjective","d":"Present or noticeable in every part of a place or thing, and spreading widely.","lb":"widespread, ubiquitous","s":["widespread","prevalent","omnipresent","ubiquitous","rife","universal"],"k":["all-embracing","endemic","far-reaching","frequent"],"a":["rare","limited","isolated","scarce"],"ex":["The smell of fried fish was pervasive and reached every room of the house.","Smartphones have a pervasive influence on how young people spend their free time.","Corruption became so pervasive in the department that honest workers felt helpless."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"perverse","p":"adjective","d":"Deliberately doing the opposite of what is reasonable or wanted, often just to be difficult.","lb":"contrary, stubborn","s":["contrary","stubborn","obstinate","willful","awkward","headstrong"],"k":["adverse","bullheaded","cantankerous","corrupt"],"a":["reasonable","cooperative","agreeable","compliant"],"ex":["It was perverse of him to refuse help and then complain that he was tired.","She took a perverse delight in arriving just as the meeting ended.","The perverse weather turned cold on the one day we planned a picnic."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"pessimistic","p":"adjective","d":"Expecting bad things to happen, or always seeing the negative side of a situation.","lb":"negative, gloomy","s":["negative","gloomy","defeatist","fatalistic","cynical","downbeat"],"k":["demoralized","discouraged","dismal","dispirited"],"a":["optimistic","hopeful","positive","upbeat"],"ex":["Rafi felt pessimistic about his chances after the difficult exam paper.","The doctor was pessimistic about the patient's recovery, but the family stayed hopeful.","Economists are pessimistic about the coming year because prices keep rising."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"petrify","p":"verb","d":"To frighten someone so much that they cannot move or think.","lb":"terrify, stun","s":["terrify","horrify","paralyze","scare stiff","frighten","stun"],"k":["appall","blunt","daunt","deaden"],"a":["calm","reassure","soothe","comfort"],"ex":["The sudden crack of thunder petrified the little boy, who froze on the spot.","Public speaking petrifies me; my knees shake and my mind goes blank.","Rafi is petrified of cockroaches and screams whenever one runs across the floor."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"petulant","p":"adjective","d":"Easily annoyed and unreasonably bad-tempered, like a child who cannot have what he wants.","lb":"sulky, peevish","s":["sulky","peevish","cranky","irritable","childish","snappish"],"k":["fractious","grumpy","moody","peckish"],"a":["cheerful","easygoing","patient"],"ex":["The petulant child threw his toys on the floor when dinner was called.","Her petulant reply showed she was still upset about losing the game.","He gave a petulant sigh when the teacher refused to extend the deadline."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"phantasm","p":"noun","d":"A ghost-like figure, or something seen or imagined that is not really there.","lb":"ghost, illusion","s":["phantom","apparition","ghost","specter","spirit","illusion"],"k":["chimera","disembodied spirit","figment","hallucination"],"a":["reality","fact"],"ex":["The old villagers swore that a pale phantasm drifted across the empty field every night.","After three sleepless nights before the exam, she began to see phantasms in the corners of her room.","In the film, a phantasm of the dead king warns the prince about his uncle."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"philanthropic","p":"adjective","d":"Giving time or money generously to help people in need or to support good causes.","lb":"charitable, generous","s":["charitable","benevolent","humanitarian","generous","altruistic","giving"],"k":["beneficent","benign","big-hearted","humane"],"a":["selfish","miserly","stingy","greedy"],"ex":["The philanthropic businessman paid school fees for hundreds of poor children.","She spends her weekends on philanthropic work, collecting clothes for families in need.","Several philanthropic groups provided food and water after the cyclone."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"philanthropy","p":"noun","d":"The practice of giving money, time or effort to help others and improve society.","lb":"charity, generosity","s":["charity","benevolence","generosity","altruism","giving","kindness"],"k":["aid","almsgiving","assistance","benefaction"],"a":["selfishness","greed","stinginess","malevolence"],"ex":["The businessman is known for his philanthropy: he built a free school in his home village.","Through philanthropy, wealthy families fund hospitals, libraries and scholarships for poor students.","Her philanthropy began with small donations of warm clothes every winter."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"philistine","p":"noun","d":"A person who does not care about or understand art, culture and learning.","lb":"uncultured person, boor","s":["boor","lowbrow","ignoramus","vulgarian","barbarian","yahoo"],"k":["anti-intellectual","churl","dullard","illiterate"],"a":["aesthete","intellectual","highbrow","connoisseur"],"ex":["He called himself a philistine because he found art galleries boring and never read poetry.","Only a philistine would put a cup of tea down on a rare painting.","The mayor was accused of being a philistine after he proposed turning the old theatre into a car park."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"phlegmatic","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and not easily excited or upset, often showing very little emotion.","lb":"calm, unemotional","s":["calm","stolid","unemotional","placid","unflappable","impassive"],"k":["collected","expressionless","relaxed","serene"],"a":["excitable","emotional","passionate","volatile"],"ex":["My phlegmatic father simply shrugged when he heard that the car had a flat tire.","The phlegmatic goalkeeper never showed any nerves, even during a penalty shootout.","She is so phlegmatic that exam results, good or bad, hardly change her mood."],"b":101,"y":1},{"w":"piety","p":"noun","d":"Deep respect for religion, shown in a sincere way of living and behaving.","lb":"devoutness, reverence","s":["devotion","godliness","holiness","reverence","faith","spirituality"],"k":["churchgoing","loyalty","observance","religiosity"],"a":["irreverence","disrespect"],"ex":["Her piety was admired by the neighbors, who saw her help the poor in every season.","The old man's quiet piety showed in his daily prayers and his gentle manners.","Filial piety, or respect for parents, is an important value in many families."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"pilgrim","p":"noun","d":"A person who travels to a holy place for religious reasons.","lb":"holy traveller","s":["devotee","wayfarer","traveller","worshipper","palmer"],"k":["crusader","sojourner","votary","wanderer"],"a":[],"ex":["Thousands of pilgrims from Bangladesh fly to Makkah every year to perform Hajj.","Every January, pilgrims walk for days to reach the temple on the mountain.","The guesthouse near the shrine offers cheap meals and a bed to tired pilgrims."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pilgrimage","p":"noun","d":"A journey to a holy place for religious reasons, or a special trip to a place that means a lot to you.","lb":"journey, trek","s":["journey","trek","expedition","odyssey","quest","trip"],"k":["devotional trip","hajj","journeying","sacred journey"],"a":[],"ex":["Every year thousands of people make a pilgrimage to the shrine in the hills.","My grandmother saved money for years to go on a pilgrimage.","Football fans make a pilgrimage to the old stadium to see where their heroes played."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pinnacle","p":"noun","d":"The highest point of success, achievement or development.","lb":"highest point, peak","s":["peak","summit","height","top","apex","zenith"],"k":["climax","crest","culmination","degree"],"a":["bottom","nadir","depths","low point"],"ex":["Winning the national prize was the pinnacle of her teaching career.","The pinnacle of his football career came at the age of twenty-six.","For many students, university is the pinnacle of years of hard work."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pious","p":"adjective","d":"Deeply religious and showing respect for your faith in the way you live.","lb":"devout, religious","s":["devout","religious","reverent","godly","devoted","faithful"],"k":["committed","dedicated","fervent","observant"],"a":["impious","irreverent","godless","profane"],"ex":["My grandmother is a pious woman who prays at the same times every day.","In the film, a pious young man gives most of his income to the poor.","My pious colleague finds a quiet corner to pray even on the busiest day at the office."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"piquancy","p":"noun","d":"A pleasantly sharp, spicy or exciting quality.","lb":"tang, zest","s":["tang","zest","spice","bite","sharpness","zing"],"k":["edge","gusto","nip","poignancy"],"a":["blandness","dullness","flatness"],"ex":["A squeeze of lime adds piquancy to the plain fried rice.","The piquancy of the green chili sauce made my eyes water.","Pickles add piquancy to an otherwise simple meal of rice and lentils."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"piquant","p":"adjective","d":"Pleasantly spicy or sharp in taste; also interesting and exciting in a lively way.","lb":"spicy, tangy","s":["spicy","tangy","zesty","sharp","pungent","savory"],"k":["attractive","engaging","salty","sour"],"a":["bland","mild","tasteless","insipid"],"ex":["The piquant green chili chutney made the plain rice taste exciting.","This piquant pickle of mango and mustard oil is a favorite at our family table.","She added lemon juice to give the soup a piquant taste."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"pivot","p":"verb","d":"To turn around a fixed point, or to change direction or approach completely.","lb":"turn, rotate","s":["turn","rotate","swivel","spin","revolve","twirl"],"k":["go around","realign","reorient","shift"],"a":[],"ex":["The basketball player pivoted on one foot and passed the ball to her teammate.","The door pivots on a single metal rod fixed in the floor.","When sales dropped, the shop owner pivoted to selling groceries online."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pivotal","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely important because other things depend on it or are changed by it.","lb":"crucial, key","s":["crucial","critical","central","vital","key","decisive"],"k":["important","indispensable","main","polar"],"a":["minor","unimportant","trivial","insignificant"],"ex":["Winning the debate was a pivotal moment in Nadia's confidence at school.","The captain's goal in the last minute played a pivotal role in the team's victory.","Choosing the right subject in Class Eleven is a pivotal decision for many students."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"placate","p":"verb","d":"To make an angry or upset person feel calmer by giving them something or by agreeing with them.","lb":"pacify, appease","s":["pacify","appease","soothe","mollify","calm","humor"],"k":["butter up","buy off","calm down","lull"],"a":["anger","enrage","provoke","infuriate"],"ex":["The shop offered a full refund to placate the angry customer.","He bought flowers to placate his wife after forgetting their anniversary.","The teacher gave extra time to placate students who thought the exam was too long."],"b":91,"y":3},{"w":"placebo","p":"noun","d":"A harmless substance with no real medicine in it, given to patients as a test or to comfort them.","lb":"dummy pill, sham","s":["sugar pill","dummy pill","sham treatment","inactive drug","inert pill","fake medicine"],"k":["bread pill","control","faux remedy","medication"],"a":[],"ex":["Half of the volunteers received the real drug, while the others were given a placebo.","My grandmother swears by her herbal drink, but the doctor says it may only be a placebo.","Some patients feel better after taking a placebo simply because they expect the treatment to help."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"placid","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and peaceful, with very little movement, noise or excitement.","lb":"calm, peaceful","s":["calm","peaceful","tranquil","serene","still","quiet"],"k":["collected","equable","imperturbable","level-headed"],"a":["agitated","turbulent","excitable","stormy"],"ex":["The lake was placid in the early morning, with not a single ripple.","Our placid cow never gets scared, even when the children run past her.","The baby is placid and sleeps through even the loudest wedding music."],"b":74,"y":1},{"w":"plagiarism","p":"noun","d":"The act of using someone else's words or ideas and presenting them as your own.","lb":"copying, literary theft","s":["copying","piracy","theft","cribbing","appropriation","infringement"],"k":["borrowing","copycatting","passing off","pilfering"],"a":["originality","creativity","authenticity"],"ex":["The university rejected her thesis because of plagiarism in two chapters.","Copying an answer from the internet without naming the source counts as plagiarism.","The teacher uses special software to check homework for plagiarism."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"plaintive","p":"adjective","d":"Sounding sad and sorrowful, as if asking for pity or sympathy.","lb":"sad, mournful","s":["mournful","sorrowful","sad","wistful","melancholy","doleful"],"k":["downcast","elegiac","gloomy","keening"],"a":["cheerful","joyful","happy","merry"],"ex":["The plaintive cry of a lost kitten could be heard outside the window all night.","She sang a plaintive folk song that made the old women in the audience weep.","In a plaintive voice, the boy asked if his father would ever come home early."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"plasticity","p":"noun","d":"The ability to be shaped or molded, or to change and adapt easily.","lb":"pliability, flexibility","s":["flexibility","adaptability","elasticity","versatility","malleability","pliability"],"k":["amenability","impressionability","mutability","neuroplasticity"],"a":["rigidity","stiffness","hardness"],"ex":["The plasticity of clay lets potters shape it into bowls and vases.","Young children learn languages quickly because of the plasticity of their brains.","Doctors were amazed by the plasticity of her brain, which helped her relearn speech after the injury."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"platitude","p":"noun","d":"A boring remark that has been said so many times that it has lost its meaning.","lb":"cliche, truism","s":["cliche","banality","commonplace","bromide","stock phrase","old chestnut"],"k":["comment","empty words","generality","hollow saying"],"a":[],"ex":["When I failed the test, my uncle only offered the platitude that everything happens for a reason.","The speaker's platitudes about hard work bored the students, who wanted real advice.","Saying that time heals everything is a platitude that does not help someone who is grieving."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"platonic","p":"adjective","d":"Describing a close, affectionate relationship that is friendly but not romantic or sexual.","lb":"non-romantic, friendly","s":["friendly","companionable","spiritual","innocent","chaste"],"k":["brotherly","non-physical","passionless","sisterly"],"a":["romantic","sexual","amorous","passionate"],"ex":["Nadia and Rafi have a platonic friendship; they have known each other since childhood.","My cousin insists that his relationship with his coworker is purely platonic.","Their platonic bond lasted forty years, with weekly tea and endless conversation."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"plausible","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming reasonable and likely to be true.","lb":"believable, credible","s":["believable","credible","convincing","reasonable","likely","probable"],"k":["glib","insincere","pat","possible"],"a":["implausible","unbelievable","unlikely","improbable"],"ex":["Rafi's excuse for being late was plausible, because the roads were flooded that day.","The police said it was a plausible story, but they still checked every detail.","The scientist gave a plausible explanation for why the fish were dying in the pond."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"plead","p":"verb","d":"To ask for something in a very emotional or urgent way.","lb":"beg, implore","s":["beg","implore","appeal","beseech","entreat","petition"],"k":["appeal to","crave","importune","invoke"],"a":["demand","insist","command"],"ex":["The little girl pleaded with her father to let her keep the stray kitten.","Students pleaded with the teacher for more time to finish the test.","He pleaded for a second chance after missing the deadline."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pleading","p":"adjective","d":"Asking for something in a desperate, emotional way, as if begging.","lb":"begging, urgent","s":["begging","imploring","urgent","desperate","appealing"],"k":["cajoling","soliciting","suppliant","supplicant"],"a":["demanding","commanding","defiant","indifferent"],"ex":["The puppy gave me a pleading look until I shared my snack.","She sent a pleading message to the teacher, asking for more time.","His pleading voice made the shopkeeper lower the price."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"plebeian","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to ordinary, common people; often used to suggest a lack of refinement.","lb":"common, unrefined","s":["common","ordinary","vulgar","lowly","unrefined","humble"],"k":["down-to-earth","earthy","everyday","homespun"],"a":["aristocratic","noble","refined","patrician"],"ex":["The snobbish critic dismissed the popular song as plebeian, but millions of people loved it.","She proudly enjoyed plebeian pleasures like street snacks and roadside tea.","In ancient Rome, a plebeian could not hold some high offices that were reserved for the nobles."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"plenteous","p":"adjective","d":"Existing in large amounts; more than enough.","lb":"abundant, plentiful","s":["plentiful","abundant","ample","copious","bountiful","generous"],"k":["fruitful","liberal","lush","luxuriant"],"a":["scarce","scanty","meagre","sparse"],"ex":["The village enjoyed a plenteous harvest after a year of good rains.","My grandfather says the river was plenteous with fish in his youth.","Plenteous sunshine and rain have made the garden bloom this spring."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"plenty","p":"noun","d":"A large amount or number of something, more than is needed.","lb":"abundance, lots","s":["abundance","lots","loads","a lot","wealth","heaps"],"k":["batch","copiousness","cornucopia","deal"],"a":["shortage","scarcity","lack","dearth"],"ex":["Don't worry about the bus; we have plenty of time before it leaves.","There is plenty of food at home, so you can invite your friends.","Plenty of fresh fish arrives at the market early in the morning."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"plethora","p":"noun","d":"A very large amount of something, usually more than is needed or useful.","lb":"abundance, excess","s":["abundance","excess","profusion","surplus","glut","overabundance"],"k":["bounty","cornucopia","embarrassment","plenty"],"a":["scarcity","shortage","lack","dearth"],"ex":["The menu offered a plethora of dishes, and we took twenty minutes to choose.","Online shopping gives buyers a plethora of options, which can make deciding difficult.","The library has a plethora of books on history but very few on science."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"pliable","p":"adjective","d":"Easy to bend or shape without breaking; also easily influenced by other people.","lb":"flexible, impressionable","s":["flexible","supple","malleable","elastic","yielding","adaptable"],"k":["adjustable","bendy","compliant","formed"],"a":["rigid","stiff","inflexible","stubborn"],"ex":["Wet clay is pliable, so you can shape it easily with your hands.","New leather shoes become more pliable after a few weeks of wear.","The young salesman was pliable and agreed to whatever his boss suggested."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"plight","p":"noun","d":"A bad, difficult or dangerous situation, especially one that is hard to escape from.","lb":"predicament, hardship","s":["predicament","difficulty","trouble","quandary","dilemma","bind"],"k":["fix","jam","jeopardy","pickle"],"a":[],"ex":["The documentary draws attention to the plight of families who lost their homes in the flood.","Nobody noticed the plight of the stray dogs during the cold winter.","Her plight was clear: she had missed the last bus and had no money for a taxi."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"plumb","p":"verb","d":"To measure the depth of something, or to explore something deep or hidden in order to understand it fully.","lb":"fathom, probe","s":["fathom","probe","sound","explore","delve into","penetrate"],"k":["dredge","ferret out","get to the bottom of","quantify"],"a":["skim","ignore","overlook"],"ex":["The boatman plumbed the channel with a long bamboo pole to check how deep it was.","The author plumbs the depths of grief in her moving first novel.","Scientists are using robots to plumb the deepest parts of the ocean."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"plummet","p":"verb","d":"To fall very quickly and suddenly from a high position or level.","lb":"plunge, fall sharply","s":["plunge","drop","nosedive","tumble","crash","dive"],"k":["bottom out","dip","free-fall","plunk"],"a":["soar","rise","climb","skyrocket"],"ex":["Temperatures plummeted overnight, and we woke up to frost on the windows.","The price of onions plummeted after farmers brought a large harvest to the market.","His marks plummeted when he started staying up all night on his phone."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"plunder","p":"verb","d":"To steal goods by force from a place, especially during a war, disaster or other disorder.","lb":"loot, ransack","s":["loot","ransack","pillage","raid","rob","sack"],"k":["rape","rifle","spoil","swag"],"a":["protect","defend","guard","preserve"],"ex":["Looters plundered several shops on the main road during the blackout.","In the fourteenth century, raiders plundered the monastery and carried off its silver.","Illegal sand traders are plundering the riverbed and weakening the banks near the village."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pluralism","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which people of different races, religions or opinions live together peacefully and are accepted.","lb":"diversity, tolerance","s":["diversity","variety","tolerance","coexistence","multiplicity"],"k":["cosmopolitanism","eclecticism","multiethnicity","open-mindedness"],"a":["uniformity","intolerance","conformity"],"ex":["Cultural pluralism is visible in the city's mix of languages, foods and festivals.","The university encourages pluralism by welcoming students from many backgrounds.","A healthy democracy depends on pluralism, where different opinions can be freely expressed."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"poignant","p":"adjective","d":"Causing a strong feeling of sadness or sympathy; deeply touching.","lb":"moving, touching","s":["moving","touching","affecting","heartbreaking","sad","tender"],"k":["emotive","heartfelt","painful","piteous"],"a":["unemotional","heartless"],"ex":["The old photograph of her late father was a poignant reminder of happier days.","It was poignant to watch the retired teacher visit his empty classroom one last time.","The film's poignant ending left many people wiping their eyes in the cinema."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"polarize","p":"verb","d":"To divide people or opinions into two sharply opposed groups.","lb":"divide, split","s":["divide","split","separate","fracture","estrange","alienate"],"k":["bifurcate","cleave","divvy up","factionalize"],"a":["unite","unify","reconcile","bring together"],"ex":["The new school uniform rule polarized parents, with half strongly in favor and half firmly against.","Social media can polarize friends who once agreed on most things.","The film's controversial ending polarized critics, and reviews ranged from brilliant to awful."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"polemic","p":"noun","d":"A strong written or spoken attack on, or defense of, an opinion or belief.","lb":"attack, argument","s":["diatribe","tirade","attack","argument","controversy","debate"],"k":["arguing","broadside","contention","invective"],"a":[],"ex":["The columnist wrote a fiery polemic against single-use plastic bags.","Her essay was less a balanced report than a polemic against fast fashion.","The pamphlet is a polemic on school fees, arguing that costs have become unfair."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"ponderous","p":"adjective","d":"Slow and heavy, especially in a clumsy, serious or boring way, as in movement or writing.","lb":"heavy, labored","s":["heavy","labored","lumbering","clumsy","dull","plodding"],"k":["bulky","cumbersome","leaden","sluggish"],"a":["light","graceful","nimble","lively"],"ex":["The old truck made its ponderous way up the steep road, shaking the whole street.","The professor's ponderous writing made the short article feel ten pages longer.","The elephant took a ponderous step toward the river, and the ground seemed to shake."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"porous","p":"adjective","d":"Having many tiny holes that let water, air or other liquids pass through.","lb":"permeable, spongy","s":["permeable","spongy","absorbent","perforated","leaky","holey"],"k":["cellular","full of holes","honeycombed","spongelike"],"a":["impermeable","airtight","waterproof","solid"],"ex":["A sponge is porous, which is why it soaks up so much water.","Porous rock under the desert can store water for hundreds of years.","Unglazed clay pots are porous, so the water inside stays cool in the summer."],"b":33,"y":0},{"w":"portent","p":"noun","d":"A sign that something important or unpleasant is going to happen in the future.","lb":"omen, sign","s":["omen","sign","warning","harbinger","augury","presage"],"k":["bellwether","foreboding","herald","indicator"],"a":[],"ex":["Dark clouds in the morning were a portent of the storm that struck by evening.","Some people see a black cat crossing the road as a portent of bad luck.","The sudden fall in the shop's sales was a portent of deeper trouble."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"possessed","p":"adjective","d":"Controlled by a powerful emotion or idea, so that you act as if you are not yourself.","lb":"driven, obsessed","s":["obsessed","driven","consumed","gripped","haunted","frenzied"],"k":["bewitched","concerned","controlled","demonic"],"a":["calm","composed","rational","detached"],"ex":["Before the final exam, she studied like a girl possessed.","He worked like a man possessed to finish the project by morning.","Possessed by a sudden fear, the child ran to his mother."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"posterity","p":"noun","d":"All the people who will live in the future, especially the descendants of a particular person.","lb":"future generations, descendants","s":["future generations","descendants","offspring","heirs","progeny","coming generations"],"k":["biological group","brood","children","future ages"],"a":["ancestors","forebears","predecessors","forefathers"],"ex":["The old photographs were scanned to preserve them for posterity.","He wrote a diary every night so that posterity would know how ordinary people lived.","The museum protects the ancient manuscripts for the benefit of posterity."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"posthumous","p":"adjective","d":"Happening, given or published after a person has died.","lb":"after death","s":["postmortem","delayed","belated","subsequent","late"],"k":["afterward","memorial","tardy"],"a":[],"ex":["The poet received a posthumous award ten years after her death.","The author's final novel was a posthumous publication that became a bestseller.","The firefighter was given a posthumous medal for saving three children from the burning building."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"postulate","p":"noun","d":"A statement accepted as true without proof, used as the starting point for an argument or theory.","lb":"assumption, axiom","s":["axiom","assumption","premise","principle","proposition","hypothesis"],"k":["basic truth","dogma","maxim","precept"],"a":[],"ex":["Euclid's first postulate says that a straight line can be drawn between any two points.","The economist built his whole theory on the postulate that people always act in their own interest.","In our physics class, we treated the speed of light as a postulate, not something to prove."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"posture","p":"verb","d":"To behave or speak in an exaggerated or unnatural way, usually to impress other people.","lb":"pose, show off","s":["pose","show off","strut","swagger","put on airs","grandstand"],"k":["acquit","bear","behave","brag"],"a":["be natural","be sincere","be humble"],"ex":["He postured in front of the cameras, pretending to be a humble volunteer.","Some students posture in class, using difficult words they barely understand just to look clever.","Rival managers posture in meetings, each trying to look more important than the others."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pottery","p":"noun","d":"Pots, bowls and other objects made from clay and baked until hard.","lb":"clay ware","s":["ceramics","crockery"],"k":["ceramic ware","delftware","faience","majolica"],"a":[],"ex":["The potters of this village sell their pottery at the weekly market.","She joined a pottery class to learn how to shape clay on a wheel.","Archaeologists found pieces of ancient pottery buried beneath the old road."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pragmatic","p":"adjective","d":"Dealing with problems in a practical, sensible way rather than following ideas or theories.","lb":"practical, realistic","s":["practical","realistic","sensible","businesslike","hardheaded","efficient"],"k":["feasible","functional","reasonable","useful"],"a":["idealistic","impractical","unrealistic","romantic"],"ex":["Rather than waiting for a perfect plan, she took a pragmatic approach and fixed the problem step by step.","My father is pragmatic about money and buys only what the family really needs.","The pragmatic solution to the traffic problem was to start office hours an hour later."],"b":595,"y":1},{"w":"prattle","p":"verb","d":"To talk on and on about unimportant things in a foolish or childish way.","lb":"chatter, babble","s":["chatter","babble","jabber","blather","gab","rattle on"],"k":["blab","blabber","clack","drivel"],"a":[],"ex":["My little cousin prattled all the way home about her new toy.","Please stop prattling on about gossip and help me finish the dishes.","He prattled on about his holiday plans while the rest of us tried to study."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"preamble","p":"noun","d":"An introduction at the start of a speech, document or law that explains its purpose.","lb":"introduction, preface","s":["introduction","preface","prologue","foreword","opening","prelude"],"k":["beginning","exordium","overture","proem"],"a":["epilogue","conclusion","postscript","ending"],"ex":["The preamble of the constitution states the main goals of the country.","After a short preamble about safety, the instructor started the lesson.","Without any preamble, my boss asked me to take over the project."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"precarious","p":"adjective","d":"Not safe or steady, and likely to fall, fail or go wrong.","lb":"unstable, risky","s":["unstable","insecure","risky","dangerous","shaky","uncertain"],"k":["dicey","dodgy","iffy","rocky"],"a":["stable","secure","safe","steady"],"ex":["The old bridge looked precarious, so the villagers crossed it one by one.","He placed a precarious pile of books on the shelf, and they soon fell.","Many daily workers live a precarious life because their income can stop any day."],"b":99,"y":1},{"w":"precedent","p":"noun","d":"An earlier action, event or decision that is used as an example or reason for doing the same later.","lb":"earlier example, model","s":["example","model","standard","pattern","instance","benchmark"],"k":["authority","case","case in point","case law"],"a":[],"ex":["If we let one student submit late, we will set a precedent for everyone else.","The judge cited an earlier case as a precedent for her decision.","There is no precedent in the city's records for such heavy rain in March."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"precept","p":"noun","d":"A general rule that guides how people should behave or think.","lb":"rule, principle","s":["rule","principle","guideline","maxim","commandment","teaching"],"k":["adage","advice","axiom","code"],"a":[],"ex":["Honesty is the first precept my grandfather taught his children.","The school lives by the precept that every child can learn.","She lived by the old precept that you should treat others as you want to be treated."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"precipitate","p":"verb","d":"To cause something, usually something bad, to happen suddenly or much sooner than expected.","lb":"trigger, hasten","s":["trigger","bring on","hasten","spark","provoke","set off"],"k":["activate","come down","fall","induce"],"a":["delay","postpone","prevent","avert"],"ex":["The sudden rise in fuel prices precipitated protests in several cities last week.","One careless remark precipitated a long argument between the two brothers at dinner.","Skipping meals for days can precipitate a serious health problem."],"b":93,"y":1},{"w":"precipitous","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely steep, like a cliff; also used for a very sudden and sharp fall or drop.","lb":"steep, sheer","s":["steep","sheer","abrupt","sharp","perpendicular","vertical"],"k":["breakneck","craggy","disconnected","dramatic"],"a":["gentle","gradual","sloping","slight"],"ex":["The hikers carefully descended the precipitous mountain path, holding onto the rope with both hands.","A precipitous drop in temperature overnight left the whole village shivering.","Online shoppers noticed a precipitous fall in phone prices right after the new model appeared."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"precise","p":"adjective","d":"Exact and accurate in every detail.","lb":"exact, accurate","s":["exact","accurate","specific","correct","strict","meticulous"],"k":["dead","detailed","distinct","exacting"],"a":["vague","imprecise","approximate","inexact"],"ex":["The recipe needs precise measurements, so use a scale instead of guessing.","Can you tell me the precise time the meeting starts?","She gave precise directions, so we found the house without any trouble."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"preclude","p":"verb","d":"To make something impossible or prevent it from happening.","lb":"prevent, rule out","s":["prevent","rule out","prohibit","exclude","forestall","stop"],"k":["ban","block","close out","debar"],"a":["allow","permit","enable","facilitate"],"ex":["A knee injury precluded him from playing in the final match.","The contract precludes the company from selling the product in other countries.","Heavy flooding precluded any chance of holding the sports day on schedule."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"precocious","p":"adjective","d":"Showing skills or mature behavior at a much younger age than usual.","lb":"gifted, advanced","s":["gifted","advanced","mature","developed","bright","talented"],"k":["early","early-blooming","intelligent","premature"],"a":["backward","immature","slow"],"ex":["A precocious six-year-old in our building can already solve difficult math puzzles.","She was a precocious writer, publishing her first story at the age of twelve.","The precocious boy asked questions that surprised even his teachers."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"precursor","p":"noun","d":"Something or someone that comes before another and prepares the way for it or hints that it is coming.","lb":"forerunner, predecessor","s":["forerunner","predecessor","harbinger","herald","antecedent","sign"],"k":["ancestor","early version","first draft","forebear"],"a":["successor","follower","descendant"],"ex":["Dark clouds and a sudden drop in temperature are often the precursors of a storm.","The telegraph was an early precursor of today's instant messaging apps.","Doctors say a persistent cough can be a precursor to more serious lung problems."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"predator","p":"noun","d":"An animal that hunts and kills other animals for food.","lb":"hunter, animal","s":["hunter","carnivore","raptor","stalker","marauder"],"k":["aggressor","assailant","attacker","hunting animal"],"a":["prey","victim","quarry"],"ex":["The tiger is the top predator in the Sundarbans forest.","Birds build nests high in the trees to hide from predators.","Without natural predators, the deer population grew too large."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"predecessor","p":"noun","d":"A person who held a job or position before someone else, or a thing that came before another.","lb":"forerunner, precursor","s":["forerunner","precursor","antecedent","ancestor","forebear","previous holder"],"k":["herald","indication","omen","root"],"a":["successor","descendant","follower","heir"],"ex":["My manager's predecessor left detailed notes that made the first weeks easy.","The new phone is much faster than its predecessor.","The current principal praised her predecessor for building the school library."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"predicament","p":"noun","d":"A difficult or unpleasant situation that is hard to get out of.","lb":"plight, difficult situation","s":["plight","dilemma","quandary","mess","jam","fix"],"k":["hardship","hole","imbroglio","impasse"],"a":["solution","relief"],"ex":["I was in a predicament when I lost my wallet in a city where I knew nobody.","The company’s predicament became worse when its biggest customer stopped ordering.","Students in a predicament over fees can ask the office for a payment plan."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"predict","p":"verb","d":"To say what you think will happen in the future, based on knowledge or experience.","lb":"forecast, foresee","s":["forecast","foretell","foresee","anticipate","project","prophesy"],"k":["augur","bode","call","divine"],"a":[],"ex":["Weather experts predict heavy rain for the coast this weekend.","No one could predict how many people would come to the fair.","The teacher predicted that the class would find the exam easy."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"predictability","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being easy to know or guess in advance.","lb":"foreseeability","s":["certainty","reliability","regularity","consistency","dependability","stability"],"k":["constancy","foregone conclusion","routine","sameness"],"a":["unpredictability","uncertainty","randomness","surprise"],"ex":["Farmers value the predictability of the seasonal rains.","Some people enjoy the predictability of a daily routine.","The predictability of the film's ending made it boring."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"predilection","p":"noun","d":"A natural or strong liking for something, which you tend to choose.","lb":"preference, liking","s":["preference","liking","fondness","partiality","penchant","inclination"],"k":["affinity","appetite","bent","disposition"],"a":["dislike","aversion","distaste","antipathy"],"ex":["My brother has a predilection for spicy food and always adds extra chili.","Her predilection for old novels led her to spend every weekend at the secondhand bookstalls.","The manager's predilection for early meetings made life hard for parents on the team."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"predispose","p":"verb","d":"To make someone more likely to have a certain condition, feeling or behaviour.","lb":"incline, make prone","s":["incline","dispose","make prone","make susceptible","prime","bias"],"k":["pave the way for","persuade","predetermine","set the stage for"],"a":["deter","discourage","dissuade"],"ex":["A family history of diabetes can predispose you to the disease.","Poor sleep predisposes students to careless mistakes in exams.","His shy nature predisposed him to prefer quiet jobs."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"predominant","p":"adjective","d":"Most noticeable or most common; having the greatest influence or power.","lb":"main, dominant","s":["dominant","main","chief","principal","leading","prevailing"],"k":["ascendant","central","frequent","overriding"],"a":["minor","secondary","subordinate","lesser"],"ex":["Green is the predominant colour in the countryside after the monsoon rains.","Rice is the predominant crop in the fields around our village.","The predominant feeling in the class was relief when the exam finished."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"preeminent","p":"adjective","d":"Better or more important than all others in a particular area.","lb":"outstanding, leading","s":["leading","foremost","outstanding","supreme","eminent","distinguished"],"k":["best","excellent","first","paramount"],"a":["minor","inferior","unknown","undistinguished"],"ex":["She is the preeminent heart surgeon in the country, and patients travel for hours to see her.","The university has long been preeminent in engineering education across the region.","Shakespeare is still regarded as the preeminent English playwright."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"preempt","p":"verb","d":"To prevent something from happening, or to take an advantage for oneself, by acting before others do.","lb":"forestall, take first","s":["forestall","anticipate","head off","prevent","preclude","ward off"],"k":["avert","avoid","displace","obviate"],"a":[],"ex":["The manager held a short briefing to preempt any complaints about the new schedule.","Rafi apologized before anyone could complain, hoping to preempt an angry reaction.","The bank preempted the problem by sending a text alert before the card expired."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"pregnant","p":"adjective","d":"Full of meaning or importance, with much that is felt but not said aloud.","lb":"meaningful, significant","s":["meaningful","significant","expressive","loaded","charged","weighty"],"k":["big","fraught","freighted","full"],"a":["meaningless","empty","insignificant","trivial"],"ex":["There was a pregnant pause before the teacher read out the exam results.","After the manager asked who had made the error, a pregnant silence fell over the meeting.","She gave him a pregnant look that said she knew exactly what had happened."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"prelude","p":"noun","d":"An event or action that comes before something larger and prepares the way for it.","lb":"introduction, precursor","s":["introduction","preamble","preface","overture","precursor","forerunner"],"k":["build-up","foretaste","foreword","inception"],"a":["epilogue","conclusion","aftermath","finale"],"ex":["The light rain was only a prelude to the heavy storm.","A short quiz is a good prelude to the main lesson.","The first meeting was merely a prelude to months of hard work."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"premeditated","p":"adjective","d":"Thought about and planned in advance, rather than done suddenly or by accident.","lb":"planned, deliberate","s":["planned","deliberate","intentional","calculated","prearranged","designed"],"k":["aforethought","cold-blooded","conscious","intended"],"a":["spontaneous","unplanned","impulsive","accidental"],"ex":["Prosecutors argued that the theft was premeditated, because the thief had studied the guard's schedule.","The judge said it was a premeditated crime, not a sudden act of anger.","Her sharp reply sounded premeditated, as if she had practised it in front of a mirror."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"premise","p":"noun","d":"An idea or statement that is accepted as true and used as the basis for an argument or plan.","lb":"assumption, basis","s":["assumption","proposition","hypothesis","postulate","supposition","basis"],"k":["cornerstone","foundation","groundwork","rationale"],"a":["conclusion","consequence","outcome"],"ex":["The whole plan rests on the premise that more people will take the new bus route.","Your argument fails because its main premise, that everyone has fast internet, is simply untrue.","The class was built on the premise that students learn best by teaching each other."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"preponderance","p":"noun","d":"A greater number, amount or importance; the fact of being larger or more powerful than others.","lb":"majority, predominance","s":["majority","dominance","bulk","superiority","greater part"],"k":["body","excess","figure","mass"],"a":["minority","handful","minimum"],"ex":["There is a preponderance of women in the nursing profession.","A preponderance of evidence pointed to the cook as the person who left the gas on.","The preponderance of positive reviews convinced me to buy the headphones."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"prepossess","p":"verb","d":"To influence someone's opinion in advance, often favorably, before they have had a chance to judge for themselves.","lb":"influence, bias","s":["influence","bias","predispose","prejudice","sway","impress"],"k":["act upon","bewitch","captivate","charm"],"a":[],"ex":["The glowing reviews prepossessed me in favor of the restaurant before I even sat down.","A friend's warning had prepossessed her against the new manager, so she barely gave him a chance.","His polite manner and neat appearance prepossessed the interview panel in his favor."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"preposterous","p":"adjective","d":"So unreasonable or silly that it is hard to take seriously.","lb":"absurd, ridiculous","s":["absurd","ridiculous","ludicrous","outrageous","laughable","farcical"],"k":["bizarre","cockeyed","comical","crazy"],"a":["sensible","reasonable","logical","rational"],"ex":["It is preposterous to expect a ten-year-old to carry such a heavy bag.","He gave a preposterous excuse about a dog eating his laptop.","The idea of finishing the whole syllabus in one night is preposterous."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"prerogative","p":"noun","d":"A special right or privilege that belongs to a particular person, position or group.","lb":"right, privilege","s":["right","privilege","entitlement","birthright","perquisite","advantage"],"k":["allowance","claim","due","exclusive right"],"a":[],"ex":["Choosing the final team is the coach's prerogative, and the players must accept it.","It is my prerogative to change my mind if I find a better offer.","As the owner, she has the prerogative to close the shop whenever she likes."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"presage","p":"verb","d":"To be a sign that something, usually bad, is going to happen.","lb":"portend, foreshadow","s":["portend","foreshadow","herald","augur","foretell","signal"],"k":["adumbrate","bespeak","betoken","bode"],"a":[],"ex":["Dark clouds in the west presaged a heavy storm before evening.","The sudden drop in sales presaged bigger problems for the company.","His long silence at dinner presaged bad news."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"presentiment","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling that something bad is going to happen.","lb":"foreboding, premonition","s":["premonition","foreboding","hunch","misgiving","apprehension","intuition"],"k":["anxiety","fear","gut feeling","inkling"],"a":[],"ex":["She had a presentiment that something was wrong when her brother did not answer his phone.","A sudden presentiment of danger made him stop and look both ways before crossing the road.","I felt a presentiment of failure the moment I opened the exam paper."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"presumably","p":"adverb","d":"Used to say that you think something is probably true, although you are not completely sure.","lb":"probably, doubtless","s":["probably","doubtless","no doubt","most likely","in all likelihood","apparently"],"k":["by all accounts","in all probability","it would seem","one assumes"],"a":["unlikely"],"ex":["The lights are off, so presumably everyone has gone home.","You presumably know the way, since you have driven here before.","Presumably, the train is late because of the heavy fog."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"presumptuous","p":"adjective","d":"Behaving with too much confidence by taking liberties or assuming rights that nobody has given you.","lb":"bold, forward","s":["forward","bold","arrogant","brazen","audacious","impertinent"],"k":["assuming","brave","bumptious","cocky"],"a":["modest","humble","deferential","respectful"],"ex":["It would be presumptuous of me to give advice when I have worked here for only a week.","The new intern was presumptuous enough to rearrange the manager's desk without asking.","Isn't it a bit presumptuous to assume that everyone will agree with your plan?"],"b":67,"y":2},{"w":"presuppose","p":"verb","d":"To assume that something is true before you start to reason, or to need something else to be true first.","lb":"assume, require","s":["assume","presume","take for granted","postulate","suppose","imply"],"k":["believe","call for","entail","expect"],"a":[],"ex":["Your survey question presupposes that everyone owns a smartphone, which simply isn't true.","The business plan presupposes that the funding will arrive on time.","Learning calculus presupposes a good grasp of basic algebra."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"prevail","p":"verb","d":"To win or succeed in the end, especially after a struggle or against opposition.","lb":"win, triumph","s":["win","triumph","succeed","overcome","win out","carry the day"],"k":["die hard","hold","obtain","persist"],"a":["lose","fail","yield","succumb"],"ex":["After a close match, the home team prevailed by a single goal.","We hope that common sense will prevail and the two sides will stop arguing.","In the long run, steady study prevails over last-night cramming."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"prevalent","p":"adjective","d":"Existing or happening commonly in a particular place or at a particular time.","lb":"widespread, common","s":["widespread","common","rife","frequent","rampant","universal"],"k":["current","dominant","epidemic","extensive"],"a":["rare","uncommon","scarce","unusual"],"ex":["Dengue fever is most prevalent during the rainy months.","Smartphones have become prevalent even in remote villages.","Cheating was once prevalent in this school, but strict supervision has reduced it."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"prevaricate","p":"verb","d":"To avoid giving a direct or honest answer, usually by being vague or misleading.","lb":"evade, equivocate","s":["equivocate","evade","hedge","dodge","stall","fudge"],"k":["circumvent","duck","elude","mislead"],"a":["come clean","speak plainly","be candid","tell the truth"],"ex":["When asked where the missing money had gone, the treasurer began to prevaricate.","Stop prevaricating and tell me whether you broke the window.","The company prevaricated for weeks before admitting that the product was faulty."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"primal","p":"adjective","d":"Very basic or original; connected with the earliest stage of something or with deep human instincts.","lb":"primitive, instinctive","s":["primitive","primeval","original","basic","instinctive","fundamental"],"k":["aboriginal","cardinal","central","early"],"a":["modern","advanced","recent","acquired"],"ex":["Fear of the dark is a primal instinct that many adults still feel.","The primal need for food and shelter comes before everything else.","The drums gave the music a primal energy that made everyone dance."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"prior","p":"adjective","d":"Happening or existing before a particular time or event.","lb":"earlier, previous","s":["earlier","previous","preceding","former","past","foregoing"],"k":["anterior","precursory","preexisting","prefatory"],"a":["later","subsequent","following","ensuing"],"ex":["This job requires no prior experience, because we train everyone from the start.","You need prior permission from the principal to use the hall.","I had a prior engagement, so I couldn't attend the meeting."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"pristine","p":"adjective","d":"Perfectly clean, fresh or unspoiled, as if it had never been used, touched or damaged.","lb":"unspoiled, spotless","s":["unspoiled","immaculate","spotless","untouched","unblemished","pure"],"k":["clean","impeccable","intact","mint"],"a":["spoiled","polluted","dirty","damaged"],"ex":["The used bike was in pristine condition, without a single scratch on the frame.","Tourists come to the island for its pristine beaches and clear blue water.","She wore a pristine white shirt to the interview and kept it spotless all day."],"b":59,"y":0},{"w":"privation","p":"noun","d":"A lack of the basic things people need to live comfortably, such as food, warmth or money.","lb":"hardship, want","s":["hardship","deprivation","want","poverty","need","austerity"],"k":["famine","hunger","impoverishment","indigence"],"a":["plenty","abundance","comfort","affluence"],"ex":["The family endured years of privation after the factory closed.","Soldiers in the story faced cold and privation during the long winter.","Children living in privation often cannot focus at school."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"probity","p":"noun","d":"Complete honesty and strong moral principles, especially in matters of money or public duty.","lb":"honesty, integrity","s":["integrity","honesty","rectitude","honor","decency","virtue"],"k":["blamelessness","fair-mindedness","impeccability","scrupulousness"],"a":["dishonesty","corruption","deceit","immorality"],"ex":["The auditor was chosen for her probity, so nobody doubted the accuracy of her report.","A bank manager must show absolute probity, because customers trust him with their savings.","Our village headmaster was known for his probity and never accepted a gift from any parent."],"b":11,"y":0},{"w":"problematic","p":"adjective","d":"Difficult to deal with or solve, or open to doubt and likely to cause trouble.","lb":"troublesome, questionable","s":["troublesome","questionable","doubtful","difficult","tricky","awkward"],"k":["apocryphal","baffling","debatable","dubious"],"a":["straightforward","easy","simple"],"ex":["Parking near the market is becoming problematic as more shops open every month.","The study's results are problematic because only twelve students took part.","A phone battery that dies by lunchtime is problematic for anyone who travels all day."],"b":9,"y":0},{"w":"proclaim","p":"verb","d":"To announce something publicly and clearly so that everyone knows it.","lb":"announce, declare","s":["announce","declare","herald","broadcast","trumpet","pronounce"],"k":["assert","avow","exalt","exclaim"],"a":["conceal","hide","suppress","withhold"],"ex":["The loudspeaker on the van proclaimed that the school fair would begin on Saturday.","In his speech, the captain proclaimed that the team would win the cup this year.","She proclaimed her innocence loudly, but the manager did not believe her."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"procrastinator","p":"noun","d":"A person who keeps delaying things they should do, often until the last moment.","lb":"delayer, dawdler","s":["slacker","idler","staller","dawdler","laggard"],"k":["dilly-dallier","lingerer","loiterer","shirker"],"a":["achiever","doer","planner"],"ex":["I am a terrible procrastinator, and I usually start my assignments the night before.","As a lifelong procrastinator, Rafi finally bought a planner to keep track of deadlines.","Procrastinators often feel anxious because unfinished tasks stay on their minds."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"procure","p":"verb","d":"To obtain something, especially by effort or careful planning.","lb":"obtain, acquire","s":["obtain","acquire","get","secure","gain","source"],"k":["attain","bag","earn","hunt down"],"a":["lose","forfeit","relinquish","surrender"],"ex":["It took the organisers weeks to procure enough chairs for the graduation ceremony.","The hospital struggled to procure oxygen cylinders during the emergency.","She procured two tickets for the cricket match by queuing overnight."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"prodigal","p":"adjective","d":"Spending money or resources freely and carelessly, in a way that wastes them.","lb":"wasteful, extravagant","s":["wasteful","extravagant","spendthrift","reckless","lavish","profligate"],"k":["dissolute","free-spending","imprudent","unthrifty"],"a":["thrifty","frugal","economical","sparing"],"ex":["After his first big bonus, Imran grew prodigal and bought gadgets he never used.","Her prodigal spending on parties left her with nothing for the rent.","The prodigal use of water in the hostel worried the caretaker during the dry season."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"prodigious","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely large or impressive, in a way that causes surprise or admiration.","lb":"enormous, remarkable","s":["enormous","colossal","immense","vast","huge","tremendous"],"k":["big","exceeding","exceptional","extraordinary"],"a":["tiny","small","minute","modest"],"ex":["The young pianist showed a prodigious talent and played in public at age seven.","Building the bridge in six months took a prodigious amount of work.","My uncle has a prodigious appetite and can finish three plates of biryani."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"prodigy","p":"noun","d":"A young person with exceptional talent or ability.","lb":"genius, wonder child","s":["genius","wunderkind","whiz","marvel","phenomenon","virtuoso"],"k":["brain","einstein","omen","portent"],"a":[],"ex":["The eight-year-old chess prodigy beat players three times her age.","My cousin is a math prodigy who solved university-level problems at twelve.","As a musical prodigy, he performed on stage before he could read."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"profane","p":"adjective","d":"Showing disrespect for religion or sacred things, or using rude and offensive language.","lb":"irreverent, vulgar","s":["irreverent","blasphemous","sacrilegious","impious","vulgar","obscene"],"k":["blue","dirty","disrespectful","godless"],"a":["sacred","holy","reverent","pious"],"ex":["The teacher warned the class not to use profane language during the school program.","He was removed from the stadium for shouting profane insults at the referee.","The editor deleted the profane comments from the website before anyone else could read them."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"profess","p":"verb","d":"To openly claim or state something, sometimes when it is not really true.","lb":"claim, declare","s":["claim","declare","assert","affirm","state","pretend"],"k":["argue","concede","confess","contend"],"a":["deny","disclaim","disown","conceal"],"ex":["He professes to know everything about computers, but he could not fix my simple problem.","She professed her love for the city, yet she planned to leave as soon as possible.","Many candidates profess a passion for teamwork in interviews, but few can give real examples."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"proficient","p":"adjective","d":"Having the skill and training to do something well.","lb":"skilled, competent","s":["skilled","competent","adept","capable","expert","accomplished"],"k":["adroit","deft","efficient","experienced"],"a":["incompetent","unskilled","inept","clumsy"],"ex":["Nadia is proficient in three languages and works as a guide for foreign visitors.","Applicants should be proficient in spreadsheet software and able to write clear reports.","After months of practice, Rafi became proficient at driving in heavy Dhaka traffic."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"profligate","p":"adjective","d":"Spending money or using resources in a careless and wasteful way.","lb":"wasteful, extravagant","s":["wasteful","extravagant","spendthrift","prodigal","lavish","reckless"],"k":["debauched","degraded","dissipated","immoral"],"a":["thrifty","frugal","economical","careful"],"ex":["His profligate spending on new gadgets left him with no money by the middle of the month.","The council was criticized for profligate use of public money on fancy offices.","Leaving all the lights and fans on all day is a profligate use of electricity."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"profound","p":"adjective","d":"Showing great depth of thought or feeling, or having a very strong and lasting effect.","lb":"deep, intense","s":["deep","intense","heartfelt","insightful","serious","thoughtful"],"k":["acute","earnest","fervent","fundamental"],"a":["shallow","superficial","trivial","slight"],"ex":["Moving to a new city had a profound effect on how she saw her own country.","The teacher's quiet advice made a profound impression on the whole class.","He felt a profound sadness when his old neighborhood was torn down."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"profuse","p":"adjective","d":"Given or produced in very large amounts; plentiful and often generous.","lb":"abundant, copious","s":["abundant","copious","plentiful","lavish","generous","ample"],"k":["exuberant","luxuriant","plenteous","prolific"],"a":["scant","meager","sparse","scarce"],"ex":["The driver made profuse apologies for being late and offered to refund the fare.","The cut was not deep, but the profuse bleeding scared the children.","She offered profuse thanks to the neighbors who helped during the flood."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"profusion","p":"noun","d":"A very large amount of something; great abundance.","lb":"abundance, plenty","s":["abundance","plenty","wealth","glut","multitude","bounty"],"k":["affluence","cornucopia","exuberance","lots"],"a":["scarcity","shortage","lack","dearth"],"ex":["Wildflowers grow in profusion along the hillside after the spring rains.","The market offers a profusion of fruit in summer, from mangoes to lychees.","A profusion of colours filled the streets during the festival."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"progeny","p":"noun","d":"The children of a person, or the young of an animal or plant.","lb":"offspring, descendants","s":["offspring","children","descendants","young","issue","heirs"],"k":["fry","kin","posterity","relation"],"a":["ancestors","parents","forebears","forefathers"],"ex":["The old farmer was proud that all his progeny had studied at university.","A female turtle lays many eggs, but only a few of her progeny survive.","The progeny of the original apple tree still grow in the orchard today."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"prohibitive","p":"adjective","d":"So high, especially in price or cost, that people cannot afford to buy or do something.","lb":"unaffordable, forbidding","s":["exorbitant","excessive","steep","restrictive","forbidding"],"k":["costly","crippling","daunting","extravagant"],"a":["affordable","reasonable","cheap","modest"],"ex":["The cost of private university tuition is prohibitive for many families in the countryside.","Air tickets during Eid week are so prohibitive that many students go home by bus.","Renting a flat in the city center is prohibitive on a junior clerk's salary."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"proletariat","p":"noun","d":"The class of ordinary working people, especially those who do manual or factory work for wages.","lb":"working class","s":["working class","workers","laborers","the masses","commoners","rank and file"],"k":["class","hoi polloi","labor","labor force"],"a":["bourgeoisie","upper class","aristocracy","elite"],"ex":["In the nineteenth century, the factory proletariat lived in crowded houses near the mills.","Writers like to describe the garment workers of Dhaka as the new urban proletariat.","The union claimed to speak for the proletariat, not the factory owners."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"proliferate","p":"verb","d":"To increase quickly in number or spread rapidly over a wide area.","lb":"multiply, spread","s":["multiply","spread","mushroom","increase","burgeon","snowball"],"k":["breed","explode","extend","grow"],"a":["dwindle","decline","diminish","shrink"],"ex":["Mosquitoes proliferate in stagnant water, so empty buckets and clear the drains after rain.","Coffee shops have proliferated across Dhaka over the past decade.","Fake news proliferates on social media faster than corrections can reach people."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"prolific","p":"adjective","d":"Producing a great amount of work, results or offspring.","lb":"productive, fertile","s":["productive","fertile","fruitful","abundant","creative","plentiful"],"k":["ample","effective","fecund","indefatigable"],"a":["unproductive","barren","sterile","infertile"],"ex":["She is a prolific writer who publishes a new children's book almost every year.","The striker was prolific this season, scoring more than thirty goals.","Rabbits are prolific breeders, so a small group can become a large family quickly."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"prolong","p":"verb","d":"To make something last longer than it normally would or should.","lb":"extend, lengthen","s":["extend","lengthen","stretch out","drag out","protract","sustain"],"k":["carry","continue","increase","keep up"],"a":["shorten","cut short","curtail","end"],"ex":["Good food and regular exercise can prolong your life.","Heavy rain prolonged our journey by almost three hours.","Let's not prolong the meeting; everyone has already made up their mind."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"prominence","p":"noun","d":"The state of being important, well known or easy to notice.","lb":"importance, fame","s":["fame","importance","renown","eminence","distinction","standing"],"k":["bulge","bump","clout","conspicuousness"],"a":["obscurity","insignificance","anonymity","unimportance"],"ex":["The young lawyer rose to prominence after winning a famous court case.","The newspaper gave the flood story great prominence by placing it on the front page.","Online shopping has grown in prominence during the last decade."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"prompt","p":"verb","d":"To cause someone to do something, or to cause something to happen.","lb":"cause, spur","s":["cause","trigger","spur","motivate","provoke","inspire"],"k":["activate","bring about","create","egg on"],"a":["deter","discourage","dissuade","prevent"],"ex":["A sudden rise in prices prompted many families to buy less meat.","The accident prompted the council to install a traffic light at the crossing.","What prompted you to apply for this course?"],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"promulgate","p":"verb","d":"To announce a law, idea or decision publicly and officially.","lb":"announce, proclaim","s":["announce","proclaim","declare","publish","issue","broadcast"],"k":["assert","avow","distribute","exclaim"],"a":["conceal","suppress","withhold","hide"],"ex":["The ministry promulgated new safety rules for all school buses.","The university will promulgate the revised exam rules next week.","Posters were used to promulgate the school's new uniform policy."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"propagate","p":"verb","d":"To spread something, such as an idea, information or a plant, so that it reaches more places or people.","lb":"spread, breed","s":["spread","circulate","disseminate","publicize","breed","multiply"],"k":["advertise","bare","communicate","disperse"],"a":["suppress","stifle","stop","contain"],"ex":["You can propagate a rose bush by planting a cutting in moist soil.","Some people propagate false rumors online without checking whether they are true.","The organization works to propagate healthy habits in rural schools."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"propensity","p":"noun","d":"A natural tendency to behave in a particular way, often one that is hard to change.","lb":"tendency, inclination","s":["tendency","inclination","leaning","proclivity","predisposition","bent"],"k":["bias","liking","proneness","readiness"],"a":["aversion","reluctance","dislike"],"ex":["My little brother has a propensity for losing his umbrella on rainy days.","Young drivers show a propensity to speed on empty roads late at night.","The old wooden house has a propensity to flood whenever the river rises."],"b":85,"y":3},{"w":"prophecy","p":"noun","d":"A statement saying what will happen in the future, especially one believed to come from a special power.","lb":"prediction, forecast","s":["prediction","forecast","augury","prognosis","divination","revelation"],"k":["foreboding","forecasting","harbinger","premonition"],"a":[],"ex":["An ancient prophecy said the river would one day turn and swallow the old town.","Her teacher's prophecy that she would become a doctor finally came true last year.","Some football fans trust the pre-match prophecy of a pet parrot, though it is only luck."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"propinquity","p":"noun","d":"Nearness in place or time; closeness of relationship.","lb":"nearness, proximity","s":["proximity","closeness","vicinity","kinship","affinity","similarity"],"k":["bordering","familiarity","juxtaposition","neighborhood"],"a":["distance","remoteness","separation","isolation"],"ex":["Friendships often grow out of propinquity, as when two students share a desk.","The propinquity of the school and the hospital makes the street very noisy.","Their propinquity as neighbors meant they met daily and became close friends."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"propitiate","p":"verb","d":"To calm someone's anger or win their goodwill by giving them something or doing something to please them.","lb":"appease, placate","s":["appease","placate","pacify","mollify","soothe","win over"],"k":["assuage","gratify","humor","lull"],"a":["provoke","anger","enrage","antagonize"],"ex":["He brought flowers and sweets to propitiate his wife after forgetting their anniversary.","The shop owner offered a full refund in order to propitiate the angry customer.","The airline gave stranded passengers free meals in an attempt to propitiate them."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"propitious","p":"adjective","d":"Giving signs that something will go well; favorable and likely to lead to success.","lb":"favorable, promising","s":["favorable","promising","auspicious","encouraging","fortunate","lucky"],"k":["approving","blessed","bright","golden"],"a":["unfavorable","inauspicious","ominous","unlucky"],"ex":["Clear skies and a gentle breeze made it a propitious morning for the boat race.","She waited for a propitious moment to ask her boss for a raise.","Low interest rates make this a propitious time to borrow money for a small business."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"proponent","p":"noun","d":"A person who publicly supports an idea, plan or cause and argues in favor of it.","lb":"advocate, supporter","s":["advocate","supporter","champion","backer","promoter","exponent"],"k":["ally","apostle","booster","evangelist"],"a":["opponent","critic","adversary","antagonist"],"ex":["She is a strong proponent of free school meals for every child.","Proponents of the new bridge say it will cut the journey time by half.","As a proponent of cycling, the mayor rides to work every day."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"propound","p":"verb","d":"To suggest an idea, theory or plan so that other people can think about it.","lb":"propose, put forward","s":["propose","put forward","advance","suggest","submit","present"],"k":["advise","air","bring up","counsel"],"a":["withdraw","retract","reject"],"ex":["The professor propounded a new theory about how languages spread.","In her speech, Nadia propounded the idea that schools should start later in the day.","Economists propounded several plans to control rising food prices."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"proprietary","p":"adjective","d":"Owned by a particular person or company and legally protected from being freely copied or used by others.","lb":"owned, protected","s":["patented","copyrighted","branded","private","exclusive","owned"],"k":["closed","in-house","own-brand","possessive"],"a":["public","generic","free","unrestricted"],"ex":["The company refused to share its proprietary software code with outside developers.","Employees must not discuss proprietary information about new products with anyone outside the firm.","Many phone makers use proprietary chargers, which forces customers to buy their accessories."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"propriety","p":"noun","d":"Behavior that follows accepted social rules and is considered polite, proper and morally correct.","lb":"decorum, correctness","s":["decorum","decency","etiquette","correctness","respectability","civility"],"k":["behavior","demeanor","deportment","fitness"],"a":["impropriety","indecency","rudeness","vulgarity"],"ex":["The headmaster reminded us to dress with propriety for the formal ceremony.","She questioned the propriety of accepting an expensive gift from a company she was auditing.","A strong sense of propriety stopped him from raising his voice at the elderly guests."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"prosaic","p":"adjective","d":"Ordinary and dull, with no imagination, beauty or excitement.","lb":"dull, ordinary","s":["dull","ordinary","mundane","unimaginative","humdrum","banal"],"k":["boring","common","commonplace","earthbound"],"a":["poetic","imaginative","exciting","colorful"],"ex":["The reason for the delay was prosaic: a flat tire on the main road.","After the thrilling first chapter, the rest of the book felt prosaic.","She wrote poetry at night, but her daytime job in the tax office was prosaic."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"proscribe","p":"verb","d":"To forbid something officially, especially by law or by a formal rule.","lb":"ban, forbid","s":["prohibit","ban","forbid","outlaw","bar","veto"],"k":["blacklist","block","censor","criminalize"],"a":["permit","allow","authorize","sanction"],"ex":["School rules proscribe the use of mobile phones during lessons.","The law proscribes the sale of cigarettes to anyone under eighteen.","Many hospitals proscribe flowers in intensive care wards for hygiene reasons."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"proselytize","p":"verb","d":"To try to persuade other people to join your religion, belief or cause.","lb":"convert, evangelize","s":["convert","preach","persuade","win over","recruit","campaign"],"k":["alter","change","convince","drum up support"],"a":[],"ex":["My cousin loves to proselytize about the benefits of a vegetarian diet.","At the party, he started to proselytize for his favorite programming language.","She doesn't proselytize about running; she simply invites friends to join her in the morning."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"protagonist","p":"noun","d":"The main character in a story, film or play, or the leading figure in an event.","lb":"main character","s":["hero","heroine","lead","main character","principal","central figure"],"k":["admirer","booster","chief actor","exponent"],"a":["antagonist","villain","opponent","adversary"],"ex":["The protagonist of the novel is a young girl who dreams of becoming a doctor.","In the film, the protagonist moves from a village to Dhaka to look for work.","Our teacher asked us to explain how the protagonist changes by the end of the story."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"protocol","p":"noun","d":"The set of formal rules and customs that guide correct behaviour on official or ceremonial occasions.","lb":"etiquette, rules","s":["etiquette","decorum","convention","formalities","courtesy","propriety"],"k":["ceremony","civility","code","communications protocol"],"a":["informality","impropriety","bad manners"],"ex":["Diplomatic protocol decides where each ambassador sits at an official state dinner.","The visiting minister's staff checked protocol carefully, including who would greet him at the airport.","Under school protocol, the chief guest is welcomed first and seated at the front."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"protract","p":"verb","d":"To make something last longer than necessary or expected.","lb":"prolong, extend","s":["prolong","lengthen","extend","drag out","draw out","stretch out"],"k":["belabor","carry","carry on","increase"],"a":["shorten","curtail","cut short","abridge"],"ex":["Endless questions from the audience protracted the meeting well beyond its scheduled hour.","The two companies had a protracted legal dispute that lasted nearly six years.","Heavy traffic protracted our journey from Dhaka to Sylhet by almost three hours."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"provident","p":"adjective","d":"Careful to plan and save for the future.","lb":"prudent, thrifty","s":["prudent","thrifty","frugal","careful","economical","cautious"],"k":["circumspect","discreet","farsighted","judicious"],"a":["improvident","wasteful","reckless","careless"],"ex":["My provident aunt saves a little money from every salary for emergencies.","It was provident of Nadia to carry an umbrella, since it rained heavily that afternoon.","Provident farmers store extra grain after a good harvest in case the next season is bad."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"provincial","p":"adjective","d":"Limited in outlook and interests, in the way of people who have not seen much of the wider world.","lb":"narrow-minded, unsophisticated","s":["parochial","insular","unsophisticated","narrow","limited"],"k":["hick","jerkwater","petty","pokey"],"a":["cosmopolitan","worldly","sophisticated","urbane"],"ex":["His provincial attitude showed when he refused to taste any food he had not eaten at home.","Moving to the capital made her realize how provincial her ideas about careers had been.","The critic called the play provincial because it only made sense to people from one small town."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"provisional","p":"adjective","d":"Arranged for now and likely to change later, once a final decision is made.","lb":"temporary, tentative","s":["temporary","interim","tentative","conditional","stopgap","makeshift"],"k":["caretaker","contingent","impermanent","intermediate"],"a":["permanent","final","definite","fixed"],"ex":["The university sent me a provisional offer, which depends on my final exam results.","He holds a provisional driving license until he passes the road test.","The provisional timetable may change after the teachers meet next week."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"provocation","p":"noun","d":"Something said or done that deliberately makes someone angry or causes a strong reaction.","lb":"incitement, taunt","s":["incitement","taunt","goading","instigation","annoyance","irritant"],"k":["aggravation","irritation","mental energy","psychic energy"],"a":["appeasement","pacification","calming"],"ex":["The dog attacked without any provocation, and the neighbours were shocked.","My brother refused to answer back, despite his friend's constant provocation at the dinner table.","The referee warned that any further provocation of the other team would lead to a red card."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"provoke","p":"verb","d":"To cause a strong reaction, especially anger, in someone or something.","lb":"cause, incite","s":["incite","arouse","stir up","anger","trigger","spark"],"k":["call forth","cause","create","elicit"],"a":["calm","soothe","pacify","appease"],"ex":["Don't provoke the dog; it may bite if you tease it.","His rude comment provoked an angry reply from the teacher.","The film provoked a long debate among the students."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"prowess","p":"noun","d":"Great skill or ability at something, especially one gained through practice.","lb":"skill, expertise","s":["skill","expertise","mastery","ability","talent","proficiency"],"k":["adroitness","art","artistry","capacity"],"a":["incompetence","ineptitude","clumsiness","weakness"],"ex":["The striker's prowess in front of goal made him the top scorer.","She impressed the interviewers with her prowess in data analysis.","Grandma is famous for her cooking prowess, especially at festival time."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"proximity","p":"noun","d":"The state of being near someone or something in distance or time.","lb":"nearness, closeness","s":["closeness","vicinity","propinquity","neighborhood","immediacy"],"k":["accessibility","approximation","convenience","handiness"],"a":["distance","remoteness","separation"],"ex":["We chose the apartment for its proximity to the metro station and my office.","The proximity of the market means we can buy fresh vegetables every morning.","Because of its proximity to the airport, the hotel is always busy with travelers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"prudence","p":"noun","d":"Careful good sense that helps you avoid risk, especially when you make decisions about money or safety.","lb":"caution, good sense","s":["caution","discretion","wisdom","foresight","care","judgment"],"k":["judgement","level-headedness","providence","sagacity"],"a":["recklessness","rashness","carelessness"],"ex":["With great prudence, she saved a part of her salary every month.","It is a matter of prudence to check the weather before a long river journey.","Prudence told him not to share his password, even with a close friend."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"prudent","p":"adjective","d":"Careful and sensible about the future, avoiding unnecessary risks and unwise spending.","lb":"careful, sensible","s":["careful","wise","sensible","cautious","judicious","thrifty"],"k":["astute","guarded","heady","provident"],"a":["imprudent","reckless","rash","careless"],"ex":["It is prudent to save some money every month in case of an emergency.","A prudent driver slows down on wet roads and keeps a safe distance from the car ahead.","She made a prudent decision to carry an umbrella during the monsoon season."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"prurient","p":"adjective","d":"Having or encouraging an unhealthy, excessive interest in sexual matters.","lb":"lewd, salacious","s":["lewd","salacious","lascivious","indecent","voyeuristic","obscene"],"k":["bawdy","carnal","dirty","lecherous"],"a":["decent","wholesome","pure","modest"],"ex":["The newspaper was criticized for printing prurient details about a celebrity's private life.","Many parents worry about prurient content on unfiltered websites.","Her prurient curiosity about her neighbours' affairs made people avoid her."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pseudonym","p":"noun","d":"A false name that a writer or other person uses instead of their real name.","lb":"alias, pen name","s":["alias","pen name","assumed name","nom de plume","stage name","false name"],"k":["cognomen","moniker","name","persona"],"a":["real name","true name"],"ex":["The author wrote her crime novels under a pseudonym so her colleagues would not know.","Many bloggers use a pseudonym to protect their privacy online.","He published his poems under a pseudonym because he was too shy to use his own name."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"psyche","p":"noun","d":"A person's mind and deepest feelings and attitudes, including the part they are not fully aware of.","lb":"mind, soul","s":["mind","soul","spirit","self","inner self","personality"],"k":["anima","brain","essence","head"],"a":["body","flesh","physique"],"ex":["Long periods of loneliness can damage a person's psyche.","The film explores the fragile psyche of a teenager who loses her father.","Failing an exam can hurt a student's psyche more than the teacher realizes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"puck","p":"noun","d":"A hard, flat rubber disc that players hit in the game of ice hockey.","lb":"hockey disc","s":["disc","hockey puck"],"k":["coin","counter","disk","plate"],"a":[],"ex":["The player shot the puck past the goalkeeper and the crowd cheered.","A hockey puck is made of hard rubber, so it can hurt if it hits you.","My cousin watched an ice hockey video and asked why the puck was not a ball."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"pummel","p":"verb","d":"To hit someone or something hard and repeatedly, especially with your fists.","lb":"pound, batter","s":["pound","batter","beat","thrash","hammer","punch"],"k":["belabor","biff","buffet","clobber"],"a":["stroke","caress","pat","soothe"],"ex":["The boxer pummeled the punching bag until his gloves were soaked with sweat.","Heavy hail pummeled the tin roof all night, and nobody could sleep.","Waves pummeled the small fishing boat as the storm grew stronger."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"punctilious","p":"adjective","d":"Very careful to follow rules, correct behaviour and small details exactly.","lb":"meticulous, careful","s":["meticulous","scrupulous","careful","precise","exacting","fastidious"],"k":["ceremonious","correct","diligent","formal"],"a":["careless","sloppy","negligent","slapdash"],"ex":["Our accountant is punctilious about keeping every receipt and recording each small payment.","The punctilious editor checked every comma and date before the book went to print.","My grandfather was punctilious about good manners and always stood up when a guest entered the room."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"pundit","p":"noun","d":"A person who is often asked to give an expert opinion on a subject, especially in the media.","lb":"expert, commentator","s":["expert","authority","commentator","analyst","specialist","scholar"],"k":["bookman","connoisseur","learned person","master"],"a":["novice","amateur","layman","beginner"],"ex":["A famous cricket pundit predicted that our team would win the final.","Economic pundits on television disagree about whether prices will fall next year.","The newspaper asked a health pundit to explain how to stay safe during the heat wave."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"pungent","p":"adjective","d":"Having a strong, sharp taste or smell that is powerful enough to sting the nose or tongue.","lb":"sharp, strong","s":["sharp","acrid","strong","piquant","tangy","biting"],"k":["aromatic","barbed","bitter","caustic"],"a":["mild","bland","faint","odorless"],"ex":["The pungent smell of mustard oil filled the kitchen as she began to fry the fish.","A pungent odor of burning rubber made the passengers cover their noses.","The cheese was so pungent that I could smell it through the sealed box."],"b":45,"y":0},{"w":"punitive","p":"adjective","d":"Intended as a punishment, or very harsh in the way it punishes.","lb":"penal, disciplinary","s":["penal","disciplinary","harsh","severe","vengeful"],"k":["correctional","draconian","heavy-handed","penitentiary"],"a":["rewarding","lenient","forgiving","merciful"],"ex":["The court imposed punitive damages on the company for hiding the defect.","The school's punitive rules made students afraid to speak up.","Punitive taxes on cigarettes aim to discourage smoking."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"puny","p":"adjective","d":"Small and weak, or too small and weak to be effective or important.","lb":"weak, feeble","s":["weak","feeble","frail","small","tiny","stunted"],"k":["decrepit","delicate","faint","fragile"],"a":["strong","sturdy","robust","mighty"],"ex":["The puny kitten could barely stand, so we fed it with a dropper.","He felt puny next to the huge wrestlers at the gym.","A puny wall of sandbags could not stop the rising river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"purblind","p":"adjective","d":"Having very poor eyesight, or lacking the insight to see what should be obvious.","lb":"short-sighted, obtuse","s":["obtuse","dense","myopic","visually impaired","visually challenged"],"k":["blind","heedless","naive","oblivious"],"a":["perceptive","insightful","observant"],"ex":["The purblind old man could only make out shapes in the dim light.","Critics called the manager purblind for ignoring the clear warning signs.","Without his glasses, he was practically purblind."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"puritanical","p":"adjective","d":"Having very strict moral rules and disapproving of pleasure, especially in behavior that others consider harmless.","lb":"strict, prudish","s":["strict","prudish","austere","rigid","severe","stern"],"k":["blue","harsh","priggish","prim"],"a":["permissive","liberal","easygoing","tolerant"],"ex":["Her puritanical aunt disapproved of music, parties and even colorful clothes.","The headmaster had a puritanical attitude and punished students for the smallest jokes.","He grew up in a puritanical home where watching television was almost forbidden."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"purported","p":"adjective","d":"Claimed or said to be true or real, although this has not been proved.","lb":"alleged, supposed","s":["alleged","supposed","claimed","so-called","reputed","ostensible"],"k":["bogus","presumed","pretended","questionable"],"a":["proven","confirmed","genuine","authentic"],"ex":["The purported benefits of the herbal drink have never been tested by doctors.","Police are investigating the purported theft of paintings from the school's art room.","The purported author of the letter denied having written a single word of it."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"putative","p":"adjective","d":"Generally believed or supposed to be a certain thing, though this has not been proved.","lb":"supposed, reputed","s":["supposed","reputed","alleged","presumed","assumed","purported"],"k":["accepted","acknowledged","claimed","conjectural"],"a":["proven","confirmed","certain","established"],"ex":["The putative cause of the fire was an old wire, but investigators are still checking.","Scientists are testing the putative health benefits of the herb in a large study.","The putative author of the poem lived five hundred years ago, though historians doubt it."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"quaint","p":"adjective","d":"Attractive or interesting because it is old-fashioned or unusual.","lb":"charming, old-fashioned","s":["charming","old-fashioned","picturesque","curious","unusual","whimsical"],"k":["archaic","bygone","endearing","fashionable"],"a":["modern","ordinary","contemporary","commonplace"],"ex":["We stayed in a quaint cottage with a thatched roof and a small garden.","The narrow lanes of Old Dhaka have a quaint charm that visitors love.","The shop sells quaint wooden toys that look like those from a hundred years ago."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"qualified","p":"adjective","d":"Limited by conditions or reservations, rather than fully approving, complete or absolute.","lb":"limited, conditional","s":["limited","conditional","restricted","guarded","reserved","tentative"],"k":["ambivalent","cautious","certified","confined"],"a":["unconditional","unqualified","absolute","wholehearted"],"ex":["The committee gave only qualified approval to the plan, with several conditions attached.","The new bus route was a qualified success: busy in the morning but nearly empty at night.","She offered qualified support for the idea, provided the cost stayed under budget."],"b":259,"y":0},{"w":"qualify","p":"verb","d":"To limit or adjust a statement so that it is less general or less strong.","lb":"limit, modify","s":["modify","limit","restrict","temper","moderate","soften"],"k":["change","characterize","confine","constrain"],"a":["overstate","generalize","exaggerate"],"ex":["I should qualify my praise: the food was good, but the service was very slow.","The scientist qualified her claim by adding that more tests were needed.","He qualified his promise with a warning that bad weather could delay the trip."],"b":280,"y":0},{"w":"qualitative","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the quality or nature of something rather than its amount or number.","lb":"quality-based, descriptive","s":["descriptive","subjective","interpretive","observational"],"k":["anecdotal","ethnographic","experiential","exploratory"],"a":["quantitative","numerical","measurable","statistical"],"ex":["The survey combined numbers with qualitative feedback, such as comments from customers about how they felt.","There is a qualitative difference between a good meal and just a full stomach.","Qualitative research uses interviews to understand why people choose one brand over another."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"quandary","p":"noun","d":"A state of not knowing what to do in a difficult situation where every choice has problems.","lb":"dilemma, predicament","s":["dilemma","predicament","plight","bind","fix","difficulty"],"k":["catch-22","conundrum","mess","muddle"],"a":[],"ex":["Nadia was in a quandary: she had two job offers and only one day to decide.","The shop owner faced a quandary when the supplier doubled prices just before Eid.","I am in a quandary about whether to study abroad or stay close to my parents."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"quarrel","p":"verb","d":"To argue angrily with someone about something.","lb":"argue, squabble","s":["argue","squabble","bicker","fight","row","dispute"],"k":["feud","hassle","have words","quibble"],"a":["agree","make up","reconcile","get along"],"ex":["My brother and I quarrel over the TV remote almost every evening.","The neighbours quarrelled about a tree whose branches hung over the wall.","Good friends may quarrel, but they usually make up within a day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"quasi","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming to be something but not completely; partly or almost so.","lb":"almost, partial","s":["almost","near","semi","pseudo","partial","apparent"],"k":["analogous","ersatz","faux","in a way"],"a":["genuine","real","true","full"],"ex":["The group is a quasi-government body, funded by taxes but run privately.","The tea stall became a quasi-office where he met his clients.","Their quasi-legal agreement was never written down properly."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"quay","p":"noun","d":"A platform built beside the water where boats can stop to load and unload.","lb":"wharf, dock","s":["wharf","dock","pier","jetty","landing stage"],"k":["berth","marina","mole","slipway"],"a":[],"ex":["Fishermen unloaded their boxes of fresh fish onto the quay at dawn.","We waited on the quay for the ferry to arrive.","Cargo ships lined up beside the quay, and cranes lifted containers all day."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"quell","p":"verb","d":"To put an end to something, especially trouble or strong feelings, by firm action or effort.","lb":"suppress, calm","s":["suppress","crush","subdue","put down","calm","silence"],"k":["appease","conquer","curb","mash"],"a":["incite","provoke","stir up","inflame"],"ex":["Extra police were sent to quell the crowd after the match ended in a noisy dispute.","The teacher raised her hand and quickly quelled the chatter in the classroom.","His calm explanation quelled her fears about the surgery."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"quench","p":"verb","d":"To satisfy your thirst by drinking something.","lb":"satisfy thirst","s":["satisfy","slake","sate","satiate","relieve","refresh"],"k":["appease","assuage","blow out","conform to"],"a":[],"ex":["Nothing quenches your thirst on a hot day like a glass of lemon water.","The runners quenched their thirst at the water stalls along the route.","After the long bus journey, he quenched his thirst with a cold green coconut."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"querulous","p":"adjective","d":"Often complaining, in a weak, irritated or whining way.","lb":"complaining, whiny","s":["complaining","whining","grumbling","petulant","peevish","grumpy"],"k":["crabby","cranky","disgruntled","fussy"],"a":["content","cheerful","easygoing","satisfied"],"ex":["The querulous customer complained about the music, the heat and the price of tea.","After waiting two hours, the patients grew querulous and began to complain to the nurse.","My grandfather's querulous voice rose whenever the television was too loud."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"query","p":"noun","d":"A question, especially one asking for information or expressing doubt about something.","lb":"question, inquiry","s":["question","inquiry","request","doubt","problem"],"k":["challenge","concern","dispute","enquiry"],"a":["answer","reply","response","solution"],"ex":["If you have any query about the exam schedule, please email the office.","The bank answered my query about the account fee within an hour.","A customer sent a query asking whether the shoes come in a larger size."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"queue","p":"noun","d":"A line of people or vehicles waiting for something, one behind the other.","lb":"line, file","s":["line","file","row","column","string","chain"],"k":["backlog","cue","gridlock","lineup"],"a":[],"ex":["A long queue formed outside the bank before it opened.","Please join the queue at the back, because everyone here has waited an hour.","There was a queue of cars at the ferry terminal on the first day of the Eid holidays."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"quibble","p":"verb","d":"To argue or complain about a small, unimportant detail instead of dealing with the main issue.","lb":"nitpick, cavil","s":["nitpick","cavil","carp","split hairs","find fault","bicker"],"k":["argue","complain","contend","dispute"],"a":["agree","concede","accept","yield"],"ex":["Let's not quibble over a few taka when the whole trip costs thousands.","The two roommates quibbled about whose turn it was to wash the dishes.","Reviewers quibbled over small details in the film but praised its moving story."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"quid pro quo","p":"noun","d":"Something given or done in return for something else, as an equal exchange of favors or benefits.","lb":"fair exchange, return favor","s":["exchange","swap","tit for tat","return","reciprocation","payback"],"k":["back-scratching","bargain","consideration","deal"],"a":[],"ex":["I'll help you with maths, and in return you'll teach me guitar; it's a fair quid pro quo.","The coach offered extra practice time as a quid pro quo for the team's full attendance.","There is always a quid pro quo: the app is free, and users give their data."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"quiescent","p":"adjective","d":"Quiet, still or inactive for a period of time, but able to become active again.","lb":"inactive, dormant","s":["dormant","inactive","still","idle","latent","inert"],"k":["lying low","motionless","sleeping","slumbering"],"a":["active","lively","energetic","erupting"],"ex":["The volcano has been quiescent for centuries, but scientists still monitor it closely.","After the exams, the usually busy hostel became quiescent for the whole holiday.","The disease can stay quiescent in the body for years before any symptoms appear."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"quintessential","p":"adjective","d":"Being the most perfect or typical example of a particular quality or type of thing.","lb":"typical, perfect","s":["typical","classic","ultimate","archetypal","definitive","perfect"],"k":["characteristic","emblematic","exemplary","final"],"a":["atypical","unusual","uncharacteristic","imperfect"],"ex":["Hilsa fish with rice is the quintessential Bengali meal.","She is the quintessential teacher: patient, kind and always well prepared.","That film is the quintessential road movie: two friends, an old car and an endless highway."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"quixotic","p":"adjective","d":"Very idealistic and generous but impractical, with little thought for reality.","lb":"idealistic, impractical","s":["idealistic","impractical","romantic","unrealistic","visionary","utopian"],"k":["airy","chimerical","dreamy","fantastical"],"a":["practical","realistic","pragmatic","sensible"],"ex":["His quixotic plan to plant a million trees all by himself made everyone smile.","It seems quixotic to start a free library in a village with no electricity, but she did it.","Rafi's quixotic dream of becoming a world champion with no coach was admirable but unrealistic."],"b":532,"y":0},{"w":"quizzical","p":"adjective","d":"Showing mild surprise or puzzlement in a questioning, slightly amused way.","lb":"puzzled, questioning","s":["questioning","puzzled","curious","inquiring","perplexed","amused"],"k":["arch","askance","at a loss","bemused"],"a":["unquestioning","indifferent","certain"],"ex":["She gave me a quizzical look when I said I had finished all the homework in ten minutes.","The teacher raised a quizzical eyebrow at the unusual excuse.","With a quizzical smile, Rafi asked why the cat was sitting in the empty box."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"quotidian","p":"adjective","d":"Happening every day; ordinary and routine, sometimes to the point of being dull.","lb":"daily, everyday","s":["daily","everyday","ordinary","routine","commonplace","mundane"],"k":["common","habitual","normal","prosaic"],"a":["unusual","extraordinary","exceptional","rare"],"ex":["Cooking, cleaning and paying bills fill most of our quotidian life.","The novel finds beauty in quotidian events, such as boiling tea or catching a bus.","After the wedding excitement ended, the family returned to its quotidian routine."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"rabble","p":"noun","d":"A noisy, disorderly crowd of people who are hard to control.","lb":"unruly crowd","s":["mob","crowd","horde","throng","mass","riffraff"],"k":["gathering","herd","hoi polloi","lower orders"],"a":[],"ex":["A rabble of fans pushed past the guards and rushed onto the field.","The teacher walked into the classroom and found a noisy rabble instead of students.","Shoppers fought for sale items, and the store soon looked like a rabble."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"race","p":"noun","d":"A competition to find out who is the fastest in reaching a place or finishing a task.","lb":"contest, competition","s":["contest","competition","sprint","run","marathon","dash"],"k":["airstream","backwash","game","match"],"a":[],"ex":["Our school holds a running race every year on Sports Day.","She won the swimming race by less than a second.","The boat race on the river drew thousands of cheering spectators."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"radical","p":"adjective","d":"Very different from what is usual, especially in a way that brings major change.","lb":"extreme, far-reaching","s":["drastic","extreme","sweeping","thorough","fundamental","revolutionary"],"k":["basal","basic","comprehensive","dire"],"a":["moderate","minor","slight","conventional"],"ex":["The school made a radical change by starting classes an hour later.","Doctors recommended a radical change in his diet.","Smartphones brought radical changes to the way people pay bills."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"ramification","p":"noun","d":"A possible, often complicated result or consequence of an action or decision.","lb":"consequence, implication","s":["consequence","result","outcome","implication","repercussion","effect"],"k":["branch","branching","byproduct","conclusion"],"a":["cause","origin","source"],"ex":["Before quitting your job, think about the financial ramifications for your whole family.","The new law has serious ramifications for small shop owners.","Nobody understood the ramifications of closing the road until traffic stopped in every nearby street."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"rampant","p":"adjective","d":"Spreading or growing very quickly in a way that is difficult to control.","lb":"widespread, unchecked","s":["widespread","unchecked","uncontrolled","rife","prevalent","unrestrained"],"k":["abundant","common","epidemic","erect"],"a":["controlled","rare","restrained","limited"],"ex":["Dengue was rampant in the city that summer, and the hospitals were full.","Cheating became rampant when the invigilators stopped checking the hall.","Rumours were rampant on social media after the match was cancelled."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"rampart","p":"noun","d":"A wide wall of earth or stone built around a castle or town to defend it.","lb":"fortification, bulwark","s":["bulwark","bastion","fortification","embankment","wall","barricade"],"k":["barrier","battlement","berm","breastwork"],"a":[],"ex":["Tourists walked along the ramparts of the old fort and took photographs of the city.","Soldiers once stood guard on the ramparts, watching the road for enemies.","The ramparts of the old fort are crumbling, and workers are repairing them stone by stone."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"rancor","p":"noun","d":"Deep, lasting bitterness and anger toward someone because of past wrongs.","lb":"bitterness, resentment","s":["bitterness","resentment","spite","animosity","hatred","ill will"],"k":["acrimony","antagonism","bad blood","enmity"],"a":["goodwill","forgiveness","kindness","affection"],"ex":["Years after the quarrel, the brothers still spoke to each other with rancor.","She forgave her friend without rancor and never mentioned the matter again.","The debate was fierce but free of rancor, and everyone shook hands afterward."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rapacious","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely greedy for money or possessions and willing to take them unfairly from others.","lb":"greedy, grasping","s":["greedy","grasping","avaricious","voracious","insatiable","predatory"],"k":["aggressive","avid","extortionate","gluttonous"],"a":["generous","charitable","unselfish","giving"],"ex":["The rapacious moneylender charged poor villagers so much interest that they could never repay him.","A rapacious landlord raised the rent three times in one year and ignored every complaint.","Critics accused the company of rapacious pricing during the shortage of cooking oil."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rapture","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of extreme joy and excitement that fills your mind completely.","lb":"ecstasy, bliss","s":["ecstasy","bliss","joy","elation","euphoria","delight"],"k":["emotional state","enchantment","exhilaration","fervor"],"a":["misery","despair","sorrow","agony"],"ex":["The children watched the fireworks in rapture, their eyes wide.","She read her admission letter again and again, her face full of rapture.","The audience listened in rapture as the violinist played the last piece."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rarefied","p":"adjective","d":"Belonging to or understood by only a small, privileged or highly educated group, and remote from ordinary life.","lb":"elite, exclusive","s":["exclusive","elite","esoteric","lofty","select","refined"],"k":["cerebral","cloistered","elevated","exalted"],"a":["ordinary","common","everyday","mundane"],"ex":["She grew up in the rarefied world of private schools and holidays abroad.","The professor's rarefied language left most first-year students completely lost.","Few people ever enter the rarefied circle of top chess champions."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"ratify","p":"verb","d":"To approve an agreement or decision officially, so that it becomes valid.","lb":"approve, confirm","s":["approve","confirm","endorse","sign","validate","authorize"],"k":["attest","back up","corroborate","formalize"],"a":["reject","veto","repeal","annul"],"ex":["The members voted to ratify the new club rules at the annual meeting.","Both countries must ratify the agreement before it takes effect.","The workers will ratify the pay deal if more than half of them vote yes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"ratiocination","p":"noun","d":"The process of thinking carefully and logically in order to reach a conclusion.","lb":"logical reasoning","s":["reasoning","logic","deduction","inference","thinking","analysis"],"k":["abstract thought","argumentation","cerebration","conclusion"],"a":["intuition","guesswork","impulse","instinct"],"ex":["The detective solved the case through careful ratiocination rather than luck.","Chess rewards patient ratiocination, because you must think several moves ahead.","Mathematics teaches students the habit of ratiocination: stating each step and giving a reason for it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rationale","p":"noun","d":"The reasons or logical thinking behind a decision, action or belief.","lb":"reason, logic","s":["reason","logic","grounds","explanation","justification","basis"],"k":["argument","case","defense","groundwork"],"a":[],"ex":["The headmaster explained the rationale for moving the exams to the morning.","I don't understand the rationale behind charging more for the smaller size.","The report sets out the rationale for building a new bridge over the river."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"raucous","p":"adjective","d":"Loud, rough and harsh in sound, often with noisy, disorderly behavior.","lb":"loud, rowdy","s":["loud","noisy","rowdy","boisterous","harsh","rough"],"k":["blaring","deafening","ear-splitting","hoarse"],"a":["quiet","soft","gentle","calm"],"ex":["A raucous crowd filled the stadium and cheered every goal as loudly as it could.","The raucous laughter from the next room kept me from sleeping.","Crows made a raucous noise at dawn outside my window."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"reactionary","p":"adjective","d":"Strongly opposed to change and wanting to return to old rules, ideas or ways of doing things.","lb":"ultraconservative, backward-looking","s":["old-fashioned","traditionalist","regressive","hidebound","conservative"],"k":["blinkered","fusty","illiberal","obstructionist"],"a":["progressive","liberal","radical"],"ex":["Reformers faced reactionary opposition from people who wanted to keep the old rules.","The headmaster's reactionary views on school uniforms surprised the younger teachers.","In the old film, the reactionary landlord refuses to let the village build a school."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rebuff","p":"verb","d":"To refuse someone's offer, request or attempt at friendship in a blunt or unfriendly way.","lb":"reject, snub","s":["reject","snub","spurn","refuse","decline","brush off"],"k":["deny","dismiss","disregard","fight off"],"a":["welcome","accept","embrace","invite"],"ex":["She rebuffed his repeated requests for money with a firm no.","The manager rebuffed our proposal without even reading it.","The tenant rebuffed the landlord's offer of a small payment to leave early."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rebuke","p":"verb","d":"To speak sharply to someone because they have done something wrong.","lb":"scold, reprimand","s":["scold","reprimand","reproach","admonish","chide","censure"],"k":["bawl out","call down","call on the carpet","call out"],"a":["praise","commend","compliment","applaud"],"ex":["The principal rebuked the students for littering the school ground.","She gently rebuked her son for not saying thank you.","The referee rebuked the player for arguing with his decision."],"b":80,"y":4},{"w":"rebut","p":"verb","d":"To argue against a statement or accusation and show that it is false or wrong.","lb":"refute, disprove","s":["refute","disprove","counter","contradict","deny","challenge"],"k":["contest","controvert","debunk","gainsay"],"a":["confirm","support","concede","admit"],"ex":["In the debate, Tania calmly rebutted every point her opponent had made.","The company released a statement to rebut claims that its product was unsafe.","He brought his bank records to rebut the accusation that he had hidden income."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"recalcitrant","p":"adjective","d":"Stubbornly refusing to obey rules or accept control, and therefore difficult to manage.","lb":"defiant, stubborn","s":["defiant","stubborn","unruly","obstinate","disobedient","uncooperative"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","dogged","fractious"],"a":["obedient","compliant","cooperative","docile"],"ex":["The recalcitrant toddler refused to put on his shoes, however gently his mother asked.","A few recalcitrant members of the club kept ignoring the new safety rules.","The recalcitrant printer jammed again, just minutes before the presentation began."],"b":533,"y":0},{"w":"recant","p":"verb","d":"To say publicly that you no longer hold a belief or statement that you made earlier.","lb":"retract, take back","s":["retract","withdraw","take back","renounce","disavow","repudiate"],"k":["backtrack","climb down","disown","eat one's words"],"a":["affirm","maintain","insist","stand by"],"ex":["The witness recanted her earlier statement after admitting she had not seen the accident clearly.","After a storm of angry comments, the blogger recanted his claims and apologized.","The researcher recanted his findings once other laboratories failed to repeat his results."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"recidivism","p":"noun","d":"The tendency of a person who has been punished for a crime to commit crimes again.","lb":"reoffending, relapse","s":["relapse","repeat offending","backsliding","return to crime","lapse","reversion"],"k":["career crime","chronic offending","criminality","delinquency"],"a":["rehabilitation","reform","recovery"],"ex":["The prison runs education classes to reduce recidivism among released inmates.","Studies show that job training lowers recidivism, because former prisoners can earn an honest living.","The judge was worried about the high recidivism among young offenders."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"reciprocal","p":"adjective","d":"Given, felt or done by each of two people or groups toward the other.","lb":"mutual, shared","s":["mutual","shared","joint","common","corresponding","complementary"],"k":["bilateral","collective","communal","interactive"],"a":["unilateral","unreturned","unrequited"],"ex":["The friendship works because the respect between them is reciprocal.","The two schools signed a reciprocal agreement that lets students attend each other's classes.","I helped him with math, and he did me a reciprocal favor by helping me with English."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"reciprocation","p":"noun","d":"The act of giving or doing something in return for what someone has given or done to you.","lb":"return, exchange","s":["repayment","return","exchange","interchange","reciprocity"],"k":["bilateral exchange","interaction","mutual aid","mutuality"],"a":[],"ex":["She invited us to dinner in reciprocation for our help with her move.","Friendship grows through the reciprocation of small kindnesses, such as sharing notes or lending books.","He gave generous gifts without expecting any reciprocation."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"recluse","p":"noun","d":"A person who chooses to live alone and avoids meeting or talking to other people.","lb":"hermit, loner","s":["hermit","loner","solitary","lone wolf","lone hand"],"k":["ascetic","introvert","misanthrope","outsider"],"a":["extrovert","socialite","people person"],"ex":["After his wife passed away, he became a recluse and rarely left the house.","The novelist lived as a recluse in the hills and refused every interview.","My neighbor is such a recluse that I have never seen her at a single festival."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"reclusive","p":"adjective","d":"Preferring to live alone and avoid other people.","lb":"solitary, withdrawn","s":["solitary","withdrawn","secluded","isolated","antisocial","retiring"],"k":["aloof","lonely","low-profile","private"],"a":["sociable","outgoing","gregarious","extroverted"],"ex":["The reclusive author rarely left his house and refused all interviews.","After her illness, she became reclusive and stopped answering calls from friends.","Our reclusive neighbor only comes out at night to feed the stray cats."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"reconcile","p":"verb","d":"To find a way to make two different ideas, facts or needs fit together without conflict.","lb":"harmonize, make compatible","s":["harmonize","square","balance","align","blend","settle"],"k":["accommodate","agree","bridge","come to terms with"],"a":["clash","conflict","contradict","divide"],"ex":["It is hard to reconcile a full-time job with preparing for the admission test.","The accountant tried to reconcile the two sets of figures but found a gap of fifty taka.","The report failed to reconcile the company's promises with what had actually happened."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reconciliation","p":"noun","d":"The act of becoming friends again after a quarrel or disagreement.","lb":"making peace","s":["reunion","rapprochement","settlement","truce","harmony","conciliation"],"k":["accord","balancing","ceasefire","cooperation"],"a":["estrangement","alienation","separation","rift"],"ex":["After years of silence, the two brothers finally achieved reconciliation.","The meeting ended in a warm reconciliation between the feuding neighbors.","Her visit to the hospital led to a reconciliation with her estranged father."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reconciling","p":"adjective","d":"Helping to end a disagreement and bring people or ideas back into harmony.","lb":"conciliatory, peacemaking","s":["conciliatory","appeasing","forgiving","healing","soothing"],"k":["accommodating","adaptive","bridging","compromising"],"a":["hostile","antagonistic","divisive","provocative"],"ex":["Her reconciling smile ended the long silence between the two sisters.","The headmaster's reconciling speech helped the rival groups sit together again.","He sent a reconciling message after their argument and offered to meet for tea."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"recondite","p":"adjective","d":"Hard to understand because it deals with a very obscure or specialized subject.","lb":"obscure, abstruse","s":["abstruse","obscure","esoteric","arcane","profound","deep"],"k":["academic","ambiguous","bookish","erudite"],"a":["clear","simple","obvious","accessible"],"ex":["The lecture on recondite points of medieval law lost most of the audience within ten minutes.","Her essay was full of recondite references that only a handful of scholars could follow.","I could not use the manual because its instructions were written in recondite technical language."],"b":29,"y":0},{"w":"reconnoiter","p":"verb","d":"To explore or observe an area to gather information about it, often before going there with others.","lb":"scout, survey","s":["scout","survey","explore","inspect","patrol","investigate"],"k":["examine","observe","review","scrutinize"],"a":[],"ex":["Before the group hike, two volunteers went ahead to reconnoiter the trail.","The team reconnoitered the wedding venue a week earlier to plan the seating.","We reconnoitered the neighborhood before deciding which apartment to rent."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"recrimination","p":"noun","d":"A bitter accusation made in answer to an accusation, often leading to angry blaming on both sides.","lb":"counter-accusation, blame","s":["mutual blame","blame","reproach","accusation","bickering"],"k":["acrimony","backbiting","censure","charge"],"a":["forgiveness","reconciliation","pardon"],"ex":["After the exam results came out, the roommates traded recriminations about who had kept the room too noisy.","The business partners parted ways with bitter recriminations about who had wasted the company's money.","Instead of blaming each other, the committee members agreed to fix the mistake without recrimination."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rectify","p":"verb","d":"To put something right that is wrong or has been done badly.","lb":"correct, fix","s":["correct","fix","remedy","amend","repair","redress"],"k":["mend","patch up","reclaim","refine"],"a":["worsen","aggravate","botch","spoil"],"ex":["The bank promised to rectify the error on my statement within two days.","The teacher rectified the mistake in the answer key before handing back the papers.","To rectify the delay, the courier company offered free delivery on my next order."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"redact","p":"verb","d":"To remove or hide private or secret parts of a document before it is shared.","lb":"censor, edit","s":["censor","black out","edit","blank out","obscure","delete"],"k":["alter","amend","change","modify"],"a":["reveal","disclose","publish","restore"],"ex":["The bank will redact your account number before sharing the document.","Journalists agreed to redact the witness's name to protect her safety.","Please redact all phone numbers from the report before you post it online."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"redeem","p":"verb","d":"To make up for a mistake or fault, or to make something bad seem better through one good quality.","lb":"make up for, atone","s":["make up for","compensate for","atone for","offset","balance","rescue"],"k":["absolve","deliver","exonerate","expiate"],"a":["condemn","ruin","worsen"],"ex":["Rafi redeemed himself by scoring twice after missing an easy chance in the first half.","The film's wonderful music redeems an otherwise weak story.","She tried to redeem the broken promise by helping her friend move house."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"redolent","p":"adjective","d":"Having a strong smell of something, usually pleasant; also, strongly reminding one of something.","lb":"fragrant, reminiscent","s":["fragrant","aromatic","scented","perfumed","evocative","reminiscent"],"k":["aware","heady","mindful","pungent"],"a":["odorless","unscented"],"ex":["The kitchen was redolent of cardamom and cinnamon as my aunt cooked the Eid biryani.","Walking through the old market, we passed shops redolent of fresh tea leaves and dried fish.","The garden was redolent with jasmine after the evening rain."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"redress","p":"noun","d":"Compensation or a remedy for harm or a wrong that has been done to someone.","lb":"remedy, compensation","s":["compensation","remedy","reparation","restitution","amends","satisfaction"],"k":["correction","damages","indemnification","indemnity"],"a":[],"ex":["Customers who receive damaged goods can seek redress by contacting the shop within seven days.","The workers demanded redress for months of unpaid overtime.","After the long delay, the airline offered redress in the form of flight vouchers."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"redundant","p":"adjective","d":"Not needed because it repeats something already said or already present.","lb":"unnecessary, repetitive","s":["unnecessary","superfluous","needless","repetitive","surplus","excessive"],"k":["excess","gratuitous","prolix","spare"],"a":["necessary","essential","needed","vital"],"ex":["The word new in brand new product is redundant, since brand already means new.","Delete redundant sentences from your essay so that it stays within the word limit.","Having three people check the same form is redundant and wastes time."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"reeking","p":"adjective","d":"Giving off a very strong and unpleasant smell.","lb":"stinking, smelly","s":["stinking","smelly","foul","rank","putrid","malodorous"],"k":["crappy","funky","fusty","icky"],"a":["fragrant","perfumed","aromatic"],"ex":["The reeking garbage heap near the market made everyone cover their noses.","My gym bag, left closed all weekend, was reeking when I opened it.","He came home from the fish market in reeking clothes and a happy mood."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reel","p":"verb","d":"To move unsteadily as if about to fall, or to feel shocked and unable to think clearly.","lb":"stagger, spin","s":["stagger","stumble","lurch","sway","wobble","whirl"],"k":["be dazed","be stunned","buckle","bumble"],"a":[],"ex":["He reeled backward when the heavy door swung open and hit him.","The town is still reeling from the effects of the flood.","She reeled with shock when she heard the news."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"referendum","p":"noun","d":"A direct vote by all the people of a place on one important question or proposal.","lb":"public vote, plebiscite","s":["plebiscite","public vote","ballot","poll","popular vote","straw poll"],"k":["consultation","election","initiative","mandate"],"a":[],"ex":["The town held a referendum on whether to build a new stadium.","In a referendum, citizens vote yes or no on a single proposal.","The club held a referendum among its members to decide on the new uniform."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"refill","p":"verb","d":"To fill a container or supply again after it has been emptied or used up.","lb":"fill again, replenish","s":["replenish","restock","top up","refuel","recharge","reload"],"k":["fill","fill again","fill up","make full"],"a":["empty","drain","deplete","exhaust"],"ex":["I refilled my water bottle at the fountain before the long walk.","The waiter kindly refilled our glasses without being asked.","Remember to refill the printer with paper before the class begins."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reflect","p":"verb","d":"To think carefully and seriously about something, especially something that happened in the past.","lb":"think deeply","s":["ponder","contemplate","consider","think","meditate","mull over"],"k":["chew over","cogitate","deem","mull"],"a":["ignore","disregard","neglect","overlook"],"ex":["After the exam, she sat on the stairs to reflect on her mistakes.","Take a day to reflect before you decide whether to accept the offer.","At the end of the year, I like to reflect on what I have learned."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"refractory","p":"adjective","d":"Stubborn and hard to control, refusing to do what you are told.","lb":"stubborn, unmanageable","s":["stubborn","unmanageable","obstinate","unruly","headstrong","obdurate"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","dogged","fractious"],"a":["obedient","compliant","docile","manageable"],"ex":["The refractory buffalo would not leave the road, and traffic stopped for ten minutes.","The refractory student argued with every rule that the new teacher announced.","Some refractory members of the team ignored the manager's instructions for months."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"refulgent","p":"adjective","d":"Shining brightly; giving off a radiant light.","lb":"shining, radiant","s":["radiant","shining","brilliant","gleaming","luminous","resplendent"],"k":["beaming","effulgent","glittering","incandescent"],"a":["dull","dim","dark","lackluster"],"ex":["The refulgent moon lit up the entire river, making the water look silver.","She smiled, refulgent with happiness, when she saw her exam results.","The refulgent golden dome of the new building caught the morning sun."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"refute","p":"verb","d":"To prove that a statement, claim or theory is wrong, using evidence or strong argument.","lb":"disprove, rebut","s":["disprove","rebut","debunk","counter","contradict","discredit"],"k":["confute","controvert","deny","dispute"],"a":["prove","confirm","support","verify"],"ex":["The scientist refuted the rumor by publishing clear data from three independent tests.","Bank records refuted his claim that he had been out of town on the day of the theft.","Nadia refuted her classmate's argument by pointing to the figures in the textbook."],"b":83,"y":2},{"w":"regale","p":"verb","d":"To entertain someone with funny or interesting stories.","lb":"entertain, delight","s":["entertain","amuse","delight","divert","charm","captivate"],"k":["cater","dazzle","feast","fete"],"a":["bore","tire","weary","annoy"],"ex":["My grandfather regaled us with stories about his school days in the village.","The guide regaled the tourists with legends about the old fort.","At the party, Rafi regaled everyone with a funny story about his first job interview."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"regime","p":"noun","d":"A government, especially one that has taken power in a way that is not fully democratic, or the system it uses to rule.","lb":"government, rule","s":["government","administration","rule","leadership","authority","system"],"k":["authorities","autocracy","cabinet","dictatorship"],"a":[],"ex":["Under the old regime, newspapers had to submit every story for approval before printing.","The new regime promised free primary education for every child.","Historians still debate why the regime collapsed so suddenly."],"b":160,"y":0},{"w":"regimen","p":"noun","d":"A fixed plan of treatment, diet or exercise that someone follows regularly to improve their health.","lb":"routine, plan","s":["routine","programme","schedule","plan","course","treatment plan"],"k":["agenda","itinerary","procedure","program"],"a":[],"ex":["The doctor prescribed a strict regimen of rest, fluids and medicine for the infection.","Her daily exercise regimen includes a short run and some stretching before breakfast.","Rafi followed a demanding study regimen in the three months before the admission test."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"reign","p":"verb","d":"To rule as a king or queen, or, of a feeling or condition, to be the strongest feature of a place or time.","lb":"rule, prevail","s":["rule","govern","hold sway","prevail","dominate","command"],"k":["be supreme","control","hold court","occupy the throne"],"a":["abdicate","submit","serve","yield"],"ex":["The queen reigned for more than sixty years, longer than any ruler before her.","The reigning champion lost in the first round of the tournament.","Silence reigned in the exam hall as the papers were handed out."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"reimbursement","p":"noun","d":"Money paid back to someone for costs they have already spent or for a loss.","lb":"repayment, refund","s":["repayment","refund","compensation","reparation","restitution","payback"],"k":["allowance","amends","cashback","damages"],"a":[],"ex":["I submitted the taxi receipts to the office and asked for reimbursement.","The company promised full reimbursement for any medicine we bought during the trip.","The airline offered reimbursement for the hotel room after the flight was cancelled."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"rein","p":"noun","d":"A long strap used to guide a horse; also, the power to control something.","lb":"strap, control","s":["bridle","harness","strap","control","check","restraint"],"k":["command","direction","governance","guidance"],"a":[],"ex":["The riding instructor showed the children how to hold the reins gently.","The coachman pulled the reins, and the horse cart stopped at the crossing.","The new manager was given free rein to redesign the whole system."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reinforce","p":"verb","d":"To make something stronger, especially by adding extra support or evidence.","lb":"strengthen, support","s":["strengthen","support","bolster","fortify","toughen","buttress"],"k":["beef up","boost","brace","consolidate"],"a":["weaken","undermine","undercut","erode"],"ex":["Builders reinforced the old bridge with steel bars before the monsoon.","Regular quizzes help reinforce what students learned in class.","The new evidence reinforced her belief that the accident was not her fault."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"reiterate","p":"verb","d":"To say something again, usually to make a point clearer or to stress it.","lb":"repeat, restate","s":["repeat","restate","say again","recap","reaffirm","emphasize"],"k":["belabor","drive home","echo","hammer home"],"a":[],"ex":["The teacher reiterated that the assignment must be submitted before Friday noon.","I want to reiterate that the offer is only valid until the end of the month.","Doctors continue to reiterate the importance of washing hands before every meal."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"relegate","p":"verb","d":"To move someone or something to a lower or less important position, rank or place.","lb":"demote, downgrade","s":["downgrade","consign","banish","lower","push aside","shunt"],"k":["assign","ban","bench","break"],"a":["promote","elevate","upgrade","raise"],"ex":["After the mistake, the coach relegated him to the bench for the next three matches.","Old textbooks were relegated to a dusty shelf in the corner of the library.","The old sofa was relegated to the balcony as soon as the new furniture arrived."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"relentless","p":"adjective","d":"Continuing in a harsh, determined way without stopping or becoming weaker.","lb":"unceasing, merciless","s":["unrelenting","unremitting","persistent","incessant","ceaseless","merciless"],"k":["constant","continual","continuous","endless"],"a":["intermittent","sporadic","merciful","yielding"],"ex":["Relentless rain flooded the streets of Dhaka for three days, and traffic nearly stopped.","Her relentless practice paid off when she finally passed the driving test on her fifth try.","The team faced relentless pressure from the manager to finish the project early."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"relevant","p":"adjective","d":"Connected with the subject being discussed or with what is happening now, and therefore important.","lb":"related, pertinent","s":["pertinent","applicable","related","appropriate","germane","apt"],"k":["apposite","connected","fitting","meaningful"],"a":["irrelevant","unrelated","immaterial","extraneous"],"ex":["Please send only the documents that are relevant to your application.","Her comment was not relevant to the topic, so the teacher moved on.","Choose a course that is relevant to the job you want in the future."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"reliable","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be trusted to do what is expected, or to give correct information.","lb":"dependable, trustworthy","s":["dependable","trustworthy","faithful","steady","responsible","sound"],"k":["authentic","certain","constant","honest"],"a":["unreliable","undependable","untrustworthy","unsound"],"ex":["My older sister is the most reliable person in our family; she never forgets a promise.","Check that the website is a reliable source before you use its facts in your essay.","A reliable internet connection is essential for working from home."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"relinquish","p":"verb","d":"To give up or let go of something, especially a position, right or possession.","lb":"surrender, abandon","s":["give up","surrender","renounce","yield","release","hand over"],"k":["abdicate","deliver","drop","forego"],"a":["keep","retain","hold","claim"],"ex":["The captain agreed to relinquish his place in the team so a younger player could play.","After forty years, the shop owner finally relinquished control of the business to his daughter.","She relinquished her seat on the crowded bus to an elderly man."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"reluctant","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to do something and slow to agree to do it.","lb":"unwilling, hesitant","s":["unwilling","hesitant","loath","disinclined","averse","resistant"],"k":["cautious","half-hearted","lukewarm","obstinate"],"a":["willing","eager","keen","enthusiastic"],"ex":["Rafi was reluctant to ask for help because he did not want to look weak.","The child was reluctant to leave the playground when his mother called.","Many people are reluctant to share personal information on social media."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"remark","p":"noun","d":"A short spoken or written comment that expresses a thought or opinion.","lb":"comment, statement","s":["comment","statement","observation","utterance","opinion","declaration"],"k":["announcement","aside","gloss","jibe"],"a":[],"ex":["His rude remark about her cooking made everyone uncomfortable.","The teacher made a kind remark about my essay.","I overheard a funny remark from the boy sitting behind me on the bus."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adjective","d":"Unusual or special in a way that makes people notice and admire it.","lb":"extraordinary, notable","s":["extraordinary","notable","striking","outstanding","exceptional","amazing"],"k":["astonishing","important","marvelous","memorable"],"a":["ordinary","unremarkable","commonplace","average"],"ex":["The boy made a remarkable recovery after the accident.","It is remarkable how fast the small shop has grown.","She has a remarkable memory for names and faces."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"remedial","p":"adjective","d":"Intended to correct a problem or to improve a weak skill or condition.","lb":"corrective, curative","s":["corrective","restorative","curative","therapeutic","healing","reparative"],"k":["bettering","compensatory","healthful","medicinal"],"a":[],"ex":["Students who struggle with reading can join remedial classes after school.","The government took remedial action to stop the river from eroding the village.","She took a remedial math course to catch up before starting engineering."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"reminiscent","p":"adjective","d":"Reminding you of someone or something from the past, or of something very similar.","lb":"evocative, suggestive","s":["evocative","suggestive","redolent","resembling","similar","recalling"],"k":["aware","bygone","mindful","nostalgic"],"a":[],"ex":["The smell of fresh bread was reminiscent of my grandmother's kitchen.","Her handwriting is strongly reminiscent of her mother's, with the same tall loops.","The old tea stall on the corner is reminiscent of the one near my school."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"remission","p":"noun","d":"A period when a serious illness becomes much less severe or seems to disappear.","lb":"abatement, respite","s":["abatement","lull","respite","relief","recovery","decrease"],"k":["absolution","comfort","hiatus","improvement"],"a":["relapse","recurrence","worsening"],"ex":["After two years of treatment, her cancer finally went into remission.","With the right diet and medicine, her arthritis stayed in remission for most of the year.","Doctors were happy to see signs of remission after the new therapy."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"remonstrate","p":"verb","d":"To protest or argue strongly against something, giving reasons for your objection.","lb":"protest, object","s":["protest","object","complain","argue","dissent","expostulate"],"k":["beef","call on the carpet","disagree","dispute"],"a":["agree","approve","consent","comply"],"ex":["Parents remonstrated with the principal about the sudden increase in school fees.","She remonstrated with the driver for ignoring the red light.","Residents remonstrated against the plan to cut down the old trees near the playground."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"remorse","p":"noun","d":"A deep feeling of guilt and sadness about something wrong that you have done.","lb":"regret, guilt","s":["guilt","regret","contrition","penitence","shame","compunction"],"k":["pangs of conscience","ruefulness","self-recrimination","self-reproach"],"a":["indifference","callousness"],"ex":["Rafi felt deep remorse after shouting at his mother.","The driver showed no remorse for leaving the scene of the accident.","She wrote a letter full of remorse to the friend she had lied to."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"remuneration","p":"noun","d":"Money paid to someone for work they have done or a service they have provided.","lb":"pay, payment","s":["payment","pay","salary","wages","earnings","compensation"],"k":["charge","emolument","honorarium","income"],"a":[],"ex":["The job offers fair remuneration, including a salary, medical insurance and two festival bonuses.","Volunteers receive no remuneration for their work at the community clinic.","Freelance writers should always agree on remuneration before they begin a project."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"renaissance","p":"noun","d":"A period of new interest and activity in something, such as art, learning or a place.","lb":"revival, rebirth","s":["revival","rebirth","resurgence","renewal","restoration","awakening"],"k":["blossoming","florescence","flowering","golden age"],"a":["decline","decay","stagnation","collapse"],"ex":["The old riverfront is enjoying a renaissance, with cafes and bookshops opening where warehouses once stood.","Handloom weaving has seen a renaissance as young designers return to traditional fabrics.","Her career went through a renaissance after she started teaching online."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"renascence","p":"noun","d":"A rebirth or revival, especially of interest in art, learning or culture.","lb":"rebirth, revival","s":["rebirth","revival","renaissance","resurgence","renewal","regeneration"],"k":["comeback","florescence","flowering","new dawn"],"a":["decline","decay","death","stagnation"],"ex":["Local music is enjoying a renascence, with young bands playing old folk songs in new ways.","The garden showed a renascence of color after the first monsoon rains.","Historians describe the late nineteenth century in Bengal as a time of intellectual renascence."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"rend","p":"verb","d":"To tear something apart violently or split it into pieces.","lb":"tear, split","s":["tear","rip","split","rupture","shred","cleave"],"k":["break","break apart","bust","divide"],"a":["mend","join","repair","unite"],"ex":["The strong wind threatened to rend the old tin roof from the walls of the house.","A sudden thunderclap seemed to rend the sky in two, and the children screamed.","Grief seemed to rend her heart when she heard the sad news."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"render","p":"verb","d":"To cause someone or something to be in a particular state or condition.","lb":"make, cause to be","s":["make","cause to be","leave","turn","transform","reduce"],"k":["alter","bring about","deliver","depict"],"a":[],"ex":["The heavy rain rendered the village road impassable for three days.","The software update rendered my old printer useless.","The shocking news rendered her speechless for a moment."],"b":98,"y":2},{"w":"rendezvous","p":"noun","d":"A planned meeting at a particular time and place, or the place chosen for it.","lb":"meeting, meeting place","s":["meeting","appointment","date","tryst","engagement","assignation"],"k":["assembly","assembly point","booking","encounter"],"a":[],"ex":["Our rendezvous was at the tea stall near the bus stop at five o'clock.","The hikers planned a rendezvous at the lake after taking different trails.","A rendezvous with my old classmates at the airport turned into a three-hour chat."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"renegade","p":"noun","d":"A person who deserts a group, cause or set of rules to follow their own way or to join the opposition.","lb":"deserter, rebel","s":["deserter","defector","traitor","turncoat","rebel","betrayer"],"k":["apostate","heretic","iconoclast","maverick"],"a":["loyalist","follower","supporter","believer"],"ex":["The captain called the player a renegade after he left the team for a rival club.","Once a loyal member, he became a renegade and shared the company's secrets with competitors.","The film's hero is a renegade police officer who refuses to follow orders."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"renewal","p":"noun","d":"The act of continuing something for a further period of time, or of making it fresh and new again.","lb":"extension, restoration","s":["extension","renovation","revival","restoration","resumption","rebirth"],"k":["reclamation","refilling","rehabilitation","replacement"],"a":["expiry","ending","termination","decay"],"ex":["The renewal of my passport takes about two weeks.","Please pay the renewal fee before your library card expires.","The renewal of the old market brought new shops and fresh paint to the area."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"renounce","p":"verb","d":"To formally give up a claim, belief, habit or position, or to reject it publicly.","lb":"give up, reject","s":["give up","abandon","relinquish","surrender","reject","forsake"],"k":["cede","discard","hand over","leave"],"a":["claim","adopt","embrace","retain"],"ex":["The prince chose to renounce his title and live as an ordinary citizen.","After the heart attack, he renounced smoking and began to walk every morning.","She renounced her claim to the family land so that her brothers would stop fighting."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"renovate","p":"verb","d":"To repair and improve an old building or room so that it looks new again.","lb":"restore, refurbish","s":["refurbish","restore","modernize","revamp","refit","overhaul"],"k":["animate","freshen up","reanimate","recreate"],"a":["demolish","neglect","ruin","wreck"],"ex":["We plan to renovate the kitchen before our relatives arrive for Eid.","The city council will renovate the old railway station and keep its original design.","He saved for years to buy and renovate a small house near the river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reparation","p":"noun","d":"Money or help given to make up for a wrong or damage that someone has suffered.","lb":"compensation, amends","s":["compensation","restitution","redress","amends","damages","indemnity"],"k":["fixing","fixture","indemnification","penance"],"a":[],"ex":["The factory owner agreed to make reparation to the villagers whose fields were polluted.","After breaking the neighbor's window, Rafi offered to wash their car as reparation.","Victims of the data leak demanded reparations from the company that lost their information."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"repartee","p":"noun","d":"Quick, clever and amusing conversation, especially when people answer each other with witty remarks.","lb":"witty reply, banter","s":["banter","badinage","wit","wordplay","retort","riposte"],"k":["comeback","crosstalk","humor","jousting"],"a":[],"ex":["The two hosts are famous for their quick repartee, which keeps the radio show lively.","Dinner at my aunt's house is always full of laughter and playful repartee between the cousins.","She enjoys the friendly repartee at the tea stall, where the regulars tease each other every evening."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"repercussion","p":"noun","d":"An indirect, usually unwelcome result of an action or event that happens later.","lb":"consequence, aftereffect","s":["consequence","aftereffect","ripple effect","result","backlash","fallout"],"k":["effect","event","issue","outcome"],"a":["cause","origin","source"],"ex":["Skipping the medicine could have serious repercussions for your health.","The sudden strike had repercussions across the city, as buses stopped and shops closed.","Think about the repercussions before you post angry comments online."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"replenish","p":"verb","d":"To fill something up again after it has been used or emptied.","lb":"refill, restock","s":["refill","restock","replace","restore","top up","refresh"],"k":["change","fill","fill again","fill up"],"a":["deplete","drain","empty","exhaust"],"ex":["The shop will replenish its shelves with fresh vegetables early tomorrow morning.","After the long walk, I drank water to replenish my energy.","Farmers need the monsoon to replenish water in the ponds and wells."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"replete","p":"adjective","d":"Filled with a large amount of something; well supplied.","lb":"full, abounding","s":["full","filled","abounding","rich","brimming","teeming"],"k":["awash","crowded","glutted","gorged"],"a":["empty","devoid","lacking","bare"],"ex":["The old market is replete with the smell of spices and the sound of bargaining.","Her essay was replete with examples, so the teacher gave her full marks.","The hotel garden was replete with roses of every color."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"replicate","p":"verb","d":"To make an exact copy of something, or to repeat it in exactly the same way.","lb":"copy, duplicate","s":["copy","duplicate","reproduce","clone","imitate","mirror"],"k":["ape","double","emulate","facsimile"],"a":["originate","invent","create"],"ex":["Other laboratories tried to replicate the experiment but got very different results.","The tailor replicated the old shirt so perfectly that nobody could tell the two apart.","The restaurant chain replicates the same menu and decor in every city."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"repose","p":"noun","d":"A state of rest, sleep or calm, free from worry or activity.","lb":"rest, calm","s":["rest","relaxation","calm","tranquility","peace","stillness"],"k":["composure","dozing","inactivity","leisure"],"a":["activity","agitation","turmoil","unrest"],"ex":["After exam week, she enjoyed a few days of quiet repose at her grandparents' home.","His face in repose looked serious, but it changed whenever he smiled.","The lake lay in perfect repose, without a single ripple, in the early morning."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"reprehensible","p":"adjective","d":"Deserving strong criticism or blame because it is very bad or wrong.","lb":"blameworthy, shameful","s":["disgraceful","shameful","deplorable","despicable","contemptible","culpable"],"k":["appalling","black","dishonorable","ignominious"],"a":["praiseworthy","admirable","commendable","laudable"],"ex":["Bullying a classmate for his accent is reprehensible and should never be accepted.","The shop owner's reprehensible behavior included selling spoiled food to poor families.","It is reprehensible to take credit for a colleague's hard work."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"repress","p":"verb","d":"To hold back a feeling, thought or desire so that it is not expressed or even noticed.","lb":"suppress, bottle up","s":["suppress","restrain","hold back","stifle","bottle up","inhibit"],"k":["clamp down on","contain","control","crush"],"a":["express","release","vent","indulge"],"ex":["He tried to repress his anger when the waiter forgot his order again.","Many people repress painful memories rather than face them.","She could not repress a smile when she saw her surprise gift."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"reprimand","p":"noun","d":"A formal or serious expression of strong disapproval, given to someone who has done wrong.","lb":"rebuke, scolding","s":["rebuke","scolding","censure","admonition","lecture","criticism"],"k":["carpeting","caution","disapproval","dressing-down"],"a":["praise","commendation","compliment","approval"],"ex":["The manager gave the late employee a formal reprimand.","She received a written reprimand for sharing confidential information.","The teacher's reprimand was short but clear: no phones during lessons."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"reprisal","p":"noun","d":"An act of harming or punishing someone in return for something they have done to you.","lb":"retaliation, revenge","s":["retaliation","revenge","retribution","vengeance","payback","counterattack"],"k":["backlash","counterblow","counterreaction","counterstrike"],"a":["forgiveness","pardon","mercy","amnesty"],"ex":["Workers were afraid to report the unsafe machines because they feared reprisals from the owner.","The company promised that no employee would face reprisal for reporting the problem.","Her brother hid her charger in reprisal for being teased about his haircut."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"reproach","p":"noun","d":"Words or looks that show disappointment or disapproval at something a person has done.","lb":"rebuke, blame","s":["rebuke","criticism","censure","blame","reprimand","disapproval"],"k":["condemnation","dishonor","disparagement","ignominy"],"a":["praise","commendation","approval","compliment"],"ex":["Her honesty is beyond reproach, so nobody ever questioned the accounts she prepared.","The little girl gave the puppy a look of reproach for chewing her new shoe.","\"You promised to call me,\" she said, with a note of reproach in her voice."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"reprobate","p":"noun","d":"A person with bad morals who shows no shame about the wrong things they do.","lb":"scoundrel, rogue","s":["scoundrel","rogue","wretch","miscreant","rascal","degenerate"],"k":["black sheep","knave","libertine","lowlife"],"a":["saint","paragon","model citizen","good person"],"ex":["The neighbors called him a reprobate because he cheated at cards and never repaid a loan.","My uncle jokes that he was a reprobate in his youth, always skipping school.","The shopkeeper chased the young reprobate who had been stealing mangoes from his stall."],"b":45,"y":0},{"w":"reprove","p":"verb","d":"To criticize someone gently for something they have done wrong.","lb":"scold, rebuke","s":["scold","rebuke","reprimand","admonish","chide","censure"],"k":["bawl out","berate","call down","call on the carpet"],"a":["praise","commend","compliment","applaud"],"ex":["The teacher gently reproved the boy for speaking while his classmate was presenting.","My grandmother reproved us for leaving our shoes in the doorway.","She reproved her little brother for texting at the dinner table."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"repudiate","p":"verb","d":"To reject something firmly, such as a claim, agreement or relationship, and refuse to accept it as valid.","lb":"reject, disown","s":["reject","disown","disavow","renounce","deny","spurn"],"k":["abjure","disclaim","rebuff","refuse"],"a":["accept","acknowledge","embrace","endorse"],"ex":["The company repudiated the rumor that it planned to close the factory.","He repudiated the contract, saying that his signature had been forged.","Club leaders publicly repudiated the rude behavior of a few fans after the match."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"repugnant","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely unpleasant or offensive, so that you feel disgust or strong dislike.","lb":"disgusting, offensive","s":["disgusting","repulsive","revolting","offensive","repellent","vile"],"k":["detestable","foul","nasty","nauseating"],"a":["pleasant","attractive","appealing","agreeable"],"ex":["The idea of cheating in the exam was repugnant to her.","The smell of the rotting garbage was so repugnant that I held my nose.","He found the manager's rude behavior toward waiters repugnant."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"repulsive","p":"adjective","d":"Causing a strong feeling of disgust; extremely unpleasant.","lb":"disgusting, revolting","s":["disgusting","revolting","repellent","vile","nauseating","loathsome"],"k":["abhorrent","detestable","distasteful","hideous"],"a":["attractive","appealing","pleasant","delightful"],"ex":["The repulsive smell from the rubbish heap made everyone cover their noses.","I found the idea of eating insects repulsive, but my friend said they were tasty.","The milk had gone bad and tasted repulsive."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"requisite","p":"adjective","d":"Needed for a particular purpose; required by rules or circumstances.","lb":"necessary, required","s":["required","necessary","essential","needed","compulsory","mandatory"],"k":["called-for","crucial","fundamental","imperative"],"a":["unnecessary","optional","needless","superfluous"],"ex":["She has the requisite experience for the job, so the company invited her to interview.","You must submit all the requisite documents before the admission deadline.","The candidate won the requisite number of votes to become class representative."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rescind","p":"verb","d":"To officially cancel a law, order, decision or agreement so that it no longer applies.","lb":"cancel, revoke","s":["revoke","cancel","repeal","annul","withdraw","overturn"],"k":["countermand","lift","nullify","strike down"],"a":["enact","approve","enforce","impose"],"ex":["The university rescinded its decision to raise fees after students held a peaceful protest.","The company rescinded the job offer when it found that the degree certificate was fake.","The city council rescinded the parking ban after shopkeepers complained of falling sales."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"resident","p":"noun","d":"A person who lives in a particular place, such as a town, building or country.","lb":"inhabitant, dweller","s":["inhabitant","dweller","occupant","local","citizen","householder"],"k":["house physician","indigene","lodger","native"],"a":["visitor","tourist","stranger","outsider"],"ex":["Every resident of the building must pay a small fee for the lift.","Local residents complained about the noise from loudspeakers late at night.","As a resident of Chittagong for ten years, he knows every shortcut in the city."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"resignation","p":"noun","d":"Calm acceptance of something bad that you cannot change, without protesting.","lb":"acceptance, submission","s":["acceptance","submission","acquiescence","passivity","patience","stoicism"],"k":["despair","equanimity","forbearance","fortitude"],"a":["protest","resistance","defiance","rebellion"],"ex":["He shrugged with resignation when the bus broke down for the third time that week.","She read the exam result with quiet resignation and went to make tea.","A look of resignation crossed his face as the rain started again."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"resist","p":"verb","d":"To refuse to give in to something, or to fight against it.","lb":"oppose, withstand","s":["withstand","oppose","fight","defy","stand up to","hold out against"],"k":["balk","defend","dissent","fend"],"a":["give in","yield","surrender","succumb"],"ex":["I could not resist buying a hot jalebi from the street stall.","Some workers resist change because they fear losing their jobs.","Vaccines help the body resist disease."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"resolute","p":"adjective","d":"Having a firm purpose and refusing to change one's mind or give up, even when things are difficult.","lb":"determined, firm","s":["determined","firm","steadfast","unwavering","resolved","staunch"],"k":["bent on","brave","committed","constant"],"a":["irresolute","hesitant","wavering","indecisive"],"ex":["Despite two failed attempts, Nadia remained resolute and applied for the scholarship a third time.","The coach was resolute in his decision to drop the star player for missing practice.","My grandmother is resolute about walking to the market every morning, even in heavy rain."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"resolution","p":"noun","d":"A firm decision to do or not do something, or the determination to carry it out.","lb":"determination, decision","s":["determination","resolve","decision","commitment","willpower","firmness"],"k":["answer","backbone","closure","declaration"],"a":["indecision","hesitation","wavering"],"ex":["My New Year's resolution is to walk for thirty minutes every morning before work.","She kept her resolution to save one thousand taka every month, despite many temptations.","He showed great resolution in finishing the race after twisting his ankle."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"resolve","p":"verb","d":"To find a solution to a problem, or to settle a disagreement or difficulty successfully.","lb":"solve, settle","s":["solve","settle","fix","sort out","clear up","work out"],"k":["adjudicate","break up","conclude","decide"],"a":["worsen","complicate","aggravate","escalate"],"ex":["The technician resolved the Wi-Fi problem by simply restarting the router.","The two neighbors finally resolved their dispute over the shared wall.","We need to resolve this billing error before the end of the month."],"b":387,"y":0},{"w":"resonate","p":"verb","d":"To have a special meaning or importance for someone, so that they strongly agree with it or feel connected to it.","lb":"connect, strike a chord","s":["strike a chord","connect","appeal","ring true","register","echo"],"k":["chime","come across","go","hit home"],"a":["alienate","bore","repel","fall flat"],"ex":["The poet's words about home resonated with students who had left their villages.","Her speech about hard work resonated with the young audience.","The film's story of a struggling family resonated with viewers across the country."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"respite","p":"noun","d":"A short break from something difficult or unpleasant, giving you time to rest.","lb":"break, relief","s":["break","rest","relief","breather","lull","pause"],"k":["cessation","comfort","halt","hiatus"],"a":["continuation","onslaught"],"ex":["A cool breeze gave the commuters a short respite from the afternoon heat.","The hospital garden offers patients' families a quiet respite from the stress of the wards.","After weeks of rain, the sunny weekend was a welcome respite for the farmers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"resplendent","p":"adjective","d":"Bright, rich and impressive to look at, often because of beautiful colours or decorations.","lb":"splendid, dazzling","s":["splendid","dazzling","radiant","glittering","gorgeous","magnificent"],"k":["beautiful","bejeweled","bright","excellent"],"a":["drab","dull","plain","shabby"],"ex":["The bride looked resplendent in a red silk sari and gold jewellery.","The old palace was resplendent with lights during the festival.","The peacock spread its resplendent tail feathers for the visitors."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"respondent","p":"noun","d":"A person who answers questions, especially in a survey, poll or questionnaire.","lb":"answerer, participant","s":["interviewee","participant","informant","survey participant","subject"],"k":["communicator","contributor","defendant","focus group member"],"a":["interviewer"],"ex":["Over sixty percent of respondents said they preferred studying at night.","Each respondent was asked to rate the new bus service from one to five.","The survey did not record the name or address of any respondent."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"resurrection","p":"noun","d":"The act of coming back to life after death, or the return of something that had faded or ended.","lb":"revival, rebirth","s":["revival","rebirth","renewal","comeback","resurgence","restoration"],"k":["reanimation","reappearance","reemergence","reincarnation"],"a":["death","decline","demise","collapse"],"ex":["The old song's resurrection on social media made it popular with teenagers again.","Many people called the team's win a resurrection of the club after ten poor seasons.","The mayor's plan promises the resurrection of the neglected riverfront."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"reticent","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to speak freely about your thoughts or feelings, and tending to stay quiet.","lb":"reserved, quiet","s":["reserved","uncommunicative","taciturn","guarded","silent","restrained"],"k":["buttoned-up","circumspect","close-mouthed","discreet"],"a":["talkative","outspoken","forthcoming","communicative"],"ex":["Rafi is reticent about his marks, so his friends never know how well he did.","The doctor was reticent about the patient's condition until the family arrived.","She was a reticent child who rarely spoke unless the teacher asked her a direct question."],"b":83,"y":3},{"w":"retort","p":"verb","d":"To answer quickly and sharply, often in anger or with wit, to something someone has said.","lb":"reply, snap","s":["reply","respond","answer","rejoin","snap","counter"],"k":["bite back","come back","fire back","react"],"a":[],"ex":["When I called him lazy, he retorted that I had never helped at home either.","“That's not my fault,” she retorted, folding her arms.","The customer retorted that the shop should have checked the price tag before printing it."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"retreat","p":"verb","d":"To move back or away, especially to escape danger or avoid a fight.","lb":"withdraw, go back","s":["withdraw","retire","fall back","back off","recoil","pull back"],"k":["back away","back out","bow out","crawfish"],"a":["advance","attack","approach","proceed"],"ex":["The floodwater began to rise, so we retreated to the roof.","The shy boy retreated behind his mother when the guests entered.","After the argument, Rafi retreated to his room and shut the door."],"b":64,"y":4},{"w":"retrospect","p":"noun","d":"A look back at past events, especially when you understand them better because time has passed.","lb":"hindsight, review","s":["hindsight","reflection","review","recollection","looking back","remembrance"],"k":["backward glance","contemplation","lookback","musing"],"a":["foresight","anticipation","prospect","forecast"],"ex":["In retrospect, I should have started studying for the exam a month earlier.","The trip looked like a disaster at the time, but in retrospect it was a great adventure.","In retrospect, buying the cheapest phone was a mistake because it broke within weeks."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"retrospective","p":"adjective","d":"Looking back at the past, or applying to something that happened in the past.","lb":"looking back, backward-looking","s":["retroactive","reflective","looking back","historical","ex post facto"],"k":["anthological","archival","backward","career-spanning"],"a":["prospective","anticipatory","future"],"ex":["The doctors carried out a retrospective study of patients treated over the last ten years.","Her retrospective view of her school days was full of laughter and small regrets.","The new rule has retrospective effect, so it applies to payments made last year too."],"b":66,"y":1},{"w":"revamp","p":"verb","d":"To change something substantially so that it looks or works better.","lb":"renovate, overhaul","s":["renovate","overhaul","redo","refurbish","remodel","rework"],"k":["reconstruct","regenerate","renew","restore"],"a":[],"ex":["The restaurant will revamp its menu this month to include more healthy options.","We plan to revamp the school website so that parents can find notices easily.","Nadia decided to revamp her room with a fresh coat of paint and new curtains."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"revealing","p":"adjective","d":"Showing or telling you something that was not obvious or was hidden before.","lb":"informative, telling","s":["telling","informative","illuminating","enlightening","significant","instructive"],"k":["candid","damning","exposing","frank"],"a":["concealing","misleading"],"ex":["The interview was revealing: it showed how hard the athlete had trained.","Her revealing answer told us she had never read the book.","A revealing report showed that most students sleep less than six hours."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"revel","p":"verb","d":"To enjoy something very much and take great pleasure in it.","lb":"delight, relish","s":["delight","relish","bask","savour","enjoy","thrive"],"k":["carouse","glory","indulge","make merry"],"a":["dislike","hate","shun","loathe"],"ex":["The children revelled in the cool rain after a long, hot week.","Nadia revelled in the silence of the library after weeks of noisy hostel life.","Football fans revelled in the victory, singing and dancing in the streets all night."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"revere","p":"verb","d":"To respect and admire someone or something very deeply.","lb":"respect, admire","s":["respect","admire","venerate","honor","worship","esteem"],"k":["deify","enshrine","exalt","glorify"],"a":["despise","scorn","disrespect","disdain"],"ex":["Students revere their old teacher, who still remembers every pupil's name.","The poet is revered across the country, and children learn his songs in school.","My grandmother is revered by the whole village for her wisdom and kindness."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"reverence","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of deep respect and admiration for someone or something.","lb":"respect, awe","s":["respect","awe","admiration","homage","deference","esteem"],"k":["adulation","appreciation","emotion","fealty"],"a":["contempt","disrespect","irreverence","scorn"],"ex":["Students spoke of their old headmaster with great reverence.","She handled her grandmother's old book with reverence, turning each page gently.","The people hold the martyrs of the language movement in deep reverence."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"reverent","p":"adjective","d":"Showing or feeling very deep respect and admiration, often in a quiet and serious way.","lb":"respectful, worshipful","s":["respectful","deferential","awed","devout","worshipful","solemn"],"k":["adoring","awful","devoted","godly"],"a":["irreverent","disrespectful","mocking","flippant"],"ex":["The crowd fell into a reverent silence as the national anthem began.","The young cricketers listened with reverent attention as the retired captain described his career.","She spoke of her late teacher in a soft, reverent tone."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"revile","p":"verb","d":"To criticize someone angrily and with hatred, using insulting words.","lb":"denounce, vilify","s":["denounce","condemn","vilify","abuse","attack","berate"],"k":["blackguard","castigate","criticize","decry"],"a":["praise","admire","honor","laud"],"ex":["Online users reviled the company for ignoring complaints about its broken product.","The coach was reviled by fans after the team lost five matches in a row.","She was reviled for speaking the truth, though later people admitted she was right."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"revival","p":"noun","d":"The act of bringing something back into use, life or popularity after a period when it had faded.","lb":"comeback, resurgence","s":["resurgence","comeback","renewal","rebirth","resurrection","restoration"],"k":["betterment","improvement","rediscovery","reemergence"],"a":["decline","decay","death","fading"],"ex":["The old folk songs are enjoying a revival among young musicians.","A revival of interest in handloom cloth has helped many weavers in the village.","The city is trying to bring about an economic revival by opening new markets."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"revulsion","p":"noun","d":"A strong feeling of disgust, horror or hatred towards something.","lb":"disgust, loathing","s":["disgust","loathing","repugnance","abhorrence","revolt","aversion"],"k":["abomination","antipathy","detestation","dislike"],"a":["attraction","liking","admiration","fondness"],"ex":["She felt revulsion when she saw the dirty kitchen of the restaurant.","Many people reacted with revulsion to the news of the animal cruelty case.","He turned away in revulsion from the rotten fish at the market."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rhapsodize","p":"verb","d":"To speak or write about something with great excitement and enthusiasm.","lb":"gush, enthuse","s":["gush","rave","wax lyrical","extol","praise","marvel"],"k":["carry on about","eulogize","go on about","hymn"],"a":["criticize","disparage","belittle"],"ex":["Tourists rhapsodized about the sunrise over the mountains.","My aunt rhapsodizes about her village mangoes every summer.","The reviewer rhapsodized over the film's music for half a page."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rhetoric","p":"noun","d":"Speech or writing meant to persuade or impress, often with more style than real meaning.","lb":"persuasive speech, bombast","s":["eloquence","oratory","persuasion","bombast","hot air","spin"],"k":["empty talk","empty words","expressive style","palaver"],"a":[],"ex":["The speech was full of fine rhetoric but offered no real plan for fixing the roads.","Advertisers use emotional rhetoric to make ordinary products sound life-changing.","Her skill in rhetoric helped her win the inter-university debate competition."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"ribald","p":"adjective","d":"Rude and vulgar in a joking way, often not suitable for polite company.","lb":"vulgar, bawdy","s":["vulgar","bawdy","crude","coarse","indecent","earthy"],"k":["common","dirty","plebeian","rough"],"a":["clean","decent","proper","polite"],"ex":["The comedian was told to avoid ribald jokes because the audience included many families.","Some of the old songs were too ribald to be played on the radio.","The teacher gently scolded the boys for their ribald laughter in the corridor."],"b":44,"y":0},{"w":"riddle","p":"noun","d":"A puzzling question or statement with a clever or hidden answer, asked for fun.","lb":"puzzle, brain-teaser","s":["puzzle","conundrum","enigma","poser","mystery","teaser"],"k":["acrostic","charade","cryptogram","paradox"],"a":[],"ex":["Grandfather asked us a riddle about a river that has no water.","Can you solve this riddle before the bell rings?","The children laughed as they tried to guess the answer to the riddle."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ridicule","p":"verb","d":"To laugh at someone or something in an unkind way, in order to make them look foolish.","lb":"mock, make fun of","s":["mock","deride","taunt","tease","scoff at","sneer at"],"k":["bait","blackguard","caricature","jest at"],"a":["praise","respect","admire","honor"],"ex":["Classmates ridiculed him for his accent until the teacher stepped in.","The critics ridiculed the film's silly plot in their reviews.","Nobody should be ridiculed for asking a question in class."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ridiculous","p":"adjective","d":"So silly or unreasonable that it makes people laugh or feel annoyed.","lb":"absurd, silly","s":["absurd","silly","ludicrous","foolish","laughable","preposterous"],"k":["cockeyed","comical","humorous","idiotic"],"a":["sensible","reasonable","serious","sound"],"ex":["It is ridiculous to charge five hundred taka for a cup of tea.","He wore a ridiculous hat with feathers to the school fair, and everyone laughed.","Her excuse that the dog ate her phone was ridiculous."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"rife","p":"adjective","d":"Very common or widespread, especially something bad or unwelcome; full of something.","lb":"widespread, abundant","s":["widespread","common","rampant","prevalent","pervasive","abundant"],"k":["dominant","extensive","general","predominant"],"a":["rare","scarce","uncommon","isolated"],"ex":["Rumors were rife on campus after the exam date suddenly changed.","The old report is rife with spelling mistakes and wrong figures.","Mosquito-borne diseases are rife in the city during the rainy season."],"b":98,"y":1},{"w":"rigorous","p":"adjective","d":"Very strict, thorough and exact, with no room for mistakes or shortcuts.","lb":"strict, thorough","s":["strict","thorough","exacting","meticulous","stringent","demanding"],"k":["conscientious","exact","harsh","painstaking"],"a":["lax","lenient","careless","sloppy"],"ex":["The vaccine went through rigorous testing before doctors were allowed to use it.","Our coach has a rigorous training plan that starts at five in the morning.","Admission to the medical college requires rigorous preparation over many months."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"rivalry","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which two people or groups compete with each other for the same thing.","lb":"competition, contest","s":["competition","contest","opposition","contention","struggle","feud"],"k":["game","group action","match","race"],"a":["cooperation","partnership","friendship","alliance"],"ex":["There is a friendly rivalry between the two schools in the annual quiz contest.","The rivalry between the two bus companies on this route has lowered the fares.","Business rivalry made the two shopkeepers cut their prices every week."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"rivet","p":"verb","d":"To hold someone's attention completely, so that they cannot look away.","lb":"engross, captivate","s":["absorb","captivate","fascinate","grip","hypnotize","engage"],"k":["arrest","bewitch","center","charm"],"a":["bore","distract","repel","tire"],"ex":["The children were riveted to the screen during the final over of the match.","The storyteller's voice riveted the whole village on a dark night.","A shocking news report riveted viewers across the country."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"roar","p":"verb","d":"To make a very loud, deep sound.","lb":"bellow, thunder","s":["bellow","thunder","boom","bawl","howl","rumble"],"k":["bluster","call","clamor","cry"],"a":["whisper","murmur","hush"],"ex":["The lion roared, and the children stepped back from the cage.","The crowd roared with joy when the home team scored a goal.","A motorbike roared down the narrow street at midnight."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"robust","p":"adjective","d":"Strong, healthy and able to withstand difficulties or pressure.","lb":"strong, sturdy","s":["strong","sturdy","vigorous","healthy","tough","hardy"],"k":["beefy","burly","chesty","forceful"],"a":["weak","frail","fragile","feeble"],"ex":["After a week of rest, the baby looked robust and healthy again.","The new bridge has a robust design that can survive floods and storms.","A robust economy creates more jobs for young graduates."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rogue","p":"noun","d":"A dishonest person who cannot be trusted, especially someone who cheats others for gain.","lb":"scoundrel, cheat","s":["scoundrel","rascal","villain","crook","cheat","swindler"],"k":["blackguard","bounder","charlatan","con artist"],"a":["honest person","saint","gentleman"],"ex":["The rogue sold fake mobile phones at half price and disappeared before anyone could complain.","My grandfather described the local trader as a rogue who cheated farmers with false scales.","In the story, the charming rogue steals from the rich, but he is secretly kind."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"rookie","p":"noun","d":"A person who is new to a job or sport and has little experience.","lb":"beginner, newcomer","s":["beginner","novice","newcomer","trainee","greenhorn","newbie"],"k":["colt","cub","fledgling","learner"],"a":["veteran","expert","professional","old hand"],"ex":["The rookie bowler took three wickets in his very first match.","As a rookie at the bank, Sadia asked many questions and wrote down every answer.","Forgetting to save the file was a rookie mistake that cost me an hour of work."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"roundabout","p":"adjective","d":"Not direct; taking a longer way than necessary to get somewhere or to say something.","lb":"indirect, circuitous","s":["indirect","circuitous","winding","meandering","tortuous","devious"],"k":["circumlocutory","digressive","evasive","periphrastic"],"a":["direct","straight","straightforward","short"],"ex":["We took a roundabout route to avoid the traffic near the stadium.","He asked for a loan in such a roundabout way that I almost missed the point.","The bus follows a roundabout path through three villages before reaching the town."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"rout","p":"verb","d":"To defeat an opponent completely and easily.","lb":"defeat, crush","s":["defeat","crush","thrash","beat","overwhelm","trounce"],"k":["annihilate","beat out","clobber","conquer"],"a":["lose to","surrender to","yield to"],"ex":["Our school's team routed their rivals 7-0 in the final.","The champion chess player routed his younger opponent in just eighteen moves.","The army routed the invading force and chased it back across the border."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"rudimentary","p":"adjective","d":"Basic or simple, and not yet fully developed.","lb":"basic, undeveloped","s":["basic","elementary","primitive","crude","simple","undeveloped"],"k":["bare-bones","easy","essential","incomplete"],"a":["advanced","sophisticated","developed","complex"],"ex":["I have only a rudimentary knowledge of French, enough to order a meal.","The farmers used rudimentary tools made from wood and bamboo.","The village clinic had rudimentary equipment, but the nurses did their best."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"rue","p":"verb","d":"To feel sorry or regret deeply about something you have done or that has happened.","lb":"regret, lament","s":["regret","lament","repent","deplore","mourn","bemoan"],"k":["be contrite","despair","feel","pine"],"a":["welcome","celebrate","rejoice","relish"],"ex":["He will rue the day he ignored his teacher's advice and skipped the revision classes.","Many people rue not saving money when they were young.","I still rue my decision to sell my old bicycle for such a low price."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"ruination","p":"noun","d":"Complete destruction or ruin, or the cause of it.","lb":"destruction, downfall","s":["ruin","destruction","devastation","downfall","undoing","collapse"],"k":["calamity","catastrophe","debacle","havoc"],"a":["restoration","salvation","rebuilding","recovery"],"ex":["The flood caused the ruination of the farmers' entire winter crop.","Gambling brought ruination to his family's finances.","Heavy investment in a failing shop led to the ruination of his savings."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"rumble","p":"noun","d":"A deep, heavy, continuous sound, like distant thunder or a large vehicle.","lb":"low rolling sound","s":["roll","boom","thunder","growl","drone","murmur"],"k":["clatter","grumble","hum","rattle"],"a":["silence","hush"],"ex":["We heard the rumble of thunder long before the rain arrived.","The rumble of trucks on the highway kept me awake all night.","A low rumble from the train shook the cups on the table."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ruminate","p":"verb","d":"To think deeply and for a long time about something.","lb":"ponder, reflect","s":["ponder","reflect","meditate","muse","brood","contemplate"],"k":["chew over","cogitate","consider","mull"],"a":["disregard","ignore","dismiss"],"ex":["She sat by the window and ruminated on whether to accept the job in another city.","I ruminated over the exam question for ten minutes before writing a single word.","He ruminated about his friend's harsh words all night and could not sleep."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"rush","p":"verb","d":"To move or do something very quickly, often because there is little time.","lb":"hurry, dash","s":["hurry","dash","race","hasten","speed","run"],"k":["accelerate","belt along","bucket along","cannonball along"],"a":["dawdle","linger","stroll","crawl"],"ex":["I rushed to the station, but the train had already left.","Don't rush your answers in the exam; read every question twice.","Parents rushed to the school gate when they heard the fire bell."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"rustic","p":"adjective","d":"Typical of country life; simple, plain and often rough in a charming way.","lb":"rural, simple","s":["rural","country","pastoral","simple","plain","homely"],"k":["agrarian","agrestic","bucolic","hick"],"a":["urban","sophisticated","elegant","polished"],"ex":["We stayed in a rustic cottage with a tin roof and a small pond.","The restaurant serves rustic food cooked on a clay stove.","Her rustic charm made the guests ask about her village."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"saccharine","p":"adjective","d":"Too sweet, or too sentimental in a way that seems insincere.","lb":"overly sweet","s":["sugary","cloying","sentimental","mawkish","sickly"],"k":["gushy","hokey","icky","maudlin"],"a":["bitter","sour","tart","unsentimental"],"ex":["The tea was so saccharine that I could barely finish half a cup.","Critics found the film's ending saccharine, with everyone hugging and crying at once.","The salesman gave me a saccharine smile that did not look sincere."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sacrilege","p":"noun","d":"A disrespectful act toward something that people consider holy or deeply valued.","lb":"desecration, blasphemy","s":["desecration","blasphemy","irreverence","violation","outrage","disrespect"],"k":["affront","iconoclasm","offense against faith","profanity"],"a":["reverence","respect","piety","devotion"],"ex":["Painting graffiti on an old temple wall is considered an act of sacrilege.","Many cricket fans think criticizing a retired legend is sacrilege.","To my uncle, putting ketchup on biryani is nothing short of sacrilege."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"sacrosanct","p":"adjective","d":"Too important or respected to be changed, criticized or interfered with.","lb":"inviolable, untouchable","s":["sacred","untouchable","hallowed","unassailable","protected","revered"],"k":["above reproach","beyond criticism","consecrated","holy"],"a":["profane","expendable","negotiable"],"ex":["In our family, Friday lunch together is sacrosanct, and nobody makes other plans.","The editor treats the deadline as sacrosanct and never accepts late articles.","Privacy should be sacrosanct, so a bank must never share your account details."],"b":82,"y":1},{"w":"sadden","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel unhappy or sorrowful.","lb":"upset, depress","s":["upset","depress","grieve","distress","dismay","hurt"],"k":["affect","cloud","dampen","discourage"],"a":["cheer","delight","please","comfort"],"ex":["It saddens me to see my old school building in such bad condition.","The news of her friend's departure saddened her for days.","We were saddened to hear that the old tea seller had closed his stall for good."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sagacious","p":"adjective","d":"Wise and shrewd, with good judgment gained from experience.","lb":"wise, shrewd","s":["wise","shrewd","discerning","astute","perceptive","judicious"],"k":["canny","discriminating","far-sighted","keen"],"a":["foolish","unwise","stupid","naive"],"ex":["The sagacious shopkeeper noticed the fake note before the customer left the counter.","A sagacious investor studies a company carefully before buying its shares.","My grandfather gave sagacious advice: save first, spend later."],"b":90,"y":2},{"w":"sage","p":"noun","d":"A person who is respected for their wisdom, experience and good judgment.","lb":"wise person, elder","s":["wise man","elder","guru","mentor","philosopher","thinker"],"k":["doyen","elder statesman","luminary","pundit"],"a":["fool","simpleton","ignoramus","dunce"],"ex":["The villagers often visited the old sage to ask for advice about their problems.","In many stories, a wise sage appears to guide the young hero.","My grandfather is the sage of our family, and everyone consults him before big decisions."],"b":65,"y":1},{"w":"salient","p":"adjective","d":"Most noticeable or important; standing out from other things.","lb":"prominent, notable","s":["prominent","conspicuous","noticeable","striking","important","key"],"k":["evident","inclined","marked","obvious"],"a":["minor","unimportant","insignificant","inconspicuous"],"ex":["The teacher asked us to list the salient points of the chapter before the test.","The most salient feature of the new phone is its battery life.","Journalists reported the salient facts of the accident and left out the rumors."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"sally","p":"noun","d":"A sudden attack or rush forward, or a short trip out somewhere.","lb":"sortie, outing","s":["sortie","foray","charge","rush","outing","excursion"],"k":["action","assault","expedition","incursion"],"a":["retreat","withdrawal","retirement"],"ex":["The defenders made a sudden sally from the gate and then withdrew.","The team's early sally into the opponents' half surprised everyone.","We made a quick sally to the shop before the rain started."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"salubrious","p":"adjective","d":"Good for your health, especially when describing a place, climate, food or habit.","lb":"healthy, wholesome","s":["healthy","healthful","wholesome","beneficial","invigorating","bracing"],"k":["curative","good for you","hale","restorative"],"a":["unhealthy","unwholesome","harmful","noxious"],"ex":["Doctors recommended the salubrious mountain air to help him recover from his chest infection.","A salubrious diet of vegetables, lentils and fish keeps the whole family strong.","The hostel stood in a less than salubrious part of town, close to an open drain."],"b":11,"y":0},{"w":"salutary","p":"adjective","d":"Having a good, healthy effect, often by teaching a lesson even when the experience is unpleasant.","lb":"beneficial, healthy","s":["beneficial","healthy","helpful","useful","wholesome","advantageous"],"k":["bracing","cautionary","chastening","edifying"],"a":["harmful","damaging","unhealthy","detrimental"],"ex":["Failing the first quiz was a salutary lesson, and Rafi began to study every day.","A short walk after dinner has a salutary effect on both body and mind.","The accident served as a salutary warning to everyone about crossing the road carelessly."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"salutation","p":"noun","d":"A greeting, or the opening words of a letter or email, such as Dear Sir.","lb":"greeting, welcome","s":["greeting","hello","welcome","address","salute","acknowledgement"],"k":["acknowledgment","dear madam","dear sir","heading"],"a":["farewell","goodbye","valediction","parting"],"ex":["The salutation in a formal letter is usually Dear Sir or Madam.","He raised his hand in friendly salutation as he passed the tea stall.","She began the email with a polite salutation and then explained her request."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"sanctimonious","p":"adjective","d":"Pretending to be more moral or religious than other people, in a way that is annoying.","lb":"self-righteous, preachy","s":["pious","preachy","smug","hypocritical","moralizing","priggish"],"k":["pharisaical","pietistic","puritanical","sermonizing"],"a":["humble","modest","tolerant","genuine"],"ex":["Nobody likes a sanctimonious friend who lectures everyone about healthy eating while sneaking sweets.","His sanctimonious tone made the advice sound like an insult.","She gave a sanctimonious speech about honesty, yet she had copied her own essay."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sanction","p":"verb","d":"To give official permission or approval for something to be done.","lb":"approve, authorize","s":["approve","authorize","permit","allow","endorse","ratify"],"k":["accept","empower","enable","let"],"a":["forbid","prohibit","ban","veto"],"ex":["The manager sanctioned a week of paid leave so Nadia could attend her sister's wedding.","The university has not sanctioned the use of mobile phones inside the exam hall.","Only the city authority can sanction new buildings along this narrow road."],"b":107,"y":1},{"w":"sanguine","p":"adjective","d":"Cheerfully hopeful and confident about the future, especially in a difficult situation.","lb":"optimistic, hopeful","s":["optimistic","hopeful","confident","positive","cheerful","buoyant"],"k":["bright","certain","chirpy","ebullient"],"a":["pessimistic","gloomy","despondent","negative"],"ex":["Despite the late start, the coach was sanguine about his team's chances in the final.","She remains sanguine about finding a job, even though many companies are not hiring.","Farmers are sanguine about the harvest after a good season of rain."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"sarcasm","p":"noun","d":"Saying the opposite of what you mean in order to mock or hurt someone, often in a joking tone.","lb":"irony, mockery","s":["irony","mockery","derision","scorn","satire","ridicule"],"k":["acerbity","backhandedness","barbs","caustic wit"],"a":["sincerity","earnestness","candor"],"ex":["“Wonderful weather,” she said, her voice dripping with sarcasm, as rain soaked her bag.","My brother's sarcasm hurts my feelings, even when he says he is only joking.","Written sarcasm is easy to miss in text messages without a tone of voice."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"sarcastic","p":"adjective","d":"Saying the opposite of what you mean in order to mock or hurt someone.","lb":"mocking, cutting","s":["mocking","sardonic","ironic","scornful","cutting","caustic"],"k":["barbed","biting","black","corrosive"],"a":["sincere","earnest","genuine","kind"],"ex":["When I arrived an hour late, my friend gave a sarcastic reply: \"Great timing!\"","The comedian's sarcastic jokes made the audience laugh but upset a few people.","Don't be sarcastic with your teacher; ask politely if you do not understand."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sardonic","p":"adjective","d":"Mocking or scornful in a dry, cynical way.","lb":"mocking, cynical","s":["mocking","cynical","sarcastic","scornful","sneering","ironic"],"k":["acerbic","biting","bitter","disrespectful"],"a":["sincere","kind","friendly","warm"],"ex":["He gave a sardonic smile when the manager announced that the project would finish early.","Her sardonic comment about the cafeteria food made the whole table laugh.","The writer's sardonic style makes even sad news sound funny and a little cruel."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"satiate","p":"verb","d":"To satisfy a need or desire, especially hunger, completely, or to give someone more than enough.","lb":"satisfy, fill","s":["satisfy","sate","fill","quench","slake","gratify"],"k":["appease","consume","gorge","have"],"a":["starve","deprive","deny","leave wanting"],"ex":["A bowl of hot khichuri on a rainy day is enough to satiate even the hungriest child.","The documentary satiated her curiosity about how paper is made.","No amount of praise could satiate his hunger for attention."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"satiated","p":"adjective","d":"Completely full or satisfied, especially after eating as much as you want.","lb":"full, satisfied","s":["full","sated","replete","satisfied","stuffed","gorged"],"k":["bloated","brimming","fed up","filled"],"a":["hungry","starving","ravenous","famished"],"ex":["After the Eid feast, the guests felt satiated and lay down to rest.","A bowl of oats keeps me satiated until lunchtime.","The satiated cat curled up on the sofa and ignored the fish."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"satiric","p":"adjective","d":"Using humor and exaggeration to criticize people's faults or foolish behavior.","lb":"mocking, ironic","s":["satirical","mocking","ironic","sarcastic","biting","caustic"],"k":["burlesque","jesting","lampooning","parodic"],"a":["earnest","sincere","serious","straightforward"],"ex":["The newspaper's satiric cartoon showed the city's traffic jam as a giant car park with no exit.","Her satiric essay made fun of students who never read the assigned books.","The comedy show is satiric, mocking the silly habits of social media users."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"saturate","p":"verb","d":"To soak something completely with liquid, or to fill it so full that it cannot hold any more.","lb":"soak, drench","s":["soak","drench","douse","steep","permeate","imbue"],"k":["fill up","glut","impregnate","infuse"],"a":["dry","drain","dehydrate"],"ex":["Three days of monsoon rain saturated the soil, and the riverbank began to collapse.","Saturate the cloth with warm water and press it on the sore muscle for ten minutes.","The market is saturated with cheap phone covers, so new sellers struggle to find customers."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"saturnine","p":"adjective","d":"Gloomy, serious and unfriendly in mood; slow to laugh.","lb":"gloomy, glum","s":["gloomy","glum","morose","sullen","somber","dour"],"k":["dark","dejected","dim","dismal"],"a":["cheerful","jovial","sunny","lively"],"ex":["The saturnine old shopkeeper never smiled at his customers.","After the long meeting, his saturnine mood spread through the whole office.","With a saturnine face, my uncle sat in the corner and watched everyone dance."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"savant","p":"noun","d":"A very learned person, or someone with an amazing mental talent in one area.","lb":"scholar, genius","s":["scholar","sage","expert","intellectual","genius","authority"],"k":["bookman","connoisseur","guru","intellect"],"a":["ignoramus","dunce","simpleton","layman"],"ex":["The village elder was a local savant who could answer questions about history, farming and law.","The young math savant solved university-level problems before he turned twelve.","My professor is a savant of ancient languages and reads texts that nobody else can."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"savoir-faire","p":"noun","d":"The ability to know the right thing to do in social situations, and to do it smoothly.","lb":"social skill, tact","s":["tact","poise","finesse","social skill","diplomacy","sophistication"],"k":["aplomb","composure","decorum","sang-froid"],"a":["clumsiness","awkwardness","ineptitude"],"ex":["The new manager handled the angry customer with real savoir-faire.","She showed great savoir-faire when she calmly fixed the microphone problem during her speech.","With his easy savoir-faire, Rafi made friends within a day of joining the new school."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"savor","p":"verb","d":"To enjoy something slowly and fully, especially a taste, a smell or a pleasant moment.","lb":"relish, enjoy","s":["relish","enjoy","appreciate","delight in","treasure","revel in"],"k":["bask","bask in","dwell on","indulge in"],"a":["dislike","loathe","disdain","scorn"],"ex":["She sat by the window and savored every sip of her hot, sweet tea.","After weeks of hard work, the team savored its first win of the season.","Take your time and savor the view before the bus leaves for the hotel."],"b":11,"y":0},{"w":"scale","p":"noun","d":"A series of marks or numbers used to measure something, or a system for ranking things from low to high.","lb":"measure, ranking","s":["measure","ladder","range","gauge","ranking","hierarchy"],"k":["calibration","criterion","degree","dimension"],"a":[],"ex":["On a scale of one to ten, how would you rate the food?","The doctor asked me to describe my pain on a scale from one to five.","The earthquake measured six on the Richter scale, and buildings shook for a minute."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"scant","p":"adjective","d":"Hardly enough; very small in amount or degree.","lb":"meager, barely enough","s":["meager","limited","scarce","sparse","minimal","insufficient"],"k":["bare","deficient","lean","meagre"],"a":["ample","plentiful","abundant","generous"],"ex":["The company paid scant attention to customer complaints, and sales soon dropped.","There is scant evidence that the old story is true.","With scant time before the bus left, we ran to the station."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"scanty","p":"adjective","d":"Too small in amount to be enough.","lb":"meagre, insufficient","s":["meagre","sparse","insufficient","scant","skimpy","thin"],"k":["bare","deficient","lean","meager"],"a":["ample","plentiful","abundant","generous"],"ex":["Rainfall was scanty this year, so many farmers worried about their crops.","The police had only scanty evidence, so they could not charge anyone.","We had scanty information about the hotel before booking, and the room was a disappointment."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scarcely","p":"adverb","d":"Almost not at all; only just.","lb":"barely, hardly","s":["barely","hardly","just","only just","narrowly","faintly"],"k":["at a push","by the skin of one's teeth","just about","marginally"],"a":["easily","fully","completely","amply"],"ex":["I was so tired that I could scarcely keep my eyes open during the lecture.","There was scarcely any traffic on the road at five in the morning.","She had scarcely sat down to eat when the phone rang."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scarcity","p":"noun","d":"A situation in which there is not enough of something that people need or want.","lb":"shortage, lack","s":["shortage","lack","dearth","paucity","insufficiency","deficiency"],"k":["absence","deficit","drought","exiguity"],"a":["abundance","plenty","surplus","glut"],"ex":["The scarcity of clean drinking water forced villagers to walk two kilometres every day.","A scarcity of cooking gas led to long queues outside the shops.","Because of the scarcity of rooms, many students share a small flat near campus."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"scatter","p":"verb","d":"To throw things loosely over an area, or to make people or animals separate and move in different directions.","lb":"disperse, spread","s":["disperse","sprinkle","spread","sow","disband","fling"],"k":["break up","discharge","dispel","dissipate"],"a":["gather","collect","assemble","concentrate"],"ex":["The farmer scattered seeds across the freshly plowed field.","When the rain began, the cricket players scattered in every direction.","Please don't scatter your clothes all over the bedroom floor."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scheme","p":"noun","d":"A carefully organised plan or system for doing something, especially one run by an organisation.","lb":"plan, programme","s":["plan","programme","project","system","strategy","plot"],"k":["agenda","blueprint","dodging","program"],"a":[],"ex":["The bank introduced a new savings scheme for students with no monthly fee.","The village women joined a loan scheme to start small poultry farms.","The council announced a scheme to plant ten thousand trees along the main road."],"b":448,"y":1},{"w":"schism","p":"noun","d":"A serious split within a group or organization, caused by disagreement about beliefs or aims.","lb":"split, rift","s":["split","division","rift","break","breach","separation"],"k":["apostasy","divergence","estrangement","factionalism"],"a":["unity","union","harmony","agreement"],"ex":["A bitter schism over the club’s budget split the members into two rival groups.","The disagreement about the new curriculum caused a schism among the teachers.","A schism in the band led to its breakup, and the singer started a solo career."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"scintillate","p":"verb","d":"To sparkle or shine with quick flashes of light, or to be lively and brilliant.","lb":"sparkle, shine","s":["sparkle","glitter","twinkle","shimmer","flash","glisten"],"k":["bubble","coruscate","emit","fizz"],"a":["dim","fade","darken","dull"],"ex":["Stars scintillate in the clear winter sky far from the city lights.","Sunlight made the river scintillate as the boat moved slowly toward the far bank.","The comedian scintillated on stage, drawing laughter with every clever line."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"score","p":"noun","d":"A number or grade that shows how well someone has done in a test or game.","lb":"mark, points","s":["mark","grade","result","points","tally","rating"],"k":["account","assessment","evaluation","grievance"],"a":[],"ex":["Her IELTS score was high enough to apply to three universities abroad.","The final score of the match was 3-2, so the crowd went home happy.","He checked his test score online and jumped with joy."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"scorn","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone or something as unworthy of respect, or to refuse something because you think it is beneath you.","lb":"despise, disdain","s":["despise","disdain","deride","mock","sneer at","spurn"],"k":["belittle","decline","freeze off","lampoon"],"a":["respect","admire","esteem","welcome"],"ex":["Some people scorn street food, though it is often fresh and delicious.","He scorned his brother’s advice and made the same mistake again.","Classmates scorned him for wearing old clothes, but he ignored them."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"script","p":"noun","d":"The written text of a play, film or broadcast, with the words that the actors or speakers say.","lb":"screenplay, text","s":["screenplay","text","lines","dialogue","libretto","scenario"],"k":["book","dramatic composition","dramatic work","hand"],"a":[],"ex":["The actors received the final script a week before the play opened.","She wrote the script for a short film about a rickshaw puller.","The call-centre staff must follow a script when they speak to customers."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scrupulous","p":"adjective","d":"Very careful to do things correctly, honestly and fairly, paying attention to every detail.","lb":"careful, honest","s":["meticulous","careful","conscientious","principled","honest","painstaking"],"k":["diligent","ethical","exact","exacting"],"a":["unscrupulous","careless","dishonest","sloppy"],"ex":["The accountant is scrupulous about recording every taka, so her reports are always accurate.","Our landlord is scrupulous in returning the deposit and never charges hidden fees.","The kitchen staff are scrupulous about washing their hands before touching any food."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"scrutinize","p":"verb","d":"To examine something very carefully and closely, looking for mistakes or small details.","lb":"examine, inspect","s":["examine","inspect","study","analyze","investigate","check"],"k":["audit","canvass","comb through","dissect"],"a":["ignore","overlook","glance at","neglect"],"ex":["Before signing the rent agreement, scrutinize every clause for hidden charges.","The teacher scrutinized the two essays and noticed they were almost identical.","Customs officers scrutinized each passport before letting travelers through."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sculpture","p":"noun","d":"A three-dimensional work of art made by carving stone or wood, shaping clay or casting metal.","lb":"statue, carving","s":["statue","carving","figure","statuette","bust","figurine"],"k":["art","artistic creation","artistic production","bas-relief"],"a":[],"ex":["A huge stone sculpture stands in the middle of the university garden.","She spent three months carving a small wooden sculpture of a bird.","Tourists took photos beside the bronze sculpture of a fisherman near the beach."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scurry","p":"verb","d":"To run with short, quick steps, usually because of fear or hurry.","lb":"scamper, hurry","s":["scamper","scuttle","dash","hurry","dart","scoot"],"k":["hasten","run","rush","scud"],"a":["amble","stroll","saunter","dawdle"],"ex":["Mice scurried across the kitchen floor when I switched on the light.","Shoppers scurried for shelter when the sudden rain began.","The children scurried back to their seats as the teacher walked in."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"scuttle","p":"verb","d":"To run quickly with short, light steps, especially because you are afraid or in a hurry.","lb":"scurry, rush","s":["scurry","scamper","dash","dart","hurry","rush"],"k":["run","scoot","scud","shoot"],"a":["stroll","amble","saunter","dawdle"],"ex":["When I turned on the kitchen light, a cockroach scuttled under the fridge.","Crabs scuttled across the wet sand as the waves went out.","The students scuttled to their seats when they heard the principal's footsteps."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"seamless","p":"adjective","d":"Smooth and continuous, with no visible joins, breaks or problems.","lb":"smooth, uninterrupted","s":["smooth","continuous","uninterrupted","fluid","flawless","effortless"],"k":["ceaseless","coherent","cohesive","consistent"],"a":["disjointed","choppy","jerky","broken"],"ex":["The app offers a seamless way to switch from your phone to your laptop.","The handover from the old manager to the new one was seamless.","The pipe is seamless, so water cannot leak through any joint."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"secede","p":"verb","d":"To formally leave a group or organization, especially a country or an association.","lb":"withdraw, break away","s":["withdraw","break away","leave","separate","split","resign"],"k":["back out","break","break up","chip off"],"a":["join","unite","merge","stay"],"ex":["Two clubs seceded from the national association after a dispute over fees.","In the novel, a small island threatens to secede from the kingdom.","Several members seceded from the debating society and started a rival club."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"seclusion","p":"noun","d":"The state of being private and away from other people.","lb":"privacy, isolation","s":["isolation","solitude","privacy","retreat","withdrawal","remoteness"],"k":["asylum","cloister","hermitage","obscurity"],"a":["company","society","publicity","exposure"],"ex":["After the exams, she went to her village home to enjoy a week of seclusion.","The author lives in seclusion in a small cottage and rarely meets visitors.","The hotel's seclusion, far from the main road, made it ideal for a quiet weekend."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"secrete","p":"verb","d":"To produce and release a liquid or other substance from a cell, a gland or a plant.","lb":"release, produce","s":["release","discharge","emit","produce","exude","ooze"],"k":["bleed","generate","issue","leak"],"a":["absorb","retain","take in","soak up"],"ex":["The pancreas secretes insulin, which helps the body control the level of sugar in the blood.","Your mouth secretes more saliva when you smell fresh bread.","Some frogs secrete a sticky liquid through their skin to protect themselves from enemies."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"sect","p":"noun","d":"A group of people with shared beliefs that has separated from a larger religion or group.","lb":"denomination, faction","s":["denomination","faction","splinter group","offshoot","order","school"],"k":["brotherhood","cabal","clique","congregation"],"a":[],"ex":["The book describes a small sect that broke away from the main church in the 1800s.","Historians study how each sect developed its own customs and teachings.","The village was home to people of many faiths and sects, who lived side by side."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"secular","p":"adjective","d":"Not connected with religion or spiritual matters.","lb":"nonreligious, worldly","s":["worldly","lay","civil","temporal","earthly","profane"],"k":["economic","impious","materialistic","mundane"],"a":["religious","sacred","spiritual","holy"],"ex":["The school offers a secular education focused on science, languages and mathematics.","The festival includes both religious ceremonies and secular events such as concerts and fairs.","Many universities are secular institutions that welcome students of every background."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"sedentary","p":"adjective","d":"Spending a lot of time sitting down and doing very little physical activity.","lb":"inactive, desk-bound","s":["inactive","stationary","seated","lethargic","sluggish"],"k":["bookish","chair-bound","housebound","immobile"],"a":["active","energetic","mobile","athletic"],"ex":["A sedentary lifestyle can increase the risk of heart disease and back pain.","Office workers have a sedentary job, so doctors advise them to walk during breaks.","Many students become sedentary during exam season, studying for hours without any exercise."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"sedition","p":"noun","d":"Speech or action that encourages people to rebel against the government or lawful authority.","lb":"rebellion, incitement","s":["incitement","insurrection","rebellion","subversion","treason","mutiny"],"k":["agitprop","defiance","dissent","infraction"],"a":["loyalty","allegiance","obedience","order"],"ex":["In history class, we learned that writing against the colonial rulers was once punished as sedition.","Critics say the old law against sedition limits free speech.","Prosecutors charged the pamphlet's author with sedition, but the court later dismissed the case."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"seer","p":"noun","d":"A person who claims to see what will happen in the future, or who has unusual insight.","lb":"prophet, visionary","s":["prophet","visionary","oracle","clairvoyant","soothsayer","augur"],"k":["astrologer","diviner","haruspex","illusionist"],"a":[],"ex":["In the old story, a blind seer warns the king that his city will fall.","Some investors treat the famous analyst as a seer, though nobody can predict the market perfectly.","A village seer once looked at my aunt's palm and promised her a happy marriage."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"segregate","p":"verb","d":"To keep people or things apart from each other, or from the main group.","lb":"separate, isolate","s":["separate","isolate","divide","set apart","quarantine","partition"],"k":["bifurcate","break up","compartmentalize","cordon off"],"a":["integrate","unite","combine","mix"],"ex":["At home, we segregate wet kitchen waste from dry waste such as paper and plastic.","The hospital segregates patients with infectious diseases from other patients.","Teachers should not segregate students by marks and make weaker pupils feel left out."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"seldom","p":"adverb","d":"Not often; only a few times.","lb":"rarely","s":["rarely","hardly ever","infrequently","scarcely","occasionally","once in a blue moon"],"k":["barely","every so often","few and far between","not often"],"a":["often","frequently","regularly","usually"],"ex":["My grandfather seldom goes out after dark, because his eyesight is poor.","It seldom rains in Dhaka in January, so umbrellas are often forgotten.","She seldom eats fast food because she prefers home cooking."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"self-determination","p":"noun","d":"The ability or right of a person or people to make their own decisions and control their own future.","lb":"independence, free will","s":["independence","autonomy","free will","sovereignty","freedom","liberty"],"k":["devolution","emancipation","home rule","self-direction"],"a":["dependence","control","domination","oppression"],"ex":["Our history lesson explained how the idea of self-determination shaped many new countries.","Teenagers need some self-determination in choosing their own subjects.","The disability center encourages self-determination, so residents plan their own daily routines."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"self-made","p":"adjective","d":"Having become successful or rich through your own efforts, without help or advantages from others.","lb":"self-reliant, independent","s":["independent","enterprising","hardworking"],"k":["ambitious","bootstrapping","driven","go-getting"],"a":["inherited","privileged","born rich","dependent"],"ex":["Our uncle is a self-made businessman who started with a single rickshaw and now owns a garage.","She is a self-made success who paid for her own degree by tutoring.","Many self-made entrepreneurs say that failure was their best teacher."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"semblance","p":"noun","d":"An outward appearance of something, especially when the real thing is only slightly there or not there at all.","lb":"appearance, trace","s":["appearance","pretense","facade","show","guise","resemblance"],"k":["affectation","color","disguise","feigning"],"a":["reality","substance","truth"],"ex":["After the storm, the town slowly returned to a semblance of normal life.","He kept a semblance of calm, although his hands were shaking.","Please tidy up quickly so the room has at least some semblance of order before the guests arrive."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"senile","p":"adjective","d":"Confused, forgetful and weak because of old age; now often considered rude or outdated.","lb":"confused with age","s":["decrepit","doddering","infirm","feeble","forgetful","confused"],"k":["doddery","dotty","failing","frail"],"a":["sharp","alert","lucid","spry"],"ex":["Doctors no longer use the word senile and prefer to name the exact illness.","People should not call an elderly relative senile just because he forgets a name.","In the novel, the old landlord grows senile and no longer recognizes his own sons."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sensation","p":"noun","d":"A physical feeling that you get through your body, such as heat, pain or tingling.","lb":"feeling, perception","s":["feeling","sense","perception","impression","awareness","tingle"],"k":["ace","consciousness","emotion","intuition"],"a":["numbness"],"ex":["I felt a tingling sensation in my fingers after holding the ice for too long.","The doctor asked whether I had any sensation of pain in my leg.","Biting into the green chili gave me a burning sensation that lasted for minutes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sensory","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the senses, or to receiving feelings and information through them.","lb":"of the senses","s":["perceptual","physical"],"k":["auditory","gustatory","haptic","olfactory"],"a":[],"ex":["Eyes, ears, skin, nose and tongue are the body's sensory organs.","A crowded festival can cause sensory overload for young children, with so many sounds and lights.","The museum has a sensory room where visitors can touch, smell and listen to different things."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sententious","p":"adjective","d":"Fond of giving moral advice in a pompous, preachy way.","lb":"preachy, moralizing","s":["preachy","moralizing","pompous","pontificating","sanctimonious","pious"],"k":["aphoristic","bombastic","concise","grandiloquent"],"a":["humble","unpretentious","modest","direct"],"ex":["My uncle gave a sententious speech about hard work and wasted time at the dinner table.","The principal's sententious tone made students stop listening to his advice.","Her essay was sententious, full of grand sayings but short on real ideas."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"sentient","p":"adjective","d":"Able to see, hear, feel and think; aware of the world through the senses.","lb":"conscious, feeling","s":["conscious","aware","living","feeling","perceptive","responsive"],"k":["alert","animated","awake","cognizant"],"a":["unconscious","inanimate","lifeless","unfeeling"],"ex":["Scientists agree that dogs and cats are sentient animals that can feel pain and fear.","In the science fiction film, a robot becomes sentient and asks to be treated as a person.","A rock is not sentient, but a fish can sense danger and react to it."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"sentimentalize","p":"verb","d":"To treat or remember something in an overly emotional way that ignores its real difficulties.","lb":"romanticize, idealize","s":["romanticize","idealize","glorify","gloss over","put on a pedestal"],"k":["beautify","belie","embellish","misrepresent"],"a":["demystify","debunk","be realistic about"],"ex":["Older people sometimes sentimentalize the past and forget how hard daily life really was.","Films about village life often sentimentalize poverty instead of showing its real struggles.","It is easy to sentimentalize your school days once the exams are over."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sequester","p":"verb","d":"To keep a person or thing separate from others, often in a private place for a particular reason.","lb":"isolate, set apart","s":["isolate","segregate","separate","set apart","quarantine","cloister"],"k":["adjourn","attach","confiscate","divide"],"a":["mix","integrate","join","mingle"],"ex":["The jury was sequestered in a hotel so that nobody could influence their decision.","Before the final exams, Nadia sequestered herself in the library and turned off her phone.","Patients with the infection were sequestered in a separate ward to protect others."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sequestered","p":"adjective","d":"Kept apart from other people or from the outside world; quiet and private.","lb":"isolated, secluded","s":["secluded","isolated","cloistered","private","remote","hidden"],"k":["monastic","out of the way","reclusive","secret"],"a":["public","exposed","open","accessible"],"ex":["The jury stayed sequestered in a hotel until they reached a verdict.","She lived a sequestered life in a quiet village far from the city.","A sequestered garden behind the old library is my favorite place to study."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"serendipity","p":"noun","d":"The luck of finding something good or valuable by chance, when you were not looking for it.","lb":"luck, happy accident","s":["luck","chance","fluke","good fortune","happy accident","coincidence"],"k":["blessing","boon","fortune","godsend"],"a":["misfortune","bad luck","ill fortune"],"ex":["By serendipity, I met my old teacher at the bus stop and heard about a job.","Their friendship began through pure serendipity when two lost students asked each other for directions.","Many great discoveries in science happened through serendipity rather than careful planning."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"serene","p":"adjective","d":"Calm, quiet and untroubled, with no sign of worry, noise or disturbance.","lb":"calm, peaceful","s":["calm","tranquil","peaceful","placid","untroubled","composed"],"k":["clear","cloudless","collected","halcyon"],"a":["agitated","troubled","stormy","turbulent"],"ex":["Even though the hall felt tense before the exam, Nadia looked serene and ready.","At sunrise the Padma looked serene, with only a few small boats drifting across the water.","Her serene expression showed that the doctor's news had not worried her."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"serenity","p":"noun","d":"A calm, peaceful state, free from worry or disturbance.","lb":"calmness, peace","s":["calm","peace","tranquility","stillness","composure","quiet"],"k":["calmness","concord","equanimity","hush"],"a":["turmoil","agitation","chaos","anxiety"],"ex":["The serenity of the lake at dawn made me forget my worries.","She meditates every morning to find a little serenity before the busy day.","The old man faced his illness with remarkable serenity."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"serpentine","p":"adjective","d":"Winding and twisting in shape or movement, like a snake.","lb":"winding, twisting","s":["winding","twisting","sinuous","snaking","meandering","curving"],"k":["crooked","curved","curvy","rambling"],"a":["straight","direct","unswerving"],"ex":["The bus climbed the serpentine mountain road, and half the passengers felt dizzy.","A long, serpentine queue of people waited outside the passport office all morning.","The river takes a serpentine path through the delta before reaching the Bay of Bengal."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"servile","p":"adjective","d":"Too eager to obey or please others, showing no independence or self-respect.","lb":"submissive, fawning","s":["submissive","subservient","obsequious","fawning","slavish","groveling"],"k":["abject","bootlicking","cowering","cringing"],"a":["independent","assertive","domineering","defiant"],"ex":["The servile assistant agreed with every word the boss said, even when he was wrong.","She disliked the servile way the shop clerk bowed to rich customers.","A servile smile appeared on his face whenever the inspector walked in."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"severance","p":"noun","d":"The ending of a connection or relationship, such as a job or ties between countries.","lb":"ending, separation","s":["separation","break","split","cutting off","termination","parting"],"k":["amputation","breach","breakup","disconnection"],"a":["union","connection","joining","link"],"ex":["She received three months' salary as severance pay when the factory closed.","The severance of ties between the two countries disrupted trade.","The contract describes how severance will be handled if an employee is dismissed."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"severe","p":"adjective","d":"Very bad, serious or intense in a way that causes great difficulty or pain.","lb":"harsh, intense","s":["harsh","serious","intense","extreme","grave","acute"],"k":["austere","bad","dangerous","grievous"],"a":["mild","gentle","slight","moderate"],"ex":["Severe storms damaged hundreds of houses along the coast.","He suffered severe pain in his back after lifting the heavy box.","The teacher gave a severe warning to the students who cheated."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"severity","p":"noun","d":"The degree to which something bad, such as pain, a storm or a punishment, is serious or harsh.","lb":"seriousness, harshness","s":["seriousness","gravity","harshness","intensity","extremity","rigour"],"k":["asperity","austerity","badness","brutality"],"a":["mildness","leniency","gentleness","lightness"],"ex":["The doctor checked the severity of her cough before giving her any medicine.","Flood warnings were issued because of the severity of the approaching storm.","The court reduced the punishment, saying it did not match the severity of the offence."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"shackle","p":"noun","d":"A metal ring fixed around a prisoner's wrist or ankle, or anything that limits a person's freedom.","lb":"restraint, fetter","s":["restraint","fetter","handcuff","chain","bond","yoke"],"k":["bind","cuff","hamper","hobble"],"a":["freedom","liberty","release","emancipation"],"ex":["In the museum, we saw iron shackles once used on prisoners.","Education can break the shackles of poverty for a whole family.","The shackle of heavy debt kept him from changing jobs."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"shadowy","p":"adjective","d":"Dark and full of shadows, so that things are hard to see clearly.","lb":"dark, dim","s":["dim","dark","shady","gloomy","murky","dusky"],"k":["cloudy","faint","indistinct","insubstantial"],"a":["bright","sunlit","illuminated","clear"],"ex":["A shadowy figure stood at the end of the lane, and I could not see his face.","The shadowy corners of the old library made it feel mysterious.","We walked through the shadowy forest, where sunlight barely reached the ground."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sham","p":"noun","d":"Something that is not what it seems to be, used to trick or fool people.","lb":"fake, pretense","s":["fake","fraud","imitation","pretense","hoax","forgery"],"k":["copy","imposter","impostor","phoney"],"a":["reality","truth","original","authenticity"],"ex":["The prize was a sham; the winners had been chosen before the contest began.","Reporters exposed the charity as a sham that kept most of the donations.","His friendly smile was a sham to hide his anger."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"shard","p":"noun","d":"A sharp, broken piece of glass, pottery, metal or another hard, brittle material.","lb":"fragment, splinter","s":["fragment","splinter","sliver","chip","piece","shiver"],"k":["chunk","crumb","potsherd","scrap"],"a":[],"ex":["Archaeologists found a shard of pottery that was nearly two thousand years old.","She swept up the shards of the broken tea cup and put them in a paper bag.","A tiny shard of glass was stuck in the sole of his sandal."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"shibboleth","p":"noun","d":"A word, phrase or custom that marks someone as a member of a particular group, often one outsiders do not know.","lb":"password, hallmark","s":["password","hallmark","slogan","buzzword","trademark","watchword"],"k":["cant","code word","countersign","earmark"],"a":[],"ex":["Using the right slang is a shibboleth among teenagers; adults who try it are quickly spotted.","On the programmers' forum, mentioning a certain text editor is a shibboleth that marks you as an insider.","The old shibboleth that boys must never cry is slowly being rejected."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"shine","p":"verb","d":"To give out or reflect bright light.","lb":"give light, glow","s":["glow","gleam","glitter","beam","sparkle","glisten"],"k":["appear","burnish","fall","glaze"],"a":["darken","dim","fade"],"ex":["The sun shone brightly on the day of the school picnic.","Her polished shoes shone like mirrors.","Shine your torch under the bed to find the lost marble."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"shrewd","p":"adjective","d":"Clever at understanding situations and making smart decisions, especially about money or people.","lb":"astute, sharp","s":["astute","sharp","canny","clever","smart","savvy"],"k":["acute","businesslike","cagey","calculative"],"a":["foolish","naive","gullible","silly"],"ex":["Her shrewd investment in land made the family much richer.","A shrewd shopper compares prices at three stores before buying.","The coach made a shrewd decision to rest his best player before the final."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"shroud","p":"verb","d":"To cover or hide something completely so that it cannot be seen or understood clearly.","lb":"cover, conceal","s":["veil","cloak","cover","conceal","envelop","blanket"],"k":["bury","cloud","dissemble","drape"],"a":["reveal","expose","uncover","unveil"],"ex":["Thick fog shrouded the river, and the ferry had to wait until dawn.","The details of the deal were shrouded in secrecy until Monday.","The company shrouded its new phone in mystery until the launch day."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"shun","p":"verb","d":"To deliberately avoid or stay away from someone or something.","lb":"avoid, reject","s":["avoid","evade","steer clear of","spurn","eschew","reject"],"k":["ban","banish","circumvent","dodge"],"a":["welcome","embrace","seek","accept"],"ex":["After the argument, my cousin shunned me at the family gathering for weeks.","The famous writer shuns publicity and rarely gives interviews.","Many people now shun sugary drinks to protect their health."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sieve","p":"noun","d":"A kitchen tool with a wire or plastic net, used to separate solid pieces from liquid or fine powder from lumps.","lb":"strainer, filter","s":["strainer","filter","colander","sifter","screen","riddle"],"k":["bolter","cheesecloth","drainer","gauze"],"a":[],"ex":["Pass the flour through a sieve to remove any lumps before you mix the cake.","My mother uses a sieve to separate the tea leaves from the hot tea.","The builder used a sieve to separate fine sand from small stones."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"signified","p":"verb","d":"Was a sign of something, or showed or meant it; the past form of signify.","lb":"meant, indicated","s":["indicated","meant","represented","showed","suggested","symbolized"],"k":["augured","bespoke","betokened","evinced"],"a":[],"ex":["The red flag signified that swimming was not safe that day.","Her nod signified that she agreed with the plan.","In the old village, the beating of the drum signified the start of the festival."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"simmer","p":"verb","d":"To cook food gently in liquid at a temperature just below boiling point.","lb":"cook gently","s":["stew","poach","boil gently","bubble","cook slowly"],"k":["boil","burble","coddle","fizz"],"a":[],"ex":["Let the lentils simmer for twenty minutes until they turn soft.","My mother left the beef curry to simmer on low heat all afternoon.","Bring the milk to a boil, then simmer it gently for ten minutes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sincerity","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being honest and meaning what you say, with no pretending.","lb":"honesty, genuineness","s":["honesty","candor","earnestness","truthfulness","frankness","seriousness"],"k":["authenticity","bona fides","directness","forthrightness"],"a":["hypocrisy","dishonesty","pretense","deceit"],"ex":["I could hear the sincerity in her voice when she said sorry.","He thanked the nurses with great sincerity for looking after his father.","In all sincerity, I think your essay needs another draft."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sine qua non","p":"noun","d":"Something absolutely essential, without which something else cannot exist or succeed.","lb":"essential condition","s":["essential","prerequisite","necessity","requirement","requisite","must"],"k":["backbone","bedrock","cornerstone","essential condition"],"a":["luxury","extra","option"],"ex":["Trust is the sine qua non of any lasting friendship.","A valid passport is a sine qua non for traveling abroad.","Employers often treat good communication as a sine qua non for office jobs."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"singular","p":"adjective","d":"Remarkable or unusual in a way that makes something stand out from everything else.","lb":"remarkable, unusual","s":["remarkable","exceptional","extraordinary","unique","outstanding","uncommon"],"k":["amazing","curious","especial","exceeding"],"a":["ordinary","common","usual","typical"],"ex":["She showed singular courage when she stopped the thief and returned the bag to its owner.","The village was known for a singular custom that visitors found both strange and charming.","His singular talent for drawing amazed the art teacher, who had never seen such detail in a child’s work."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"sinister","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming evil or dangerous, or suggesting that something bad is going to happen.","lb":"threatening, evil","s":["ominous","menacing","threatening","evil","malevolent","foreboding"],"k":["alarming","black","forbidding","hostile"],"a":["harmless","benign","friendly","reassuring"],"ex":["A sinister silence filled the house as the lights went out one by one.","The stranger's sinister smile made the children walk faster toward the school gate.","Dark clouds gathered over the bay, giving the sky a sinister look."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"sinuous","p":"adjective","d":"Having many smooth curves and bends, like a snake or a river.","lb":"winding, curving","s":["winding","curving","twisting","serpentine","curvy","meandering"],"k":["arced","crooked","curved","graceful"],"a":["straight","direct","linear","rigid"],"ex":["The sinuous river curved through the green fields like a silver ribbon.","We drove along a sinuous mountain road with a sharp bend every minute.","The dancer's sinuous movements held the audience's eyes throughout the performance."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"skeptic","p":"noun","d":"A person who doubts claims or beliefs that most people accept and wants proof first.","lb":"doubter, questioner","s":["cynic","disbeliever","pessimist","doubter","scoffer"],"k":["debunker","doubting thomas","intellect","intellectual"],"a":["believer","optimist","devotee","follower"],"ex":["My father is a skeptic about miracle diets and always asks to see the evidence.","Even the biggest skeptics changed their minds after seeing the test results.","As a skeptic, Tania never trusts online offers that sound too good to be true."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"skeptical","p":"adjective","d":"Doubting whether something is true or useful, and needing proof before you believe it.","lb":"doubtful, unconvinced","s":["doubtful","dubious","unconvinced","suspicious","cynical","distrustful"],"k":["doubting","in question","questionable","sceptical"],"a":["convinced","trusting","credulous","certain"],"ex":["I am skeptical about any diet that promises quick weight loss.","The teacher was skeptical when Rafi said the dog had eaten his homework.","Many investors are skeptical of schemes that promise huge profits."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"skewer","p":"noun","d":"A long thin stick of metal or wood used to hold pieces of food together while they are cooked.","lb":"spit, pin","s":["spit","pin","rod","stick","spike"],"k":["bamboo stick","barbecue stick","dowel","kebab stick"],"a":[],"ex":["The cook pushed pieces of chicken and onion onto a metal skewer.","Soak wooden skewers in water first so they don't burn on the grill.","At the winter picnic, my uncle turned the skewers over the hot charcoal."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"skirmish","p":"noun","d":"A short, small fight or argument, usually part of a larger conflict.","lb":"clash, scuffle","s":["clash","scuffle","fight","brush","encounter","tussle"],"k":["affray","bout","combat","conflict"],"a":["peace","truce","agreement","harmony"],"ex":["A brief skirmish broke out between rival fans outside the stadium, but police stopped it quickly.","The two sisters had a small skirmish over who would use the bathroom first.","The meeting began with a skirmish between the sales and accounts teams over the budget."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"skittish","p":"adjective","d":"Easily frightened or nervous, and likely to react suddenly or unpredictably.","lb":"nervous, jumpy","s":["nervous","jumpy","restless","edgy","excitable","jittery"],"k":["anxious","flighty","frisky","highly strung"],"a":["calm","steady","composed","placid"],"ex":["Rafi grew skittish whenever the teacher mentioned a surprise test.","Our new kitten is skittish and hides whenever someone walks in.","Skittish investors sold their shares at the first sign of bad news about the company."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"slake","p":"verb","d":"To satisfy a need, especially thirst, completely.","lb":"quench, satisfy","s":["quench","satisfy","sate","satiate","relieve","appease"],"k":["abate","alleviate","conform to","drench"],"a":["whet","arouse","stimulate"],"ex":["After the long walk, he drank a glass of cold water to slake his thirst.","Street vendors sell fresh sugarcane juice to slake the thirst of passersby in summer.","She read three books about space to slake her curiosity about the stars."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"slander","p":"verb","d":"To say false things about someone in order to damage their good name.","lb":"defame, smear","s":["defame","smear","malign","vilify","besmirch","disparage"],"k":["accuse","bad-mouth","blacken","calumniate"],"a":["praise","compliment","defend","commend"],"ex":["Someone slandered the shopkeeper online, claiming he sold expired food, and his sales dropped quickly.","She was upset that her former friend had slandered her to the whole neighborhood.","You should not slander a rival candidate just because you lost the school election."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"slaughter","p":"verb","d":"To kill an animal for its meat.","lb":"kill for meat","s":["butcher","kill","cull","massacre","slay"],"k":["bleed","dispatch","do in","dress"],"a":[],"ex":["The farmer slaughtered two chickens for the family's Friday lunch.","Animals must be slaughtered only in clean, licensed slaughterhouses.","Many families buy cattle in the weeks before Eid, planning to slaughter an animal and share the meat."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sleazy","p":"adjective","d":"Dishonest or morally low in a way that seems cheap and unpleasant.","lb":"seedy, disreputable","s":["seedy","shabby","squalid","sordid","disreputable","tacky"],"k":["brassy","bum","cheap","cheesy"],"a":["respectable","reputable","decent","honorable"],"ex":["The detective met his informant in a sleazy hotel near the bus terminal.","Customers complained about the sleazy tricks of a company that hid fees in tiny print.","The newspaper printed a sleazy story about the private life of a local businessman."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sloth","p":"noun","d":"Unwillingness to work or make an effort; laziness.","lb":"laziness, idleness","s":["laziness","idleness","indolence","inertia","lethargy","apathy"],"k":["dawdling","deadly sin","inactivity","loafing"],"a":["diligence","industry","energy","hard work"],"ex":["Sloth kept him in bed until noon, and he missed the morning class.","After the holidays, the whole family had to fight against sloth and get back to a routine.","The manager blamed the team's sloth for the missed deadlines."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"slothful","p":"adjective","d":"Unwilling to work or make any effort; lazy.","lb":"lazy, sluggish","s":["lazy","idle","indolent","sluggish","lethargic","inactive"],"k":["dilatory","feckless","lackadaisical","languid"],"a":["diligent","industrious","energetic","hardworking"],"ex":["After a slothful weekend on the sofa, he had no energy to study.","The manager warned that slothful workers would not receive a bonus.","Her slothful habits meant that dishes piled up in the sink for days."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sly","p":"adjective","d":"Clever at getting what you want in a quiet, secret way, often by tricking people.","lb":"cunning, crafty","s":["cunning","crafty","wily","artful","devious","foxy"],"k":["dodgy","furtive","impish","slick"],"a":["honest","straightforward","open","frank"],"ex":["The sly shopkeeper hid the damaged items at the bottom of the box.","With a sly smile, she hid the surprise gift behind her back.","The fox in the story was so sly that it tricked the crow out of its food."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"smother","p":"verb","d":"To cover someone or something so thickly or tightly that air is cut off, or to cover it completely.","lb":"cover, suffocate","s":["suffocate","stifle","choke","extinguish","snuff out","cover"],"k":["asphyxiate","blow out","deluge","drown"],"a":["uncover","expose","reveal","bare"],"ex":["She smothered the oil fire with a damp towel.","The pancakes were smothered in honey and sliced banana.","Weeds soon smothered the young seedlings in the garden."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"snatch","p":"verb","d":"To grab something quickly, often roughly or without permission.","lb":"grab, seize","s":["grab","seize","grasp","snap up","pluck","take"],"k":["abduct","clasp","filch","grip"],"a":["give","offer","hand over","release"],"ex":["A thief on a motorbike tried to snatch her phone and speed away.","The child snatched the biscuit from the plate before anyone else could reach it.","The eagle swooped down and snatched a fish from the river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"soaked","p":"adjective","d":"Completely wet, with water dripping from you or your clothes.","lb":"drenched, wet through","s":["drenched","sodden","wet through","saturated","sopping","dripping"],"k":["bedraggled","besotted","blind drunk","blotto"],"a":["dry","parched","arid"],"ex":["We got caught in a sudden monsoon shower and arrived home soaked to the skin.","The soaked towel was too heavy to carry, so I wrung it out first.","Rafi's soaked shoes left wet footprints across the clean floor."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sobriety","p":"noun","d":"A calm, serious way of thinking and behaving; also the state of not being drunk.","lb":"seriousness, restraint","s":["seriousness","gravity","moderation","restraint","solemnity","temperance"],"k":["circumspection","clear-headedness","dryness","earnestness"],"a":["drunkenness","frivolity","intoxication","excess"],"ex":["The sobriety of the ceremony reminded everyone of the importance of the occasion.","The judge spoke with sobriety, choosing every word carefully.","He celebrated one year of sobriety with a quiet dinner with his family."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"soil","p":"noun","d":"The top layer of the ground in which plants grow.","lb":"earth, ground","s":["earth","dirt","ground","loam","humus","clay"],"k":["filth","grime","mud","sphere"],"a":[],"ex":["The rich soil along the river is perfect for growing rice and jute.","Add compost to the soil before planting the tomato seedlings.","Heavy rain washed away the soil from the steep hillside."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"solace","p":"noun","d":"Comfort or relief that you feel when you are sad, disappointed or worried.","lb":"comfort, consolation","s":["comfort","consolation","relief","support","cheer","reassurance"],"k":["ease","haven","refuge","repose"],"a":["distress","torment","anguish","discomfort"],"ex":["After failing the exam, Rafi found solace in a long walk by the river.","Music has always been a solace for her when she feels lonely.","The family took solace in the fact that everyone had escaped the fire unhurt."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"solely","p":"adverb","d":"Only; not involving anyone or anything else.","lb":"only, entirely","s":["only","exclusively","entirely","purely","completely","just"],"k":["all alone","altogether","but","by itself"],"a":["partly","partially","jointly","also"],"ex":["She is solely responsible for the cleaning of the lab.","He chose the university solely because it was close to his home.","The shop's success depends solely on its loyal customers."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"solemnity","p":"noun","d":"A serious, dignified manner or quality, especially at an important occasion.","lb":"seriousness, formality","s":["gravity","seriousness","formality","dignity","earnestness","sobriety"],"k":["decorum","grandeur","gravitas","importance"],"a":["levity","frivolity","humor","playfulness"],"ex":["The solemnity of the ceremony made even the children stand quietly.","The judge spoke with great solemnity as she read the verdict.","A sudden joke broke the solemnity of the meeting, and everyone relaxed."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"solicitous","p":"adjective","d":"Showing careful concern for someone's comfort, health or happiness.","lb":"caring, attentive","s":["caring","attentive","concerned","considerate","thoughtful","protective"],"k":["heedful","kindly","mindful","ministering"],"a":["indifferent","uncaring","neglectful","careless"],"ex":["The nurse was solicitous, asking the elderly patient every hour if she needed anything.","Her solicitous neighbor brought soup every evening while she had the flu.","He was always solicitous about his mother's health and called her twice a day."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"solidarity","p":"noun","d":"Agreement and mutual support among people who share a purpose, interests or feelings.","lb":"unity, fellowship","s":["unity","fellowship","togetherness","cohesion","camaraderie","harmony"],"k":["allegiance","brotherhood","commonality","companionship"],"a":["disunity","division","discord","disagreement"],"ex":["Students collected money in solidarity with a classmate whose family lost its home in a fire.","Neighbors showed solidarity by cooking meals for the families hit by the flood.","The workers stood in solidarity when one of them was unfairly dismissed."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"solvent","p":"adjective","d":"Having enough money to pay all the debts and bills one owes.","lb":"debt-free, financially sound","s":["financially sound","in the black","able to pay","stable","secure","sound"],"k":["affluent","flush","in funds","liquid"],"a":["insolvent","bankrupt","broke","in the red"],"ex":["After paying off her loan, the small bakery finally became solvent again.","The bank will only lend money to a company that can prove it is solvent.","Rafi barely stays solvent each month because rent takes most of his salary."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"somber","p":"adjective","d":"Serious, sad and gloomy in mood or appearance.","lb":"grave, gloomy","s":["grave","solemn","sober","gloomy","serious","sad"],"k":["colorless","depressing","drab","dreary"],"a":["cheerful","bright","lively","joyful"],"ex":["The mood at the memorial was somber, and nobody spoke above a whisper.","The manager's somber expression told us the news about the factory was bad.","The newsreader's somber voice told us the story was serious."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"soothe","p":"verb","d":"To make someone calmer or less upset, or to make pain less severe.","lb":"calm, comfort","s":["calm","comfort","ease","relieve","pacify","placate"],"k":["appease","assuage","console","mitigate"],"a":["agitate","irritate","upset","aggravate"],"ex":["She soothed the crying baby by singing softly and rocking him in her arms.","A warm cup of tea can soothe a sore throat.","Soft music helps soothe my nerves before an exam."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sophisticated","p":"adjective","d":"Having a lot of experience of life and good taste in culture, fashion and manners.","lb":"cultured, refined","s":["cultured","refined","worldly","urbane","cosmopolitan","polished"],"k":["advanced","civilized","cultivated","debonair"],"a":["naive","unsophisticated","provincial","crude"],"ex":["She looked sophisticated in a simple dark dress and a silk scarf.","The restaurant attracts a sophisticated crowd who enjoy fine food and quiet music.","He gave a sophisticated answer that showed a wide knowledge of history and art."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sophomoric","p":"adjective","d":"Childish and silly, showing a lack of experience while trying to seem clever.","lb":"immature, childish","s":["immature","childish","juvenile","puerile","silly","callow"],"k":["babyish","half-baked","infantile","jejune"],"a":["mature","sophisticated","sensible","wise"],"ex":["The comedian's sophomoric jokes made the adults groan, though the teenagers laughed.","It was a sophomoric prank, and the principal was not amused.","Critics called the film sophomoric, full of silly humour and short on real ideas."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"soporific","p":"adjective","d":"Making you feel sleepy, or causing you to fall asleep.","lb":"sleep-inducing, drowsy","s":["sedative","hypnotic","drowsy","lulling","narcotic"],"k":["depressant","dull","humdrum","monotonous"],"a":["stimulating","invigorating","energizing","exciting"],"ex":["The warm room and the teacher's slow voice had a soporific effect on the class.","Some cold medicines are soporific, so you should not drive after taking them.","The soporific hum of the train soon sent the tired passengers to sleep."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"sordid","p":"adjective","d":"Dirty or morally low; involving dishonesty, greed or shameful behavior.","lb":"squalid, shameful","s":["squalid","filthy","shameful","vile","seedy","base"],"k":["acquisitive","dirty","disgraceful","disreputable"],"a":["honorable","noble","clean","decent"],"ex":["The newspaper revealed the sordid details of how the owner had cheated the workers.","They lived in a sordid, damp room with no windows.","The film tells a sordid story of greed and betrayal inside a wealthy family."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"sordidness","p":"noun","d":"The state of being very dirty, shabby and depressing to look at.","lb":"squalor, dirtiness","s":["squalor","filth","dirtiness","squalidness","seediness"],"k":["decay","dinginess","dirt","grime"],"a":["cleanliness","neatness","purity","freshness"],"ex":["The sordidness of the cheap hotel room shocked the tired travellers.","Visitors were shocked by the sordidness of the crowded, rubbish-filled alley.","Nothing could hide the sordidness of the old bus stand, with its broken benches and puddles."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sovereign","p":"noun","d":"A king or queen; a ruler who holds the highest power in a country.","lb":"monarch, ruler","s":["monarch","ruler","king","queen","emperor","empress"],"k":["chief of state","head of state","khan","pharaoh"],"a":["subject","commoner","vassal"],"ex":["The sovereign opened the new session with a speech written by the government.","In the old days, a sovereign could order any subject to pay new taxes.","Tourists lined up to see the palace where the sovereign once lived."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"sparing","p":"adjective","d":"Careful not to use or give too much of something.","lb":"economical, frugal","s":["frugal","economical","thrifty","careful","restrained","prudent"],"k":["abstemious","cautious","cost-conscious","niggardly"],"a":["lavish","generous","wasteful","liberal"],"ex":["Be sparing with the salt when you cook for people with high blood pressure.","During the water shortage, everyone had to be sparing in their use of water.","The teacher was sparing with praise, so a kind word from her meant a lot."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sparse","p":"adjective","d":"Present in small amounts, or spread out so that there is a lot of space between things.","lb":"thin, scattered","s":["scanty","thin","scattered","meager","scarce","sporadic"],"k":["distributed","inadequate","insufficient","lean"],"a":["dense","thick","abundant","plentiful"],"ex":["Rainfall in the desert is sparse, so only a few plants can survive.","The old man's sparse gray hair moved in the wind.","Attendance at the lecture was sparse because of the heavy rain."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sparsely","p":"adverb","d":"In a thin or scattered way, with large spaces between things or with very little of something.","lb":"thinly, scantily","s":["thinly","scantily","scarcely","lightly","barely","sporadically"],"k":["faintly","hardly","in clumps","intermittently"],"a":["densely","thickly","heavily","abundantly"],"ex":["The northern hills are sparsely populated, with only a few small villages.","The classroom was sparsely furnished, with just a table, a chair and a blackboard.","Grass grew sparsely on the dry, rocky slope."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"spate","p":"noun","d":"A sudden large number of similar events or things coming one after another in a short time.","lb":"flood, sudden series","s":["flood","wave","rush","series","torrent","outbreak"],"k":["avalanche","barrage","batch","billow"],"a":[],"ex":["A spate of mobile phone thefts has worried students in the area.","After the advertisement, the shop received a spate of calls from new customers.","The village suffered a spate of power cuts in the middle of the exam season."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"spawn","p":"verb","d":"To cause something, often in large numbers, to be produced or to develop.","lb":"produce, give rise to","s":["produce","generate","create","give rise to","bring about","cause"],"k":["beget","build","do","father"],"a":["suppress","stop","prevent","end"],"ex":["The success of the first film spawned two sequels and a popular cartoon series.","One careless post online can spawn thousands of angry replies within an hour.","Poor drainage during the monsoon can spawn swarms of mosquitoes in the neighborhood."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"specious","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming correct or convincing at first, but actually wrong or false.","lb":"misleading, fallacious","s":["misleading","fallacious","deceptive","false","spurious","unsound"],"k":["beguiling","casuistic","erroneous","gilded"],"a":["genuine","sound","valid","authentic"],"ex":["The salesman gave a specious argument that sounded logical but ignored the hidden fees.","His excuse for missing the meeting was specious, because the roads were completely clear that morning.","Specious claims about instant weight loss fill the internet and fool many readers."],"b":115,"y":1},{"w":"specter","p":"noun","d":"A ghost; also something frightening that people fear may happen in the future.","lb":"ghost, phantom","s":["ghost","phantom","spirit","apparition","spook","wraith"],"k":["bogeyman","bugbear","dread","menace"],"a":[],"ex":["The old house was said to be haunted by the specter of a woman in white.","Children told stories about a specter that walked the school corridor at midnight.","The specter of another flood hung over the village as the river kept rising."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"spectrum","p":"noun","d":"A wide range of related things, ideas or opinions that run from one extreme to another.","lb":"range, scale","s":["range","scale","gamut","continuum","span","array"],"k":["band","breadth","compass","diversity"],"a":[],"ex":["The survey recorded a wide spectrum of opinions about the new school timetable.","The shop sells a full spectrum of phones, from cheap basic models to costly flagships.","The weather here covers a spectrum, from hot, dry summers to heavy monsoon rains."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"speculation","p":"noun","d":"Opinions or guesses about something when you do not have enough facts to be sure.","lb":"guesswork, conjecture","s":["conjecture","guesswork","supposition","surmise","theory","hypothesis"],"k":["dead reckoning","guessing","meditation","opinion"],"a":["fact","certainty","proof","knowledge"],"ex":["There is a lot of speculation about who will be the next captain of the team.","The police refused to comment until they had facts rather than speculation.","Rumors and speculation spread quickly on social media after the company closed its office."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"spendthrift","p":"noun","d":"A person who spends money carelessly and wastes it.","lb":"squanderer, big spender","s":["prodigal","big spender","profligate","free spender"],"k":["bankrupt","debtor","gambler","high roller"],"a":["miser","saver","scrooge","skinflint"],"ex":["My uncle is a spendthrift who buys every new gadget as soon as it appears.","The young spendthrift had spent his whole first salary within three days.","Don't be a spendthrift at the fair; you have to make your pocket money last all month."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"spiraling","p":"adjective","d":"Rising or getting worse quickly and in a way that is hard to control.","lb":"escalating, rising fast","s":["escalating","soaring","rocketing","mounting","runaway","skyrocketing"],"k":["accelerating","ballooning","burgeoning","climbing"],"a":["falling","declining","dropping","stable"],"ex":["Spiraling food prices have forced many families to cut back on meat and fish.","The company closed its factory because of spiraling costs for fuel and raw materials.","Students struggle with spiraling rents near the university."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"splendor","p":"noun","d":"Great beauty, richness or impressive appearance.","lb":"magnificence, grandeur","s":["magnificence","grandeur","brilliance","glory","majesty","pomp"],"k":["elegance","gorgeousness","lavishness","luster"],"a":["squalor","ugliness","dullness"],"ex":["Visitors gasped at the splendor of the palace's golden halls.","The sunrise over the Padma River was a sight of great splendor.","The bride arrived in all her splendor, wearing a red silk saree."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"spontaneous","p":"adjective","d":"Happening or done naturally, without being planned or forced.","lb":"impulsive, unplanned","s":["impulsive","unplanned","instinctive","natural","impromptu","voluntary"],"k":["ad hoc","automatic","casual","impetuous"],"a":["planned","deliberate","calculated","rehearsed"],"ex":["The crowd broke into spontaneous applause when the little girl finished her song.","We made a spontaneous decision to visit the beach on Saturday.","Her speech was spontaneous; she had no notes at all."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sporadic","p":"adjective","d":"Happening only occasionally or at irregular intervals, rather than regularly or continuously.","lb":"occasional, irregular","s":["occasional","irregular","intermittent","scattered","infrequent","patchy"],"k":["broken","episodic","fitful","on-and-off"],"a":["regular","constant","continuous","frequent"],"ex":["Sporadic showers fell through the afternoon, but the match was never stopped.","Load-shedding in our area is sporadic these days: sometimes one cut a day, sometimes none.","There were sporadic cases of flu at the school, but no serious outbreak."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"spurious","p":"adjective","d":"False or not genuine, although it may look real or sound reasonable.","lb":"false, fake","s":["false","fake","bogus","counterfeit","sham","phony"],"k":["bastard","dummy","ersatz","fictitious"],"a":["genuine","authentic","real","valid"],"ex":["The company rejected the spurious claim that its snacks had caused illness.","Don't share spurious messages that you haven't checked on trusted news sites.","His excuse was spurious, because the shop had been open all afternoon."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"spurn","p":"verb","d":"To reject someone or something in a proud, scornful way.","lb":"reject, scorn","s":["reject","rebuff","scorn","snub","disdain","repudiate"],"k":["decline","deny","despise","dismiss"],"a":["accept","welcome","embrace","court"],"ex":["She spurned his offer of money, saying she would rather earn it herself.","The singer spurned the contract because its terms were insulting.","He spurned every attempt his old friends made to reconnect with him."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"squalid","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely dirty and unpleasant, especially because of neglect or poverty.","lb":"filthy, wretched","s":["filthy","dirty","sordid","grimy","wretched","seedy"],"k":["corrupt","dingy","disreputable","nasty"],"a":["clean","spotless","pristine","tidy"],"ex":["The students complained about the squalid state of the hostel bathrooms.","Inspectors closed the restaurant after finding squalid conditions in its kitchen.","Many families lived in squalid rooms without clean water until the new housing project was built."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"squalor","p":"noun","d":"A dirty, unpleasant and neglected condition, especially in a place where poor people live.","lb":"filth, misery","s":["filth","dirt","grime","misery","poverty","sordidness"],"k":["decay","degradation","deprivation","destitution"],"a":["cleanliness","luxury","comfort","splendor"],"ex":["Many families once lived in squalor beside the railway line, without clean water or proper toilets.","The inspector closed the restaurant after finding squalor in its kitchen, including rats and rotten food.","He grew up in squalor, but he studied hard and eventually became a doctor."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"squander","p":"verb","d":"To waste money, time or chances in a careless way.","lb":"waste, misspend","s":["waste","fritter away","blow","dissipate","lavish","throw away"],"k":["consume","expend","fool away","fritter"],"a":["save","conserve","preserve","economize"],"ex":["He squandered his salary on video games and had nothing left by the middle of the month.","Don't squander your time on your phone when the exam is only a week away.","The team squandered a two-goal lead and lost the match."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"squirrel","p":"noun","d":"A small animal with a long bushy tail that lives in trees and eats nuts and seeds.","lb":"rodent, animal","s":[],"k":["chickaree","chipmunk","gopher","marmot"],"a":[],"ex":["A squirrel ran up the mango tree with a piece of bread in its mouth.","The squirrel's long bushy tail helps it balance on thin branches.","Every morning a squirrel visits our balcony to look for rice grains."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stagnant","p":"adjective","d":"Not flowing or moving, or not growing, developing or changing.","lb":"motionless, inactive","s":["still","motionless","standing","stale","inactive","sluggish"],"k":["dead","fetid","frozen","inert"],"a":["flowing","running","active","thriving"],"ex":["Mosquitoes breed in stagnant water, so empty any old buckets and tires.","The stagnant pond behind the school smells terrible in summer.","Wages have stayed stagnant while prices keep rising."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stagnation","p":"noun","d":"A state in which there is no growth, movement or progress.","lb":"standstill, inactivity","s":["inactivity","standstill","stasis","inertia","torpor","idleness"],"k":["doldrums","hiatus","impasse","inaction"],"a":["growth","progress","development","activity"],"ex":["Years of economic stagnation left many young graduates without jobs.","Standing water in the pond led to stagnation, and mosquitoes soon began to breed.","After ten years in the same position, she felt a sense of stagnation and decided to change careers."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"stalwart","p":"adjective","d":"Strong, loyal and dependable, especially in difficult times.","lb":"loyal, steadfast","s":["loyal","steadfast","sturdy","staunch","robust","dependable"],"k":["brave","committed","constant","courageous"],"a":["disloyal","weak","wavering","fickle"],"ex":["She has been a stalwart supporter of the local library for thirty years.","The stalwart volunteers kept working through the night to fill sandbags.","A stalwart friend stays beside you in both good times and bad."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"stark","p":"adjective","d":"Harsh, plain and impossible to ignore, as in a stark difference or a stark warning.","lb":"harsh, plain","s":["harsh","bleak","severe","plain","bare","grim"],"k":["arrant","barren","complete","consummate"],"a":["soft","mild","gentle","ornate"],"ex":["There is a stark contrast between the busy city center and the quiet village.","The doctor gave a stark warning: if he does not stop smoking, his health will fail.","The empty white walls gave the room a stark look."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"startled","p":"adjective","d":"Suddenly surprised or slightly frightened, often shown by a quick movement.","lb":"surprised, jumpy","s":["surprised","alarmed","shocked","jumpy","taken aback","frightened"],"k":["afraid","amazed","anxious","astonished"],"a":["calm","unruffled","composed"],"ex":["The startled cat leapt off the sofa when the door banged shut.","She gave a startled cry when her friend tapped her on the shoulder.","Startled by the loud horn, the old man almost dropped his tea."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"static","p":"adjective","d":"Not moving, changing or developing; staying in the same state.","lb":"unchanging, still","s":["stationary","unchanging","fixed","motionless","constant","still"],"k":["dormant","electrostatic","inactive","regular"],"a":["dynamic","changing","moving","mobile"],"ex":["Prices in the market have been static for months, so shoppers are happy.","A static picture on a website loads faster than a video.","Her career felt static, so she looked for a job with more challenges."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"status quo","p":"noun","d":"The existing state of affairs, especially regarding social or political matters.","lb":"current situation","s":["existing situation","current state","present condition","established order","way things are","current situation"],"k":["conservatism","orthodoxy","situation","stability"],"a":["change","reform","revolution","innovation"],"ex":["Some people prefer the status quo because change makes them uncomfortable.","The new manager wanted to challenge the status quo and try different methods.","Both teams agreed to maintain the status quo until the rules were reviewed."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"staunch","p":"adjective","d":"Strongly loyal and firm in supporting a person, belief or cause, and not likely to change.","lb":"loyal, steadfast","s":["loyal","steadfast","faithful","devoted","committed","firm"],"k":["constant","dedicated","reliable","resolute"],"a":["disloyal","fickle","unfaithful","wavering"],"ex":["My uncle is a staunch supporter of the national cricket team and never misses a match.","Nadia stayed a staunch friend through all the difficult months of her sister's illness.","The professor is a staunch defender of free libraries and open learning."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"steadfast","p":"adjective","d":"Firmly loyal and unwavering, refusing to change your mind, purpose or loyalty.","lb":"loyal, unwavering","s":["loyal","faithful","devoted","constant","resolute","unwavering"],"k":["ardent","dependable","reliable","stiff"],"a":["disloyal","fickle","wavering","unfaithful"],"ex":["Through her illness, her steadfast friends visited her every week.","He remained steadfast in his decision to study medicine, whatever others said.","The staff stayed steadfast to the company even when salaries were delayed."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"steadily","p":"adverb","d":"At a regular, continuous pace, without sudden changes or stops.","lb":"gradually, constantly","s":["constantly","continuously","regularly","gradually","evenly","consistently"],"k":["endlessly","frequently","incessantly","incrementally"],"a":["erratically","suddenly","intermittently"],"ex":["Rain fell steadily all night, and by morning the yard was full of water.","Her English has improved steadily since she began reading the news every day.","The price of rice has risen steadily over the past year."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"stem","p":"noun","d":"The main thin part of a plant that holds up the leaves and flowers.","lb":"plant stalk","s":["stalk","trunk","shoot","cane","twig","stock"],"k":["bough","bow","branch","fore"],"a":[],"ex":["Cut the rose stem at an angle so that it can drink more water.","The strong wind snapped the stem of the young banana plant.","In biology class, we learned how water travels up the stem to the leaves."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stereotype","p":"noun","d":"A fixed, oversimplified idea about what a type of person or thing is like.","lb":"cliche, preconception","s":["cliche","generalization","caricature","formula","stock idea","assumption"],"k":["bias","cardboard cutout","internal representation","label"],"a":[],"ex":["It is a stereotype that all engineering students are quiet and only like maths.","The film breaks the stereotype that elderly people cannot learn new technology.","Advertisements often repeat the stereotype that only women cook at home."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sterile","p":"adjective","d":"Completely clean and free from germs, as medical tools and bandages must be.","lb":"germ-free, aseptic","s":["aseptic","sanitized","disinfected","sterilized","antiseptic","uncontaminated"],"k":["barren","immaculate","infertile","pristine"],"a":["contaminated","infected","dirty","unsterilized"],"ex":["The nurse opened a sterile bandage and covered the wound carefully.","Surgeons wear sterile gloves so that germs do not enter the patient's body.","Baby bottles should be sterile before every feed."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"sterility","p":"noun","d":"The condition of being completely free from germs and bacteria.","lb":"germ-free state","s":["cleanliness","hygiene","purity","sanitation","disinfection"],"k":["decontamination","immaculacy","infertility","neatness"],"a":["contamination","infection","dirtiness"],"ex":["Nurses wear gloves and masks to protect the sterility of the operating room.","The sterility of the needle is checked before it is used for the injection.","Keep baby bottles sealed so that their sterility is not lost before use."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stern","p":"adjective","d":"Serious and strict, and not likely to be kind or flexible, especially when dealing with bad behaviour.","lb":"strict, severe","s":["strict","severe","harsh","firm","grim","austere"],"k":["demanding","dour","exacting","implacable"],"a":["lenient","gentle","soft","kind"],"ex":["The headmaster gave the noisy students a stern look, and the hall fell silent.","My father's stern voice told me I was in real trouble.","The police issued a stern warning to drivers who ignore the speed limit."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stifle","p":"verb","d":"To hold back a feeling or sound, or to prevent something from developing.","lb":"suppress, hold back","s":["suppress","smother","muffle","hold back","restrain","curb"],"k":["asphyxiate","bottle up","check","dampen"],"a":["express","encourage","release","foster"],"ex":["She tried to stifle a yawn during the long lecture.","He could not stifle his laughter when his friend made a funny face.","Too many rules can stifle creativity in young students."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stigma","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of shame or disapproval that society attaches to a person or condition, harming their reputation.","lb":"shame, disgrace","s":["disgrace","shame","dishonor","taint","stain","blot"],"k":["blemish","censure","disapproval","ignominy"],"a":["honor","credit","glory","esteem"],"ex":["There is still a stigma attached to mental illness, so many people avoid asking for help.","Dropping out of school carried a heavy stigma in her small town.","The stigma of the failed business followed him whenever he applied for a bank loan."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"stigmatize","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone as shameful or disgraceful, so that people look down on them unfairly.","lb":"shame, disgrace","s":["brand","shame","disgrace","vilify","denounce","label"],"k":["castigate","defame","dishonor","malign"],"a":["praise","honor","celebrate","accept"],"ex":["Society should not stigmatize people who seek help for depression or anxiety.","Some villagers stigmatized the widow as unlucky, which made her life lonely and difficult.","Employers must not stigmatize job seekers just because they once lost a job."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"stimulate","p":"verb","d":"To make something more active, or to encourage it to grow or develop.","lb":"encourage, rouse","s":["encourage","spur","activate","boost","inspire","rouse"],"k":["agitate","arouse","brace","cause"],"a":["discourage","depress","dull","suppress"],"ex":["Reading stories aloud can stimulate a young child's imagination.","Lower interest rates are meant to stimulate the economy by encouraging people to borrow.","The teacher asked unusual questions to stimulate discussion in the class."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stint","p":"noun","d":"A fixed period of time that someone spends doing a particular job or activity.","lb":"spell, period","s":["spell","period","stretch","term","shift","tour"],"k":["assignment","continuance","duration","engagement"],"a":[],"ex":["After a two-year stint in Dubai, he returned to Dhaka and opened a small shop.","She did a short stint as a volunteer teacher before starting university.","My father's last stint on the night shift lasted six exhausting months."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"stipend","p":"noun","d":"A fixed regular payment, such as an allowance for a student or a small salary.","lb":"allowance, payment","s":["allowance","salary","grant","pay","payment","scholarship"],"k":["earnings","emolument","honorarium","income"],"a":[],"ex":["The scholarship includes a monthly stipend to cover food and travel.","As an intern, she received a small stipend instead of a full salary.","Graduate students at the university receive a stipend for working as teaching assistants."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"stipulate","p":"verb","d":"To state clearly that something must be done as a condition of an agreement or rule.","lb":"specify, require","s":["specify","require","demand","lay down","insist","provide"],"k":["call for","claim","decree","dictate"],"a":["waive","relax","leave open"],"ex":["The contract stipulates that rent must be paid by the fifth of every month.","The scholarship rules stipulate a minimum grade point average of 3.5 each semester.","My parents stipulated that I finish my homework before I could use the computer."],"b":21,"y":0},{"w":"stipulation","p":"noun","d":"A condition or requirement that is clearly stated as part of an agreement or offer.","lb":"condition, requirement","s":["condition","requirement","provision","proviso","term","clause"],"k":["assumption","caveat","judicial admission","limitation"],"a":[],"ex":["The scholarship has one stipulation: students must maintain a high grade average.","Her parents agreed to the trip with the stipulation that she call every night.","The contract includes a stipulation that payment is due within thirty days."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stoic","p":"adjective","d":"Showing little emotion and not complaining, especially when facing pain or hardship.","lb":"impassive, uncomplaining","s":["impassive","unemotional","calm","patient","composed","phlegmatic"],"k":["collected","dauntless","enduring","expressionless"],"a":["emotional","excitable","expressive","sensitive"],"ex":["Rafi stayed stoic when he heard the bad news and simply nodded.","The stoic farmer replanted his field after the flood without a single complaint.","She was stoic about her injury and finished the race."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"stolid","p":"adjective","d":"Showing little emotion or excitement, and not easily moved or upset.","lb":"unemotional, impassive","s":["impassive","unemotional","phlegmatic","expressionless","placid","stoic"],"k":["calm","composed","deadpan","dour"],"a":["emotional","excitable","expressive","lively"],"ex":["The stolid referee showed no reaction to the angry shouts of the crowd.","Her stolid father listened to the whole story and only nodded.","Despite the shocking news, the manager remained stolid and carried on with the meeting."],"b":99,"y":1},{"w":"stout","p":"adjective","d":"Having a rather fat, solid body; also thick, strong and firm.","lb":"plump, sturdy","s":["plump","stocky","burly","sturdy","portly","chubby"],"k":["beefy","compact","fat","hardy"],"a":["slim","thin","slender","skinny"],"ex":["My grandfather was a stout man with a loud laugh and a warm smile.","She carried a stout wooden stick for walking on the muddy path.","A stout rope held the small boat safely to the dock."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"stratagem","p":"noun","d":"A clever plan or trick used to outwit an opponent or to gain an advantage.","lb":"trick, scheme","s":["ruse","ploy","scheme","maneuver","trick","tactic"],"k":["contrivance","deception","feint","gambit"],"a":[],"ex":["Her stratagem was to arrive early so that she could choose the best seat.","The chess player used a clever stratagem, sacrificing a piece to trap the opponent's king.","Offering a free sample was a simple stratagem to attract more customers to the stall."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"stratum","p":"noun","d":"A layer of rock or soil, or a level of society.","lb":"layer, level","s":["layer","level","tier","bed","seam","class"],"k":["caste","degree","deposit","echelon"],"a":[],"ex":["Geologists found a thin stratum of volcanic ash in the cliff.","A thin stratum of cream separated the two soft layers of the cake.","The survey covered people from every social stratum, from rickshaw pullers to company directors."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"striated","p":"adjective","d":"Marked with thin parallel lines, bands or grooves.","lb":"streaked, grooved","s":["streaked","striped","banded","grooved","lined","furrowed"],"k":["corrugated","fluted","layered","marbled"],"a":["smooth","plain","uniform","unmarked"],"ex":["The cliff face was striated with layers of red and gray rock.","Skeletal muscle looks striated under a microscope, with fine parallel lines running across it.","Her cotton scarf was striated with thin blue and white bands."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"stricture","p":"noun","d":"A rule that limits what you may do, or a strong criticism of someone’s behavior.","lb":"restriction, criticism","s":["restriction","limitation","restraint","rule","condemnation","criticism"],"k":["disapproval","limit","reprimand","reproach"],"a":["freedom","liberty","praise","license"],"ex":["She wanted to work abroad, but strict family strictures about travel made it difficult.","The writer faced harsh strictures from critics who thought the novel was too long.","Under the strictures of the old dress code, students could not wear colored shoes."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"strife","p":"noun","d":"Angry or bitter disagreement or fighting between people or groups.","lb":"conflict, discord","s":["conflict","discord","friction","dissension","quarreling","rivalry"],"k":["animosity","bad blood","battle","clash"],"a":["peace","harmony","agreement","accord"],"ex":["Money problems caused constant strife between the two brothers after their father died.","The village had been torn by strife over water rights for years.","Many people leave regions torn by civil strife to find safer places to live."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"stringent","p":"adjective","d":"Very strict and demanding, with rules or conditions that are hard to meet.","lb":"strict, severe","s":["strict","rigorous","tough","rigid","severe","demanding"],"k":["difficult","draconian","hard","hardline"],"a":["lenient","lax","flexible","relaxed"],"ex":["The airline has stringent rules about the weight of luggage you can take.","Banks apply stringent checks before approving a large loan.","The medicine must pass stringent safety tests before it can be sold in pharmacies."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"strive","p":"verb","d":"To try very hard to achieve something or to make something happen.","lb":"try hard, struggle","s":["endeavor","struggle","labor","toil","aim","attempt"],"k":["aspire","assay","grapple","hard work"],"a":["give up","quit","neglect","idle"],"ex":["Students strive for higher marks by revising every night.","The nurses strive to keep every patient comfortable.","We should strive to be kind even when we are tired."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"strut","p":"noun","d":"A bar or rod that supports part of a structure, such as a roof, a bridge or an aircraft wing.","lb":"brace, support","s":["brace","support","beam","prop","stay","rod"],"k":["crossbeam","girder","joist","prance"],"a":[],"ex":["A rusty metal strut was all that held up the old shop's sagging roof.","Engineers replaced a cracked strut under the footbridge before opening it to the public.","The car's front suspension strut was damaged by a deep pothole."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"stupefy","p":"verb","d":"To surprise or shock someone so much that they cannot think clearly.","lb":"astonish, daze","s":["astonish","amaze","stun","daze","astound","shock"],"k":["baffle","beat","benumb","confound"],"a":[],"ex":["The size of the bill stupefied us; we had never paid so much for one dinner.","The sudden news that the exam was canceled stupefied the students.","Hours of heat and noise in the crowded bus stupefied the passengers."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"stupendous","p":"adjective","d":"Amazingly large, impressive or great in a way that fills you with wonder.","lb":"amazing, huge","s":["amazing","astounding","staggering","tremendous","colossal","phenomenal"],"k":["astonishing","big","enormous","fantastic"],"a":["ordinary","modest","unimpressive","trivial"],"ex":["From the summit, we gazed at a stupendous view of snow-capped peaks stretching to the horizon.","The team's stupendous effort in the final left the crowd speechless.","A stupendous crowd of nearly a hundred thousand fans filled the stadium."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"stupor","p":"noun","d":"A state in which you are almost unconscious or unable to think or react normally.","lb":"daze, torpor","s":["daze","trance","torpor","lethargy","numbness","haze"],"k":["apathy","drowsiness","inertia","insensibility"],"a":["alertness","awareness","vigour","wakefulness"],"ex":["After the long flight, he sat in a stupor and could not answer simple questions.","The shocking news left her in a stupor for several minutes.","The strong sleeping pills left him in a stupor all morning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"stymie","p":"verb","d":"To prevent someone from doing something or stop a plan from making progress.","lb":"thwart, hinder","s":["thwart","hinder","frustrate","block","foil","hamper"],"k":["blockade","embarrass","forbid","foreclose"],"a":["help","assist","aid","facilitate"],"ex":["Poor internet connections stymied our attempts to hold the online class.","Lack of money stymied the club's plan to buy new football gear.","Heavy traffic stymied the ambulance as it tried to reach the hospital."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"subjugate","p":"verb","d":"To defeat a person or group and take complete control over them.","lb":"conquer, dominate","s":["conquer","subdue","dominate","enslave","overpower","crush"],"k":["bring to heel","colonize","enthrall","hold down"],"a":["liberate","free","emancipate","release"],"ex":["Invading armies tried to subjugate the people, but the villagers kept their own language and customs.","A bully tries to subjugate classmates through fear, but teachers can stop it.","The empire grew by subjugating the neighboring kingdoms one by one."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"sublime","p":"adjective","d":"So beautiful or excellent that it fills you with awe and admiration.","lb":"awe-inspiring, excellent","s":["majestic","magnificent","glorious","splendid","exalted","superb"],"k":["brilliant","elated","elevated","elysian"],"a":["ordinary","mundane","ugly","base"],"ex":["The view of sunrise over the hills was sublime, and nobody wanted to speak.","The pianist's sublime performance brought the audience to its feet.","Grandmother's fish curry is sublime; no restaurant has ever matched it."],"b":84,"y":1},{"w":"submit","p":"verb","d":"To formally give a document, proposal or request to someone so that it can be considered.","lb":"hand in, present","s":["hand in","turn in","present","send in","tender","propose"],"k":["accede","advise","bow","defer"],"a":["withdraw","retract","retain","keep"],"ex":["All students must submit their assignments before midnight on Friday.","She submitted her visa application two months before the trip.","The team submitted a detailed proposal for the new bridge to the city council."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"subordinate","p":"adjective","d":"Lower in rank or importance than something or someone else.","lb":"lower, secondary","s":["lower","junior","secondary","minor","inferior","lesser"],"k":["beneath","incidental","low-ranking","reporting"],"a":["superior","senior","chief","principal"],"ex":["As a subordinate officer, he had to report every decision to the department head.","In a good team, personal pride should be subordinate to the shared goal.","The committee gave the youngest member a subordinate role, but she soon proved her worth."],"b":144,"y":0},{"w":"subpoena","p":"noun","d":"A legal order that requires a person to appear in court or to hand over documents.","lb":"court order, summons","s":["summons","writ","court order","legal order","citation"],"k":["injunction","judicial writ","legal demand","mandate"],"a":[],"ex":["The court issued a subpoena requiring the shop owner to hand over his sales records.","She received a subpoena in the mail and had to appear as a witness next Monday.","The lawyer promised to serve a subpoena on anyone who refused to testify voluntarily."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"subside","p":"verb","d":"To become less strong, loud or intense, and gradually return to a normal level.","lb":"die down, abate","s":["abate","die down","ease","decrease","recede","wane"],"k":["alleviate","decline","diminish","lessen"],"a":["intensify","increase","rise","escalate"],"ex":["After the monsoon rain stopped, the floodwater slowly subsided and families returned home.","The pain in my knee finally subsided after two days of rest.","Wait until the noise in the hall subsides before you start your speech."],"b":99,"y":1},{"w":"subsidiary","p":"adjective","d":"Less important than something else, and existing to support or add to it.","lb":"secondary, supporting","s":["secondary","supporting","minor","auxiliary","subordinate","lesser"],"k":["accessory","additional","contributory","extra"],"a":["main","primary","chief","principal"],"ex":["Cost is only a subsidiary concern; our main goal is safety.","She studied economics as her main subject and statistics as a subsidiary subject.","The committee heard the main complaint first and the subsidiary issues afterwards."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"subsidize","p":"verb","d":"To pay part of the cost of something, so that it can be sold or provided at a lower price.","lb":"fund, support","s":["fund","finance","support","sponsor","underwrite","back"],"k":["champion","defray","endow","keep afloat"],"a":["tax","charge","penalize","cut funding"],"ex":["The government subsidizes fertilizer so that farmers can buy it at a lower price.","Our university subsidizes meals in the cafeteria, so students can eat cheaply.","Rich companies sometimes subsidize local sports clubs by paying for their uniforms and trips."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"substantiate","p":"verb","d":"To prove that something is true by giving evidence or facts.","lb":"prove, verify","s":["prove","verify","confirm","validate","corroborate","back up"],"k":["affirm","bear out","body forth","embody"],"a":["disprove","refute","contradict","discredit"],"ex":["You must substantiate your claims with data before the committee will believe you.","The journalist could not substantiate the rumor, so the story was never published.","Photographs and receipts helped substantiate her insurance claim after the fire."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"substantive","p":"adjective","d":"Having real importance or meaning; dealing with the main points rather than small details.","lb":"meaningful, real","s":["substantial","meaningful","significant","real","solid","important"],"k":["ample","large","major","meaty"],"a":["superficial","trivial","insubstantial","minor"],"ex":["The two companies held substantive talks about sharing the building, not just polite chats.","The teacher wanted substantive feedback on the course, not just comments like “good.”","After months of planning, the school finally made substantive changes to its schedule."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"subterfuge","p":"noun","d":"A trick or dishonest plan used to hide the truth or to get what one wants.","lb":"trick, deception","s":["ruse","trick","deception","ploy","dodge","stratagem"],"k":["chicanery","cover-up","deceit","dissembling"],"a":["honesty","openness","candor","frankness"],"ex":["He used a clever subterfuge to get into the match without a ticket.","The children planned a subterfuge to hide their sister's birthday gift.","She got the information by subterfuge, pretending to be a new student."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"subtle","p":"adjective","d":"Not obvious or direct; small and delicate, so that it is difficult to notice.","lb":"delicate, understated","s":["delicate","understated","faint","slight","nuanced","indirect"],"k":["elusive","harmful","insidious","perceptive"],"a":["obvious","blatant","overt","glaring"],"ex":["Learners often miss the subtle difference in meaning between two similar words.","The soup had a subtle flavor of ginger that you noticed only after the third spoonful.","The teacher dropped a subtle hint about the exam question, and only a few students noticed it."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"subversive","p":"adjective","d":"Intended to weaken or overthrow an established system, authority or accepted idea.","lb":"undermining, rebellious","s":["seditious","rebellious","undermining","disruptive","revolutionary","insurgent"],"k":["anarchic","anti-establishment","disloyal","incendiary"],"a":["loyal","supportive","conformist","obedient"],"ex":["The satirical cartoon was considered subversive because it mocked the school's rigid rules.","Teachers worried that the subversive posters might encourage students to ignore the dress code.","The poet's subversive verses challenged old ideas about who should hold power in a family."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"succinct","p":"adjective","d":"Expressed clearly in few words, without anything unnecessary.","lb":"brief, concise","s":["concise","brief","terse","compact","pithy","short"],"k":["brusque","clipped","curt","economical"],"a":["wordy","verbose","rambling","lengthy"],"ex":["Please give a succinct answer, because we have only five minutes for each candidate.","Her email was succinct: the meeting is moved to Tuesday at ten.","A succinct summary of the chapter helped me revise the night before the exam."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"succumb","p":"verb","d":"To give in to something too strong to resist, such as temptation, pressure or illness; sometimes, to die from it.","lb":"give in, yield","s":["yield","give in","surrender","submit","capitulate","cave in"],"k":["accept","buckle under","cede","collapse"],"a":["resist","withstand","overcome","survive"],"ex":["I tried to avoid sweets, but I finally succumbed to temptation and ate a whole cake.","After hours of begging, their father succumbed and let them stay up for the match.","Many small shops succumbed to competition from big online stores within a few years."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"suede","p":"noun","d":"Soft leather with a slightly rough, velvety surface on one side.","lb":"soft leather","s":["leather","chamois"],"k":["buckskin","calfskin","doeskin","lambskin"],"a":[],"ex":["My brother saved for months to buy a pair of brown suede shoes.","Water can leave marks on suede, so keep your jacket away from the rain.","The sofa was covered in soft grey suede that felt warm to the touch."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"suffice","p":"verb","d":"To be enough for a particular purpose or need.","lb":"be enough, satisfy","s":["be enough","do","serve","satisfy","be adequate","be sufficient"],"k":["be acceptable","cut it","fit","fulfil"],"a":["fall short","lack","be inadequate"],"ex":["A short email will suffice; you don't need to write a long letter.","Five hundred taka should suffice for the taxi fare and a snack.","A cup of tea and a biscuit will suffice for lunch today."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"suffrage","p":"noun","d":"The right to vote in political elections.","lb":"right to vote","s":["franchise","vote","ballot","voting rights","right to vote"],"k":["citizenship","democracy","electoral rights","political rights"],"a":[],"ex":["Women fought for suffrage for many decades before they won the right to vote.","Universal suffrage means that every adult citizen has the right to vote.","In civics class, we discussed why suffrage is considered a basic right in a democracy."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"suffuse","p":"verb","d":"To spread through or over something completely, as a colour, light, liquid or feeling does.","lb":"spread over, flood","s":["flood","pervade","permeate","imbue","bathe","saturate"],"k":["cloud","flush","penetrate","shade"],"a":["drain","bleach","fade"],"ex":["Golden light from the setting sun suffused the whole classroom.","Her face was suffused with joy when she opened the letter from the university.","The smell of fresh bread suffused the kitchen on Friday morning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"sui generis","p":"adjective","d":"Unique and different from all others, forming a class of its own.","lb":"unique, singular","s":["unique","one of a kind","unparalleled","singular","peerless","distinctive"],"k":["extraordinary","incomparable","one","one and only"],"a":["ordinary","common","typical","conventional"],"ex":["The artist's style is sui generis; no one can say which school it belongs to.","Lawyers argued that the case was sui generis, so older rulings did not apply.","Our old principal was a sui generis figure, strict yet funny, and nobody has replaced him."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"sullen","p":"adjective","d":"Silent and bad-tempered, showing that you are annoyed or unhappy.","lb":"sulky, gloomy","s":["sulky","moody","glum","morose","gloomy","brooding"],"k":["cloudy","dark","dejected","dour"],"a":["cheerful","friendly","happy","pleasant"],"ex":["The sullen teenager sat at the back of the car and refused to speak.","She gave a sullen shrug when her mother asked about school.","After losing the argument, he stayed sullen for the rest of the evening."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"sully","p":"verb","d":"To spoil the good quality or reputation of something, or to make it dirty.","lb":"stain, tarnish","s":["tarnish","stain","taint","blacken","defile","smear"],"k":["blemish","blob","blot","contaminate"],"a":["cleanse","purify","honor","clear"],"ex":["One careless post online can sully a student's reputation for years.","The scandal sullied the company's good name and cost it many customers.","I did not want to sully my new white shirt, so I ate carefully."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"summit","p":"noun","d":"The highest point of a mountain or hill.","lb":"mountaintop","s":["peak","top","crest","pinnacle","apex","crown"],"k":["acme","apogee","climax","elevation"],"a":["foot","base","bottom"],"ex":["After six hours of climbing, we finally reached the summit before sunrise.","Snow covered the summit even in the middle of summer.","From the summit, you can see the whole valley and the river below."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sumptuous","p":"adjective","d":"Very rich, grand and expensive-looking, especially of food, clothes or surroundings.","lb":"lavish, luxurious","s":["lavish","luxurious","opulent","splendid","rich","magnificent"],"k":["gilded","lush","palatial","princely"],"a":["plain","modest","simple","austere"],"ex":["The wedding guests enjoyed a sumptuous dinner of biryani, kebabs and sweet yogurt.","Our hotel room had a sumptuous bed with soft pillows and silk curtains.","The magazine showed sumptuous homes with marble floors and huge gardens."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"sundry","p":"adjective","d":"Of several different kinds, and not important enough to be listed separately.","lb":"various, assorted","s":["various","assorted","miscellaneous","diverse","varied","several"],"k":["different","heterogeneous","motley","multifaceted"],"a":["uniform","identical","same","single"],"ex":["The bag contained sundry items: pens, a torn map and an old key.","Sundry expenses such as stationery and snacks added up to a large sum.","She spent the afternoon dealing with sundry tasks that had piled up."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"supercilious","p":"adjective","d":"Behaving as if one is better than other people, often with a cold, scornful look or manner.","lb":"haughty, arrogant","s":["haughty","arrogant","condescending","disdainful","snobbish","patronizing"],"k":["imperious","lordly","overbearing","prideful"],"a":["humble","modest","respectful","unassuming"],"ex":["The supercilious waiter looked down at us because we ordered only tea.","He gave a supercilious smile when I asked him to explain the simple rule again.","Her supercilious tone made the new employees feel small and unwelcome."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"superficial","p":"adjective","d":"Not deep or thorough, dealing with only the obvious or outer part of something.","lb":"shallow, surface-level","s":["shallow","cursory","surface","perfunctory","hasty","slight"],"k":["apparent","brief","careless","casual"],"a":["thorough","deep","profound","detailed"],"ex":["He has only a superficial knowledge of cooking, so he follows every recipe word for word.","The doctor said the cut was superficial and only needed a clean bandage.","A superficial check of the report missed several serious mistakes in the budget figures."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"superfluous","p":"adjective","d":"More than is needed or wanted; not necessary.","lb":"unnecessary, excess","s":["unnecessary","excess","redundant","surplus","needless","extra"],"k":["dispensable","excessive","otiose","pointless"],"a":["necessary","essential","needed","vital"],"ex":["Cut every superfluous word from your essay so the main point is clear.","Buying a third phone charger felt superfluous, since I already had two at home.","The teacher said the extra decoration on the poster was superfluous."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"supersede","p":"verb","d":"To take the place of something older or less suitable, which is then no longer used.","lb":"replace, supplant","s":["replace","supplant","displace","succeed","override","take over from"],"k":["come after","eclipse","follow","outdate"],"a":["keep","retain","preserve","uphold"],"ex":["Mobile payment apps have superseded cash in many small shops.","The new timetable supersedes the one pinned on the notice board last month.","This version of the app supersedes all earlier ones, so please update it."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"supine","p":"adjective","d":"Lying flat on your back with your face upward.","lb":"on one's back","s":["reclining","horizontal","lying down","sprawled","laid out"],"k":["couchant","inactive","inert","languid"],"a":["prone","upright","erect"],"ex":["The nurse asked the patient to lie supine on the examination table.","He lay supine on the grass, watching the clouds drift across the sky.","In yoga class, we rest in a supine position at the end."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"supple","p":"adjective","d":"Bending or moving easily and gracefully; flexible and not stiff.","lb":"flexible, pliable","s":["flexible","pliable","limber","bendy","elastic","graceful"],"k":["adaptable","agile","lissome","malleable"],"a":["stiff","rigid","inflexible","unbending"],"ex":["Regular yoga keeps my back supple, even after long hours at a desk.","The shoemaker rubbed oil into the leather to keep it soft and supple.","The young dancer's supple body bent into shapes that amazed the audience."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"supplication","p":"noun","d":"A humble and sincere request for help or mercy, often made in prayer.","lb":"plea, entreaty","s":["plea","appeal","petition","prayer","request","begging"],"k":["application","beseeching","cry for help","genuflection"],"a":["demand","order","command","defiance"],"ex":["Her supplication to the judge for a second chance moved many people in the room.","He knelt in supplication, asking his elder brother for forgiveness.","The mother's tearful supplication to the doctors was to save her child."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"supposition","p":"noun","d":"Something that you believe is true without having proof, or the act of believing it.","lb":"assumption, guess","s":["assumption","guess","hypothesis","conjecture","presumption","speculation"],"k":["hunch","idea","notion","opinion"],"a":["fact","certainty","proof","knowledge"],"ex":["Your theory is only a supposition until someone collects real evidence.","We planned the picnic on the supposition that the weather would stay dry.","The police rejected the supposition that the fire had been started deliberately."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"suppress","p":"verb","d":"To stop something from continuing or from being shown or expressed, often by force or effort.","lb":"quash, stifle","s":["quash","crush","subdue","stifle","restrain","repress"],"k":["bottle up","check","conquer","contain"],"a":["allow","encourage","express","release"],"ex":["She tried to suppress a laugh when the teacher's chair squeaked loudly.","The company tried to suppress the news about the faulty batteries.","Some medicines suppress the immune system, so patients must avoid crowds."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"surface","p":"noun","d":"The outside or top layer of something.","lb":"outer layer, top","s":["exterior","outside","top","face","covering","skin"],"k":["artefact","artifact","coating","control surface"],"a":["interior","inside","depth","core"],"ex":["Wipe the table surface with a damp cloth before you start.","A thin layer of ice formed on the surface of the pond.","The road surface was damaged by the monsoon floods."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"surfeit","p":"noun","d":"An amount of something that is too much, especially of food, drink or any pleasure.","lb":"excess, glut","s":["excess","surplus","glut","overabundance","plethora","overload"],"k":["abundance","overdose","overindulgence","overkill"],"a":["shortage","lack","scarcity","deficiency"],"ex":["A surfeit of sweets at the festival left the children with stomach aches.","There is a surfeit of graduates in the city, so jobs are hard to find.","After a surfeit of social media, she decided to switch off her phone for a week."],"b":18,"y":0},{"w":"surmise","p":"verb","d":"To guess that something is true using the evidence you have, even though it is incomplete.","lb":"guess, infer","s":["guess","infer","suppose","conjecture","presume","assume"],"k":["believe","conclude","deduct","derive"],"a":["know","confirm","verify","prove"],"ex":["From the dark clouds, we surmised that the match would be canceled.","I surmise that she is angry, because she has not replied to any of my messages.","Police surmised from the broken window that the thief had entered at night."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"surplus","p":"noun","d":"An amount of something that is more than is needed or used.","lb":"excess, extra","s":["excess","surfeit","glut","overflow","remainder","leftover"],"k":["overabundance","overage","overload","overrun"],"a":["shortage","deficit","lack","shortfall"],"ex":["The farmers had a surplus of rice, so they sold the extra in the city.","The shop sold its surplus stock at half price at the end of the season.","The government announced a budget surplus after collecting more tax than expected."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"surreal","p":"adjective","d":"Strange and dreamlike, so that it does not seem real.","lb":"dreamlike, bizarre","s":["dreamlike","bizarre","unreal","fantastic","weird","strange"],"k":["eccentric","freaky","gonzo","outlandish"],"a":["ordinary","realistic","normal","mundane"],"ex":["Walking through the empty streets at dawn felt surreal, like a scene from a dream.","It was surreal to see my own name on the merit list.","The painter's surreal landscapes show clocks melting and fish floating through the sky."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"surreptitious","p":"adjective","d":"Done secretly and carefully so that no one notices.","lb":"secret, stealthy","s":["secret","stealthy","furtive","covert","sneaky","clandestine"],"k":["concealed","private","sneak","undercover"],"a":["open","public","honest","blatant"],"ex":["He took a surreptitious glance at his phone during the lecture.","She slipped a surreptitious note to her friend across the classroom.","The child made a surreptitious grab for the last biscuit when no one was looking."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"surreptitiously","p":"adverb","d":"In a secret, quiet way, so that other people do not notice.","lb":"secretly, stealthily","s":["secretly","stealthily","covertly","quietly","in secret","on the sly"],"k":["behind someone's back","by stealth","discreetly","hush-hush"],"a":["openly","publicly","blatantly","overtly"],"ex":["During the lecture, he surreptitiously checked his phone under the desk.","She surreptitiously slipped a note into her friend's bag before class.","The boy surreptitiously fed the stray cat from his plate under the table."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"surrogate","p":"noun","d":"A person or thing that takes the place of another, or acts on someone's behalf.","lb":"substitute, stand-in","s":["substitute","replacement","proxy","deputy","understudy","representative"],"k":["agent","alternate","backup","backup man"],"a":[],"ex":["Teachers sometimes become surrogate parents for students who live far from home.","The injured captain sent a younger player as his surrogate to the awards ceremony.","Many people use social media as a surrogate for real conversations with friends."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"susceptible","p":"adjective","d":"Easily affected, influenced or harmed by something.","lb":"exposed, vulnerable","s":["vulnerable","prone","liable","subject","open","sensitive"],"k":["allergic","amenable","apt","at risk"],"a":["immune","resistant","invulnerable","unaffected"],"ex":["Babies are more susceptible to colds during the winter months.","If you skip sleep before exams, you become susceptible to careless mistakes.","Old laptops are more susceptible to viruses, so keep your software updated."],"b":544,"y":0},{"w":"svelte","p":"adjective","d":"Slim, smooth and elegant in shape, in an attractive way.","lb":"slim, graceful","s":["slender","slim","graceful","sleek","willowy","trim"],"k":["elegant","fine-boned","petite","shapely"],"a":["stocky","heavy","bulky","plump"],"ex":["The dancer looked svelte in her simple blue dress.","After months of swimming and walking, he became noticeably more svelte.","The new phone has a svelte design that slips easily into a pocket."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"sweeping","p":"adjective","d":"Wide in range or effect, affecting or including very many things or people.","lb":"far-reaching, broad","s":["extensive","broad","comprehensive","wholesale","radical","thorough"],"k":["across-the-board","all-embracing","blanket","broad-brush"],"a":["limited","narrow","minor","slight"],"ex":["The principal announced a sweeping reform of the school's exam schedule.","The company made sweeping cuts to its budget, and almost every department was affected.","The new law gives inspectors sweeping powers to check food factories."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"swept","p":"verb","d":"Past form of sweep: cleaned with a broom, or moved quickly and forcefully across a place.","lb":"cleaned, rushed","s":["brushed","cleaned","scoured","raced","surged","rushed"],"k":["careered","carried","hurtled","swooped"],"a":[],"ex":["Mum swept the front yard every morning before the guests arrived.","A strong wind swept across the open field and blew the hats away.","The news swept through the school within minutes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"swiftly","p":"adverb","d":"Very quickly; in a short time.","lb":"quickly, rapidly","s":["quickly","rapidly","speedily","fast","briskly","promptly"],"k":["apace","hurriedly","in a flash","in short order"],"a":["slowly","gradually","leisurely"],"ex":["The river flowed swiftly after the heavy rain upstream.","The nurse acted swiftly when the patient suddenly fainted.","News spreads swiftly on social media, whether it is true or not."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"sycophant","p":"noun","d":"A person who praises powerful people too much in order to gain an advantage for themselves.","lb":"flatterer, yes-man","s":["flatterer","toady","bootlicker","lackey","parasite"],"k":["apple-polisher","claqueur","crawler","flunky"],"a":["critic","rebel"],"ex":["The director was surrounded by sycophants who praised every idea, however bad.","A true friend tells you the truth, while a sycophant only says what you want to hear.","He is a sycophant who laughs loudly at every joke his boss makes."],"b":530,"y":0},{"w":"synthesis","p":"noun","d":"The combining of different ideas or parts to form a new whole.","lb":"combination, blend","s":["combination","blend","fusion","merger","union","integration"],"k":["amalgam","assembly","chemical action","chemical change"],"a":["analysis","separation","division","breakdown"],"ex":["Her thesis is a synthesis of ideas from biology and computer science.","The restaurant's menu is a synthesis of Bengali and Thai flavors.","The report offers a synthesis of what ten different studies found about sleep."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"systemic","p":"adjective","d":"Affecting or involving the whole of a system, organization or body, not just one part.","lb":"widespread, system-wide","s":["widespread","pervasive","general","overall","fundamental","institutional"],"k":["broad","common","embedded","entrenched"],"a":["local","isolated","localized","superficial"],"ex":["Late deliveries are a systemic problem, not just the fault of one careless driver.","The infection became systemic and spread through the patient’s whole body.","Auditors found systemic weaknesses in how the bank checks new accounts."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"tacit","p":"adjective","d":"Understood or meant without being said openly.","lb":"implied, unspoken","s":["implied","unspoken","implicit","understood","unstated","silent"],"k":["assumed","mute","presumed","suggested"],"a":["explicit","stated","spoken","express"],"ex":["There was a tacit agreement among the roommates that nobody would cook on Fridays.","Her silence was taken as tacit approval of the plan.","The teacher gave tacit permission by looking away when students whispered in class."],"b":91,"y":1},{"w":"taciturn","p":"adjective","d":"Not talking much; quiet and reserved, especially around other people.","lb":"reserved, quiet","s":["reserved","quiet","silent","reticent","uncommunicative","laconic"],"k":["aloof","concise","guarded","hushed"],"a":["talkative","chatty","communicative","garrulous"],"ex":["My taciturn uncle can sit through a whole family dinner without saying ten words.","The taciturn driver answered every question with a nod or a single word.","She is taciturn at school but chatters happily with her close friends."],"b":530,"y":0},{"w":"tactical","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the careful plans and actions used to achieve a short-term goal, especially in war or sport.","lb":"strategic, planned","s":["strategic","calculated","planned","deliberate","shrewd","clever"],"k":["expedient","intended","maneuvering","operational"],"a":["unplanned","random","impulsive","haphazard"],"ex":["The coach made a tactical change at half-time by moving a defender to the wing.","The army's tactical withdrawal from the hill saved many lives.","One careless move was a tactical error that cost her the chess match."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"taint","p":"noun","d":"A trace of something bad or spoiled that damages the quality or reputation of something.","lb":"stain, blemish","s":["stain","blemish","stigma","smear","contamination","blot"],"k":["disgrace","impurity","mark","scandal"],"a":["purity","honor","innocence"],"ex":["The taint of the scandal followed the company for years.","There was a taint in the water that made the tea taste strange.","No one wanted to buy meat with even a slight taint of spoilage."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"tangential","p":"adjective","d":"Only slightly connected to the main subject, and so not really relevant to it.","lb":"irrelevant, peripheral","s":["peripheral","irrelevant","incidental","secondary","marginal","unrelated"],"k":["auxiliary","beside the point","divergent","extraneous"],"a":["relevant","central","pertinent","germane"],"ex":["Her comments about the weather were tangential to the discussion on the budget.","The lawyer objected that the question was tangential and did not help the court.","Let's skip the tangential details and focus on the main problem."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"tangible","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be touched, or real and clear enough to be noticed and measured.","lb":"real, touchable","s":["palpable","concrete","solid","real","physical","material"],"k":["actual","apparent","clear","corporeal"],"a":["intangible","abstract","imaginary","unreal"],"ex":["The museum lets children handle tangible objects, such as old coins and clay pots, instead of only reading about them.","After months of practice, Tania saw tangible progress when her test scores rose by twenty points.","The police could not arrest him because they had no tangible evidence, only rumors."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"tantamount","p":"adjective","d":"Having the same effect or meaning as something worse or more serious.","lb":"equivalent, equal","s":["equivalent","equal","as good as","synonymous","identical","comparable"],"k":["akin","in all but name","in effect","matching"],"a":["different","unlike","dissimilar","distinct"],"ex":["Resigning now would be tantamount to admitting that you made a mistake.","For a small shop, losing its only supplier is tantamount to closing down.","Her silence was tantamount to agreement, so the team went ahead with the plan."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"taut","p":"adjective","d":"Pulled tight, with no slack; also tense and nervous.","lb":"tight, stretched","s":["tight","stretched","rigid","tense","strained","firm"],"k":["edgy","high-strung","nervy","springy"],"a":["slack","loose","limp","relaxed"],"ex":["He pulled the rope taut and tied it to the tree.","The tent canvas was stretched taut across the poles.","His face was taut with worry as he waited for the results."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"tautological","p":"adjective","d":"Saying the same thing twice in different words, so that the second part adds nothing.","lb":"redundant, circular","s":["redundant","repetitive","circular","repetitious","superfluous","wordy"],"k":["duplicative","extra","iterative","overlapping"],"a":["concise","succinct","terse"],"ex":["Saying free gift is tautological, because a gift is already free.","The advertisement was tautological, claiming that the product was fresh and new.","His explanation was tautological: he said the rule exists because that is the rule."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"tedium","p":"noun","d":"The feeling of being bored because something is dull, slow or repeated for a long time.","lb":"boredom, monotony","s":["boredom","monotony","dullness","drudgery","ennui","sameness"],"k":["dissatisfaction","drabness","dreariness","flatness"],"a":["excitement","interest","thrill","stimulation"],"ex":["The tedium of the long bus journey was broken only by a stop for tea.","Filling in forms by hand was pure tedium.","To escape the tedium of load-shedding evenings, we played cards by candlelight."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"teem","p":"verb","d":"To be full of living things or people moving about in large numbers.","lb":"swarm, abound","s":["swarm","abound","crawl","bristle","overflow","throng"],"k":["abound in","buzz","hum","pour"],"a":["lack","be devoid of","be bare"],"ex":["The market teems with shoppers on Friday evenings.","The pond behind our house teems with tiny fish after the monsoon.","Online forums teem with advice, but not all of it is reliable."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"teeming","p":"adjective","d":"Completely full of people, animals or other living things moving about.","lb":"swarming, crowded","s":["swarming","crowded","packed","bustling","abundant","overflowing"],"k":["alive","full","infested","jammed"],"a":["empty","deserted","bare","barren"],"ex":["The pond behind our house is teeming with tiny fish after the rains.","The railway station was teeming with passengers on the day before Eid.","Rotting garbage left the drain teeming with flies and mosquitoes."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"teller","p":"noun","d":"A bank employee who deals with customers' deposits, withdrawals and payments at a counter.","lb":"bank clerk","s":["bank clerk","cashier","counter clerk","bank employee","bank officer","clerk"],"k":["banker","cash handler","money handler","narrator"],"a":[],"ex":["The teller counted my cash twice before giving me the receipt.","I asked the bank teller how long it would take for the cheque to clear.","Nadia worked as a teller during her summer break to save money for university."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"temerity","p":"noun","d":"Reckless boldness; the nerve to do something that other people would not dare to do.","lb":"nerve, audacity","s":["audacity","nerve","boldness","gall","cheek","effrontery"],"k":["cheekiness","chutzpah","courage","daring"],"a":["caution","timidity","prudence","fear"],"ex":["He had the temerity to ask the principal for a longer holiday.","Nobody expected the new intern to have the temerity to correct the director.","She laughed at his temerity in challenging the national chess champion."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"temperament","p":"noun","d":"A person's natural character, especially how calm, angry or cheerful they usually are.","lb":"nature, disposition","s":["nature","disposition","character","personality","temper","mood"],"k":["bent","frame of mind","humor","inclination"],"a":[],"ex":["My brother has a calm temperament and never loses his patience.","A fiery temperament made her quick to argue but also quick to forgive.","Teachers need a gentle temperament to work with very young children."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"temperate","p":"adjective","d":"Mild and moderate, not extreme, whether in weather or in behavior.","lb":"mild, moderate","s":["mild","moderate","balanced","gentle","restrained","clement"],"k":["abstemious","balmy","cautious","equable"],"a":["extreme","harsh","severe","excessive"],"ex":["Many European countries have a temperate climate, with neither extreme heat nor extreme cold.","Rafi is temperate in his habits: he eats lightly, sleeps early and avoids wasteful spending.","The teacher's temperate reply calmed the angry parents instead of making them angrier."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"temporal","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to time, or to ordinary worldly life rather than spiritual matters.","lb":"time-related, worldly","s":["chronological","secular","worldly","earthly","mundane","material"],"k":["economic","materialistic","profane","sophisticated"],"a":["eternal","spiritual","timeless","spatial"],"ex":["The story follows temporal order, moving from morning to night.","Scientists study the temporal changes in the river's width across ten years.","Patients with the condition may become confused about temporal details, such as the day or month."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"temporize","p":"verb","d":"To delay making a decision or giving a clear answer in order to gain time.","lb":"stall, hedge","s":["stall","hedge","procrastinate","delay","equivocate","play for time"],"k":["beat around the bush","defer","dilly-dally","draw out"],"a":["decide","commit","act","resolve"],"ex":["When I asked for a refund, the manager temporized and said he would think about it.","He temporized for weeks instead of telling his parents he wanted to change his course.","The committee temporized, asking for more reports instead of voting."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"tempt","p":"verb","d":"To make someone want to do or have something, especially something they should not.","lb":"lure, appeal to","s":["entice","lure","attract","tantalize","seduce","coax"],"k":["allure","captivate","charm","draw"],"a":["deter","repel","discourage","put off"],"ex":["The bakery window tempted me to buy a cake even though I was on a diet.","Don't let a free phone game tempt you away from your homework.","I was tempted to skip class and join my friends at the cricket ground."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"tenable","p":"adjective","d":"Able to be defended with good reasons; reasonable enough to be believed or kept.","lb":"defensible, valid","s":["defensible","justifiable","sound","reasonable","plausible","viable"],"k":["arguable","believable","fair","feasible"],"a":["untenable","indefensible","unsound","unreasonable"],"ex":["His claim that the exam was unfair is not tenable, since every student received the same paper.","After the new evidence appeared, the theory was no longer tenable.","In a debate, you need a tenable argument supported by facts, not just strong feelings."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"tenacious","p":"adjective","d":"Holding firmly to something and refusing to give up, even when it is difficult.","lb":"persistent, determined","s":["persistent","determined","resolute","stubborn","dogged","unyielding"],"k":["adhesive","coherent","continual","dour"],"a":["irresolute","yielding","weak","indecisive"],"ex":["Thanks to her tenacious effort, Sadia finally passed the admission test on her third try.","The tenacious reporter kept asking questions until the officials gave her a straight answer.","A tenacious weed had grown through the crack in the concrete and refused to die."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"tenant","p":"noun","d":"A person who pays rent to the owner of a house, flat, shop or land in order to use it.","lb":"renter, occupant","s":["renter","lodger","leaseholder","occupant","lessee","boarder"],"k":["householder","inhabitant","occupant of the flat","resident"],"a":["landlord","landlady","owner","proprietor"],"ex":["Our tenant on the second floor pays the rent on the first day of every month.","The tenants complained to the landlord about the broken lift and the leaking water pipe.","As a new tenant, check the flat's wiring and taps before you sign the contract."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"tenet","p":"noun","d":"A principle or belief, especially one of the main beliefs of a group or system.","lb":"principle, belief","s":["principle","belief","doctrine","creed","conviction","precept"],"k":["article of faith","axiom","church doctrine","credo"],"a":[],"ex":["Honesty is a basic tenet of our family, and lying is never excused.","A central tenet of good teaching is that students learn best by doing.","The club’s first tenet is that every member has an equal voice."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"tentative","p":"adjective","d":"Not certain or final; made or done carefully because one is unsure.","lb":"uncertain, provisional","s":["provisional","uncertain","hesitant","cautious","unconfirmed","preliminary"],"k":["conditional","doubtful","indecisive","probationary"],"a":["definite","confident","firm","final"],"ex":["We made tentative plans to meet on Friday, but I will confirm closer to the day.","The two companies reached a tentative agreement, which still needs the directors' approval.","She gave a tentative smile, unsure whether the stranger was friendly."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"tenuous","p":"adjective","d":"Weak, thin or slight, with little strength or evidence to support it.","lb":"flimsy, weak","s":["flimsy","weak","slight","shaky","fragile","thin"],"k":["delicate","faint","feeble","frail"],"a":["strong","solid","firm","substantial"],"ex":["The link between the two events is tenuous, so we cannot say one caused the other.","The team held a tenuous lead of one point until the final minute.","Their friendship became tenuous after he moved abroad and stopped replying to messages."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"tepid","p":"adjective","d":"Slightly warm, especially when it should be hot or cold; or showing little enthusiasm.","lb":"lukewarm, half-hearted","s":["lukewarm","cool","indifferent","apathetic","mild"],"k":["aloof","barely warm","blah","cold"],"a":["hot","boiling","enthusiastic","eager"],"ex":["The tea had gone tepid while I was talking, so I asked for a fresh cup.","A tepid shower is better than a cold one when you have a fever.","The audience gave only tepid applause after the long, boring speech."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"terminal","p":"noun","d":"A building or place where bus, train, ferry or air passengers begin or end their journeys.","lb":"station, depot","s":["station","depot","terminus","stop","interchange","end of the line"],"k":["airport building","bus station","concourse","end"],"a":[],"ex":["We waited at the bus terminal for two hours because the roads were flooded.","The airport's new terminal has more shops, seats and charging points.","Passengers hurried to the ferry terminal to catch the last boat to the island."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"terrestrial","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to the Earth or to land, rather than to water or air.","lb":"earthly, land-based","s":["earthly","earthbound","worldly","mundane","secular"],"k":["onshore","overland","pedestrian","planetary"],"a":["aquatic","celestial","extraterrestrial","marine"],"ex":["Frogs live partly in water, but tigers are fully terrestrial animals.","Terrestrial planets like Earth and Mars are made mostly of rock, unlike gas giants.","Many villages still receive terrestrial TV signals through an antenna on the roof."],"b":68,"y":1},{"w":"terse","p":"adjective","d":"Using very few words, often in a way that sounds rude or unfriendly.","lb":"brief, curt","s":["curt","brief","short","abrupt","brusque","clipped"],"k":["crisp","cryptic","discourteous","fleeting"],"a":["wordy","verbose","chatty","rambling"],"ex":["When I asked why he was late, his terse reply was “Traffic.”","The manager sent a terse email that said only, “Report due Monday.”","Her terse text message made me wonder whether she was upset with me."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"theology","p":"noun","d":"The study of God and religious beliefs.","lb":"religious study","s":["divinity","religious studies","doctrine","dogma","religious thought","religious philosophy"],"k":["bailiwick","belief","creed","discipline"],"a":[],"ex":["She studied theology at university to understand how different faiths explain the nature of God.","A theology class often involves discussing sacred texts and ethical questions.","The professor of theology gave a talk on how religion and science can learn from each other."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"thorny","p":"adjective","d":"Full of difficulties or hard to deal with, usually because it causes disagreement.","lb":"difficult, problematic","s":["difficult","tricky","problematic","knotty","awkward","delicate"],"k":["armed","barbed","catchy","challenging"],"a":["easy","simple","straightforward","uncomplicated"],"ex":["Dividing the family land among five brothers turned into a thorny issue.","The teacher answered a thorny question about exam marks very carefully.","The committee faced the thorny problem of raising fees without upsetting parents."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"threshold","p":"noun","d":"The bottom of a doorway that you step over; also the point where something new begins.","lb":"doorway, starting point","s":["doorstep","doorway","entrance","sill","entry","verge"],"k":["access","borderline","cutoff","door"],"a":["end","exit","conclusion"],"ex":["She stood on the threshold, waiting for someone to invite her inside.","The bride crossed the threshold of her new home with a smile.","The young scientist is on the threshold of an important discovery."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"thrifty","p":"adjective","d":"Careful about spending money and not wasting things.","lb":"frugal, economical","s":["frugal","economical","careful","sparing","prudent","saving"],"k":["cautious","cheap","parsimonious","penny-pinching"],"a":["wasteful","extravagant","spendthrift","lavish"],"ex":["My thrifty mother turns leftover rice into a tasty snack instead of throwing it away.","Thrifty students buy second-hand textbooks to save money.","Being thrifty doesn't mean being stingy; it means spending wisely."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"thriving","p":"adjective","d":"Growing, developing or succeeding very well.","lb":"flourishing, prosperous","s":["flourishing","prosperous","booming","successful","healthy","blooming"],"k":["buoyant","burgeoning","on the rise","prospering"],"a":["failing","struggling","declining","dying"],"ex":["My uncle runs a thriving bakery that sells out of bread every morning.","The thriving market near the bus stand is crowded from dawn until night.","A thriving garden on the roof gives us tomatoes and chilies all year."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"throng","p":"noun","d":"A large crowd of people packed closely together.","lb":"crowd, multitude","s":["crowd","mass","horde","multitude","swarm","crush"],"k":["drove","gang","heap","jam"],"a":["handful","few","scattering"],"ex":["A throng of shoppers filled the market on the last day before Eid.","The singer pushed through the throng of fans waiting outside the hotel.","We got lost in the throng at the book fair and had to call each other."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"throttle","p":"verb","d":"To reduce the speed, flow or growth of something; also to choke someone by squeezing their throat.","lb":"choke, restrict","s":["choke","strangle","suppress","restrict","curb","stifle"],"k":["confine","control","hold back","quell"],"a":["boost","increase","release","accelerate"],"ex":["The driver throttled back as the road became slippery after the rain.","High taxes can throttle the growth of small businesses.","The wire wrapped around the vine and slowly throttled the young plant."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"thwart","p":"verb","d":"To prevent someone from doing something, or to stop a plan from succeeding.","lb":"foil, frustrate","s":["foil","frustrate","block","prevent","stop","obstruct"],"k":["bilk","blockade","cross","double cross"],"a":["help","assist","aid","support"],"ex":["Heavy rain thwarted our plan for a picnic by the river.","The security guard thwarted the theft by locking the gate in time.","A broken laptop thwarted his attempt to finish the assignment on time."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"timbre","p":"noun","d":"The quality of a sound that makes a voice or instrument sound different from others, even at the same pitch.","lb":"tone, sound quality","s":["tone","tone color","resonance","quality","sound","character"],"k":["sonority","sound color","sound property","tonal quality"],"a":[],"ex":["Although both singers hit the same note, the timbre of their voices was completely different.","The cello has a rich, warm timbre that suits sad songs.","I recognized my father's voice on the phone by its deep timbre."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"timidity","p":"noun","d":"A lack of courage or confidence, especially in dealing with new people or situations.","lb":"shyness, fearfulness","s":["shyness","nervousness","diffidence","meekness","cowardice"],"k":["fear","fright","hesitancy","mousiness"],"a":["boldness","courage","confidence","audacity"],"ex":["His timidity kept him from raising his hand, even when he knew the answer.","Years of timidity disappeared once she joined the debate club.","The puppy's timidity made it hide whenever visitors came to the house."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"timorous","p":"adjective","d":"Easily frightened; shy and lacking the courage to act.","lb":"timid, fearful","s":["timid","fearful","afraid","nervous","shy","apprehensive"],"k":["anxious","bashful","frightened","hesitant"],"a":["bold","brave","fearless","confident"],"ex":["The timorous kitten hid under the bed whenever visitors came.","He gave a timorous knock on the principal's door and waited.","Too timorous to speak in class, Mina wrote her ideas in a notebook instead."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"tirade","p":"noun","d":"A long, angry speech that criticizes or blames someone or something.","lb":"rant, outburst","s":["rant","diatribe","harangue","outburst","broadside","lecture"],"k":["fulmination","invective","jeremiad","philippic"],"a":["praise","compliment","tribute"],"ex":["The customer launched into a tirade about the slow service and the cold food.","Our coach delivered a ten-minute tirade after we lost the match.","When the electricity went out again, my uncle broke into a tirade against load-shedding."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"titillate","p":"verb","d":"To excite someone's interest or senses in a mild, teasing and pleasurable way.","lb":"excite, tease","s":["excite","stimulate","intrigue","tease","arouse","entice"],"k":["inspire","provoke","shake","shake up"],"a":["bore","repel","disgust"],"ex":["The movie trailer was cut to titillate viewers without giving away the ending.","Tabloid headlines titillate readers with gossip about the private lives of film stars.","A mysterious poster in the corridor titillated the students' curiosity for days."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"titular","p":"adjective","d":"Having a title or position in name only, without real power or duties.","lb":"nominal, token","s":["nominal","so-called","formal","token","ceremonial","honorary"],"k":["figurehead","front man","honorific","minimal"],"a":["actual","real","effective","working"],"ex":["The queen is the titular head of the country, but elected leaders make the real decisions.","He was the titular manager, while his deputy did all of the actual work.","As the titular president of the club, she attended ceremonies but never made financial decisions."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"toil","p":"noun","d":"Long, hard and tiring work.","lb":"labor, drudgery","s":["labor","drudgery","effort","exertion","grind","hard work"],"k":["brunt work","donkey work","drudge","elbow grease"],"a":["leisure","rest","ease","idleness"],"ex":["After years of toil in the fields, the farmer finally bought his own land.","The success of the small restaurant came from years of daily toil.","Her mother's daily toil paid for her university fees."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"torpid","p":"adjective","d":"Slow, lazy and without energy, either in body or in mind.","lb":"sluggish, lethargic","s":["sluggish","lethargic","inactive","slow","dull","apathetic"],"k":["asleep","dormant","drowsy","hibernating"],"a":["active","energetic","lively","alert"],"ex":["After a heavy Eid lunch, everyone lay torpid on the sofas.","The heat made the whole town torpid, and even the street dogs lay still.","Frogs become torpid in cold weather and hardly move at all."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"torpor","p":"noun","d":"A state of physical or mental sluggishness in which you feel unable to move or care about anything.","lb":"lethargy, sluggishness","s":["lethargy","inertia","languor","apathy","drowsiness","dullness"],"k":["inactivity","indifference","indolence","lassitude"],"a":["energy","vigor","activity","alertness"],"ex":["The heavy lunch left everyone in the office in a state of torpor.","A long, hot summer afternoon can sink the whole village into torpor.","After weeks without exercise, a torpor settled over him and even small tasks felt hard."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"tortuous","p":"adjective","d":"Full of twists and turns, either in shape or in complicated, confusing steps.","lb":"winding, convoluted","s":["winding","twisting","convoluted","circuitous","serpentine","meandering"],"k":["complicated","crooked","devious","indirect"],"a":["straight","direct","straightforward","simple"],"ex":["The bus climbed the tortuous mountain road, and many passengers felt sick.","Renewing a passport was a tortuous process involving five different offices.","The tortuous path through the old bazaar confused every first-time visitor."],"b":37,"y":0},{"w":"touchstone","p":"noun","d":"A standard or measure against which the quality or value of other things can be judged.","lb":"standard, benchmark","s":["benchmark","standard","yardstick","criterion","gauge","measure"],"k":["barometer","bellwether","exemplar","litmus"],"a":[],"ex":["For many readers, that novel is the touchstone against which all other mysteries are judged.","Honesty is the touchstone of a good friendship.","The old tea stall's milk tea became the touchstone by which we judged every other tea in town."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"tout","p":"verb","d":"To praise something strongly and publicly, usually to persuade people to like or buy it.","lb":"promote, praise","s":["promote","advertise","hype","publicize","push","extol"],"k":["ballyhoo","boast","endorse","flog"],"a":["criticize","disparage","downplay","belittle"],"ex":["The company touts its new phone as the fastest one it has ever made.","Hotels tout their free breakfast and fast Wi-Fi to attract business travelers.","The coaching center touts its high admission-test success rate on every poster."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"toxic","p":"adjective","d":"Poisonous and able to cause serious harm or death.","lb":"poisonous, harmful","s":["poisonous","harmful","deadly","noxious","venomous","lethal"],"k":["contagious","contaminated","infectious","injurious"],"a":["harmless","safe","nontoxic","healthy"],"ex":["Never mix cleaning products, because some combinations make toxic fumes.","Toxic waste from the factory polluted the nearby canal.","Some wild mushrooms look harmless but are highly toxic."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"tractable","p":"adjective","d":"Easy to manage, control or persuade, and willing to do what you are told.","lb":"docile, manageable","s":["docile","manageable","compliant","obedient","amenable","cooperative"],"k":["accommodating","agreeable","biddable","dutiful"],"a":["stubborn","unmanageable","obstinate","unruly"],"ex":["The new puppy was tractable and learned to sit within two days.","Copper is a tractable metal that can easily be bent into wire.","Once the changes were explained clearly, the tractable client agreed to them."],"b":11,"y":0},{"w":"tranquility","p":"noun","d":"A calm, peaceful state, free from noise, worry or disturbance.","lb":"calm, peace","s":["calm","peace","serenity","stillness","quiet","peacefulness"],"k":["equanimity","halcyon calm","harmony","hush"],"a":["turmoil","chaos","agitation","disturbance"],"ex":["We enjoyed the tranquility of the village after a noisy week in Dhaka.","Early in the morning, the lake has a tranquility that no photograph can capture.","Meditation helped her find some tranquility during the stressful exam season."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"transcend","p":"verb","d":"To go beyond the limits of something, or to be greater or better than it.","lb":"surpass, rise above","s":["surpass","exceed","outdo","rise above","overcome","outstrip"],"k":["beat","best","better","outperform"],"a":["fall short of","sink to","succumb to","lag behind"],"ex":["Good music can transcend language, so people enjoy songs they cannot understand.","The athlete transcended her injury and won the race by a clear margin.","True friendship transcends differences in age, money and background."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"transfix","p":"verb","d":"To make someone so amazed, frightened or interested that they cannot move or look away.","lb":"mesmerize, rivet","s":["fascinate","captivate","rivet","paralyze","hypnotize","petrify"],"k":["absorb","arrest","bewitch","charm"],"a":["bore","repel"],"ex":["The children sat transfixed as the magician pulled a rabbit from his hat.","A glowing meteor streaked across the sky and transfixed everyone on the rooftop.","She was transfixed by the news on her phone and forgot her tea."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"transgress","p":"verb","d":"To break a rule, law or moral limit.","lb":"violate, break","s":["violate","break","breach","infringe","offend","disobey"],"k":["crack","defy","do wrong","err"],"a":["obey","comply","observe","follow"],"ex":["Students who transgress the exam rules may be banned from the hall.","The company was fined for transgressing environmental laws by dumping waste in the river.","He felt he had transgressed an unwritten rule by reading his friend's messages."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"transgression","p":"noun","d":"An act that breaks a law, a rule or a moral principle.","lb":"violation, offense","s":["violation","offense","breach","wrongdoing","sin","infringement"],"k":["error","indiscretion","infraction","lapse"],"a":["obedience","compliance","observance","virtue"],"ex":["Copying homework is a serious transgression of the school's honesty rules.","He apologized for his earlier transgression and promised to follow the rules.","Parking in front of a hospital gate is a minor transgression that carries a heavy fine."],"b":5,"y":0},{"w":"transient","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting only a short time, or staying in a place only briefly.","lb":"temporary, fleeting","s":["temporary","brief","fleeting","passing","momentary","ephemeral"],"k":["drifting","evanescent","flitting","itinerant"],"a":["permanent","lasting","enduring","stable"],"ex":["The pain was transient and disappeared after a few minutes of rest.","Online fame can be transient, because a viral video is often forgotten within weeks.","The hostel mostly houses transient guests who stay only a night or two."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"transitory","p":"adjective","d":"Lasting only a short time and soon passing away.","lb":"temporary, fleeting","s":["temporary","brief","fleeting","passing","momentary","ephemeral"],"k":["ethereal","evanescent","fickle","flitting"],"a":["permanent","lasting","enduring","eternal"],"ex":["The fame of a viral video is often transitory and forgotten within a week.","Her anger was transitory and had disappeared by dinner.","Teenage trends are transitory; what is popular today may look silly next year."],"b":10,"y":0},{"w":"trauma","p":"noun","d":"A very upsetting experience that causes lasting emotional pain, or a serious physical injury.","lb":"shock, distress","s":["shock","distress","anguish","ordeal","suffering","injury"],"k":["affliction","agony","breakdown","damage"],"a":["recovery","comfort","calm"],"ex":["The accident left her with trauma that made her afraid to ride in cars.","Counselors help children cope with the trauma of losing their homes in a flood.","He needed surgery for head trauma after falling from the roof."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"travesty","p":"noun","d":"Something so poor or unfair that it seems a ridiculous and shameful imitation of what it should be.","lb":"mockery, farce","s":["mockery","farce","parody","caricature","sham","distortion"],"k":["botch","charade","debacle","farce comedy"],"a":[],"ex":["Giving the prize to the student who copied the answers was a travesty.","The film was such a travesty of the original novel that many readers walked out of the cinema.","Many viewers called the referee's decision a travesty of fair play."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"trenchant","p":"adjective","d":"Expressed in a sharp, forceful and clear way, especially when criticizing something.","lb":"sharp, incisive","s":["incisive","cutting","biting","sharp","penetrating","pointed"],"k":["astute","clear","distinct","effective"],"a":["vague","mild","feeble","bland"],"ex":["The critic wrote a trenchant review that exposed every weakness in the plot.","Her trenchant questions forced the committee to explain exactly how the money was spent.","In his trenchant essay, Karim explained why the city's bus system keeps failing."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"trepidation","p":"noun","d":"A feeling of fear or nervous worry about something that is about to happen.","lb":"fear, apprehension","s":["apprehension","anxiety","dread","fear","unease","nervousness"],"k":["butterflies","jitters","misgiving","qualm"],"a":["calm","confidence","composure","courage"],"ex":["Nadia opened her exam results with trepidation, afraid that she had missed her target score.","He approached the dentist's chair with trepidation, gripping the armrests tightly.","There was some trepidation among the staff when the manager called a surprise meeting."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"trifling","p":"adjective","d":"Of very little importance, value or size.","lb":"trivial, unimportant","s":["trivial","petty","minor","insignificant","unimportant","negligible"],"k":["footling","measly","niggling","nugatory"],"a":["important","significant","serious","weighty"],"ex":["They quarreled over a trifling matter, like who should wash the cups.","The repair cost a trifling sum, so we fixed the fan the same day.","Don't worry about trifling mistakes in your first draft; you can fix them later."],"b":66,"y":2},{"w":"triumvirate","p":"noun","d":"A group of three powerful people who share control or leadership.","lb":"trio, ruling group","s":["trio","threesome","triad","trinity","three"],"k":["leash","ternion","trey","triarchy"],"a":[],"ex":["A triumvirate of experienced teachers ran the school after the principal retired.","In ancient Rome, a triumvirate of three men shared control of the republic.","The club is led by a triumvirate made up of the president, treasurer and coach."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"trivial","p":"adjective","d":"Of very little importance or value.","lb":"unimportant, minor","s":["unimportant","minor","insignificant","petty","trifling","negligible"],"k":["fiddling","footling","frivolous","little"],"a":["important","significant","major","serious"],"ex":["Don't waste time arguing over trivial details when the main plan is clear.","Their quarrel started over something trivial, like who would wash the dishes.","A trivial spelling mistake will not lower your whole grade."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"truculence","p":"noun","d":"A readiness to argue or fight, shown through a rude, hostile and defiant manner.","lb":"belligerence, hostility","s":["aggression","hostility","defiance","bad temper","ferocity"],"k":["aggressiveness","bellicosity","bloody-mindedness","contentiousness"],"a":["gentleness","meekness","friendliness"],"ex":["Her truculence in meetings made the team dread every discussion.","She answered every question with such truculence that the interviewer ended the meeting early.","His truculence at the bank counter made the other customers nervous."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"truculent","p":"adjective","d":"Aggressive and ready to argue or fight, often in a rude, defiant way.","lb":"aggressive, defiant","s":["belligerent","hostile","aggressive","combative","bellicose","pugnacious"],"k":["argumentative","bullish","combatant","contentious"],"a":["peaceable","gentle","friendly","cooperative"],"ex":["The truculent customer shouted at the cashier before anyone had said a word.","My little brother gets truculent whenever we ask him to switch off the TV.","The truculent driver jumped out of his car and argued over a tiny scratch."],"b":12,"y":0},{"w":"tryst","p":"noun","d":"A secret meeting between lovers, usually arranged for a particular time and place.","lb":"secret meeting","s":["rendezvous","secret meeting","assignation","date","liaison"],"k":["appointment","clandestine meeting","engagement","hook-up"],"a":[],"ex":["The novel begins with a secret tryst between two students beside the old campus lake.","Neighbours whispered about the late-night tryst between the young doctor and the baker's daughter.","They chose a quiet tea stall far from the college for their first tryst."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"tumult","p":"noun","d":"Loud, confused noise and excitement, especially from a large crowd.","lb":"uproar, commotion","s":["uproar","commotion","din","clamour","turmoil","hubbub"],"k":["brouhaha","cacophony","disruption","flutter"],"a":["calm","quiet","peace","silence"],"ex":["I could hardly hear my phone over the tumult of the crowd at the railway station.","A tumult of voices filled the hall when the exam results were announced.","The tumult of the market, with sellers shouting and rickshaw bells ringing, never stops before noon."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"turbid","p":"adjective","d":"Cloudy or muddy because it is full of mud or tiny particles, so that you cannot see through it.","lb":"murky, cloudy","s":["murky","cloudy","muddy","opaque","thick","dirty"],"k":["brackish","dim","foggy","mucky"],"a":["clear","transparent","limpid","clean"],"ex":["After the heavy rain, the river was brown and turbid.","The turbid water in the pond was unsafe to drink.","Scientists measure how turbid a lake is to judge how healthy it is."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"turbulent","p":"adjective","d":"Full of sudden violent changes, disorder or unrest; rough and unsteady.","lb":"stormy, chaotic","s":["stormy","unsettled","chaotic","rough","restless","tumultuous"],"k":["boisterous","churning","disruptive","fierce"],"a":["calm","peaceful","tranquil","still"],"ex":["The flight was turbulent, and the pilot asked everyone to stay in their seats.","She grew up in turbulent times, moving cities three times before the age of ten.","Fishermen avoid the turbulent waters of the Bay of Bengal during the cyclone season."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"turmoil","p":"noun","d":"A state of great confusion, worry or disturbance.","lb":"chaos, upheaval","s":["upheaval","chaos","unrest","commotion","disorder","tumult"],"k":["bedlam","convulsion","din","disruption"],"a":["calm","peace","order","tranquillity"],"ex":["My mind was in turmoil the night before the admission test.","The sudden fall in prices threw the local market into turmoil.","Floods and power cuts left the city in turmoil for several days."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"turpitude","p":"noun","d":"Very wicked or shameful behavior; a deeply immoral character.","lb":"depravity, wickedness","s":["depravity","wickedness","corruption","immorality","iniquity","villainy"],"k":["corruptness","degeneracy","dishonesty","evil"],"a":["virtue","goodness","integrity","honor"],"ex":["A crime of moral turpitude, such as fraud, can cost a person a professional license.","The newspaper exposed the turpitude of officials who stole money meant for flood relief.","The novel traces a young man's slide into turpitude after he starts gambling."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"tweak","p":"verb","d":"To make small changes to something in order to improve it.","lb":"adjust, fine-tune","s":["adjust","modify","adapt","refine","alter","fiddle with"],"k":["acclimatize","amend","change","convert"],"a":[],"ex":["I tweaked my study schedule so I could revise difficult chapters in the morning.","The chef tweaked the recipe by adding a little lemon juice.","Developers tweaked the app to make it load faster on slow phones."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"tyrannical","p":"adjective","d":"Using power in a cruel and unfair way, without allowing others any freedom.","lb":"oppressive, domineering","s":["oppressive","autocratic","dictatorial","domineering","authoritarian","harsh"],"k":["absolutist","bossy","draconian","imperious"],"a":["democratic","liberal","lenient","gentle"],"ex":["Our tyrannical boss refuses to let anyone leave the office before seven.","The tyrannical king taxed the villagers until they could barely afford rice.","Her tyrannical father decided everything, from her university subjects to her friends."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"ubiquitous","p":"adjective","d":"Seeming to be present everywhere at the same time; very common.","lb":"omnipresent, everywhere","s":["omnipresent","pervasive","universal","widespread","prevalent","common"],"k":["all over","cosmopolitan","endemic","everywhere"],"a":["rare","scarce","uncommon","absent"],"ex":["Smartphones are ubiquitous now, and even small children know how to use them.","The ubiquitous rickshaw is the most common way to cross short distances in Dhaka.","Advertisements are ubiquitous online, appearing on almost every website you visit."],"b":594,"y":2},{"w":"ubiquity","p":"noun","d":"The fact of being found everywhere, or of seeming to be very common.","lb":"pervasiveness, commonness","s":["omnipresence"],"k":["all-pervasiveness","endemicity","everywhereness","inescapability"],"a":["scarcity","rarity","absence","uniqueness"],"ex":["The ubiquity of smartphones means that almost everyone can take a photo instantly.","Because of the ubiquity of rickshaws in Dhaka, you can find one on almost every street.","Teachers worry about the ubiquity of social media in students' lives."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"unabated","p":"adjective","d":"Continuing with no loss of strength, speed or intensity.","lb":"continuing, relentless","s":["relentless","continuous","unrelenting","persistent","intense","constant"],"k":["ceaseless","continual","dogged","grim"],"a":["diminishing","subsiding","waning","weakening"],"ex":["The rain continued unabated for three days, and the streets of the city turned into rivers.","Despite the warnings, the traffic on the highway continued unabated through the night.","Her enthusiasm for learning English remained unabated even after months of hard study."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"uncalled","p":"adjective","d":"Not needed or deserved, especially when describing a remark or action that is rude or unfair (usually \"uncalled for\").","lb":"unnecessary, unjustified","s":["unnecessary","unwarranted","unjustified","undeserved","gratuitous","unprovoked"],"k":["gratis","out of place","redundant","superfluous"],"a":["justified","warranted","deserved","necessary"],"ex":["Your sarcastic comment about my handwriting was completely uncalled for.","The referee's angry shouting at the young player seemed uncalled for.","I thought her harsh criticism was uncalled for, since the mistake was so small."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"uncanny","p":"adjective","d":"Strange and surprising in a way that is hard to explain, almost as if not natural.","lb":"eerie, strange","s":["eerie","strange","weird","spooky","unnatural","mysterious"],"k":["amazing","eldritch","extraordinary","odd"],"a":["ordinary","normal","natural","commonplace"],"ex":["My little sister has an uncanny resemblance to our grandmother in old photographs.","The coach showed an uncanny ability to predict which player would score.","It was uncanny how the phone rang just as I was thinking about my friend."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"unconscionable","p":"adjective","d":"Morally wrong and unfair, or so excessive that it is unreasonable.","lb":"unethical, excessive","s":["unscrupulous","unethical","immoral","outrageous","shameful","inexcusable"],"k":["disgraceful","dishonourable","egregious","immoderate"],"a":["ethical","fair","reasonable","moral"],"ex":["It is unconscionable to charge sick people triple the price for basic medicine.","The company's unconscionable delay left families waiting months for their refunds.","Hiding the safety problem from customers was an unconscionable act."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"unctuous","p":"adjective","d":"Too friendly and flattering in a way that seems false and unpleasant.","lb":"oily, insincere","s":["oily","smarmy","slimy","fawning","ingratiating","glib"],"k":["buttery","fat","fatty","flattering"],"a":["sincere","genuine","honest","blunt"],"ex":["The unctuous salesman kept calling us dear friends while pushing the most expensive sofa in the shop.","His unctuous praise for the boss made his colleagues roll their eyes.","I distrust waiters with an unctuous smile who compliment everything I order."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"underlying","p":"adjective","d":"Basic and important but not obvious at first; forming the real cause or foundation of something.","lb":"basic, hidden","s":["fundamental","basic","root","essential","hidden","latent"],"k":["implicit in","inherent","primary","rudimentary"],"a":["superficial","apparent","surface","outward"],"ex":["Doctors are still searching for the underlying cause of her constant headaches.","The underlying problem in our group is poor communication, not lack of effort.","Beneath the funny story is a serious underlying message about kindness."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"undermine","p":"verb","d":"To weaken something gradually or secretly, so that it becomes less strong or effective.","lb":"weaken, sabotage","s":["weaken","sabotage","subvert","erode","impair","damage"],"k":["cave","chip away at","compromise","counteract"],"a":["strengthen","support","reinforce","bolster"],"ex":["Constant rumors about the manager began to undermine the team's trust in him.","Skipping breakfast and sleep can undermine your health before important exams.","Cheating in exams undermines the value of honest students' hard work."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"underpinning","p":"noun","d":"A support or foundation that something rests on, or the basic ideas that make something work.","lb":"foundation, basis","s":["foundation","basis","support","base","cornerstone","groundwork"],"k":["buttress","footing","keystone","pier"],"a":[],"ex":["Strong trust is the underpinning of any good friendship.","Workers added steel underpinnings to the old house so it would not sink further.","The economic theory has a simple underpinning: people respond to prices."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"underscore","p":"verb","d":"To emphasize something and show that it is important or true.","lb":"emphasize, highlight","s":["emphasize","highlight","stress","underline","accentuate","spotlight"],"k":["bring out","call attention to","demonstrate","evidence"],"a":["downplay","minimize","play down","understate"],"ex":["The recent floods underscore the need for better drainage in the city.","The teacher underscored the importance of reading the question carefully before answering.","Her success underscores how much hard work and patience can achieve."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"underwrite","p":"verb","d":"To agree to pay the costs of something, or to accept financial responsibility for it, especially as an insurer.","lb":"sponsor, insure","s":["sponsor","finance","fund","back","subsidize","guarantee"],"k":["assist","bankroll","champion","check"],"a":["withdraw","cancel"],"ex":["A local business agreed to underwrite the cost of the school science fair.","The bank will underwrite the loan if the borrower has a stable income.","Insurance companies underwrite policies only after checking the risks carefully."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"undiluted","p":"adjective","d":"Pure and strong because nothing has been added to weaken it.","lb":"pure, concentrated","s":["pure","concentrated","neat","straight","unadulterated","strong"],"k":["black","clean","potent","raw"],"a":["diluted","weak","thinned","mixed"],"ex":["Never drink undiluted syrup; mix it with plenty of water first.","The cleaner is very strong, so don't use it undiluted on the floor.","She felt undiluted joy when she saw her exam results."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"uniform","p":"adjective","d":"Staying the same in form, size or quality everywhere or at all times, without variation.","lb":"consistent, same","s":["consistent","even","regular","constant","steady","identical"],"k":["coherent","fixed","flat","harmonious"],"a":["varied","inconsistent","irregular","uneven"],"ex":["The tailor cut all the shirts to a uniform length so that the whole set looked neat.","Heat from the new oven is uniform, so every cake bakes evenly.","Schools need a uniform standard for grading so that all students are treated fairly."],"b":400,"y":0},{"w":"unilateral","p":"adjective","d":"Done or decided by one person, group or country alone, without the agreement of the others involved.","lb":"one-sided, independent","s":["independent","solo","sole","individual","lone","separate"],"k":["arbitrary","autocratic","autonomous","direct"],"a":["bilateral","mutual","joint","collective"],"ex":["The manager made a unilateral decision to change the deadline without asking the team.","A unilateral change to the contract is not legal without the other party's agreement.","She was upset by his unilateral choice of the holiday destination."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"unravel","p":"verb","d":"To undo something tangled or woven; also to explain a mystery, or, of a plan, to fall apart.","lb":"undo, untangle","s":["untangle","undo","unwind","disentangle","unscramble"],"k":["come apart","crack","decipher","extricate"],"a":["tangle","knot","entangle","twist"],"ex":["The old sweater began to unravel at the sleeve after one careless pull.","It took me ten minutes to unravel my tangled earphone cable.","Her grandmother patiently unraveled the knotted fishing net on the veranda."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"unremitting","p":"adjective","d":"Continuing without any pause or reduction in strength, often in a tiring or unpleasant way.","lb":"constant, relentless","s":["relentless","constant","unceasing","incessant","persistent","continuous"],"k":["ageless","continual","dogged","eternal"],"a":["intermittent","occasional","sporadic","periodic"],"ex":["Unremitting rain for three days flooded the low roads around the market.","Her unremitting hard work over two years finally earned her a scholarship.","The nurses faced unremitting pressure as patients kept arriving through the night."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"unrivalled","p":"adjective","d":"Better than all others; having no equal.","lb":"unmatched, supreme","s":["unmatched","unequaled","unparalleled","peerless","supreme","incomparable"],"k":["best in class","one","one and only","preeminent"],"a":["mediocre","ordinary","inferior","average"],"ex":["The chef's skill with spices is unrivalled in the whole city.","The Sundarbans offer an unrivalled variety of wildlife for visitors.","Her unrivalled knowledge of grammar made her the best teacher in the school."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"unruffled","p":"adjective","d":"Calm and not upset or worried, even when something difficult happens.","lb":"calm, composed","s":["calm","composed","serene","cool","untroubled","collected"],"k":["peaceful","placid","quiet","relaxed"],"a":["agitated","flustered","upset","ruffled"],"ex":["The pilot remained unruffled during the storm and spoke calmly to the passengers.","She stayed unruffled when the customer shouted at her across the counter.","Our teacher was unruffled by the sudden power cut and finished the lesson by candlelight."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"unruly","p":"adjective","d":"Difficult to control or manage, and not willing to obey rules or discipline.","lb":"disorderly, rebellious","s":["disobedient","wild","rowdy","disorderly","undisciplined","uncontrollable"],"k":["difficult","fractious","insubordinate","rambunctious"],"a":["obedient","orderly","disciplined","manageable"],"ex":["The teacher stayed calm even when the unruly class kept shouting at the back.","A few unruly fans were asked to leave the stadium after the match.","My little brother's unruly hair never stays flat, however much water he uses."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"unsettle","p":"verb","d":"To make someone feel worried, nervous or uncomfortable.","lb":"disturb, upset","s":["disturb","upset","unnerve","rattle","disconcert","agitate"],"k":["bother","discomfit","discompose","enervate"],"a":["calm","soothe","reassure","comfort"],"ex":["The strange noise in the empty house unsettled the children.","Bad news about the exam date unsettled the whole class.","Frequent changes in the schedule can unsettle young children."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"unswerving","p":"adjective","d":"Not changing or weakening; firm and loyal even when things are difficult.","lb":"steadfast, constant","s":["steadfast","unwavering","constant","resolute","firm","loyal"],"k":["adamant","committed","dedicated","determined"],"a":["wavering","fickle","unsteady","inconsistent"],"ex":["Her unswerving support helped me keep going during my final-year project.","The shopkeeper's unswerving honesty made customers trust him completely.","He showed unswerving commitment to his training, running every morning even in the rain."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"untapped","p":"adjective","d":"Not yet used or developed, but available for use.","lb":"unused, unexploited","s":["unused","latent","undeveloped","hidden","dormant"],"k":["concealed","fallow","inactive","quiescent"],"a":["used","exploited","developed","tapped"],"ex":["The coach believes the young goalkeeper has untapped potential.","Rural areas are an untapped market for online shopping companies.","The island has untapped reserves of fresh water."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"untenable","p":"adjective","d":"Impossible to defend or keep believing because of strong objections or opposing evidence.","lb":"indefensible, unsustainable","s":["indefensible","unsustainable","insupportable","unsound","flawed","groundless"],"k":["hopeless","inexcusable","irrational","unarguable"],"a":["tenable","defensible","justifiable","sound"],"ex":["After the new evidence appeared, his claim that he was at home became untenable.","Paying such high rent on a part-time salary is untenable for most students.","The doctor said the old theory about the disease was untenable."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"untoward","p":"adjective","d":"Unexpected and unfortunate, or not suitable or proper.","lb":"unfortunate, improper","s":["unfortunate","inappropriate","improper","unexpected","unseemly","adverse"],"k":["disagreeable","distressing","hapless","inauspicious"],"a":["favorable","fortunate","proper","suitable"],"ex":["The police found nothing untoward at the house, so no one was arrested.","If anything untoward happens during the trip, call me immediately.","He apologized for the untoward comment he had made at dinner."],"b":8,"y":0},{"w":"unwitting","p":"adjective","d":"Not aware of what is happening or of the effects of your own actions.","lb":"unaware, unintentional","s":["unaware","unknowing","unintentional","accidental","innocent","unconscious"],"k":["blind","credulous","fortuitous","heedless"],"a":["aware","deliberate","intentional","knowing"],"ex":["The delivery boy was an unwitting accomplice, since he did not know what was in the parcel.","I made an unwitting mistake by sending the invitation to the wrong group.","Many internet users are unwitting victims of scams that look like official messages."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"uphold","p":"verb","d":"To support and keep a rule, decision or principle in force.","lb":"support, maintain","s":["maintain","support","defend","preserve","sustain","champion"],"k":["affirm","assist","bear on","carry on"],"a":["overturn","reject","abandon","undermine"],"ex":["The court upheld the decision to cancel the contract.","Teachers must uphold the rules fairly for every student.","A good journalist upholds the truth even when it is uncomfortable."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"uproar","p":"noun","d":"A sudden loud, confused noise or excited public reaction, usually because people are angry or upset.","lb":"commotion, outcry","s":["commotion","din","outcry","tumult","racket","clamour"],"k":["brouhaha","cacophony","disruption","disturbance"],"a":["calm","silence","peace","quiet"],"ex":["The classroom was in an uproar when the teacher announced a surprise test.","News of the ticket price increase caused an uproar among fans.","The crowd burst into an uproar when the referee ignored the foul."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"urban","p":"adjective","d":"Relating to a town or city, rather than the countryside.","lb":"city, metropolitan","s":["city","metropolitan","municipal","civic","town","downtown"],"k":["conurbation","cosmopolitan","inner-city","megacity"],"a":["rural","rustic","country","agricultural"],"ex":["Dhaka is one of the most crowded urban areas in the world.","Many young people move from villages to urban centers in search of jobs.","Rooftop gardens help urban families grow fresh vegetables."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"urbane","p":"adjective","d":"Polite, confident and relaxed in social situations, with smooth and refined manners.","lb":"polite, sophisticated","s":["suave","polished","refined","sophisticated","courteous","cultivated"],"k":["affable","charming","civilized","cultured"],"a":["uncouth","boorish","crude","rude"],"ex":["The urbane host greeted every guest by name and made even shy visitors feel at ease.","Our new principal is urbane, speaking calmly and politely even when parents complain loudly.","He had an urbane way of turning a difficult interview question into a joke."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"urbanization","p":"noun","d":"The process by which more people come to live in towns and cities, and cities grow larger.","lb":"city growth","s":["urban growth","city growth","urban expansion","urban development","metropolitan growth","city expansion"],"k":["city-building","condition","conurbation growth","gentrification"],"a":[],"ex":["Rapid urbanization has made Dhaka one of the most crowded cities in the world.","Urbanization pulls young people from villages to cities in search of jobs and better schools.","Experts warn that unplanned urbanization can cause flooding when drains and canals get blocked."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"urge","p":"verb","d":"To strongly advise or encourage someone to do something.","lb":"encourage strongly","s":["encourage","press","push","advise","implore","exhort"],"k":["advocate","cheer","counsel","egg on"],"a":["discourage","dissuade","deter","restrain"],"ex":["Doctors urge people to drink plenty of water during the summer heat.","My teacher urged me to apply for the scholarship.","Parents urged the school to repair the broken fence."],"b":320,"y":2},{"w":"usurp","p":"verb","d":"To take someone's position, power or right by force or without any legal right.","lb":"seize, take over","s":["seize","take over","commandeer","appropriate","grab","assume"],"k":["arrogate","clutch","depose","dethrone"],"a":["relinquish","cede","surrender","yield"],"ex":["In the story, the prince's uncle tried to usurp the throne while the king was ill.","The assistant manager tried to usurp the manager's authority by giving orders to the whole team.","A group of residents tried to usurp the committee's power by changing the locks on the community hall."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"usury","p":"noun","d":"The practice of lending money at an extremely high, often illegal, rate of interest.","lb":"loan-sharking, extortion","s":["extortion","profiteering","overcharging","exploitation"],"k":["extortionate lending","interest racketeering","interest rate","moneygrubbing"],"a":[],"ex":["Lending money at forty percent a month is usury, and it is against the law.","Poor farmers once fell into deep debt to moneylenders who practiced usury.","The bank was fined after customers complained about usury hidden in the loan contract."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"utilitarian","p":"adjective","d":"Designed to be useful and practical rather than attractive or comfortable.","lb":"practical, functional","s":["practical","functional","serviceable","pragmatic","useful","sensible"],"k":["bare-bones","functional-only","matter-of-fact","realistic"],"a":["ornamental","decorative","impractical","useless"],"ex":["The hostel room was utilitarian, with a bed, a desk and a single shelf.","She chose a utilitarian backpack with strong zips instead of a fashionable one.","The utilitarian design of the bridge ignored beauty and focused on carrying traffic safely."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"utopia","p":"noun","d":"An imaginary place or society where everything is perfect.","lb":"paradise, ideal world","s":["paradise","heaven","dreamland","ideal world","heaven on earth"],"k":["bliss","eden","el dorado","ideal state"],"a":["hell","nightmare","inferno"],"ex":["No city is a utopia, but we can still work to make ours cleaner and safer.","In his novel, the island is a utopia where nobody is poor and everyone shares the work.","My little sister’s idea of a utopia is a world with no homework and unlimited ice cream."],"b":80,"y":1},{"w":"vacillate","p":"verb","d":"To keep changing your mind between different choices or opinions because you cannot decide.","lb":"waver, hesitate","s":["waver","hesitate","dither","falter","oscillate","teeter"],"k":["be unsure","flip-flop","seesaw","sway"],"a":["decide","resolve","commit","persist"],"ex":["Nadia vacillated between studying medicine and engineering until the last day of admission.","The shopper vacillated for an hour between a red phone and a black one.","Don't vacillate; tell the hotel today whether you want the room."],"b":531,"y":0},{"w":"vacuous","p":"adjective","d":"Empty of thought, meaning or intelligence.","lb":"empty, mindless","s":["empty","blank","vapid","inane","mindless","hollow"],"k":["asinine","bare","brainless","dim"],"a":["meaningful","thoughtful","intelligent","profound"],"ex":["He gave a vacuous smile and nodded, though he had understood nothing.","The talk show was full of vacuous chatter about celebrity gossip.","Her vacuous reply, “It depends,” told us nothing."],"b":40,"y":0},{"w":"vagary","p":"noun","d":"An unexpected and unpredictable change in a situation or in the way a person behaves.","lb":"whim, unpredictable change","s":["whim","caprice","quirk","fluctuation","change","fancy"],"k":["alteration","fickleness","freak","impulse"],"a":["constancy","stability","regularity","consistency"],"ex":["Farmers must plan their planting around the vagaries of the monsoon.","Investors learn quickly to live with the vagaries of the stock market.","I never understood the vagaries of my grandfather's moods; he could turn cheerful or silent within minutes."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vague","p":"adjective","d":"Not clear or exact; lacking detail so that the meaning or shape is hard to see.","lb":"unclear, indefinite","s":["unclear","indistinct","hazy","ambiguous","imprecise","fuzzy"],"k":["blurred","blurry","cloudy","dim"],"a":["clear","precise","definite","explicit"],"ex":["The manager gave a vague answer, so nobody knew the real date.","I have only a vague memory of the house where we lived as children.","The instructions were so vague that everyone built the shelf differently."],"b":64,"y":3},{"w":"vanquish","p":"verb","d":"To defeat someone or something completely.","lb":"defeat, conquer","s":["defeat","conquer","beat","overcome","crush","overpower"],"k":["beat out","best","circumvent","get the better of"],"a":["lose","surrender","yield","succumb"],"ex":["The home team vanquished its rivals in the final and won the trophy.","In the legend, the hero vanquished a dragon with a single arrow.","She vanquished her fear of public speaking by practising in front of a mirror every day."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vapid","p":"adjective","d":"Lacking interest, energy or flavor; dull and boring.","lb":"dull, insipid","s":["dull","bland","insipid","flat","lifeless","boring"],"k":["banal","dreary","empty-headed","flavorless"],"a":["lively","interesting","exciting","spirited"],"ex":["The vapid conversation about the weather lasted an hour.","The singer's vapid lyrics said nothing new or interesting.","Without spices, the soup tasted vapid and watery."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vehement","p":"adjective","d":"Showing very strong, intense feeling or opinion, often in an angry or forceful way.","lb":"forceful, passionate","s":["forceful","passionate","fervent","intense","fierce","ardent"],"k":["avid","devoted","earnest","enthusiastic"],"a":["mild","apathetic","indifferent","calm"],"ex":["The shopkeeper gave a vehement denial when a customer accused him of selling fake medicine.","Residents voiced vehement opposition to the plan to cut down the old trees in the park.","The doctor was vehement that smoking must stop immediately after the heart attack."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"venal","p":"adjective","d":"Willing to do dishonest things in return for money, such as taking bribes.","lb":"corrupt, bribable","s":["corrupt","mercenary","crooked","dishonest","unscrupulous","corruptible"],"k":["avaricious","bent","buyable","grafting"],"a":["honest","incorruptible","honorable","upright"],"ex":["The venal inspector approved the unsafe building after accepting an envelope of cash.","Villagers complained that the venal clerk would not process any paper without a bribe.","A venal referee who takes money to favor one team ruins the whole game."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"venation","p":"noun","d":"The pattern of veins in a leaf or in an insect's wing.","lb":"vein pattern","s":["vein pattern"],"k":["arrangement","nervation","vascularity","vasculature"],"a":[],"ex":["In biology class we compared the venation of a mango leaf with that of a grass blade.","Grass leaves show parallel venation, while most broad leaves have a branching net pattern.","The insect's wings have such delicate venation that each species can be identified from it."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"veneer","p":"noun","d":"A thin surface layer of attractive material, or a false outward appearance that hides what is underneath.","lb":"facade, front","s":["facade","front","mask","disguise","pretense","show"],"k":["coat","face","facing","finish"],"a":["reality","truth","substance","core"],"ex":["Behind his veneer of politeness, he was a very angry man.","Her veneer of confidence hid how scared she felt before the speech.","The company's friendly veneer disappeared when customers complained."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"venerate","p":"verb","d":"To treat someone or something with great respect and admiration, especially because of age, wisdom or importance.","lb":"revere, honor","s":["revere","respect","honor","worship","esteem","adore"],"k":["admire","bow down to","exalt","glorify"],"a":["despise","disrespect","scorn","dishonor"],"ex":["Students in the village venerate their old teacher and still visit him every year.","Many families venerate their grandparents and ask for their advice on important decisions.","Every February, people across Bangladesh venerate the martyrs of the Language Movement by laying flowers."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"veracious","p":"adjective","d":"Always telling the truth, or being accurate and true.","lb":"truthful, honest","s":["truthful","honest","accurate","reliable","candid","sincere"],"k":["correct","dependable","exact","frank"],"a":["lying","untruthful","dishonest","false"],"ex":["The judge trusted the veracious witness, who had no reason to hide anything.","Our teacher praised Rafi as a veracious boy who always admitted his mistakes.","A veracious report of the accident helped the insurance company decide quickly."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"veracity","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being truthful and accurate.","lb":"truthfulness, accuracy","s":["truthfulness","honesty","accuracy","truth","candor","reliability"],"k":["correctness","exactness","faithfulness","fidelity"],"a":["falsehood","dishonesty","deceit","untruth"],"ex":["The police checked the veracity of his story before releasing him.","Readers questioned the veracity of the news after the photo proved to be edited.","Her reputation for veracity made everyone believe her account of the accident."],"b":26,"y":0},{"w":"verbose","p":"adjective","d":"Using more words than necessary, so that speaking or writing becomes long and tiring.","lb":"wordy, long-winded","s":["wordy","rambling","prolix","windy","garrulous","loquacious"],"k":["diffuse","discursive","expansive","flowery"],"a":["concise","brief","terse","succinct"],"ex":["His email was so verbose that I had to read it twice to find the request.","The professor's verbose explanation confused us more than the original question did.","Cut the verbose introduction and begin your essay with the main point."],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"verdant","p":"adjective","d":"Green and fresh with growing grass, plants or trees.","lb":"green, lush","s":["green","lush","leafy","grassy","luxuriant","flourishing"],"k":["abundant","bloomy","emerald","fecund"],"a":["barren","arid","bare","withered"],"ex":["After weeks of rain, the hills near my uncle's farm turned bright and verdant.","From the train window, we saw verdant tea gardens rolling over the hills of Sreemangal.","The verdant lawn behind the library is a favorite spot for students to read."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"verdict","p":"noun","d":"A decision reached by a jury or judge at the end of a trial, or a judgment someone gives after thinking carefully.","lb":"judgment, decision","s":["judgment","decision","ruling","finding","conclusion","sentence"],"k":["adjudication","arbitration","award","decree"],"a":[],"ex":["The jury took two days to reach a verdict in the case.","The court's verdict was announced on Monday morning, and the courtroom was full.","The judge delivered a verdict of not guilty because there was no evidence."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"verge","p":"noun","d":"The edge or limit of something, especially the point just before something happens or changes.","lb":"edge, brink","s":["brink","edge","threshold","border","margin","brim"],"k":["boundary","cusp","fringe","outskirts"],"a":["centre","middle","interior"],"ex":["The factory was on the verge of closing when a new investor arrived.","She was on the verge of tears when she saw her exam score.","Scientists say the species is on the verge of extinction because its forest home is shrinking."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"verisimilitude","p":"noun","d":"The quality of seeming true or real.","lb":"realism, plausibility","s":["realism","authenticity","plausibility","credibility","believability","semblance of truth"],"k":["color","faithfulness","gloss","lifelike quality"],"a":["unreality","fantasy","artificiality"],"ex":["The film's costumes and sets give it a strong sense of verisimilitude.","The writer added tiny details, such as bus numbers and tea prices, to give the story verisimilitude.","Actors often study real doctors to bring verisimilitude to a hospital scene."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"verity","p":"noun","d":"The quality of being true; also a true statement or principle.","lb":"truth, validity","s":["truth","reality","fact","accuracy","authenticity","veracity"],"k":["actuality","axiom","bedrock","genuineness"],"a":["falsehood","lie","untruth","fiction"],"ex":["Scientists test the verity of a claim by repeating the experiment many times.","She doubted the verity of the rumour and checked the news for herself.","The judge asked each witness to swear to the verity of their statement."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vernacular","p":"noun","d":"The ordinary spoken language of a particular country or region, as opposed to formal or written language.","lb":"everyday speech, dialect","s":["dialect","idiom","slang","native tongue","common speech","jargon"],"k":["accent","cant","common tongue","everyday language"],"a":["standard language","literary language"],"ex":["The doctor explained the illness in the local vernacular so that the villagers could follow.","Textbooks use formal English, but students chat in the vernacular on social media.","The poet wrote in the vernacular of the river people, not in the polished language of the court."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vessel","p":"noun","d":"A ship or large boat used for carrying people or goods on water.","lb":"ship, boat","s":["ship","boat","craft","steamer","ferry","freighter"],"k":["clipper","hull","liner","sailing ship"],"a":[],"ex":["A cargo vessel carrying rice docked at Chattogram port early this morning.","The fishing vessel returned to shore after the storm warning was lifted.","Passengers boarded the large vessel at Sadarghat for the overnight trip down the river."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"vestige","p":"noun","d":"A small remaining trace of something that has almost disappeared.","lb":"trace, remnant","s":["trace","remnant","remains","sign","relic","hint"],"k":["echo","hangover","indication","remainder"],"a":[],"ex":["Only a few vestiges of the old fort wall remain beside the road.","There was not a vestige of fear in her voice as she spoke to the crowd.","Her accent still carries a vestige of the village where she grew up."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"vex","p":"verb","d":"To annoy or worry someone, especially with small, repeated problems.","lb":"annoy, irritate","s":["annoy","irritate","bother","irk","trouble","pester"],"k":["agitate","chafe","devil","displease"],"a":["please","soothe","delight","calm"],"ex":["The constant noise from the building site vexed everyone living on our street.","It vexes me that the bus never arrives on time, even though I check the schedule.","The slow internet connection vexed Tania while she was trying to submit her assignment."],"b":28,"y":0},{"w":"vexed","p":"adjective","d":"Annoyed, frustrated or worried, especially by a small but continuing problem.","lb":"annoyed, troubled","s":["annoyed","irritated","bothered","troubled","frustrated","irked"],"k":["difficult","exasperated","harassed","hard"],"a":["pleased","calm","delighted","content"],"ex":["Mother was vexed when the guests arrived two hours earlier than promised.","He looked vexed after waiting an hour for a bus that never came.","The vexed customer asked to speak to the manager about the broken product."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"viable","p":"adjective","d":"Able to work successfully, or likely to succeed in practice.","lb":"workable, feasible","s":["workable","feasible","realistic","sustainable","possible","practical"],"k":["alive","attainable","doable","pragmatic"],"a":["unworkable","impractical","unrealistic","impossible"],"ex":["Solar panels are a viable option for homes that suffer from regular power cuts.","The bank said the shop was not a viable business because its costs were too high.","Is there any viable alternative to the bus during the rail strike?"],"b":19,"y":0},{"w":"vicarious","p":"adjective","d":"Felt or experienced by watching or imagining another person's actions rather than doing them yourself.","lb":"indirect, secondhand","s":["indirect","secondhand","surrogate","substitute","imagined","shared"],"k":["abnormal","borrowed","delegated","deputed"],"a":["direct","firsthand","personal","actual"],"ex":["My mother takes vicarious pride in my brother's success and tells every neighbor about it.","Reading travel blogs gave him a vicarious thrill since he could not afford to travel.","Watching the climbers on television, she felt vicarious excitement without leaving the sofa."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vicariously","p":"adverb","d":"In a way that you experience something through another person's actions or feelings, not your own.","lb":"through others","s":["indirectly","secondhand","at one remove","by proxy","through another"],"k":["by deputy","by surrogate","empathetically","sympathetically"],"a":["directly","firsthand","personally","in person"],"ex":["My mother lives vicariously through my travels because she never had the chance to go abroad.","Fans enjoy sports vicariously by watching their heroes win.","He experienced the mountain climb vicariously through his friend's photographs."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"vicious","p":"adjective","d":"Cruel and violent, or meant to hurt someone badly.","lb":"cruel, savage","s":["cruel","brutal","savage","ferocious","malicious","spiteful"],"k":["barbarous","deplorable","evil","fell"],"a":["gentle","kind","mild","harmless"],"ex":["The neighbors warned us about a vicious dog that bites strangers.","She was hurt by the vicious rumors spread about her at school.","The online comments were vicious, full of cruel jokes about his appearance."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"vicissitude","p":"noun","d":"A change of circumstances or fortune, often an unwelcome one, that happens during a life or process.","lb":"ups and downs, change","s":["ups and downs","fluctuation","change","upheaval","shift","reversal"],"k":["alteration","instability","turn of events","turn of fortune"],"a":["stability","constancy","sameness","permanence"],"ex":["My grandmother survived many vicissitudes, from poverty in childhood to success in business.","A good friend stays with you through all the vicissitudes of life.","The vicissitudes of the stock market made him nervous about investing his savings."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"vie","p":"verb","d":"To compete with other people for something that only one or a few can win or get.","lb":"compete, contend","s":["compete","contend","contest","struggle","jockey","fight"],"k":["challenge","clash","dispute","jostle"],"a":["cooperate","collaborate","yield","give way"],"ex":["Several students vied for the top place in the class.","Twenty teams vied for the championship trophy.","Street vendors vie for customers near the busy bus terminal."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vigilant","p":"adjective","d":"Watching carefully for danger or problems and ready to act.","lb":"watchful, alert","s":["watchful","alert","attentive","wary","observant","on guard"],"k":["circumspect","guarded","heedful","on one's toes"],"a":["careless","inattentive","negligent","unwary"],"ex":["Parents must stay vigilant when children play near a busy road.","Online shoppers should be vigilant about fake websites that steal card details.","The vigilant security guard noticed the open window and called the manager."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vignette","p":"noun","d":"A short, vivid piece of writing, film or acting that captures one small scene or moment.","lb":"short sketch, scene","s":["sketch","scene","snapshot","portrait","miniature","cameo"],"k":["essay","fragment","impression","portrayal"],"a":[],"ex":["The author opens each chapter with a short vignette about life in a small riverside town.","In a two-minute vignette, the film shows a tired rickshaw puller sharing his lunch with a stray dog.","Our teacher asked us to write a vignette describing one busy morning at the family breakfast table."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adjective","d":"Strong, active and full of energy or force.","lb":"energetic, strong","s":["energetic","robust","strong","active","lively","dynamic"],"k":["emphatic","hardy","powerful","resilient"],"a":["weak","feeble","lethargic","sluggish"],"ex":["Doctors recommend thirty minutes of vigorous exercise on most days of the week.","The two debaters had a vigorous discussion about homework.","My grandfather is eighty but still vigorous enough to climb the stairs every day."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"vile","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely bad or unpleasant, especially in a way that disgusts you.","lb":"disgusting, foul","s":["disgusting","foul","revolting","nasty","repulsive","horrible"],"k":["atrocious","awful","distasteful","evil"],"a":["pleasant","lovely","delightful","wonderful"],"ex":["The vile smell from the blocked drain made us close all the windows.","The medicine tasted so vile that the child refused to swallow it.","Spreading false rumours about a friend is a vile thing to do."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"vilify","p":"verb","d":"To say or write very unpleasant, untrue things about someone to damage their reputation.","lb":"slander, defame","s":["defame","slander","smear","malign","denigrate","disparage"],"k":["abuse","blackguard","discredit","shout"],"a":["praise","extol","glorify","honor"],"ex":["Some people online vilify anyone who disagrees with them, instead of answering their arguments.","The shop was vilified in angry posts that claimed it sold fake goods.","Instead of arguing fairly, he tried to vilify his opponent with rumors."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vindicate","p":"verb","d":"To prove that someone or something was right or not guilty, after doubts or blame.","lb":"clear, justify","s":["clear","exonerate","acquit","absolve","justify","support"],"k":["champion","discharge","exculpate","free"],"a":["blame","condemn","accuse","convict"],"ex":["The video footage vindicated the driver, showing that the other car had caused the crash.","When the test results came out, they vindicated her decision to study every night.","Years later, new evidence vindicated the scientist whose work had been ignored."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"vindictive","p":"adjective","d":"Wanting to hurt someone who has harmed or offended you, often in a cruel or spiteful way.","lb":"vengeful, spiteful","s":["vengeful","spiteful","revengeful","malicious","resentful","unforgiving"],"k":["bitter","grudge-bearing","punitive","reprisal-minded"],"a":["forgiving","merciful","charitable","benevolent"],"ex":["After their argument, she became vindictive and told everyone his secret.","It would be vindictive to fail a student just because he once disagreed with you.","The vindictive neighbor kept calling the police about our harmless wedding music."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"virile","p":"adjective","d":"Having the strength, energy and qualities that are traditionally seen as manly.","lb":"manly, vigorous","s":["manly","masculine","strong","vigorous","robust","macho"],"k":["hardy","male","manlike","potent"],"a":["weak","feeble","frail","timid"],"ex":["The actor was famous for playing virile heroes who rescue people from danger.","In his youth, my grandfather was a virile wrestler known across the district.","Many old paintings show kings as strong, virile leaders."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"virtuoso","p":"noun","d":"A person with outstanding skill in an art or craft, especially a musician who performs brilliantly.","lb":"master, expert","s":["maestro","master","expert","genius","ace","wizard"],"k":["adept","connoisseur","hotshot","maven"],"a":["amateur","novice","beginner"],"ex":["The young violin virtuoso played for an hour, and nobody in the hall moved.","Our neighbor is a virtuoso on the tabla, and people gather whenever he plays at weddings.","In the kitchen, my aunt is a virtuoso who can turn a few leftover vegetables into a feast."],"b":80,"y":2},{"w":"virulent","p":"adjective","d":"Extremely harmful or infectious, like a strong poison or disease; also full of bitter hostility.","lb":"deadly, venomous","s":["deadly","poisonous","toxic","harmful","lethal","malignant"],"k":["acerbic","acrid","damaging","dangerous"],"a":["harmless","benign","mild","gentle"],"ex":["A virulent strain of the flu spread quickly through the dormitory last winter.","Doctors warned that the new virus was more virulent than the old one.","The crop disease was so virulent that farmers lost the entire harvest within weeks."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"viscous","p":"adjective","d":"Thick and sticky, so that it flows very slowly.","lb":"thick, sticky","s":["thick","sticky","gluey","gooey","tacky","gummy"],"k":["adhesive","clotted","gelatinous","heavy"],"a":["watery","runny","thin","fluid"],"ex":["Honey is so viscous that it takes a long time to drip off the spoon.","Engine oil becomes more viscous in cold weather and flows more slowly.","The viscous mud on the village road stuck to everyone's sandals after the rain."],"b":45,"y":0},{"w":"visionary","p":"noun","d":"A person with bold ideas about the future, who may seem unrealistic to others.","lb":"dreamer, innovator","s":["dreamer","idealist","prophet","seer","romantic","utopian"],"k":["far-seeing leader","illusionist","intellect","intellectual"],"a":["realist","pragmatist","skeptic"],"ex":["The founder was a visionary who imagined a school in every village.","Everyone laughed at the visionary's plan for a floating market, but it was built ten years later.","My uncle is a visionary who saw how much people would use mobile phones before anyone else did."],"b":24,"y":0},{"w":"vitality","p":"noun","d":"Great energy and liveliness, especially a strong, healthy ability to keep going.","lb":"energy, liveliness","s":["energy","vigor","zest","stamina","spirit","life"],"k":["animation","buoyancy","exuberance","life force"],"a":["lethargy","weakness","apathy"],"ex":["Even at seventy, my grandfather walks with surprising vitality every morning.","Regular exercise and enough sleep help students keep their vitality during exam week.","The new cafe has brought fresh vitality to the quiet street."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"vitiate","p":"verb","d":"To spoil or weaken something so that it is no longer effective, pure or valid.","lb":"spoil, impair","s":["spoil","impair","undermine","corrupt","weaken","ruin"],"k":["alter","botch","change","damage"],"a":["improve","purify","strengthen","enhance"],"ex":["One careless mistake in the data can vitiate the results of the whole experiment.","Constant arguments vitiated the friendly atmosphere in our hostel.","The contract was declared invalid because pressure on one side vitiated their free agreement."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vitriolic","p":"adjective","d":"Full of bitter, cruel and angry criticism.","lb":"bitter, scathing","s":["scathing","caustic","bitter","venomous","acid","savage"],"k":["acidic","acrid","acrimonious","blistering"],"a":["gentle","kind","mild","complimentary"],"ex":["The critic wrote a vitriolic review that left the young author in tears.","After the match, the manager launched a vitriolic attack on the referee.","Her vitriolic comment under the photo started a fight between the cousins."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vituperative","p":"adjective","d":"Full of bitter, angry and abusive criticism.","lb":"abusive, scathing","s":["abusive","scathing","venomous","scolding","vicious","caustic"],"k":["biting","brutal","critical","cutting"],"a":["complimentary","kind","gentle","polite"],"ex":["The comments section was full of vituperative messages after the team lost the final.","She sent a vituperative email to the landlord about the broken water pump.","The old man's vituperative remarks about young people embarrassed his whole family."],"b":1,"y":0},{"w":"vivacious","p":"adjective","d":"Full of life, energy and fun, especially of a person.","lb":"lively, spirited","s":["lively","animated","spirited","bubbly","energetic","sparkling"],"k":["active","boisterous","bouncy","dynamic"],"a":["dull","listless","lifeless","subdued"],"ex":["My vivacious aunt fills every family gathering with laughter and stories.","The vivacious host kept the audience entertained throughout the long show.","She has a vivacious personality that makes strangers feel like friends."],"b":96,"y":2},{"w":"vocation","p":"noun","d":"A particular job or career, especially one that you feel strongly suited to and committed to.","lb":"occupation, calling","s":["occupation","profession","career","calling","trade","job"],"k":["bent","business","craft","destiny"],"a":["avocation","hobby","pastime"],"ex":["Teaching is not just a job for her; it is her true vocation.","After years in banking, he left to follow his real vocation as a carpenter.","Counselors help students discover a vocation that matches their skills, not just one that pays well."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"vociferous","p":"adjective","d":"Expressing opinions or protest loudly and with strong feeling.","lb":"loud, outspoken","s":["loud","noisy","vehement","outspoken","insistent","forceful"],"k":["blatant","boisterous","deafening","emphatic"],"a":["quiet","silent","subdued","muted"],"ex":["Residents were vociferous in their protest against the closure of the neighborhood clinic.","My aunt is a vociferous supporter of the local football team.","Parents were vociferous about the lack of safe walkways outside the school."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"vogue","p":"noun","d":"A popular fashion or style at a particular time.","lb":"fashion, trend","s":["fashion","trend","craze","rage","style","mode"],"k":["appreciation","buzz","currency","favor"],"a":["disfavor","obsolescence"],"ex":["Short hair is in vogue among college students this year.","Bell-bottom jeans have come back into vogue after many years.","Healthy snacks are in vogue among busy office workers."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"volatile","p":"adjective","d":"Likely to change quickly and unpredictably, especially for the worse.","lb":"unstable, changeable","s":["unstable","changeable","unpredictable","erratic","fickle","unsettled"],"k":["capricious","impulsive","inconstant","jumpy"],"a":["stable","steady","constant","calm"],"ex":["Share prices have been volatile this month, rising and falling by the hour.","The situation outside the stadium was volatile, so the police asked fans to leave quietly.","My volatile uncle can be laughing one minute and shouting the next."],"b":83,"y":1},{"w":"volition","p":"noun","d":"The power to make a conscious choice or decision by one's own will.","lb":"free will, choice","s":["will","free will","choice","decision","preference","discretion"],"k":["agency","autonomy","desire","election"],"a":["compulsion","coercion","force"],"ex":["Nobody forced him to join the club; he did it of his own volition.","The student donated blood of his own volition, without anyone asking him to.","She left the company of her own volition and was not asked to resign."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"voluminous","p":"adjective","d":"Very large in size or quantity, taking up a lot of space or running to great length.","lb":"large, extensive","s":["bulky","ample","copious","extensive","capacious","massive"],"k":["big","bountiful","crooked","generous"],"a":["small","scanty","slight","compact"],"ex":["The voluminous curtains in the old hall blocked the afternoon sun completely.","Her voluminous handbag held a water bottle, an umbrella, two novels and a small first-aid kit.","His voluminous diary, spread over twenty notebooks, gives a detailed picture of village life."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"voluminously","p":"adverb","d":"In a very long, detailed way, especially when writing or speaking.","lb":"at great length","s":["copiously","extensively","at length","abundantly","profusely","in great detail"],"k":["digressively","discursively","expansively","extravagantly"],"a":["briefly","concisely","succinctly","sparingly"],"ex":["The professor wrote voluminously about river erosion over forty years.","My grandfather kept a diary and wrote voluminously about village life.","Online reviewers commented voluminously on the phone's battery problems."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"voluntary","p":"adjective","d":"Done or given by choice, not because you are forced or paid to do it.","lb":"optional, willing","s":["optional","willing","unpaid","elective","spontaneous","discretionary"],"k":["conscious","free","freewill","intended"],"a":["compulsory","mandatory","obligatory","forced"],"ex":["Joining the school debating club is voluntary, so only interested students attend.","Many students do voluntary work at the local library on weekends.","The company offered voluntary retirement to older staff, and some accepted."],"b":192,"y":1},{"w":"voluptuous","p":"adjective","d":"Giving great pleasure to the senses; rich, soft and luxurious.","lb":"sensuous, luxurious","s":["sensuous","luxurious","lush","opulent","sumptuous","rich"],"k":["busty","buxom","curvaceous","deluxe"],"a":["austere","plain","spartan","harsh"],"ex":["The shop sold voluptuous velvet curtains in deep red and gold.","A voluptuous scent of roses and sandalwood filled the wedding hall.","She sank into the voluptuous softness of the hotel bed after a long journey."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"voracious","p":"adjective","d":"Eating or wanting something in very large amounts, and never seeming to be satisfied.","lb":"greedy, insatiable","s":["greedy","ravenous","insatiable","gluttonous","hungry","avid"],"k":["acquisitive","avaricious","covetous","devouring"],"a":["satisfied","full","moderate","indifferent"],"ex":["My little brother has a voracious appetite and finishes two plates of rice at dinner.","She is a voracious reader who finishes a novel every two days.","Voracious fish ate everything we threw into the pond."],"b":96,"y":1},{"w":"waft","p":"verb","d":"To move gently through the air, carrying a smell, sound or light object.","lb":"drift, float","s":["drift","float","glide","flow","blow","stream"],"k":["be adrift","bear","breathe","breeze"],"a":[],"ex":["The smell of frying onions wafted from the kitchen and made everyone hungry.","Soft music wafted across the garden from the neighbor’s window.","A cool breeze wafted through the open window, finally giving us some relief from the heat."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"waive","p":"verb","d":"To officially choose not to use a right, rule, fee or requirement.","lb":"relinquish, forgo","s":["relinquish","forgo","give up","renounce","set aside","dispense with"],"k":["cede","forego","forfeit","forsake"],"a":["enforce","insist on","claim","demand"],"ex":["The bank agreed to waive the late fee because the delay was its own mistake.","The university may waive the entrance fee for students from low-income families.","By signing the form, you waive your right to join a legal case later."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"wake","p":"noun","d":"A gathering held before a funeral, when family and friends stay with the body of the dead person.","lb":"funeral vigil","s":["vigil","deathwatch","viewing","watch","visitation"],"k":["aftermath","backwash","funeral","laying-out"],"a":[],"ex":["Relatives and neighbours came to the wake and sat quietly with the family through the night.","At his grandfather's wake, people shared warm stories about the old man's kindness and humour.","Nadia travelled overnight so she could attend her uncle's wake before the burial the next morning."],"b":288,"y":0},{"w":"wane","p":"verb","d":"To become gradually weaker, smaller or less important.","lb":"decline, fade","s":["decline","dwindle","fade","diminish","decrease","ebb"],"k":["dim","drop","fall","fall off"],"a":["wax","grow","increase","strengthen"],"ex":["The moon wanes after the full moon, getting a little smaller each night.","Her interest in the course began to wane after the first month.","As the daylight waned, the fishermen turned their boats towards the shore."],"b":544,"y":0},{"w":"wanton","p":"adjective","d":"Cruel or harmful and done deliberately, without any reason or care for the result.","lb":"senseless, malicious","s":["malicious","senseless","gratuitous","deliberate","unprovoked","reckless"],"k":["easy","loose","malevolent","motiveless"],"a":["justified","provoked","careful","necessary"],"ex":["Vandals caused wanton damage to the school's new library, breaking windows for no reason.","The report condemned the wanton cutting down of forests near the river.","Wanton cruelty to stray animals is a crime in many countries."],"b":20,"y":0},{"w":"warfare","p":"noun","d":"The activity of fighting a war, including the methods used.","lb":"armed conflict","s":["war","combat","fighting","hostilities","battle","conflict"],"k":["armed conflict","arms","belligerence","bloodshed"],"a":["peace","truce","harmony","ceasefire"],"ex":["Our history teacher explained how warfare changed after the invention of aircraft.","The museum shows weapons used in ancient warfare.","Cyber warfare is a growing concern for governments around the world."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"warrant","p":"verb","d":"To be a good enough reason for something, or to make an action seem fair and necessary.","lb":"justify, merit","s":["justify","merit","deserve","call for","excuse","entitle"],"k":["authorize","certify","defend","guarantee"],"a":[],"ex":["A single late arrival does not warrant such a harsh punishment.","The situation is serious enough to warrant a visit to the doctor.","The results warrant further research."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"warranted","p":"adjective","d":"Fully justified or deserved, so that there is a good reason for it.","lb":"justified, deserved","s":["justified","deserved","called for","reasonable","legitimate","appropriate"],"k":["authorized","sanctioned","substantiated","valid"],"a":["unjustified","unreasonable","groundless","unwarranted"],"ex":["Given the long delays, her complaint to the airline was fully warranted.","The doctor said that surgery was not warranted because the injury would heal on its own.","Is such a harsh punishment warranted for being five minutes late?"],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"wary","p":"adjective","d":"Careful and watchful because you think something may be dangerous or may go wrong.","lb":"cautious, careful","s":["cautious","careful","watchful","guarded","alert","suspicious"],"k":["attentive","distrustful","leery","mistrustful"],"a":["trusting","careless","reckless","heedless"],"ex":["After being cheated once, I am wary of buying things from strangers online.","The cat was wary of the new puppy and stayed on top of the cupboard.","Drivers should be wary of slippery roads during the first rain of the season."],"b":35,"y":0},{"w":"wavering","p":"adjective","d":"Not firm or certain; changing in opinion, purpose or strength.","lb":"unsteady, hesitant","s":["hesitant","undecided","unsteady","irresolute","shaky","uncertain"],"k":["ambivalent","faltering","indecisive","precarious"],"a":["firm","steady","resolute","determined"],"ex":["Her wavering voice showed that she was nervous before the speech.","The coach's wavering decisions confused the players before the final.","Wavering customers often change their minds at the last minute and leave without buying."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"wayward","p":"adjective","d":"Behaving in a stubborn, unpredictable way and refusing to accept advice or discipline.","lb":"unruly, headstrong","s":["unruly","disobedient","headstrong","willful","stubborn","rebellious"],"k":["defiant","fractious","froward","insubordinate"],"a":["obedient","docile","compliant","dutiful"],"ex":["The wayward teenager ignored every warning and skipped school again.","Their wayward cousin refused every job offer and kept ignoring family advice.","My wayward puppy runs off whenever I open the gate."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"weekend","p":"noun","d":"The days at the end of the week when most people do not go to work or school.","lb":"days off","s":["days off","time off","break"],"k":["downtime","holiday","leisure time","non-working days"],"a":["weekday","workday"],"ex":["We usually visit my grandparents in the village on the weekend.","Traffic is lighter on the weekend, so the trip takes half the time.","I plan to study for the admission test all weekend."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"welter","p":"noun","d":"A confused mass of things all mixed together, which makes everything hard to understand.","lb":"jumble, confusion","s":["jumble","muddle","mess","tangle","confusion","hodgepodge"],"k":["chaos","clutter","disorder","farrago"],"a":["order","organization","clarity","arrangement"],"ex":["I was lost in a welter of forms, stamps and signatures at the passport office.","She felt a welter of emotions, including pride, fear and excitement, on her first day at university.","The report was a welter of numbers that nobody could understand."],"b":13,"y":0},{"w":"whimsical","p":"adjective","d":"Playfully unusual and unpredictable, often because of sudden fanciful ideas rather than sensible reasons.","lb":"playful, fanciful","s":["fanciful","playful","quirky","capricious","eccentric","fantastic"],"k":["arbitrary","impulsive","offbeat","strange"],"a":["serious","practical","sensible","predictable"],"ex":["The café has a whimsical design, with colorful teapots hanging from the ceiling.","On a whimsical impulse, she painted her old bicycle bright yellow.","He has a whimsical sense of humor and often makes up silly songs."],"b":3,"y":0},{"w":"willful","p":"adjective","d":"Doing what one wants stubbornly despite advice or orders; also, done deliberately, knowing it is wrong.","lb":"stubborn, deliberate","s":["stubborn","obstinate","headstrong","deliberate","intentional","wayward"],"k":["bullheaded","cantankerous","contrary","defiant"],"a":["obedient","docile","compliant","unintentional"],"ex":["The willful child refused to wear a coat even though it was freezing outside.","The mechanic was fired for willful damage to a customer's car.","My willful little sister always insists on choosing the movie, and nobody can change her mind."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"wistful","p":"adjective","d":"Feeling a quiet, slightly sad longing for something past or out of reach.","lb":"longing, nostalgic","s":["longing","yearning","nostalgic","pensive","melancholy","sad"],"k":["bittersweet","doleful","forlorn","hankering"],"a":["content","cheerful","satisfied","glad"],"ex":["He gave a wistful smile as he looked at photos of his old school.","She felt wistful watching her friends leave for university while she stayed behind.","The old man's wistful sigh showed how much he missed the village of his youth."],"b":16,"y":0},{"w":"wit","p":"noun","d":"The ability to say things that are clever and amusing.","lb":"humor, cleverness","s":["humor","cleverness","repartee","banter","drollery","esprit"],"k":["badinage","brain","brainpower","card"],"a":["dullness","seriousness","gravity"],"ex":["The speaker's quick wit kept the audience laughing for an hour.","She is famous for her dry wit, and even her serious emails make people smile.","My uncle uses his wit to calm tense family arguments."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"withdrawal","p":"noun","d":"The act of taking money out of a bank account.","lb":"taking out, payout","s":["debit","payout","taking out","removal","extraction"],"k":["cash out","detachment","drug withdrawal","evacuation"],"a":["deposit","payment","credit","contribution"],"ex":["I made a cash withdrawal from the ATM before I took the bus.","The bank limits each daily withdrawal to fifty thousand taka for safety.","A sudden large withdrawal from her account made the bank call to check."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"wither","p":"verb","d":"To become dry and weak, and slowly lose life, freshness or strength.","lb":"dry up, fade","s":["shrivel","wilt","dry up","fade","droop","decay"],"k":["decline","decrease","diminish","fall"],"a":["bloom","flourish","thrive","blossom"],"ex":["The roses on the balcony withered because nobody watered them while we were away.","Without rain for two months, the crops in the field slowly withered.","Her confidence began to wither after the teacher criticized every answer she gave."],"b":64,"y":2},{"w":"witness","p":"verb","d":"To see an event happen, especially an accident, crime or important change.","lb":"see, observe","s":["see","observe","watch","view","notice","spot"],"k":["catch sight of","experience","eyewitness","find"],"a":["miss","overlook","ignore"],"ex":["Several shoppers witnessed the accident and gave their names to the police.","Our generation has witnessed huge changes in how people use mobile phones.","I witnessed a rickshaw puller return a lost wallet full of money."],"b":320,"y":1},{"w":"wizened","p":"adjective","d":"Dried up and covered with wrinkles, usually because of old age.","lb":"shriveled, wrinkled","s":["shriveled","withered","wrinkled","shrunken","gnarled","lined"],"k":["crinkled","dry","frail","lean"],"a":["plump","smooth","youthful","fresh"],"ex":["A wizened old fisherman mended his net beside the river as the sun went down.","The apples in the forgotten bowl had turned wizened and brown.","Her grandmother's wizened hands still knew exactly how to knead the dough."],"b":36,"y":0},{"w":"woe","p":"noun","d":"Great sadness, trouble or suffering in someone's life.","lb":"sorrow, misery","s":["sorrow","grief","misery","distress","anguish","suffering"],"k":["agony","calamity","dolour","heartbreak"],"a":["joy","happiness","delight","bliss"],"ex":["He told us a long tale of woe about his lost luggage and cancelled flight.","The company's financial woes grew worse when its largest customer left.","Her woes began when she lost her job and then fell ill."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"woven","p":"adjective","d":"Made by passing threads or strips over and under each other, on a loom or by hand.","lb":"interlaced, handmade","s":["interlaced","braided","interwoven","intertwined","plaited","entwined"],"k":["crocheted","knitted","matted","netted"],"a":[],"ex":["Jamdani is a famous woven cloth with delicate patterns made by skilled weavers.","Villagers sell woven baskets and mats at the weekly market.","My grandmother wore a woven shawl on cold winter evenings."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"wrath","p":"noun","d":"Very strong, fierce anger, especially when it leads to a wish to punish someone.","lb":"anger, fury","s":["fury","rage","anger","ire","outrage","indignation"],"k":["bile","choler","craze","exasperation"],"a":["calm","peace","forgiveness","mildness"],"ex":["She was afraid to confess the broken window and face her father's wrath.","The manager's wrath fell on the whole team when the report arrived three days late.","Customers vented their wrath online after the airline cancelled the flight without any warning."],"b":32,"y":0},{"w":"yeast","p":"noun","d":"A tiny fungus used in baking to make dough rise and become light and soft.","lb":"baking agent","s":["ferment","starter"],"k":["barm","bread starter","brewer's yeast","fungus"],"a":[],"ex":["Add a spoonful of yeast to warm water and wait ten minutes.","Bread without yeast stays flat and dense after baking.","The yeast in the dough produces gas that makes the loaf rise."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"yield","p":"verb","d":"To produce or provide something such as a crop, profit or result.","lb":"produce, provide","s":["produce","provide","generate","bear","deliver","bring in"],"k":["afford","bring about","cause","cede"],"a":["withhold","consume","lose"],"ex":["The rice fields yielded a bumper crop this year.","The savings account yields interest of five percent a year.","Our experiment yielded surprising results."],"b":64,"y":1},{"w":"zeal","p":"noun","d":"Great energy and enthusiasm for a cause, an activity or a belief.","lb":"enthusiasm, passion","s":["enthusiasm","passion","fervor","ardor","eagerness","zest"],"k":["avidity","elan","excitement","fanaticism"],"a":["apathy","indifference","lethargy"],"ex":["The volunteers worked with great zeal to rebuild the school after the cyclone.","Her zeal for learning English led her to read one new article every day.","The new coach brought such zeal to training that even tired players smiled."],"b":66,"y":3},{"w":"zealot","p":"noun","d":"A person who is extremely enthusiastic about a cause or belief and may refuse to consider other views.","lb":"fanatic, extremist","s":["fanatic","extremist","partisan","militant","diehard","radical"],"k":["activist","believer","bigot","exponent"],"a":["moderate","skeptic"],"ex":["My cousin is a fitness zealot who will not miss a workout even when he has a fever.","The cleanliness zealot in our office wipes every desk twice a day.","Football zealots argued until midnight about which team deserved the trophy."],"b":65,"y":2},{"w":"zealous","p":"adjective","d":"Very enthusiastic and eager, showing great energy in supporting a cause or doing something.","lb":"enthusiastic, devoted","s":["enthusiastic","eager","passionate","ardent","devoted","fervent"],"k":["committed","dedicated","eager-beaver","fiery"],"a":["apathetic","indifferent","lukewarm"],"ex":["The zealous volunteers worked all weekend to clean the riverbank.","She is a zealous student who stays after class to ask more questions.","A zealous fan, he has not missed a single home match in ten years."],"b":592,"y":1},{"w":"zeitgeist","p":"noun","d":"The general mood, ideas and beliefs that are typical of a particular period in history.","lb":"spirit of the age","s":["spirit of the age","spirit of the times","mood","climate","ethos","atmosphere"],"k":["cultural moment","current","disposition","feeling"],"a":[],"ex":["The song perfectly captured the zeitgeist of the late nineties, when everyone was talking about the internet.","Fashion designers try to read the zeitgeist so they know what people will want to wear next year.","Her novel reflects the zeitgeist of a generation worried about jobs and climate."],"b":48,"y":0},{"w":"zenith","p":"noun","d":"The highest point of something, or the time when it is at its most successful or powerful.","lb":"peak, highest point","s":["peak","summit","pinnacle","apex","height","acme"],"k":["apogee","celestial point","crest","high-water mark"],"a":["nadir","bottom","low point","depths"],"ex":["The sun reaches its zenith around noon, when shadows are shortest.","The singer's career was at its zenith when she filled the city's biggest stadium.","For many students, the zenith of the school year is the annual sports day."],"b":34,"y":0},{"w":"zestful","p":"adjective","d":"Full of enthusiasm, energy and enjoyment.","lb":"enthusiastic, energetic","s":["enthusiastic","energetic","spirited","lively","vigorous","keen"],"k":["active","ardent","avid","barmy"],"a":["listless","apathetic","lethargic","dull"],"ex":["The zestful dancers filled the stage with energy and bright smiles.","She greeted the new term with a zestful attitude and a long list of plans.","My grandfather tells stories in a zestful way that keeps the children listening."],"b":64,"y":1}]});
